\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Key takeaways from day three of the Republican national convention\b0\par\par\uc2 Lois Beckett \par \uc2 1,317 \uc2 words\par \uc2 18 July 2024\par 15:33 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 JD Vance\u8217\'20\'19s addressed an enamored audience that chanted his name and a ringing silence on the topic of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 Republicans had a new chant on Wednesday night: not just \u8220\'20\'1CTrump! Trump!\u8221\'20\'1D but also \u8220\'20\'1CJD! JD! JD!\u8221\'20\'1D in honor of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s new vice-presidential pick, Ohio senator JD Vance, who introduced himself to the country Wednesday night in a confident and personal primetime address.\par \par \uc2 Also new: the professionally printed signs reading \u8220\'20\'1CMass Deportations Now,\u8221\'20\'1D a reference to Trump\u8217\'20\'19s campaign pledge to engage in the biggest mass deportation of undocumented migrants in US history.\par \par \uc2 Here are five key takeaways from the night:\par \par \uc2 Republicans are simply not talking about \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 During his race for the US senate in Ohio, Vance said that he did not support {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/16/jd-vance-abortion-rights-groups"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 rape and incest exceptions}}}\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans. In 2022, he {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2024/07/17/politics/kfile-jd-vance-abortion-comments/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  he \u8220\'20\'1Cwould like \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  to be illegal nationally\u8221\'20\'1D, expressing sympathy for the view that a national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban was necessary to stop women from traveling to different states in order to get abortions.\par \par \uc2 A section on Vance\u8217\'20\'19s Senate website, accessible as late as Monday, read, simply, \u8220\'20\'1CEnd \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D calling him \u8220\'20\'1C100% pro-life\u8221\'20\'1D, a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/jbendery/status/1813614058668716218"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 HuffPost reporter noted}}}\uc2 . By Wednesday, that message had vanished, as Vance\u8217\'20\'19s old website simply redirected to Trump\u8217\'20\'19s presidential campaign site.\par \par \uc2 Vance similarly erased his anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  views from his primetime speech to the RNC on Wednesday, and as my colleagues have noted, he\u8217\'20\'19s far from alone. There\u8217\'20\'19s been a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jul/17/rnc-jd-vance-speech-trump-day-3-live-updates?page=with:block-669875068f081a868efc7ddf#block-669875068f081a868efc7ddf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 conspicuous silence}}}\uc2  on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  throughout the Republican convention, as well as on other issues that Republicans appear to see as weaknesses, like Project 2025 and the future of American democracy.\par \par \uc2 Warm reaction to Vance\u8217\'20\'19s bestselling life story, as \u8216\'20\'18hillbilly\u8217\'20\'19 aims for White House\par \par \uc2 The Republican national convention crowd was already eating out of Vance\u8217\'20\'19s hand, as the charismatic 39-year-old Ohio senator talked them through the life story that made him into the bestselling author of Hillbilly Elegy, a 2016 memoir that became a 2020 feature film starring Amy Adams and Glenn Close.\par \par \uc2 Vance had described growing up \u8220\'20\'1Ca working-class boy born far from the halls of power\u8221\'20\'1D in Middletown, Ohio, with a single mother who struggled with addiction, and a tough, loving grandmother who kept him from falling prey to a local drug dealer. He described his journey from the Marine Corps, to Yale, to working in venture capital, to being chosen as Trump\u8217\'20\'19s vice-presidential pick.\par \par \uc2 He neatly contrasted his youth to Biden\u8217\'20\'19s age, noting policies Biden supported when he was in high school, and saying: \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has been a politician in Washington for longer than I\u8217\'20\'19ve been alive.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Then, talking about other single mothers like his, who had struggled with addiction but never given up, he revealed that his mother, Beverly Aikins, was in the RNC audience with him, and that she is \u8220\'20\'1C10 years clean and sober\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI love you, mom,\u8221\'20\'1D he said, suggesting that she might he able to celebrate her full 10 years of sobriety next year in the White House.\par \par \uc2 As the cameras panned to Vance\u8217\'20\'19s smiling mother, she mouthed, \u8220\'20\'1CThat\u8217\'20\'19s my boy! That\u8217\'20\'19s my boy!\u8221\'20\'1D And the crowd started chanting, \u8220\'20\'1CJD\u8217\'20\'19s mom! JD\u8217\'20\'19s mom!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s clear that JD\u8217\'20\'19s job is to woo the rust belt\par \par \uc2 Vance shouted out to his home state of Ohio in his speech, but he quickly cut off the chants of \u8220\'20\'1CO-H-I-O,\u8221\'20\'1D quipping, \u8220\'20\'1CWe gotta win Michigan too.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 His speech was threaded with references to rust belt states like Pennsylvania, Michigan and Kentucky, which he connected to the struggles of his Ohio hometown, and to the importance of restoring American factories and American manufacturing.\par \par \uc2 Vance described a series of economic and foreign policy choices Biden made over his long career that, he argued, hurt American workers, particularly those in towns like he grew up in. Some {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/TomCruise/status/1674062557517168643?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw%7Ctwcamp%5Etweetembed%7Ctwterm%5E1674062557517168643%7Ctwgr%5Ea0158578ce8442acd8e1a3e78d786653bdd99b80%7Ctwcon%5Es1_&ref_url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.vanityfair.com%2Fhollywood%2F2023%2F07%2Ftom-cruise-is-seeing-both-barbie-and-oppenheimer-but-which-one-first"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 observers }}}\uc2  saw the speech as a rewriting of Vance\u8217\'20\'19s own life narrative, shifting from Hillbilly Elegy\u8217\'20\'19s preoccupation with Appalachian poverty\u8217\'20\'19s connection to cultural problems and personal responsibility, to instead blaming politician \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  for creating the conditions that left the people he grew up with, impoverished.\par \par \uc2 Strikingly, Vance came onstage to the country twang of Merle Haggard\u8217\'20\'19s 2005 protest ballad, America First, which expressed the singer\u8217\'20\'19s opposition to the Iraq war.\par \par \uc2 Republicans highlighted grief and anger over the chaotic withdrawal from Afghanistan in 2021\par \par \uc2 Some of the family members of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/aug/28/us-military-killed-kabul-names"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the 13 soldiers killed}}}\uc2  in an Islamic State terrorist attack at Kabul airport during the \u8220\'20\'1Cdisastrous\u8221\'20\'1D US withdrawal from Afghanistan spoke at the RNC to criticize Biden.\par \par \uc2 Alicia Lopez, whose son, Corporal Hunter Lopez, was killed on 26 August 2021, said: \u8220\'20\'1CDespite our pleas for answers and accountability, they have pushed us away and tried to silence us. The Biden administration has not owned up to the bad decisions, they have not been transparent about their failures and their so-called leaders work to protect themselves, rather than our sons and daughters who took the oath to defend our country.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 A mother-in-law of a marine killed at Abbey Gate said that Trump, in contrast, had spent dedicated time with family members, offering them what she felt was genuine support in their grief. The family members were also featured in a video in which they said that when they met with Biden as their loved ones\u8217\'20\'19 bodies arrived at a military base in Delaware, the president appeared to check his watch during the ceremony.\par \par \uc2 Other pro-Trump veterans also spoke to the lasting sense of anger and betrayal they felt in witnessing the US withdrawal from Afghanistan, and in the struggles and fears of the Afghans they had worked with who were left behind as the \uc2 Taliban\uc2  seized control of the country.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThroughout our careers, we never had regrets about our service, but this moral injury caused many of us to ask: \u8216\'20\'18Why did we serve, if this was the outcome?\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D Scott Neil, a retired green beret, said.\par \par \uc2 A {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jun/30/us-afghanistan-war-military-pullout-report-biden-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 scathing state department review}}}\uc2  of the military withdrawal from Afghanistan concluded that both the Trump and Biden administrations were to blame as \u8220\'20\'1Cduring both administrations there was insufficient senior-level consideration of worst-case scenarios and how quickly those might follow\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 But the RNC\u8217\'20\'19s focus on the withdrawal also took aim at one of Biden\u8217\'20\'19s political strengths. As someone who has lost family members to a car accident and cancer, he has often been praised for his ability to grieve with people, and offer them support in moments of profound loss, even being referred to as \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nybooks.com/articles/2020/01/16/joe-biden-designated-mourner/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the designated mourner}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D. But on Wednesday, the RNC offered multiple speakers who portrayed Trump as the man who would comfort Americans in their grief and Biden as a self-involved politician.\par \par \uc2 Chants of \u8220\'20\'1CBring them home\u8221\'20\'1D as parents of 7 October hostage speak\par \par \uc2 Orna and Ronen Neutra, whose son, Omer Neutra, was kidnapped during the 7 October attack in Israel, said Trump had supported them, asked the RNC for continued support in securing their son\u8217\'20\'19s safe return. Omer is one of eight American hostages, Ronen Neutra said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CPresident Trump called us personally right after the attack, when Omer was taken captive,\u8221\'20\'1D Ronen Neutra said. \u8220\'20\'1CWe know he stands with the American hostages. We need our beautiful son back and we need your support. We need your support to end this crisis and bring all the hostages back home.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Shabbos Kestenbaum, a recent {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.thecrimson.com/article/2024/7/18/nekritz-RNC-jewish-perspective/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Harvard Divinity School student}}}\uc2  who was part of a group of students who {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.thecrimson.com/article/2024/7/16/harvard-student-sued-republican-convention/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 filed a lawsuit}}}\uc2  alleging that Harvard failed to address antisemitism on campus, also spoke, as did members of a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://abc11.com/post/unc-fraternity-brothers-held-american-flag-among-speakers/15056045/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 University of North Carolina fraternity}}}\uc2  who held up an American flag during a pro-Palestine campus protest.\par \par \uc2 Chris Stein and Carter Sherman contributed reporting\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240718ek7i000p2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
