\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 JD Vance tells Republican convention \u8216\'20\'18people who govern this country have failed and failed again\u8217\'20\'19 \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Chris Stein in Milwaukee (now); Joanna Walters and Fran Lawther (earlier) \par \uc2 8,217 \uc2 words\par \uc2 18 July 2024\par 05:02 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 This live blog is now closed. You can read some of our latest stories on the \uc2 RNC\uc2  below:JD Vance fires salvos at Democrats in first speech as Trump\u8217\'20\'19s running mateWho is Usha Vance, wife of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s running mate?\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.40am BST\par \par \uc2 Hundreds of people who gathered to remember the former fire chief fatally shot at a rally for former President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  have been urged to find \u8220\'20\'1Cunity\u8221\'20\'1D as the area in rural Pennsylvania seeks to recover.\par \par \uc2 Wednesday\u8217\'20\'19s public event was the first of two organized to memorialize and celebrate Corey Comperatore\u8217\'20\'19s life, with the second to happen Thursday.\par \par \uc2 A sign outside Lernerville Speedway in Sarver, where the vigil for Corey Comperatore was held Wednesday, night read: \u8220\'20\'1CRest in Peace Corey, Thank You For Your Service,\u8221\'20\'1D with the logo of his fire company. The 50-year-old died Saturday during an attempt to kill Trump at the rally in Butler, Pennsylvania.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.04am BST\par \par \uc2 At the Republic national convention in Milwaukee, some Trump supporters have a new way of showing their support for their favorite presidential candidate beyond a red Maga cap: wearing bandages on their ears, as \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  did himself when he first appeared at the convention on Monday in his first public appearance since Saturday\u8217\'20\'19s assassination attempt.\par \par \uc2 Our video editors have put together this report on this new trend:\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.54am BST\par \par \uc2 What we learned on night three of the Republican national convention\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 JD Vance {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jul/17/rnc-jd-vance-speech-trump-day-3-live-updates?page=with:block-669883c38f08d8344a28f5b2#block-669883c38f08d8344a28f5b2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 accepted}}}\uc2  the GOP\u8217\'20\'19s nomination as vice-president with a speech where he harkened back to his Ohio upbringing to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jul/17/rnc-jd-vance-speech-trump-day-3-live-updates?page=with:block-669885e28f08d8344a28f5bc#block-669885e28f08d8344a28f5bc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 condemn}}}\uc2  the past US leaders who \u8220\'20\'1Chave failed and failed again\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Vance said: \u8220\'20\'1CAs always, America\u8217\'20\'19s ruling class wrote the checks, communities like mine paid the price. For decades that divide between the few with their power and comfort in Washington and the rest of us only widened. From Iraq to Afghanistan, from the financial crisis to the Great Recession, from open borders to stagnating wages, the people who govern this country have failed and failed again.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jul/17/rnc-jd-vance-speech-trump-day-3-live-updates?page=with:block-66986cb78f08155bce435d57#block-66986cb78f08155bce435d57"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Reports}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jul/17/rnc-jd-vance-speech-trump-day-3-live-updates?page=with:block-66988c3a8f08155bce435e05#block-66988c3a8f08155bce435e05"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 emerged}}}\uc2  that three of the most powerful Democrats in Washington \u8211\'20\'13 the Senate majority leader \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2 , the House minority leader \uc2 Hakeem Jeffries\uc2  and the former House speaker \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 have told \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  he cannot win the election.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The White House {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jul/17/rnc-jd-vance-speech-trump-day-3-live-updates?page=with:block-66986f638f081a868efc7dbd#block-66986f638f081a868efc7dbd"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  Biden told Jeffries and Schumer, in reply, that \u8220\'20\'1Che is the nominee of the party\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 a sign he won\u8217\'20\'19t drop out, at least not yet.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump Jr\uc2  is known for incendiary commentary. In his speech to the convention, he {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jul/17/rnc-jd-vance-speech-trump-day-3-live-updates?page=with:block-66987bc98f08155bce435da6#block-66987bc98f08155bce435da6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 was somber}}}\uc2  at first, before reverting to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jul/17/rnc-jd-vance-speech-trump-day-3-live-updates?page=with:block-66987cb18f08d8344a28f57c#block-66987cb18f08d8344a28f57c"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 his usual}}}\uc2  fire breathing self.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Relatives of some of the 13 US soldiers killed in an Islamic State attack during the chaotic pullout from Afghanistan in 2021 staged {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jul/17/rnc-jd-vance-speech-trump-day-3-live-updates?page=with:block-669872878f08155bce435d77#block-669872878f08155bce435d77"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 an emotional denunciation}}}\uc2  of Biden.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Things {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jul/17/rnc-jd-vance-speech-trump-day-3-live-updates?page=with:block-669875068f081a868efc7ddf#block-669875068f081a868efc7ddf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 we did not hear}}}\uc2  much, if anything, about at the convention: \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , democracy and Project 2025.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Republican delegates{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jul/17/rnc-jd-vance-speech-trump-day-3-live-updates?page=with:block-66985fbc8f08155bce435d2a#block-66985fbc8f08155bce435d2a"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 shrugged off}}}\uc2  the possibility of Biden stepping aside for a more electable Democratic candidate.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Peter Navarro\uc2  got out of prison, and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jul/17/rnc-jd-vance-speech-trump-day-3-live-updates?page=with:block-669855678f08d8344a28f4b5#block-669855678f08d8344a28f4b5"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 was on}}}\uc2  the convention stage not long after.\par \par \uc2 Thanks for reading our live coverage of the third night of the Republican national convention.\par \par \uc2 Delegates are back in Milwaukee\u8217\'20\'19s Fiserv Forum tomorrow at 5.45pm CT for the convention\u8217\'20\'19s last evening, when \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is scheduled to speak, and accept the party\u8217\'20\'19s presidential nomination.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.06am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.34am BST\par \par \uc2 The third night of the Republican national convention concludes.\par \par \uc2 And we\u8217\'20\'19re done.\par \par \uc2 Chair Michael Whatley has brought the gavel down, and the third night of the Republican national convention is finished.\par \par \uc2 Only one more to go.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.38am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.32am BST\par \par \uc2 Pelosi warned Biden he cannot beat Trump \u8211\'20\'13 report\par \par \uc2 But how much longer will it be called the Biden-Harris campaign?\par \par \uc2 CNN reports that \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2 , the Democratic former House speaker who is one of the lawmakers closest to \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , warned him that he could not defeat \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , and if the president continued his re-election bid, Democrats may fail to retake the House:\par \par \uc2 enltrExclusive CNN reporting: Former House Speaker \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  privately told President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  in a recent conversation that polling shows that the president cannot defeat \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and that the president could destroy Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 chances of winning the House. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/mj_lee?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @mj_lee}}}\uc2  \u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Abby D. Phillip (@abbydphillip) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/abbydphillip/status/1813773643203117369?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 18, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 It had been speculated that if Pelosi tells Biden it\u8217\'20\'19s over, the president will listen. We will find out if that ends up being the case.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.37am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.29am BST\par \par \uc2 'It\u8217\'20\'19s working families and the middle class who will suffer' from Vance's policies, Biden campaign warns\par \par \uc2 The Biden campaign quickly issued a statement bashing JD Vance right after he got off stage, linking him to Project 2025, the rightwing blueprint to remake the \uc2 US government\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Vance did not mention the plan in his speech, which was generally light on policy proposals.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTonight, JD Vance, the poster boy for Project 2025, took center stage. But it\u8217\'20\'19s working families and the middle class who will suffer if he\u8217\'20\'19s allowed to stay there,\u8221\'20\'1D Michael Tyler, the Biden-Harris communications manager, said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBacked by Silicon Valley and the billionaires who bought his vice-presidential selection, Vance is Project 2025 in human form \u8211\'20\'13 an agenda that puts extremism and the ultra-wealthy over our democracy. An agenda that cuts healthcare, bans \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , slashes Social Security and Medicare and is a rubber stamp for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  to become a dictator on \u8216\'20\'18day one\u8217\'20\'19 and \u8216\'20\'18terminate\u8217\'20\'19 our constitution as he wishes.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Tyler concluded: \u8220\'20\'1CJD Vance is unprepared, unqualified and willing to do anything \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  demands.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.37am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.25am BST\par \par \uc2 After his speech finished, Vance was joined onstage by several relatives, who he shared hugs and handshakes with.\par \par \uc2 As they walked off stage, Vance appeared to pause and point to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , who is seated across the arena.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.29am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.24am BST\par \par \uc2 Vance tells US: 'I will give you everything I have to serve you'\par \par \uc2 After a recitation of why he believes America is special, JD Vance then told the audience that re-electing \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  was essential to preserving that greatness.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe only thing that we need to do right now, the most important thing that we can do for those people, for that American nation that we all love, is to re-elect \uc2 Donald J Trump\uc2  president of the United States,\u8221\'20\'1D Vance said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMr President, I will never take for granted the trust you have put in me and what an honor it is to help achieve the extraordinary vision that you have for this country. Now, I pledge to every American, no matter your party, I will give you everything I have to serve you and to make this country a place where every dream you have for yourself, your family and your country will be possible once again.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.28am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.14am BST\par \par \uc2 When \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  selected JD Vance, word spread that the choice was made in part because his campaign believed the Ohio senator could sway voters in the rust belt swing states, like Michigan and Pennsylvania.\par \par \uc2 And in his speech tonight, Vance has mentioned those states repeatedly.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re done buying energy from countries that hate us. We\u8217\'20\'19re going to get it right here, from American workers in Pennsylvania and Ohio and across the country,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.21am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.11am BST\par \par \uc2 JD Vance told the crowd how, after his grandmother, who he called Mamaw, died in 2005, they found \u8220\'20\'1C19 loaded handguns\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe thing is that they were stashed all over her house, under her bed, in her closet, in the silverware drawer and we wondered what was going on,\u8221\'20\'1D Vance said. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd it occurred to us that towards the end of her life, Mamaw couldn\u8217\'20\'19t get around so well, and so this frail old woman made sure that no matter where she was, she was within arm\u8217\'20\'19s length of whatever she needed to protect her family. That\u8217\'20\'19s who we fight for. That\u8217\'20\'19s the American spirit.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The praise of gun ownership pleased the crowd, which broke into the familiar chant: \u8220\'20\'1CUSA! USA! USA!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.19am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.07am BST\par \par \uc2 This is an audience that clearly enjoys compliments.\par \par \uc2 After a line about how \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is willing to buy energy from tin-pot dictators across the world when he could buy it from his own citizens, right here in our own country\u8221\'20\'1D drew applause, JD Vance remarked, \u8220\'20\'1CYou guys are a great crowd.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Then the crowd started chanting, \u8220\'20\'1CYes we are! Yes we are! Yes we are!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.11am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.05am BST\par \par \uc2 'The people who govern this country have failed and failed again', Vance tells Republicans\par \par \uc2 Turning again to the trials of his Ohio hometown, JD Vance argued that repeated administrations had failed it \u8211\'20\'13 until \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  came along.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMy friends, things did not work out well for a lot of kids I grew up with. Every now and then, I will get a call from a relative back home, who asks, did you know so and so? And I\u8217\'20\'19ll remember a face from years ago, and then I\u8217\'20\'19ll hear they died of an overdose,\u8221\'20\'1D Vance said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAs always, America\u8217\'20\'19s ruling class wrote the checks, communities like mine paid the price. For decades that divide between the few with their power and comfort in Washington and the rest of us only widened. From Iraq to Afghanistan, from the financial crisis to the Great Recession, from open borders to stagnating wages, the people who govern this country have failed and failed again.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 And then: \u8220\'20\'1CThat is, of course, until a guy named \uc2 Donald J Trump\uc2  came along. President Trump represents America\u8217\'20\'19s last best hope to restore what, if lost, may never be found again.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.09am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.01am BST\par \par \uc2 JD Vance then turned to his tough childhood in Ohio and found a way to blame both \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and, obliquely, two Republican former presidents.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNow, never in my wildest imagination, could I have believed that I\u8217\'20\'19d be standing here tonight,\u8221\'20\'1D the senator said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI grew up in Middletown, Ohio, a small town where people spoke their minds, built with their hands and loved their God, their family, their community and their country with their whole hearts. But it was also a place that had been cast aside and forgotten by America\u8217\'20\'19s ruling class in Washington. When I was in the fourth grade, a career politician by the name of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  supported Nafta, a bad trade deal that sent countless good jobs to Mexico,\u8221\'20\'1D Vance said, neglecting Republican president \uc2 George HW Bush\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s role in getting the trade deal passed.\par \par \uc2 Then, he turned his attack on the Iraq war, which was a project of Republican president \uc2 George W Bush\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhen I was a senior in high school, that same \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  supported the disastrous invasion of Iraq, and at each step of the way in small towns like mine, in Ohio or next door in Pennsylvania or Michigan, in states all across our country, jobs were sent overseas and our children were sent to war,\u8221\'20\'1D Vance said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.05am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.55am BST\par \par \uc2 Vance accepts Trump's nomination as running mate\par \par \uc2 JD Vance made official his acceptance of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s offer to be his vice-president, if he returns to the White House.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CShouldn\u8217\'20\'19t we be governed by a party that is unafraid to debate ideas and come to the best solution? That\u8217\'20\'19s the Republican party of the next four years, united in our love for this country and committed to free speech and the open exchange of ideas. And so, tonight, Mr Chairman, I stand here humbled, and I\u8217\'20\'19m overwhelmed with gratitude to say I officially accept your nomination to be vice-president of the United States of America,\u8221\'20\'1D Vance said.\par \par \uc2 Applause followed, as did chants of: \u8220\'20\'1CJD! JD! JD!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.59am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.53am BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  did indeed call for unity after the attempted assassination \u8211\'20\'13 and for that, he deserves credit, JD Vance is arguing.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNow, consider what they said. They said he was a tyrant. They said he must be stopped at all costs. But how did he respond? He called for national unity, for national calm, literally right after an assassin nearly took his life,\u8221\'20\'1D Vance said.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.51am BST\par \par \uc2 Vance has made the attempted assassination the backbone of his speech thus far.\par \par \uc2 Speaking of Trump, the Ohio senator said: \u8220\'20\'1CPrior to running for president, he was one of the most successful businessmen in the world. He had everything anyone could ever want in a life. And yet, instead of choosing the easy path, he chose to endure abuse, slander and persecution, and he did it because he loves this country.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI want all Americans to go and watch the video of a would-be assassin coming a quarter of an inch from taking his life,\u8221\'20\'1D Vance said. \u8220\'20\'1CConsider the lies they told you about \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , and then look at that photo of him defiant, fist in the air. When \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  rose to his feet in that Pennsylvania field, all of America stood with him.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 As the crowd clapped, Trump smiled from his seat in the VIP section. Usha Vance was seated to his right.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.57am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.49am BST\par \par \uc2 JD Vance began his remarks by looking back on the attempted assassination of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  on Saturday.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAs we meet tonight, we cannot forget that this evening could have been so much different. Instead of a day of celebration, this could have been a day of heartache and mourning,\u8221\'20\'1D Vance said.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.46am BST\par \par \uc2 JD Vance was introduced by his wife, Usha Vance, who said of her husband : \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s hard to imagine a more powerful example of the American dream.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CRaised by his grandmother through tough times, chosen to help lead our country through some of its greatest challenges. I am grateful to all of you for the trust you\u8217\'20\'19ve placed in him and in our family,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 And with that, her husband arrived on stage.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.57am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.45am BST\par \par \uc2 JD Vance takes stage at Republican convention\par \par \uc2 Ohio senator JD Vance is about to make his first speech since \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  picked him as his running mate on Monday.\par \par \uc2 He has previously spoken {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/16/jd-vance-abortion-rights-groups"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in favor}}}\uc2  of a national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/17/trump-jd-vance-vp-ukraine#:~:text=In%20public%2C%20Vance%20has%20criticized,to%20actually%20finish%20the%20job%E2%80%9D."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 criticized}}}\uc2  military aid to Ukraine. We\u8217\'20\'19ll see if he hits on those themes in his speech.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.41am BST\par \par \uc2 We are now seeing on the arena Jumbotron a video recalling JD Vance\u8217\'20\'19s background.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s nothing short of a miracle that JD Vance is a household name,\u8221\'20\'1D the narrator said, recalling how Vance was \u8220\'20\'1Cborn into poverty\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CJD Vance\u8217\'20\'19s story is one of perseverance, of duty, of commitment to what\u8217\'20\'19s right. It\u8217\'20\'19s an American story, and it\u8217\'20\'19s just getting started,\u8221\'20\'1D the video concluded.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.46am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.39am BST\par \par \uc2 Up next on the schedule is Usha Vance, wife of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s running mate, JD Vance.\par \par \uc2 Usha Vance was, at one point, a registered Democrat, yet here she is, set to address the Republican national convention. Here\u8217\'20\'19s more about her, from the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/davidsmith"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 David Smith}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/17/who-is-usha-vance-jd-vance-wife"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Who is Usha Vance, the Indian American lawyer married to JD Vance?}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.36am BST\par \par \uc2 As he wrapped up his speech, \uc2 Donald Trump Jr\uc2  hit on the theme, adopted by others at this convention including House speaker Mike Johnson, that this election was a choice between two visions of the country.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis November, we have a choice. It\u8217\'20\'19s a choice between one team that wants to build this country up, and another that wants to tear this country down. It\u8217\'20\'19s a choice between people who are proud of America and people who are ashamed of America. And ultimately, it\u8217\'20\'19s a choice between America last and America first,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump Jr said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSo, if you love this country from the bottom of your heart, if you want to bring back common sense, if you want to save the American dream, if you want to stand up and fight for the future of our nation, you must re-elect my father, \uc2 Donald J Trump\uc2 .\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.40am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.33am BST\par \par \uc2 Senators confront Secret Service director at Republican convention\par \par \uc2 Tennessee senator \uc2 Marsha Blackburn\uc2  has posted a video that appears to show her and Wyoming senator \uc2 John Barrasso\uc2  confronting Kimberly Cheatle, the Secret Service director, in the halls of the Fiserv Forum, where the Republican national convention is taking place.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is exactly what you were doing today on the call, stonewalling,\u8221\'20\'1D Barrasso yells at Cheatle in the video:\par \par \uc2 enltrThe American people deserve answers from the Secret Service. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/PNFF11v00Q"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/PNFF11v00Q}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Marsha Blackburn\uc2  (@VoteMarsha) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/VoteMarsha/status/1813754599276413035?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 18, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s a sign of how the GOP is training its ire on Cheatle, amid questions over whether the Secret Service properly arranged security for Trump during his ill-fated rally in Pennsylvania.\par \par \uc2 We did not personally witness the confrontation, but are sure to hear plenty more about it in the days to come.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.37am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.28am BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump Jr\uc2  leaned further into inflammatory rhetoric, casting the Democratic party and the media as collaborators who have teamed up to dupe the American people on issues like crime, immigration and democracy.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe lies, oh yeah the lies,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump Jr said, denouncing the press for lying \u8220\'20\'1Cnonstop about my father\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s a stark escalation and departure from the message of unity that the Trump campaign briefly signaled it would adopt in the wake of the assassination attempt on the former president on Saturday.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey could only run away from reality for so long,\u8221\'20\'1D said Trump Jr. \u8220\'20\'1CAll hell has broken loose in America.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.33am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.27am BST\par \par \uc2 And with that out of the way, \uc2 Donald Trump Jr\uc2  is back to spitting the venom for which he has become {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/oct/31/donald-trump-jr-misinformation-memes-paul-pelosi-hammer"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 so well known}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CRemember Build Back Better?\u8221\'20\'1D Trump Jr asked, referring to \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/oct/18/what-is-build-back-better-crash-course"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 proposed overhaul}}}\uc2  of US social services. \u8220\'20\'1CInstead, we got broke, bumbling Biden. Nothing is built, nothing is back and nothing is better.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 What followed was six sentences that were as good a distillation of modern American conservatism as any:\par \par \uc2 Bridges are collapsing, our credibility is crumbling, and our money is worth less and less every single day. It was just one giant bait and switch, and normal Americans are the ones left holding the bag. Housing costs, gasoline prices, grocery bills just keep going up, wave after wave of illegal aliens, deadly drugs keep pouring across our border.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, pro-crime district attorneys have turned our cities into giant crime zones. They\u8217\'20\'19ve turned criminals into victims, prosecutors into criminal defense attorneys and police into public enemies. Leftwing activists are pretending to be educators, teaching our kids that there are 57 genders, but they can\u8217\'20\'19t even define what a woman is.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.21am BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump Jr\uc2  says 'we came millimeters away from one of the darkest moments in our nation's history'\par \par \uc2 Continuing the somewhat sober tone, \uc2 Donald Trump Jr\uc2  remarked on how close his father came to assassination at his rally in Pennsylvania on Saturday.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMy father came under literal fire as an incredible, patriotic rally turned into a tragedy on a field in Butler, Pennsylvania,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump Jr said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CA brave firefighter died, others were injured, and as those bullets rained down, we came millimeters away from one of the darkest moments in our nation\u8217\'20\'19s history. But we did lose an American hero that day. We wish that he were with us tonight, but his memory will live on forever in the hearts of his family, his community and the nation that he loved.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.19am BST\par \par \uc2 As soon as he came onstage, \uc2 Donald Trump Jr\uc2  declared: \u8220\'20\'1CBefore I begin my remarks, I\u8217\'20\'19m going to do something a little uncharacteristic: a Trump is going to give up the microphone.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Out came his daughter, Kai Madison Trump, who described how the former president is \u8220\'20\'1Cto me \u8230\'20\'26 just a normal, grandpa\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHe gets us candy and soda when our parents aren\u8217\'20\'19t looking. He always wants to know how we\u8217\'20\'19re doing in school. When I made the high honor roll, he printed it out to show his friends how proud he was of me,\u8221\'20\'1D Madison Trump said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe media makes my grandpa seem like a different person, but I know him for who he is. He\u8217\'20\'19s very caring and loving. He truly wants the best for this country, and he will fight every single day to make America great again.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s a lot like the speech \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s daughter-in-law \uc2 Lara Trump\uc2  gave last night, in which she described him as a caring father-in-law \u8211\'20\'13 perhaps a strategy by the campaign to better relate the former president to voters wary of his well-publicized antics.\par \par \uc2 Trump Jr is now back at the podium.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.12am BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump Jr\uc2  to address Republican convention\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump Jr\uc2 , the president\u8217\'20\'19s son who is a bit of a bomb thrower, is up next at the Republican national convention.\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19ll let you know what he says.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.07am BST\par \par \uc2 Chants of \u8220\'20\'1C Bring them home!\u8221\'20\'1D broke out in the arena when Orna and Ronen Neutra, whose son, Omer Neutra, was kidnapped during the 7 October attack in Israel, addressed the convention.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COmer is one of eight American hostages and one of 120 hostages. Still left in Gaza, citizens of 24 countries and five different religions, still held by \uc2 Hamas\uc2 , denied basic human needs, their lives threatened every day,\u8221\'20\'1D Ronen Neutra said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CPresident Trump called us personally right after the attack, when Omer was taken captive. We know he stands with the American hostages. We need our beautiful son back and we need your support. We need your support to end this crisis and bring all the hostages back home.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.14am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.01am BST\par \par \uc2 Words that you are unlikely to hear often at this year\u8217\'20\'19s Republican national convention: \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , democracy and Project 2025.\par \par \uc2 Speakers have generally avoided touching on what are seen as \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s biggest vulnerabilities after the 6 January 2021 insurrection and the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s decision to overturn Roe v Wade.\par \par \uc2 Ben Wikler, chair of the Democratic party of Wisconsin, said: \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s most striking what the Republicans are not talking about, that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  just blew his platform to smithereens by choosing a vice-president [JD Vance] who wants a national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban. And yet I haven\u8217\'20\'19t heard a single mention of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the stage.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CLast time Trump was in Wisconsin, he kept repeating that he had won here and the election was stolen from him and there was widespread fraud and he needed to crack down on all these different forms of voting. It\u8217\'20\'19s pretty clear that a Republican party that is still totally committed to suppressing votes and overturning elections is not making a show of that from the national stage.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Republicans addressing the convention have repeatedly accused \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  of throwing open the southern border and welcoming killers, rapists and other criminals. But studies show that immigrants commit fewer crimes than people born in the US.\par \par \uc2 Wikler, who is inside the convention hall, added: \u8220\'20\'1CThey can tell that the biggest issues in this election are actually toxic for them and so they\u8217\'20\'19re resorting to fear of immigrants and fear of crime and grisly stories to try to push the country into the arms of a strongman instead of addressing the elephant in the room.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhat that misses is that, at dinner tables across the country, people are talking about what they will do if the Republican Project 2025 actually becomes a reality and they\u8217\'20\'19re not doing anything to assuage those concerns. They\u8217\'20\'19re just pretending that they don\u8217\'20\'19t exist.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.09am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.50am BST\par \par \uc2 'They have pushed us away and tried to silence us' \u8211\'20\'13 families of US soldiers killed in Afghanistan condemn Biden\par \par \uc2 The Republican national convention just devoted a lengthy segment to recounting the messy US military withdrawal from Afghanistan under \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  three years ago, and in particular {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/aug/28/us-military-killed-kabul-names"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the 13 soldiers killed}}}\uc2  in an Islamic State terrorist attack at Kabul airport.\par \par \uc2 It began with a video in which the families of the soldiers described their lost loved ones, then recounted how, when they met with Biden as their bodies arrived at a military base in Delaware, the president appeared to check his watch during the ceremony. The families then came onstage to encourage viewers to vote Biden out of office.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COur son, Corporal Hunter Lopez, whose name \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has refused to say out loud, was killed on August 26, 2021,\u8221\'20\'1D said Lopez\u8217\'20\'19s mother, Alicia Lopez. \u8220\'20\'1CHe died during \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s disastrous withdrawal from Afghanistan.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Referring to the Biden administration, Lopez said:\par \par \uc2 Despite our pleas for answers and accountability, they have pushed us away and tried to silence us. The Biden administration has not owned up to the bad decisions, they have not been transparent about their failures and their so-called leaders work to protect themselves, rather than our sons and daughters who took the oath to defend our country.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.06am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.30am BST\par \par \uc2 Biden told Schumer and Jeffries 'he is the nominee of the party' \u8211\'20\'13 spokesperson\par \par \uc2 Responding to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/2024/07/17/jeffries-schumer-biden-hurting-democrats/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Washington Post\u8217\'20\'19s report}}}\uc2  that the Senate\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic leader \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  and House minority leader \uc2 Hakeem Jeffries\uc2  warned \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  that his candidacy will imperil their efforts to control Congress, White House spokesman Andrew Bates indicated Biden had no intention of stepping aside.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe President told both leaders he is the nominee of the party, he plans to win and looks forward to working with both of them to pass his 100 days agenda to help working families,\u8221\'20\'1D Bates said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.33am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.26am BST\par \par \uc2 Top congressional Democrats warn Biden his candidacy jeopardizes their chances of retaking majority - report\par \par \uc2 Hakeem Jeffries\uc2 , the Democratic House minority leader, warned \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  that if he continues his bid for re-election, it will be difficult for his party to retake the majority in Congress\u8217\'20\'19s lower chamber, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/2024/07/17/jeffries-schumer-biden-hurting-democrats/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Washington Post reports}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2 , the Senate majority leader, delivered a similarly dire message to Biden about Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 chances of holding on to the majority in that chamber, the Post reported. The top lawmakers\u8217\'20\'19 comments to the president are the latest sign of the pressure Biden is facing to reconsider his bid for another four years following his disastrous performance in his debate against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more on the conversations, from the Post:\par \par \uc2 In a separate one-on-one conversation, a person close to Biden told the president directly that he should end his candidacy, saying that was the only way to preserve his legacy and save the country from another Trump term, the person said. Biden responded that he adamantly disagreed with that opinion and that he is the best candidate to defeat {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/donald-trump/?itid=lk_inline_manual_5"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2 . The person spoke on the condition of anonymity to describe a private conversation.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.30am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.18am BST\par \par \uc2 A rare creature is roaming Milwaukee. It is the Lesser Spotted Establishment Republican, namely Asa Hutchinson, the former governor of Arkansas.\par \par \uc2 At a Republican national convention that has gone full Maga, totally devoted to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , the dissenting Hutchinson represents the last of a dying breed.\par \par \uc2 But even this hardened Trump critic, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/jan/14/asa-hutchinson-presidential-race-republican-party"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 who ran a quixotic campaign}}}\uc2  against him in this year\u8217\'20\'19s Republican primary election, praised the way the former US president reacted to an attempt on his life last Saturday.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI very much admired what he did,\u8221\'20\'1D Hutchinson told the Guardian. \u8220\'20\'1CIt was one of those moments where his reaction was others and what this means to America and our democracy.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHe showed strength and that impressed me, obviously, but also how he handled afterwards and said this is a time we\u8217\'20\'19ve got to tone down the rhetoric some, the harshness. I applaud him for that and it\u8217\'20\'19s to a certain extent demonstrated at the convention. But we\u8217\'20\'19ll see how long that lasts.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The former governor stopped short of backing Trump, however. \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19ll just keep my options open. I didn\u8217\'20\'19t come here to endorse anyone. I haven\u8217\'20\'19t been asked for it and so I\u8217\'20\'19ll keep my powder dry.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Hutchinson did have some advice for Democrats dithering over whether to ditch \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  as their nominee, however. \u8220\'20\'1CYou got to switch. You got to roll the dice. Take a chance on somebody else. It\u8217\'20\'19s strength versus weakness. Strength wins every time.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.05am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.06am BST\par \par \uc2 This evening, Republican convention attendees have been given a sign with a message we had not seen in the past two nights: \u8220\'20\'1CMass deportation now!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s an indication that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  believes campaigning on hardline immigration policies will get him to the White House. He has previously vowed that \u8220\'20\'1Con day one, we will begin the largest domestic deportation operation in American history\u8221\'20\'1D. Here\u8217\'20\'19s more about that:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/may/03/trump-mass-deportations-detention-camps-military-migrants"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Mass deportations, detention camps, troops on the street: Trump spells out migrant plan}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.07am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.57am BST\par \par \uc2 Trump returns to Republican convention hall for third night\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , his right ear still bandaged from the assassination attempt on Saturday, is back in the arena where the Republican national convention is being held.\par \par \uc2 The former president walked out and pumped his fist to the crowd, to rapturous cheers. It\u8217\'20\'19s A Man\u8217\'20\'19s Man\u8217\'20\'19s Man\u8217\'20\'19s World by James Brown is playing on the PA.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.02am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.55am BST\par \par \uc2 Republican delegates shrug off possibility of Biden stepping aside\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  up, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  down.\par \par \uc2 That, in a nutshell, has been the theme of this Republican national convention, where speakers have spent their time relentlessly attacking the Democratic president, and occasionally vice-president \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 But what if Biden {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/17/voters-concerned-biden-age-presidential-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 bows to the pressure from his party}}}\uc2  to end his re-election bid after his uneven performance in the first debate against Trump, and makes way for a younger candidate, perhaps someone who has more luck rallying Democrats? Do the delegates gathered in Milwaukee for the convention fear that could make Trump\u8217\'20\'19s road back to the White House more treacherous?\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s US politics live blog took to the floor of the convention hall to hear their answers.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe real problem Democrats are facing is there really is only one other candidate they can run, and that\u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D said Blake Marnell, a California delegate. The San Diego resident was wearing an orange suit with a brick pattern, which he said was \u8220\'20\'1Ca metaphor for strong borders, which he had under president Trump, and which \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  reversed\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Harris, a former senator from his home state, was \u8220\'20\'1Ca disaster\u8221\'20\'1D, he said.\par \par \uc2 Clayton Manthorpe, a delegate from the president\u8217\'20\'19s home state of Delaware, said the Democrats \u8220\'20\'1Cdon\u8217\'20\'19t really have a strong candidate besides \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , and I\u8217\'20\'19m not saying he\u8217\'20\'19s a good candidate\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHe\u8217\'20\'19s a stubborn old man,\u8221\'20\'1D Manthorpe continued. \u8220\'20\'1CNobody wants to be told: \u8216\'20\'18You can\u8217\'20\'19t be president of the United States.\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 But Manthorpe, a self-described \u8220\'20\'1Cconspiracy theorist\u8221\'20\'1D, referred to the announcement this evening that the president had Covid-19 as potentially setting up a narrative Biden could use to step aside.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf Trump\u8217\'20\'19s not going out by the bullet, something has to change on the other side of the equation,\u8221\'20\'1D Manthorpe said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.04am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.46am BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and his allies have increasingly flung accusations that they engage in authoritarian rhetoric and behavior back at Democrats.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAt home, Biden is acting like a dictator,\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 Doug Burgum\uc2 , the North Dakota governor, told the Republican convention on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 Trump, who has said he would be a \u8220\'20\'1Cdictator on day one\u8221\'20\'1D if re-elected has already {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://january6th-benniethompson.house.gov/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 tried to overturn}}}\uc2  a presidential election and has not committed to accepting the results of this year\u8217\'20\'19s vote.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.53am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.36am BST\par \par \uc2 Doug Burgum\uc2 , the North Dakota governor, compares Trump to 'a beautiful breeze at our back'\par \par \uc2 Doug Burgum\uc2 , the North Dakota governor who was on the shortlist to be \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s running mate, took a metaphorical tone in his remarks to the convention.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CServing as a governor with president Trump was like having a beautiful breeze at our back. He cut taxes, and cut red tape,\u8221\'20\'1D Burgum said. \u8220\'20\'1CServing as a governor under \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has been like a gale force wind in our face. Biden\u8217\'20\'19s war on energy hurts every American because the cost of energy is in everything we use or touch every day.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Much like the East Palestine mayor Trent Conaway, who spoke right before him, Burgum argued that Trump was a fighter for the working class.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CPresident Trump cares deeply about every American, rig workers, truck drivers, roughnecks and yes, America\u8217\'20\'19s great farmers and ranchers, President Trump cares deeply about you. We know that he\u8217\'20\'19ll fight for us. He\u8217\'20\'19ll fight for our families,\u8221\'20\'1D said Burgum.\par \par \uc2 In a reference to the ongoing conservative revolt against electric vehicles, Burgum added, \u8220\'20\'1CAnd we know one more thing: he\u8217\'20\'19ll let all of you keep driving your gas powered cars.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.46am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.30am BST\par \par \uc2 The saga of East Palestine, Ohio, where a \uc2 Norfolk Southern\uc2  train derailed and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jun/19/east-palestine-toxic-derailment-chemicals-spread"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 spread chemicals}}}\uc2  far and wide, gripped the country in early 2023.\par \par \uc2 More than a year later, the town\u8217\'20\'19s mayor, Trent Conaway, strolled onstage at the Republican convention to describe the Biden administration as unconcerned with his town\u8217\'20\'19s plight.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe Biden administration\u8217\'20\'19s federal response was much different. It consisted almost entirely of meetings and press events. They talked and talked, but they delivered little help,\u8221\'20\'1D Conaway told the crowd.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFor the longest time, the White House was silent and we never heard a word from vice-president Harris. I guess we weren\u8217\'20\'19t their type of folks, no Hollywood elites or Wall Street billionaires live in East Palestine, just hard-working Americans.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Conaway continued:\par \par \uc2 But \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  cared. First, he called to ask permission to visit, not wanting to intrude and then he asked how he could help. When he arrived with fresh pales of drinking water, he met with everyone from first responders to local officials and residents. He toured the derailment site, he listened to us, and he shared a meal with volunteers at a local \uc2 McDonald\u8217\'20\'19s\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 His presence was genuine. His concern was real. After a year of criticism, President Biden finally did show up. His appearance was brief, forced and scripted. He met with a select few, and then left. We needed so much, and he delivered so little.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.40am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.19am BST\par \par \uc2 Greg Abbott, the Texas governor, vows to continue bussing migrants 'until we finally secure our border'\par \par \uc2 In his speech to the Republican convention, Greg Abbott gave a strenuous and well-received defense of his state\u8217\'20\'19s forays into immigration enforcement, and vowed to keep up his {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jul/23/asylum-seekers-bus-los-angeles-texas"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 controversial practice}}}\uc2  of bussing migrants from the state to cities nationwide.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhen Biden took 50 acres of Texas border property to illegally process up to 5,000 illegal immigrants a day, I directed the Texas National Guard to take back our land and wire it shut,\u8221\'20\'1D Abbott said, in an apparent reference to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/jan/18/texas-border-access-homeland-security"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a legal clash}}}\uc2  between the state government and the Biden administration earlier this year.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNow there\u8217\'20\'19s no longer 5,000 people crossing the border like there was under \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 . Now that the National Guard wired that shut, on average, there is one illegal immigrant crossing the border at that location a day.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Both \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  have visited the US-Mexico border during their administration. Ignoring that fact, Abbott vowed:\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  refused to even come to Texas and to see the border crisis that they created. I took the border to them. I began bussing illegal immigrants to Washington DC, and we have continued bussing migrants to sanctuary cities across the entire country, and those busses will continue to roll until we finally secure our border.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.23am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.07am BST\par \par \uc2 Eric Trump\uc2  joins calls for head of Secret Service to resign\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s second eldest son, Eric, has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/17/trump-rally-shooting-cellphone-detonator"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 joined other Republicans}}}\uc2  calling for the director of the Secret Service to step aside following the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donald-trump-pennsylvania-rally-shooting"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 assassination attempt}}}\uc2  on his fatheron the weekend.\par \par \uc2 Eric Trump\uc2  sat down for an interview with Kristen Welker earlier today, the anchor of the Sunday Meet the Press politics talk show on NBC.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CPeople are calling for the resignation of the Secret Service director. Are you saying you think the Secret Service director should resign?\u8221\'20\'1D Welker asked Trump, referring to the head of the \uc2 USSS\uc2 , Kimberly Cheatle, according to a rush transcript issued by the TV network.\par \par \uc2 Eric Trump\uc2  didn\u8217\'20\'19t mince his words. \u8220\'20\'1CNo question about it. There\u8217\'20\'19s no question about it,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 He continued: \u8220\'20\'1CHow can this possibly happen? How can \u8230\'20\'26 think just what that would do, Kristen. On the world stage. If our leader, you guys were covering it, and Fox was covering it, CNN, everybody was covering it, got assassinated, took a rifle round to the head on live TV, while the entire nation \u8230\'20\'26 we\u8217\'20\'19d look like a third world country.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Trump added: \u8220\'20\'1CThis can\u8217\'20\'19t happen in the United States. And somebody\u8217\'20\'19s got be held accountable. You can\u8217\'20\'19t just sweep that kind of stuff under the rug.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.20am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.52am BST\par \par \uc2 In pantomime style, Navarro is delivering lines to the \uc2 RNC\uc2  crowd designed to attract lots of boos as well as cheers. No audible hissing yet.\par \par \uc2 Navarro has railed against his conviction and is spinning the line further that the US justice system is \u8220\'20\'1Cout to get\u8221\'20\'1D any and all rightwingers.\par \par \uc2 He accused the judge {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/may/30/trump-trial-hush-money-verdict"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 who convicted}}}\uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in New York earlier this year of a hush-money plot to influence the 2016 election of running \u8220\'20\'1Ca kangaroo court\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou may be thinking this could not happen to you, make no mistake they are already coming for you, Joe and Kamala,\u8221\'20\'1D he said, without explaining how.\par \par \uc2 Then Navarro also repeated the Trumpesque far-right line that migrants crossing the US-Mexico border without authorization, as they flee danger, oppression and destitution in countries ranging from Venezuela, Haiti, China, parts of Africa and Central America are nothing but \u8220\'20\'1Cmurderers and rapists\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 He\u8217\'20\'19s left the stage now. Many attendees are enthusiastically holding or waving signs that say, simply: \u8220\'20\'1CMass Deportation Now\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.03am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.40am BST\par \par \uc2 Former Trump trade adviser Navarro addresses \uc2 RNC\uc2  after release from prison\par \par \uc2 To massive cheers across the convention floor, \uc2 Peter Navarro\uc2  has taken the stage. He just got out of prison.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYes, this morning I did walk out of a federal prison in Miami. \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and his department of INjustice put me there,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 He added: \u8220\'20\'1CIf they can come for me, if they can come for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , believe me they can come for you,\u8221\'20\'1D Navarro said, repeating a populist line that Trump and the Maga crowd like to use.\par \par \uc2 Navarro is a former trade adviser to Trump and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/mar/19/trump-adviser-peter-navarro-prison"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in March became}}}\uc2  the first former White House official ever jailed for contempt of Congress.\par \par \uc2 He was sentenced to four months in prison for refusing to cooperate with the House January 6 committee investigating the insurrection at the US Capitol in 2021 when extremists wanted to overturn Trump\u8217\'20\'19s defeat by \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  in the presidential election.\par \par \uc2 The the 74-year-old economist {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/mar/11/trump-peter-navarro-prison"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 appealed}}}\uc2  all the way to the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RealPNavarro/status/1767218142344864036"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 claiming}}}\uc2  he could not testify as his work with Trump on attempts to overturn the 2020 election was covered by executive privilege.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.45am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.28am BST\par \par \uc2 Matt Gaetz\uc2 , a Florida congressman, took to the stage at the Republican national convention on Wednesday with a brief but charged-up speech that took aim at Democrats, and in particular, at \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAppointing \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  to oversee the border is like appointing \uc2 Bernie Madoff\uc2  to oversee your retirement plan,\u8221\'20\'1D said Gaetz, to jeers and applause.\par \par \uc2 With some Democrats urging \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  to step down amid concerns about the president\u8217\'20\'19s health and cognition following a devastating debate in early July, the possibility of Harris at the top of the Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 2024 presidential ticket seems top-of-mind for Republican speakers at the \uc2 RNC\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.44am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.27am BST\par \par \uc2 The third day of speeches got under way in Milwaukee a short while ago.\par \par \uc2 Nancy Mace, a South Carolina congresswoman, kicked off Wednesday\u8217\'20\'19s evening program, began her speech by introducing herself as \u8220\'20\'1CNancy, \u8216\'20\'18Don\u8217\'20\'19t call me Pelosi\u8217\'20\'19, Mace.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 There was muted applause for the joke.\par \par \uc2 enltr. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/NancyMace?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @NancyMace}}}\uc2  : "We can never project strength around the world when WEAKNESS stands in the White House." {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/H7SrxU3DVx"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/H7SrxU3DVx}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Team Trump (Text TRUMP to 88022) (@TeamTrump) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/TeamTrump/status/1813715770259787817?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 17, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.40am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.22am BST\par \par \uc2 Profile: Who is Usha Vance, JD Vance's wife\par \par \uc2 Many Republicans have welcomed Usha Vance, the Indian American wife of vice-presidential nominee {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/15/jd-vance-trump-analysis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 JD Vance}}}\uc2 , as a symbol of generational change and growing diversity in the party ranks.\par \par \uc2 Usha, 38, a corporate lawyer who used to be a registered Democrat, is the daughter of Indian immigrants and a practicing Hindu.\par \par \uc2 Danny Willis, 25, chair of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.facebook.com/YRDelaware/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Delaware Young Republicans}}}\uc2 , said: \u8220\'20\'1CWith this ticket, with the show of diversity in what would be the second gentleman and second lady of the United States, I\u8217\'20\'19m extremely proud to be a Hispanic male and a Republican.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Usha has a very different story to tell from the last Republican second lady, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://trumpwhitehouse.archives.gov/people/karen-pence/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Karen Pence}}}\uc2 , a white grandmother and devout Christian from Indiana who was an elementary school teacher and watercolour artist.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/17/who-is-usha-vance-jd-vance-wife"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Who is Usha Vance, the Indian American lawyer married to JD Vance?}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.20am BST\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s choice of JD Vance has sparked concern in Europe, where leaders fear the potential new vice-president would be catastrophic news for Ukraine and its ability to keep fighting Russia.\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Andrew Roth has this:\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/15/trump-vp-pick-jd-vance"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 choice of JD Vance}}}\uc2  as his vice-presidential pick has reignited fears in Europe that he would pursue a transactional \u8220\'20\'1CAmerica first\u8221\'20\'1D foreign policy that could culminate in the US pushing for Ukraine to acquiesce to \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  and sue for peace with Russia.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s bad for us but it\u8217\'20\'19s terrible news for [Ukraine],\u8221\'20\'1D said one senior European diplomat in Washington. \u8220\'20\'1C[Vance] is not our ally.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Foreign diplomats and observers have frequently called Trump\u8217\'20\'19s actual policies a \u8220\'20\'1Cblack box\u8221\'20\'1D, saying that was impossible to know for certain what the unpredictable leader would do when in power.\par \par \uc2 Some have soothed themselves by suggesting that names tipped for top positions, such as former national security adviser \uc2 Robert O\u8217\'20\'19Brien\uc2 , would maintain a foreign policy status quo while Trump focuses on domestic affairs.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/17/trump-jd-vance-vp-ukraine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s choice of Vance \u8216\'20\'18terrible news\u8217\'20\'19 for Ukraine, Europe experts warn}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.35am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.13am BST\par \par \uc2 Trump sees former \u8216\'20\'18Never Trumper\u8217\'20\'19 JD Vance as a way to expand his base, insiders say\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  and his campaign see his running mate, the Ohio senator JD Vance, as a way to expand Trump\u8217\'20\'19s voter base, according to sources familiar with the matter, intending to lean into Vance\u8217\'20\'19s previous criticisms of Trump to convince voters who dislike both 2024 candidates to back the former president.\par \par \uc2 In the years before Vance ran for the \uc2 US Senate\uc2 , he repeatedly criticized Trump and his presidency in interviews where he made clear he never liked the former president and considered him \u8220\'20\'1Ccultural heroin\u8221\'20\'1D and in private conversations, where he suggested Trump was \u8220\'20\'1CAmerica\u8217\'20\'19s Hitler\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 But the criticisms, which once angered Trump, are now being seen by the Trump campaign as a unique asset that could resonate with voters who could be in a similar position: people who have previously found Trump unsavory but might prefer him to Biden, the sources said.\par \par \uc2 The Trump campaign has suggested that they want Vance to lean in to the fact that he was previously a so-called \u8220\'20\'1CNever Trumper\u8221\'20\'1D, with the hope that it could give independent and uncommitted voters a path towards supporting the former president in November.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/17/jd-vance-criticism-trump-voters"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump sees former \u8216\'20\'18Never Trumper\u8217\'20\'19 JD Vance as a way to expand his base, insiders say}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.29am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.09am BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 's running mate JD Vance to take center stage on Republican convention's third night\par \par \uc2 Good evening, US politics blog readers, and thanks for joining us as we cover the third night of the Republican national convention in Milwaukee. Dubbed \u8220\'20\'1CMake America Strong Once Again\u8221\'20\'1D, tonight\u8217\'20\'19s session will center on foreign policy, and the marquee event comes around 9.30pm CT, when Ohio senator JD Vance will address the convention for the first time since \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  named him his running mate on Monday. We\u8217\'20\'19ll hear from plenty of other prominent Republicans before Vance takes the stage, including \uc2 Doug Burgum\uc2 , the North Dakota governor, who was on the shortlist to be Trump\u8217\'20\'19s vice-presidential pick, Greg Abbott, the Texas governor the Florida congressman \uc2 Matt Gaetz\uc2  and the former House speaker \uc2 Newt Gingrich\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The convention is scheduled to begin at 5.45pm CT. Here are a few things we\u8217\'20\'19ll be looking out for tonight:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 How will JD Vance introduce himself to America? While Ohio voters and people who read his 2016 memoir Hillbilly Elegy know who he is, an AP-NORC Center for Public Affairs Research poll released today {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnorc.org/projects/most-say-biden-should-withdraw-from-the-presidential-race/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 found}}}\uc2 , \u8220\'20\'1CMost of the public does not know enough about \u8230\'20\'26 Vance to have an opinion\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 What will Republicans say about their policies towards Ukraine and Israel, the two major conflicts the United States is involved in? The GOP has grown increasingly hostile towards military aid to Ukraine, and European diplomats {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/17/trump-jd-vance-vp-ukraine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 fear}}}\uc2  Vance\u8217\'20\'19s ascension is a bad sign for future assistance. Meanwhile, the Republicans have been steadfast in their support of Israel\u8217\'20\'19s invasion of Gaza, and attacked \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  for not doing enough to support America\u8217\'20\'19s top ally in the Middle East. We\u8217\'20\'19ll see what Vance and other speakers have to say about these two wars.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Will the convention speakers touch on Trump\u8217\'20\'19s most divisive beliefs, such as that the 2020 election was stolen, or that the former president\u8217\'20\'19s enemies should be prosecuted? Or will they go along with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jul/17/trump-vance-biden-democrats-election-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-66982a6d8f081a868efc7c22#block-66982a6d8f081a868efc7c22"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the reported wishes of the Trump campaign}}}\uc2  and tone down their rhetoric in favor of a message of unity?\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.20am BST\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240717ek7h003eb\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
