\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  tests positive for Covid; \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  says report he told president to quit race is \u8216\'20\'18idle speculation\u8217\'20\'19 \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Fran Lawther (now); Maanvi Singh, Chris Stein, Maya Yang and L\u233\'00\'E9onie Chao-Fong (earlier) \par \uc2 9,139 \uc2 words\par \uc2 18 July 2024\par 01:08 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 This blog is now closed. You can read our full report here on Biden\u8217\'20\'19s Covid news and follow the latest from the Republican national convention hereBiden tests positive for Covid and cancels campaign eventRepublican national convention \u8211\'20\'13 live updates\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.38am BST\par \par \uc2 Summary of the day\par \par \uc2 The Republican National Convention\u8217\'20\'19s third night of speeches is under way, after an eventful political news day. Here\u8217\'20\'19s what\u8217\'20\'19s happened so far:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has tested positive for Covid-19. His illness was announced at the \uc2 UnidosUS\uc2  conference \u8211\'20\'13 where Biden was meant to deliver the keynote address. The president said he was doing \u8220\'20\'1Cgood\u8221\'20\'1D as he boarded Air Force One to return to Delaware, where he plans to quarantine and recover.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Biden had said he would consider dropping out of the presidential race if a \u8220\'20\'1Cmedical condition\u8221\'20\'1D emerged, the \uc2 New York Times\uc2  reports, citing an excerpt released from Biden\u8217\'20\'19s interview with Ed Gordon of BET News. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2024/07/17/us/politics/biden-health-election-drop-out.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 According to}}}\uc2  the Times, Biden was asked if there was any reason that would make him reconsider staying in the presidential race. In response, Biden said: \u8220\'20\'1CIf I had some medical condition that emerged, if somebody, if doctors came to me and said, you got this problem and that problem.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 John Hinckley, the man who shot and wounded president \uc2 Ronald Reagan\uc2  in 1981, has released his own statement following \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s assassination attempt on Saturday. In a tweet on Wednesday, Hinckley, who was released in 2022 after spending 41 years under federal oversight, wrote: \u8220\'20\'1CViolence is not the way to go. Give peace a chance.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  has accepted a third possible date to hold a \uc2 CBS\uc2 -hosted vice-presidential debate against Trump\u8217\'20\'19s newly announced running mate, Ohio senator {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/jd-vance"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 JD Vance}}}\uc2 . The Biden-Harris campaign said it was open to a showdown with Vance on Monday, 12 August, as well. Harris had previously agreed to participate in the debate on either Tuesday, 23 July, or Tuesday, 13 August.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The high-profile California Democrat Adam Schiff has called on \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  to drop out of the presidential race. Schiff, in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.latimes.com/politics/story/2024-07-17/schiff-calls-on-biden-to-drop-out-citing-serious-concerns-that-he-can-win"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 statement}}}\uc2  to the \uc2 Los Angeles Times\uc2 , said that Biden \u8220\'20\'1Chas been one of the most consequential presidents in our nation\u8217\'20\'19s history, and his lifetime of service as a Senator, a vice president, and now as president has made our country better\u8221\'20\'1D adding: \u8220\'20\'1CBut our nation is at a crossroads.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Biden lashed out at a \u8220\'20\'1Ctense\u8221\'20\'1D meeting with dozens of House Democrats who bluntly questioned his viability as their party\u8217\'20\'19s presidential nominee, according to reports. During the Saturday Zoom call, Colorado representative \uc2 Jason Crow\uc2  told Biden that voters are concerned about his vigor and strength, and noted the importance of national security in the November election, the reports say.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  has said media reporting that he told \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  to get out of the race was \u8220\'20\'1Cidle speculation\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Lloyd Doggett\uc2 , the Texas representative who became the first House Democrat to publicly call on \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  to step aside, has doubled down and urged the president to withdraw from the ticket in the face of \u8220\'20\'1Cthe reality of steadily, worsening poll numbers\u8221\'20\'1D. \u8220\'20\'1CMy call for President Biden to step aside remains even more urgent,\u8221\'20\'1D Doggett said in a statement on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 During the Democratic press conference in Milwaukee, the Minnesota governor, \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2 , was pressed on the party\u8217\'20\'19s plans to nominate \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  via a roll call vote in the coming days. Walz, who co-chairs the Democratic national convention\u8217\'20\'19s rules committee, confirmed that delegates would not begin voting before 1 August, and the governor\u8217\'20\'19s spokesperson confirmed that the process should wrap up by 7 August.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  does not have stitches but has a \u8220\'20\'1Cnice flesh wound\u8221\'20\'1D, his son \uc2 Eric Trump{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cbsnews.com/news/assassination-attempt-trump-rally-shooting-ear-doesnt-have-stitches-nice-flesh-wound-eric-trump/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  following his father\u8217\'20\'19s assassination attempt. In an interview with \uc2 CBS\uc2 , Eric said: \u8220\'20\'1CYou know, he was millimeters away from having his life expunged... I\u8217\'20\'19m sure the ear doesn\u8217\'20\'19t feel well.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Nearly two-thirds of Democrats want \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  to withdraw his re-election bid, a new AP-NORC {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnorc.org/projects/most-say-biden-should-withdraw-from-the-presidential-race/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 poll}}}\uc2  has found. According to the poll, which was mostly conducted before \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s assassination attempt on Saturday, 65% of Democrats say that Biden should withdraw. Overall, seven in 10 American adults say that Biden should drop out of the race.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Democratic National Committee\uc2  said that its virtual roll call to officially nominate Biden as its party\u8217\'20\'19s presidential nominee will happen in August, \uc2 CBS{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cbsnews.com/news/democratic-national-committee-letter-joe-biden-virtual-roll-call/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports}}}\uc2 . In a letter obtained and reported by \uc2 CBS\uc2  on Wednesday, the chairs of the Democratic national convention\u8217\'20\'19s rules committee, Leah Daughtry and \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2 , wrote: \u8220\'20\'1CWe have confirmed with the \uc2 Democratic National Committee\uc2  and the Democratic National Convention that no virtual voting will begin before August 1 \u8230\'20\'26.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Follow the \uc2 Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s live coverage of the \uc2 RNC\uc2  here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jul/17/rnc-jd-vance-speech-trump-day-3-live-updates"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 JD Vance to make first speech as Donald Trump\u8217\'20\'19s vice-presidential pick \u8211\'20\'13 live}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.20am BST\par \par \uc2 Schumer spokesperson says report he told Biden to quit race is 'idle speculation'\par \par \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s team has commented on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jul/17/trump-vance-biden-democrats-election-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-669850d88f081a868efc7d1b#block-669850d88f081a868efc7d1b"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ABC reporting}}}\uc2  that the Senate minority leader told Biden it would be best if he bowed out of the race.\par \par \uc2 A spokesperson for Schumer called the report \u8220\'20\'1Cidle speculation\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The spokesperson said: \u8220\'20\'1CUnless ABC\u8217\'20\'19s source is Senator \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  or President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  the reporting is idle speculation. Leader Schumer conveyed the views of his caucus directly to President Biden on Saturday.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.44am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.10am BST\par \par \uc2 Shortly after news of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Covid bout broke, the president\u8217\'20\'19s personal \uc2 Twitter\uc2 /X account posted a tongue-in-cheek fundraising appeal.\par \par \uc2 In a two-part post, the president wrote: \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m sick,\u8221\'20\'1D before adding: \u8220\'20\'1Cof \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  and his rich buddies trying to buy this election. And if you agree, pitch in here.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrI'm sick\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  (@JoeBiden) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JoeBiden/status/1813715902250017022?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 17, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrof \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  and his rich buddies trying to buy this election.\par \par \uc2 And if you agree, pitch in here. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/V93cYUUFQu"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/V93cYUUFQu}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  (@JoeBiden) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JoeBiden/status/1813716534499393678?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 17, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 The official @Potus account, meanwhile, shared his diagnosis in a more sober fashion:\par \par \uc2 I tested positive for COVID-19 this afternoon, but I am feeling good and thank everyone for the well wishes.\par \par \uc2 I will be isolating as I recover, and during this time I will continue to work to get the job done for the American people.\par \par \uc2 enltrI tested positive for COVID-19 this afternoon, but I am feeling good and thank everyone for the well wishes.\par \par \uc2 I will be isolating as I recover, and during this time I will continue to work to get the job done for the American people.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 President Biden (@POTUS) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/POTUS/status/1813715823053193685?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 17, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.14am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.57am BST\par \par \uc2 Jill Biden is planning to stay in Rehoboth Beach, Delaware, CNN reports a White House official as saying.\par \par \uc2 The first lady last saw the president on Saturday and is not symptomatic, the official said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.43am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.41am BST\par \par \uc2 JD Vance to give first speech as Trump's running mate\par \par \uc2 JD Vance is the main attraction at the convention tonight. The Ohio senator is scheduled to give his first speech as Trump\u8217\'20\'19s vice-presidential pick.\par \par \uc2 He is due on stage at about 9.30pm CT. We\u8217\'20\'19ll have his speech and all the latest news from the convention in our standalone blog here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jul/17/rnc-jd-vance-speech-trump-day-3-live-updates"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 JD Vance to make first speech as Donald Trump\u8217\'20\'19s vice-presidential pick \u8211\'20\'13 live}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.39am BST\par \par \uc2 Away from \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Covid news, the Republican national convention speeches have gotten under way.\par \par \uc2 One of the first speakers was rightwing Florida representative \uc2 Matt Gaetz\uc2 .\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/alice-herman"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Alice Herman}}}\uc2  , who is at the convention in Milwaukee, writes:\par \par \uc2 Gaetz took to the stage at the Republican national convention on Wednesday with a brief but charged-up speech that took aim at Democrats and, in particular, at \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAppointing \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  to oversee the border is like appointing \uc2 Bernie Madoff\uc2  to oversee your retirement plan,\u8221\'20\'1D said Gaetz, to jeers and applause.\par \par \uc2 With some Democrats urging \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  to step down amid concerns about the president\u8217\'20\'19s health and cognition following a devastating debate in early July, the possibility of \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  at the top of the Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 2024 presidential ticket seems top-of-mind for Republican speakers at the convention.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.51am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.18am BST\par \par \uc2 ABC\u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 Jonathan Karl\uc2  is reporting that \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2 , the Senate majority leader, told \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  that it would be best if the president bowed out.\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2  has not independently verified this report.\par \par \uc2 Karl tweeted: \u8220\'20\'1CI am told \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  had a blunt one-on-one conversation with Biden Saturday afternoon in Rehoboth. Schumer forcefully made the case that it would be best if Biden bowed out of the race.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSchumer\u8217\'20\'19s office wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t comment on the specifics of the conversation, telling me only, \u8220\'20\'1CLeader Schumer conveyed the views of his caucus.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrI am told \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  had a blunt one-on-one conversation with Biden Saturday afternoon in Rehoboth. Schumer forcefully made the case that it would be best if Biden bowed out of the race.\par \par \uc2 Schumer's office wouldn't comment on the specifics of the conversation, telling me only,\u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Jonathan Karl\uc2  (@jonkarl) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/jonkarl/status/1813713397437104272?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 17, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.19am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.15am BST\par \par \uc2 As Biden boarded Air Force One, on his way back to Delaware following a positive Covid-19 test, he told reporters travelling with him: \u8220\'20\'1CI feel good.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He was not wearing a mask as he boarded.\par \par \uc2 The president last tested positive for Covid-19 two years ago. But cases of the virus are now surging, and health officials have reported spikes in emergency room visits and hospitalizations due to Covid.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.36am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.07am BST\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  and his campaign see his running mate, JD Vance, as a way to expand Trump\u8217\'20\'19s voter base, according to sources familiar with the matter, intending to lean into the senator\u8217\'20\'19s previous criticisms of Trump to convince voters who dislike both 2024 candidates to back the former president.\par \par \uc2 In the years before Vance ran for the \uc2 US Senate\uc2 , he repeatedly criticized Trump and his presidency in interviews where he made clear he never liked the former president and considered him \u8220\'20\'1Ccultural heroin\u8221\'20\'1D and in private conversations where he suggested Trump was \u8220\'20\'1CAmerica\u8217\'20\'19s Hitler\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 But the criticisms, which once angered Trump, are now being seen by the Trump campaign as a unique asset that could resonate with voters who could be in a similar position: people who have previously found Trump unsavory but might prefer him to Biden, the sources said.\par \par \uc2 The Trump campaign has suggested that they want Vance to lean in to the fact that he was previously a so-called \u8220\'20\'1CNever Trumper\u8221\'20\'1D, with the hope that it could give independent and uncommitted voters a path towards supporting the former president in November.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/17/jd-vance-criticism-trump-voters"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump sees former \u8216\'20\'18Never Trumper\u8217\'20\'19 JD Vance as a way to expand his base, insiders say}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.10am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.49pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Biden/Harris campaign earlier released a statement chastising their rivals for backing away from a vice-presidential debate, linking it to Vance\u8217\'20\'19s resurfaced comments endorsing an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is the one whose campaign said he would debate \u8216\'20\'18anytime, anyplace; and who picked JD Vance specifically for his debating skills,\u8221\'20\'1D the campaign said in a statement. \u8220\'20\'1CNow suddenly right after a damning new leak showing his support for a nationwide \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, Vance is backing off a debate against Vice President Harris, who has spent the last two years prosecuting the case on behalf of reproductive freedom.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The Trump campaign, meanwhile, has said they are hesitant to schedule the debate due to uncertainty over who will be the Democratic nominee for vice-president.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.08am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.29pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is headed back to Delaware.\par \par \uc2 enltr.? {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/POTUS?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @POTUS}}}\uc2  ? is back on Air Force One and we\u8217\'20\'19re headed to Delaware {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/SLGfL8pcN1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/SLGfL8pcN1}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Nandita Bose (@nanditab1) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/nanditab1/status/1813701030355628170?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 17, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.27pm BST\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile at the Republican national convention, \uc2 Paul Manafort\uc2 , Trump\u8217\'20\'19s 2016 campaign chair, has been spotted on the floor.\par \par \uc2 Manafort was pardoned after being found guilty of several financial crimes in 2018, following an investigation by special counsel {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/robert-mueller"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Robert Mueller}}}\uc2  and his team.\par \par \uc2 Manafort, 69, was convicted on Tuesday of five counts of tax fraud, two counts of bank fraud and one count of failure to report a foreign bank account.\par \par \uc2 Trump had signalled that he wanted to bring Manafort {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/2024/03/18/trump-manafort-2024-campaign/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 back in the fold}}}\uc2  for his latest campaign, but it is unclear whether he has been officially enlisted and, if so, in what capacity.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.32pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.17pm BST\par \par \uc2 White House says Biden has tested positive for Covid but has mild symptoms\par \par \uc2 The White House confirmed \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has been tested positive for Covid.\par \par \uc2 According to the press secretary \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2 , the president is \u8220\'20\'1Cvaccinated and boosted\u8221\'20\'1D and has mild symptoms.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe White House will provide regular updates on the President\u8217\'20\'19s status as he continues to carry out the full duties of the office while in isolation,\u8221\'20\'1D she said in a statement to the press.\par \par \uc2 The president\u8217\'20\'19s doctor said that Biden \u8220\'20\'1Cpresented this afternoon with upper respiratory symptoms, to include rhinorhea (runny nose) and non-productive cough, with general malaise.\par \par \uc2 He \u8220\'20\'1Cfelt okay for his first event of the day, but given that he was not feeling better, point of care testing for Covid-19 was conducted, and the results were positive\u8221\'20\'1D,\u8221\'20\'1D in a statement shared with media. \u8220\'20\'1CHis symptoms remain mild, his respiratory rate is normal at 16, his temperature is normal at 97.8 and his pulse oximetry is normal at 97%. The President has received his first dose of Paxlovid. He will be self-isolating at his home in Rehoboth.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.42pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.14pm BST\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHe needs to take the precautions that have been recommended,\u8221\'20\'1D Murgu\u237\'00\'EDa said. \u8220\'20\'1CHe obviously didn\u8217\'20\'19t want to put anybody at risk. He said to tell my folks that we\u8217\'20\'19re not going to get rid of him that quickly \u8211\'20\'13 we\u8217\'20\'19re going to hear from him in the future directly.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Biden was scheduled to deliver the keynote address at the conference, before 1,500 Latino leaders, advocates and allies.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.06pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  tests positive for Covid\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has cancelled a speaking engagement at the \uc2 UnidosUS\uc2  annual conference because he has tested positive for Covid, according to the organization\u8217\'20\'19s president and CEO \uc2 Janet Murgu\u237\'00\'EDa\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe appreciate very much his wanting to have been here,\u8221\'20\'1D she announced from the podium where he was expected to speak shortly.\par \par \uc2 enltrhere's the moment news of Biden's positive covid test was announced at the \uc2 UnidosUS\uc2  conference in Las Vegas, where people were assembled waiting for his speech that was supposed to start 90 minutes ago {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/OPOl14QE6b"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/OPOl14QE6b}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Aaron Rupar (@atrupar) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/atrupar/status/1813697457173496083?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 17, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.10pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.58pm BST\par \par \uc2 Peter Navarro\uc2 , a former Donald Trump White House advis er who was just released from prison, has been spotted in Milwaukee:\par \par \uc2 The Associated Press {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/peter-navarro-prison-republican-national-committee-2b443fdbf14164fed4650332aaf6d0c9"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports}}}\uc2  that Navarro was released today from the prison where he was serving a four-month sentence after being convicted of contempt of Congress for defying a subpoena from the January 6 committee. He is expected to address the Republican national convention tonight.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.08pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden campaign resumes advertising after Trump assassination attempt\par \par \uc2 The president\u8217\'20\'19s re-election campaign has ended the pause on advertising it imposed following the Saturday assassination attempt against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , a Biden-Harris campaign official told the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s US politics live blog.\par \par \uc2 The first new ad features \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights activist Hadley Duvall, and in addition to attacking Trump singles out JD Vance, Trump\u8217\'20\'19s newly announced running mate. See it here:\par \par \uc2 enltrNEW {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/BidenHQ?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @BidenHQ}}}\uc2  Ad: "They Don't Care" featuring Kentuckian Hadley Duvall, who became pregnant at 12 after being raped by her stepfather.\par \par \uc2 "Trump and JD Vance don\u8217\'20\'19t care about women. They don\u8217\'20\'19t care about girls in this situation. They will continue to take our rights away." {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/dexvqSJKJr"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/dexvqSJKJr}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 James Singer (@Jemsinger) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Jemsinger/status/1813675399076823240?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 17, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.59pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.14pm BST\par \par \uc2 Special counsel appeals dismissal of Trump's classified documents case\par \par \uc2 Jack Smith, the justice department special counsel, has filed an appeal of judge Aileen Cannon \u8217\'20\'19s ruling earlier this week dismissing \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s indictment on charges of illegally possessing classified documents.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s the latest on this long-running legal saga:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/17/trump-classified-documents-dismissal-appeal"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Special counsel Jack Smith appeals dismissal of Trump classified files case}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.18pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.54pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump campaign declines to schedule vice-presidential debate, citing uncertainty over Democratic ticket\par \par \uc2 The Trump campaign has announced that it will not yet schedule a debate between JD Vance and \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , citing uncertainty over who will be the Democratic nominee for vice-president.\par \par \uc2 The decision is a reference to continued tension among Democrats over whether \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  should seek re-election, after his poor showing at his first debate with \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . The president insists he has no plans to step aside, but if he did, the new nominee would have to find their own running mate.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe don\u8217\'20\'19t know who the Democrat nominee for vice-president is going to be, so we can\u8217\'20\'19t lock in a date before their convention. To do so would be unfair to \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2 , JB Pritzker, \uc2 Gretchen Whitmer\uc2 , or whoever \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  picks as her running mate,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump campaign senior adviser Brian Hughes said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 The Biden-Harris campaign {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jul/17/trump-vance-biden-democrats-election-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-669807c88f08d8344a28f290#block-669807c88f08d8344a28f290"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 had previously proposed}}}\uc2  three possible dates for the vice-presidential debate, all before the beginning of the Democratic convention on 19 August, where the party will formalize the presidential ticket.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.36pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump campaign moved to tone down convention rhetoric \u8211\'20\'13 report\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s campaign has encouraged speakers at the Republican national convention to stay away from extreme rhetoric, and in some cases directly edited their speeches, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/2024-election/trump-campaign-edits-gop-convention-speeches-tone-political-rhetoric-rcna162394"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 NBC News reports}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 At the convention thus far, there have been few to no mentions of topics liked the January 6 insurrection, or Trump\u8217\'20\'19s baseless claims that he lost the 2020 election unfairly. That\u8217\'20\'19s a deliberate strategy his campaign shifted to following the assassination attempt on Saturday, as it now looks to project an image of unity.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more on that, from NBC:\par \par \uc2 Trump said that he had rewritten his own speech accepting the Republican presidential nomination ahead of Thursday night after surviving an assassination attempt. The Trump campaign has said that now he intends to home in on the theme of unifying America.\par \par \uc2 Former House Speaker \uc2 Newt Gingrich\uc2 , R-Ga, said Wednesday before delivering his convention address, \u8216\'20\'18Frankly, they sent the same message to those of us giving speeches.\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18We always planned to be a reflection of our party\u8217\'20\'19s unity and remind the American people of the difference between President Trump\u8217\'20\'19s success and Crooked \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s failure,\u8217\'20\'19 Brian Hughes, a senior Trump campaign adviser, said in a statement. \u8216\'20\'18The convention messages from everyday Americans and policymakers have met that goal. This convention is one of the greatest ever held and will launch us forward to victory in November.\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 While convention speakers this week have served up plenty of red meat to the thousands of delegates in attendance, particularly on the issues of immigration and crime, they have steered away from some of the party\u8217\'20\'19s more divisive topics and talk of seeking retribution.\par \par \uc2 Through the convention\u8217\'20\'19s first two nights, speakers have not mentioned the following issues: unfounded claims of stolen elections; the Jan 6, 2021, attack on the U.S. Capitol; investigating Trump\u8217\'20\'19s political opponents, including Biden; and investigating the prosecutors who have sought indictments against him, like Special Counsel Jack Smith, Manhattan District Attorney \uc2 Alvin Bragg\uc2  or Fulton County District Attorney \uc2 Fani Willis\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 A video where Trump mentions the unsubstantiated threat of Democrats \u8216\'20\'18cheating\u8217\'20\'19 in the upcoming election was played during the first two nights of the convention.\par \par \uc2 Asked if the toned-down theme would continue through the week, Rep. \uc2 Dan Meuser\uc2 , R-Pa., said, \u8216\'20\'18I do.\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18I mean, it starts with Trump,\u8217\'20\'19 he continued. \u8216\'20\'18Hopefully, JD [Vance] picks that up. And others. Trump said he didn\u8217\'20\'19t want people to change their speeches, but I think that they will.\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.23pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.17pm BST\par \par \uc2 Anyone attending the Republican national convention could be forgiven for thinking they have stepped into a mirror world where \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is a saint, not a twice-impeached former president convicted of 34 felonies.\par \par \uc2 On Wednesday, Brenna Bird, the attorney general of Iowa, was asked why she travelled to New York to support the former US president during his hush-money trial.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI was glad to go out to New York to support him during that trial because I\u8217\'20\'19m a prosecutor and I have prosecuted many criminal defendants, but I\u8217\'20\'19ve never seen anything like that,\u8221\'20\'1D Bird told international reporters at a Foreign Press Centers briefing.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s a travesty. It\u8217\'20\'19s not how the legal process is supposed to work. As a prosecutor, I\u8217\'20\'19ve never taken someone\u8217\'20\'19s politics into account when deciding whether to charge a crime. That is just wrong and, if it\u8217\'20\'19s allowed to happen, it breaks down the rule of law and the constitutional order.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Bird added: \u8220\'20\'1CI went there specifically as a prosecutor to support President Trump because what was happening was an injustice and I wanted to be there and stand up for what was right and support President Trump. I think we saw his character during that trial. He doesn\u8217\'20\'19t give up and he keeps on moving forward and that\u8217\'20\'19s exactly what our country needs right now.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In May, Trump was convicted of 34 felony counts of falsifying business records alleging he was involved in a scheme that sought to cover up extramarital affairs in advance of the 2016 presidential election. The New York state prosecution had no connection to Biden and there was no evidence of jury bias against Trump.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.25pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.01pm BST\par \par \uc2 Interim summary\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s where the day stands:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  said he would consider dropping out of the presidential race if a \u8220\'20\'1Cmedical condition\u8221\'20\'1D emerged, the \uc2 New York Times\uc2  reports, citing an excerpt released from Biden\u8217\'20\'19s interview with Ed Gordon of BET News. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2024/07/17/us/politics/biden-health-election-drop-out.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 According to}}}\uc2  the Times, Biden was asked if there was any reason that would make him reconsider staying in the presidential race. In response, Biden said: \u8220\'20\'1CIf I had some medical condition that emerged, if somebody, if doctors came to me and said, you got this problem and that problem.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 John Hinckley, the man who shot and wounded president \uc2 Ronald Reagan\uc2  in 1981, has released his own statement following \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s assassination attempt on Saturday. In a tweet on Wednesday, Hinckley, who was released in 2022 after spending 41 years under federal oversight, wrote: \u8220\'20\'1CViolence is not the way to go. Give peace a chance.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  has accepted a third possible date to hold a \uc2 CBS\uc2 -hosted vice-presidential debate against Trump\u8217\'20\'19s newly announced running mate, Ohio senator {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/jd-vance"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 JD Vance}}}\uc2 . The Biden-Harris campaign said it was open to a showdown with Vance on Monday, 12 August, as well. Harris had previously agreed to participate in the debate on either Tuesday, 23 July, or Tuesday, 13 August.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The high-profile California Democrat Adam Schiff has called on \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  to drop out of the presidential race. Schiff, in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.latimes.com/politics/story/2024-07-17/schiff-calls-on-biden-to-drop-out-citing-serious-concerns-that-he-can-win"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 statement}}}\uc2  to the \uc2 Los Angeles Times\uc2 , said that Biden \u8220\'20\'1Chas been one of the most consequential presidents in our nation\u8217\'20\'19s history, and his lifetime of service as a Senator, a vice president, and now as president has made our country better\u8221\'20\'1D adding: \u8220\'20\'1CBut our nation is at a crossroads.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  lashed out at a \u8220\'20\'1Ctense\u8221\'20\'1D meeting with dozens of House Democrats who bluntly questioned his viability as their party\u8217\'20\'19s presidential nominee, according to reports. During the Saturday Zoom call, Colorado representative \uc2 Jason Crow\uc2  told Biden that voters are concerned about his vigor and strength, and noted the importance of national security in the November election, the reports say.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Lloyd Doggett\uc2 , the Texas representative who became the first House Democrat to publicly call on \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  to step aside, has doubled down and urged the president to withdraw from the ticket in the face of \u8220\'20\'1Cthe reality of steadily, worsening poll numbers\u8221\'20\'1D. \u8220\'20\'1CMy call for President Biden to step aside remains even more urgent,\u8221\'20\'1D Doggett said in a statement on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 During the Democratic press conference in Milwaukee, the Minnesota governor, \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2 , was pressed on the party\u8217\'20\'19s plans to nominate \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  via a roll call vote in the coming days. Walz, who co-chairs the Democratic national convention\u8217\'20\'19s rules committee, confirmed that delegates would not begin voting before 1 August, and the governor\u8217\'20\'19s spokesperson confirmed that the process should wrap up by 7 August.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  does not have stitches but has a \u8220\'20\'1Cnice flesh wound\u8221\'20\'1D, his son \uc2 Eric Trump{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cbsnews.com/news/assassination-attempt-trump-rally-shooting-ear-doesnt-have-stitches-nice-flesh-wound-eric-trump/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  following his father\u8217\'20\'19s assassination attempt. In an interview with \uc2 CBS\uc2 , Eric said: \u8220\'20\'1CYou know, he was millimeters away from having his life expunged... I\u8217\'20\'19m sure the ear doesn\u8217\'20\'19t feel well.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Nearly two-thirds of Democrats want \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  to withdraw his re-election bid, a new AP-NORC {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnorc.org/projects/most-say-biden-should-withdraw-from-the-presidential-race/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 poll}}}\uc2  has found. According to the poll, which was mostly conducted before \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s assassination attempt on Saturday, 65% of Democrats say that Biden should withdraw. Overall, seven in 10 American adults say that Biden should drop out of the race.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Democratic National Committee\uc2  said that its virtual roll call to officially nominate \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  as its party\u8217\'20\'19s presidential nominee will happen in August, \uc2 CBS{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cbsnews.com/news/democratic-national-committee-letter-joe-biden-virtual-roll-call/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports}}}\uc2 . In a letter obtained and reported by \uc2 CBS\uc2  on Wednesday, the chairs of the Democratic national convention\u8217\'20\'19s rules committee, Leah Daughtry and \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2 , wrote: \u8220\'20\'1CWe have confirmed with the \uc2 Democratic National Committee\uc2  and the Democratic National Convention that no virtual voting will begin before August 1 \u8230\'20\'26.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.55pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden hasn't done enough to ease age concerns - former top Obama adviser\par \par \uc2 David Axelrod, a former senior adviser to President \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2 , warns that \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has not done enough to relieve voters\u8217\'20\'19 concern about his age since last month\u8217\'20\'19s hapless debate performance.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19ve felt for a long time, and I\u8217\'20\'19ve said for a long time, it\u8217\'20\'19s not in any way a commentary on his record, which I think will be honoured more by history than it is by voters right now,\u8221\'20\'1D Axelrod told the Guardian in Milwaukee on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBut it\u8217\'20\'19s a very hard case to make that anyone should be elected president in the United States at the age of 82, not for political reasons but for actuarial reasons. This is the hardest job on the planet. It takes a lot out of you. It\u8217\'20\'19s a legitimate concern that people have and that concern has been intensified by what happened at the debate. I don\u8217\'20\'19t think anything that\u8217\'20\'19s happened has relieved that concern.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Axelrod, chief strategist for the 2008 and 2012 Obama presidential campaigns, was speaking after an event organised by the University of Chicago Institute of Politics and the Cook Political Report on the sidelines of the Republican national convention.\par \par \uc2 Asked whether he thinks Biden can survive, Axelrod replied: \u8220\'20\'1CThat\u8217\'20\'19s entirely in his hands and that\u8217\'20\'19s been the case. This whole race has been in his hands, his decision to run and now his decision to stay.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere\u8217\'20\'19s a lot to think about because I know he\u8217\'20\'19s laid out the stakes in this election. The question he has to answer is, what are the odds of his winning? Would the odds be better with another candidate? I\u8217\'20\'19m sure there\u8217\'20\'19s a lot of discussion about that.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.18pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 Following \uc2 Rudy Giuliani\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s fall at the Republican national convention in Milwaukee on Tuesday, the 80-year-old disbarred lawyer\u8217\'20\'19s spokesperson Ted Goodman released the following statement on Wednesday:\par \par \uc2 Mayor \uc2 Rudy Giuliani\uc2  appreciates everyone\u8217\'20\'19s concern after tripping over a dip in the walkway on the convention floor of the convention.\par \par \uc2 The mayor and I were both filming footage for his social media and livestream programs on the floor of the convention, when he turned to set some equipment on a chair and tripped over a dip between the walkway and chairs.\par \par \uc2 Those falsely suggesting anything else are misleading the public for their own agendas.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.08pm BST\par \par \uc2 The rift among Democrats is deepening over \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s presidential candidacy despite party leaders saying Biden is the nominee.\par \par \uc2 Joan E Greve and Martin Pengelly report for the Guardian:\par \par \uc2 Demands for Joe {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/08/democrats-calling-joe-biden-to-step-down"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Biden to step aside}}}\uc2  as the Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 presidential pick to face \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  have slowed since the Republican survived an assassination attempt last weekend, to the extent that on Wednesday one \u8220\'20\'1Cprominent strategist\u8221\'20\'1D was moved to say of the rebellion: \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s over.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The strategist spoke anonymously to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thehill.com/homenews/campaign/4775982-biden-withdrawal-democratic-fracture/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Hill}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 and before the influential California congressman {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/17/biden-adam-schiff-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Adam Schiff}}}\uc2  said publicly that Biden should quit.\par \par \uc2 Nonetheless, in Milwaukee, at a press conference during the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/republican-national-convention-2024"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republican national convention}}}\uc2 , \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2 , the Minnesota governor and a party grandee, said Biden would be confirmed as the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/16/joe-biden-nomination-democratic-convention"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Democratic nominee by virtual vote}}}\uc2  between 1 and 7 August, before the Chicago convention.\par \par \uc2 For the full story, click here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/17/joe-biden-democrats-candidacy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Democratic rift over Biden candidacy deepens even as party says he will be nominee}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s campaign team released a new ad on Wednesday featuring Hadley Duvall, a 22-year-old \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights activist from Owensboro, Kentucky.\par \par \uc2 In the ad, Duvall, who was in an emotional {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://kentuckylantern.com/2023/09/28/woman-in-beshears-abortion-ad-says-she-wants-to-give-voice-to-victims/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ad}}}\uc2  last year during governor \uc2 Andy Beshear\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s re-election campaign, describes her experience of being impregnated by her stepfather, who raped her when she was 12 years old.\par \par \uc2 She said:\par \par \uc2 I\u8217\'20\'19m from Kentucky where, because of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , an extreme \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban is now in place, with no exceptions for rape or incest. During the overturn [of Roe v Wade], I went back to the time I was 12 years old and I was holding my first pregnancy test in my hand \u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 Trump brags about overturning Roe v Wade. He is \u8216\'20\'18proudly responsible\u8217\'20\'19 for each and every \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban across the country. And he calls them a \u8216\'20\'18beautiful thing to watch.\u8217\'20\'19 What is so beautiful about telling a 12-year-old girl that she must have the baby of her stepfather who raped her? The stakes of this election could not be higher for our choices.\par \par \uc2 enltrHer name is Hadley Duvall, and you need to hear her story. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/ub5Kmhi5pD"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/ub5Kmhi5pD}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Dr. Jill Biden (@DrBiden) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/DrBiden/status/1813598818299990300?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 17, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.36pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.19pm BST\par \par \uc2 Man who tried to assassinate Reagan says 'violence is not the way to go' after Trump assassination attempt\par \par \uc2 John Hinckley, the man who shot and wounded president \uc2 Ronald Reagan\uc2  in 1981, has released his own statement following \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s assassination attempt on Saturday.\par \par \uc2 In a tweet on Wednesday, Hinckley, who was released in 2022 after spending 41 years under federal oversight, wrote:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CViolence is not the way to go. Give peace a chance.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrViolence is not the way to go. Give peace a chance.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 John Hinckley (@JohnHinckley20) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JohnHinckley20/status/1813618282500653337?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 17, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.05pm BST\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  has accepted a third possible date to hold a \uc2 CBS\uc2 -hosted vice-presidential debate against Trump\u8217\'20\'19s newly-announced running mate, Ohio senator JD Vance.\par \par \uc2 The Biden-Harris campaign said it was open to a showdown with Vance on Monday, 12 August, as well. Harris had previously agreed to participate in the debate on either Tuesday, 23 July, or Tuesday, 13 August.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNow that the Trump campaign has selected a running mate, we encourage them to agree to a debate between vice-president Harris and senator Vance,\u8221\'20\'1D a campaign official said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.37pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.52pm BST\par \par \uc2 Here is video of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  saying he would consider dropping out of the presidential race if a \u8220\'20\'1Cmedical condition\u8221\'20\'1D emerges:\par \par \uc2 Biden goes on to say that he would consider the option if \u8220\'20\'1Cdoctors came and said: \u8216\'20\'18You\u8217\'20\'19ve got this problem and that problem.\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He adds that he \u8220\'20\'1Cmade a serious mistake in the whole debate\u8221\'20\'1D with \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  which prompted a wave of scrutiny from the Democratic party over his mental competency as president.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.19pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.39pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden says he'd consider withdrawing if 'medical condition' emerges \u8211\'20\'13 report\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  said he would consider dropping out of the presidential race if a \u8220\'20\'1Cmedical condition\u8221\'20\'1D emerged, the \uc2 New York Times\uc2  reports, citing an excerpt released from Biden\u8217\'20\'19s interview with Ed Gordon of BET News.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2024/07/17/us/politics/biden-health-election-drop-out.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 According to}}}\uc2  the Times, Biden was asked if there was any reason that would make him reconsider staying in the presidential race.\par \par \uc2 In response, Biden said:\par \par \uc2 If I had some medical condition that emerged, if somebody, if doctors came to me and said, you got this problem and that problem.\par \par \uc2 Earlier this month, Biden said during an interview with ABC host George Stephanopoulos that he would only drop out of the race if the \u8220\'20\'1CLord Almighty\u8221\'20\'1D told him to do so.\par \par \uc2 Biden\u8217\'20\'19s comments come amid increasing calls from Democrats for him to withdraw his re-election bid over concerns of his age and mental competency, particularly after his poor debate performance against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.38pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.16pm BST\par \par \uc2 California representative Adam Schiff is the most prominent Democrat to publicly call on \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  to drop out of the race.\par \par \uc2 Over the weekend, Schiff told donors that Biden remaining on top of the ticket for November would cost the party the presidency and probably the House and Senate, too, the \uc2 New York Times{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2024/07/16/us/politics/schiff-biden-democrats.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI think if he is our nominee, I think we lose,\u8221\'20\'1D Schiff told donors in East Hampton, New York, last Saturday, the paper said, citing \u8220\'20\'1Ca person with access to a transcription of a recording of the event\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 And we may very, very well lose the Senate and lose our chance to take back the House.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/16/adam-schiff-biden-democrats-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Adam Schiff reportedly tells donors \u8216\'20\'18I think we lose\u8217\'20\'19 if Biden is nominee}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.38pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.08pm BST\par \par \uc2 Adam Schiff calls on Biden to drop out\par \par \uc2 The high-profile California Democrat Adam Schiff has called on \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  to drop out of the presidential race.\par \par \uc2 Schiff, in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.latimes.com/politics/story/2024-07-17/schiff-calls-on-biden-to-drop-out-citing-serious-concerns-that-he-can-win"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 statement}}}\uc2  to the \uc2 Los Angeles Times\uc2 , said that Biden \u8220\'20\'1Chas been one of the most consequential presidents in our nation\u8217\'20\'19s history, and his lifetime of service as a Senator, a Vice President, and now as President has made our country better\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBut our nation is at a crossroads,\u8221\'20\'1D he added.\par \par \uc2 A second Trump presidency will undermine the very foundation of our democracy, and I have serious concerns about whether the President can defeat \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in November.\par \par \uc2 Schiff said the \u8220\'20\'1Cchoice to withdraw from the campaign is President Biden\u8217\'20\'19s alone\u8221\'20\'1D, but that he believes it is time for Biden \u8220\'20\'1Cto pass the torch\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Csecure his legacy of leadership\u8221\'20\'1D by allowing another Democrat to beat \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 He added that he would fully support whoever ends up at the top of the Democratic ticket \u8211\'20\'13 including if it remains Biden. \u8220\'20\'1CI will do everything I can to help them succeed,\u8221\'20\'1D Schiff said.\par \par \uc2 There is only one singular goal: defeating \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . The stakes are just too high.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.59pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.01pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  faced withering criticism over his recent claim that he had done \u8220\'20\'1Cmore for the Palestinian community than anybody\u8221\'20\'1D, as Israel {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/article/2024/jul/16/dozens-of-people-killed-in-israeli-airstrikes-across-the-gaza-strip"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 continues to strike Gaza}}}\uc2  with some of the fiercest bombardments in months.\par \par \uc2 The comments were made in an interview with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=XJP2zlH2nt8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Complex\u8217\'20\'19s Chris \u8220\'20\'1CSpeedy\u8221\'20\'1D Morman}}}\uc2  that was recorded last week in Detroit and published on Monday. While defending his administration\u8217\'20\'19s response to the conflict in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/gaza"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Gaza}}}\uc2 , Biden said:\par \par \uc2 By the way, I\u8217\'20\'19m the guy that did more for the Palestinian community than anybody. I\u8217\'20\'19m the guy that opened up all the assets. I\u8217\'20\'19m the guy that made sure that I got the Egyptians to open the border to let goods through, medicine and food.\par \par \uc2 More than {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.reuters.com/world/middle-east/biden-says-israel-gaza-war-should-end-now-2024-07-11/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 38,000 Palestinians}}}\uc2 , the majority of them civilians, have been killed since the war began 10 months ago, according to Gaza\u8217\'20\'19s health ministry. About 1,200 Israelis were killed in \uc2 Hamas\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s cross-border assault on 7 October.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.49pm BST\par \par \uc2 House Democrats are scrapping a letter raising \u8220\'20\'1Cserious concerns\u8221\'20\'1D about a plan to fast-track \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s virtual roll call nomination after the \uc2 Democratic National Committee\uc2  announced the vote would not take place until August.\par \par \uc2 The letter to the DNC, which had not been sent, called a proposal to fast-track Biden\u8217\'20\'19s nomination a \u8220\'20\'1Cterrible idea\u8221\'20\'1D that would effectively end the internal debate over whether Biden should remain the party\u8217\'20\'19s nominee.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re glad to see that the pressure has worked and the DNC will not rush this virtual process through in July,\u8221\'20\'1D a spokesperson for Congressman \uc2 Jared Huffman\uc2 , a California Democrat, told the Guardian. \u8220\'20\'1CWe won\u8217\'20\'19t be sending the letter at this time.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrNEW: House Democrats will not be sending their letter against the DNC's plan to nominate Biden ASAP.\par \par \uc2 "We're glad to see that the pressure has worked and the DNC will not rush this virtual process through in July," a spox for Rep. Huffman said.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Lauren Gambino (@laurenegambino) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/laurenegambino/status/1813604997507981419?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 17, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 During a press conference in Milwaukee on Wednesday morning, Minnesota governor \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2 , who heads the rules committee with Leah Daughtry, said delegates would not begin voting before 1 August, and the governor\u8217\'20\'19s spokesperson later confirmed that the process should wrap up by 7 August.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe need to get these things done. We need to get the roll call done,\u8221\'20\'1D Walz said. \u8220\'20\'1CBut it won\u8217\'20\'19t happen before the first of August.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Nearly 20 congressional Democrats have publicly called on Biden to resign, though the debate had stalled in the immediate aftermath of the assassination attempt on Trump. These House Democrats are suggesting a wider discussion should take place, even if the president insists he\u8217\'20\'19s not going anywhere.\par \par \uc2 According to a copy of the now-scrapped letter, obtained by the Guardian, a contingent of House Democrats was prepared to accuse the DNC of preparing to press ahead with a vote that could \u8220\'20\'1Cdeeply undermine the morale and unity of Democrats.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.11pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.43pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  lashed out at a \u8220\'20\'1Ctense\u8221\'20\'1D meeting with dozens of House Democrats who bluntly questioned his viability as their party\u8217\'20\'19s presidential nominee, according to reports.\par \par \uc2 During the Saturday Zoom call, Colorado congressman \uc2 Jason Crow\uc2  told Biden that voters are concerned about his vigor and strength, and noted the importance of national security in the November election, the reports say.\par \par \uc2 According to CNN, the president said to Crow, a former Army Ranger who served two tours in Afghanistan and one in Iraq, that he knew that he had a Bronze Star recipient, like his son Beau, but that \u8220\'20\'1Che didn\u8217\'20\'19t rebuild Nato.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 At one point, Biden told Crow to \u8220\'20\'1Ccut that crap out\u8221\'20\'1D and that if Crow wants to walk away from him, then he can walk away, according to the report. According to Puck News, Biden told Crow:\par \par \uc2 On national security, nobody has been a better president than I\u8217\'20\'19ve been. Name me one. Name me one! So I don\u8217\'20\'19t want to hear that crap!\par \par \uc2 Democrat lawmakers who were on the call told Puck that Biden was \u8220\'20\'1Crambling\u8221\'20\'1D, \u8220\'20\'1Cdismissive of concerns\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cunable or unprepared to present a campaign strategy.\u8221\'20\'1D One told the outlet:\par \par \uc2 He\u8217\'20\'19d start an answer then lose his train of thought, then would just say \u8216\'20\'18whatever.\u8217\'20\'19 He really couldn\u8217\'20\'19t complete an answer. I lost a ton of respect for him.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.31pm BST\par \par \uc2 Lloyd Doggett\uc2 , the Texas congressman who became the first House Democrat to publicly call on \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  to step aside, has doubled down and urged the president to withdraw from the ticket in the face of \u8220\'20\'1Cthe reality of steadily, worsening poll numbers\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMy call for President Biden to step aside remains even more urgent,\u8221\'20\'1D Doggett said in a statement on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 Our decision must consider the reality of steadily, worsening poll numbers, not just more wishful thinking. The risk of Trump tyranny is so great that we must put forward our strongest nominee.\par \par \uc2 He added:\par \par \uc2 Every day this decision is delayed, the focus is not on Trump\u8217\'20\'19s lies, and a new Democratic nominee is offered less time to achieve victory. What we need is a fair, open democratic process to select a new nominee that can excite and engage more Americans.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.26pm BST\par \par \uc2 Today\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/17/republican-convention-jd-vance-address-foreign-policy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 theme}}}\uc2  at the Republican national convention will be \u8220\'20\'1CMake America Strong Once Again,\u8221\'20\'1D and many of the speeches are expected to focus on foreign policy.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CEach one of these has a theme, like last night was \u8216\'20\'18bend the knee and grovel\u8217\'20\'19 apparently,\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2 , the governor of Minnesota, said at a Democratic press conference in Milwaukee. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd today is \u8216\'20\'18celebrate Russia day,\u8217\'20\'19 I guess.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 JD Vance will deliver his first speech since becoming \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8216\'20\'18s running mate, and given the theme, his remarks may highlight his isolationist views on foreign policy.\par \par \uc2 Vance has been one of the most outspoken critics of US aid to Ukraine, and European diplomats fear his elevation could heighten the risk of a Russian victory in the war.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/17/trump-jd-vance-vp-ukraine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Read Andrew Roth\u8217\'20\'19s full piece on Vance\u8217\'20\'19s foreign policy views.}}}\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/17/trump-jd-vance-vp-ukraine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s choice of Vance \u8216\'20\'18terrible news\u8217\'20\'19 for Ukraine, Europe experts warn}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.19pm BST\par \par \uc2 During the Democratic press conference in Milwaukee, Minnesota governor \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  was pressed on the party\u8217\'20\'19s plans to nominate \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  via a roll call vote in the coming days.\par \par \uc2 Walz, who co-chairs the DNC Rules Committee, confirmed that delegates would not begin voting before 1 August, and the governor\u8217\'20\'19s spokesperson confirmed that the process should wrap up by 7 August.\par \par \uc2 The news comes as 19 congressional Democrats have publicly called on Biden to drop out of the race following his disastrous debate performance last month.\par \par \uc2 The rules committee will meet on Friday to set out an agenda, Walz said, and he added that the meeting was never meant to kick off the virtual roll call vote.\par \par \uc2 Democrats have previously cited a ballot deadline of 7 August in Ohio as justification for the virtual roll call vote, but state legislators passed a bill to delay that deadline. Still, Walz argued that Democrats needed to confirm their nominee quickly to avoid potential legal challenges, as a number of states have August deadlines.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe need to get these things done. We need to get the roll call done,\u8221\'20\'1D Walz said. \u8220\'20\'1CBut it won\u8217\'20\'19t happen before the first of August.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Quentin Folks, Biden\u8217\'20\'19s principal deputy campaign manager, appeared to grow frustrated with the questions, telling reporters, \u8220\'20\'1CThe Republicans are lying to the American people about virtually every single issue that impacts their lives. And we\u8217\'20\'19re caught up in process stores.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.06pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  campaign officials and Democratic lawmakers held a press conference in Milwaukee this morning to attack Republicans\u8217\'20\'19 anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  policies.\par \par \uc2 Quentin Folks, Biden\u8217\'20\'19s principal deputy campaign manager, specifically called out \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8216\'20\'18s running mate, JD Vance, over his views on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Vance, who will speak at the Republican convention tonight, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/16/jd-vance-abortion-rights-groups"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has indicated}}}\uc2  he does not support \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  even in cases of rape or incest.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CJD Vance is an anti-choice politician whose views on reproductive freedom and women\u8217\'20\'19s rights would take us back decades,\u8221\'20\'1D Folks said.\par \par \uc2 The Democratic officials were joined by Amanda Zurawski, who nearly died because she could not obtain an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Texas after it became clear her pregnancy was not viable.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt was in that dark and lonely hospital room where I realized I was actually lucky. I lived. And I knew others might not be so lucky,\u8221\'20\'1D Zurawski said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhat I went through was nothing short of barbaric, and it didn\u8217\'20\'19t need to happen. But it did because of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.52pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has a 'nice flesh wound,' says \uc2 Eric Trump\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  does not have stitches but has a \u8220\'20\'1Cnice flesh wound,\u8221\'20\'1D his son \uc2 Eric Trump{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cbsnews.com/news/assassination-attempt-trump-rally-shooting-ear-doesnt-have-stitches-nice-flesh-wound-eric-trump/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  said}}}\uc2  following his father\u8217\'20\'19s assassination attempt.\par \par \uc2 In an interview with \uc2 CBS\uc2 , Eric said:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou know, he was millimeters away from having his life expunged... I\u8217\'20\'19m sure the ear doesn\u8217\'20\'19t feel well.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Eric added that his father said that the injury felt like the \u8220\'20\'1Cgreatest earache he\u8217\'20\'19s ever had,\u8221\'20\'1D and went on to say that his father\u8217\'20\'19s hearing is fine and that he is in \u8220\'20\'1Cgreat spirits.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Trump has appeared at the \uc2 RNC\uc2  this week in Milwaukee with a white bandage taped over his ear amid a heavily intensified security team.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.56pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.24pm BST\par \par \uc2 Nearly two-thirds of Democrats want Biden to withdraw - poll\par \par \uc2 Nearly two-thirds of Democrats want \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  to withdraw his re-election bid, a new AP-NORC {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnorc.org/projects/most-say-biden-should-withdraw-from-the-presidential-race/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 poll}}}\uc2  has found.\par \par \uc2 According to the poll which was mostly conducted before \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s assassination attempt on Saturday, 65% of Democrats say that Biden should withdraw.\par \par \uc2 Overall, 7 in 10 American adults say that Biden should drop out from the race.\par \par \uc2 57% of American adults say that Trump should withdraw from the race and allow the GOP to name a replacement. Meanwhile, 73% of Republicans say that Trump should remain in the race.\par \par \uc2 In stark contrast, only 35% of Democrats say that Biden should remain in the race.\par \par \uc2 Moreover, nearly half of Democrats are not very or not at all confident that Biden has the mental capability to serve as president, up from a third in a February poll. 27% of Democrats are extremely or very confident in his ability to be an effective president, down from 40% in the February poll.\par \par \uc2 Republicans have more confidence in Trump. 60% of Republicans are extremely or very confident that Trump has the mental capability to serve effectively as president.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.58pm BST\par \par \uc2 DNC virtual roll call to nominate Biden scheduled for August - report\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Democratic National Committee\uc2  said that its virtual roll call to officially nominate \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  as its party\u8217\'20\'19s presidential nominee will happen in August, \uc2 CBS{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cbsnews.com/news/democratic-national-committee-letter-joe-biden-virtual-roll-call/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  reports.}}}\par \par \uc2 In a letter obtained and reported by \uc2 CBS\uc2  on Wednesday, the DNC rules committee chairs Leah Daughtry and \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  wrote:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe have confirmed with the \uc2 Democratic National Committee\uc2  and the Democratic National Convention that no virtual voting will begin before August 1\u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 None of this will be rushed. Unlike our nation\u8217\'20\'19s other major political party, our rules are set in public meetings, anchored in the Party\u8217\'20\'19s charter and its traditions. That will continue in the 2024 cycle, as it must with so much at stake.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Daughtry and Walz added that they will propose a framework on Friday for \u8220\'20\'1Chow best to proceed\u8221\'20\'1D and that they will follow up with a second meeting next week to \u8220\'20\'1Cconsider and adopt specific rules for that purpose.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrSCOOP: DNC says the virtual roll call to nominate Biden will happen in AUGUST, according to letter first obtained by CBS News\par \par \uc2 Sent today by heads of the rules convention committee Gov. Walz and Leah Daughtry. DNC and DNCC have buy in.\par \par \uc2 Developing story... {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/LyfEPZ456C"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/LyfEPZ456C}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/lT4ETBtFr2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/lT4ETBtFr2}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 aaron navarro (@aaronlarnavarro) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/aaronlarnavarro/status/1813567258951823718?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 17, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 Reports of the virtual roll call date comes amid Democratic infighting over whether Biden should remain the party\u8217\'20\'19s nominee or withdraw his re-election bid.\par \par \uc2 Concerns over Biden\u8217\'20\'19s capability as president have swirled intensely following his poor debate performance and repeated public faux pas including accidentally calling Ukrainian president \uc2 Volodymyr Zelenskiy\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1CPresident Putin\u8221\'20\'1D at last week\u8217\'20\'19s Nato summit in Washington DC.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.21pm BST\par \par \uc2 Efforts to replace Biden in 2024 race 'over', Democratic strategist says - report\par \par \uc2 The Hill is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thehill.com/homenews/campaign/4775982-biden-withdrawal-democratic-fracture/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  reporting}}}\uc2  that efforts to replace \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is \u8220\'20\'1Cgame over \u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 In a new report on Wednesday, the outlet quoted one Democratic strategist saying: \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s over. There\u8217\'20\'19s been no meaningful movement in a week.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere is little to no time left. People are focused elsewhere. It\u8217\'20\'19s a collective action problem and we have no solution \u8230\'20\'26 Game over,\u8221\'20\'1D the strategist added.\par \par \uc2 Following Biden\u8217\'20\'19s poor debate performance, Democrats have scrambled amid the political fallout to determine the trajectory of the party. In recent weeks, numerous sitting congressional members and celebrity donors including \uc2 George Clooney\uc2  have called on Biden to drop out from the race.\par \par \uc2 Yet, the president has remained defiant, repeatedly pushing back on criticisms of his age and mental competency.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.06pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.49pm BST\par \par \uc2 Ahead of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s address at \uc2 UnidosUS\uc2  today in Las Vegas, the White House unveiled new actions to expand opportunities across Latino communities.\par \par \uc2 In a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.whitehouse.gov/briefing-room/statements-releases/2024/07/17/fact-sheet-biden-harris-administration-announces-new-actions-to-expand-opportunities-for-latino-communities-and-ensure-every-family-has-a-fair-shot-at-the-american-dream/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 statement}}}\uc2  released on Wednesday, the White House said some of the actions include:\par \par \uc2 To strengthen the federal government\u8217\'20\'19s commitment to advancing opportunity, today, president Biden will sign an executive order establishing the White House Initiative on Advancing Educational Equity, Excellence, and Economic Opportunity through Hispanic-Serving Institutions \u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 On June 18th, the president announced a new process to help US citizens with noncitizen spouses and children who have been here for 10 years or more keep their families together \u8230\'20\'26 And today, the president is announcing that beginning on August 19, 2024, eligible spouses and children will be able to apply for this process to obtain legal status while remaining with their families\u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 The Department of Homeland Security\u8217\'20\'19s US Citizenship and Immigration Services (USCIS) is announcing the launch of a new initiative \u8211\'20\'13 \u8216\'20\'18\uc2 USCIS\uc2  to You\u8217\'20\'19 \u8211\'20\'13 to bring immigration-related assistance into local communities, including rural and underserved areas \u8230\'20\'26\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.27pm BST\par \par \uc2 With JD Vance scheduled to take center stage tonight, here is the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s Sam Levine\u8217\'20\'19s report from Milwaukee on the senator\u8217\'20\'19s expected address and the \uc2 RNC\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s third day:\par \par \uc2 Vance will be introduced by \uc2 Donald Trump Jr.\uc2  The theme for Wednesday \u8211\'20\'13 \u8220\'20\'1CMake America Strong Once Again\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 comes amid internal divisions on how to handle the war in Ukraine. Earlier this year, House speaker Mike Johnson only narrowly passed a bill {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/20/us-house-approves-61bn-aid-ukraine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 to provide additional funding}}}\uc2  for Ukraine over the loud objection of some Republicans.\par \par \uc2 The day will also offer an opportunity for Republicans to attack \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  over his handling of the US military\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jun/30/us-afghanistan-war-military-pullout-report-biden-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 withdrawal from Afghanistan}}}\uc2  and the war between Israel and Gaza.\par \par \uc2 For the full story, click here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/17/republican-convention-jd-vance-address-foreign-policy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republican convention day three: JD Vance to speak as focus turns to foreign policy}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 Republican convention to focus on foreign policy as JD Vance prepares for speech\par \par \uc2 Good morning,\par \par \uc2 With the Republican national convention entering its third day, Trump\u8217\'20\'19s vice-presidential pick, 39-year-old JD Vance, is set to deliver perhaps the most significant speech of his political career today.\par \par \uc2 The Ohio senator is expected to address the \uc2 RNC\uc2  this evening following the announcement of his selection as \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s running mate on Monday.\par \par \uc2 Vance, a former critic of Trump who once {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/15/trump-vp-pick-jd-vance"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 called}}}\uc2  the former president \u8220\'20\'1CAmerica\u8217\'20\'19s Hitler\u8221\'20\'1D as well as a \u8220\'20\'1Ctotal fraud\u8221\'20\'1D, is set to make his appearance tonight amid the \uc2 RNC\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s theme for today \u8211\'20\'13 \u8220\'20\'1CMake America Strong Once Again\u8221\'20\'1D. On Tuesday, Trump\u8217\'20\'19s former opponents \uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2  and \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  both made appearances at the Milwaukee convention during which they heavily endorsed Trump.\par \par \uc2 Wednesday\u8217\'20\'19s theme, an ode to Trump\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1CMake America Great Again\u8221\'20\'1D tagline, is expected to largely revolve around US foreign policy, which Vance has been heavily critical of with regards to US military aid to Ukraine. Following the announcement of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s vice-presidential pick, European experts have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/17/trump-jd-vance-vp-ukraine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 warned}}}\uc2  that Vance is a \u8220\'20\'1Cterrible choice\u8221\'20\'1D for Ukraine in its fight against Russian aggression.\par \par \uc2 Here are other developments in US politics:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is in Las Vegas, where he is expected to deliver remarks at \uc2 UnidosUS\uc2 , the largest annual {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://unidosus.org/press-releases/president-biden-to-keynote-final-day-of-unidosus-annual-conference/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 gathering}}}\uc2  of Latino advocates and policymakers.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The White House is reaffirming its {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/17/biden-administration-transgender-surgeries-minors"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 support}}}\uc2  for surgeries for trans minors following backlash over its comments that the surgeries \u8220\'20\'1Cshould be limited to adults\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A former White House official has been {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/17/ex-white-house-official-sue-mi-terry-south-korea-agent-allegations"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 accused}}}\uc2  of working as South Korea agent in exchange for luxury goods, according to an indictment filed in a Manhattan federal court.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.39pm BST\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240717ek7h001p8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
