\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Biden says \u8216\'20\'18time to outlaw\u8217\'20\'19 AR-15 rifle used in Trump assassination attempt \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Chris Stein (now) and L\u233\'00\'E9onie Chao-Fong (earlier) \par \uc2 11,185 \uc2 words\par \uc2 16 July 2024\par 22:49 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 This live blog is closed. For the latest from the Republican national convention \u8211\'20\'13 including speeches from ex-Trump rivals \uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2 , \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  and \uc2 Marco Rubio\uc2 , follow our dedicated \uc2 RNC\uc2  live blog here:Republican national convention \u8211\'20\'13 live updates\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.39pm BST\par \par \uc2 This live blog is now closed. For all the latest from the Republican national convention \u8211\'20\'13 including speeches from former Trump rivals \uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2 , \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  and \uc2 Marco Rubio\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 follow our dedicated \uc2 RNC\uc2  live blog here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jul/16/rnc-haley-desantis-rubio-speeches-day-2-live-updates"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s former rivals to stage show of unity as Haley, DeSantis and Rubio expected to address Republican national convention \u8211\'20\'13 live}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.49pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.28pm BST\par \par \uc2 Summary\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has addressed the \uc2 NAACP\uc2  national convention, his first public speech since the assassination attempt on \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  at the weekend.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 In the speech in Las Vegas, Nevada, the president said it was \u8220\'20\'1Ctime to outlaw\u8221\'20\'1D the AR-15 rifle used in the shooting at a Trump campaign rally in Butler, Pennsylvania, that injured the former president, killed one spectator and injured at least two more people. \u8220\'20\'1CAn AR-15 was used in the shooting of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2 . This was the assault weapon that killed so many others, including children. It\u8217\'20\'19s time to outlaw them,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 In a sign that the detente between Biden and Trump will be brief, the president criticized his predecessor for his {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jun/30/black-swing-voters-georgia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 comments about \u8220\'20\'1CBlack jobs\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2  during their first debate. Trump had claimed undocumented immigrants are \u8220\'20\'1Ctaking Black jobs now\u8221\'20\'1D. Biden said: \u8220\'20\'1CFolks, I know what a Black job is. It\u8217\'20\'19s a vice-president of the United States.\u8221\'20\'1D He added: \u8220\'20\'1CI know what a Black job is. The first Black president \u8230\'20\'26 \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden added.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Biden also again rebutted criticisms of his age, telling the crowd: \u8220\'20\'1CI know how to do this job, and I know the good Lord hasn\u8217\'20\'19t brought us this far to leave us now there\u8217\'20\'19s more work to do.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Over in Milwaukee, the Republican national convention entered its second day. Speakers tonight include \uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2 , the last of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Republican presidential rivals to drop out of the race, Florida governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , Florida senator and failed hopeful for running mate \uc2 Marco Rubio\uc2 , as well as New York representative \uc2 Elise Stefanik\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The former first lady,Melania Trump, is expected to attend the Republican national convention on Thursday, when her husband, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , will formally accept his party\u8217\'20\'19s presidential nomination, NBC reported, citing a senior Trump campaign official. She hasn\u8217\'20\'19t much been seen or heard from on the campaign trail or during Trump\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/may/30/trump-trial-hush-money-verdict"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 criminal trial}}}\uc2  in New York. But {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/14/melania-trump-statement-donald-trump-rally-shooting"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 she issued}}}\uc2  a statement on Saturday after the former president was shot in the ear in an assassination attempt.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Democratic National Committee (DNC)\uc2  is quietly moving ahead with plans to formally nominate \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  as the party\u8217\'20\'19s presidential candidate weeks before the Democratic national convention next month, according to a report. Party chiefs are moving to kill off efforts to force Biden from the party\u8217\'20\'19s presidential ticket by rushing ahead with plans for convention delegates to vote electronically in a week-long roll call starting in late July, Axios reported.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The senator {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/16/bob-menendez-bribery-verdict"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bob Menendez }}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/16/bob-menendez-bribery-verdict"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has been found guilty on all counts in his federal corruption trial}}}\uc2 . The New Jersey Democrat, 70, had pleaded not guilty to 16 criminal charges including bribery, acting as a foreign agent and obstructing justice.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.28pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.24pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden is planning to announce his endorsement for supreme court term limits and other major reforms of the country\u8217\'20\'19s highest courts, according to a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/2024/07/16/biden-supreme-court-reforms/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 report}}}\uc2  from the \uc2 Washington Post\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The president is expected to soon call for legislation to establish an enforceable ethics code for the supreme court, and will weigh whether to call for a constitutional amendment to eliminate broad immunity for presidents and other constitutional officeholders, the Post reports, citing anonymous sources.\par \par \uc2 The report has not yet been independently verified by the Guardian. If Biden does announce support for such reforms, it would be a radical shift for a president who has previously resisted calls from progressive lawmakers to reform the supreme court.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.29pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.22pm BST\par \par \uc2 A threat from Iran prompted the \uc2 US Secret Service\uc2  to boost protection around \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  before {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donald-trump-pennsylvania-rally-shooting"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Saturday\u8217\'20\'19s attempted assassination of the former president}}}\uc2 , though it appears unrelated to the rally attack, according to two US officials.\par \par \uc2 Upon learning of the threat, the Biden administration contacted senior officials at the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/secret-service"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Secret Service}}}\uc2  to make them aware, the officials said, adding that information have been shared with the lead agent on Trump\u8217\'20\'19s protection detail and the Trump campaign. That prompted the agency to surge resources and assets. The officials spoke on the condition of anonymity to discuss sensitive intelligence matters.\par \par \uc2 Iran\u8217\'20\'19s mission to the United Nations dismissed the allegations as \u8220\'20\'1Cunsubstantiated and malicious\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The additional resources did not prevent {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/13/trump-rally-gun-shots-pennsylvania"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Saturday\u8217\'20\'19s attack at a Trump rally}}}\uc2  in Pennsylvania that left Trump injured to the ear, killed one rally-goer and severely injured two more when a 20-year-old man with an AR-style rifle {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/14/trump-rally-shooting-fbi-names-20-year-old-from-bethel-park-as-subject-involved"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 opened fire from a nearby rooftop}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/16/iran-assassination-plot-trump-shooting"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Iran threat led to boosting of Trump security before shooting, US officials say}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.30pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.42pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden says 'I know how to do this job' as he rebuts criticism of his age\par \par \uc2 As he closed his speech to the \uc2 NAACP\uc2 , \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  defended his ability to continue serving as president, despite mounting worries among Democrats over his advanced age.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHopefully, with age, I\u8217\'20\'19ve demonstrated a little bit of wisdom. Here\u8217\'20\'19s what I do know: I know how to tell the truth. I know right from wrong. I know how to do this job, and I know the good Lord hasn\u8217\'20\'19t brought us this far to leave us now there\u8217\'20\'19s more work to do,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said.\par \par \uc2 His comments came amid reports that the \uc2 Democratic National Committee\uc2  is moving to quickly nominate Biden, and quell a rebellion by lawmakers and others concerned about his ability to defeat \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/16/joe-biden-nomination-democratic-convention"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Democrats seek to lock in Biden nomination before convention}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.38pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is warning the \uc2 NAACP\uc2  that a second \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  administration would \u8220\'20\'1Cundo everything\u8221\'20\'1D they stand for.\par \par \uc2 The president said he has been \u8220\'20\'1Call about working people in this nation my whole career\u8221\'20\'1D, and: \u8220\'20\'1CThat\u8217\'20\'19s a stark contrast to my predecessor and his Maga visions. They\u8217\'20\'19ll undo everything, undo everything the \uc2 NAACP\uc2  stands for. But now they\u8217\'20\'19re trying to deny it. They\u8217\'20\'19re lying about their Project 2025. They want to deny your freedom, the freedom to vote.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.31pm BST\par \par \uc2 The crowd at the \uc2 NAACP\uc2  convention has started chanting \u8220\'20\'1Cfour more years!\u8221\'20\'1D after \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  vowed to restore the constitutional right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAnd, guess what, come hell or high water, we\u8217\'20\'19re going to restore Roe v Wade as the law of the land,\u8221\'20\'1D the president said.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.26pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden attacks Trump over 'Black job' comment as campaign shifts back into gear\par \par \uc2 In a sign that the detente between \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  will be brief, the president has attacked his predecessor for his comments about \u8220\'20\'1CBlack jobs\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Biden was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jun/30/black-swing-voters-georgia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 referencing a comment}}}\uc2  Trump made during their first debate, in which he claimed undocumented immigrants are \u8220\'20\'1Ctaking Black jobs now\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COf course he thinks of Black jobs,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden told the crowd at the \uc2 NAACP\uc2  convention. \u8220\'20\'1CI love his phrase, \u8216\'20\'18Black jobs\u8217\'20\'19, tells a lot about the man and about his character. Folks, I know what a Black job is. It\u8217\'20\'19s a vice-president of the United States.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI know what a Black job is. The first Black president \u8230\'20\'26 \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden added.\par \par \uc2 It was a reversion to form for the president, who had toned down his rhetoric over the past couple of days following the assassination attempt on Trump. Expect the former president to follow suit.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.34pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.19pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden says 'time to outlaw' AR-15 rifle used in Trump assassination attempt\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is commenting at length about the toll gun violence takes on American communities, and singled out the impact of assault weapons such as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/16/ar-15-rifles-explainer"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the AR-15}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAn AR-15 was used in the shooting of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . This was the assault weapon that killed so many others, including children. It\u8217\'20\'19s time to outlaw them,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said.\par \par \uc2 In what was likely a reference to his involvement in passing the 1994 assault weapons ban, which expired 10 years later, Biden said: \u8220\'20\'1CI did it once, and I will do it again.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.15pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  appears to be making light of the efforts by his fellow Democrats to get him to step aside in favor of what they feel would be a more electable candidate.\par \par \uc2 He related the adage, credited to former president \uc2 Harry Truman\uc2 , that \u8220\'20\'1Cif you want a friend in Washington, get a dog\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAfter the last couple weeks, I know what he means,\u8221\'20\'1D quipped Biden, who had earlier described Truman as someone who \u8220\'20\'1Cwas often counted out\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.12pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden takes stage at \uc2 NAACP\uc2  convention\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is now speaking to the \uc2 NAACP\uc2  convention.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMy name is \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , and I\u8217\'20\'19m a lifetime member of the \uc2 NAACP\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D the president began, speaking of the longstanding civil rights group.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.36pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.07pm BST\par \par \uc2 Derrick Johnson\uc2 , the president of the \uc2 NAACP\uc2 , is introducing \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , who will address the civil rights group\u8217\'20\'19s convention in Las Vegas.\par \par \uc2 He recounted how Black voters were crucial to determining the 2020 election, but noted, \u8220\'20\'1Cnot everyone shares the same investment in a progressive vision\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Johnson is singling out Project 2025, the rightwing plan to remake the \uc2 US government\uc2  that several officials tied to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  are involved in.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is a 900-page manifesto that seeks to undermine progress, promote violence, inflict harm on our community. They must know that \uc2 NAACP\uc2 , we will be here for that fight,\u8221\'20\'1D Johnson said.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 At a lawmaker panel hosted by the rightwing organization Moms for \uc2 Liberty\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 a group that has earned a reputation for advancing local book bans \u8211\'20\'13 the conversation, which was largely focused on the virtues of private education, shifted to teachers\u8217\'20\'19 unions.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou have the teachers, and then you have the union,\u8221\'20\'1D said the Florida congressman Byron Donalds, to jeers from the crowd. \u8220\'20\'1CThe Democrats can\u8217\'20\'19t win elections without the power of unions.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Proponents of private education rarely speak so candidly about the political motives behind the push to defund public education. Donalds\u8217\'20\'19 acknowledgment of the electoral power of unions offers a more complete picture of the conservative push to expand private schools, where union density is low.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.03pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.36pm BST\par \par \uc2 Former UK prime minister \uc2 Boris Johnson\uc2  has said he has \u8220\'20\'1Cno doubt\u8221\'20\'1D that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  would continue supporting Ukraine, following a meeting with him.\par \par \uc2 In a post on X, Johnson wrote: \u8220\'20\'1CWe discussed Ukraine and I have no doubt that he will be strong and decisive in supporting that country and defending democracy.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The meeting comes amid growing concern that Trump could withdraw support for Ukraine and possibly seek a peace deal directly with the Kremlin that may involve territorial concessions.\par \par \uc2 enltrGreat to meet President Trump who is on top form after the shameful attempt on his life. We discussed Ukraine and I have no doubt that he will be strong and decisive in supporting that country and defending democracy. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/OEVZPZsRE1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/OEVZPZsRE1}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Boris Johnson\uc2  (@BorisJohnson) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/BorisJohnson/status/1813284028298240086?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 16, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 Boris Johnson\uc2  met Trump on the sidelines of the Republican national convention in Milwaukee. He\u8217\'20\'19s not the only former British prime minister to swing through:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/15/nigel-farage-liz-truss-republican-national-convention"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Farage and Truss to attend US Republican national convention}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.04pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.27pm BST\par \par \uc2 Harris invites Vance to vice-presidential debate\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  has formally invited JD Vance, the Ohio senator who \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  yesterday named as his running mate, to debate, the Biden-Harris campaign said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CVice-President Harris reached out to Senator Vance and left a message to congratulate him on his selection, welcome him to the race and express her hope that the two can meet in the vice-presidential debate proposed by CBS News,\u8221\'20\'1D a campaign official said.\par \par \uc2 It is unclear when the debate will happen. CBS News {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cbsnews.com/news/when-is-second-presidential-debate-2024/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 proposed}}}\uc2  23 July or 13 August, which the Biden campaign has accepted.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.40pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.11pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden to make first public speech since assassination attempt on Trump\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is expected to soon make his first speech in public since a gunman attempted to kill \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  at a campaign rally over the weekend.\par \par \uc2 In the aftermath of the failed assassination, in which a rallygoer and the gunman were killed, Biden and Trump have dialed back their relentless attacks on each others\u8217\'20\'19 records ahead of the 5 November election.\par \par \uc2 The president is scheduled to address the convention of the \uc2 National Association for the Advancement of Colored People\uc2  civil rights group in Las Vegas, Nevada, a swing state that could prove crucial to both campaigns.\par \par \uc2 Biden is once again late to begin his speech, but we\u8217\'20\'19ll let you know he says when it starts.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.04pm BST\par \par \uc2 Sharon Yancey, 77, said she has been a Republican voter for 10 to 15 years.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHe\u8217\'20\'19s a patriot and I\u8217\'20\'19m a patriot. I love America, and he does too. And he wants to make America the best for everyone, all people, that are here, including the minorities,\u8221\'20\'1D Yancey, who was wearing a red Make America great again hat, said of Trump.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COther groups of people, they vote their conscience and they\u8217\'20\'19re not vilified for it, they\u8217\'20\'19re not looked down on and told to feel like you\u8217\'20\'19re less of a person if you don\u8217\'20\'19t vote Democrat,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COne of my son-in-laws is white; he votes the way he wants to vote. And I have another son-in-law who\u8217\'20\'19s Asian; he votes the way he wants to vote. So why am I vilified and called you know, less than a human being, and all those other derogatory things they say about Black people who don\u8217\'20\'19t follow the line?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.05pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 Tim Scott, the South Carolina senator who was among the candidates to be \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s vice-presidential pick, stopped at an outreach event for Black voters in Milwaukee on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 Speaking at the Wisconsin GOP\u8217\'20\'19s Black coalition headquarters, alongside four local politicians, Scott was more subdued than he had been on Monday night, when he {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/live-updates/2024/07/15/rnc-live-updates-coverage/tim-scott-roars-into-the-microphone-00168529"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 literally roared into a microphone}}}\uc2  after dubbing Trump an \u8220\'20\'1CAmerican lion\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 As Scott entered the room there were 16 people seated, 10 of whom were Black, and they sat through a rather dry conversation about \u8220\'20\'1Copportunity zones\u8221\'20\'1D, a bipartisan 2017 program designed to boost investment in lower-income communities.\par \par \uc2 There was no mention of Trump, and little mention of the Republican party as a whole, aside from Scott saying: \u8220\'20\'1CWe have not been as good at marketing the success that\u8217\'20\'19s come out of the conservative movement as we should be.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In a room which had portraits of \uc2 Abraham Lincoln\uc2 , \uc2 Martin Luther King Jr\uc2 , \uc2 Ronald Reagan\uc2  and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  mounted along one wall, some people said they would vote for Trump in November.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19ve just recently made the shift over to being a Republican. My family were Democrat, I think I was just born into it,\u8221\'20\'1D said Mario Dickens. A local business owner, he said he became a Republican about a year ago.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe just haven\u8217\'20\'19t seen much benefit at all over last four years. And four years prior things were going great for us,\u8221\'20\'1D Dickens said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.50pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump Jr\uc2  joked with his father about hair in the aftermath of Saturday\u8217\'20\'19s assassination attempt at a campaign rally in Pennsylvania.\par \par \uc2 Don Jr was out fishing with his daughter in Jupiter, Florida, when he received a call from his fiancee, Kimberly Guilfoyle, informing him that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  had been shot.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt was 90 minutes before I even knew he was alive,\u8221\'20\'1D Don Jr said at Axios House on the sidelines of the Republican national convention in Milwaukee.\par \par \uc2 That was a tough moment and then finally, get hit him on the phone and honestly, considering the heaviness of that moment, sort of give me a window for some levity and I asked him, well, most importantly, how\u8217\'20\'19s the hair?\par \par \uc2 The audience laughed and Don Jr proceeded to imitate his father\u8217\'20\'19s voice: \u8220\'20\'1C The hair\u8217\'20\'19s fine, Don, the hair\u8217\'20\'19s fine. A lot of blood in it but it\u8217\'20\'19s fine.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Reverting to his normal voice, Don Jr added:\par \par \uc2 To be shot and to stand up with that kind of resolve, I just felt like: you\u8217\'20\'19re the biggest badass I know. That was my opening salvo and then we started joking hair and I said, can I call you Evander Holyfield because of the little missing chunk of ear?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 [Heavyweight boxer Holyfield had a part of his ear bitten off by opponent Mike Tyson in 1997.]\par \par \uc2 Don Jr claimed this is why the world was at peace during Trump\u8217\'20\'19s presidency.\par \par \uc2 Compare and contrast that honestly to just about any clip of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  these days.One exudes strength, the other exudes weakness. And when you exude weakness, it\u8217\'20\'19s the nature of predation: predators prey on the weak. Our enemies will prey on us.\par \par \uc2 Even so, Don Jr promised that Trump\u8217\'20\'19s Thursday speech will be \u8220\'20\'1Ctoned down\u8221\'20\'1D and warned against complacency in the Republican ranks. \u8220\'20\'1CPeople are like, \u8216\'20\'18Oh, after Saturday it\u8217\'20\'19s over,\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D he told the Axios gathering.\par \par \uc2 Nothing is over. There\u8217\'20\'19s no level the other side won\u8217\'20\'19t go. There\u8217\'20\'19s no nonsense they won\u8217\'20\'19t play. This is not in the bag. We have to keep our foot on the gas every second of the day until November.\par \par \uc2 Don Jr welcomed the idea of \uc2 Robert Kennedy Jr\uc2  serving under Trump in a second term \u8211\'20\'13 \u8220\'20\'1CMaybe there\u8217\'20\'19s a great place for him somewhere in an administration\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 and described his own potential role in a presidential transition.\par \par \uc2 All I want to do is block the guys that would be a disaster. I want to block the liars. I want to block the guys that are pretending they\u8217\'20\'19re with you \u8230\'20\'26 You guys pick the guy that\u8217\'20\'19s right. I want the veto power to cut out each and every one of those people.\par \par \uc2 Asked by interviewer \uc2 Mike Allen\uc2  for his \u8220\'20\'1Cleast Trumpy\u8221\'20\'1D quality, Don Jr replied: \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t play golf.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.36pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.31pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Texas congresswoman \uc2 Veronica Escobar\uc2 , a co-chair of Biden\u8217\'20\'19s campaign, said the president will tout his record during remarks at the \uc2 UnidosUs\uc2  conference in Las Vegas on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 Among \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s accomplishments, she said, was being the steward of record low unemployment for Latinos. Latinos are also starting businesses at a record pace. Meanwhile, she added, crime is down and wages are up.\par \par \uc2 But polls have shown \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  making inroads with Hispanic voters, particularly men. Escobar said the Biden campaign was pouring resources into reaching Latino voters, but that more was needed before November.\par \par \uc2 Referencing the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/may/26/what-is-project-2025-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Heritage Foundation\u8217\'20\'19s radical plan }}}\uc2  to reshape the federal government, she said:\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19ve been talking to Latino communities, I\u8217\'20\'19ve traveled the country to meet with Latino groups, to hear them out, to talk to them about the president\u8217\'20\'19s positive vision for America and contrast that with the incredibly dark, terrifying vision that the Trump-Vance campaign has laid out through Project 2025.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere\u8217\'20\'19s a lot of work we still have to do to make sure that Latino voters feel heard and that we inspire them to get to the polls,\u8221\'20\'1D she continued. \u8220\'20\'1CThat\u8217\'20\'19s the work that we have been doing and will continue to do on the Biden-Harris campaign.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.30pm BST\par \par \uc2 Immigration advocates are pre-empting what they anticipate will be a \u8220\'20\'1Cdark and dystopian vision\u8221\'20\'1D on display during the second night of the Republican national convention, themed \u8220\'20\'1CMake America Safe Again.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The congresswoman \uc2 Veronica Escobar\uc2 , a co-chair of Biden\u8217\'20\'19s re-election campaign, said she wanted to \u8220\'20\'1Csound the alarm\u8221\'20\'1D on Republicans\u8217\'20\'19 escalating attacks on immigrants.\par \par \uc2 As the Democratic congresswoman from El Paso, Texas, where five years ago a white supremecist targeted Latino shoppers at a \uc2 Walmart\uc2  in the city, killing 23 people, Escobar said she knows first hand how dangerous rhetoric can have deadly consequences. She told reporters on a call Tuesday:\par \par \uc2 The incredibly dark vision that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and his running mate and the Republican GOP have in store for America is a throwback to very, very dark days that we have seen in American history.\par \par \uc2 She added that Republicans \u8220\'20\'1Cwant the American public to fear and loathe immigrants\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 On the call, advocates warned that Republicans would likely twist the facts and repeat many of their false claims about immigration and crime. \u8220\'20\'1CHere\u8217\'20\'19s what they won\u8217\'20\'19t tell you,\u8221\'20\'1D Vanessa C\u225\'00\'E1rdenas, executive director of America\u8217\'20\'19s Voice, said.\par \par \uc2 They will not tell you about the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/cbo-budget-outlook-debt-deficit-5954f45ee9a0c11fd4f91ac40260eb60"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 essential role that immigrants play}}}\uc2  in the Wisconsin economy and across the country. They won\u8217\'20\'19t tell you about the fact that there is no correlation between crime and immigration. And they also won\u8217\'20\'19t tell you that despite their anti-immigration crusade and the millions of political ads being spent this cycle on immigration, the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://news.gallup.com/poll/647123/sharply-americans-curb-immigration.aspx"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  support for citizenship is durable}}}\uc2  and consistent.\par \par \uc2 The quote by Vanessa C\u225\'00\'E1rdenas was amended.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.09pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.24pm BST\par \par \uc2 Asked about whether the assassination attempt against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  would alter the Biden team\u8217\'20\'19s messaging strategy moving forward, Biden campaign officials said that it would not.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe president and the vice-president have been very clear on their vision when it comes to the agenda that they want to put forward for Americans,\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 Quentin Fulks\uc2 , Biden\u8217\'20\'19s principal deputy campaign manager, said at the press conference in Milwaukee.\par \par \uc2 And we\u8217\'20\'19re going to continue to draw the contrast of what that work actually means and what it means for the lives of the American people.\par \par \uc2 At a time when political violence has escalated to dangerous levels, the senator \uc2 Cory Booker\uc2  implored Americans to support a candidate who would help the country heal and unite.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn this moment in our democracy, please vote for decency and kindness and empathy and grace. Those are the best American values,\u8221\'20\'1D Booker said.\par \par \uc2 The thing we really need in this country right now is patriotism. And patriotism is love of country, and you cannot love your country unless you truly love your countrymen and women \u8211\'20\'13 all of them.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.26pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.18pm BST\par \par \uc2 A police officer has reportedly shot an individual while working in Milwaukee as part of the security efforts surrounding the Republican national convention.\par \par \uc2 According to a Columbus Dispatch {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.dispatch.com/story/news/local/2024/07/16/columbus-police-officer-involved-in-shooting-in-milwaukee-ohio-republican-national-convention-rnc/74428246007/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 report}}}\uc2 , Brian Steel, president of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.dispatch.com/story/news/local/2024/03/11/columbus-police-dialogue-teams-mission-more-than-lip-service-ohio-protest-response-willis-johnson/72713478007/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Fraternal Order of Police Capitol City Lodge No 9}}}\uc2 , said details are limited but he was contacted about a possible shooting in Milwaukee involving a Columbus police officer.\par \par \uc2 The shooting occurred near North 14th and West Vliet Streets outside the security perimeter for the convention, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.jsonline.com/story/news/crime/2024/07/16/police-shooting-in-milwaukee-kills-1-outside-rnc-security-zone/74428028007/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according}}}\uc2  to the Milwaukee Journal Sentinel, citing law enforcement sources.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.21pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.11pm BST\par \par \uc2 Police officers have shot an individual near the Republican national convention in Milwaukee, according to the talkshow host Dan O\u8217\'20\'19Donnell.\par \par \uc2 More details to follow.\par \par \uc2 enltr??????BREAKING?????? A man is dead a mile away from the Republican National Convention in Milwaukee after he was shot by a Columbus, Ohio Police officer in Milwaukee to help with TNC security.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Dan O'Donnell (@DanODonnellShow) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/DanODonnellShow/status/1813288175521132759?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 16, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrThe intersection is in a residential neighborhood about a mile from the Fiserv Forum, site of the convention. The Columbus officers are in Milwaukee to provide security for the \uc2 RNC\uc2 . {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/nOLZejrYRR"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/nOLZejrYRR}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Dan O'Donnell (@DanODonnellShow) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/DanODonnellShow/status/1813284487029014734?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 16, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.18pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.06pm BST\par \par \uc2 During their press conference in Milwaukee, Biden campaign officials also defended their decision to move forward with a virtual roll call vote to nominate the president before the party\u8217\'20\'19s convention in August next month.\par \par \uc2 The roll call plan was initially formulated to meet a ballot deadline of 7 August in Ohio, but state legislators passed a bill to address that concern. Still, campaign officials said they would continue with their plans, even as 19 congressional Democrats have publicly called on Biden to step aside.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe have moved forward,\u8221\'20\'1D said \uc2 Quentin Fulks\uc2 , Biden\u8217\'20\'19s principal deputy campaign manager.\par \par \uc2 We instituted this before they had a fix, and we\u8217\'20\'19re going to continue on that path because we\u8217\'20\'19re not going to leave it up to them to change the rules again.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.02pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden campaign officials held a press conference in Milwaukee this morning, where they attacked \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s policy proposals and his selection of JD Vance as a running mate.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Republican party will always choose big, greedy, anti-union extremists over the working men and women of America,\u8221\'20\'1D said \uc2 Quentin Fulks\uc2 , Biden\u8217\'20\'19s principal deputy campaign manager.\par \par \uc2 President Biden is the most pro-union, pro-worker president this nation has ever seen.\par \par \uc2 Senator \uc2 Cory Booker\uc2  of New Jersey, who traveled to Milwaukee for the press conference, said Vance\u8217\'20\'19s selection alarmed him given the Ohio senator\u8217\'20\'19s past comments on the 2020 election.\par \par \uc2 In {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://abcnews.go.com/Politics/jd-vance-defends-trump-claims-invoking-jean-carroll/story?id=106925954"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 an interview}}}\uc2  with ABC News in February, Vance argued that Congress should not have immediately certified Biden\u8217\'20\'19s victory because of concerns about tainted results, even though Trump presented no substantive evidence of widespread election fraud.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CVice-President Pence did the right thing for our democracy,\u8221\'20\'1D Booker said.\par \par \uc2 And now [Trump] has chosen a vice-president who said that he would not have done that. If he was the vice-president then, he would have marched our country perhaps into its worst constitutional crisis in my lifetime.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.06pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.59pm BST\par \par \uc2 The congressman \uc2 Ruben Gallego\uc2 , who is running for a Senate seat in Arizona, has joined calls for the senator \uc2 Bob Menendez\uc2  to resign in the wake of his conviction on corruption charges.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CGiven today\u8217\'20\'19s guilty verdict, it is clear that Senator \uc2 Bob Menendez\uc2  must do what is right and resign,\u8221\'20\'1D Gallego said in a statement. \u8220\'20\'1CHis constituents and this country both deserve better.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.32pm BST\par \par \uc2 US received intel weeks ago about Iranian plot to assassinate Trump \u8211\'20\'13 report\par \par \uc2 The United States received intelligence from a human source in recent weeks about an Iranian plot to try to assassinate the former president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2024/07/16/politics/iran-plot-assassinate-trump-secret-service/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 CNN reported}}}\uc2  moments ago, citing people briefed on the matter.\par \par \uc2 CNN reported that there was no indication that the 20-year-old who tried to assassinate Trump on Saturday was connected to the plot, the Reuters news agency reports.\par \par \uc2 The cable news channel says there appears to be no connection between any such Iranian conspiracy and the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donald-trump-pennsylvania-rally-shooting"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 attempted assassination}}}\uc2  of Trump at the weekend by a gunman in Pennsylvania.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.49pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.28pm BST\par \par \uc2 Interim summary\par \par \uc2 Hello, US politics and Republican national convention (\uc2 RNC\uc2 ) watchers, it\u8217\'20\'19s been a busy news morning and there\u8217\'20\'19s much more in store this afternoon and evening, so stick with the blog to read about developments as they happen.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s where things stand:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Speakers due to address everyone at the \uc2 RNC\uc2  tonight in Milwaukee include late entrant \uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2 , the former US ambassador to the United Nations during the Trump administration and the Republican challenger who stayed in the primary contest against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  longer than any other rival, criticizing him assertively, until she had to cave and then of course threw her lot in with the former president. Also the House speaker, Mike Johnson, and Florida senator \uc2 Marco Rubio\uc2 , who was passed over to be the Republican vice-presidential nominee yesterday in favor of JD Vance.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The US senatorBob Menendez was found guilty in federal court in New York on all counts, in his federal corruption trial. The New Jersey Democrat, 70, had pleaded not guilty to 16 criminal charges including bribery, acting as a foreign agent and obstructing justice. He had refused to step down from the chamber during his case but after the verdict, Senate majority leader and New York Democrat \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  and Menendez\u8217\'20\'19s fellow New Jersey senator, \uc2 Cory Booker\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jul/16/republican-convention-trump-jd-vance-biden-latest-updates?page=with:block-6696ac488f089592211e4e78#block-6696ac488f089592211e4e78"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 called on}}}\uc2  him to resign. Menendez said he would appeal the verdict, but the governor of New Jersey, \uc2 Phil Murphy\uc2 , a Democrat, said the Senate should vote to oust him if he doesn\u8217\'20\'19t quit. Arizona congressman \uc2 Ruben Gallego\uc2  also called publicly for Menendez to resign.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The former first lady,Melania Trump, is expected to attend the Republican national convention on Thursday, when her husband, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , will formally accept his party\u8217\'20\'19s presidential nomination, NBC reported, citing a senior Trump campaign official. She hasn\u8217\'20\'19t much been seen or heard from on the campaign trail or during Trump\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/may/30/trump-trial-hush-money-verdict"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 criminal trial}}}\uc2  in New York. But {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/14/melania-trump-statement-donald-trump-rally-shooting"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 she issued}}}\uc2  a statement on Saturday after the former president was shot in an assassination attempt.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Democratic National Committee (DNC)\uc2  is quietly moving ahead with plans to formally nominate \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  as the party\u8217\'20\'19s presidential candidate weeks before the Democratic national convention next month, according to a report. Party chiefs are moving to kill off efforts to force Biden from the party\u8217\'20\'19s presidential ticket by rushing ahead with plans for convention delegates to vote electronically in a week-long roll call starting in late July, Axios reported.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy\uc2 , the biotech entrepreneur and former Republican presidential candidate, said he is interested in filling the Ohio Senate seat occupied by JD Vance, if the Trump-Vance ticket wins in the presidential election this November and Vance, a US senator from Ohio, has to relinquish his seat. He is a peer of Vance\u8217\'20\'19s at Yale Law School.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The director of the \uc2 US Secret Service\uc2 , Kimberly Cheatle, said that the attempted assassination of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  at a Pennsylvania campaign rally on Saturday was not acceptable adding that though \u8220\'20\'1Cthe buck stops with me\u8221\'20\'1D, she would not resign. \u8220\'20\'1CIt was unacceptable,\u8221\'20\'1D Kimberly Cheatle{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://abcnews.go.com/US/trump-rally-shooting-unacceptable-secret-service-director-abc-exclusive/story?id=111962314"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told ABC News}}}\uc2  on yesterday evening. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd it\u8217\'20\'19s something that shouldn\u8217\'20\'19t happen again.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Robert F Kennedy Jr\uc2 , running for the White House as an independent candidate, has apologized to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  after footage of a private phone call between the two was leaked online. In the video of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/robert-f-kennedy-jr"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 RJK Jr}}}\uc2  standing with his phone talking to Trump, the former president can be heard discussing the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donald-trump-pennsylvania-rally-shooting"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 assassination attempt}}}\uc2  on him at the weekend. He described the bullet that grazed his ear as feeling like \u8220\'20\'1Cthe world\u8217\'20\'19s largest mosquito\u8221\'20\'1D. Trump can also be heard criticizing vaccines, with RFK Jr being known as a vehement anti-vaxxer, and telling Kennedy that \u8220\'20\'1Cwe\u8217\'20\'19re going to win\u8221\'20\'1D the election in November.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The Republican national convention ( {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/republican-national-convention-2024"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 RNC}}}\uc2  ) headed into its second day in Milwaukee, Wisconsin \u8211\'20\'13 now with \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  as the party\u8217\'20\'19s official presidential nominee and Ohio senator JD Vance as his running mate.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.10pm BST\par \par \uc2 The New Jersey senator \uc2 Cory Booker\uc2  said that the need for his counterpart, \uc2 Bob Menendez\uc2 , to resign after being found guilty by the jury in a federal corruption case was urgent.\par \par \uc2 Posting on X, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/SenBooker/status/1813271577435512937"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Booker said}}}\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Cwith this conviction, the urgency for Senator Menendez to step down and for the governor to appoint a replacement has even more urgency\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Phil Murphy\uc2 , the governor of New Jersey, also a Democrat, will have the duty of appointing someone to fill Menendez\u8217\'20\'19s seat if he resigns or is ousted from the Senate, as the seat would become vacant between elections.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.19pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.05pm BST\par \par \uc2 Cory Booker\uc2  joins chorus calling on Senator Menendez to resign\par \par \uc2 New Jersey\u8217\'20\'19s junior US senator, \uc2 Cory Booker\uc2 , moments ago joined other senior figures in calling on the state\u8217\'20\'19s senior senator, \uc2 Bob Menendez\uc2 , to resign from Congress following his conviction in a federal corruption trial earlier today.\par \par \uc2 Booker, a fellow Democrat, to whom Menendez was a mentor, posted a statement on X, formerly \uc2 Twitter\uc2 , calling it \u8220\'20\'1Ca dark painful day for the people of New Jersey\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Booker had already called on Menendez to resign once, earlier in the legal process, to no avail, but with Tuesday\u8217\'20\'19s overwhelming conviction on all 16 counts by a jury, Booker joined the Senate majority leader, \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2 , and the New Jersey governor, \uc2 Phil Murphy\uc2 , in issuing calls today for Menendez to step down.\par \par \uc2 The junior senator said that Menendez had was afforded his due process rights and able to mount a full defense before a jury of his peers, but was convicted nonetheless.\par \par \uc2 enltrMy statement on Menendez trial verdict {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/15Unn6uVgi"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/15Unn6uVgi}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Sen. \uc2 Cory Booker\uc2  (@SenBooker) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SenBooker/status/1813271577435512937?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 16, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.07pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.53pm BST\par \par \uc2 The US senator \uc2 Bob Menendez\uc2  will appeal his conviction at trial on charges related to corruption, after being found guilty this morning in a federal court in New York.\par \par \uc2 The New Jersey senator, 70, was convicted on 16 criminal charges including bribery, acting as a foreign agent and obstructing justice.\par \par \uc2 The governor of New Jersey, the Democrat \uc2 Phil Murphy\uc2 , stated moments ago that if Menendez refuses to resign from his seat that the congressional chamber should vote to expel him, Reuters reported.\par \par \uc2 Murphy had posted on X, formerly \uc2 Twitter\uc2 , that the verdict \u8220\'20\'1Cdemonstrates that the Senator broke the law, violated the trust of his constituents, and betrayed his oath of office. In America, everyone \u8211\'20\'13 no matter how powerful \u8211\'20\'13 is accountable to our laws.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrToday's verdict finding Senator \uc2 Bob Menendez\uc2  guilty on 16 counts demonstrates that the Senator broke the law, violated the trust of his constituents, and betrayed his oath of office.\par \par \uc2 In America, everyone \u8211\'20\'13 no matter how powerful \u8211\'20\'13 is accountable to our laws. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/ljJrQFB2eu"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/ljJrQFB2eu}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Governor \uc2 Phil Murphy\uc2  (@GovMurphy) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/GovMurphy/status/1813264740581249273?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 16, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.56pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.23pm BST\par \par \uc2 Schumer calls on Menendez to resign after conviction\par \par \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2 , the Senate majority leader, has called on \uc2 Bob Menendez\uc2  to resign after the Democratic senator from New York {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jul/16/republican-convention-trump-jd-vance-biden-latest-updates?page=with:block-6696a5a08f08e299b199306e#block-6696a5a08f08e299b199306e"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 was convicted }}}\uc2  on all 16 criminal counts he faced including bribery at his corruption trial.\par \par \uc2 Schumer, in a post to X, wrote:\par \par \uc2 In light of this guilty verdict, Senator Menendez must now do what is right for his constituents, the Senate, and our country, and resign.\par \par \uc2 enltrIn light of this guilty verdict, Senator Menendez must now do what is right for his constituents, the Senate, and our country, and resign.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  (@SenSchumer) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SenSchumer/status/1813261987809210648?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 16, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.57pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.16pm BST\par \par \uc2 RNC\uc2  speakers tonight include Haley, DeSantis, Rubio and Johnson\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s presidential primary opponents, the former South Carolina governor \uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2  and the Florida governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , are expected to speak at the Republican national convention today.\par \par \uc2 Among those scheduled to speak on Tuesday are:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 House speaker Mike Johnson\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Former \uc2 UN\uc2  ambassador \uc2 Nikki Haley\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Florida governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Florida senator \uc2 Marco Rubio\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Florida senator \uc2 Rick Scott\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Arkansas governor \uc2 Sarah Huckabee Sanders\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 West Virginia governor \uc2 Jim Justice\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Louisiana congressman Steve Scalise\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 New York congresswoman \uc2 Elise Stefanik\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Minnesota congressman \uc2 Tom Emmer\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Entrepreneur \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Republican National Committee\uc2  co-chair \uc2 Lara Trump\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Arizona Senate candidate Kari Lake\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Ohio Senate candidate \uc2 Bernie Moreno\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.19pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.11pm BST\par \par \uc2 I just spoke with one of the protesters, Caroline Smith, who is the executive director of the progressive anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  uprising. They\u8217\'20\'19re standing just outside an outdoor area where Republican attendees are having brunch.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere\u8217\'20\'19s this fancy, rich neighborhood with a bunch of people in here discussing the road to 2024 just days, hours, after they have erased the lives of unborn people from their own platform,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 The GOP is supposed to be the pro-life party and they watered down, completely erased pre-born children from their platform.\par \par \uc2 You can faintly hear the protest inside the hotel where the event is set to take place. So far I\u8217\'20\'19ve seen the Republican congresswoman \uc2 Elise Stefanik\uc2  and the \uc2 US Senate\uc2  candidate Kari Lake here.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.17pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.05pm BST\par \par \uc2 Senator \uc2 Bob Menendez\uc2  found guilty in federal corruption trial\par \par \uc2 The senator \uc2 Bob Menendez\uc2  has been found guilty on all counts in his federal corruption trial.\par \par \uc2 The New Jersey Democrat, 70, pleaded not guilty to 16 criminal charges including bribery, acting as a foreign agent and obstructing justice.\par \par \uc2 Menendez denied accepting bribes \u8211\'20\'13 including gold bars, a luxury car and almost half a million dollars in cash \u8211\'20\'13 as he promoted Egypt\u8217\'20\'19s interests in his influential role as chair of the Senate foreign relations committee.\par \par \uc2 Menendez\u8217\'20\'19s wife, Nadine Menendez, was also charged in the case, but her trial was postponed indefinitely after her breast cancer diagnosis.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.18pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.51pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Biden campaign will resume political advertising this week, according to Reuters, days after it suspended ads following the attempted assassination of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 presidential campaign, already in disarray amid uncertainty over Biden\u8217\'20\'19s fate after his calamitous debate performance, was plunged into further confusion after the shooting.\par \par \uc2 They suspended a $50m advertising blitz and quickly pulled television attack ads, in moves consistent with Biden\u8217\'20\'19s plea in a Sunday night speech from the White House to \u8220\'20\'1Clower the temperature in our politics\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The Biden campaign also told staff members to \u8220\'20\'1Crefrain from issuing any comments on social media or in public\u8221\'20\'1D and to \u8220\'20\'1Cpause any proactive campaign communication across all platforms and in all circumstances until we know more\u8221\'20\'1D, NBC {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/2024-election/democratic-effort-replace-biden-comes-standstill-trump-rally-rcna161751"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 Peter Navarro\uc2 , the former Trump White House adviser who is currently in jail on contempt of Congress charges, is expected to speak at the Republican national convention after his release from prison.\par \par \uc2 Navarro is due to finish his four-month sentence at the federal prison camp in Miami on Wednesday morning.\par \par \uc2 According to CNN, Navarro\u8217\'20\'19s fiancee plans to pick him up from prison and drive him to Miami airport, where a private plan provided by his book publisher will be waiting to take him to the convention in Milwaukee.\par \par \uc2 Navarro was found guilty in September of contempt of Congress charges for refusing to cooperate with a congressional investigation into the 6 January 2021 attack.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.50pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.34pm BST\par \par \uc2 Melania Trump to attend \uc2 RNC\uc2  on Thursday \u8211\'20\'13 report\par \par \uc2 The former first lady Melania Trump is expected to attend the Republican national convention on Thursday, when \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  will formally accept his party\u8217\'20\'19s presidential nomination, NBC reported, citing a senior Trump campaign official.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.24pm BST\par \par \uc2 I\u8217\'20\'19ve just arrived at a hotel in downtown Milwaukee, where Chris LaCivita, one of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s campaign managers is set to speak shortly. Outside, a small group of anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  protesters has gathered.\par \par \uc2 enltrOutside of an event with Chris LaCivita in downtown Milwaukee, protesters are chanting \u8220\'20\'1C\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is murder\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/cT9bGMYUiD"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/cT9bGMYUiD}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Sam Levine (@srl) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/srl/status/1813245152900882643?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 16, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 Earlier this month, the \uc2 RNC\uc2  omitted a national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban from its platform {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://amp.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/09/republican-abortion-ban-policy-platform-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 for the first time}}}\uc2  in 40 years.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.14pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and his running mate, Ohio senator JD Vance, are scheduled to appear in the hall of the Republican national convention every night, according to AP.\par \par \uc2 Vance is expected to give his own speech on Wednesday night, and Trump will headline Thursday night\u8217\'20\'19s closing evening.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.05pm BST\par \par \uc2 JD Vance, a venture capitalist turned Ohio junior senator who rose to fame with his 2016 memoir Hillbilly Elegy, once said he \u8220\'20\'1Cnever liked Trump\u8221\'20\'1D and that he was \u8220\'20\'1Cleading people in a very dark direction\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 He has now been declared as \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s running mate ahead of the 2024 presidential election. So what changed?\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s our video profile of Vance:\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 Democrats to push ahead with Biden nomination before convention\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Democratic National Committee\uc2  is quietly moving ahead with plans to formally nominate \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  as the party\u8217\'20\'19s presidential candidate weeks before the Democratic national convention next month, according to a report.\par \par \uc2 Democratic bosses are moving to kill off efforts to force Biden from the party\u8217\'20\'19s presidential ticket by rushing ahead with plans for convention delegates to vote electronically in a week-long roll call starting in late July, Axios {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.axios.com/2024/07/16/biden-dnc-vote-nomination-states-2024-election?utm_source=newsletter&utm_medium=email&utm_campaign=newsletter_axiosam&stream=top"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  reported}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 If a majority of the 4,000 delegates back Biden, it will make his candidacy technically unchallengeable when the convention starts on 19 August.\par \par \uc2 The move comes while the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/12/biden-press-conference-reaction"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 rebellion triggered by last month\u8217\'20\'19s debate fiasco}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 which prompted {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/14/biden-hits-back-at-calls-for-withdrawal-as-democrats-are-locked-in-battle-of-wills"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 multiple calls from within the party for Biden to be replaced}}}\uc2  as the candidate \u8211\'20\'13 has stalled following Saturday\u8217\'20\'19s failed assassination attempt on \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . Under the plan, the electronic vote would probably start on 29 July and end on 5 August, meaning Biden will in effect secure his candidacy if he can survive the mutiny for another two weeks.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 Ramaswamy interested in filling Vance's Ohio Senate seat \u8211\'20\'13 report\par \par \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy\uc2 , the biotech entrepreneur and former Republican presidential candidate, said he is interested in filling the Ohio Senate seat occupied by JD Vance.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI would strongly consider it if I were asked to serve,\u8221\'20\'1D Ramaswamy said about the Senate seat that would be vacated if \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is re-elected to the White House with Vance as his vice-president, the Hill reported. He added:\par \par \uc2 I would also want to have a serious conversation with President Trump about the other ways I could have an impact on the country. My top passion is taking on the regulatory state.\par \par \uc2 Ramaswamy, who was speaking in an interview with NBC News at the Republican national convention, said he had not discussed the issue yet with the Ohio governor, \uc2 Mike DeWine\uc2 , but noted: \u8220\'20\'1CI would strongly consider it if asked.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He added that he has also discussed with Trump the possibility of serving in a future cabinet, saying:\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19ve talked about a lot of different possibilities, President Trump and I. I mean, we talk regularly. I spoke to him, actually most recently, it was after midnight on the night that he suffered that injury, tragedy, assassination attempt on Saturday night. So, we\u8217\'20\'19ve talked about different ideas, potentially, in a cabinet or other ways of driving change.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.43pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.28pm BST\par \par \uc2 Before \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  chose JD Vance as his running mate, there was some speculation that the junior Ohio senator\u8217\'20\'19s presence on the party\u8217\'20\'19s presidential ticket might boost the Republican \uc2 Bernie Moreno\uc2  in his effort to unseat the Ohio senator \uc2 Sherrod Brown\uc2 , the Democratic incumbent.\par \par \uc2 Republicans are bullish about winning the Senate, and the Ohio race is seen as one of their best opportunities to flip a seat.\par \par \uc2 The race was already going to be a challenge for Brown, who will have to attract some of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s supporters to defy the political headwinds in his state. Vance\u8217\'20\'19s nomination is unlikely to change those dynamics, said Kyle Kondik of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://centerforpolitics.org/crystalball/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Crystal Ball}}}\uc2 , which has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://centerforpolitics.org/crystalball/2024-senate/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 rated the race a \u8220\'20\'1Ctoss up\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2 . Kondik wrote in an email:\par \par \uc2 Trump was already going to win [Ohio] and Vance has not been around all that long and didn\u8217\'20\'19t perform all that well in his 2022 race relative to other Republicans.\par \par \uc2 He noted that Vance, author of Hillbilly Elegy, faced a stronger Democratic opponent in the former Ohio congressman \uc2 Tim Ryan\uc2  than other Republicans running in the midterm cycle, but nevertheless was not viewed as an influential political force in the state.\par \par \uc2 Ohio, once a perennial presidential battleground, is now seen as safely Republican. Brown has managed to defy the trend, winning a tough re-election race in 2018. The Democrat\u8217\'20\'19s team is squarely focused on Moreno and is not adjusting strategy in any way as a result of Vance\u8217\'20\'19s nomination.\par \par \uc2 Kondik, who authored The Bellwether, an analysis of Ohio\u8217\'20\'19s presidential voting history, said, contrary to popular perception, running mates rarely deliver a home state boost to anymore.\par \par \uc2 The last major party vice-presidential candidate to hail from Ohio, John Bricker, may have helped Republican presidential nominee Thomas Dewey clinch the state, Kondik said. But that was in 1944, and he ultimately lost the election to the incumbent, Franklin Roosevelt.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.10pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.22pm BST\par \par \uc2 Adam Schiff, a California Democrat running for Senate, warned donors in a private meeting on Saturday that his party was likely to suffer overwhelming losses if \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  remained at the top of the ticket, according to a report.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI think if he is our nominee, I think we lose,\u8221\'20\'1D Schiff said during the meeting, the \uc2 New York Times{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2024/07/16/us/politics/schiff-biden-democrats.html#:~:text=Representative%20Adam%20B.%20Schiff%2C%20the,with%20direct%20knowledge%20of%20Mr."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported.}}}\par \par \uc2 And we may very, very well lose the Senate and lose our chance to take back the House.\par \par \uc2 Schiff also said during the fundraiser held on Saturday in East Hampton, New York, that Biden and his campaign staff had been generally unwilling to engage the views of outside pollsters and political experts, the report said.\par \par \uc2 At least one donor who attended the event said he left dejected, believing that Biden\u8217\'20\'19s chances of winning were now slim and that they should focus on giving their time and money to down-ballot candidates in the hopes of salvaging something for the Democratic party, it said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.25pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.15pm BST\par \par \uc2 Secret Service director says \u8216\'20\'18the buck stops with me\u8217\'20\'19 after Trump rally shooting\par \par \uc2 The attempted assassination of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  at a Pennsylvania rally on Saturday was \u8220\'20\'1Cunacceptable\u8221\'20\'1D, the director of the \uc2 US Secret Service\uc2  said, adding that though \u8220\'20\'1Cthe buck stops with me\u8221\'20\'1D, she would not resign.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt was unacceptable,\u8221\'20\'1D Kimberly Cheatle {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://abcnews.go.com/US/trump-rally-shooting-unacceptable-secret-service-director-abc-exclusive/story?id=111962314"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told ABC News}}}\uc2  on Monday. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd it\u8217\'20\'19s something that shouldn\u8217\'20\'19t happen again.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Cheatle told ABC in her interview:\par \par \uc2 It was obviously a situation that as a Secret Service agent, no one ever wants to occur in their career. The buck stops with me. I am the director of the Secret Service, and I need to make sure that we are performing a review and that we are giving resources to our personnel as necessary.\par \par \uc2 She would not resign, she said.\par \par \uc2 A former agent, Cheatle was appointed by \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  in 2022 as the 27th director of the Secret Service and the second woman in the role. Some Republicans calling for her to quit have said her appointment was a result of policies meant to increase diversity.\par \par \uc2 The Republican-run House oversight committee has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://oversight.house.gov/release/comer-announces-hearing-with-u-s-secret-service-director-on-the-attempted-assassination-of-president-trump/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 called}}}\uc2  Cheatle to testify next Monday, 22 July. The committee chair, James Comer of Kentucky, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://oversight.house.gov/release/comer-oversight-committee-republicans-call-on-secret-service-to-provide-documents-and-communications-regarding-the-assassination-attempt-of-president-trump/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 United States Secret Service\uc2  has a no-fail mission, yet it failed on Saturday when a madman attempted to assassinate president Trump, killed an innocent victim, and harmed others. Americans demand answers from Director Kimberly Cheatle.\par \par \uc2 Cheatle has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.secretservice.gov/newsroom/releases/2024/07/statement-us-secret-service-director-kimberly-cheatle"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  she will \u8220\'20\'1Cwork with the appropriate congressional committees on any oversight action\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cparticipate fully\u8221\'20\'1D in an independent review announced by Biden.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.05pm BST\par \par \uc2 Jack Black has put his rock duo Tenacious D on hold following an onstage comment made by his bandmate Kyle Gass, which seemed to support the assassination of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Gass was celebrating his birthday during a concert in Sydney on Sunday, with a cake presented to him on stage. Black told Gass to make a wish as he blew out the candles, and Gass responded, to audience laughter, \u8220\'20\'1CDon\u8217\'20\'19t miss Trump next time\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 a reference to the failed assassination attempt by 20-year-old Thomas Matthew Crooks at a Trump rally the previous day.\par \par \uc2 Black continued with the concert following Gass\u8217\'20\'19s comments, but has now put out a statement:\par \par \uc2 I was blindsided by what was said at the show on Sunday. I would never condone hate speech or encourage political violence in any form. After much reflection, I no longer feel it is appropriate to continue the Tenacious D tour, and all future creative plans are on hold. I am grateful to the fans for their support and understanding.\par \par \uc2 Tenacious D had been due to perform four more dates across Australia before travelling to New Zealand.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.57pm BST\par \par \uc2 Senior figures in Britain\u8217\'20\'19s Labour party have rejected comments by \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s vice-presidential pick, JD Vance, that the UK could become the first \u8220\'20\'1Ctruly Islamist country that will get a nuclear weapon\u8221\'20\'1D under the party.\par \par \uc2 Angela Rayner, the deputy prime minister, told \uc2 ITV\uc2  that Vance had said \u8220\'20\'1Cquite a lot of fruity things in the past\u8221\'20\'1D and she looked forward to meeting him and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  if they won the US election in November.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t recognise that characterisation. I\u8217\'20\'19m very proud of the election success that Labour had recently,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 We won votes across all different communities, across the whole of the country, and we\u8217\'20\'19re interested in governing on behalf of Britain and also working with our international allies.\par \par \uc2 The jibe is likely to be embarrassing for the UK\u8217\'20\'19s foreign secretary, \uc2 David Lammy\uc2 , who has attempted to build bridges with Vance in recent months, comparing their impoverished childhoods. Lammy described Vance as a friend in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/politics/article/2024/may/08/david-lammy-tells-us-republicans-he-can-find-common-cause-with-donald-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 short speech}}}\uc2  he gave at the \uc2 Hudson Institute\uc2  in May when he was in opposition.\par \par \uc2 Vance was speaking at the National Conservatism conference last week, where he said:\par \par \uc2 I have to beat up on the UK \u8211\'20\'13 just one additional thing. I was talking with a friend recently and we were talking about, you know, one of the big dangers in the world, of course, is nuclear proliferation, though, of course, the Biden administration doesn\u8217\'20\'19t care about it. And I was talking about, you know, what is the first truly Islamist country that will get a nuclear weapon, and we were like, maybe it\u8217\'20\'19s Iran, you know, maybe Pakistan already kind of counts, and then we sort of finally decided maybe it\u8217\'20\'19s actually the UK, since Labour just took over.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.53pm BST\par \par \uc2 Who is JD Vance, Trump\u8217\'20\'19s vice-presidential pick?\par \par \uc2 The announcement of JD Vance as \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s running mate in the presidential race on Monday marked the culmination of Vance\u8217\'20\'19s stunning political evolution over the past several years.\par \par \uc2 Vance was once an outspoken critic of Trump, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://ohiocapitaljournal.com/2022/04/19/americas-hitler-old-j-d-vance-message-turns-up-in-heated-senate-primary/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 mocking}}}\uc2  him as \u8220\'20\'1CAmerica\u8217\'20\'19s Hitler\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Ca total fraud\u8221\'20\'1D. But Vance came to embrace Trump as he sought a Senate seat in 2022, and he eventually won the former president\u8217\'20\'19s endorsement in a crowded Republican primary.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHe\u8217\'20\'19s the guy that said some bad shit about me,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/apr/29/jd-vance-senate-ohio-trump-influence-republican-party"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  at a rally in 2022. \u8220\'20\'1CIf I went by that standard, I don\u8217\'20\'19t think I would have ever endorsed anybody in the country.\u8221\'20\'1D Vance echoed that assessment, telling rally-goers:\par \par \uc2 The president is right. I wasn\u8217\'20\'19t always nice, but the simple fact is, he\u8217\'20\'19s the best president of my lifetime, and he revealed the corruption in this country like nobody else.\par \par \uc2 Vance first rose to fame in 2016 following the publication of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/books/2016/dec/07/hillbilly-elegy-by-jd-vance-review"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Hillbilly Elegy}}}\uc2 , which detailed his upbringing in south-western Ohio and his later ascension to Yale law school. The book was later adapted into a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/film/2020/nov/10/hillbilly-elegy-review-ron-howard-glenn-close-amy-adams-jd-vance"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 2020 film}}}\uc2  starring Glenn Close and Amy Adams.\par \par \uc2 In the months following Trump\u8217\'20\'19s victory in the 2016 presidential election, Vance\u8217\'20\'19s account of his family\u8217\'20\'19s experiences with poverty and drug addiction came to be viewed by some critics as a revealing portrait into the lives of Americans who helped determine the outcome of the election.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/15/trump-vp-pick-jd-vance"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Read our full profile of JD Vance.}}}\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/15/trump-vp-pick-jd-vance"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Who is JD Vance, Trump\u8217\'20\'19s vice-presidential pick?}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.56pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.42pm BST\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Democratic National Committee\uc2  has released its first media campaign since \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 s naming of the Ohio senator JD Vance as his running mate, according to the Hill\u8217\'20\'19s Julia Manchester.\par \par \uc2 The DNC {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://democrats.org/news/dnc-statement-on-donald-trump-announcing-j-d-vance-as-his-running-mate/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 issued}}}\uc2  a statement on Monday that described Vance as having \u8220\'20\'1Cchampioned and enabled Trump\u8217\'20\'19s worst policies for years\u8221\'20\'1D, adding that he \u8220\'20\'1Cembodies Maga \u8211\'20\'13 with an out-of-touch extreme agenda and plans to help Trump force his Project 2025 agenda on the American people\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Let\u8217\'20\'19s be clear: A Trump-Vance ticket would undermine our democracy, our freedoms, and our future.\par \par \uc2 enltrNEW: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/DNC?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @DNC}}}\uc2  launches its first paid media campaign hitting the Trump-Vance ticket\par \par \uc2 16 billboards and a mobile billboard in the Milwaukee area as the \uc2 RNC\uc2  takes place this week {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/zAysXALVY7"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/zAysXALVY7}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Julia Manchester (@JuliaManch) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JuliaManch/status/1813197182293483772?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 16, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.34pm BST\par \par \uc2 Here are some of the defining images from day one of the Republican national convention.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.38pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.18pm BST\par \par \uc2 RFK Jr apologizes to Trump for leaked video of their private call\par \par \uc2 Robert F Kennedy Jr\uc2  has apologized to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  after footage of a private call between the two was leaked online.\par \par \uc2 In the video, Trump can be heard discussing the assassination attempt on him on Saturday to Kennedy Jr and describing the bullet that grazed his ear as feeling like \u8220\'20\'1Cthe world\u8217\'20\'19s largest mosquito\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The former president can also be heard criticizing vaccines and telling Kennedy that \u8220\'20\'1Cwe\u8217\'20\'19re going to win\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 enltrA video of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s call with RFK Jr. was leaked - Trump talks about vaccines, tells RFK Jr. doing something with him would be \u8220\'20\'1Cbig,\u8221\'20\'1D mentioned his call with Biden and said the bullet was like \u8220\'20\'1Cthe world\u8217\'20\'19s largest mosquito.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 RFK Jr apologized for the leak. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/Z6DQ955P6W"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/Z6DQ955P6W}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Meridith McGraw (@meridithmcgraw) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/meridithmcgraw/status/1813201574518288387?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 16, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 Kennedy, in a post to X this morning, said he was \u8220\'20\'1Cmortified\u8221\'20\'1D about the leak and said he wanted to \u8220\'20\'1Capologize to the president\u8221\'20\'1D, referring to former president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 enltrWhen President Trump called me I was taping with an in-house videographer. I should have ordered the videographer to stop recording immediately. I am mortified that this was posted. I apologize to the president.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Robert F. Kennedy Jr\uc2  (@RobertKennedyJr) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RobertKennedyJr/status/1813198830281593269?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 16, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/16/rfk-jr-trump-phone-call-video-recording"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 RFK Jr apologises after leaked phone call in which Trump seems to offer deal}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.12pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.10pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  met with the independent presidential candidate \uc2 Robert F Kennedy Jr\uc2  on Monday in Milwaukee, just hours before Trump was officially named the Republican party\u8217\'20\'19s presidential nominee.\par \par \uc2 The Kennedy campaign confirmed the meeting after reports that Kennedy was planning to drop out of the race and possible endorse Trump, the \uc2 New York Times{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2024/07/15/us/politics/rfk-jr-trump-rnc.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  reported}}}\uc2 . The report cites Stefanie Spear, a spokesperson for the Kennedy campaign:\par \par \uc2 Yes, Mr. Kennedy met with President Trump today to discuss national unity, and he hopes to meet with leaders of the Democratic Party as well. And no, he is not dropping out of the race.\par \par \uc2 She added:\par \par \uc2 He is the only pro-environment, pro-choice, antiwar candidate who beats \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in head-to-head polls.\par \par \uc2 The meeting was brokered by former Fox News host \uc2 Tucker Carlson\uc2 , according to the report.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.51pm BST\par \par \uc2 As the Republican national convention kicked off in Milwaukee on Monday, about a thousand people led a spirited demonstration against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and his party on the streets outside.\par \par \uc2 The March on the \uc2 RNC\uc2  gathered in a park a couple of blocks from the Fiserv Forum, where Trump was formally nominated at the Republican candidate for president.\par \par \uc2 Armed with pro-Palestinian flags, anti-Trump posters and even a ventriloquist\u8217\'20\'19s puppet of Trump, the coalition of progressive groups marched through downtown Milwaukee, stopping traffic and chanting \u8220\'20\'1CFree Palestine\u8221\'20\'1D as they walked.\par \par \uc2 The group had begun proceedings with a rally at Red Arrow park, where Omar Flores, co-chair of the Coalition to March on the \uc2 RNC\uc2 , was among the speakers. Flores told the Guardian:\par \par \uc2 Today is about telling the Republicans that they\u8217\'20\'19re not welcome in our city, they\u8217\'20\'19re not welcome anywhere and anywhere they show up, we\u8217\'20\'19re going to show the opposition to their ideas.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/15/republican-national-convention-protest"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Not welcome in our city\u8217\'20\'19: protesters march on Republican convention}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.56pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.47pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Milwaukee mayor, Cavalier Johnson, said demonstrations that took place outside the Republican national convention yesterday proceeded \u8220\'20\'1Cwithout any major problem\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Two arrests were made on Monday, Johnson said, AP reported. One when someone tried to climb a fence into a restricted area and a second arrest when a demonstrator was blocking traffic and did not move when officers repeatedly asked her to do so. Johnson said:\par \par \uc2 No one was hurt and there was no significant property damage that was reported as a result of these demonstrations.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.49pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.39pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  was pressed, during his interview with NBC Nightly News anchor Lester Holt on Monday, on whether he had done any \u8220\'20\'1Csoul-searching\u8221\'20\'1D about whether his language could \u8220\'20\'1Cincite people who are not balanced\u8221\'20\'1D. Biden said:\par \par \uc2 Look. How do you talk about the threat to democracy, which is real, when the president says things like he says? Do you just not say anything because you might incite somebody?\par \par \uc2 Look. I have not engaged in that rhetoric. Now, my opponent has engaged in that rhetoric. He talks about there will be a bloodbath if he loses, talking about how he\u8217\'20\'19s going to forgive all the \u8230\'20\'26 actually, I guess suspend the sentence of all that were arrested and sentenced to go jail because of what happened at the Capitol. I\u8217\'20\'19m not out there making fun of \u8230\'20\'26 like, remember the picture of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  when \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s husband was hit with a hammer, talking about it? Joking about it?\par \par \uc2 Biden suggested that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s apparent forgiveness of January 6 rioters was also an incitement to violence.\par \par \uc2 When you say that there\u8217\'20\'19s nothing wrong with going to the Capitol \u8230\'20\'26 putting up a noose for the former vice-president, and then you say you\u8217\'20\'19re going to forgive people for that?\par \par \uc2 enltrLester Holt, asking Biden about the use of heated political rhetoric: \u8220\'20\'1CYou said, "It\u8217\'20\'19s time to put Trump in the bullseye.\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Biden: \u8220\'20\'1CIt was a mistake to use the word.\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/EaFQXbciMd"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/EaFQXbciMd}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1812970155107905621?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 15, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.41pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.30pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has addressed his previous comments about putting \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Cin the bullseye\u8221\'20\'1D, saying he thinks there needs to be more focus on the former president\u8217\'20\'19s agenda.\par \par \uc2 During a high-stakes conversation at the White House with NBC Nightly News anchor Lester Holt on Monday, Biden was asked about the language he had used to describe Trump \u8211\'20\'13 as an \u8220\'20\'1Cexistential threat\u8221\'20\'1D, and, on a call with Democratic donors, that \u8220\'20\'1Cit\u8217\'20\'19s time to put Trump in the bullseye\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 and the consequences for the election of the attempted assassination of his opponent two days ago in Pennsylvania. Biden said:\par \par \uc2 I didn\u8217\'20\'19t say crosshairs. I was talking about \u8216\'20\'18focus on\u8217\'20\'19. The truth of the matter was, I guess what I was talking about at the time was, there was very little focus on Trump\u8217\'20\'19s agenda.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe term was \u8216\'20\'18bullseye\u8217\'20\'19,\u8221\'20\'1D Holt said. Biden replied:\par \par \uc2 It was a mistake to use the word. I didn\u8217\'20\'19t mean \u8230\'20\'26 I didn\u8217\'20\'19t say crosshairs. I meant bullseye \u8230\'20\'26 I meant focus on it. Focus on what he\u8217\'20\'19s doing. Focus on his policies. Focus on the number of lies he told in the debate.\par \par \uc2 Biden fumbled somewhat during the answer, leaving it unclear whether he was apologizing for telling donors to put Trump in a bullseye or whether he was correcting himself after using the word \u8220\'20\'1Ccrosshairs\u8221\'20\'1D instead of \u8220\'20\'1Cbullseye\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.26pm BST\par \par \uc2 Liz Cheney\uc2 , the former Republican congresswoman and co-chair of the House January 6 committee, has issued a warning about \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s running mate, the Ohio senator JD Vance.\par \par \uc2 Vance has \u8220\'20\'1Cpledged he would do what \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t \u8211\'20\'13 overturn an election and illegally seize power\u8221\'20\'1D, Cheney wrote in a post to X this morning. \u8220\'20\'1CHe says the president can ignore the rulings of our courts.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He would capitulate to Russia and sacrifice the freedom of our allies in Ukraine. The Trump GOP is no longer the party of Lincoln, Reagan or the Constitution.\par \par \uc2 enltrJD Vance has pledged he would do what \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t - overturn an election and illegally seize power. He says the president can ignore the rulings of our courts. He would capitulate to Russia and sacrifice the freedom of our allies in Ukraine. The Trump GOP is no longer the\u8230\'20\'26 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/l0O64J3pSj"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/l0O64J3pSj}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Liz Cheney\uc2  (@Liz_Cheney) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Liz_Cheney/status/1813182588476952702?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 16, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.34pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.14pm BST\par \par \uc2 Key takeaways from day one of the \uc2 RNC\par \par \uc2 Just two days after a gunman targeted a Trump campaign rally in Pennsylvania, leaving the candidate grazed by a bullet and one of his supporters dead, the Republican national convention kicked off in Milwaukee in a strikingly normal fashion.\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , who made his first public appearance but did not yet address the convention, has now been officially nominated as the Republican presidential candidate. Here are key takeaways from the day:\par \par \uc2 1. As VP, Trump picks JD Vance, Hillbilly Elegy author who once called him \u8216\'20\'18America\u8217\'20\'19s Hitler\u8217\'20\'19: For his vice-president, Trump chose 39-year-old JD Vance, a bestselling author who swiftly transformed himself from a self-described \u8220\'20\'1Cnever Trumper\u8221\'20\'1D to a Trump loyalist.\par \par \uc2 2. Trump makes his first public appearance since surviving a shooting attack in Pennsylvania: \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  looked unusually somber as he emerged from backstage and joined his sons, and his new vice-presidential pick, JD Vance, in a VIP section of the convention hall audience.\par \par \uc2 3. Post-shooting speeches focus on Trump\u8217\'20\'19s relationship with God, not blaming Biden: Amid multiple media reports that Trump wanted to strike a note of unity after what he saw as his own miraculous escape from death, Axios {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.axios.com/2024/07/15/trump-convention-speech-rnc-milwaukee"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2  that \u8220\'20\'1CTrump ordered aides not to allow the convention\u8217\'20\'19s prime-time speakers to update their remarks to dial up outrage over the shooting.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 4. \uc2 Teamsters\uc2  president Sean O\u8217\'20\'19Brien praises Trump\u8217\'20\'19s toughness in defiant pro-labor speech: One of the most prominent labor union leaders in the US brought a fiercely anti-corporate message into the heart of the GOP convention, where he wove together a denunciation of corporate power with praise of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s willingness to hear from alternate voices.\par \par \uc2 5. \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  is reportedly discussing major donations to a pro-Trump Super Pac: Trump\u8217\'20\'19s choice of former venture capitalist and \uc2 Peter Thiel\uc2  protege JD Vance as his vice-presidential nominee already strengthened the link between the 2024 Trump campaign and Silicon Valley.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/16/rnc-day-one-key-takeaways"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Read full story: }}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/16/rnc-day-one-key-takeaways"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s arrival and \u8216\'20\'18our God saves\u8217\'20\'19: key takeaways from day one of the RNC}}}\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/16/rnc-day-one-key-takeaways"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s arrival and \u8216\'20\'18our God saves\u8217\'20\'19: key takeaways from day one of the RNC}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.05pm BST\par \par \uc2 RNC\uc2  enters second day after Trump's first appearance since shooting\par \par \uc2 Good morning {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-politics"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US politics}}}\uc2  readers. The Republican national convention heads into its second day in Milwaukee, Wisconsin \u8211\'20\'13 now with \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  as its official presidential nominee and Ohio senator JD Vance as his running mate.\par \par \uc2 Republicans will be looking to keep party members\u8217\'20\'19 energy high on Tuesday after an eventful day, during which the former president made a surprise appearance at Fiserv Forum with a bandage over his injured ear, his first since the assassination attempt against him on Saturday. Trump is expected to give his nomination acceptance speech on Thursday, while Vance is expected to take the stage on Wednesday night.\par \par \uc2 The theme for the convention today is \u8220\'20\'1CMake America Safe Once Again\u8221\'20\'1D, with speakers expected to focus on immigration and border security. Among those we\u8217\'20\'19re expecting to hear from is \uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2 , Trump\u8217\'20\'19s former primary rival.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else we\u8217\'20\'19re watching:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Democratic National Committee\uc2  are moving quickly to confirm \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  as his party\u8217\'20\'19s presidential nominee by the end of July, weeks before the Democratic national convention next month, according to reports.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  wants to curb rent increases by penalizing landlords who hike rents beyond 5% each year, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/16/biden-rent-control-plan"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  but he needs}}}\uc2  the help of Congress to put the plan into action.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The House oversight committee will receive a briefing from the Secret Service about the attempted assassination of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240716ek7g001s0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
