\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Trump joins crowd at Republican convention hall with bandaged ear, in first public appearance since assassination attempt \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Chris Stein in Milwaukee (now); L\u233\'00\'E9onie Chao-Fong and Martin Belam (earlier) \par \uc2 19,538 \uc2 words\par \uc2 16 July 2024\par 03:42 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Our live coverage of the Republican national convention is over for the day. You can read our latest full news reports here:Trump appears with bandaged ear at Republican national conventionTrump names fierce former critic JD Vance as running mate\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.16am BST\par \par \uc2 Trump makes first public appearance since shooting: key moments of first day of the Republican national convention\par \par \uc2 The first day of the Republican national convention in Milwaukee has now concluded.\par \par \uc2 Delegates will return to the Fiserv Forum at 5pm CT tomorrow for the second day of the four-day event, which is a crucial moment on the road to the 5 November election.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s a look back at what happened today so far.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The Republican party{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jul/15/donald-trump-republican-national-convention-speech-milwaukee-shooting-joe-biden-us-politics-latest-news-updates?page=with:block-669576eb8f08ee3616ac7076#block-669576eb8f08ee3616ac7076"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 formally nominated}}}\uc2 Donald Trump as their candidate for president, and the former president in the evening {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jul/15/donald-trump-republican-national-convention-speech-milwaukee-shooting-joe-biden-us-politics-latest-news-updates?page=with:block-6695d3c58f08938d143b87f2#block-6695d3c58f08938d143b87f2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 appeared}}}\uc2  at the convention, his first public outing since being wounded by a gunman on Saturday.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jul/15/donald-trump-republican-national-convention-speech-milwaukee-shooting-joe-biden-us-politics-latest-news-updates?page=with:block-669572e88f080e1800f4c22a#block-669572e88f080e1800f4c22a"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 announced}}}\uc2  that Ohio senator JD Vance would be his running mate. Not long after, Vance {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jul/15/donald-trump-republican-national-convention-speech-milwaukee-shooting-joe-biden-us-politics-latest-news-updates?page=with:block-66958bb68f08ee3616ac70e3#block-66958bb68f08ee3616ac70e3"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 turned up}}}\uc2  on the floor of the convention, and the GOP {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jul/15/donald-trump-republican-national-convention-speech-milwaukee-shooting-joe-biden-us-politics-latest-news-updates?page=with:block-66958e928f08ee3616ac70fd#block-66958e928f08ee3616ac70fd"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 made him}}}\uc2  their vice-presidential nominee by acclamation.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jul/15/donald-trump-republican-national-convention-speech-milwaukee-shooting-joe-biden-us-politics-latest-news-updates?page=with:block-66958f398f080e1800f4c2dd#block-66958f398f080e1800f4c2dd"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  Vance was \u8220\'20\'1Ca clone of Trump on the issues\u8221\'20\'1D. ABC News {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jul/15/donald-trump-republican-national-convention-speech-milwaukee-shooting-joe-biden-us-politics-latest-news-updates?page=with:block-66958cc88f08ee3616ac70ea#block-66958cc88f08ee3616ac70ea"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports}}}\uc2  that \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  tried to call Vance, but couldn\u8217\'20\'19t reach him, and left a voicemail.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The president acknowledged that it was a \u8220\'20\'1Cmistake\u8221\'20\'1D to say that he wanted to put a \u8220\'20\'1Cbullseye\u8221\'20\'1D on Trump, in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jul/15/donald-trump-republican-national-convention-speech-milwaukee-shooting-joe-biden-us-politics-latest-news-updates?page=with:block-669597308f08938d143b867c#block-669597308f08938d143b867c"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 an interview}}}\uc2  with NBC News.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Robert F Kennedy Jr\uc2  met with \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in Milwaukee, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jul/15/donald-trump-republican-national-convention-speech-milwaukee-shooting-joe-biden-us-politics-latest-news-updates?page=with:block-6695827e8f080e1800f4c28b#block-6695827e8f080e1800f4c28b"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Politico reports}}}\uc2 , as Trump sought his endorsement. Kennedy, an independent presidential candidate, is polling at around 9% nationally, and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jul/15/donald-trump-republican-national-convention-speech-milwaukee-shooting-joe-biden-us-politics-latest-news-updates?page=with:block-66959fcb8f080e1800f4c34e#block-66959fcb8f080e1800f4c34e"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 received}}}\uc2  Secret Service protection today.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  Jr{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jul/15/donald-trump-republican-national-convention-speech-milwaukee-shooting-joe-biden-us-politics-latest-news-updates?page=with:block-66957e968f080e1800f4c273#block-66957e968f080e1800f4c273"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told the Guardian}}}\uc2  he advised his father to pick JD Vance because he thought the senator would fight for him.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene\uc2 , the rightwing congresswoman, said {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jul/15/donald-trump-republican-national-convention-speech-milwaukee-shooting-joe-biden-us-politics-latest-news-updates?page=with:block-6695b4308f08938d143b872b#block-6695b4308f08938d143b872b"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 divine intervention}}}\uc2  kept Trump safe on Saturday.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The Biden campaign{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jul/15/donald-trump-republican-national-convention-speech-milwaukee-shooting-joe-biden-us-politics-latest-news-updates?page=with:block-66957dc38f08ee3616ac709c#block-66957dc38f08ee3616ac709c"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 characterized Vance}}}\uc2  as an enabler of Trump.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Sean O\u8217\'20\'19Brien, the president of the \uc2 Teamsters\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jul/15/donald-trump-republican-national-convention-speech-milwaukee-shooting-joe-biden-us-politics-latest-news-updates?page=with:block-6695dac78f08938d143b882b#block-6695dac78f08938d143b882b"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 defended}}}\uc2  his {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jul/15/donald-trump-republican-national-convention-speech-milwaukee-shooting-joe-biden-us-politics-latest-news-updates?page=with:block-6695da538f08ee3616ac72cd#block-6695da538f08ee3616ac72cd"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 controversial}}}\uc2  decision to address the convention, then said Trump was \u8220\'20\'1Cone tough SOB\u8221\'20\'1D for surviving the assassination attempt.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.19am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.56am BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  pumped his fist repeatedly and waved at supporters as he leisurely walked down the stairs from the VIP seating and into a tunnel that led backstage.\par \par \uc2 Secret Service agents followed him closely.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.54am BST\par \par \uc2 Michael Whatley, the chair of the convention, has just gaveled the night\u8217\'20\'19s session closed.\par \par \uc2 Before he did, he congratulated \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and JD Vance on their nominations.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSenator Vance, congratulations,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CPresident Trump, we are honored to have you here tonight and on behalf of the entire Republican party all across America, we are grateful for you to be our nominee for the 47th president of the United States of America.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The crowd burst into applause, as Trump pumped his fist and clasped hands with Vance.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.56am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.46am BST\par \par \uc2 Sean O\u8217\'20\'19Brien concluded his speech by declaring : \u8220\'20\'1CIf the powers to be stop me from raising my voice on behalf of American workers, I will not have one single regret,\u8221\'20\'1D and will go back to being a truck driver.\par \par \uc2 As he walked off stage, the crowd resumed chanting: \u8220\'20\'1CWe want Trump!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.48am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.43am BST\par \par \uc2 Teamsters\uc2  president Sean O\u8217\'20\'19Brien started his speech off on a high note with praise for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  after he survived an assassination attempt on Saturday.\par \par \uc2 But the meat of his speech is a pitch to the GOP to reconsider its stance on unions, after the party decades spent promoting policies that make it more difficult for organized labor to thrive.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou know, corporatists hate when working people join together to form unions. But for a century, major employers have waged a war against labor by forming corporate unions of their own. We need to call the Chamber of Commerce and the Business Toundtables what they are. They are unions for big business,\u8221\'20\'1D O\u8217\'20\'19Brien said.\par \par \uc2 He then decried \u8220\'20\'1Celites\u8221\'20\'1D, a common target of attacks from Trump and his allies:\par \par \uc2 Remember, elites have no party. Elites have no nation. Their loyalty is to the balance sheet and the stock price at the expense of the American worker.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.34am BST\par \par \uc2 Trump is 'one tough SOB', \uc2 Teamsters\uc2  president says\par \par \uc2 Sean O\u8217\'20\'19Brien has shown his knack for bringing the crowd to its feet, drawing one of the loudest applauses of the night by saying that, after surviving an assassination attempt on Saturday, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is \u8220\'20\'1Cone tough SOB\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CPresident Trump had the backbone to open the doors to this Republican convention, and that\u8217\'20\'19s unprecedented. No other nominee in the race would have invited the \uc2 Teamsters\uc2  into this arena,\u8221\'20\'1D O\u8217\'20\'19Brien said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou can have whatever opinion you want, but one thing is clear: President Trump is a candidate who is not afraid of hearing from new, loud and often critical voices, and I think we all can agree whether people like him or they don\u8217\'20\'19t like him, in light of what happened to him on Saturday, he has proven to be one tough SOB.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 And at that, the crowd went wild.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.36am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.30am BST\par \par \uc2 Teamsters\uc2  president says union 'not beholden to anyone, or any party'\par \par \uc2 By way of justifying his decision to address the Republican national convention, Teamster president Sean O\u8217\'20\'19Brien said that the union was \u8220\'20\'1Cnot beholden\u8221\'20\'1D to any politician or party.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe American people aren\u8217\'20\'19t stupid. They know the system is broken. We all know how Washington is run. Working people have no chance of winning this fight. That\u8217\'20\'19s why I\u8217\'20\'19m here today, because I refuse to keep doing the same things my predecessors did,\u8221\'20\'1D O\u8217\'20\'19Brien said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CToday, the \uc2 Teamsters\uc2  are here to say we are not beholden to anyone or any party. We will create an agenda and work with a bipartisan coalition ready to accomplish something real for the American worker.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 And in a remark that brought the convention to its feet, he said:\par \par \uc2 And I don\u8217\'20\'19t care about getting criticized, it\u8217\'20\'19s an honor to be the first Teamster in our 121-year history to address the Republican national convention.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.32am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.27am BST\par \par \uc2 Teamsters\uc2  president Sean O\u8217\'20\'19Brien is now onstage.\par \par \uc2 Some senior members of his union are not happy that he is addressing the Republican convention. Here\u8217\'20\'19s more about that:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/12/teamsters-boss-gop-convention-speech-backlash"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Teamsters president faces backlash over \u8216\'20\'18unconscionable\u8217\'20\'19 GOP convention speech}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.24am BST\par \par \uc2 Actor and model Amber Rose was up next, rebutting the assertion that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is racist.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe first person I knew who supported \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  was my father. I was shocked. My entire family is racially diverse, and I believed the leftwing propaganda that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  was a racist. My father said: \u8216\'20\'18No, he\u8217\'20\'19s not Amber, what are you talking about?\u8217\'20\'19 And when I insisted, he said, prove it. So to prove my father wrong, I did my research and looked into all things \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D Rose said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CPeople have to do their research. I watched all the rallies, and I started meeting so many of you, his red-hat wearing supporters. I realized \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and his supporters don\u8217\'20\'19t care if you\u8217\'20\'19re Black, white, gay or straight \u8211\'20\'13 it\u8217\'20\'19s all love.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.26am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.13am BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  listened to a story from western Michigan resident Mark Laws, who was talking about how inflation has affected him.\par \par \uc2 JD Vance is sitting to Trump\u8217\'20\'19s left, and to his right is congressman Byron Donalds. Next to him is \uc2 Tucker Carlson\uc2 , the conservative former Fox News commentator. Carlson appears to be leaning over Donalds to talk to Trump.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.23am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.07am BST\par \par \uc2 The crowd has broken into chants of \u8220\'20\'1CUSA! USA! USA!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 As well as \u8220\'20\'1CFight! Fight! Fight!\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1CWe want Trump!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.08am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.05am BST\par \par \uc2 Trump is standing next to JD Vance, who he just selected as his running mate.\par \par \uc2 They\u8217\'20\'19re in a VIP section alongside members of Congress, including House speaker Mike Johnson.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.03am BST\par \par \uc2 Trump greets supporters at Republican national convention\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is now walking into the VIP seating of the Republican national convention, pumping his fist in the air.\par \par \uc2 Country singer Lee Greenwood is on stage, singing his hit God Bless the USA.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.04am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.59am BST\par \par \uc2 Trump appears with bandaged ear at convention\par \par \uc2 The jumbotron at the Republican national convention is now showing video of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , apparently backstage.\par \par \uc2 His right ear is covered in a bandage, after it was hit by a bullet during the assassination attempt targeting him on Saturday. He motioned to the camera, as if signaling he could still hear the convention crowd through that ear, drawing cheers.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.05am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.58am BST\par \par \uc2 Amid {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/2024-election/poll-debate-aftermath-damages-biden-democratic-party-matchup-trump-unc-rcna161154"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 widespread concerns}}}\uc2  about \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8216\'20\'18s ability to serve another four years in office, JD Vance boasted that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is in great health because of his \u8220\'20\'1Cridiculous genes\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is as healthy as anybody I\u8217\'20\'19ve ever met. I tell him all the time, he\u8217\'20\'19s got ridiculous genes,\u8221\'20\'1D Vance told Fox News host \uc2 Sean Hannity\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CI plan to be a very good vice- president to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  for four years.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.59am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.55am BST\par \par \uc2 In his Fox News interview, JD Vance echoed \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s call to \u8220\'20\'1Cdeport a large number of people who have come here illegally\u8221\'20\'1D. Trump has previously expressed his wish to deport 15 to 20 million undocumented migrants if he wins in November.\par \par \uc2 Vance agreed with Fox News host \uc2 Sean Hannity\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s description of the US-Mexico border as the country\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cnumber-one national security threat\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe have to deport people. We have to deport people who broke our laws who came in here. And I think we need to start with the violent criminals,\u8221\'20\'1D Vance said.\par \par \uc2 Pointing to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://news.gallup.com/poll/1660/immigration.aspx"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 polls}}}\uc2  showing declining support for immigration, Vance said the proposed mass deportations would represent \u8220\'20\'1Ca policy victory for the American people\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.58am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.48am BST\par \par \uc2 JD Vance claims media to blame for his previous critical views of Trump\par \par \uc2 Vice-presidential nominee JD Vance, who once described \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  as \u8220\'20\'1CAmerica\u8217\'20\'19s Hitler\u8221\'20\'1D, blamed his past criticism of the former president on \u8220\'20\'1Cthe media\u8217\'20\'19s lies and distortions\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Speaking to Fox News\u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 Sean Hannity\uc2 , Vance said: \u8220\'20\'1CI bought into this idea that somehow he was going to be so different, a terrible threat to democracy. It was a joke.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 As a reminder, Trump\u8217\'20\'19s presidency ended with a violent attack on the US Capitol after a group of his supporters stormed the building in an effort to prevent the certification of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s electoral victory.\par \par \uc2 Vance told Hannity: \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is the one who is trying to undermine American law and order. President Trump did a really good job. And I actually think it\u8217\'20\'19s a good thing, when you see somebody [and] you were wrong about them, you ought to admit the mistake and admit that you were wrong.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.57am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.44am BST\par \par \uc2 PayPal\uc2  co-founder and tech entrepreneur \uc2 David Sacks\uc2  just came on stage to give what was perhaps the worst-received speech of the night thus far.\par \par \uc2 His lines just were not hitting with a crowd that has been generous with its applause throughout the night.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe Biden-Harris administration has taken a world that was at peace under President Trump and they lit it on fire,\u8221\'20\'1D Sacks said, pausing for cheers that never really came.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFirst, President Biden botched the Afghanistan withdrawal, displaying incompetence and weakness for the whole world to see. Then, he provoked, yes, provoked, the Russians to invade Ukraine with talk of Nato expansion,\u8221\'20\'1D he said, to not much more reaction.\par \par \uc2 After saying, to indifference, that Biden was taking the world \u8220\'20\'1Cto the brink of world war three\u8221\'20\'1D, Sacks went on for a few minutes more before walking off stage.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.57am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.22am BST\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, it\u8217\'20\'19s now more than 20 minutes past 8pm in Milwaukee and there are no indications of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  stopping in at the Republican national convention.\par \par \uc2 But there\u8217\'20\'19s still time. The night\u8217\'20\'19s session has about an hour and a half more to go.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.24am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.17am BST\par \par \uc2 Blocks away from the \uc2 Fiserv\uc2  center in downtown Milwaukee, where Republicans are holding their convention, protesters converged to demonstrate against the party\u8217\'20\'19s policies.\par \par \uc2 Here are images from the news wires of the protests, which are expected to continue throughout the convention:\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more on the protests today outside the Republican national convention:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/15/republican-national-convention-protest"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Not welcome in our city\u8217\'20\'19: protesters march on Republican convention}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.21am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.11am BST\par \par \uc2 Kristi Noem\uc2 , the South Dakota governor who shot her dog and, after that was revealed, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/30/kristi-noem-puppy-trump-vp-candidate"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 her chances}}}\uc2  of being \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s vice-president, is on stage now.\par \par \uc2 She\u8217\'20\'19s mostly reciting her administration\u8217\'20\'19s accomplishments, including her handling of the Covid-19 pandemic and of the state\u8217\'20\'19s economy.\par \par \uc2 After condemning the assassination attempt on Trump Saturday, she made something of a plea for unity:\par \par \uc2 Donald J Trump\uc2  is our man in the arena. He will never stop fighting for us. He will never stop, and now he is bringing all of us together. Now, I know that many of you are angry, but now is the time to unite, and we have to get to work. We have to win the hearts and minds of every single American. Wake them up with truth and with wisdom. We need to listen to them. You can\u8217\'20\'19t win people over by arguing with them. Visit with your neighbors, at your job, at your church, at the gas station or even at the grocery store.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.03am BST\par \par \uc2 Robert Unanue\uc2 , the CEO of \uc2 Goya Foods\uc2  who has previously been criticized for his support of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , just delivered a robust endorsement of the former president.\par \par \uc2 Unanue is no stranger to controversy, as some customers {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/mar/01/goya-ceo-robert-unanue-cpac-donald-trump-boycott"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 called}}}\uc2  for a boycott of \uc2 Goya Foods\uc2  in 2021 after the CEO repeated false claims about the 2020 presidential election.\par \par \uc2 At the time, Unanue praised Trump as \u8220\'20\'1Cthe real, legitimate and still actual president of the United States\u8221\'20\'1D, despite no substantive evidence of widespread election fraud in 2020.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.06am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.00am BST\par \par \uc2 The man who runs the gun-centric {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cbsnews.com/news/trump-rally-shooter-thomas-matthew-crooks-demolition-ranch/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 YouTube page Demolition Ranch}}}\uc2  is speaking out after his channel was thrust into the spotlight following images of Thomas Matthew Crooks, the man who shot at \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  at a campaign stop in Pennsylvania, wearing a T-shirt from Demolition Ranch.\par \par \uc2 In his first video since Saturday\u8217\'20\'19s shooting Matt Carriker, the Texas veterinarian who has run the page since 2011, expressed his condolences to the family of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2024/07/14/politics/corey-comperatore-trump-shooting-victim/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Corey Comperatore}}}\uc2  and well-wishes to the injured and said that he purposefully keeps politics out of his videos and was shocked to see the shooter wearing his merchandise.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CJust like \uc2 Nike\uc2  doesn\u8217\'20\'19t vet who buys their shoes. I wish I could. I would love to keep people like that from wearing, being associated with that article of clothing. I wish he couldn\u8217\'20\'19t get a shirt. But it happened,\u8221\'20\'1D he said in the video posted on Monday.\par \par \uc2 The target audience for the video, Carriker emphasized, is people who were unfamiliar with him before Saturday\u8217\'20\'19s shooting.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is mostly for the people just tuning in to see if I am a guy that is trying to make people do stuff like that,\u8221\'20\'1D Carricker continued. \u8220\'20\'1CI am not. Obviously, I don\u8217\'20\'19t have to explain that to those who know me. But I feel like I might need to say that for those who don\u8217\'20\'19t. This channel is not about violence. This channel will never be.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The full five-minute video can be found {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=GAnvLjavON0&t=1s"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.06am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.53am BST\par \par \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  plans to commit $45m per month to pro-Trump Pac \u8211\'20\'13 report\par \par \uc2 The world\u8217\'20\'19s richest man \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  will commit $45m per month to a new Super Pac intended to support \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s campaign, the Wall Street Journal reports, citing people familiar with the matter.\par \par \uc2 Musk announced his endorsement of Trump on Saturday, shortly after an assassin opened fire on the former president at his rally in Pennsylvania. Here\u8217\'20\'19s more on the billionaire\u8217\'20\'19s new commitment, from the Journal:\par \par \uc2 Other backers of the group, called America PAC, include {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/market-data/quotes/PLTR"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Palantir Technologies}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/market-data/quotes/PLTR"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 PLTR 2.14%increase; green up pointing triangle}}}\uc2  co-founder Joe Lonsdale, the Winklevoss twins, former U.S. ambassador to Canada Kelly Craft and her husband, \uc2 Joe Craft\uc2 , who is chief executive of coal producer {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/market-data/quotes/ARLP"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Alliance Resource Partners}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/market-data/quotes/ARLP"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ARLP -0.04%decrease; red down pointing triangle}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Formed in June, America PAC is focused on registering voters and persuading constituents to vote early and request mail-in ballots in swing states, according to one of the people. The coalition assessed that the Democrats have historically had very robust \u8220\'20\'1Cget out the vote\u8221\'20\'1D campaigns and took note of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/joe-biden-campaign-north-carolina-2024-election-4fe5a736?mod=article_inline"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the amounts of money}}}\uc2  that the Biden administration has dedicated to so-called on the ground efforts in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/battleground-map-shows-signs-of-expansion-for-trump-as-biden-struggles-77d19e67?mod=article_inline"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 swing states}}}\uc2 . America PAC will try to counter that.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.57am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.39am BST\par \par \uc2 Despite Republicans\u8217\'20\'19 claims of rampant crime in US cities because of Democratic policies, violent crime has actually declined in recent months.\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Oliver Milman {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jun/11/violent-crime-rate-data-decline"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2  last month:\par \par \uc2 Violent crime in the US dropped by 15% in the first three months of the year, new figures have shown, the latest evidence in a broader decline of crime across the country that has occurred over the past year.\par \par \uc2 The decrease in violent crime, from January to March compared to the same period in 2023, has been accompanied by a major drop in murders and reported rapes, which both fell by more than a quarter in the first three months of 2024, according to the new quarterly data released by the \uc2 FBI\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Aggravated assaults fell by 12.5% in this period, while robberies dropped by 17.8%, the figures \u8211\'20\'13 gathered from more than 13,000 law enforcement agencies across the US \u8211\'20\'13 show.\par \par \uc2 Read Oliver\u8217\'20\'19s full report:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jun/11/violent-crime-rate-data-decline"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Violent crime in the US plummeted in first months of 2024, FBI data reveals}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.38am BST\par \par \uc2 Scott declares 'America is not a racist country' as he attacks Democrats\par \par \uc2 Reprising an attack line from his days as a presidential candidate, Tim Scott said Democrats were making life worse for African Americans.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAmerica, we deserve better \u8230\'20\'26 we deserve so much better. I was raised by a single mom in poverty. We had plastic spoons, not silver spoons, but she taught me to work hard, to take responsibility and reject victimhood. Thank God for my wonderful mama. I know, I know this is going to offend the liberal elites. Every time I say it, it offends them, but let me say it one more time, America is not a racist country,\u8221\'20\'1D said Scott, the lone Black Republican in the Senate.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBut if you are looking for racism today, you find it in cities run by Democrats. Look on the south \u8230\'20\'26 side of Chicago, poor Black kids trapped in failing schools, thousands shot every single year, including one of my former interns, DaQuawn. But there\u8217\'20\'19s good news. It\u8217\'20\'19s conservative values that restores hope. It\u8217\'20\'19s Republican policies that lifts people up.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.40am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.30am BST\par \par \uc2 Tim Scott on rally shooting: 'an American lion got back up... and he roared'\par \par \uc2 In describing what happened at \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s rally on Saturday, Tim Scott deployed language that any reader of the Chronicles of Narnia would recognize.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf you didn\u8217\'20\'19t believe in miracles before Saturday, you better be believing right now. Thank God almighty that we live in a country that still believes in the king of kings and the lord of lords, the alpha and the omega,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COur God still saves, he still delivers, and he still sets free, because on Saturday, the devil came to Pennsylvania holding a rifle, but an American lion got back up on his feet, and he roared!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.01am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.22am BST\par \par \uc2 Tim Scott takes to the stage\par \par \uc2 Tim Scott, the Republican senator who made a quixotic bid for the presidential nomination and is now a prominent \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  surrogate, has taken the stage to big cheers.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWow!\u8221\'20\'1D Scott boomed. \u8220\'20\'1CHello Milwaukee! Are you ready for four more years of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 ?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.01am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.20am BST\par \par \uc2 Fact check on \uc2 RNC\uc2  gas price statistic\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 RNC\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s statistics on gas prices need a bit more context. According to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://fred.stlouisfed.org/series/GASREGW"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 data}}}\uc2  compiled by the \uc2 Federal Reserve Bank of St Louis\uc2 , average gas prices ranged from $1.773 per gallon to $2.962 per gallon over the four years of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 s presidency.\par \par \uc2 But prices only dipped below $2 per gallon during the earliest days of the Covid-19 pandemic, when demand for gas plummeted as Americans stayed at home to limit the spread of the virus.\par \par \uc2 By the time Trump left office in January 2021, the average gas price stood at $2.379 per gallon. Today, the average gas price is $3.521 per gallon after reaching a record high of $5.016 per gallon in June 2022, according to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://gasprices.aaa.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 AAA}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.29am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.12am BST\par \par \uc2 Michigan congressman John James gave one of the more energetic speeches of the evening so far, which focused on attacking Democrats for failing to deliver for Black Americans.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBlack people were sold on hope. Now our streets are rife with crime. Our kids can\u8217\'20\'19t read, and illegals are getting better help from Democrats in four days than we\u8217\'20\'19ve gotten in 400 years,\u8221\'20\'1D said James, who is African American.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CLook, our daughters were sold on hope, and now they\u8217\'20\'19re being forced on the playing fields and changing rooms of biological males. America was sold on hope, and now the world\u8217\'20\'19s on fire.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The Trump campaign has been hoping to make inroads with Black voters, a group that typically votes Democratic. As he wrapped up his speech, James linked the struggles of African Americans to the country at large:\par \par \uc2 Look, I heard a little early today, if you don\u8217\'20\'19t vote \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , you ain\u8217\'20\'19t Black. But, see, here\u8217\'20\'19s the thing, by the grace of God and the proven leadership of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  for every American, regardless of race, color and creed, we can once again have a land where a child\u8217\'20\'19s outcome isn\u8217\'20\'19t determined by their zip code. We can once again have a land where hard work truly does get you ahead. We can once again have a land where you can go from poverty to prosperity in a single generation, I believe that land is still America. America is the greatest idea that\u8217\'20\'19s ever been.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.27am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.05am BST\par \par \uc2 Trump expected to appear at Republican convention around 8pm CT\par \par \uc2 I have heard from multiple people that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  will appear at the Republican national convention at about 8pm CT, but he will not make remarks.\par \par \uc2 It would be the former president\u8217\'20\'19s first public appearance since he was hit in the ear by a bullet while campaigning in Pennsylvania on Saturday.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.12am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.59am BST\par \par \uc2 Next up was \uc2 Mark Robinson\uc2 , the North Carolina lieutenant governor who is the GOP nominee for governor.\par \par \uc2 He has a history of outrageous remarks, such as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/mar/05/mark-robinson-north-carolina"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 quoting Hitler}}}\uc2 , but his speech mostly stuck to tried-and-true Republican rhetoric.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAs governor, I will not forget where I came from, or the struggles of the people I meet. And you know, there\u8217\'20\'19s someone else who will fight just as hard for you: President \uc2 Donald J Trump\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D Robinson said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CUnder President Trump, the American dream was alive and well. Under President Trump, there was hope, and we need that now more than ever. So this November, let\u8217\'20\'19s select the Braveheart of our time, \uc2 Donald J Trump\uc2 , to get our economy back on track, restore the American Dream and make America great again.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.03am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.54am BST\par \par \uc2 Fact check: Taylor Greene transgender day claim misleading\par \par \uc2 Contrary to \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s insinuation otherwise, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  did not set Transgender Day of Visibility to coincide with Easter Sunday this year.\par \par \uc2 Transgender Day of Visibility occurs on 31 March every year, and Biden has released annual proclamations recognizing the occasion since taking office in 2021.\par \par \uc2 The date of Easter Sunday varies year by year and just happened to fall on 31 March this year. In addition to his proclamation about Transgender Day of Visibility, Biden, who is a devout Catholic, also released {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.whitehouse.gov/briefing-room/statements-releases/2024/03/31/statement-from-president-joe-biden-on-easter-2/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a statement}}}\uc2  in celebration of Easter on the same day.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.21am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.49am BST\par \par \uc2 True to form, Greene leaned into the conservative culture wars in her address to the Republican national convention.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFor far too long, the establishment in Washington has sold us out. They promised unity and delivered division. They promised peace and brought war. They promised normalcy and gave us transgender visibility day on Easter Sunday. And let me state this clearly, there are only two genders,\u8221\'20\'1D Greene said.\par \par \uc2 Then she accused Democrats of driving up unemployment (even though the labor market continued its recovery from the Covid-19 pandemic under \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/article/2024/jul/05/us-economy-jobs-labor-market#:~:text=The%20number%20of%20new%20jobs,4%25%20in%20over%20two%20years."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the most recent data}}}\uc2  shows hiring has remained resilient), and said:\par \par \uc2 The Democrats\u8217\'20\'19s economy is of, by and for illegal aliens.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.45am BST\par \par \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene\uc2  thanks 'God that his hand was on President Trump' at rally\par \par \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene\uc2 , the Georgia congresswoman known for her far-right rhetoric, is on the stage now.\par \par \uc2 She began by reflecting on the assassination attempt targeting \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  on Saturday.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CToday is a celebration. The American spirit is alive and well, and we have once again, nominated for president, the founding father of the America First movement, \uc2 Donald John Trump\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D Greene said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CUnfortunately, this is also a somber moment for our nation. Two days ago, evil came for the man we admire and love so much. I thank God that his hand was on President Trump.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.53am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.33am BST\par \par \uc2 The first speech was from Wisconsin\u8217\'20\'19s Republican senator \uc2 Ron Johnson\uc2 , who has managed to twice win re-election to his seat representing the swing state.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CToday\u8217\'20\'19s Democrat agenda, their policies, are a clear and present danger to America, to our institutions, our values and our people. Democrats have forgotten American families. They have abandoned the hardworking middle class, but with President Trump and Republicans, those forgotten Americans are forgotten no more,\u8221\'20\'1D Johnson said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19ve repaired the damage caused by Democrats before, and we will do it again. We will complete the mission President Trump first articulated in 2016 to make America great again.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 After he wrapped up, a video montage played on the jumbotron of Trump dancing and pumping his fists at various rallies, to the tune of the Village People\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=CS9OO0S5w2k"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 YMCA}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 enltrThis is an official \uc2 RNC\uc2  video, no joke ?? {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/JYVTmwBBT1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/JYVTmwBBT1}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1812995742220648810?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 15, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.53am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.28am BST\par \par \uc2 The economic statistics highlighted in a video played at the start of the convention\u8217\'20\'19s second session are somewhat cherry-picked, as the rate of inflation has subsided in recent months.\par \par \uc2 It is true that the inflation rate {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2022/jun/10/us-inflation-rate-may-2022-four-decade-high"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 hit}}}\uc2  a 40-year high in 2022, but the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/11/us-inflation-fall-june"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 most recent government report}}}\uc2  showed the consumer price index\u8217\'20\'19s annual increase now stands at 3%, compared with 9.1% two years ago.\par \par \uc2 And while the convention video highlighted record-high gas prices in 2022, those prices have decreased significantly in the time since. According to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://gasprices.aaa.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 AAA}}}\uc2 , the national average price for a gallon of regular gas currently stands at $3.521, compared with $5.016 in June 2022.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.29am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.20am BST\par \par \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene\uc2 , \uc2 Teamsters\uc2  president to address convention on first night\par \par \uc2 Several prominent Republican lawmakers, including rightwing icon \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene\uc2  and former presidential candidate Tim Scott, are expected to address the party\u8217\'20\'19s convention this evening.\par \par \uc2 So, too, is Sean O\u8217\'20\'19Brien, president of the \uc2 Teamsters\uc2 , whose members have traditionally supported Democrats. His appearance at the convention is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/12/teamsters-boss-gop-convention-speech-backlash"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 deeply controversial}}}\uc2  with some in the labor union.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more on who we expect to hear from in the hours to come:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/15/republican-national-convention-first-night-speeches-marjorie-taylor-greene-tim-scott"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 RNC: Marjorie Taylor Greene, Tim Scott and Ron Johnson to speak on first night}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.11am BST\par \par \uc2 The Republican convention has now resumed, with its evening session centered on the theme: \u8220\'20\'1CMake America wealthy again\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Delegates just watched a video decrying \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s handling of the economy, which ended with something resembling a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://batman.fandom.com/wiki/Bat-Signal"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 bat-signal}}}\uc2  lighting up the clouds with the word \u8220\'20\'1CTRUMP\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.57pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Republican national convention\u8217\'20\'19s second session of the day is supposed to be starting.\par \par \uc2 But it seems like the program is a little behind schedule. Delegates are still filing onto the floor of the arena, and many seats are empty.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.50pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  tells NBC in an interview airing in full later tonight that his age (81) is \u8220\'20\'1Ca legitimate question\u8221\'20\'1D, while saying his \u8220\'20\'1Cmental acuity has been pretty damn good\u8221\'20\'1D in defending his decision to run for re-election and his refusal to drop out after a dire debate performance against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  last month.\par \par \uc2 The US president says he doesn\u8217\'20\'19t know if the attempted assassination of Trump over the weekend has changed the trajectory of the election, Reuters reports.\par \par \uc2 But he did say, in contrasting his record with Trump:\par \par \uc2 I am not the guy that said I want to be a dictator on Day One. I am not the guy that refused to accept the outcome of the election.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  said in an interview with Fox host \uc2 Sean Hannity\uc2  earlier in the campaign, when asked if he would behave like a dictator if he got back into the White House, told him, no, \u8220\'20\'1Conly on Day One\u8221\'20\'1D. And Trump continues to deny that he lost the 2020 election to Biden, claiming against all available evidence, that widespread fraud effectively stole the result from him.\par \par \uc2 He is under federal criminal indictment for election interference for trying to overturn his electoral loss.\par \par \uc2 enltrIn interview with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/LesterHoltNBC?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @LesterHoltNBC}}}\uc2 , President Biden says his "mental acuity has been pretty damn good" in defending his decision to stay in the race. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/fULztVQTLo"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/fULztVQTLo}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 NBC News (@NBCNews) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/NBCNews/status/1812977978411774462?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 15, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.52pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.40pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Biden team\u8217\'20\'19s call marked something of a return to normal campaigning for the Democrats, after Saturday\u8217\'20\'19s shocking assassination attempt on \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  plunged the race deeper into uncharted territory.\par \par \uc2 The Biden campaign pressed ahead on Monday, after pausing all negative advertising over the weekend in response to the shooting. On the call, officials said the contrast between the Trump-Vance ticket and the Biden-Harris ticket was clearer than ever.\par \par \uc2 Biden-Harris campaign chair \uc2 Jen O\u8217\'20\'19Malley Dillon\uc2  said: \u8220\'20\'1CWith Trump and Vance now entering the general election, they\u8217\'20\'19re facing off against the Biden-Harris ticket and I will certainly take that matchup any day of the week and twice on Sunday.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Eager to turn the page on the intra-party turmoil set in motion by Biden\u8217\'20\'19s disastrous debate performance last month, the campaign emphasized that they had already committed to participating in a vice-presidential debate and looked forward to the televised showdown between \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and Vance.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CShe is strong. She knows what she\u8217\'20\'19s talking about and she doesn\u8217\'20\'19t give an inch,\u8221\'20\'1D Senator Elizabeth Warren said of Harris.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.45pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.37pm BST\par \par \uc2 For four years, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  knew he could count on the loyalty of his vice-president, \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 But on January 6, Pence resisted Trump\u8217\'20\'19s plea for him to use his ceremonial role as president of the Senate to help overturn the results of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s election in 2020. The Biden campaign is now warning that Trump\u8217\'20\'19s new choice for running mate, Ohio senator JD Vance, should not be trusted to put country over party.\par \par \uc2 In a call with reporters, Biden campaign officials and advocates highlighted Vance\u8217\'20\'19s anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  record, accusing him of wanting to \u8220\'20\'1Ctake women back decades\u8221\'20\'1D. Massachusetts senator Elizabeth Warren assailed him as a faux populist, part of Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 criticism of the Hillbilly Elegy author. Warren said his nomination was \u8220\'20\'1Cgreat news for the wealthiest Americans and lousy news for everyone else\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBillionaires on Wall Street and Silicon Valley are cheering but there is no joy for working people,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.40pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.31pm BST\par \par \uc2 Outside of the Fiserv Forum in downtown Milwaukee, news slowly spread that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  had picked JD Vance as his running mate.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI think it\u8217\'20\'19s a great choice. I like that he\u8217\'20\'19s young. I like that he\u8217\'20\'19s from Ohio. There\u8217\'20\'19s a lot of positives about him. Future of the party,\u8221\'20\'1D said Nick D\u8217\'20\'19Alessandro, an alternate delegate from New York.\par \par \uc2 Larry Johnson, a convention attendee from West Virginia, said he thought Vance could bring more attention to Appalachia. \u8220\'20\'1CI think for a long time that area has been kind of overlooked.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Asa Hutchinson, the former Arkansas governor who was one of the most outspoken Trump critics said Vance was a \u8220\'20\'1Cstrategic\u8221\'20\'1D choice.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CObviously he went to appeal to the base of the party. And we\u8217\'20\'19ll see what the tone is whenever JD makes his acceptance speech,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CI was a fan of course of my fellow governor \uc2 Doug Burgum\uc2 . \uc2 Marco Rubio\uc2  would have been brought. All three very good quality choices. That\u8217\'20\'19s why you\u8217\'20\'19re president, you get to make those choices.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Keith Kellogg, who served as \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s national security adviser, doubted picking Vance would really mean anything.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHe could have picked Peter Pan or Snow White, it wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t have made a difference. It\u8217\'20\'19s all about Trump,\u8221\'20\'1D he said in an interview.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.38pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.25pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden orders Secret Service protection for candidate \uc2 Robert F Kennedy Jr\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  a little earlier today directed the Secret Service to protect independent presidential candidate \uc2 Robert F Kennedy Jr.\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jul/15/donald-trump-republican-national-convention-speech-milwaukee-shooting-joe-biden-us-politics-latest-news-updates?page=with:block-6695827e8f080e1800f4c28b#block-6695827e8f080e1800f4c28b"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reportedly met}}}\uc2  with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/robert-f-kennedy-jr"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 RFK Jr}}}\uc2  in person earlier today, while the independent rival to both Trump and Biden and these days a maverick member of the Kennedy political dynasty, has said he won\u8217\'20\'19t drop out of the presidential race.\par \par \uc2 RFK Jr has been asking for a long time for federal protection. Trump said earlier today that Kennedy should get it. This follows the assassination attempt on Trump over the weekend.\par \par \uc2 On Monday, the Associated Press reported, Kennedy said in a statement:\par \par \uc2 Thank you, President Biden, for extending me Secret Service protection.\par \par \uc2 He also thanked his private security firm, \uc2 Gavin de Becker & Associates\uc2 , \u8220\'20\'1Cfor keeping me safe for the past 15 months of my presidential campaign\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Kennedy\u8217\'20\'19s uncle, President \uc2 John F Kennedy\uc2 , and his father, Senator \uc2 Robert F Kennedy\uc2 , were both assassinated, in 1963 and 1968, respectively.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.28pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.07pm BST\par \par \uc2 Special counsel to appeal dismissal of documents case against Trump\par \par \uc2 Special counsel Jack Smith intends to appeal a judge\u8217\'20\'19s dismissal of the classified documents case against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 A spokesperson for Smith revealed the move in a statement today hours after US district judge Aileen Cannon threw out the case, the Associated Press reports.\par \par \uc2 The judge sided with Trump\u8217\'20\'19s lawyers, who said Smith\u8217\'20\'19s appointment as special counsel violated the constitution.\par \par \uc2 A successful appeal by prosecutors could result in the indictment being reinstated, though even if that there were to happen, it would be virtually impossible for a trial to take place before the November presidential election.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s my colleague {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/hugo-lowell"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Hugo Lowell}}}\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s report on the unexpected news this morning that Cannon had, after so many months of proceedings, decided to throw out the case. Read it {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/15/judge-dismisses-trump-classified-documents-case"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 And my colleague {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/edpilkington"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ed Pilkington}}}\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s analysis highlighting the direct line of thinking from hard right-leaning supreme court justice \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2  to the Trump-appointed Cannon. Read it {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/15/clarence-thomas-trump-classified-documents-case"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.17pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.58pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  sat down for the interview with NBC\u8217\'20\'19s Lester Holt earlier today before heading to the battleground state of Nevada.\par \par \uc2 The interview is scheduled to air on the network this evening. It was planned before the weekend attempt on Trump\u8217\'20\'19s life at a rally in Pennsylvania and had been part of Biden\u8217\'20\'19s broader strategy to prove his fitness for office after angst grew among Democrats because of his disastrous June debate performance, the Associated Press reports.\par \par \uc2 The Biden re-election campaign recalibrated some of its political plans in the immediate aftermath of the assassination attempt on Saturday, pulling advertising off the air and hitting pause on messaging. The White House also scrapped Biden\u8217\'20\'19s planned Monday visit to the Lyndon B Johnson library, where he had been slated to deliver remarks on civil rights, in Texas.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s still not finalized when Biden\u8217\'20\'19s campaign ads will resume airing. But Biden is pressing on with the Nevada portion of his previously scheduled western swing, which will include remarks to the \uc2 NAACP\uc2  and \uc2 UnidosUS\uc2 , a Latino civil rights and advocacy group. He\u8217\'20\'19ll also headline what\u8217\'20\'19s been billed as a \u8220\'20\'1Ccampaign community event\u8221\'20\'1D on Wednesday in Las Vegas.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.46pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden admits mistake in saying he wanted 'bullseye' on Trump\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/NBCNightlyNews/status/1812959915444470117"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told NBC News}}}\uc2  in an interview airing Monday that it was a \u8220\'20\'1Cmistake\u8221\'20\'1D to say he wanted to put a \u8220\'20\'1Cbullseye\u8221\'20\'1D on Republican nominee \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , which the US president {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/14/trump-rally-shooting-campaign-rnc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 had said}}}\uc2  prior to the assassination attempt on the former president on Saturday.\par \par \uc2 But Biden also argued in the sit-down with the TV network that rhetoric coming from his election opponent was more incendiary, the Associated Press reports.\par \par \uc2 It was a mistake to use the word,\u8217\'20\'19 Biden told NBC anchor Lester Holt in a clip released by the network.\par \par \uc2 enltrIn an exclusive interview with Lester Holt, President Biden said it was a mistake to use the word \u8220\'20\'1Cbullseye\u8221\'20\'1D while discussing former President Trump, but said to \u8220\'20\'1Cfocus on what [Trump is] doing\u8221\'20\'1D. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/TufdyiZq8v"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/TufdyiZq8v}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 NBC Nightly News with Lester Holt (@NBCNightlyNews) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/NBCNightlyNews/status/1812959915444470117?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 15, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 He said he wanted the \u8216\'20\'18focus\u8217\'20\'19 to be on \u8216\'20\'18what he\u8217\'20\'19s saying\u8217\'20\'19.\par \par \uc2 Biden continued:\par \par \uc2 How do you talk about the threat to democracy which is real, when a president says things like he says? Do you just not say anything because it may incite somebody?\par \par \uc2 The president said he is not the one who engages in \u8220\'20\'1Cthat rhetoric\u8221\'20\'1D, referring to Trump\u8217\'20\'19s past comments about a \u8220\'20\'1Cbloodbath\u8221\'20\'1D if the Republican loses to Biden in November.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/15/biden-nbc-interview"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Biden decries political violence in high-stakes NBC interview}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.03am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.28pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump and Vance formally nominated: key moments of first day of the Republican national convention so far\par \par \uc2 The Republican national convention is now taking a break, after completing the first of two sessions it has planned today.\par \par \uc2 The delegates will return at 5.45pm CT for what are expected to be more speeches by high-profile Republicans and party supporters.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what has happened at the convention so far:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The Republican party{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jul/15/donald-trump-republican-national-convention-speech-milwaukee-shooting-joe-biden-us-politics-latest-news-updates?page=with:block-669576eb8f08ee3616ac7076#block-669576eb8f08ee3616ac7076"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 formally nominated}}}\uc2 Donald Trump as their candidate for president.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jul/15/donald-trump-republican-national-convention-speech-milwaukee-shooting-joe-biden-us-politics-latest-news-updates?page=with:block-669572e88f080e1800f4c22a#block-669572e88f080e1800f4c22a"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 announced}}}\uc2  that Ohio senator JD Vance would be his running mate. Not long after, Vance {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jul/15/donald-trump-republican-national-convention-speech-milwaukee-shooting-joe-biden-us-politics-latest-news-updates?page=with:block-66958bb68f08ee3616ac70e3#block-66958bb68f08ee3616ac70e3"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 appeared}}}\uc2  on the floor of the convention, and the GOP {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jul/15/donald-trump-republican-national-convention-speech-milwaukee-shooting-joe-biden-us-politics-latest-news-updates?page=with:block-66958e928f08ee3616ac70fd#block-66958e928f08ee3616ac70fd"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 made him}}}\uc2  their vice-presidential nominee by acclamation.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jul/15/donald-trump-republican-national-convention-speech-milwaukee-shooting-joe-biden-us-politics-latest-news-updates?page=with:block-66958f398f080e1800f4c2dd#block-66958f398f080e1800f4c2dd"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  Vance was \u8220\'20\'1Ca clone of Trump on the issues\u8221\'20\'1D. ABC News {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jul/15/donald-trump-republican-national-convention-speech-milwaukee-shooting-joe-biden-us-politics-latest-news-updates?page=with:block-66958cc88f08ee3616ac70ea#block-66958cc88f08ee3616ac70ea"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports}}}\uc2  that \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  tried to call Vance, but couldn\u8217\'20\'19t reach him, and left a voicemail.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Robert F Kennedy Jr\uc2  met with \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in Milwaukee, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jul/15/donald-trump-republican-national-convention-speech-milwaukee-shooting-joe-biden-us-politics-latest-news-updates?page=with:block-6695827e8f080e1800f4c28b#block-6695827e8f080e1800f4c28b"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Politico reports}}}\uc2 , as the former president sought his endorsement. Kennedy, an independent presidential candidate, is polling at around 9% nationally.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  Jr{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jul/15/donald-trump-republican-national-convention-speech-milwaukee-shooting-joe-biden-us-politics-latest-news-updates?page=with:block-66957e968f080e1800f4c273#block-66957e968f080e1800f4c273"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told the Guardian}}}\uc2  he advised his father to pick JD Vance because he thought the senator would fight for him.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The Biden campaign{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jul/15/donald-trump-republican-national-convention-speech-milwaukee-shooting-joe-biden-us-politics-latest-news-updates?page=with:block-66957dc38f08ee3616ac709c#block-66957dc38f08ee3616ac709c"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 characterized Vance}}}\uc2  as an enabler of Trump.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.36pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.11pm BST\par \par \uc2 In nominating JD Vance as their vice-presidential candidate at the convention, Republicans opted for a vote of accl amation, where those in favor said \u8220\'20\'1Caye\u8221\'20\'1D, and those opposed said \u8220\'20\'1Cno\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The cries of \u8220\'20\'1Caye\u8221\'20\'1D were overwhelming. Maybe one person said \u8220\'20\'1Cno\u8221\'20\'1D. And now Vance is Trump\u8217\'20\'19s running mate.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.12pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.08pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden calls Vance 'a clone of Trump on the issues'\par \par \uc2 As he heads for campaign events in Las Vegas, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  was asked for his thoughts on JD Vance, the Ohio senator who is \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s running mate.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CA clone of Trump on the issues,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden replied. \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t see any difference.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.05pm BST\par \par \uc2 GOP formally nominates JD Vance as vice-presidential candidate\par \par \uc2 By a vote of acclamation at the Republican national convention, the GOP has formally nominated JD Vance to be \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s running mate in the November election.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.03pm BST\par \par \uc2 The crowd is breaking out into chants of \u8220\'20\'1CJD! JD! JD!\u8221\'20\'1D as Ohio lieutenant governor John Husted gives a speech nominating him as vice-president.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe vice presidency is an office of sacred trust. The man who accepts this nomination accepts with it the awesome responsibility to give wise counsel to the president, to represent America abroad, to preside over the Senate and to be ready to lead our nation at a moment\u8217\'20\'19s notice. Such a man must have an America First attitude in his heart,\u8221\'20\'1D Husted said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CJD Vance is such a man!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.56pm BST\par \par \uc2 ABC News reports that \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  called JD Vance following the announcement that has was \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s running mate, but was not able to reach him:\par \par \uc2 enltrVice President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  called Sen. JD Vance after Trump announced him as his running mate, a source familiar tells ABC News.\par \par \uc2 Harris and Vance did NOT speak but I'm told Harris did leave a voicemail.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Rachel Scott (@rachelvscott) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/rachelvscott/status/1812952375608680504?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 15, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.55pm BST\par \par \uc2 JD Vance is making his way through the packed convention floor, shaking hands with delegates while being trailed by camera operators.\par \par \uc2 The Ohio senator just took a selfie with someone, and autographed a Trump campaign sign.\par \par \uc2 We don\u8217\'20\'19t yet know if he will speak now, or later during the four-day convention.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.51pm BST\par \par \uc2 JD Vance appears at Republican national convention\par \par \uc2 JD Vance, the Ohio senator \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  just chose as his running mate, has arrived on the floor of the Republican national convention.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.50pm BST\par \par \uc2 On the convention floor, a large group of delegates and reporters appears to be gathering around where the Ohio delegation is seated.\par \par \uc2 That could be a sign that JD Vance, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s newly anointed running mate, is set to make an appearance.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.38pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Republican national convention appears to be in a holding pattern, and it\u8217\'20\'19s not clear if this was planned.\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19ve been listening to a live band play covers of rock-and-roll hits for the past half hour. Just before they started playing, House speaker Mike Johnson was onstage, and appeared to be about to introduce an attorney general, before he suddenly said his teleprompter was broken, and walked off stage.\par \par \uc2 Democratic social media accounts quickly seized on the moment:\par \par \uc2 enltrMike Johnson's teleprompter goes out and he immediately runs off stage ?? {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/oSivTxuPQb"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/oSivTxuPQb}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 DNC War Room (@DNCWarRoom) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/DNCWarRoom/status/1812944751219347852?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 15, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 About 45 minutes ago, convention attendees {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jul/15/donald-trump-republican-national-convention-speech-milwaukee-shooting-joe-biden-us-politics-latest-news-updates?page=with:block-66957f8c8f080e1800f4c27f#block-66957f8c8f080e1800f4c27f"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 received a text message}}}\uc2  saying a \u8220\'20\'1Cspecial guest\u8221\'20\'1D would soon appear at the convention. That person does not seem to have shown up yet.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.26pm BST\par \par \uc2 The chair of the \uc2 Democratic National Committee\uc2 , \uc2 Jaime Harrison\uc2 , said the selection of JD Vance as \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8216\'20\'18s running mate only raised the already high stakes of the presidential race.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CJD Vance embodies MAGA \u8211\'20\'13 with an out-of-touch extreme agenda and plans to help Trump force his Project 2025 agenda on the American people,\u8221\'20\'1D Harrison said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CA Trump-Vance ticket would undermine our democracy, our freedoms, and our future. There is so much on the line, and it\u8217\'20\'19s more important than ever that we reelect President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and Vice President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  this November.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.15pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump met with RFK Jr to seek his endorsement \u8211\'20\'13 report\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  met today in Milwaukee with \uc2 Robert F Kennedy Jr\uc2 , and discussed the independent presidential candidate\u8217\'20\'19s endorsement, Politico reports.\par \par \uc2 If Kennedy were to drop out and endorse Trump, it could further scramble the race. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://projects.fivethirtyeight.com/polls/president-general/2024/national/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Polls show}}}\uc2  Kennedy has about 9% support nationally.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYes, Mr Kennedy met with President Trump today to discuss national unity, and he hopes to meet with leaders of the Democratic Party as well,\u8221\'20\'1D Kennedy campaign press secretary Stefanie Spear told Politico. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd no he is not dropping out of the race. He is the only pro-environment, pro-choice, anti-war candidate who beats \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in head-to-head polls.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.24pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.09pm BST\par \par \uc2 Reproductive rights advocates also warned that the selection of JD Vance heightened the threat \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s reelection would pose to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  selecting JD Vance as his pick for vice president provides even more evidence that a Trump administration will stop at nothing to ban all \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Make no mistake, Trump picked him because of \u8212\'20\'14not in spite of\u8212\'20\'14 his anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bonafides,\u8221\'20\'1D said \uc2 Mini Timmaraju\uc2 , \uc2 Reproductive Freedom for All\uc2  president and CEO.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CA Trump-Vance administration will be the most dangerous administration for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and reproductive freedom in this country\u8217\'20\'19s history. We must re-elect President Biden and Vice President Harris to not only restore our rights but to safeguard our democracy.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.03pm BST\par \par \uc2 Mike Johnson announces GOP has nominated Trump for president\par \par \uc2 After all of the state delegations had been heard from, Republican House speaker Mike Johnson took to the stage to announce that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  won all of the votes, and is formally the Republican party\u8217\'20\'19s nominee for president.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe following candidate received the following votes: 2,387 votes for president \uc2 Donald J Trump\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D Johnson said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CLet\u8217\'20\'19s make it official. Accordingly, the chair announces that president \uc2 Donald J Trump\uc2 , having received a majority of the votes entitled to be cast at the convention, has been selected as the Republican party nominee for president of the United States.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.08pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 Convention attendees just received a text message saying \u8220\'20\'1Cmake your way to Fiserv Forum for a special guest appearance very soon!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The Fiserv Forum is where convention is taking place. Will Donald Trump, JD Vance, or both, make an appearance after all of the states announce their votes?\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.57pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump Jr\uc2  told me on the floor of the Republican national convention that he informed his father that JD Vance was the best pick for vice-president because he would fight for him.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI watched JD go into \u8230\'20\'26 enemy territory, from a media perspective, doing the most liberal TV shows, and prosecute the case for my father and against the Democrat lunacy that we\u8217\'20\'19ve seen,\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s son said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHe does that better than almost any of our people can do on more conservative television. And you see that, you see the intelligence and you hear his life story. That\u8217\'20\'19s gonna resonate.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.06pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.53pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden campaign says JD Vance will 'bend over backwards to enable Trump'\par \par \uc2 In a statement released following JD Vance \u8217\'20\'19s announcement as \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s running mate, Biden-Harris campaign chair \uc2 Jen O\u8217\'20\'19Malley Dillon\uc2  described the senator as an enabler for the former president.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  picked JD Vance as his running mate because Vance will do what \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t on January 6: bend over backwards to enable Trump and his extreme Maga agenda, even if it means breaking the law and no matter the harm to the American people,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more:\par \par \uc2 As Trump\u8217\'20\'19s running mate, Vance will make it his mission to enact Trump\u8217\'20\'19s Project 2025 agenda at the expense of American families. This is someone who supports banning \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  nationwide while criticizing exceptions for rape and incest survivors; railed against the Affordable Care Act , including its protections for millions with preexisting conditions; and has admitted he wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t have certified the free and fair election in 2020.\par \par \uc2 Billionaires and corporations are literally rooting for JD Vance: they know he and Trump will cut their taxes and send prices skyrocketing for everyone else.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.06pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.36pm BST\par \par \uc2 While Republicans celebrated the selection of JD Vance as \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s running mate, progressives responded to the news with dismay and outrage.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CVance is an extremist election denier who will be a rubber stamp for Trump\u8217\'20\'19s continued assault on our democracy and women\u8217\'20\'19s freedom,\u8221\'20\'1D said Adam Green, co-founder of the Progressive Change Campaign Committee. \u8220\'20\'1CThis extremist and faker is unfit for the White House, which makes him a perfect running mate for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Rahna Epting, executive director of MoveOn Political Action, added: \u8220\'20\'1CAt a time when our nation is deeply divided, JD Vance\u8217\'20\'19s selection only divides us further and harms any effort to unite this country.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Tiffany Muller, president of End Citizens United, said Trump\u8217\'20\'19s selection \u8220\'20\'1Csolidifies that his campaign is working overtime to appease wealthy donors and corporate interests\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere should be no lingering doubt that Trump and Vance will create one of the most extreme and corrupt administrations in our nation\u8217\'20\'19s history,\u8221\'20\'1D Muller said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.45pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.29pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Senate\u8217\'20\'19s Republican minority leader \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  announced Kentucky\u8217\'20\'19s votes for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 But in a sign of his {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/books/2022/sep/21/mitch-mcconnell-trump-crazy-capitol-attack-unchecked"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 continued shaky standing}}}\uc2  with Trump\u8217\'20\'19s faithful, some in the arena booed McConnell, and for whatever reason, his announcement could not be heard over its PA system.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe Commonwealth of Kentucky, proudly cast 46 votes for the next president, \uc2 Donald J Trump\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D McConnell said, according to a TV feed of the convention.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.24pm BST\par \par \uc2 GOP officially makes Trump presidential nominee\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has received the votes necessary from delegates to the Republican national convention to officially become the party\u8217\'20\'19s nominee for president in this year\u8217\'20\'19s presidential election.\par \par \uc2 Not all states have been called, but Trump has an insurmountable lead.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more from the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/alice-herman"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Alice Herman}}}\uc2  on JD Vance\u8217\'20\'19s road from Trump foe to the former president\u8217\'20\'19s running mate in his bid to return to the White House:\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has named JD Vance, the Ohio senator who has aligned himself with the populist right, as his running mate at the Republican national convention on Monday.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAfter lengthy deliberation and thought, and considering the tremendous talents of many others, I have decided that the person best suited to assume the position of Vice President of the United States is Senator JD Vance of the Great State of Ohio,\u8221\'20\'1D wrote Trump on Truth Social.\par \par \uc2 When Trump first ran for office, Vance\u8217\'20\'19s eventual nomination to run alongside him would have seemed implausible. Vance, a venture capitalist who rocketed into the public eye with his 2016 memoir turned \uc2 Netflix\uc2  movie Hillbilly Elegy, was once among Trump\u8217\'20\'19s conservative critics.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m a never-Trump guy, I never liked him,\u8221\'20\'1D Vance said during an October 2016 interview with \uc2 Charlie Rose\uc2 . Trump was, by Vance\u8217\'20\'19s estimation at the time, a \u8220\'20\'1Cterrible candidate\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 He even wondered aloud, in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://ohiocapitaljournal.com/2022/04/19/americas-hitler-old-j-d-vance-message-turns-up-in-heated-senate-primary/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 texts to a former roommate}}}\uc2 , whether Trump was more of \u8220\'20\'1Ca cynical asshole like Nixon\u8221\'20\'1D, or worse, \u8220\'20\'1CAmerica\u8217\'20\'19s Hitler\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Since then, Vance has made a dramatic transformation into a Maga power figure and close ally of the former president who has supported some of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s more authoritarian impulses, like questioning the results of the 2020 election and, in a 2021 podcast interview, suggesting Trump should purge civil servants from the federal government if re-elected.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/15/trump-vp-jd-vance-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump names Ohio senator JD Vance as vice-presidential running mate}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.17pm BST\par \par \uc2 House speaker Mike Johnson cheers Trump's selection of JD Vance as running mate\par \par \uc2 Mike Johnson, the Republican speaker of the House of Representatives, hailed \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s choice of JD Vance as his running mate.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSenator JD Vance was born and raised in Appalachia, served our country as a US Marine, and is regarded as one of the most thoughtful Senators in Congress. He possesses a profound understanding of the anxieties of working families and has both the lived experience and the policy expertise to help President Trump deliver a government worthy of the people it is supposed to serve,\u8221\'20\'1D Johnson said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFrom our economy, to the border, to our standing in the world, our nation is in turmoil under four years of President Biden. President Trump needs a vice president with innovative ideas and the ability to articulate them to every single American voter and Senator JD Vance fits that mold perfectly. It is time to unite our nation and we are eager to grow our House majority and get to work with this ticket to restore America\u8217\'20\'19s greatness once again.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.14pm BST\par \par \uc2 JD Vance just received a big cheer in the convention hall, after Mike Lee, Utah\u8217\'20\'19s Republican senator, named-dropped him as he announced his state\u8217\'20\'19s vote for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn Utah, from the red rocks to the snow-capped mountains with the greatest snow on Earth, we know what heaven on Earth looks like. Utah, the 45th state admitted to the Union today proudly casts all of its 40 delegate votes for president \uc2 Donald J Trump\uc2  and his newly announced running mate, my friend and colleague, JD Vance,\u8221\'20\'1D Lee said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.31pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.07pm BST\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s the rest of what \uc2 Donald Trump{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://truthsocial.com/@realDonaldTrump/posts/112792060910716829"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wrote on Truth Social}}}\uc2 , as he announced JD Vance as his running mate:\par \par \uc2 \u8230\'20\'26.As Vice President, J.D. will continue to fight for our Constitution, stand with our Troops, and will do everything he can to help me MAKE AMERICA GREAT AGAIN. Congratulations to Senator J.D. Vance, his wife, Usha, who also graduated from Yale Law School, and their three beautiful children. MAGA2024!\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.06pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump picks JD Vance as his running mate\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has announced that Ohio senator JD Vance will be his running mate.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what the former president wrote, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://truthsocial.com/@realDonaldTrump/posts/112792061935980928"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 on Truth Social}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 After lengthy deliberation and thought, and considering the tremendous talents of many others, I have decided that the person best suited to assume the position of Vice President of the United States is Senator J.D. Vance of the Great State of Ohio. J.D. honorably served our Country in the Marine Corps, graduated from \uc2 Ohio State University\uc2  in two years, Summa Cum Laude, and is a Yale Law School Graduate, where he was Editor of The Yale Law Journal, and President of the Yale Law Veterans Association. J.D.\u8217\'20\'19s book, \u8220\'20\'1CHillbilly Elegy,\u8221\'20\'1D became a Major Best Seller and Movie, as it championed the hardworking men and women of our Country. J.D. has had a very successful business career in Technology and Finance, and now, during the Campaign, will be strongly focused on the people he fought so brilliantly for, the American Workers and Farmers in Pennsylvania, Michigan, Wisconsin, Ohio, Minnesota, and far beyond\u8230\'20\'26.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.01pm BST\par \par \uc2 Back at the Republican national convention, the leaders of each state\u8217\'20\'19s delegation are being called on to announce who they are supporting.\par \par \uc2 Iowa, Nevada and Oklahoma have been called on so far, and announced their votes for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.50pm BST\par \par \uc2 If \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  chooses JD Vance as his running mate, it would be quite the turnaround for the Ohio senator.\par \par \uc2 Vance, a Marine Corps veteran and former venture capitalist, became well known for his 2016 memoir Hillbilly Elegy, which became popular with many Trump foes for its depiction of the impoverished white communities that turned out big that year to elect him to the White House.\par \par \uc2 Vance himself made critical comments about the then-president, before shifting his career into politics and winning Trump\u8217\'20\'19s endorsement when he successfully ran for Senate in 2022.\par \par \uc2 If he becomes Trump\u8217\'20\'19s running mate, Vance could be in a prime position to take over as the GOP presidential nominee in 2028, when term limits prevent Trump from running again. And despite speculation, the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/martin-pengelly"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Martin Pengelly}}}\uc2  recently reported that Vance\u8217\'20\'19s beard is not a problem for Trump:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/10/jd-vance-trump-vp-pick-contender"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bearded JD Vance remains a contender for Trump VP \u8211\'20\'13 by a whisker}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.59pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 Republican senator \uc2 Marsha Blackburn\uc2 , who is chair of the convention\u8217\'20\'19s platform committee, has given the highlights of the document.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis platform is built on the values of our founders and great Republicans, from Lincoln and Reagan to Trump, who are committed to freedom, restrained government and peace through strength,\u8221\'20\'1D Blackburn told the convention.\par \par \uc2 She continued:\par \par \uc2 The platform contains 20 promises, including securing our border, getting inflation under control, restoring our energy dominance, defending our constitution, protecting our second amendment rights, securing our country, restoring our military strength and keeping boys out of girls sports, and protecting life for the born and unborn.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.43pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.25pm BST\par \par \uc2 With \uc2 Doug Burgum\uc2 , the governor of North Dakota, and \uc2 Marco Rubio\uc2 , the Florida senator, reportedly both told they will not be \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s running mate, the last frontrunner still in contention is Ohio senator JD Vance.\par \par \uc2 Of course, anything is possible when it comes to Trump. But it\u8217\'20\'19s also worth noting that the \uc2 Guardian\uc2  has previously reported that \uc2 Donald Trump Jr\uc2  will speak before whoever is chosen as vice-president on Wednesday \u8211\'20\'13 and he has endorsed Vance.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.11pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.19pm BST\par \par \uc2 Burgum told he will not be Trump's running mate \u8211\'20\'13 report\par \par \uc2 Fox News reports that North Dakota governor \uc2 Doug Burgum\uc2  has been informed he will not be \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s pick for vice-president:\par \par \uc2 enltr??????\par \par \uc2 A source tells {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/steinhauserNH1?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @steinhauserNH1}}}\uc2  that North Dakota Gov. \uc2 Doug Burgum\uc2  has received a call notifying the senator that he\u8217\'20\'19s NOT Trump\u8217\'20\'19s choice for running mate.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Aishah Hasnie (@aishahhasnie) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/aishahhasnie/status/1812913487812702584?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 15, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 Burgum was an unsuccessful challenger to Trump for the GOP nomination this year, before making amends with the former president.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.15pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump has decided on his running mate and will announce pick at 3.30pm CT \u8211\'20\'13 source\par \par \uc2 I am hearing from a \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  official that the former president has decided on his running mate.\par \par \uc2 He will announce his decision at 3.30pm CT.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.17pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.13pm BST\par \par \uc2 Following a live band\u8217\'20\'19s performance of the song {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=-KoXt9pZLGM"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 God Bless }}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=-KoXt9pZLGM"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the USA}}}\uc2  by Lee Greenwood, a section of the audience broke out into another chant.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFight! Fight! Fight!\u8221\'20\'1D they yelled. It was what Trump said on Saturday, after being wounded during a shooting at his rally in Pennsylvania.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.17pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.07pm BST\par \par \uc2 We are now through the pledge of allegiance and the national anthem, which concluded with chants of \u8220\'20\'1CUSA! USA! USA!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 An honor guard bearing the US flag that was standing in front of the stage is now departing.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.12pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.01pm BST\par \par \uc2 Republican national convention officially begins\par \par \uc2 Chair Michael Whatley has gaveled in the Republican national convention, signaling its official start.\par \par \uc2 He then held a moment of silence in remembrance of the shooting at \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s rally in Pennsylvania on Saturday.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.58pm BST\par \par \uc2 Marco Rubio\uc2  informed he will not be Trump's running mate\par \par \uc2 Marco Rubio\uc2  has been told that he will not be \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s pick for vice-president, Reuters reports.\par \par \uc2 The Florida senator was among the challengers Trump faced in the GOP primaries ahead of the 2016 election, then became an ally during his presidency.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.12pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.51pm BST\par \par \uc2 Delegates have just heard an announcement to take their seats.\par \par \uc2 The Republican national convention is set to begin soon.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.43pm BST\par \par \uc2 Fox News reports that the leading candidates to be \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s running mate are all in Milwaukee, waiting to be told if the former president has chosen them.\par \par \uc2 They are North Dakota governor \uc2 Doug Burgum\uc2 , Ohio senator JD Vance, Florida senator \uc2 Marco Rubio\uc2  and Virginia governor \uc2 Glenn Youngkin\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 enltrBreaking: Burgham/Vance/Rubio/Youngkin are ALL in Milwaukee and we are hearing that all are still awaiting President Trump\u8217\'20\'19s tap on the shoulder. Apprentice vibes anyone?\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Martha MacCallum (@marthamaccallum) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/marthamaccallum/status/1812893076035174633?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 15, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.29pm BST\par \par \uc2 Republicans disagree with \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  about Milwaukee, according to the city\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic mayor.\par \par \uc2 Last month the former US president allegedly called Milwaukee a \u8220\'20\'1Chorrible city\u8221\'20\'1D and reportedly considered staying in Chicago during the convention instead.\par \par \uc2 Cavalier Johnson, the mayor of Milwaukee, told international reporters at a briefing on Monday: \u8220\'20\'1CA couple of weeks ago Mr Trump decided to say some words about Milwaukee that were patently false, that were untrue, and that\u8217\'20\'19s unfortunate.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe fact of the matter is that Republicans, folks in his own party, obviously disagree with him because they selected Milwaukee to be the host city for their presidential nominating convention, so obviously he was wrong.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Johnson, whose city has closed streets and built a security perimeter of roughly one mile by half a mile around the convention centre, added: \u8220\'20\'1CAs I\u8217\'20\'19ve had the opportunity yesterday and today to greet Republicans who are here from all over the country, they\u8217\'20\'19re having an outstanding time.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMany of them that I\u8217\'20\'19ve engaged say they really enjoy Milwaukee. This is their first time here, their first time in the state of Wisconsin, and they\u8217\'20\'19re looking forward to coming back not related to \uc2 Republican National Committee\uc2  business but simply just coming back to visit on their own and bring their families.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.32pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.29pm BST\par \par \uc2 I\u8217\'20\'19ve just spoken with a few people around the Republican national convention to get their reaction to Judge Aileen Cannon dismissing the documents case this morning.\par \par \uc2 Rick Williams, an alternate delegate from Tennessee said he was \u8220\'20\'1Coverjoyed\u8221\'20\'1D the case had been dismissed.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CProbably never should have been a case to begin with,\u8221\'20\'1D he said in an interview near the \uc2 Fiserv\uc2  forum in downtown Milwaukee, where the convention is set to begin today. \u8220\'20\'1CLike all the other cases against President Trump, they\u8217\'20\'19ve fallen apart over time.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Joe Sell, an alternate delegate from Illinois, said he didn\u8217\'20\'19t think the decision would make much of a difference in the campaign because people had made up their minds already about Trump. He said the documents case was \u8220\'20\'1Cphony\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI wasn\u8217\'20\'19t going to not vote for Trump because of that. I think it\u8217\'20\'19s all baloney,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CThey staged it. They put pictures of documents and said Trump had done all this stuff when it was actually the authorities that had done that.\u8221\'20\'1D There is no evidence that\u8217\'20\'19s true and Trump has not denied taking the documents.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.34pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.27pm BST\par \par \uc2 In a sign that things are soon to kick off, they\u8217\'20\'19re now blasting covers of rock songs inside the arena where the Republican national convention is taking place.\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19re currently listening to a cover of the Foo Fighters\u8217\'20\'19 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=1VQ_3sBZEm0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Learn to Fly}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.39pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.17pm BST\par \par \uc2 Delegates, guests and members of the news media are filing into the \uc2 Fiserv\uc2  forum in downtown Milwaukee ahead of the first session of the Republican national convention, which is scheduled to start at 12.45pm CT.\par \par \uc2 The arena, which is usually home of the Milwaukee Bucks NBC team, is far from as full as it will be tonight and in coming evenings. Nonetheless, a little bit ago, chants of \u8220\'20\'1Cfight, fight, fight,\u8221\'20\'1D briefly broke out among delegates:\par \par \uc2 zxxltr {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/pDrtOMEBFF"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/pDrtOMEBFF}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Chris Stein (@ChrisJStein) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ChrisJStein/status/1812898022335885779?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 15, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 As people walk into the arena, they\u8217\'20\'19re greeted by a video showing the theme of today\u8217\'20\'19s session, which is \u8220\'20\'1CMake America Wealthy Again\u8221\'20\'1D:\par \par \uc2 zxxltr {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/y2mEwHOjz1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/y2mEwHOjz1}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Chris Stein (@ChrisJStein) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ChrisJStein/status/1812898426310328801?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 15, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 Road work is taking place around Milwaukee, and within sight of the arena are signs saying that it was paid for by the $1t law overhauling the nation\u8217\'20\'19s infrastructure, which \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  signed three years ago:\par \par \uc2 zxxltr {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/QJFU5EiWX4"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/QJFU5EiWX4}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Chris Stein (@ChrisJStein) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ChrisJStein/status/1812898799792132465?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 15, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.32pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.56pm BST\par \par \uc2 Here are some of the latest images from the newswires from the Fiserv Forum in Milwaukee, where the main Republican national convention events are being held this week.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.19pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.43pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  received an updated briefing from homeland security and law enforcement officials on the investigation into the attempted assassination of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The briefing took place in the Situation Room and included the attorney general, homeland security secretary, \uc2 FBI\uc2  director and the director and deputy director of the Secret Service, according to the White House.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.31pm BST\par \par \uc2 My colleague Joan E Greve and I have just arrived at the press center in downtown Milwaukee. It\u8217\'20\'19s a hot \u8211\'20\'13 lots of seersucker suits on hand \u8211\'20\'13 but quiet morning.\par \par \uc2 Delegates and reporters are slowly starting to file in to the security perimeter around the Fiserv Forum, the arena where the convention festivities are being held. As you might imagine, there is a heavy security presence with lots of police and Secret Service downtown.\par \par \uc2 Vendors are just starting to set up merchandise and food (there is a stand for fried cheese curds and s\u8217\'20\'19mores that we may be sampling later). There\u8217\'20\'19s also lots of Trump merchandise.\par \par \uc2 enltrVendors are just setting up this morning. Here\u8217\'20\'19s a sampling of t shirts at one stand {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/7vMlKmxB2k"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/7vMlKmxB2k}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Sam Levine (@srl) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/srl/status/1812884800258163103?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 15, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.47pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 Prominent US business leaders have been speaking today about Saturday\u8217\'20\'19s shooting.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt is a sad moment for our country,\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 David Solomon\uc2 , the \uc2 Goldman Sachs\uc2  boss, said at the start of a conference call on the Wall Street bank\u8217\'20\'19s latest earnings. \u8220\'20\'1CThere\u8217\'20\'19s no place in our politics for violence.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Larry Fink\uc2 , CEO of \uc2 BlackRock\uc2 , told CNBC:\par \par \uc2 It is a statement of America today, though. We need to create hope. All of us have a responsibility \u8211\'20\'13 every political candidate, every leader, every pastor, minister, rabbi \u8211\'20\'13 we all have a responsibility of bringing our community together to bring hope.\par \par \uc2 In a memo to employees, \uc2 Jamie Dimon\uc2 , chairman of \uc2 JP Morgan Chase\uc2 , America\u8217\'20\'19s largest bank, stressed the need to stand against \u8220\'20\'1Cany acts of hate, intimidation or violence that seek to undermine our democracy or inflict harm\u8221\'20\'1D, adding that it was \u8220\'20\'1Conly through constructive dialogue\u8221\'20\'1D that the country can deal with its \u8220\'20\'1Ctoughest challenges\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Senior figures in Silicon Valley, including \uc2 Apple\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 Tim Cook\uc2  and Meta\u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 Mark Zuckerberg\uc2 , condemned the attack on social media this weekend.\par \par \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 who owns X, formerly \uc2 Twitter\uc2 , and runs \uc2 Tesla\uc2  and \uc2 SpaceX\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 endorsed \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and criticized the news media in the aftermath of the shooting.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.47pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.13pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , in a Truth Social post, has called for \uc2 Robert F Kennedy Jr\uc2 , the independent presidential candidate, to \u8220\'20\'1Cimmediately\u8221\'20\'1D receive Secret Service protection.\par \par \uc2 The post by Trump reads:\par \par \uc2 In light of what is going on in the world today, I believe it is imperative that \uc2 Robert F. Kennedy Jr.\uc2  receive Secret Service protection \u8212\'20\'14 immediately. Given the history of the Kennedy Family, this is the obvious right thing to do!\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.15pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.02pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Trump campaign will announce \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s pick for his vice-presidential running mate at about 4.30pm ET (20:30 GMT) today at the Republican National Convention, Reuters is reporting, citing a source.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.57pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s lawyer Alina Habba has issued a statement responding to a judge\u8217\'20\'19s ruling to dismiss his criminal case on charges that he illegally retained classified documents. She said:\par \par \uc2 This dismissal marks the first step in ending the weaponization of our justice system, restoring the rule of law, and Making America Great Again.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.45pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has said the decision by Aileen Cannon, the US district judge, to dismiss his classified documents criminal case was \u8220\'20\'1Cjust the first step\u8221\'20\'1D and called for the other cases against him, which he described as \u8220\'20\'1Cwitch hunts\u8221\'20\'1D, to also be dismissed.\par \par \uc2 Trump, in a Truth Social post, wrote:\par \par \uc2 As we move forward in Uniting our Nation after the horrific events on Saturday, this dismissal of the Lawless Indictment in Florida should be just the first step, followed quickly by the dismissal of ALL the Witch Hunts \u8212\'20\'14 The January 6th Hoax in Washington, D.C., the Manhattan D.A.\u8217\'20\'19s Zombie Case, the New York A.G. Scam, Fake Claims about a woman I never met (a decades old photo in a line with her then husband does not count), and the Georgia \u8220\'20\'1CPerfect\u8221\'20\'1D Phone Call charges. The Democrat Justice Department coordinated ALL of these Political Attacks, which are an Election Interference conspiracy against \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Political Opponent, ME. Let us come together to END all Weaponization of our Justice System, and Make America Great Again!\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.16pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 Jill Biden spoke to Melania Trump after shooting\par \par \uc2 Jill Biden, the first lady, and her predecessor, Melania Trump, spoke on Sunday afternoon following the attempted assassination attempt on \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The first ladies\u8217\'20\'19 phone call followed a phone call on Saturday night between \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CLast night I spoke with \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D said Biden at a White House press conference on Sunday. Biden noted the conversation was brief. \u8220\'20\'1CJill and I are keeping him and his family in our prayers.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.43pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.28pm BST\par \par \uc2 Video footage shows attendees of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s campaign rally on Saturday shouted to alert police officers as they saw a man with a gun on top of a roof at the Pennsylvania venue.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.13pm BST\par \par \uc2 Schumer calls Trump documents case dismissal 'breathtakingly misguided'\par \par \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2 , the Senate majority leader, has called Judge Aileen Cannon \u8217\'20\'19s dismissal of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s classified documents case \u8220\'20\'1Cbreathtakingly misguided\u8221\'20\'1D and called for the case to be resassigned.\par \par \uc2 The judge\u8217\'20\'19s ruling \u8220\'20\'1Cflies in the face of long-accepted practice and repetitive judicial precedence,\u8221\'20\'1D Schumer said in a statement shared by Fox News\u8217\'20\'19s Chad Pergram.\par \par \uc2 It is wrong on the law and must be appealed immediately. This is further evidence that Judge Cannon cannot handle this case impartially and must be reassigned.\par \par \uc2 enltrSchumer: This breathtakingly misguided ruling flies in the face of long-accepted practice and repetitive judicial precedence. It is wrong on the law and must be appealed immediately. This is further evidence that Judge Cannon cannot handle this case impartially and must be\u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Chad Pergram (@ChadPergram) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ChadPergram/status/1812865094193422819?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 15, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.07pm BST\par \par \uc2 Shares in \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s media company have surged by more than a third to their highest value in five weeks after the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/13/trump-rally-gun-shots-pennsylvania"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 attempted assassination}}}\uc2  of the former president, adding more than $1bn (\u163\'00\'A3770m) to the valuation of the business behind the X rival Truth Social.\par \par \uc2 Trump Media and Technology Group\uc2 , which uses his initials DJT as its ticker, has been a volatile stock since {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2024/mar/27/how-can-donald-trumps-lossmaking-truth-social-be-worth-8bn"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 its blockbuster debut in March}}}\uc2 . However, after Saturday night\u8217\'20\'19s attack increased Trump\u8217\'20\'19s perceived chances of winning November\u8217\'20\'19s presidential election, traders pushed the share price back to the highest level since 10 June.\par \par \uc2 It soared as high as $46.27 on Monday morning in New York, up from $30.89 on Friday evening. The price then dropped back to $41 after an hour of trading, a gain of 34%.\par \par \uc2 Trump Media is 60% owned by the former president, meaning the paper value of his stake, worth about $3.8bn on Friday, had risen by as much as $1bn.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/15/shares-trump-media-group-assassination-attempt-shooting-bitcoin-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Shares in Trump\u8217\'20\'19s media group leap by a third after assassination attempt}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.04pm BST\par \par \uc2 The House oversight committee will receive a briefing with the Secret Service on Tuesday, according to NBC News\u8217\'20\'19 Ryan Nobles.\par \par \uc2 Kim Cheatle, the director of the Secret Service, is expected to appear before the committee next Monday, he added.\par \par \uc2 enltrUPDATE:\par \par \uc2 The House Oversight Committee will hold a bi-partisan member briefing with the Secret Service tomorrow.. Based on their conversations with the agency, they expect Director Cheatle will appear for a hearing on Monday, July 22.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Ryan Nobles (@ryanobles) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ryanobles/status/1812857319174094848?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 15, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.54pm BST\par \par \uc2 Nigel Farage and \uc2 Liz Truss\uc2  are among the UK politicians set to attend the Republican national convention this week as the British right seeks to deepen ties with its American counterparts before a predicted victory for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in the presidential race.\par \par \uc2 An assassination attempt on Trump on Saturday had prompted Farage, the Reform UK party leader, to make plans to fly to the US, he said, adding that he was doing it \u8220\'20\'1Cnot just as a friend but because we have to stand up for democracy\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The convention also provides Farage with an opportunity to meet influential rightwing US figures as well as leveraging his personal brand in advance of his return as a presenter on Britain\u8217\'20\'19s GB News channel.\par \par \uc2 Truss, Britain\u8217\'20\'19s shortest-serving prime minister, is expected to speak at the event on Wednesday. Other speakers on the same day will include the oil magnate \uc2 Harold Hamm\uc2 , who has contributed $814,000 (\u163\'00\'A3627,000) to Trump\u8217\'20\'19s 2024 re-election bid.\par \par \uc2 Truss had already been seeking to build a profile in the US as a guiding force on the right after her brief stint in Downing Street, but has even more reason to try to carve out a new political career after losing her parliamentary seat in the 4 July general election.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.51pm BST\par \par \uc2 Matt Gaetz\uc2 , a Republican congressman from Florida, has hailed US district Judge Aileen Cannon \u8217\'20\'19s decision to dismiss \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s criminal case on charges that he illegally retained classified documents at his Mar-a-Lago club.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFuture Supreme Court Justice Cannon,\u8221\'20\'1D Gaetz wrote in a post on X.\par \par \uc2 enltrFuture Supreme Court Justice Cannon {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/fdDJk1tASt"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/fdDJk1tASt}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Matt Gaetz\uc2  (@mattgaetz) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/mattgaetz/status/1812850083269845272?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 15, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.57pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump to announce his vice-presidential pick today - report\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has told Fox News reporter Brett Baier that he will announce his pick for his vice-presidential running mate today.\par \par \uc2 enltrTRUMP tells {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/BretBaier?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @BretBaier}}}\uc2  he is making his VP announcement TODAY\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Aishah Hasnie (@aishahhasnie) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/aishahhasnie/status/1812857218481508610?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 15, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.58pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.43pm BST\par \par \uc2 Brendan Boyle\uc2 , a Democratic congressman from Pennsylvania and ranking member of the House budget committee, has criticized Judge Aileen Cannon \u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cdeeply corrupt act\u8221\'20\'1D after she dismissed \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s classified documents case.\par \par \uc2 enltrThis is a deeply corrupt act by a Trump judge. Very scary the powers his people want to give him. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/fa53Ulvdco"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/fa53Ulvdco}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 US Rep \uc2 Brendan Boyle\uc2  (@RepBrendanBoyle) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RepBrendanBoyle/status/1812854019213111766?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 15, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.26pm BST\par \par \uc2 The shooter in Saturday\u8217\'20\'19s assassination on \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  bought 50 rounds of ammunition at a local gun store just hours before carrying out his attack, CNN reported, citing a senior law enforcement official.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.12pm BST\par \par \uc2 A Trump-appointed judge in Florida has dismissed the criminal case against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  that charged him with illegally holding on to classified documents at his Mar-a-Lago resort.\par \par \uc2 The US district judge Aileen Cannon made the ruling after a hearing in which the former president\u8217\'20\'19s legal team urged her to drop the charges brought by special counsel Jack Smith, and notably, after the supreme court said the president has immunity for official acts.\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s team had argued that he is the victim of selective prosecution and is being targeted by Democrats as he seeks to regain the presidency.\par \par \uc2 In February, a federal prosecutor said \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  would not face criminal charges for knowingly keeping classified documents at an office and at home after he left the vice-presidency in 2017. \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2 , who served as vice-president under Trump, also was investigated but not charged for keeping classified documents at his Indiana home.\par \par \uc2 Federal prosecutors, who brought a 40-count indictment against Trump, had said his conduct was different.\par \par \uc2 While Biden and Pence cooperated with investigators, prosecutors alleged Trump discussed lying to those who were trying to recover the documents, and moved the documents around his Mar-a-Lago resort to prevent their discovery.\par \par \uc2 Some of those documents discussed national security issues including nuclear weapons capabilities and US vulnerability to military attack, according to prosecutors.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.25pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.07pm BST\par \par \uc2 Judge rules special counsel appointment 'unlawful' in case dismissal\par \par \uc2 US district judge Aileen Cannon, in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jul/15/donald-trump-republican-national-convention-speech-milwaukee-shooting-joe-biden-us-politics-latest-news-updates?page=with:block-66952afc8f08938d143b81cf#block-66952afc8f08938d143b81cf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 dismissing the classified documents criminal case}}}\uc2  against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , ruled that the special counsel, Jack Smith, was unlawfully appointed to his role and did not have the authority to bring the case.\par \par \uc2 Cannon, who was nominated by Trump, wrote in her ruling:\par \par \uc2 The Clerk is directed to CLOSE this case. Any scheduled hearings are CANCELLED. Any pending motions are DENIED AS MOOT, and any pending deadlines are TERMINATED.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.26pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 Judge dismisses classified documents case against Trump\par \par \uc2 The judge overseeing \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s classified documents case has dismissed the case, citing the unlawful appointment of special counsel Jack Smith.\par \par \uc2 enltrBREAKING: JUDGE CANNON DISMISSES TRUMP CLASSIFIED DOCS CASE CITING UNLAWFUL APPOINTMENT OF SPECIAL COUNSEL JACK SMITH {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/2figBi2KmI"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/2figBi2KmI}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/cz2t3x3sDj"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/cz2t3x3sDj}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Hugo Lowell (@hugolowell) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hugolowell/status/1812848407943229676?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 15, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.22pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.46pm BST\par \par \uc2 Keir Starmer\uc2  was initially advised to send \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  a note after the shooting, but wanted to speak to him directly, the \uc2 Guardian\uc2  understands.\par \par \uc2 The UK prime minister got in touch with Trump through the UK\u8217\'20\'19s ambassador in Washington, Karen Pierce.\par \par \uc2 The former president\u8217\'20\'19s team responded swiftly and the two men then had a short conversation lasting five or ten minutes.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.45pm BST\par \par \uc2 In Bethel Park, where the man who is suspected of opening fire at a \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  campaign rally on Saturday lived with his mother and sister, the houses are small and built of brick, \uc2 Walmart\uc2  and Target form central social hubs, and mothers watch over their children at a junior league baseball park next to a tributary of the Allegheny River.\par \par \uc2 The attempted assassination of the Republican former president just 45 miles north has put a focus on Bethel Park, as investigators attempt to establish the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/15/donald-trump-shooting-suspect-thomas-matthew-crooks-motive-investigation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 motivations of the 20-year-old shooter}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Authorities on Sunday identified the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/14/trump-rally-suspected-gunman-what-we-know"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 suspect as }}}\uc2  Thomas Matthew Crooks. Officials said they believe Crooks acted alone. But so far, they have not been able to uncover a motivation that drove the young man to unleash a hail of bullets at Trump, wounding the former president and killing a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/14/corey-comperatore-killed-trump-rally"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 former fire chief}}}\uc2  who was shielding his daughters.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 FBI\uc2  said Crook had not been on their radar. Since his identification, a fragmentary portrait has emerged, almost by virtue of its omissions. He was employed as a dietary aide at Bethel Park Skilled Nursing and Rehabilitation Center. The nursing home\u8217\'20\'19s administrator Marcie Grimm said Crooks \u8220\'20\'1Cperformed his job without concern and his background check was clean\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Nor have there been significant clues found in his political affiliations. He had registered Republican but had also donated $15 to the liberal ActBlue political action committee on \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s inauguration day. He had no past criminal cases against him, according to public court records.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/15/trump-rally-shooter-bethel-park-pennsylvania"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Read the full story: }}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/15/trump-rally-shooter-bethel-park-pennsylvania"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Focus on Bethel Park as classmates describe suspected Trump gunman}}}\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/15/trump-rally-shooter-bethel-park-pennsylvania"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Focus on Bethel Park as classmates describe suspected Trump gunman}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.24pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.31pm BST\par \par \uc2 The homeland security secretary, Alejandro Mayorkas, has described the attempted assassination of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  on Saturday as \u8220\'20\'1Ca failure\u8221\'20\'1D of security.\par \par \uc2 Mayorkas, speaking on ABC News this morning, said:\par \par \uc2 A direct line of sight like that to the former president should not occur.\par \par \uc2 He denied reports that the Secret Service had rebuffed requests from Trump\u8217\'20\'19s security detail for greater resources before the shooting.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAn incident like this cannot happen,\u8221\'20\'1D Mayorkas said in an interview on CNN, noting that \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has directed an independent review.\par \par \uc2 We are going to analyze through an independent review how that occurred, why it occurred and make recommendations and findings to make sure it doesn\u8217\'20\'19t happen again. I couldn\u8217\'20\'19t be clearer.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.23pm BST\par \par \uc2 Video shows Trump gunman crawling on roof before attack as multiple onlookers alert police\par \par \uc2 Video footage posted on social media shows the man who targeted \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in an assassination attempt on Saturday crawling on to the roof of a building from where he shot at the former president, as multiple onlookers frantically pointed him out to nearby police officers.\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/dc_draino/status/1812642041391915384?s=46&t=5d0289ex1Xv47-d5NoPIhQ"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 video}}}\uc2  on X, reported by New York Post, shows several people pointing at Thomas Matthew Crooks, 20, as he climbed on to the roof of a manufacturing plant about 400 feet from where Trump was speaking at the rally in Butler, Pennsylvania.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CLook they\u8217\'20\'19re all pointing,\u8221\'20\'1D a person is heard saying in the video, as several people point and watch Crooks, who can be seen rolling on the roof and crawling forward on his hands and knees.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYeah, someone\u8217\'20\'19s up on the top of the roof. There he is right there,\u8221\'20\'1D the person says. Others are heard saying: \u8220\'20\'1CRight here, right on the roof.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 One person is heard shouting \u8220\'20\'1Cofficer\u8221\'20\'1D and others say \u8220\'20\'1Che\u8217\'20\'19s on the roof\u8221\'20\'1D while pointing.\par \par \uc2 Trump can be heard giving his remarks in the background. During the video, police officers appeared largely unresponsive to the onlookers\u8217\'20\'19 concerns.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.59pm BST\par \par \uc2 Cavalier Johnson, has said he is feeling \u8220\'20\'1Cpretty confident\u8221\'20\'1D in the level of security at the Republican National Convention in Milwaukee.\par \par \uc2 The city\u8217\'20\'19s mayor, at a Monday morning briefing, said:\par \par \uc2 The folks on the ground here have confidence in the work that they\u8217\'20\'19ve put in over the course of the last 18 months. I have faith and confidence as well in the Secret Service and the police and fire departments and other agencies providing security today.\par \par \uc2 Wisconsin is an \u8220\'20\'1Copen carry\u8221\'20\'1D state which does not restrict the carrying of unconcealed, loaded firearms in public, so individuals will be allowed to have firearms within the soft perimeter outside Fiserv Forum that is not under Secret Service jurisdiction, CNN reported.\par \par \uc2 Johnson said his concern about gun safety goes beyond a single event. He said:\par \par \uc2 There are far too many people who have access to deadly weapons who should not have access to deadly weapons.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.28pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.50pm BST\par \par \uc2 Glenn Youngkin\uc2  has ordered US and Virginia state flags to be flown at half-staff to honor Corey Comperatore, the Pennsylvania volunteer firefighter chief who was shot and killed amidst an assassination attempt on \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  on Saturday.\par \par \uc2 The flags will be lowered at noon ET and remain at half-staff until sunset on Tuesday. The Virginia governor\u8217\'20\'19s statement reads:\par \par \uc2 Virginia stands in solidarity with and extends prayers to all Pennsylvanians, especially those who remain in critical condition and their families.\par \par \uc2 Comperatore, 50, was shot at Trump\u8217\'20\'19s rally as he shielded his family to protect them as gunshots rang out. In a \uc2 Facebook\uc2  post, his daughter, Allyson Comperatore, wrote:\par \par \uc2 He shielded my body from the bullet that came at us. He loved his family. He truly loved us enough to take a real bullet for us.\par \par \uc2 Two other rally attendants were wounded: 57-year-old David Dutch of New Kensington, Pennsylvania, and 74-year-old James Copenhaver of Moon Township, Pennsylvania.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.28pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.39pm BST\par \par \uc2 Secret Service director says changes made to Trump's security detail\par \par \uc2 Kimberly Cheatle, the director of the Secret Service, has issued her first major statement since the assassination attempt on \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , in which she said the agency was increasing security for the former president and the Republican National Convention in Milwaukee.\par \par \uc2 The statement reads:\par \par \uc2 I would like to start by extending my deepest condolences to the family and friends of Corey Comperatore, who was killed during the assassination attempt on former President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s life in Butler, Pennsylvania, Saturday, as well as those who were injured during this senseless act of violence.\par \par \uc2 Secret Service personnel on the ground moved quickly during the incident, with our counter sniper team neutralizing the shooter and our agents implementing protective measures to ensure the safety of former president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Since the shooting, I have been in constant contact with Secret Service personnel in Pennsylvania who worked to maintain the integrity of the crime scene until the \uc2 FBI\uc2  assumed its role as the lead investigating agency into the assassination attempt. I have also been coordinating with the protective detail for former President Trump and have briefed President Biden on the details of the incident.\par \par \uc2 The Secret Service is working with all involved Federal, state and local agencies to understand what happened, how it happened, and how we can prevent an incident like this from ever taking place again. We understand the importance of the independent review announced by President Biden yesterday and will participate fully. We will also work with the appropriate Congressional committees on any oversight action.\par \par \uc2 The incident in Pennsylvania has understandably led to questions about potential updates or changes to the security for the Republican National Convention in Milwaukee. The \uc2 U.S. Secret Service\uc2 , in conjunction with our Federal, state and local law enforcement and public safety partners, designs operational security plans for National Special Security Events (NSSE) to be dynamic in order to respond to a kinetic security environment and the most up-to-date intelligence from our partners.\par \par \uc2 I am confident in the security plan our Secret Service RNC coordinator and our partners have put in place, which we have reviewed and strengthened in the wake of Saturday\u8217\'20\'19s shooting. The security plans for National Special Security Events are designed to be flexible. As the conventions progress, and in accordance with the direction of the President, the Secret Service will continuously adapt our operations as necessary in order to ensure the highest level of safety and security for convention attendees, volunteers and the City of Milwaukee. In addition to the additional security enhancements we provided former President Trump\u8217\'20\'19s detail in June, we have also implemented changes to his security detail since Saturday to ensure his continued protection for the convention and the remainder of the campaign.\par \par \uc2 The Secret Service is tasked with the tremendous responsibility of protecting the current and former leaders of our democracy. It is a responsibility that I take incredibly seriously, and I am committed to fulfilling that mission.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.25pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump to 'bring the whole country' together in new \uc2 RNC\uc2  speech\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  arrived yesterday in Milwaukee for the Republican National Convention, where he is due to accept his party\u8217\'20\'19s formal nomination with a speech later this week after being the target of an attempted assassination at his campaign rally on Saturday.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe speech I was going to give on Thursday was going to be a humdinger,\u8221\'20\'1D the former president told the Washington Examiner in an interview {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonexaminer.com/news/campaigns/presidential/3082180/trump-rewrites-republican-convention-speech-focus-unity-not-biden/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 published}}}\uc2  on Sunday evening.\par \par \uc2 In his newly revised nomination acceptance speech, Trump said, he will call for a new effort at national unity, noting that people from different political views have called him. He said:\par \par \uc2 This is a chance to bring the whole country, even the whole world, together. The speech will be a lot different, a lot different than it would\u8217\'20\'19ve been two days ago.\par \par \uc2 Republicans will gather today in downtown Milwaukee to Thursday, where they will officially annoint Trump as their presidential nominee. He is also expected to announce his vice-presidential pick, who will be expected to deliver a speech of their own on Wednesday night.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 In an interview Sunday Michael Whatley, Republican party chairman, said this weeks convention\u8217\'20\'19s programming wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t be changed after the shooting. The agenda, he said, will feature more than 100 speakers overwhelmingly focused on Trump\u8217\'20\'19s plans.\par \par \uc2 Associated Press quotes Whatley saying: \u8220\'20\'1CWe have to be able to lay out a vision for where we want to take this country. We are going to have the convention that we have been planning for the last 18 months. We are a combination of relieved and grateful that the president is going to be here and is going to accept the nomination.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.30pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.23pm BST\par \par \uc2 Dan Milmo and Jasper Jolly report:\par \par \uc2 Shares in \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s media company surged by 50% in pre-market trading after the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/13/trump-rally-gun-shots-pennsylvania"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 attempted assassination}}}\uc2  of the former US president, potentially adding nearly $3bn (\u163\'00\'A32.3bn) to the valuation of the business behind the X rival Truth Social.\par \par \uc2 Trump Media and Technology Group\uc2 , which uses Trump\u8217\'20\'19s initials DJT as its ticker, has been a volatile stock since its debut on 26 March this year.\par \par \uc2 However, traders are set to push the share price back towards levels not experienced since May after the attack on Saturday night appeared to increase Trump\u8217\'20\'19s chances of winning November\u8217\'20\'19s presidential election.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/15/shares-trump-media-group-assassination-attempt-shooting-bitcoin-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Shares in Trump\u8217\'20\'19s media group leap after assassination attempt}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.30pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.14pm BST\par \par \uc2 Nearly 2,500 delegates are gathering in Milwaukee this week for a roll call vote to select the Republican presidential nominee, formally ending the presidential primary.\par \par \uc2 A vast majority of those delegates are already bound to support \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , who only needs a majority to win the Republican nomination.\par \par \uc2 Trump himself is expected to speak on Thursday to accept the nomination, with a speech he says has been rewritten after the assassination attempt on him at the weekend.\par \par \uc2 150 Republican delegates \u8211\'20\'13 including the entire delegations from Montana, New Mexico and South Dakota \u8211\'20\'13 are technically \u8220\'20\'1Cunbound,\u8221\'20\'1D meaning they can vote for any candidate at the convention. Dozens of those delegates, howver, have already confirmed to Associated Press that they plan to vote for Trump.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.38am BST\par \par \uc2 Angela Giuffrida is the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s Rome correspondent.\par \par \uc2 An Italian sports journalist and blogger has described how he became the target of fake news after he was accused of being the suspect behind \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s attempted assassination.\par \par \uc2 Marco Violi told Il Messaggero that he woke up to hundreds of messages in the early hours of Sunday after two accounts on X posted a photo of him alongside a message saying that Butler police department had identified Trump\u8217\'20\'19s shooter as \u8220\'20\'1CMark Violets, a rabid Antifa member\u8221\'20\'1D. Mark Violets is a direct English translation of his name. The accounts had millions of followers, with the message circulating for several hours and republished on a number of international websites before the real suspect was identified.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFirst my name was mangled as Mark Violets but then my real name appeared,\u8221\'20\'1D Violi told Il Messaggero. \u8220\'20\'1CI immediately realised that it all started from a tweet from a couple of accounts on X which have been persecuting me on social media for six years. The incredible thing is they went viral in an instant. Media from all over the world covered this fake news without anyone trying to verify it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The Rome-based journalist said he had become a target of online trolls after criticising James Pallotta, an American businessman and the former owner of AS Roma football club. Violi said he was ready to take legal action \u8220\'20\'1Cto protect my image\u8221\'20\'1D and to ask for closure of the online accounts \u8220\'20\'1Cwhich have been persecuting my family and I since 2018\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.31pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.28am BST\par \par \uc2 Our video team have cut together more of the dramatic footage from the attempt to assassinate \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  at the weekend.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.21am BST\par \par \uc2 Mehdi Hasan has written for the Guardian today, arguing people need to talk about the cult-like turn of the Democratic party:\par \par \uc2 Is the Democratic party, the self-proclaimed party of liberal values and scientific data, morphing into a Maga-like cult in front of our eyes?\par \par \uc2 Over the past few weeks, the calls for \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  to step aside have been met not with thoughtful critiques or reasoned counter-arguments but with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/imbecilesrus/status/1811563058801586195"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 furious accusations}}}\uc2  of treason, disloyalty, and betrayal.\par \par \uc2 Whatever happened to the importance of voicing dissent? Of speaking truth to power? Weren\u8217\'20\'19t liberals supposed to be the folks who value open debate and discussion?\par \par \uc2 Read more here: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/article/2024/jul/15/democrats-joe-biden-maga"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Mehdi Hasan \u8211\'20\'13 Blue Maga: we need to talk about the cult-like turn of the Democratic party}}}\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/article/2024/jul/15/democrats-joe-biden-maga"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Blue Maga: We need to talk about the cult-like turn of the Democratic party | Mehdi Hasan}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.12am BST\par \par \uc2 Democratic party still plan to nominate \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  in virtual vote before their convention\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will receive the official nomination from fellow Democrats for a second term in a virtual vote as planned in late July, ahead of the party\u8217\'20\'19s national convention, despite calls for him to step aside and the shock of an assassination attempt on Biden\u8217\'20\'19s likely opponent, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Reuters cited four people involved in the process, but said it remains unclear how the early nominating process will work.\par \par \uc2 Reuters spoke to more than 20 of the 4,500 delegates who will be involved in the nomination. Eight told Reuters they either had not heard about what senior Democrats have described as a \u8220\'20\'1Cvirtual roll call\u8221\'20\'1D or they had not heard any details on it recently.\par \par \uc2 The early nomination is needed to deal with an Ohio law that could have kept Biden\u8217\'20\'19s name off ballots in the state if he wasn\u8217\'20\'19t nominated by 7 August, prior to party\u8217\'20\'19s convention in Chicago. The plan was put in place before Biden\u8217\'20\'19s performance in the 27 June debate.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.54am BST\par \par \uc2 King Charles writes privately to Trump after assassination attempt\par \par \uc2 Britain\u8217\'20\'19s King Charles III is understood to have written privately to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  after the former US president survived an assassination attempt, Buckingham Palace has said.\par \par \uc2 PA Media reports Charles\u8217\'20\'19s message was in keeping with UK prime minister \uc2 Keir Starmer\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s conversation with Trump, in which he condemned the violence, expressed his condolences for the victims and their families, and wished the former president and those injured a quick recovery.\par \par \uc2 The king\u8217\'20\'19s message was delivered on Sunday via the UK embassy in Washington DC. Buckingham Palace said the contents of the correspondence would be kept private.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.47pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.35am BST\par \par \uc2 Writing for the \uc2 New York Times\uc2 , \uc2 David French\uc2  has looked at the likely impact of the weekend\u8217\'20\'19s shooting on the way the Republican National Convention plays out over the next few days. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2024/07/15/opinion/trump-republican-convention.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 He said}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 The key change will be in the intensity of the gathering. Expect to see an immense amount of anger and pride. Republicans are rightly proud of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s immediate response to the shooting. His presence of mind to raise his fist to the crowd to signal that he was very much alive and defiant was an impressive act of leadership. And we should all feel angry when someone tries to assassinate a former president and current candidate. We also know, however, that anger can be dangerous. Our great national challenge will be responding to that anger, to keep it from spiraling out of control. The key player here will be Trump, of course, and his nomination speech may well be the most-watched address in a generation. He has a historic opportunity to rise to the moment \u8211\'20\'13 or pull us deeper into darkness.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.34am BST\par \par \uc2 Former \uc2 US Secret Service\uc2  agents spent the early aftermath of what authorities say was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donald-trump-pennsylvania-rally-shooting"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 an attempt to assassinate Donald Trump}}}\uc2  at a political rally on Saturday speaking out about what might have prevented their previous employer from failing to halt the shooter before he opened fire.\par \par \uc2 Evy Poumpouras, who served in the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/secret-service"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Secret Service}}}\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s presidential protective division during \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s time in the White House, told NBC\u8217\'20\'19s Today show that rallies like the one this weekend \u8211\'20\'13 in a relatively exposed rural tract of Butler county, Pennsylvania \u8211\'20\'13 \u8220\'20\'1Care the most anxious you\u8217\'20\'19re ever going to be as an agent because you\u8217\'20\'19re trying to secure all of it\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 In her {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.today.com/video/former-secret-service-analyzes-moments-around-trump-shooting-214822469940"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 remarks}}}\uc2  Sunday, the author and journalist suggested local- and state-level law enforcement officers who collaborate with the Secret Service for such events were likely the first line of defense in the area surrounding the Trump rally venue \u8211\'20\'13 a position reportedly confirmed by agency spokesperson {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://nypost.com/2024/07/14/us-news/secret-service-blames-local-police-says-it-was-tasked-with-securing-properties-surrounding-trumps-pa-rally/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Anthony Guglielmi}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 At Saturday\u8217\'20\'19s rally, a man with a rifle was able to climb atop the roof of a bottle manufacturing plant and fire several shots at the former president at a distance of only about 165 yards.\par \par \uc2 Multiple people who were outside the venue but near that building \u8211\'20\'13 listening to Trump campaign for another presidency \u8211\'20\'13 reported trying to point out the gunman to police officers stationed there. But Poumpouras said a key question to answer moving forward is to determine whether those people were directly speaking to officers or if they were unsuccessfully trying to get their attention.\par \par \uc2 Read more here: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/15/secret-service-trump-rally-shooting"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ex-Secret Service agents say \u8216\'20\'18massive realignment\u8217\'20\'19 warranted after Trump rally shooting}}}\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/15/secret-service-trump-rally-shooting"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ex-Secret Service agents say \u8216\'20\'18massive realignment\u8217\'20\'19 warranted after Trump rally shooting}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.18am BST\par \par \uc2 Putin has not contacted Trump and does not plan to, Kremlin says\par \par \uc2 The Kremlin said on Monday that Russian president Vladimir Putin had not contacted Donald Trump after the assassination attempt on the Republican US presidential candidate and had no plans to do so, Reuters reports.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.47pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.59am BST\par \par \uc2 Edward Helmore reports for the Guardian\par \par \uc2 In Bethel Park, where the man who is suspected of opening fire at a Donald Trump campaign rally on Saturday lived with his mother and sister, the houses are small and built of brick, Walmart and Target form central social hubs, and moms watch over their children at a junior league baseball park next to a tributary of the Allegheny river.\par \par \uc2 Claire, a young woman who had known Thomas Matthew Crooks through his elder sister and who did not provide a last name, said she could not quite believe the boy she had once knew had attempted to assassinate a US president. \u8220\'20\'1CHe\u8217\'20\'19s so young to want to go do that\u8221\'20\'1D, she said.\par \par \uc2 She said Crooks had had a difficult time socially. \u8220\'20\'1CHe wasn\u8217\'20\'19t the most attractive-looking and I don\u8217\'20\'19t think he did sports that can add appeal\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 Jameson Myers said that Crooks had tried out for the school rifle team but had not made the roster. \u8220\'20\'1CHe didn\u8217\'20\'19t just not make the team, he was asked not to come back because how bad of a shot he was, it was considered like, dangerous\u8221\'20\'1D, Myers {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://abcnews.go.com/Politics/trump-rally-shooting-suspect-fbi-names-pennsylvania-man/story?id=111921870"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told ABC News.}}}\uc2  Jameson Murphy {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://nypost.com/2024/07/14/us-news/would-be-trump-assassin-tried-to-join-high-school-shooting-club-was-rejected-for-being-comically-bad-shot/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told the Post}}}\uc2  that Crooks was \u8220\'20\'1Ca comically bad shot\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.44am BST\par \par \uc2 Biden postpones Texas trip\par \par \uc2 President Joe Biden has postponed a planned trip to Texas today, where he was to speak on the 60th anniversary of the Civil Rights Act at the Lyndon B Johnson presidential library.\par \par \uc2 An NBC News interview between Biden and anchor Lester Holt will now occur at the White House, instead of in Texas, as initially planned, Associated Press reports.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.49pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.22am BST\par \par \uc2 Here is the key passage from president Joe Biden \u8217\'20\'19s response on Sunday to the shooting at Donald Trump \u8217\'20\'19s Pennsylvania rally at the weekend:\par \par \uc2 There is no place in America for this kind of violence or for any violence for that matter.\par \par \uc2 An assassination attempt is contrary to everything we stand for as a nation. Everything. It\u8217\'20\'19s not who we are as a nation. It\u8217\'20\'19s not America, and we cannot allow this to happen.\par \par \uc2 Unity is the most elusive goal of all, but nothing is important than that right now \u8211\'20\'13 unity.\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19ll debate, and we\u8217\'20\'19ll disagree. That\u8217\'20\'19s not going to change. But we\u8217\'20\'19re going to not lose sight of the fact of who we are as Americans.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.17am BST\par \par \uc2 FBI: Trump rally shooter acted alone but motive is still unclear\par \par \uc2 Speaking in a telephone briefing, FBI special agent in charge Kevin Rojek gave the media this update, saying:\par \par \uc2 At this time, the information that we have indicates that the shooter acted alone and that there are currently no public safety concerns. At present we have not identified an ideology associated with the subject, but I want to remind everyone that we\u8217\'20\'19re still very early in this investigation.\par \par \uc2 The FBI said they found a suspected explosive device in the suspects vehicle. Rojek said \u8220\'20\'1CWe have seized the device, rendered it safe and we are also in the process of analyzing that further.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 A later FBI update said suspicious devices had been found in the home of the suspect.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.50pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.14am BST\par \par \uc2 Reuters has spoken to residents of Bethel Park, where the suspected shooter came from.\par \par \uc2 Wes Morgan, a 42-year-old who works at an investment management company and bikes with his children on the same street as Thomas Matthew Crooks\u8217\'20\'19 residence said \u8220\'20\'1CBethel Park is a pretty blue-collar type of area, and to think that somebody was that close is a little insane.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 A couple standing on the porch of their nearby brick ranch-style home was left processing the events and spotlight on their neighbourhood.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere\u8217\'20\'19s never been a gun issue. There\u8217\'20\'19s never been the police being called,\u8221\'20\'1D Mary Priselac, 67, said alongside her husband. \u8220\'20\'1CYou kind of have to wonder what didn\u8217\'20\'19t he get in life? What led to this extreme?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Crooks\u8217\'20\'19 gun \u8211\'20\'13 an AR-style-5.56 caliber rifle \u8211\'20\'13 had been legally bought, FBI officials said.\par \par \uc2 Jim Knapp, who retired from his job as the school counselor at Bethel Park High School in 2022, said Crooks had always been \u8220\'20\'1Cquiet as a churchmouse,\u8221\'20\'1D \u8220\'20\'1Crespectful\u8221\'20\'1D and kept to himself.\par \par \uc2 He contradicted some statements by former pupils which suggested Crooks had been frequently bullied, telling Reuters he rarely came across Crooks because \u8220\'20\'1Che wasn\u8217\'20\'19t a needy type kid.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Crooks occasionally ate lunch by himself in the school cafeteria, said Knapp, who would engage such students to see if they wanted company.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CKids weren\u8217\'20\'19t calling him names, kids weren\u8217\'20\'19t bullying him,\u8221\'20\'1D Knapp said.\par \par \uc2 Knapp said he never knew Crooks to be political in any way \u8220\'20\'1CAnybody could snap, anybody could have issues,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CSomething triggered that young man and drove him to drive up to Butler yesterday and do what he did.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.12am BST\par \par \uc2 Helen Sullivan has spoken to Evan Vucci, the photographer who took the picture of Donald Trump that seems likely to be remembered as an iconic imagine in US history:\par \par \uc2 The photograph was taken by Evan Vucci, chief Washington photographer for the Associated Press. Vucci has been covering Trump since his candidacy eight years ago and in 2020 won a Pulitzer for a photograph of protests after {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/may/22/george-floyd-murder-change-across-world-blm"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 George Floyd\u8217\'20\'19s death}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI heard the shots. So I ran to the stage as the Secret Service agents were starting to cover President Trump up. They were coming up on the stage from all different directions, and they were going on top of him. I went to the front, side of the stage and I started photographing everything I could,\u8221\'20\'1D says Vucci, who told the Guardian he has covered hundreds of rallies like the one in Pennsylvania on Sunday.\par \par \uc2 More agents arrived, he said, and what appeared to be a Swat team.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI started thinking, OK, what\u8217\'20\'19s going to happen next? Where is he going to go? Where do I need to be? Where do I need to stand? What is going to happen?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe job is all about anticipation,\u8221\'20\'1D Vucci says.\par \par \uc2 Vucci started thinking about the evacuation route. It would be on the other side of the stage, the quickest way to Trump\u8217\'20\'19s SUV. He positioned himself at the stairs near the stage.\par \par \uc2 Vucci says he \u8220\'20\'1Cwas somewhat taken aback\u8221\'20\'1D when Trump raised his fist, but there was only one thing was running through his mind: \u8220\'20\'1CSlow down, think, compose. Slow down, think, compose.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Read more here: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/15/trump-rally-shooting-photographer-evan-vucci-story"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18The job is all about anticipation\u8217\'20\'19: behind the lens of the defining photo of the Trump rally shooting}}}\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/15/trump-rally-shooting-photographer-evan-vucci-story"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18The job is all about anticipation\u8217\'20\'19: behind the lens of the defining photo of the Trump rally shooting}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.08am BST\par \par \uc2 My colleague Ramon Antonio Vargas overnight has pulled together everything we know so far about the man who attempted to kill Donald Trump:\par \par \uc2 The early portrait that has emerged of the 20-year-old Pennsylvania man who authorities say {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donald-trump-pennsylvania-rally-shooting"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 tried to assassinate Donald Trump}}}\uc2  at a campaign rally in the state on Saturday before secret service agents shot him to death is a complicated and so far sparse one.\par \par \uc2 Thomas Matthew Crooks resided in Bethel Park, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/pennsylvania"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Pennsylvania}}}\uc2 , a predominantly white, generally affluent suburb of Pittsburgh. Public records show he shared a home with parents who were licensed behavioral care counselors. Those same records contain no mention of any criminal or traffic citations \u8211\'20\'13 as well as any financial problems such as foreclosures.\par \par \uc2 Actions that Crooks took late in his time as a student at Bethel Park high school offered virtually no hint of his political leanings. He was a junior at the school, and it was the first day of Joe Biden\u8217\'20\'19s presidency, when Crooks donated $15 to the Progressive Turnout Project, a political action committee aligned with the president\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic party. Public records show his father is a registered Republican and his mother a registered Democrat.\par \par \uc2 A former classmate of Crooks\u8217\'20\'19 said he had not shown any particular interest in politics in high school, but they would discuss computers and games. Another young man who described himself as a former schoolmate of Crooks at Bethel Park high school spoke with reporters Sunday, recalling how his ex-companion \u8220\'20\'1Cwas bullied almost every day\u8221\'20\'1D on campus.\par \par \uc2 Read more here: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/14/trump-rally-suspected-gunman-what-we-know"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump rally shooting \u8211\'20\'13 what we know about the suspected gunman}}}\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/14/trump-rally-suspected-gunman-what-we-know"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump rally shooting: what we know about the suspected gunman}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.06am BST\par \par \uc2 Protest organisers say they will still demonstrate during RNC despite Trump shooting\par \par \uc2 Associated Press reports thast activists gathering in Milwaukee for the start of the Republican National Convention say the assassination attempt on Donald Trump won\u8217\'20\'19t affect their longstanding plans to demonstrate outside the convention site this week.\par \par \uc2 A diverse range of organizations and activists is expected outside the downtown Fiserv Forum, it says. The largest expected demonstration was slated to start Monday morning. The Coalition to March on the RNC, comprised largely of local groups, planned to protest for access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, for immigrant rights, and against the war in Gaza among other issues.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe shooting has nothing to do with us,\u8221\'20\'1D said Omar Flores, a coalition spokesperson. \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re going to continue with the march as we planned.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Organizers expect an estimated 5,000 to 10,000 attendees. Separately, the Philadelphia-based Poor People\u8217\'20\'19s Army, which organizes for economic justice, plans an afternoon march.\par \par \uc2 The US Secret Service has said security plans for the Republica National Convention, which have been in the works for more than a year, remain the same.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.02am BST\par \par \uc2 The investigations and likely recriminations after someone was able to breach security and shoot at Donald Trump during his rally in Pennsylvania will most likely continue apace.\par \par \uc2 On Sunday evening House speaker Mike Johnson said \u8220\'20\'1CCongress will do a full investigation of the tragedy yesterday to determine where there were lapses in security and anything else that the American people need to know and deserve to know.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Secret Service director, Kimberly A Cheatle, has already been summoned to appear before the House oversight committee on 22 July.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.01am BST\par \par \uc2 Republican national convention has yet to announce speaker schedule\par \par \uc2 If you wanted to plan ahead who and what to watch at this week\u8217\'20\'19s Republican National Convention, then I have bad news: the party hasn\u8217\'20\'19t released a full slate of speakers, and it\u8217\'20\'19s possible we won\u8217\'20\'19t know who is taking the stage each night until hours before.\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump is expected to give his nomination acceptance speech Thursday. The day prior to that, his as-yet-unannounced pick for VP is due to give a speech in their own right on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 There are themes for each night\u8217\'20\'19s speeches, from economics to immigration to crime to national security, and we know that several members of the Trump family and their associates are due to speak. The RNC will livestream proceedings across a number of online platforms, including YouTube.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.49pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.59am BST\par \par \uc2 Welcome and opening summary \u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 Welcome to our rolling coverage of US politics, which is dominated by the aftermath of the attempted assasination of former president and presumptive Republican nominee for this year\u8217\'20\'19s election, Donald Trump. Here is the latest \u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump gave an interview, his first since the shooting, to the conservative newspaper the Washington Examiner, saying that he has rewritten his RNC speech. \u8220\'20\'1CThe speech I was going to give on Thursday was going to be a humdinger,\u8221\'20\'1D he said, and that it \u8220\'20\'1Cwould\u8217\'20\'19ve been one of the most incredible speeches\u8221\'20\'1D. Its focus was Biden\u8217\'20\'19s policies while in office, Trump said. \u8220\'20\'1CThis is a chance to bring the whole country, even the whole world, together. The speech will be a lot different, a lot different than it would\u8217\'20\'19ve been two days ago,\u8221\'20\'1D he said\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump said that the reason he wasn\u8217\'20\'19t killed was that he looked away from the crowd and to a screen with speech notes. \u8220\'20\'1CI rarely look away from the crowd. Had I not done that in that moment, well, we would not be talking today, would we?\u8221\'20\'1D. Trump arrived in Milwaukee on Sunday night for the Republican National Convention, which is expected to continue as scheduled\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Two other rally attendees were also shot and survived. One man, Corey Comperatore, 50, died in the shooting, and has been hailed as a hero from trying to protect his daughters from the bullets\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 CNN and the ABC reported that Trump underwent a precautionary CT scan after he was grazed by a bullet at a rally on Saturday. The ABC cited unnamed sources who said the scan came back clear\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 FBI officials said on Sunday they were assessing the shooting as a possible domestic terrorism attack and assassination attempt. The suspected shooter is dead. He was named as 20-year-old Thomas Matthew Crooks of Bethel Park, Pennsylvania\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Early details shed little light on why Crooks might have wanted to carry out an attack on Trump or his supporters. Public records showed he was a registered Republican, though he had once donated $15 to a progressive PAC.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Early attempts to identify social media posts or other writings that would explain the shooting were not successful. FBI officials said on Sunday afternoon that they did not \u8220\'20\'1Ccurrently have an identified motive\u8221\'20\'1D and that \u8220\'20\'1Cat present, we have not identified an ideology associated with the subject\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden gave an address to the nation, calling for unity and a rejection of political violence. His campaign was reportedly planning to tone down verbal attacks and television attack ads against Trump in the wake of the shooting, while still continuing to tout Biden\u8217\'20\'19s political message about why voters should elect him in November\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240715ek7f000xi\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
