\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Welcome to the Trump show: Republican convention to resemble coronation\b0\par\par\uc2 David Smith in Washington \par \uc2 2,041 \uc2 words\par \uc2 14 July 2024\par 13:19 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Speaker after speaker will line up in Milwaukee to pay tribute to their nominee \u8211\'20\'13 who they are likely to hail as literally bulletproof after an apparent assassination attempt\par \par \uc2 The political iconography was instant and indelible. His face bloodied, his fist raised, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  stood defiant as Secret Service agents scrambled around him against the backdrop of the Stars and Stripes and a brilliant blue sky.\par \par \uc2 The apparent attempt to assassinate the former president at a campaign rally in Pennsylvania on Saturday shook the American political kaleidoscope once again. It cast a shadow over the Republican national convention, due to start in Milwaukee, Wisconsin, on Monday \u8211\'20\'13 but potentially handed Trump and his allies a political opportunity.\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s allies will probably praise Trump as a strongman who is quite literally bulletproof \u8211\'20\'13 and blame his opponents for the explosion of violence.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CToday is not just some isolated incident,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/JDVance1/status/1812280973628965109"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 tweeted JD Vance}}}\uc2 , an Ohio senator widely tipped to be name as Trump\u8217\'20\'19s running mate at the convention. \u8220\'20\'1CThe central premise of the Biden campaign is that President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is an authoritarian fascist who must be stopped at all costs. That rhetoric led directly to President Trump\u8217\'20\'19s attempted assassination.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Host city Milwaukee, in the battleground state of Wisconsin, has sudden historical resonance. It was here in 1912 that Theodore Roosevelt, a former president seeking to regain the White House, was the victim of a would-be assassination. The bullet was slowed by a steel case for his glasses and a manuscript of his 50-page speech, ultimately lodging in his chest. Roosevelt went on to deliver the speech while bleeding through his shirt.\par \par \uc2 Steve Schmidt\uc2 , a former Republican strategist, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/SteveSchmidtSES/status/1812272029959373146"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wrote on X}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CThe political consequences of this assassination attempt will be immense, and they will benefit \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , who just responded to being shot in the exact same way that Teddy Roosevelt did.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Even before Saturday\u8217\'20\'19s shooting, the convention was set to be a coronation of Trump as Republicans\u8217\'20\'19 presidential nominee, throwing in sharp relief the Democratic discord over \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s viability as a candidate.\par \par \uc2 Republicans have nominated Trump for the presidency twice before. But in 2016 and even 2020 he faced critics inside his own party and was the underdog in the race for the White House. This time, however, Trump has the edge in opinion polls following Biden\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jun/28/biden-trump-first-presidential-debate"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 calamitous debate performance}}}\uc2 . And his takeover of the Republican party is complete.\par \par \uc2 Dissenters have been purged, losing their congressional seats to Trump allies or quietly fading into retirement. The \uc2 Republican National Committee\uc2  co-chair is Trump\u8217\'20\'19s daughter-in-law Lara. This week {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/hub/nikki-haley"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Nikki Haley}}}\uc2 , who was Trump\u8217\'20\'19s closest challenger in the Republican primary election, released the delegates she won so that they are free to support him at the convention.\par \par \uc2 Haley herself will not be there. Nor will \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2 , the former vice-president who was a key figure at the past two conventions. Nor will \uc2 Mitt Romney\uc2  and \uc2 Paul Ryan\uc2 , the Republican ticket that took on Democrat \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  in the 2012 election.\par \par \uc2 But delegates will hear from \uc2 Tucker Carlson\uc2 , a broadcaster who promotes white nationalism; \uc2 Franklin Graham\uc2 , a Christian evangelical who has called Islam \u8220\'20\'1Cwicked\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cevil\u8221\'20\'1D; Tom Homan, an immigration hardliner who has vowed to run the biggest deportation force in American history; Charlie Kirk, a far-right activist and election denier; and \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy\uc2 , a biotech entrepreneur who wants to increase fossil fuel production. All are sure to play their part in the Trump show.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.centerforpolitics.org/crystalball/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Larry Sabato}}}\uc2 , director of the Center for Politics at the \uc2 University of Virginia\uc2 , said: \u8220\'20\'1CTrump\u8217\'20\'19s coronation will for once put British ceremony to shame. You will see speaker after speaker, delegation after delegation, trying to top one another in their superlatives about the greatest president, not just in American history but in world history.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Delegates will hear from Trump, 78, and ratify the Republican policy platform that he personally approved. They will be introduced to Trump\u8217\'20\'19s vice-presidential running mate. They will hear speakers mock Biden as a weak, 81-year-old failure who is facing calls from fellow Democrats to exit the race.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2020/sep/06/michael-steele-donald-trump-republican-party-interview"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Michael Steele}}}\uc2 , a former chairman of the \uc2 Republican National Committee\uc2 , said: \u8220\'20\'1CThe Democrats have spent the last 10 days giving them soundbites to talk about. The Republicans are going to take four days and everything coming out of their mouths will be a reminder that \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is old, Democrats don\u8217\'20\'19t want him, why should you?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Republicans have been given a gift, Steele added. \u8220\'20\'1CDemocrats are too stupid to realise what the gift is, and they keep giving it. Just shut the hell up, get behind the man like the Republicans have gotten behind their criminal and run the race. Because the American people are going to line up with \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  if you give them a reason to do that.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Convention delegates, numbering almost 2,400, are sure to approve a policy platform that ranks among the most extreme in American history. Echoing Trump talking points, it backs the mass deportation of undocumented immigrants, calls for an end to \u8220\'20\'1Cthe weaponisation of government\u8221\'20\'1D and demands {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.axios.com/2024/06/02/legal-battle-2024-election-begun-biden-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 election integrity}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 code for Trump\u8217\'20\'19s false assertion that the 2020 election was stolen.\par \par \uc2 The 16-page platform is heavily influenced by Christian nationalism and shares significant ideological DNA with Project 2025, a 922-page plan from a conservative thinktank that outlines {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/election-2024-conservatives-trump-heritage-857eb794e505f1c6710eb03fd5b58981"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a dramatic expansion}}}\uc2  of presidential power and a plan to fire as many as 50,000 government workers to replace them with Trump loyalists.\par \par \uc2 Biden\u8217\'20\'19s re-election campaign has worked to turn Project 2025 into an electoral liability for Trump, which may explain why last week he sought to distance himself from it. \u8220\'20\'1CI know nothing about Project 2025,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump posted on his social media website, adding that \u8220\'20\'1Csome of the things they\u8217\'20\'19re saying are absolutely ridiculous and abysmal\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 But both \uc2 Russ Vought\uc2 , the Republican National Convention\u8217\'20\'19s platform committee\u8217\'20\'19s policy director, and his deputy, Ed Martin, have strong connections to Project 2025. Both men have also previously taken a hard line against \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/kfile-ed-martin-rnc-platform-committee-anti-abortion-exceptions/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Martin has advocated}}}\uc2  for a national ban without exceptions for rape or incest and entertained the idea of imprisoning women and their doctors. He once said: \u8220\'20\'1CIf you ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Louisiana, is a doctor who has an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  breaking the law? Yes. Should he be punished? Yes \u8211\'20\'13 I think that seems obvious. What is the punishment? Not sure yet. Could be criminal, could be a jail sentence, I suppose.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The platform committee is packed with other anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  extremists including \uc2 David Barton\uc2 , a Christian nationalist who has called the separation of church and state a \u8220\'20\'1Cmyth\u8221\'20\'1D, Kimberly Guilfoyle, fiancee of \uc2 Donald Trump Jr\uc2 ; \uc2 Tony Perkins\uc2 , president of the \uc2 Family Research Council\uc2 ; and Chad Connelly, a former chairman of the South Carolina Republican party who has described \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  as \u8220\'20\'1Cmurder of an innocent child\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Weighing the political risks, Trump intervened to ensure that, for the first time in 40 years, the party platform omits the explicit basis for a national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, leaving the policy to state governments instead. But the compromise remains fragile: if dissenting voices are raised at the convention, it will fuel Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 argument that Republicans\u8217\'20\'19 true intentions are as extreme as ever.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/emiliawinterro?lang=en"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Emilia Rowland}}}\uc2 , national press secretary of the \uc2 Democratic National Committee\uc2 , said: \u8220\'20\'1CThe reality is that Trump literally put architects of Project 2025 in charge of the Republican platform, and the result is not only the most extreme platform in GOP history but one containing lie after lie after lie.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe American people know that Trump wants a nationwide \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban and they know the only thing standing in the way of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s terrifying second-term agenda is re-electing President Biden and Vice-President Harris in November.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Delegates will also formally designate the presidential ticket: Trump and his yet-to-be-named running mate. The leading contender is Vance, followed by the North Dakota governor, \uc2 Doug Burgum\uc2 , and Florida senator \uc2 Marco Rubio\uc2 . All three are expected to address delegates along with the Florida governor, \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , who challenged Trump for the nomination and later endorsed him.\par \par \uc2 To critics, the vice-presidential pick is irrelevant. Steele, a broadcaster and former lieutenant governor of Maryland, said: \u8220\'20\'1CTo be honest, I couldn\u8217\'20\'19t care less who his running mate is. It is a mindless zombified politician who has given up his soul to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  for the chance that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  will smile at him and pat him on the head.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt doesn\u8217\'20\'19t matter to me. It will be an unprincipled individual. That\u8217\'20\'19s all I know. They could take a stick figure and stand it next to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . Folks in that hall would applaud it, lap it up, nominate it and call it vice-president.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Trump family members will also address the convention, organisers announced on Saturday. The former president\u8217\'20\'19s sons, \uc2 Donald Trump Jr\uc2  and \uc2 Eric Trump\uc2 , will both have speaking slots, along with their partners Kimberly Guilfoyle and \uc2 Lara Trump\uc2 . The former first lady Melania Trump is expected in Milwaukee but she is not listed among the speakers. She has been notably absent from the 2024 campaign \u8211\'20\'13 a stark contrast to the first lady Jill Biden\u8217\'20\'19s prominent role at her husband\u8217\'20\'19s side.\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s campaign has outlined daily messaging with themes that riff on his signature \u8220\'20\'1CMake America great again\u8221\'20\'1D slogan. Monday\u8217\'20\'19s theme is economics: \u8220\'20\'1CMake America wealthy once again.\u8221\'20\'1D Trump has outlined an agenda of sweeping tariffs and accelerated production of oil and gas, even though it already hit a record under Biden.\par \par \uc2 On Tuesday the theme is immigration and crime: \u8220\'20\'1CMake America safe once again.\u8221\'20\'1D Trump and Republicans believe the border debate is among their strongest issues. They have arranged speeches for the family members of people killed, allegedly by undocumented immigrants, as part of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s broader attempts to blame crime on border policies.\par \par \uc2 Wednesday will be national security day: \u8220\'20\'1CMake America strong once again.\u8221\'20\'1D Delegates and the viewing audience can expect to hear arguments that Biden is a \u8220\'20\'1Cweak\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cfailed\u8221\'20\'1D commander-in-chief and head of state. This is the day, typically, that the vice-presidential nominee addresses the convention.\par \par \uc2 Thursday will culminate with Trump himself: \u8220\'20\'1CMake America great once again.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 His speech accepting the party nomination will be watched closely for the tension between red meat for the base and outreach to swing state votes. His 2016 address included the memorable line \u8220\'20\'1CI alone can fix it\u8221\'20\'1D and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2016/jul/22/donald-trump-speech-republican-national-convention"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 drew comparisons}}}\uc2  with the trappings of fascist rallies.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jan/27/frank-luntz-interview-pollster-us-uk-politics"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Frank Luntz}}}\uc2 , a political consultant and pollster, said: \u8220\'20\'1C The question is whether he goes 80% Maga, 90% Maga or 100% Maga. They would be best off with low-fat milk rather than the 2%, because 2% just goes overboard. He has four days of unchallenged, uninterrupted messaging, and there\u8217\'20\'19s usually a bounce.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHe\u8217\'20\'19s going into his convention so strong and with curiosity over who his VP candidate is going to be. If they have discipline and they can exercise it then their their lead will grow. But there\u8217\'20\'19s only so many votes available among the undecideds.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Protesters are expected but will not be permitted inside the security zone established around the convention arena by the Secret Service. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.principlesfirst.us/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Principles First}}}\uc2 , which describes itself as a nationwide grassroots movement of pro-democracy, anti-Trump conservatives, is holding a rally on Wednesday with Steele among the speakers.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Democratic National Committee\uc2  is also holding events in Milwaukee, promising daily press conferences, counter-programming and voter engagement in the Democratic stronghold. But the Republican mood inside the arena is likely to be triumphant, lavishing praise on Trump as a great survivor while hammering Democrats over their uncertainty about Biden.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.fordham.edu/info/24277/ma_in_elections_and_campaign_management_faculty/6866/monika_l_mcdermott"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Monika McDermott}}}\uc2 , a political science professor, at \uc2 Fordham University\uc2  in New York, said: \u8220\'20\'1CThat\u8217\'20\'19s a winning point for the Republicans after the debate and they\u8217\'20\'19re going to continue to run with it. The Democratic party has been showing such cracks in their support behind President Biden at this point that it would be smart to stick a crowbar in there to make those cracks larger.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240717ek7e002ij\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
