\par\par \uc2 Opinion\par \b \uc2 Don\u8217\'20\'19t believe it \u8211\'20\'13 the Republicans aren\u8217\'20\'19t \u8216\'20\'18softening\u8217\'20\'19 their stance on  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 Judith Levine \par \uc2 1,011 \uc2 words\par \uc2 13 July 2024\par 13:52 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 If Trump is re-elected, and a Republican Congress hands him a federal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, does anyone think he\u8217\'20\'19d veto it?\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/2024/07/08/trump-abortion-republican-platform/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 press}}}\uc2  has pointed to the near erasure of the word \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the new Republican platform as evidence that the mind and soul of the Republican party now reside in the body of Donald J Trump. The document omits the right\u8217\'20\'19s top-priority goal of a federal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban and replaces it with Trump\u8217\'20\'19s preference to let the states do the dirty work. Missing too is the holy grail of the antiabortion movement: a \u8220\'20\'1Chuman life amendment,\u8221\'20\'1D which would extend to fetuses and embryos the constitutional protections that were seized from pregnant people when the supreme court overturned Roe v Wade in June 2022.\par \par \uc2 The consensus is that the changes from the 2016 platform, which was used in the 2020 elections, to the 2024 version subordinate the Republican party\u8217\'20\'19s long-held principles and strategies \u8211\'20\'13 not just on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  but also on trade, entitlement cuts, and same-sex marriage \u8211\'20\'13 to the transient political needs and desires of its leader.\par \par \uc2 On \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , news outlets from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2024/07/08/politics/republican-platform-trump-abortion/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 CNN}}}\uc2  to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.foxnews.com/politics/softened-abortion-language-trump-approved-gop-platform-irks-some-social-conservatives"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Fox}}}\uc2  to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://rollcall.com/2024/07/08/rnc-softens-platform-stance-on-abortion/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Roll Call}}}\uc2  have called the shift a \u8220\'20\'1Csoftening\u8221\'20\'1D of the party\u8217\'20\'19s stance.\par \par \uc2 Don\u8217\'20\'19t be fooled. Apart from the fact that voters don\u8217\'20\'19t read platforms and elected officials rarely abide by them, the \u8220\'20\'1Cnew\u8221\'20\'1D \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  position will make no practical or political difference.\par \par \uc2 First \u8211\'20\'13 if this doesn\u8217\'20\'19t go entirely without saying \u8211\'20\'13 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s word is as good as the paper he flushes down his golden toilet. If a Republican Congress handed a President Trump a federal ban, does anyone think he\u8217\'20\'19d veto it? Trump doesn\u8217\'20\'19t really care about \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  anyhow. His stated opinions have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/donald-trump/trumps-many-abortion-positions-timeline-rcna146601"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 swung every which way}}}\uc2 , from \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m very pro-choice\u8221\'20\'1D in 1999 to \u8220\'20\'1CGod made the decision\u8221\'20\'1D to overturn Roe in 2022, not a \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  packed with the far-right justices he appointed.\par \par \uc2 Second, the court is already taking care of things. Yes, it rejected a challenge to the \uc2 Food and Drug Administration\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s approval of the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  drug mifepristone \u8211\'20\'13 but did so only on the grounds that the plaintiffs, an ad hoc group of antiabortion medical professionals, did not have standing to sue. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://publichealth.jhu.edu/2024/scotus-mifepristone-and-emtala-decisions-explained"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Public health}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.lawdork.com/p/mifepristone-challenge-fails-scotus"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 legal}}}\uc2  experts say that the ruling almost guarantees another challenge, this time with more carefully vetted plaintiffs. And state laws banning mifepristone are untouched.\par \par \uc2 The supreme court also left in place two \uc2 FDA\uc2  regulations loosening the prescription and use of mifepristone, but only while the regulations are under appeal. And if the appeal reaches the high court? This session, the majority {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/supreme-court/supreme-court-delivers-blow-power-federal-agencies-rcna145344"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 declared}}}\uc2  itself the boss of the federal agencies. Should the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  activists challenge the \uc2 FDA\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s authority again, there\u8217\'20\'19s a good chance they will prevail.\par \par \uc2 So far, neither judges no state lawmakers have succeeded in shutting down \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access. In fact, the number of pregnancy terminations {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://19thnews.org/2024/06/two-years-roe-overturn-abortions/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 increased}}}\uc2  in 2023, after Roe\u8217\'20\'19s undoing, thanks to telemedical providers prescribing and a global feminist underground sending pills into \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  deserts. Laws still protect these activities. Statutes in liberal states shield providers from prosecution by authorities in conservative states, and the fourth amendment protects first-class letters and packages from illegal search and seizure.\par \par \uc2 However, federal {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.uspis.gov/wp-content/uploads/2019/05/USPIS-FAQs.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 postal inspectors}}}\uc2  can get a warrant to open the mail if they have probable cause to believe the contents violate federal law. The 1873 Comstock Act prohibits the mailing of anything that can be used to cause an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . It is still on the books. The executive branch holds authority over the \uc2 US Postal Service\uc2 . With the president\u8217\'20\'19s nod, the Postal Service could train its dogs to sniff out the little white pills and direct its enforcers to tear open parcels in search of contraband. US Customs is authorized to check international mail for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cbp.gov/travel/us-citizens/know-before-you-go/prohibited-and-restricted-items"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 prohibited items}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 whether that\u8217\'20\'19s gold, fresh fruit, animal fur, or illegal drugs.\par \par \uc2 The 2024 Republican platform may be no more than a script for political theater. But, there\u8217\'20\'19s another document \u8211\'20\'13 finally discovered by the media \u8211\'20\'13 that shows the party ain\u8217\'20\'19t playing: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.project2025.org/policy/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Project 2025}}}\uc2 , \uc2 the Heritage Foundation\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s plan for transition to an extreme-right America under an imperial presidency. All the positions Trump finessed or \u8220\'20\'1Csoftened\u8221\'20\'1D in the platform are laid out in flagrant detail in the 900-page tome.\par \par \uc2 Trump has disavowed connection with it, while proudly owning the platform. \u8220\'20\'1CI know nothing about Project 2025. I have not seen it, have no idea who is in charge of it, and unlike our very well received Republican platform, had nothing to do with it,\u8221\'20\'1D he {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://newrepublic.com/post/183697/trump-project-2025-meltdown"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 posted}}}\uc2  on Truth Social. But {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2024/07/11/politics/trump-allies-project-2025/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 CNN}}}\uc2  found at least 140 people involved in Project 2025 who served in the Trump administration, including six cabinet members.\par \par \uc2 While peeved that the Republican platform committee flouted their input, antiabortion leaders have dismissed it as a temporary setback. \u8220\'20\'1CThe 2024 platform is a decent statement of campaign priorities,\u8221\'20\'1D said \uc2 Family Research Council\uc2  president \uc2 Tony Perkins\uc2 , \u8220\'20\'1Cbut not necessarily the enduring principles of the party.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Whoever ends up in the White House, the antis will not rest until every baby that can be born is born and anybody who gets in the way is punished \u8211\'20\'13 slandered, delicensed, sued, fined, imprisoned, even executed for homicide, or, hardly least of all, forced to carry and bear a child they do not want.\par \par \uc2 Republican-dominated state legislatures have indicated their eagerness to enact the most stringent limitations and the harshest penalties. And because the supreme court has immunized presidents from criminal prosecution (with the insane proviso that they commit the crime as an official act), a second-term President Trump would be free to follow his instincts and impose his will over the bodies of women. That\u8217\'20\'19s what he has always done. But this time he will be accountable to nobody.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Judith Levine is a Brooklyn journalist and essayist, a contributing writer to the Intercept and the author of five books\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240713ek7d00105\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
