\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Arkansas rejects initiative seeking to ease  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  ban despite over 100,000 supporters\b0\par\par\uc2 Jessica Glenza \par \uc2 563 \uc2 words\par \uc2 11 July 2024\par 14:33 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Secretary of state claims paid canvassers who delivered signatures of support failed to submit sworn statements\par \par \uc2 Arkansas officials rejected a ballot initiative that sought to loosen the state\u8217\'20\'19s strict \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, after canvassers delivered more than 101,000 signatures to state offices.\par \par \uc2 In a letter, the secretary of state, John Thurston, said he would reject the canvassers\u8217\'20\'19 attempt to appear on the November ballot because they failed to submit sworn statements by paid canvassers.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou did not submit any statements meeting this requirement,\u8221\'20\'1D Thurston said {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/lbengilmore/status/1811119926066958457"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in a letter}}}\uc2  on Wednesday. \u8220\'20\'1CBy contrast, other sponsors of initiative petitions complied with this requirement. Therefore, I must reject your submission.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Thurston said that even if he had not rejected the ballot measure for lack of sworn statements by paid canvassers, he would have rejected the signatures they collected.\par \par \uc2 Of the 101,525 signatures submitted, 14,143 were collected by paid canvassers. Excluding them left campaigners 3,322 signatures short of what is required to appear on the fall ballot.\par \par \uc2 Republicans in the state cheered the rejection.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CToday is a great day for life in Arkansas,\u8221\'20\'1D said Ben Gilmore, an Arkansas state senator. \u8220\'20\'1CLife is the most basic God-given human right and Arkansas will continue to protect the lives of our unborn children.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/MatthewrMoore/status/1811214790955602237/photo/1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Arkansans for Limited Government}}}\uc2  (AFLG), reproductive rights canvassers in the state, called the disqualification \u8220\'20\'1Cridiculous\u8221\'20\'1D, said they worked with the secretary\u8217\'20\'19s office at \u8220\'20\'1Cmultiple junctures\u8221\'20\'1D and called the sworn statement requirement an \u8220\'20\'1Cunfounded legal interpretation\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMore than 101,000 Arkansans participated in this heroic act of direct democracy and stood up to proclaim their support for access to healthcare,\u8221\'20\'1D said AFLG. \u8220\'20\'1CThey deserve better than a state government that seeks to silence them.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe will fight this ridiculous disqualification attempt with everything we have. We will not back down.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://arliberty.org/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/Arkansas-Abortion-Amendment-of-202.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ballot measure}}}\uc2  would have asked voters to allow \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  up to 20 weeks\u8217\'20\'19 gestation and later in cases of rape or incest, when a pregnancy causes a life-threatening condition for a woman, or if a fetus is unlikely to survive.\par \par \uc2 Today, Arkansas bans \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  at conception, affecting 668,000 women of reproductive age. Although the state allows abortions in the case of medical emergencies, the state department of health reported zero abortions in 2023, according to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/2024-election/arkansas-abortion-rights-groups-signatures-ballot-measure-constitution-rcna160266"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 NBC News}}}\uc2 .\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/abortion-trump-biden-election-2024-dobbs-498d14f6e2bbfe1f313f006ad089de4e"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Recent polls}}}\uc2  show support for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights has risen since {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jun/24/roe-v-wade-overturned-abortion-summary-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the US supreme court overturned Roe v Wade}}}\uc2 , the 1973 decision that provided a constitutional protection for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights for nearly 50 years.\par \par \uc2 Before the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s decision, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions were a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/dec/05/abortion-opposition-focus-white-evangelical-anger"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 point of strength}}}\uc2  for the Republican party. The issue of restrictions reliably turned out conservative voters, even as the party faced little risk that severe restrictions would go into effect.\par \par \uc2 After \uc2 Donald Trump{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/2020/sep/19/trump-supreme-court-pick-replace-ruth-bader-ginsburg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 successfully shifted}}}\uc2  the balance of the court and Roe v Wade was overturned, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2023/nov/10/state-abortion-laws-us"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 14 states}}}\uc2  enacted near-total \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans. As stories of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/dec/05/texas-woman-emergency-abortion-lawsuit"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 hardships of women}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jun/08/texas-abortion-high-risk-patients"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 families}}}\uc2  have emerged, and Republicans attacked even {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/society/2024/feb/23/fertility-doctors-reaction-alabama-embryo-ruling"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 basic fertility services}}}\uc2 , support for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights has risen nationally and momentum swung {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/may/09/florida-abortion-democrats-voting"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 decidedly to the left}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Still, the ballot measure in Arkansas faced an uphill battle. Polls note that the state is one of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.prri.org/research/abortion-views-in-all-50-states-findings-from-prris-2023-american-values-atlas/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 only five}}}\uc2  nationally where a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2024/07/01/us/politics/arkansas-abortion-ballot-measure.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 minority of voters}}}\uc2  (46%) believe \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  should be legal in all or most cases.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240711ek7b00231\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
