\par\par \uc2 Global\par \b \uc2 The \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  question: even if Biden steps down, could she win?\b0\par\par\uc2 Adam Gabbatt \par \uc2 1,415 \uc2 words\par \uc2 10 July 2024\par 17:47 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Plus, Project 2025, a dispatch from Philadelphia and the candidate who insists he didn\u8217\'20\'19t eat a dog\par \par \uc2 Hello!\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has embarked on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/08/biden-msnbc-interview-open-letter-democrats"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 an apology tour}}}\uc2  in the wake of his debate disaster, but with the Democrats remaining in crisis, much focus has turned to \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , the vice-president, who some are talking about as a potential Biden replacement should he step aside.\par \par \uc2 Harris has been thrust in front of cameras around the country in recent days, offering support to her 81-year-old colleague \u8211\'20\'13 but despite Biden insisting that he {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://abcnews.go.com/Politics/biden-sends-letter-democrats-time-questions-end/story?id=111742809"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 will stay in the race}}}\uc2 , speculation continues about whether Harris could be an alternative.\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19ll have a look at that, but first here\u8217\'20\'19s what else has been going on in the election.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what you need to know\par \par \uc2 1. Biden takes to the airwaves\par \par \uc2 The embattled president has conducted a series of interviews as he seeks to move on from that damaging debate. Biden appeared {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://abc.com/movies-and-specials/8b1296d6-a9bf-49a6-afe1-4d4e400f8e8a"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 on ABC}}}\uc2  for a live interview on Friday, phoned {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.msnbc.com/morning-joe/watch/-i-am-not-going-anywhere-biden-confirms-he-s-staying-in-2024-race-214393925734"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in to MSNBC}}}\uc2  on Monday and spoke to local radio stations over the weekend. He has been blaming his halting debate performance on both a cold and on jetlag (despite being back in Washington for 12 days before the debate), but his media appearances since then have not been flawless, either \u8211\'20\'13 nor did it help that his ABC interviewer subsequently {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.independent.co.uk/news/world/americas/us-politics/biden-george-stephanopoulos-abc-interview-b2577247.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told some guy in the street}}}\uc2  that Biden shouldn\u8217\'20\'19t serve for four more years.\par \par \uc2 2. Republicans soften language on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 For the first time in 40 years, the \uc2 Republican National Committee\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s official platform will {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/09/republican-abortion-ban-policy-platform-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 not propose a national \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  ban}}}\uc2 , in response to Trump wanting his campaign to steer clear of talking about \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . While the platform does not suggest a complete ban on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Republicans have celebrated the fact that 14 states have adopted near-total \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans since the supreme court overturned Roe v Wade in 2022 \u8211\'20\'13 a decision Trump {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/12/donald-trump-abortion-roe-v-wade-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 takes credit for}}}\uc2 . About 63% of Americans say \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  should be legal in all or most cases, and just 36% say it should be illegal in all or most cases, according to the \uc2 Pew Research Center\uc2 , putting the Republican party broadly at odds with public opinion.\par \par \uc2 3. Biden tells Nato: \u8216\'20\'18Russia will not prevail\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 Biden has suggested a key test of his viability for another presidential run should be the Nato summit in Washington, which he hosts this week and opened with a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/article/2024/jul/09/nato-biden-ukraine-air-defenses"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 speech}}}\uc2  on Tuesday. In it, the president pledged new resources to Ukraine and condemned a missile strike against a paediatric cancer hospital as a \u8220\'20\'1Chorrific reminder of Russia\u8217\'20\'19s brutality\u8221\'20\'1D. Biden said \uc2 Nato\uc2  would provide Ukraine with new air defense systems after the Russian attack. \u8220\'20\'1CRussia will not prevail,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said. \u8220\'20\'1CUkraine will prevail.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 As Biden flaps, Harris takes flight\par \par \uc2 As Biden has struggled to lift his campaign in recent days, Kamala {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/KamalaHarris/status/735197253153914881"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 (pronounced \u8220\'20\'1Ccomma-la\u8221\'20\'1D)}}}\uc2  Harris has soared. With questions coming thick and fast about Biden\u8217\'20\'19s ability to do his job, the campaign has dispatched Harris to rallies and fundraising events in Nevada, Louisiana, California and Utah as it seeks to shore up support.\par \par \uc2 Harris, who {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2019/dec/03/kamala-harris-drops-out-democratic-2020-presidential-race-reports#:~:text=Kamala%20Harris%20has%20suspended%20her,the%20wall%2C%20Kamala%20Harris%20surged."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ran against Biden}}}\uc2  for the Democratic nomination four years ago \u8211\'20\'13 she dropped out before the first primary, amid {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnbc.com/2019/12/03/kamala-harris-drops-out-of-2020-presidential-race.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports}}}\uc2  of a chaotically run campaign \u8211\'20\'13 has recently been placed under more scrutiny than ever before, and, in a bit of a surprise, new polling suggests the vice-president might well do better than Biden against Trump.\par \par \uc2 Last week a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.documentcloud.org/documents/24787646/cnn-poll.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 poll}}}\uc2  by SSRS and CNN, conducted after the debate, found Harris trailing Trump by just two points nationally, within the margin of error. (Biden was losing by six points.) In a different survey on Wednesday, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.usnews.com/news/national-news/articles/2024-07-10/poll-other-democrats-outperform-biden-in-matchups-against-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Harris outperformed Biden}}}\uc2  among young voters \u8211\'20\'13 a key bloc for the Democrats. It\u8217\'20\'19s too soon to say whether her upward trend will continue, however, and in a recent Emerson poll Harris was down six points to Trump, while Biden only trailed Trump by three.\par \par \uc2 Among Democrats, for now at least, she appears to be the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://today.yougov.com/politics/articles/49986-who-democrats-would-want-to-replace-biden"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 most popular choice}}}\uc2  to replace Biden. The former California attorney general, elected as a senator in 2017, has had a pretty quiet first term as vice-president. But even before the Biden debate debacle, Harris had begun to be a more visible face of the campaign, particularly reaching out to women and voters of colour.\par \par \uc2 Harris seems happy enough to be stepping into the limelight. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/07/assured-kamala-harris-cuts-a-transformed-figure-in-new-orleans-and-carefully-avoids-any-mention-of-bidens-fitness-for-office"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 At a Harris event in New Orleans}}}\uc2  on Saturday, \u8220\'20\'1Cgone was the \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  of the drab brown, chair-matching suit and the halting, technical commentary about American policy needs\u8221\'20\'1D, wrote Janell Ross for the Guardian.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CInstead, on Saturday, Harris \u8211\'20\'13 dressed in a bright teal suit and tailed by a press contingent which had expanded to more than four times its previous size \u8211\'20\'13 spoke to a standing-room-only crowd in a room equipped to seat more than 500 people.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 There are some problems with her being anointed as the Democratic saviour. Harris has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://projects.fivethirtyeight.com/polls/approval/kamala-harris/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 approval numbers}}}\uc2  nearly as low as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://projects.fivethirtyeight.com/polls/approval/joe-biden/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Biden\u8217\'20\'19s}}}\uc2 . And her rise has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.pbs.org/newshour/politics/republicans-ramp-up-attacks-on-harris-as-talk-of-replacing-biden-on-2024-ticket-intensifies"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 brought greater attention}}}\uc2  from Republicans, including Trump \u8211\'20\'13 who has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://truthsocial.com/@realDonaldTrump/posts/112729384937320696"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 begun to attack}}}\uc2  Harris on his ailing Truth Social website, giving her the less-than-punchy nickname \u8220\'20\'1CLaffin\u8217\'20\'19 \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Trump usually reserves nicknames and attacks (he also branded Harris \u8220\'20\'1Cpathetic\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cso fucking bad\u8221\'20\'1D in comments {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.thedailybeast.com/donald-trump-caught-on-video-claiming-broken-down-joe-biden-has-quit-its-kamala?ref=home?ref=home"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 made from a golf cart}}}\uc2  last week) for people who threaten him, so it could be a sign he sees Harris, who is 19 years younger, as a legitimate threat.\par \par \uc2 But of course, Harris\u8217\'20\'19s future rests on whether Biden does decide to step aside \u8211\'20\'13 and in his ABC interview, Biden {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=_WjPVK8u5Tk"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  that \u8220\'20\'1Cif the Lord almighty comes down\u8221\'20\'1D and tells him to pull out of the race, \u8220\'20\'1CI might do that.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/10/blitz-primary-biden-successor-younger-candidates"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Some in the Democratic party are now musing}}}\uc2  that rather than a) Biden staying in or b) Biden stepping down and anointing Harris, the party should instead go for a third option: a \u8220\'20\'1Cblitz primary\u8221\'20\'1D, in which a small group of prominent Democrats run against each other and a new candidate is chosen. But if Democrats do decide to sidestep their {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jan/20/kamala-harris-sworn-in-vice-president"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 history-making}}}\uc2  vice-president \u8211\'20\'13 the first woman, as well as the first woman of African American and south Asian descent, to serve as vice-president \u8211\'20\'13 that might not look particularly great either.\par \par \uc2 Worst week: the American voter\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 . And \uc2 Robert F Kennedy Jr\uc2  has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/02/robert-f-kennedy-jr-sexual-assault-allegation-response"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 brushed off sexual assault allegations}}}\uc2  by saying: \u8220\'20\'1CI am who I am.\u8221\'20\'1D It leaves the American public with distinctly underwhelming choices in November: a convicted felon, a visibly diminished incumbent and a fantasist who has spent the past week {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://nymag.com/intelligencer/article/rfk-jr-dog-videos.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 denying that he once ate a dog}}}\uc2 . USA! USA!\par \par \uc2 Out and about: Philadelphia\par \par \uc2 Times are certainly tough for the president right now. But in the Mount Airy Church of God in Christ on Sunday morning, you could be forgiven for not noticing. Biden was greeted by rapturous applause, and departed to chants of \u8220\'20\'1Cfour more years\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Outside church, a handful of signs highlighted the division stretching the Democratic coalition. \u8220\'20\'1CThank U Joe but time to go,\u8221\'20\'1D read one. Another urged Biden to \u8220\'20\'1Cpass the torch\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 But inside, before an overwhelmingly supportive audience, he did not touch on the growing calls for him to stand aside. In a brief seven-minute address, Biden focused on hope, the need for unity and his administration\u8217\'20\'19s achievements for Black Americans.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19ve been doing this a long time,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/07/biden-campaign-philadelphia-church-support"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 he acknowledged}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CAnd I\u8217\'20\'19ve honest to God never felt more optimistic about America\u8217\'20\'19s future.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Read more {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/07/biden-campaign-philadelphia-church-support"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8211\'20\'13 Callum Jones, deputy business editor\par \par \uc2 Lie of the week \u8211\'20\'13 Trump claims he \u8216\'20\'18has no idea\u8217\'20\'19 who is behind Project 2025\par \par \uc2 Trump has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/09/project-2025-trump-connections-similarities"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 attempted to distance himself}}}\uc2  from Project 2025, a plan from \uc2 the Heritage Foundation\uc2  for the next conservative presidency \u8211\'20\'13 including stacking the government with political lackeys, attacking LGBTQ+ rights and diversity efforts, and starting mass deportations.\par \par \uc2 Despite Trump\u8217\'20\'19s claims otherwise, the policies aren\u8217\'20\'19t too far off from what he has proposed for a second term, in his own platform, Agenda 47.\par \par \uc2 And he knows the people behind Project 2025: the authors of the project are stacked with Trumpworld figures. No fewer than 31 of the 38 people who helped write or edit it served in Trump\u8217\'20\'19s administration or transition team, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://popular.info/p/what-trump-doesnt-want-you-to-know?utm_source=post-email-title&publication_id=1664&post_id=146375738&utm_campaign=email-post-title&isFreemail=false&r=5g4f&triedRedirect=true&utm_medium=email"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 noted}}}\uc2  journalist Judd Legum.\par \par \uc2 \u8211\'20\'13 Rachel Leingang, misinformation reporter\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240710ek7a002s3\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
