\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Republicans omit national  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  ban from platform for first time in 40 years\b0\par\par\uc2 Jessica Glenza \par \uc2 890 \uc2 words\par \uc2 9 July 2024\par 16:42 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par 31\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Party instead opts to focus on power of states to regulate \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in move that reflects Trump\u8217\'20\'19s position\par \par \uc2 The Republican party has omitted a national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban from its official party platform for the first time in 40 years, opting instead to focus on the power of states to regulate \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in a move that reflects {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s preferred position.\par \par \uc2 Fourteen states have adopted {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2023/nov/10/state-abortion-laws-us"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 near-total \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  bans}}}\uc2  since the supreme court overturned Roe v Wade in 2022, ending the federal constitutional right to obtain an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The party\u8217\'20\'19s new policy platform is the first {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://prod-cdn-static.gop.com/media/documents/DRAFT_12_FINAL%5B1%5D-ben_1468872234.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 since Trump won the White House in 2016}}}\uc2 , and is significantly slimmer, down from 66 pages {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.npr.org/2024/07/08/nx-s1-5033015/rnc-republican-party-platform-2024"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 to 16}}}\uc2 . In the 2020 race, which Trump went on to lose to \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  , the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.vox.com/2020/8/24/21399396/republican-convention-platform-2020-2016"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 party }}}\uc2  did not adopt a new platform.\par \par \uc2 The document \u8211\'20\'13 approved within a few hours on Monday in Milwaukee, Wisconsin, where the party will hold its convention next week \u8211\'20\'13 includes many slogans that will be familiar to Trump supporters. On oil production, for instance, it says the president will \u8220\'20\'1Cdrill baby drill\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The 20-point plan, written in all-capital letters, lays out an agenda that includes a pledge to \u8220\'20\'1Cseal the border and stop the migrant invasion\u8221\'20\'1D, as well as continue building a border wall that Trump promised during his presidency but largely failed to deliver. It also promises to \u8220\'20\'1Cend inflation and make America great again\u8221\'20\'1D, to enact tax cuts for workers with \u8220\'20\'1Cno tax on tips\u8221\'20\'1D and to make college campuses \u8220\'20\'1Csafe\u8221\'20\'1D by deporting so-called \u8220\'20\'1Cpro-\uc2 Hamas\uc2  radicals\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The platform repeatedly criticizes policies to empower transgender individuals, specifically their involvement in sports. It also promises to repeal emissions regulations on gas vehicles and to build an \u8220\'20\'1CIron Dome\u8221\'20\'1D, a reference to Israel\u8217\'20\'19s anti-missile defense system. It pledges to ensure \u8220\'20\'1Celection integrity\u8221\'20\'1D with new voting restrictions, end \u8220\'20\'1Cgender insanity\u8221\'20\'1D and support for trans inclusion policies, \u8220\'20\'1Cstop woke\u8221\'20\'1D government and \u8220\'20\'1Cprotect free speech\u8221\'20\'1D online. Notably, Republicans also said they would \u8220\'20\'1Cwelcome\u8221\'20\'1D greater political participation from US territories, such as Puerto Rico and Guam.\par \par \uc2 On \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the policy document starts by saying that the president would support the 14th amendment, which generally provides the right to due process.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe believe that the 14th amendment to the constitution of the United States guarantees that no person can be denied Life or \uc2 Liberty\uc2  without Due Process, and that the States are, therefore, free to pass Laws protecting those Rights,\u8221\'20\'1D it says.\par \par \uc2 Anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  activists have long argued the amendment should be {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.heritage.org/life/report/can-the-fourteenth-amendment-be-used-protect-human-life-birth"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 interpreted by courts}}}\uc2  to include fetuses in utero, thereby guaranteeing \u8220\'20\'1Cpersonhood\u8221\'20\'1D rights. Such an interpretation would probably make many aspects of in vitro fertilization (IVF) illegal, similar to how Alabama\u8217\'20\'19s supreme court {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/society/2024/feb/23/fertility-doctors-reaction-alabama-embryo-ruling"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 threw IVF into turmoil}}}\uc2  this spring.\par \par \uc2 The document continues: \u8220\'20\'1CAfter 51 years, because of us, that power [to regulate \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ] has been given to the States and to a vote of the People.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 It adds that Republicans would oppose \u8220\'20\'1Clate term \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 a non-medical term used in the political sphere to generally mean \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  past 20 weeks\u8217\'20\'19 gestation \u8211\'20\'13 and that the party would support \u8220\'20\'1Cmothers and policies that advance prenatal care, access to birth control, and IVF\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The aspirations of those who helped craft the president\u8217\'20\'19s platform on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  are significantly more radical than what the policy document lays out.\par \par \uc2 Kristi Hamrick, a representative of Students for Life who told Catholic News Agency (CNA ) she has been working with the Trump campaign, said activists are already considering how a prospective second Trump administration could advance these goals.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf we de-tangled and cut out the cancer of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -related programming from our federal budgets, we can have a healthier budget and a life-affirming budget,\u8221\'20\'1D Hamrick told CNA . That work would, in Hamrick\u8217\'20\'19s words, constitute \u8220\'20\'1Ca very vibrant and vigorous term\u8221\'20\'1D, for anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  activists.\par \par \uc2 In communications to the broader public, anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  activists have generally leaned toward more {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jul/13/anti-abortion-language-restrictions-bans-roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ambiguous language}}}\uc2  about their goals. Popular support for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights has risen since the supreme court overturned Roe v Wade.\par \par \uc2 A national poll released this week by the Associated Press-Norc Center for Public Affairs Research finds a solid majority of Americans oppose a national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, and a rising number support the procedure for any reason.\par \par \uc2 Democrats responded to the new Republican platform by pointing out that the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.rollingstone.com/politics/politics-features/donald-trump-project-2025-1235053996/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 architects of the 20-point plan}}}\uc2  were also connected to the controversial {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/09/project-2025-trump-connections-similarities#:~:text=As%20the%20Guardian%20has%20reported,would%20erode%20checks%20and%20balances."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Project 2025}}}\uc2 , a plan Trump has publicly disavowed but shares a joint vision with the president\u8217\'20\'19s statements.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTrump is so desperate to distance himself from Project 2025 as the American people are grappling with the terrifying truth about his second-term agenda that he and his team overhauled the Republican platform process to keep the public and the press in the dark, all caps-ed 20 bullet points behind closed doors, and blasted it out to divert attention from his real plans,\u8221\'20\'1D said the \uc2 Democratic National Committee\uc2  press secretary, Emilia Rowland.\par \par \uc2 Rowland continued: \u8220\'20\'1CThe American people know that Trump wants a nationwide \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban and they know the only thing standing in the way of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s terrifying second term agenda is re-electing President Biden and Vice-President [Kamala] Harris in November.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240709ek7900232\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
