\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 US politics: debate to cap day of major supreme court decisions \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 L\u233\'00\'E9onie Chao-Fong (now) and Maya Yang (earlier) \par \uc2 7,473 \uc2 words\par \uc2 3 July 2024\par 14:39 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 This live blog is now closed. You can follow live coverage of the first presidential debate here.What to know about the Biden-Trump debateTen defining presidential debate momentsDebate could open up the race for the White HouseAn election rarity: two ex-presidents in a contest\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.14am BST\par \par \uc2 Closing summary\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jun/27/presidential-debate-trump-biden-updates"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19ve launched a separate live blog}}}\uc2  to cover tonight\u8217\'20\'19s presidential debate. In the meantime, here\u8217\'20\'19s a recap of today\u8217\'20\'19s developments:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The supreme court issued three major decisions on cases involving OxyContin maker \uc2 Purdue Pharma\uc2 , an air pollution rule by the \uc2 Environmental Protection Agency\uc2  and \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access in Idaho.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The court {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/jun/27/us-supreme-court-purdue-pharma-opioids"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 rejected}}}\uc2 Purdue Pharma \u8217\'20\'19s bankruptcy settlement plan that included an extraordinary measure to protect its Sackler family owners from further liability over the American opioid epidemic, in exchange for providing funds for compensation and rehabilitation treatment.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The court {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/jun/27/supreme-court-allows-emergency-abortions-idaho"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 cleared}}}\uc2  the way for Idaho hospitals to provide emergency abortions, for now, in a procedural order that left key questions unanswered and potentially delayed a final decision to beyond the November elections.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The court also {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/jun/27/supreme-court-epa-pollution-ruling"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 decided}}}\uc2  to put a hold on an attempt by the \uc2 Environmental Protection Agency\uc2  (\uc2 EPA\uc2 ) to reduce harmful air pollution that drifts across state lines.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The US district judge Aileen Cannon, who is overseeing \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s prosecution for retaining classified documents, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jun/27/trump-classified-documents-case"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ruled}}}\uc2  that she would schedule a hearing to weigh excluding key evidence that forms the backbone of the obstruction-of-justice part of the case against the former president.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  arrived in Atlanta ahead of tonight\u8217\'20\'19s debate. Jill Biden, the first lady, will watch the debate from a separate hold room. It is not clear if Melania Trump, the former first lady, is in Atlanta tonight.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.33am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.55pm BST\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19ve come a long way from Milwaukee where, for the first {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/24/a-republican-debate-that-offered-no-alternative-to-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republican presidential primary debate}}}\uc2  ( sans \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 ), the media were housed in a parking garage with outside porta-potties.\par \par \uc2 For Joe Biden v Trump, reporters are perched high in \uc2 Georgia Tech\uc2  university\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://ramblinwreck.com/sports/w-baskbl/facilities/mccamish-pavilion/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 McCamish Pavilion}}}\uc2 , an Atlanta sports arena on a site that used to be known as the \u8220\'20\'1CThrillerdome\u8221\'20\'1D. There are plenty of bathrooms and two concessions available: one is selling hot dogs and giant pretzels; the other is that Republican favourite \uc2 Chick-fil-A\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The arena is festooned with CNN logos. Every available video screen says \u8220\'20\'1CCNN presidential debate\u8221\'20\'1D. Down below, on what would normally be a basketball court, there is a bright red carpet, more CNN branding and a CNN set where guests are being interviewed. After the debate this will become the melee that is known as the \u8220\'20\'1Cspin room\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 As grand as the setting is, the one thing reporters don\u8217\'20\'19t see at presidential debates is the candidates themselves. Biden and Trump will be inside a nearby studio without an audience. Reporters will be watching on TV like everyone else.\par \par \uc2 On my way here I observed numerous surrounding roads have been closed to traffic to create a security bubble. On grass embankments, I saw numerous signs for Biden and \uc2 Robert F Kennedy Jr\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 leaving Trump trailing in a poor third.\par \par \uc2 enltrAt McCamish Pavilion in Atlanta, where Biden and Kennedy signs appear to outnumber Trump\u8217\'20\'19s: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/jsgN13Bi4x"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/jsgN13Bi4x}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 David Smith\uc2  (@SmithInAmerica) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SmithInAmerica/status/1806449002709414003?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 27, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.52pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden 'confident' and 'ready to go', Jill Biden says\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is \u8220\'20\'1Cready to go\u8221\'20\'1D and feeling \u8220\'20\'1Cconfident\u8221\'20\'1D ahead of tonight\u8217\'20\'19s debate, according to his wife, Jill Biden.\par \par \uc2 The first lady arrived at Dobbins Air Reserve Base in Marietta, Georgia, where she was greeted by Democratic officials including Atlanta mayor \uc2 Andre Dickens\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 She then made a brief stop at a Biden-Harris fundraising retreat in downtown Atlanta, where she told a group of supporters:\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19re almost there. I know Joe\u8217\'20\'19s ready to go. He\u8217\'20\'19s prepared; he\u8217\'20\'19s confident. You\u8217\'20\'19ve all seen him today. You know what a great debater he is.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.00am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.41pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  posted photos of him meeting with \u8220\'20\'1Cincredible\u8221\'20\'1D supporters in Atlanta ahead of tonight\u8217\'20\'19s debate. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s good to be back,\u8221\'20\'1D he wrote.\par \par \uc2 enltrAtlanta, it\u8217\'20\'19s good to be back!\par \par \uc2 I met some incredible supporters who are fired up ahead of tonight\u8217\'20\'19s debate. Let\u8217\'20\'19s finish the job. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/hGDGtuvnC8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/hGDGtuvnC8}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  (@JoeBiden) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JoeBiden/status/1806452539069538723?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 27, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.29pm BST\par \par \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2 , the governor of California and a lead Biden surrogate, stopped to talk to reporters at the McCamish Pavilion, a sports arena in Atlanta that has been turned into a media centre and post-debate spin room.\par \par \uc2 I asked Newsom what difference muted microphones and lack of studio audience might make.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI have a little bias because I did {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/dec/01/pugilistic-us-presidential-undercard-provides-snapshot-of-a-nation-divided-ron-desantis-gavin-newsome"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a debate here in Georgia}}}\uc2  without an audience and it\u8217\'20\'19s just better for the American people because now you\u8217\'20\'19re not playing to the audience, you\u8217\'20\'19re not just playing to a crowd in the room,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 You\u8217\'20\'19ve got to create a framework of engagement that speaks to a much larger audience so that\u8217\'20\'19s a very healthy thing. It\u8217\'20\'19s a very good thing for the Biden campaign. We\u8217\'20\'19ll see how it plays out and same thing with the mic and talking over each other, which is part and parcel of Trump the bully, so that\u8217\'20\'19s a helpful and healthy thing too.\par \par \uc2 From my perspective, in many ways Biden\u8217\'20\'19s already won this debate. First of all, it\u8217\'20\'19s on his calendar, it\u8217\'20\'19s on his timeline, he asserted himself and Trump blinked in every single category as it relates to this effort. I\u8217\'20\'19ve been really impressed and inspired by the Biden strategy so far.\par \par \uc2 I wondered if Biden might miss the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/mar/08/joe-biden-came-out-swinging-at-his-state-of-the-union-address-will-it-be-enough"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 energy of the audience}}}\uc2  that fired him up at the State of the Union address. But Newsom insisted:\par \par \uc2 Biden\u8217\'20\'19s a good debater. He\u8217\'20\'19s done a lot of these debates over many, many decades so one should not underestimate them. It was indicative of the Trump campaign completely flipping the last 72 hours, realising that they\u8217\'20\'19ve set such a low bar of expectation that if he even shows up at the podium that he\u8217\'20\'19s somehow confident he\u8217\'20\'19s going to win this campaign.\par \par \uc2 So they start to panic a little bit in that respect, hedge bets, which is indicative of a little broader consciousness that Biden is very effective in these formats. I honestly have tremendous confidence in the outcome tonight - the message, obviously, the record and, more importantly, the vision. I hope we get to that.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.10pm BST\par \par \uc2 What you need to know about tonight's debate\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  will hold the first of two scheduled US presidential debates on Thursday, a high-stakes rematch between two well-defined political foes.\par \par \uc2 The earlier-than-usual confrontation will give both men a chance to make their case for a second-term to what could be one of the largest television \u8211\'20\'13 and internet \u8211\'20\'13 audiences of the election cycle.\par \par \uc2 Thursday\u8217\'20\'19s show down also carries the risk that Americans already dissatisfied with their options will come away even more dismayed. Polls show an extremely {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2024/06/25/upshot/introducing-2024-poll-tracker.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 tight race}}}\uc2  between the 81-year-old incumbent and the 78-year-old former US president \u8211\'20\'13 and both candidates remain broadly unpopular.\par \par \uc2 The 90-minute debate is scheduled to kick off at 9pm ET inside a CNN studio in Atlanta.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jun/27/biden-trump-debate-what-to-know"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what to know and what to watch.}}}\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jun/27/biden-trump-debate-what-to-know"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Joe Biden v Donald Trump: what you need to know about the first 2024 presidential debate}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.58pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  was pictured stepping off his plane after it touched down at Hartsfield-Jackson international airport in Atlanta.\par \par \uc2 Also seen exiting Trump\u8217\'20\'19s private plane were his campaign advisers \uc2 Steven Cheung\uc2  , \uc2 Jason Miller\uc2 , Susie Wiles and Chris LaCivita , as well as his former campaign adviser \uc2 Corey Lewandowski\uc2  and the Florida congressman \uc2 Matt Gaetz\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.08pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.46pm BST\par \par \uc2 It could be the moment when a rematch that few seem to want finally comes to life: like two ageing prizefighters, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  will enter the arena of political bloodsport on Thursday evening to resume a verbal sparring bout that will revive memories of the ugly exchanges when the two debated face to face four years ago.\par \par \uc2 A CNN studio in Atlanta will host the first presidential debate of the campaign between the same two candidates who contested the last election, which Biden won.\par \par \uc2 With more than four months to go until polling day in November, it is the earliest in any US presidential campaign that a debate between the two main candidates has ever been staged.\par \par \uc2 While some see the timing as premature, it could provide a chance to open up a contest that has become overshadowed by, among other things, Trump\u8217\'20\'19s recent felony conviction, as well as assorted other legal travails that see him facing 54 criminal charges for trying to overturn the last election and for retaining classified documents.\par \par \uc2 Both candidates are deeply unpopular: Trump because his opponents see him as an aspiring dictator who threatens democracy, Biden because, at 81 (although just three years older than his Republican opponent), he is viewed \u8211\'20\'13 even among many Democrats \u8211\'20\'13 as too old for another term as president.\par \par \uc2 Knife-edge polls indicate a race essentially tied, with a national polling average for May and June showing {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2024/us/elections/polls-president.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the candidates at 46% each}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Polls in seven key battleground states \u8211\'20\'13 Wisconsin, Michigan, Pennsylvania, Nevada, Arizona, Georgia and North Carolina \u8211\'20\'13 give Trump a narrow advantage, though usually within the margin of error.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 NBC News\u8217\'20\'19 Sahil Kapur writes that the debate hall is right next to the Kappa Sigma fraternity house at \uc2 Georgia Tech\uc2 , which is currently hosting a party under a sign that reads \u8220\'20\'1CMake America DRUNK Again\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 enltrATLANTA \u8212\'20\'14 The Biden-Trump debate hall is next to a frat house, where they are currently partying under a sign that reads \u8220\'20\'1CMake America DRUNK Again.\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/MADA?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #MADA}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/DebateNight?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #DebateNight}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/noTNPTo3Rr"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/noTNPTo3Rr}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Sahil Kapur (@sahilkapur) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/sahilkapur/status/1806431104045289678?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 27, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.29pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump lands in Atlanta\par \par \uc2 A private plane carrying \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has touched down in Atlanta ahead of tonight\u8217\'20\'19s debate.\par \par \uc2 The former president\u8217\'20\'19s plane was greeted by a group of his supporters on the tarmac.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 It is not clear if Melania Trump, the former first lady, will join her husband at tonight\u8217\'20\'19s debate.\par \par \uc2 Melania Trump\u8217\'20\'19s office did not return a request for comment about whether she would be in Atlanta during the presidential debate, according the \uc2 New York Times\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The former first lady has largely been absent from the campaign trail this year, and she notably did not attend Trump\u8217\'20\'19s criminal hush money trial in New York.\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump Jr\uc2 , Trump\u8217\'20\'19s eldest child, will not attend the debate due to a family commitment involving his oldest daughter, according to NBC News, citing a source.\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s second son, \uc2 Eric Trump\uc2 , is not expected to be in Atlanta for the debate, but Eric\u8217\'20\'19s wife, \uc2 Lara Trump\uc2 , will attend in her official capacity as \uc2 Republican National Committee\uc2  (\uc2 RNC\uc2 ) chair, NBC reports.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.09pm BST\par \par \uc2 Jill Biden, the first lady, will be in Atlanta for tonight\u8217\'20\'19s debate, according to the Biden campaign.\par \par \uc2 Jill Biden is expected to be the only Biden family member in attendance, according to the \uc2 New York Times\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 She is expected to watch the debate from a separate hold room on the debate campus.\par \par \uc2 After the debate, Biden and his wife are scheduled to stop by a nearby Democratic watch party, before flying to Raleigh overnight.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.04pm BST\par \par \uc2 'He must be stopped': Trump's niece to join Biden campaign in debate spin room\par \par \uc2 Candidates traditionally bring along their family members for support during a debate. Less common: bringing a member of your opponent\u8217\'20\'19s family for support.\par \par \uc2 On Thursday night, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s niece, Mary Trump, will be in the post-debate spin room making the case for \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Mary Trump, one of the former president\u8217\'20\'19s harshest critics, has warned that her uncle is a threat to democracy and should not be re-elected.\par \par \uc2 She did not hold back. In a statement, she said:\par \par \uc2 I\u8217\'20\'19m in Atlanta tonight to remind everyone who Donald is as a person and how he would rule as a president because the stakes are far too high for us to get this wrong: We cannot afford to allow \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  anywhere near the levers of power again.\par \par \uc2 Donald cannot be trusted and we must recognize that his last administration was simply a warm-up for much worse to come just as January 6th was a dress rehearsal for a man who will stop at nothing to ascend, once again, to this country\u8217\'20\'19s highest office. He is desperate for power and has shown himself both unworthy of wielding it and obsessed with regaining it purely for his own benefit. He must be stopped.\par \par \uc2 Joining Mary Trump in the spin-room \u8211\'20\'13 a chaotic room where campaign staff and surrogates try to persuade reporters that their candidate won the debate \u8211\'20\'13 will be:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Keisha Lance-Bottoms\uc2 , former Atlanta mayor and a senior advisor on the Biden-Harris campaign\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Texas congresswoman Jasmine Crockett\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 California governor \uc2 Gavin Newsom\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 California congressman Robert Garcia\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Former Louisiana congressman \uc2 Cedric Richmond\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Georgia senator Raphael Warnock\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.51pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  will debate on Thursday for the first time this election cycle and it holds the potential for some history-making moments.\par \par \uc2 Debates can inform voters on both the issues and temperaments of the candidates, potentially swaying an undecided voter toward one candidate\u8217\'20\'19s direction. They can also make for good TV, creating soundbites that resonate for decades to come.\par \par \uc2 From the candidates\u8217\'20\'19 physical appearances to gaffes to planned attacks to off-the-cuff retorts, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jun/27/famous-us-presidential-debate-moments"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here are some memorable moments from US presidential debate history.}}}\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jun/27/famous-us-presidential-debate-moments"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Make or break: the defining moments of US presidential debates}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.01pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.43pm BST\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 White House Correspondents\u8217\'20\'19 Association (WHCA)\uc2  has released a statement complaining that CNN rejected its request to include a pool reporter inside the studio during tonight\u8217\'20\'19s presidential debate.\par \par \uc2 The WHCA \u8220\'20\'1Cis deeply concerned that CNN has rejected our repeated requests to include the White House travel pool inside the studio\u8221\'20\'1D, a statement by WHCA president and NBC correspondent Kelly O\u8217\'20\'19Donnell reads.\par \par \uc2 The debate, which is being held on a closed set, will not feature an audience. Print pool photographers will be present for the entirety of the debate, while one print pool reporter will be permitted to enter during commercial breaks, according to CNN.\par \par \uc2 The letter says:\par \par \uc2 That is not sufficient in our view and diminishes a core principle of presidential coverage. The White House pool has a duty to document, report and witness the president\u8217\'20\'19s events and his movements on behalf of the American people.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.26pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is on his way to Atlanta, where he is scheduled to land in about an hour.\par \par \uc2 Trump aide Margo Martin, in a post to X, shared a video of the former president boarding his plane.\par \par \uc2 enltrPresident {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/realDonaldTrump?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @realDonaldTrump}}}\uc2  departs for DEBATE NIGHT! ???? {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/8aE35SizPI"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/8aE35SizPI}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Margo Martin (@margommartin) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/margommartin/status/1806412298937938128?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 27, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.21pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden arrives in Atlanta ahead of debate\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has arrived in Atlanta ahead of tonight\u8217\'20\'19s presidential debate, where he was greeted by a crowd of supporters who chanted \u8220\'20\'1Cfour more years\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Clet\u8217\'20\'19s go Joe\u8221\'20\'1D, according to a pool report.\par \par \uc2 While on Air Force One en route to Georgia, \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2 , the White House\u8217\'20\'19s press secretary was asked how the president feels about \u8220\'20\'1Cstanding toe to toe with his main adversary tonight\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 According to the \uc2 Washington Post\uc2 , replied:\par \par \uc2 He likes to fight. He likes to fight for the American people.\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  walks to greet supporters outside the Hyatt Regency, Atlanta. Photograph: Elizabeth Frantz/Reuters\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.32pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.01pm BST\par \par \uc2 US district judge Aileen Cannon, who is presiding over \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s classified documents case, has granted a request from the former president\u8217\'20\'19s defense team to hold a hearing to challenge some of the evidence gathered against him.\par \par \uc2 Cannon said she would schedule a hearing to consider whether prosecutors had improperly obtained the cooperation of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s lawyers through an exception to attorney-client privilege.\par \par \uc2 From my colleague Hugo Lowell:\par \par \uc2 enltrNEW: Judge Cannon will grant \uc2 TRUMP\uc2  an evidentiary hearing to potentially suppress key obstruction evidence in the classified docs case\par \par \uc2 Cannon will decide AFRESH the extent the crime-fraud exception applies to ex-Trump lawyer Evan Corcoran's notes {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/mhRdScSvli"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/mhRdScSvli}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Hugo Lowell (@hugolowell) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hugolowell/status/1806368464321323173?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 27, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 But Judge Cannon also denied a defense request for a hearing on a separate claim that \uc2 FBI\uc2  officials had submitted false or misleading information to obtain a warrant to search Trump\u8217\'20\'19s Mar-a-Lago estate for classified documents.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.05pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.43pm BST\par \par \uc2 The supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s ruling {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jun/27/supreme-court-decision-politics-trump-biden-debate-latest-updates?page=with:block-667d765c8f082c039b8c7863#block-667d765c8f082c039b8c7863"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 earlier today }}}\uc2  to allow Idaho hospitals to provide emergency abortions \u8211\'20\'13 for now \u8211\'20\'13 has left key questions unanswered and could mean a final decision is delayed to beyond the November elections.\par \par \uc2 A draft decision in the case was briefly posted on the court\u8217\'20\'19s website yesterday and abruptly removed. The final version of the decision published today appeared to closely resemble the draft.\par \par \uc2 Responding to the order, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  said the ruling ensures that Idaho women can get the care they need while the case continues to play out, adding:\par \par \uc2 Doctors should be able to practice medicine. Patients should be able to get the care they need.\par \par \uc2 enltrNo woman should be denied care, made to wait until she\u8217\'20\'19s near death, or forced to flee her home to receive the health care she needs.\par \par \uc2 Today\u8217\'20\'19s Supreme Court order ensures women in Idaho can access the emergency medical care they need for now.\par \par \uc2 But {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/VP?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @VP}}}\uc2  and I will continue to fight\u8230\'20\'26 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/cfeuZVbLjg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/cfeuZVbLjg}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 President Biden (@POTUS) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/POTUS/status/1806366109936845079?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 27, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 The White House\u8217\'20\'19s press secretary, \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2 , said:\par \par \uc2 No woman should be denied care or wait until she\u8217\'20\'19s near death or forced to flee her home state just to receive the healthcare she needs.\par \par \uc2 Merrick Garland\uc2 , the attorney general, said the justice department will continue pressing its case and using \u8220\'20\'1Cevery available tool to ensure that women in every state have access to that care\u8221\'20\'1D. His statement reads:\par \par \uc2 Today\u8217\'20\'19s order means that, while we continue to litigate our case, women in Idaho will once again have access to the emergency care guaranteed to them under federal law.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.45pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.34pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has appeared to share his talking points for tonight\u8217\'20\'19s debate on his Truth Social platform.\par \par \uc2 The post shows what appears to be a set of recommendations from \uc2 Andrew Wheeler\uc2 , Trump\u8217\'20\'19s former \uc2 Environmental Protection Agency\uc2  chief.\par \par \uc2 Wheeler, in the post, advises Trump to pledge to reduce carbon emissions and to point out that \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  rejoined the Paris climate accord, and \u8220\'20\'1Call that does is send American dollars overseas\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Ammar Moussa, a Biden campaign spokesperson, shared Trump\u8217\'20\'19s talking points on \uc2 Twitter\uc2 /X, writing:\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is just posting his debate talking points. Thanks I guess.\par \par \uc2 enltrDonald Trump is just posting his debate talking points.\par \par \uc2 Thanks I guess. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/OfOCTmckIT"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/OfOCTmckIT}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Ammar Moussa (@ammarmufasa) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ammarmufasa/status/1806383074277515498?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 27, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 Robert F Kennedy Jr\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jun/27/supreme-court-decision-politics-trump-biden-debate-latest-updates?page=with:block-667db9478f086bfb3f8ef908#block-667db9478f086bfb3f8ef908"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 anger}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jun/27/supreme-court-decision-politics-trump-biden-debate-latest-updates?page=with:block-667db9478f086bfb3f8ef908#block-667db9478f086bfb3f8ef908"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 and frustration}}}\uc2  at what he describes as his exclusion from the debate despite six qualifying polls and confirmed ballot access in five states \u8211\'20\'13 with Democratic legal challenges to his inclusion in five more, including one in New Jersey under the state\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://pub.njleg.gov/bills/9899/a2500/2228_i1.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sore loser law}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 comes as Democrats accuse him of being a political stooge for Republicans.\par \par \uc2 Biden supporters worry Kennedy\u8217\'20\'19s famous name and his history of environmental advocacy could {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/jun/09/rfk-biden-trump-2024-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sway voters}}}\uc2  from the left.\par \par \uc2 His family members are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/18/kennedy-family-endorse-biden"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 largely against his candidacy}}}\uc2 , which they have made clear in public statements and by visiting the Biden White House en masse on St Patrick\u8217\'20\'19s Day in March.\par \par \uc2 But Republicans also have not welcomed his quixotic intervention in a tight race that could serve to siphon off vital votes from both candidates.\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has described him as \u8220\'20\'1Cfar more LIBERAL than anyone running as a Democrat, including West and Stein\u8221\'20\'1D, referring to third-party candidates Cornel West and Jill Stein.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.24pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.11pm BST\par \par \uc2 Robert F Kennedy Jr\uc2 , the independent US presidential candidate polling at about 8%, won\u8217\'20\'19t be at tonight\u8217\'20\'19s Biden-Trump TV smackdown in Atlanta.\par \par \uc2 But he\u8217\'20\'19s not taking the diss quietly, and has accused debate host CNN of colluding with the major party campaigns to exclude him.\par \par \uc2 In an email statement on Wednesday, the Kennedy campaign claimed that 71% of Americans want to see him on the debate stage, and in an act of counter-programming he plans an alternative {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://therealdebate.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Creal\u8221\'20\'1D debate}}}\uc2  on Elon\u8217\'20\'19s Musk\u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 Twitter\uc2 /X platform at the same time.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe American people want leaders who trust them to make up their own minds,\u8221\'20\'1D Kennedy said.\par \par \uc2 Instead, our last two presidents are restricting voters from choosing anyone other than themselves. Presidents Biden and Trump have sucked trillions of dollars from the pockets of working people and Americans deserve to hear from the one candidate who can hold them to account.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.58pm BST\par \par \uc2 Young voters were key to \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s victory in 2020. And they helped forestall a Republican \u8220\'20\'1Cred wave\u8221\'20\'1D in 2022.\par \par \uc2 But recent polling suggests the 81-year-old president may have a problem with the youth of America.\par \par \uc2 One theory for the shift is that young people don\u8217\'20\'19t have strong memories of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s presidency. Some who will vote for the first time this year were just 10 when the reality-TV star was first elected. They have only ever known polarization and politics in the age of Trump.\par \par \uc2 One gen Z-led group is working to remind their peers of what the Trump presidency was like. Ahead of the debate, the group is warning viewers not to believe what the former president is telling them.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 a criminally convicted liar \u8211\'20\'13 will undoubtedly lie about his destructive record and alarming agenda tonight,\u8221\'20\'1D said Santiago Mayer, the 22-year-old founder and executive director of Voters of Tomorrow.\par \par \uc2 Trump will try to distract us from the fact that his presidency was the worst thing to happen to gen Z in our lifetime.\par \par \uc2 The group has launched, ironically, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://genzfortrump.org/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 GenZforTrump.org}}}\uc2 , as a resource for young people to fact-check the former president, whose relationship with the truth has always been \u8230\'20\'26 casual.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.09pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 Responding to the Harrington v \uc2 Purdue Pharma\uc2  decision, several state attorneys general issued statements praising the court\u8217\'20\'19s ruling.\par \par \uc2 Josh Stein\uc2 , the attorney general of North Carolina, said in a statement reported by Reuters:\par \par \uc2 Purdue and the Sacklers must pay so we can save lives and help people live free of addiction. If they won\u8217\'20\'19t pay up, I\u8217\'20\'19ll see them in court.\par \par \uc2 William Tong\uc2 , the attorney general of Connecticut, whose office first sued and eventually agreed to the deal, said:\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  got it right \u8211\'20\'13 billionaire wrongdoers should not be allowed to shield blood money in bankruptcy court \u8230\'20\'26 We will be front and center again in any new negotiations.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.07pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.34pm BST\par \par \uc2 Elizabeth Warren, the Democratic senator for Massachusetts, said the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19 s ruling blocking \uc2 Purdue Pharma\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s bankruptcy settlement plan was a \u8220\'20\'1Cfirst step towards accountability for the Sackler family\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The Sacklers \u8220\'20\'1Cmade a fortune from hooking people to opioids that killed hundreds of thousands of Americans, and then tried to use the bankruptcy system to keep their money,\u8221\'20\'1D Warren said in a statement posted to social media.\par \par \uc2 The Supreme Court closed this bankruptcy loophole, but that doesn\u8217\'20\'19t make things right for the millions of people who have lost loved ones to opioid overdoses.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s time for the Sacklers to pay up.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.13pm BST\par \par \uc2 Opponents of the \uc2 Purdue Pharma\uc2  settlement praised the court\u8217\'20\'19s decision, while some called on the justice department to seek criminal charges against members of the Sackler family.\par \par \uc2 Mike Quinn, who represents Ellen Isaacs, whose son Ryan died after becoming dependent on Oxycontin and who filed a brief in support of the plaintiffs in the supreme court case, said:\par \par \uc2 This is a victory for all Americans \u8211\'20\'13 a victory for everybody that wealthy wrong-doers don\u8217\'20\'19t have the right to receive liability and write the law, that anybody can stand up against them and protect their rights under the constitution.\par \par \uc2 Ed Bisch, whose son Eddie died from an overdose after taking OxyContin, said he would have accepted the deal if he thought it would have made a dent in the opioid crisis. A statement to AP read:\par \par \uc2 This is a step toward justice. It was outrageous what they were trying to get away with. They have made a mockery of the justice system and then they tried to make a mockery of the bankruptcy system.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.06pm BST\par \par \uc2 Purdue Pharma\uc2  calls supreme court decision \u8216\'20\'18heart crushing\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 In a statement following the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s Harrington v \uc2 Purdue Pharma\uc2  decision, the company described the ruling as \u8220\'20\'1Cheart-crushing\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Members of the Sackler family branches who own Purdue suggested they plan return to negotiations. A statement to AP reads:\par \par \uc2 While we are confident that we would prevail in any future litigation given the profound misrepresentations about our families and the opioid crisis, we continue to believe that a swift negotiated agreement to provide billions of dollars for people and communities in need is the best way forward.\par \par \uc2 Edward Neiger, a lawyer representing more than 60,000 overdose victims, said the court\u8217\'20\'19s decision was a major setback.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe Purdue plan was a victim-centered plan that would provide billions of dollars to the states to be used exclusively to abate the opioid crisis and $750m for victims of the crisis, so that they could begin to rebuild their lives,\u8221\'20\'1D Neiger said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 As a result of the senseless three-year crusade by the government against the plan, thousands of people died of overdose, and today\u8217\'20\'19s decision will lead to more needless overdose deaths.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.18pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.59pm BST\par \par \uc2 The supreme court, in its decision to reject \uc2 Purdue Pharma\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 s bankruptcy settlement plan {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jun/27/supreme-court-decision-politics-trump-biden-debate-latest-updates?page=with:block-667d72ee8f08cd2412988f4f#block-667d72ee8f08cd2412988f4f"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 earlier today, }}}\uc2  blocked a controversial deal that would have protected the Sackler family from further liability over the US opioid epidemic, in exchange for providing funds for compensation and rehabilitation treatment.\par \par \uc2 The 5-4 decision, written by Justice \uc2 Neil M Gorsuch\uc2 , was voted on non-ideological lines. It was backed by Justices \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2 , \uc2 Samuel A Alito Jr\uc2 , \uc2 Amy Coney Barrett\uc2  and \uc2 Ketanji Brown Jackson\uc2 . Justice \uc2 Brett M Kavanaugh\uc2 , Chief Justice \uc2 John G Roberts Jr\uc2  and Justices \uc2 Sonia Sotomayor\uc2  and \uc2 Elena Kagan\uc2  dissented.\par \par \uc2 The deal was constructed to allow Purdue, the Connecticut company behind the prescription opioid OxyContin, to restructure and also shield the relevant Sackler billionaires without them having to declare personal bankruptcy.\par \par \uc2 As part of the deal, the Sackler family had agreed to contribute $6bn to the settlement from the vast fortune they made from OxyContin and give up ownership.\par \par \uc2 Court filings showed that 95% of creditors in the Purdue bankruptcy case had agreed to sign on to the plan, although many reluctantly, partly seeing it as the only way to finally get some recompense. But several states, Canadian municipalities and Indigenous tribes, and more than 2,600 individuals, including high-profile activists, were opposed.\par \par \uc2 Today\u8217\'20\'19s ruling now leaves matters between the company and plaintiffs unresolved. The case is seen as having consequences for other corporate bankruptcies where company owners or officials want immunity from liability.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.46pm BST\par \par \uc2 Michigan governor \uc2 Gretchen Whitmer\uc2  left the door open to a presidential run in 2028 when Katie Couric asked her about her plans for the political future during a session this morning at the Aspen Ideas festival.\par \par \uc2 Whitmer is often mentioned as one of the top Democratic contenders to be the next president.\par \par \uc2 Noting she had a tough job for the next two and a half years, Whitmer said:\par \par \uc2 I\u8217\'20\'19m making no plans right now and then I\u8217\'20\'19ll see what happens next.\par \par \uc2 She added:\par \par \uc2 Maybe there\u8217\'20\'19s someone I\u8217\'20\'19m gonna be excited about. Maybe another scenario. That\u8217\'20\'19s as far as I am down that path.\par \par \uc2 She also weighed in on whether \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  could face trouble in Michigan, a key battleground state, from its large concentration of Arab-American voters. More than 100,000 people voted uncommitted in the Democratic primary in the state amid concerns over how Biden handled the war in Gaza.\par \par \uc2 While Whitmer said the Biden campaign was \u8220\'20\'1Cnot thrilled\u8221\'20\'1D about that result, she said she actually thought it was a positive thing because \u8220\'20\'1Cpeople were able to register their discontent and it opened up a line of communication.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Whitmer also acknowledged that she thought \u8220\'20\'1Cwe can do more\u8221\'20\'1D to make American voters understand that Biden gets their concerns about the economy.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.26pm BST\par \par \uc2 Pressure grows on Congress to rescind invitation to Netanyahu\par \par \uc2 Congress is facing increasing pressure to withdraw its invitation to Israeli prime minister \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2  who is set to speak on Capitol Hill next month.\par \par \uc2 Robert Tait reports for the Guardian:\par \par \uc2 A group of prominent Israelis \u8211\'20\'13 including a former prime minister and an ex-head of \uc2 Mossad\uc2 , the foreign intelligence service \u8211\'20\'13 have added their voices to the growing domestic calls in the US for Congress to withdraw its invitation to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/benjamin-netanyahu"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu}}}\uc2  to address it next month, calling the move \u8220\'20\'1Ca terrible mistake\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The plea, in an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2024/06/26/opinion/congress-netanyahu-gaza-war.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 op-ed article}}}\uc2  in the \uc2 New York Times\uc2 , argues that the invitation rewards Netanyahu, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/israel"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Israel}}}\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s current prime minister, for \u8220\'20\'1Cscandalous and destructive conduct\u8221\'20\'1D, including intelligence failures that led to last {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/oct/07/hamas-launches-surprise-attack-on-israel-as-palestinian-gunmen-reported-in-south"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October\u8217\'20\'19s deadly Hamas attack}}}\uc2  and the ensuing bloody war in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/gaza"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Gaza}}}\uc2  which shows no sign of ending.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CCongress has made a terrible mistake. Mr Netanyahu\u8217\'20\'19s appearance in Washington will not represent the State of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/israel"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Israel}}}\uc2  and its citizens, and it will reward his scandalous and destructive conduct toward our country,\u8221\'20\'1D the article\u8217\'20\'19s six authors argue in a blistering critique that also accuses the Israeli prime minister of failing to secure the release of scores of hostages taken in last year\u8217\'20\'19s attack and still held captive.\par \par \uc2 For the full story, click here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/article/2024/jun/27/israelis-congress-netanyahu-joint-session"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US Congress faces growing calls to withdraw Netanyahu invitation: \u8216\'20\'18a terrible mistake\u8217\'20\'19}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.40pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.04pm BST\par \par \uc2 Pro-democracy groups gathered at the Wisconsin state capitol Thursday morning to call on the resignation of Robert Spindell, a Republican who served as a pro-Trump false elector in 2020, from the Wisconsin Elections Commission.\par \par \uc2 Spindell has also bragged about GOP voter suppression efforts in Milwaukee.\par \par \uc2 In an email first reported in January 2023, Spindell wrote that Republicans could be \u8220\'20\'1Cespecially proud of the City of Milwaukee (80.2% Dem Vote) casting 37,000 less votes than cast in the 2018 election with the major reduction happening in the overwhelming Black and Hispanic areas.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 During public comments before the Wisconsin Elections Commission, speakers decried Spindell\u8217\'20\'19s participation in the false elector scheme and his comments about voters of color.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou wanna know what\u8217\'20\'19s exhausting? Living in a country where people get to live above the law,\u8221\'20\'1D said Nick Ramos, director of the watchdog group Wisconsin Democracy Campaign.\par \par \uc2 In response to comments calling on his resignation, Spindell made repeated reference to \u8220\'20\'1CMilwaukee\u8217\'20\'19s white Democrats,\u8221\'20\'1D who he blamed for voter suppression in Milwaukee.\par \par \uc2 Individuals who served as false electors in Arizona and Michigan are facing prosecution over their role in \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s attempts to overturn the 2020 election.\par \par \uc2 Earlier this month, Wisconsin attorney general \uc2 Josh Kaul\uc2  filed felony charges against two attorneys involved in the false elector scheme; the ten Wisconsin false electors, including Spindell, have not yet been charged.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.47pm BST\par \par \uc2 I\u8217\'20\'19m sitting in a packed auditorium here at the Aspen Ideas Festival where attendees are packed in to hear from Michigan governor \uc2 Gretchen Whitmer\uc2 , who is speaking with journalist Katie Couric.\par \par \uc2 Talking about her childhood, Couric brought up how Whitmer was a troublemaking teenager and even once threw up on her high school principal from drinking. \u8220\'20\'1CNot my best day,\u8221\'20\'1D Whitmer said to laughs.\par \par \uc2 She then paused and took a shot at \uc2 Kristi Noem\uc2 , the South Dakota governor who has come under fire for sharing a story about killing her pets.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19ve never executed any dogs or goats,\u8221\'20\'1D Whitmer said, prompting more laughter.\par \par \uc2 I couldn\u8217\'20\'19t make it out exactly, but one woman in front of me whispered to her friend, \u8220\'20\'1Cshe\u8217\'20\'19s got my vote.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.11pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.34pm BST\par \par \uc2 In run-up to debate, Biden camp leans into message: Trump is a threat to democracy\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and his allies are leaning heavily into their message that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  represents a threat to democracy in the final hours leading up to tonight\u8217\'20\'19s debate.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Democratic National Committee\uc2  plans to run a mobile billboard around the debate venue in Atlanta, with the featured ad highlighting Trump\u8217\'20\'19s effort to overturn the results of the 2020 election and the reversal of Roe v Wade.\par \par \uc2 The DNC has also placed ads on five billboards near the debate venue to spotlight Trump\u8217\'20\'19s policy proposals and his recent felony conviction in New York.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAs \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  prepares to lie for 90 straight minutes on the debate stage this evening, the DNC is already on the ground in Atlanta to remind voters of how he tried to undermine Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s democracy, threatens to leave working families behind again, and is hellbent on ripping away reproductive freedoms,\u8221\'20\'1D DNC spokesperson Abhi Rahman said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTonight, voters across the country will see the clear choice in front of them, and they will make Trump a loser once again in November.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.39pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.11pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Democratic Legislative Campaign Committee has issued a similar statement following the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s Idaho \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  case decision, saying:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CToday\u8217\'20\'19s SCOTUS ruling reiterates that state legislatures remain the arbiters of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access. The best defense against Republicans\u8217\'20\'19 assault on reproductive freedoms is to elect Democrats to state legislatures who will champion reproductive care and counter GOP extremism.\par \par \uc2 The balance of power in the states is especially important given the supreme court remains hostile to reproductive freedoms and has demonstrated a repeated willingness to catapult extreme GOP state laws to the national stage to become law of the land \u8211\'20\'13 as they did with Dobbs.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.40pm BST\par \par \uc2 Reproductive Freedom for All\uc2  has issued a response to the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s decision on Idaho\u8217\'20\'19s emergency \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  case, saying:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe court could have upheld this basic right, but they refused to. Instead, the conservative majority kicked the case back to a lower court, punting so that they didn\u8217\'20\'19t need to weigh in before an election where attacks on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access are already top of mind for voters.\par \par \uc2 While the Biden administration is fighting tooth and nail to ensure people can get the emergency \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care they need, anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  extremists will continue to do whatever they can to stop them. Let this serve as a reminder of what\u8217\'20\'19s at stake this November.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.13pm BST\par \par \uc2 Supreme court issues three major decisions surrounding \uc2 Purdue Pharma\uc2 , the \uc2 EPA\uc2  and \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 The supreme court on Thursday issued three major decisions on cases involving OxyContin maker \uc2 Purdue Pharma\uc2 , an air pollution rule by the \uc2 Environmental Protection Agency\uc2  and \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access in Idaho.\par \par \uc2 In a 5-4 decision, the conservative-majority court rejected \uc2 Purdue Pharma\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s multi-billion dollar settlement that would have shielded the wealthy Sackler family from future lawsuits over the country\u8217\'20\'19s deadly opioid epidemic, but would have also provided compensation and rehabilitation funds to victims.\par \par \uc2 In his opinion, conservative justice \uc2 Neil Gorsuch\uc2  wrote:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe Sacklers seek greater relief than a bankruptcy discharge normally affords, for they hope to extinguish even claims for wrongful death and fraud, and they seek to do so without putting anything close to all their assets on the table.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In a separate 5-4 decision, the court put on hold an attempt by the \uc2 EPA\uc2  to reduce air pollution from power plants in \u8220\'20\'1Cupwind\u8221\'20\'1D states that would affect air quality in \u8220\'20\'1Cdownwind\u8221\'20\'1D states. Along with industry allies, Ohio, West Virginia and Indiana have been challenging the \uc2 EPA\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s rule.\par \par \uc2 Conservative justice \uc2 Amy Coney Barrett\uc2 , who joined the court\u8217\'20\'19s three liberal justices, in dissent, wrote that the court \u8220\'20\'1Cjustifies this decision based on an alleged procedural error that likely had no impact on the plan.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, in a victory for reproductive rights activists, the court dismissed a case over whether emergency room doctors can perform abortions to save a pregnant woman\u8217\'20\'19s life.\par \par \uc2 The court\u8217\'20\'19s 6-3 decision marks a win for the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/joebiden"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Joe Biden}}}\uc2  administration, for now, as the case is returned to a lower court and potentially delays a final decision until after the election. Idaho had tried to have the procedure exempted from the Emergency Medical Treatment and Labor Act.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.47pm BST\par \par \uc2 Supreme court dismisses case blocking emergency abortions in Idaho\par \par \uc2 The supreme court has dismissed a case that sought to block emergency abortions in Idaho, a state with a near-total \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban.\par \par \uc2 The court\u8217\'20\'19s decision marks a win for the \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  administration, for now, as the case is returned to a lower court and potentially delays a final decision until after the election.\par \par \uc2 Idaho had tried to have the procedure exempted from the Emergency Medical Treatment and Labor Act.\par \par \uc2 The court\u8217\'20\'19s 6-3 decision, which came after a version of the ruling was prematurely posted on to its website yesterday, reinstates a lower court\u8217\'20\'19s decision that EMTALA takes precedence over Idaho\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban.\par \par \uc2 Samuel Alito\uc2 , \uc2 Neil Gorsuch\uc2  and \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2  were in the minority opinion.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.16pm BST\par \par \uc2 Supreme court blocks \uc2 Purdue Pharma\uc2 's multi-billion dollar bankruptcy settlement\par \par \uc2 In its second decision of the morning, the supreme court has blocked \uc2 Purdue Pharma\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s multi-billion dollar bankruptcy settlement.\par \par \uc2 The settlement would have excused and shielded the wealthy Sackler family and their company \uc2 Purdue Pharma\uc2 , maker of the highly addictive opioid OxyContin, from lawsuits surrounding the country\u8217\'20\'19s opioid epidemic.\par \par \uc2 The decision came at 5-4, with \uc2 Brett Kavanaugh\uc2 , \uc2 John Roberts\uc2 , \uc2 Sonia Sotomayor\uc2  and \uc2 Elena Kagan\uc2  dissenting.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CToday\u8217\'20\'19s decision is wrong on the law and devastating for more than 100,000 opioid victims and their families,\u8221\'20\'1D Kavanaugh wrote.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.09pm BST\par \par \uc2 Supreme court issues hold on \uc2 EPA\uc2 's enforcement of pollution rule\par \par \uc2 In its first decision of the morning, the supreme court has issued a ruling that puts on hold the \uc2 Environmental Protection Agency\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s enforcement of an air pollution rule.\par \par \uc2 With a 5-4 decision with \uc2 Amy Coney Barrett\uc2 , \uc2 Sonia Sotomayor\uc2 , \uc2 Elena Kagan\uc2  and \uc2 Ketanji Brown Jackson\uc2  dissenting, the decision grants states the application to put the \uc2 EPA\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s rule on hold as the case moves to the lower courts.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 EPA\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cgood neighbor\u8221\'20\'1D rule seeks to restrict air pollution from power plants in \u8220\'20\'1Cupwind\u8221\'20\'1D states that would affect air quality in \u8220\'20\'1Cdownwind\u8221\'20\'1D states.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.17pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.40pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s 2024 campaign has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://joebiden.com/project2025/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 launched}}}\uc2  a new website landing page in attempts to underscore the threat of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Project 2025.\par \par \uc2 The launch comes in response to Trump\u8217\'20\'19s blueprint of policy proposals that could dismantle and disrupt the \uc2 US government\uc2  while replacing career staff with political loyalists.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CProject 2025 is the plan by \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Maga Republican allies to give Trump more power over your daily life, gut democratic checks and balances, and consolidate power in the Oval Office if he wins.\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s campaign advisors and close allies wrote it \u8211\'20\'13 and are doing everything they can to elect him so he can execute their playbook immediately,\u8221\'20\'1D the page reads.\par \par \uc2 It goes on to break down the various ways Trump \u8220\'20\'1Cis planning to reach into your daily life and how his extreme Maga allies are planning to consolidate power.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The website\u8217\'20\'19s new landing page launch comes ahead of the first presidential debate tonight between Trump and Biden where the current president is expected to highlight the various threats surrounding Project 2025.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.23pm BST\par \par \uc2 Recent major decisions by the supreme court\par \par \uc2 Here is a look at some of the major decisions the supreme court has issued so far this term:\par \par \uc2 On Wednesday, the court struck down a lower court ruling, in turn allowing the federal government to request the removal of misinformation from social media platforms.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/jun/26/supreme-court-decision-social-media-misinformation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US supreme court allows government to request removal of misinformation on social media}}}\par \par \uc2 Earlier this month, the court upheld access to the common \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill mifepristone, marking a major victory for reproductive rights activists since the court overturned Roe v Wade two years ago.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/jun/13/supreme-court-abortion-pill-access"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US supreme court unanimously upholds access to \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  pill mifepristone}}}\par \par \uc2 The court, in a 8-1 ruling - with conservative justice \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2  dissenting - also upheld a federal ban that prevents domestic violence abusers from possessing guns.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/jun/21/supreme-court-domestic-violence-gun-ban"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US supreme court upholds ban on domestic abusers possessing guns}}}\par \par \uc2 In a setback for gun control activists, the court struck down a federal ban on \u8220\'20\'1Cbump stock\u8221\'20\'1D accessories for guns, which allow semiautomatic firearms to fire as quickly as machine guns.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/ng-interactive/2024/jun/14/supreme-court-bump-stock-ban-decision"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US supreme court strikes down federal ban on \u8216\'20\'18bump stock\u8217\'20\'19 devices for guns}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.43pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.14pm BST\par \par \uc2 Supreme court to issue decisions with blockbuster rulings outstanding\par \par \uc2 Good morning,\par \par \uc2 The supreme court is set to issue another set of opinions today at 10am which may include major decisions on \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s presidential immunity case and whether states are allowed to carry out emergency abortions.\par \par \uc2 So far, the conservative-majority court this term has upheld access to the common \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill mifepristone, upheld a federal ban that prevents domestic abusers from possessing guns, struck down a federal ban on \u8220\'20\'1Cbump stock\u8221\'20\'1D accessories for guns, as well as a struck down a lower court ruling to allow the federal government to request misinformation removal from social media.\par \par \uc2 The decisions for major cases that have yet to be released include Trump\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/25/supreme-court-trump-immunity-claim"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 immunity petition }}}\uc2  from the federal charges he faces over the 2020 presidential election interference, as well as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/2024/apr/24/us-supreme-court-abortion-rights-emtala"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 whether hospitals}}}\uc2  in states with \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans are required to perform emergency abortions \u8211\'20\'13 a case fought between the \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  administration and the state of Idaho. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jun/26/supreme-court-emergency-abortion-idaho-decision"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 According to}}}\uc2  a report from \uc2 Bloomberg\uc2 , the court\u8217\'20\'19s alleged opinion on the Idaho \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  case \u8211\'20\'13 which would allow for emergency abortions in the state \u8211\'20\'13 was briefly posted on the court\u8217\'20\'19s website on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 Here are other developments in US politics:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The first presidential debate between Biden and Trump is set to take place this evening in Atlanta, Georgia.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Transportation secretary \uc2 Pete Buttigieg\uc2  is set to testify before the House\u8217\'20\'19s transportation and infrastructure committee.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Renowned polling expert Nate Silver has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.natesilver.net/p/the-presidential-election-isnt-a"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 predicted}}}\uc2  a 66% chance of Trump winning the 2024 presidential election.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240627ek6r001s4\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
