\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  decisions: the biggest cases this term and their outcomes\b0\par\par\uc2 Guardian staff \par \uc2 2,440 \uc2 words\par \uc2 1 July 2024\par 19:14 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 The court has wrapped up its term, issuing blockbuster decisions with enormous implications and the conservative supermajority in the driver\u8217\'20\'19s seat\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  has wrapped up its 2023-2024 term, issuing a string of blockbuster decisions with enormous implications for American democracy, individual and civil rights, and the basic functioning of the federal government.\par \par \uc2 Once again, the conservative supermajority, with half its justices appointed by \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , was in the driver\u8217\'20\'19s seat \u8211\'20\'13 strengthening the power of the presidency in its immunity ruling for Trump, and overturning precedent in a dramatic blow to the administrative state. There were crumbs of comfort for liberals, including a gun rights ruling related to domestic violence and a unanimous decision upholding access to a key \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill, but what the US public increasingly sees as an activist court majority continues in full swing.\par \par \uc2 Some of the major decisions from this term\u8217\'20\'19s docket:\par \par \uc2 ***\par \par \uc2 Trump has \u8216\'20\'18absolute immunity\u8217\'20\'19 for official acts\par \par \uc2 Decided 6-3\par \par \uc2 Conservative bloc\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Alito \u8211\'20\'13 Majority\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Barrett \u8211\'20\'13 Majority\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Gorsuch \u8211\'20\'13 Majority\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Kavanaugh \u8211\'20\'13 Majority\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Roberts \u8211\'20\'13 Majority\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Thomas \u8211\'20\'13 Majority\par \par \uc2 Liberal bloc\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Jackson \u8211\'20\'13 Minority\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Kagan \u8211\'20\'13 Minority\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Sotomayor \u8211\'20\'13 Minority\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  ruled in Trump v United States that former presidents are entitled to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/jul/01/supreme-court-decision-trump-immunity-ruling"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 some degree of immunity}}}\uc2  from criminal prosecution, dramatically reducing the likelihood that the federal criminal case against {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  on charges he plotted to stop the transfer of power will proceed before the 2024 election.\par \par \uc2 The court\u8217\'20\'19s conservative majority \u8211\'20\'13 which Trump helped create \u8211\'20\'13 found that presidents are protected from prosecution for official actions that extend to the \u8220\'20\'1Couter perimeter\u8221\'20\'1D of the office, but could face charges for conduct undertaken in a personal or private manner.\par \par \uc2 ***\par \par \uc2 Returns decision on Republican-backed social media laws to lower courts\par \par \uc2 Decided 9-0\par \par \uc2 Conservative bloc\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Alito \u8211\'20\'13 Majority\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Barrett \u8211\'20\'13 Majority\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Gorsuch \u8211\'20\'13 Majority\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Kavanaugh \u8211\'20\'13 Majority\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Roberts \u8211\'20\'13 Majority\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Thomas \u8211\'20\'13 Majority\par \par \uc2 Liberal bloc\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Jackson \u8211\'20\'13 Majority\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Kagan \u8211\'20\'13 Majority\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Sotomayor \u8211\'20\'13 Majority\par \par \uc2 In NetChoice v Paxton, the supreme court {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/01/supreme-court-texas-florida-social-media-laws"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  threw out judicial decisions involving challenges to Republican-backed laws}}}\uc2  in Florida and Texas that restricted the power of social media companies to remove or down-rank objectionable content.\par \par \uc2 The justices directed lower appeals courts to reconsider a pair of decisions regarding these 2021 laws authorizing the states to regulate the content-moderation practices of large social media platforms. Tech industry trade groups had challenged the two laws under the US constitution\u8217\'20\'19s first amendment limits on the government\u8217\'20\'19s ability to restrict speech. The ruling came on the final day of the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s term that began in October.\par \par \uc2 ***\par \par \uc2 Court strikes down 40-year precedent, reducing power of federal agencies\par \par \uc2 Decided 6-3\par \par \uc2 Conservative bloc\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Alito \u8211\'20\'13 Majority\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Barrett \u8211\'20\'13 Majority\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Gorsuch \u8211\'20\'13 Majority\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Kavanaugh \u8211\'20\'13 Majority\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Roberts \u8211\'20\'13 Majority\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Thomas \u8211\'20\'13 Majority\par \par \uc2 Liberal bloc\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Jackson \u8211\'20\'13 Minority\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Kagan \u8211\'20\'13 Minority\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Sotomayor \u8211\'20\'13 Minority\par \par \uc2 The court overturned one of its own {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/jun/28/us-supreme-court-chevron-doctrine-ruling"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 most important precedents}}}\uc2 , the \uc2 Chevron\uc2  doctrine, that for the past 40 years has guided the work of the federal government in critical areas of public life, from food and drug safety to environmental protection.\par \par \uc2 In a ruling in two cases \u8211\'20\'13 Loper Bright Enterprises v Raimondo; Relentless v Department of Commerce \u8211\'20\'13 that the Biden administration warned could have a \u8220\'20\'1Cconvulsive\u8221\'20\'1D impact on the functioning of government, the court\u8217\'20\'19s hardline conservative majority voted as a block to throw out the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s own 1984 opinion in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.oyez.org/cases/1983/82-1005"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Chevron USA Inc v Natural Resources Defense Council}}}\uc2 . That decision required the courts to defer to the knowledge of government experts in their reasonable interpretation of ambiguous laws. It has long been a target of the conservative legal movement.\par \par \uc2 ***\par \par \uc2 Decision to narrow obstruction law could affect prosecutions of 6 January rioters \u8211\'20\'13 and Trump\par \par \uc2 Decided 6-3\par \par \uc2 Conservative bloc\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Alito \u8211\'20\'13 Majority\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Barrett \u8211\'20\'13 Minority\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Gorsuch \u8211\'20\'13 Majority\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Kavanaugh \u8211\'20\'13 Majority\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Roberts \u8211\'20\'13 Majority\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Thomas \u8211\'20\'13 Majority\par \par \uc2 Liberal bloc\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Jackson \u8211\'20\'13 Majority\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Kagan \u8211\'20\'13 Minority\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Sotomayor \u8211\'20\'13 Minority\par \par \uc2 The court {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/jun/28/supreme-court-january-6-rioters"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  narrowed}}}\uc2  the statute that prosecutors have relied on in the cases of hundreds of rioters who took part in the January 6 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-capitol-breach"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Capitol attack}}}\uc2  for obstruction of an official proceeding \u8211\'20\'13 a ruling with profound implications for participants on that day in 2021.\par \par \uc2 The 6-3 ruling in Fischer v United States could also affect the federal criminal case against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , who is charged with similar offences in special counsel \uc2 Jack Smith\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s investigation into the assault. The decision stems from the conviction of Joseph Fischer, a former Pennsylvania police officer, who took part in Trump\u8217\'20\'19s so-called \u8220\'20\'1Cstop the steal\u8221\'20\'1D rally on the morning of January 6 before then entering the Capitol with the mob.\par \par \uc2 ***\par \par \uc2 Unhoused people sleeping outside can be fined and jailed\par \par \uc2 Decided 6-3\par \par \uc2 Conservative bloc\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Alito \u8211\'20\'13 Majority\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Barrett \u8211\'20\'13 Majority\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Gorsuch \u8211\'20\'13 Majority\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Kavanaugh \u8211\'20\'13 Majority\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Roberts \u8211\'20\'13 Majority\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Thomas \u8211\'20\'13 Majority\par \par \uc2 Liberal bloc\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Jackson \u8211\'20\'13 Minority\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Kagan \u8211\'20\'13 Minority\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Sotomayor \u8211\'20\'13 Minority\par \par \uc2 The court ruled that cities in the US west can {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/jun/28/supreme-court-decision-unhoused-sleeping-outside"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 criminalize unhoused people for sleeping outside}}}\uc2  even when they lack access to shelter. The ruling is a victory for Grants Pass, Oregon, which for years has prohibited sleeping and camping in its public parks and on its streets, banning unhoused people from \u8220\'20\'1Cusing a blanket, pillow, or cardboard box for protection from the elements\u8221\'20\'1D. The city\u8217\'20\'19s policies call for $295 fines and criminal prosecution punishable by up to 30 days in jail after multiple offenses.\par \par \uc2 In City of Grants Pass v Johnson, the court ruled 6-3 that it is not \u8220\'20\'1Ccruel and unusual punishment\u8221\'20\'1D under the eighth amendment to ban unhoused people from camping outside when they have nowhere else to go. The decision stands to broadly affect how American cities approach homelessness and could lead to more jurisdictions passing laws to ticket, fine and jail people for living outside, marking a significant erosion of unhoused people\u8217\'20\'19s rights.\par \par \uc2 ***\par \par \uc2 Court allows emergency abortions in Idaho for now\par \par \uc2 Decided 6-3\par \par \uc2 Conservative bloc\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Alito \u8211\'20\'13 Minority\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Barrett \u8211\'20\'13 Majority\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Gorsuch \u8211\'20\'13 Minority\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Kavanaugh \u8211\'20\'13 Majority\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Roberts \u8211\'20\'13 Majority\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Thomas \u8211\'20\'13 Minority\par \par \uc2 Liberal bloc\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Jackson \u8211\'20\'13 Majority\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Kagan \u8211\'20\'13 Majority\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Sotomayor \u8211\'20\'13 Majority\par \par \uc2 In Moyle v United States, the justices {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/jun/27/supreme-court-allows-emergency-abortions-idaho"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 dismissed a case}}}\uc2  over whether emergency room doctors can perform abortions to save a woman\u8217\'20\'19s health, returning the case to a lower court.\par \par \uc2 Idaho had sought to have \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  exempted from the Emergency Medical Treatment and Labor Act (Emtala), which requires hospitals that receive federal dollars to stabilize the health of patients who show up at their emergency rooms with medical emergencies. Although many states allow doctors to perform an emergency \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  when a woman\u8217\'20\'19s life or health is at risk, in effect mirroring Emtala, Idaho only allowed doctors to intervene when a woman was on the brink of death, a much higher bar for intervention. The Biden administration sued Idaho to enforce the law.\par \par \uc2 ***\par \par \uc2 Court blocks \uc2 EPA\uc2  attempt to reduce pollution that drifts across states\par \par \uc2 Decided 5-4\par \par \uc2 Conservative bloc\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Alito \u8211\'20\'13 Majority\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Barrett \u8211\'20\'13 Minority\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Gorsuch \u8211\'20\'13 Majority\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Kavanaugh \u8211\'20\'13 Majority\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Roberts \u8211\'20\'13 Majority\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Thomas \u8211\'20\'13 Majority\par \par \uc2 Liberal bloc\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Jackson \u8211\'20\'13 Minority\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Kagan \u8211\'20\'13 Minority\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Sotomayor \u8211\'20\'13 Minority\par \par \uc2 The court {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/jun/27/supreme-court-epa-pollution-ruling"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 put a hold}}}\uc2  on an attempt by the \uc2 Environmental Protection Agency\uc2  (\uc2 EPA\uc2 ) to reduce harmful air pollution that drifts across state lines. The ruling in Ohio v \uc2 Environmental Protection Agency\uc2  sided with three states \u8211\'20\'13 Ohio, West Virginia and Indiana \u8211\'20\'13 and industry allies seeking to derail so-called \u8220\'20\'1Cgood neighbor\u8221\'20\'1D regulations, which prevent pollution from billowing into neighboring states.\par \par \uc2 The program, first drawn up by the \uc2 EPA\uc2  in 2015, is designed to prevent \u8220\'20\'1Cupwind\u8221\'20\'1D states from causing air pollution that flows to \u8220\'20\'1Cdownwind\u8221\'20\'1D neighbors. The primary target of the regulation is ground-level ozone, which forms smog that causes an array of health problems. The case will continue to play out in lower courts.\par \par \uc2 ***\par \par \uc2 Decision blocks \uc2 Purdue Pharma\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s bankruptcy settlement that would shield Sacklers from lawsuits\par \par \uc2 Decided 5-4\par \par \uc2 Conservative bloc\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Alito \u8211\'20\'13 Majority\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Barrett \u8211\'20\'13 Majority\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Gorsuch \u8211\'20\'13 Majority\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Kavanaugh \u8211\'20\'13 Minority\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Roberts \u8211\'20\'13 Minority\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Thomas \u8211\'20\'13 Majority\par \par \uc2 Liberal bloc\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Jackson \u8211\'20\'13 Majority\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Kagan \u8211\'20\'13 Minority\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Sotomayor \u8211\'20\'13 Minority\par \par \uc2 In Harrington v \uc2 Purdue Pharma\uc2 , the court {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/jun/27/us-supreme-court-purdue-pharma-opioids"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 rejected painkiller maker Purdue Pharma\u8217\'20\'19s bankruptcy settlement}}}\uc2  plan that included an extraordinary measure to protect its Sackler family owners from further liability over the American opioid epidemic, in exchange for providing funds for compensation and rehabilitation treatment.\par \par \uc2 The deal was constructed to allow Purdue, the Connecticut company behind the prescription opioid OxyContin, to restructure and also shield the relevant Sackler billionaires without them having to declare personal bankruptcy. The family agreed to contribute $6bn to the settlement from the vast fortune they made from OxyContin and give up ownership.\par \par \uc2 The company wanted to use the bankruptcy agreement to resolve thousands of lawsuits, many filed by state and local governments across the US, alleging that \uc2 Purdue Pharma\uc2  fueled a crisis that ultimately killed half a million Americans by claiming its flagship drug was non-addictive while incentivizing massive over-prescribing.\par \par \uc2 ***\par \par \uc2 SEC\u8217\'20\'19s in-house rulings violate US constitution\par \par \uc2 Decided 6-3\par \par \uc2 Conservative bloc\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Alito \u8211\'20\'13 Majority\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Barrett \u8211\'20\'13 Majority\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Gorsuch \u8211\'20\'13 Majority\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Kavanaugh \u8211\'20\'13 Majority\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Roberts \u8211\'20\'13 Majority\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Thomas \u8211\'20\'13 Majority\par \par \uc2 Liberal bloc\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Jackson \u8211\'20\'13 Minority\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Kagan \u8211\'20\'13 Minority\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Sotomayor \u8211\'20\'13 Minority\par \par \uc2 The court {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jun/27/supreme-court-ruling-securities-and-exchange-commission"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 stripped the Securities and Exchange Commission (SEC) of a major tool}}}\uc2  in fighting securities fraud in a decision that could have far-reaching effects on other regulatory agencies.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.documentcloud.org/documents/24779202-sec-v-jarkesy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The justices ruled}}}\uc2  in a 6-3 vote in Securities and Exchange Comission v Jarkesy that people accused of fraud by the SEC, which regulates securities markets, have the right to a jury trial in federal court. The in-house proceedings the SEC has used in some civil fraud complaints violate the constitution, the court said.\par \par \uc2 ***\par \par \uc2 Government is allowed to request removal of misinformation on social media\par \par \uc2 Decided 6-3\par \par \uc2 Conservative bloc\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Alito \u8211\'20\'13 Minority\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Barrett \u8211\'20\'13 Majority\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Gorsuch \u8211\'20\'13 Minority\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Kavanaugh \u8211\'20\'13 Majority\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Roberts \u8211\'20\'13 Majority\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Thomas \u8211\'20\'13 Minority\par \par \uc2 Liberal bloc\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Jackson \u8211\'20\'13 Majority\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Kagan \u8211\'20\'13 Majority\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Sotomayor \u8211\'20\'13 Majority\par \par \uc2 The court {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/jun/26/supreme-court-decision-social-media-misinformation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 struck down a lower court ruling}}}\uc2  in the case of Murthy v Missouri, in a decision that did not find that the government\u8217\'20\'19s communications with social media platforms about Covid-19 misinformation violated the first amendment. The decision permits the government to call on tech companies to remove falsehoods, a key concern as misinformation spreads around this year\u8217\'20\'19s presidential election.\par \par \uc2 The court ruled 6-3 that the plaintiffs had no standing to bring the case against the Biden administration, with conservative justices \uc2 Samuel Alito\uc2 , \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2  and \uc2 Neil Gorsuch\uc2  dissenting. Although many of the arguments in the case centered on how governments and platforms interact with free speech online, the ruling focused more on procedural issues and a lack of legal grounds to bring the case.\par \par \uc2 ***\par \par \uc2 Ban on domestic abusers possessing guns is found to be constitutional\par \par \uc2 Decided 8-1\par \par \uc2 Conservative bloc\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Alito \u8211\'20\'13 Majority\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Barrett \u8211\'20\'13 Majority\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Gorsuch \u8211\'20\'13 Majority\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Kavanaugh \u8211\'20\'13 Majority\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Roberts \u8211\'20\'13 Majority\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Thomas \u8211\'20\'13 Minority\par \par \uc2 Liberal bloc\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Jackson \u8211\'20\'13 Majority\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Kagan \u8211\'20\'13 Majority\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Sotomayor \u8211\'20\'13 Majority\par \par \uc2 The court {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/jun/21/supreme-court-domestic-violence-gun-ban"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 upheld a federal ban}}}\uc2  preventing anyone placed under a domestic violence restraining order from possessing a gun. The ruling in United States v Rahimi was supported by eight justices, with \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2  dissenting. It leaves in place legal protections against a major source of gun violence in America.\par \par \uc2 Writing the opinion, the chief justice, \uc2 John Roberts\uc2 , said that individuals can be temporarily disarmed if they pose a \u8220\'20\'1Ccredible threat to the physical safety of another\u8221\'20\'1D without violating the second amendment to the constitution that allows the right to bear arms.\par \par \uc2 ***\par \par \uc2 Court rules against Washington couple in foreign investment taxation case\par \par \uc2 Decided 7-2\par \par \uc2 Conservative bloc\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Alito \u8211\'20\'13 Majority\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Barrett \u8211\'20\'13 Majority\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Gorsuch \u8211\'20\'13 Minority\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Kavanaugh \u8211\'20\'13 Majority\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Roberts \u8211\'20\'13 Majority\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Thomas \u8211\'20\'13 Minority\par \par \uc2 Liberal bloc\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Jackson \u8211\'20\'13 Majority\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Kagan \u8211\'20\'13 Majority\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Sotomayor \u8211\'20\'13 Majority\par \par \uc2 The court {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/ng-interactive/2024/jun/20/supreme-court-foreign-investment-tax-ruling"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ruled against a Washington couple}}}\uc2  who argued they were unconstitutionally taxed $15,000 for their investment in a foreign company \u8211\'20\'13 in a case some have argued was a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/25/us-thinktank-billionaires-supreme-court-wealth-tax-lobbying"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 backdoor attempt}}}\uc2  to ban future wealth taxes.\par \par \uc2 The case, Moore v United States, put into question what assets are considered taxable income. The couple argued the tax was unconstitutional because they didn\u8217\'20\'19t receive any cash from the investment, but the court ultimately agreed with the government that the investment was a form of income.\par \par \uc2 ***\par \par \uc2 Federal ban on \u8216\'20\'18bump stock\u8217\'20\'19 devices for guns struck down\par \par \uc2 Decided 6-3\par \par \uc2 Conservative bloc\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Alito \u8211\'20\'13 Majority\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Barrett \u8211\'20\'13 Majority\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Gorsuch \u8211\'20\'13 Majority\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Kavanaugh \u8211\'20\'13 Majority\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Roberts \u8211\'20\'13 Majority\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Thomas \u8211\'20\'13 Majority\par \par \uc2 Liberal bloc\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Jackson \u8211\'20\'13 Minority\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Kagan \u8211\'20\'13 Minority\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Sotomayor \u8211\'20\'13 Minority\par \par \uc2 The court {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/ng-interactive/2024/jun/14/supreme-court-bump-stock-ban-decision"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 struck down a federal ban on \u8220\'20\'1Cbump stocks\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2 , the devices that can vamp up semiautomatic firearms to discharge ammunition almost as rapidly as machine guns and that have been behind some of the most devastating mass shootings in recent history.\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.supremecourt.gov/opinions/23pdf/22-976_e29g.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ruling}}}\uc2 , in Garland v Cargill, was 6-3, with the court\u8217\'20\'19s liberal justices dissenting from the conservative majority\u8217\'20\'19s decision. Writing for the majority, Justice \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2  said that a semiautomatic firearm equipped with a bump stock did not meet the definition of a machine gun; machine guns are subject to stricter regulations.\par \par \uc2 ***\par \par \uc2 Court upholds access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill mifepristone\par \par \uc2 Decided 9-0\par \par \uc2 Conservative bloc\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Alito \u8211\'20\'13 Majority\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Barrett \u8211\'20\'13 Majority\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Gorsuch \u8211\'20\'13 Majority\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Kavanaugh \u8211\'20\'13 Majority\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Roberts \u8211\'20\'13 Majority\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Thomas \u8211\'20\'13 Majority\par \par \uc2 Liberal bloc\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Jackson \u8211\'20\'13 Majority\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Kagan \u8211\'20\'13 Majority\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Sotomayor \u8211\'20\'13 Majority\par \par \uc2 The availability of a common {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  pill will remain unchanged, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/jun/13/supreme-court-abortion-pill-access"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the court ruled in a unanimous 9-0 decision}}}\uc2 , handing a major victory to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights supporters who feared that the court that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jun/24/roe-v-wade-overturned-abortion-summary-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 overturned}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Roe v Wade}}}\uc2  just two years ago would further hack away at access to the procedure.\par \par \uc2 The case, FDA v Alliance for Hippocratic Medicine, dealt with the \uc2 FDA\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s ability to regulate mifepristone, one of two drugs typically used in medication abortions, which now make up more than 60% of all US abortions and have become a major target of anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  activists. A coalition of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  opponents had tried to persuade the supreme court to roll back a series of moves by the \uc2 FDA\uc2  to expand access to the drug, such as allowing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers to mail mifepristone to patients.\par \par \uc2 ***\par \par \uc2 South Carolina doesn\u8217\'20\'19t need to redraw congressional map to consider Black voters\par \par \uc2 Decided 6-3\par \par \uc2 Conservative bloc\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Alito \u8211\'20\'13 Majority\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Barrett \u8211\'20\'13 Majority\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Gorsuch \u8211\'20\'13 Majority\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Kavanaugh \u8211\'20\'13 Majority\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Roberts \u8211\'20\'13 Majority\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Thomas \u8211\'20\'13 Majority\par \par \uc2 Liberal bloc\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Jackson \u8211\'20\'13 Minority\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Kagan \u8211\'20\'13 Minority\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Sotomayor \u8211\'20\'13 Minority\par \par \uc2 The court ruled that South Carolina Republicans {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/article/2024/may/23/south-carolina-redistricting-case-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 do not need to redraw their congressional map}}}\uc2 , deciding that a lower court had not properly evaluated the evidence when it ruled that the lawmakers had discriminated against Black voters.\par \par \uc2 In a 6-3 decision, the justices sent the case back to the lower court for further consideration. The ruling, in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/oct/11/supreme-court-south-carolina-congressional-map-case"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Alexander v South Carolina Conference of the NAACP}}}\uc2 , is a major win for Republicans, who hold a slim margin in the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/house-of-representatives"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US House}}}\uc2  with six of South Carolina\u8217\'20\'19s seven congressional seats. It also could give lawmakers more leeway to discriminate in redistricting and use partisanship as a proxy for race. That could be enormously powerful in the US south, where voting is often racially polarized.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240701ek71002s5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
