\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Biden acknowledges shaky debate performance and vows to stay in race: \u8216\'20\'18when you get knocked down, you get back up\u8217\'20\'19 \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Chris Stein (now), with L\u233\'00\'E9onie Chao-Fong, Martin Belam, Helen Sullivan and Maanvi Singh (earlier) \par \uc2 26,323 \uc2 words\par \uc2 28 June 2024\par 20:21 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 This live blog is now closed. For the latest on the US election, you can read our full coverage here.Defiant Biden resists call to drop out as campaign surrogates maintain supportExplainer: Who could replace \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 ? Here are six possibilities\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.04pm BST\par \par \uc2 Closing summary\par \par \uc2 Last night, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and \uc2 Donald Trump{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jun/27/presidential-debate-trump-biden-updates?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-667e0ac08f086bfb3f8efb60#block-667e0ac08f086bfb3f8efb60"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 took to the debate stage}}}\uc2  at CNN studios in Atlanta, looking to break through in a presidential race where polls have for months shown a close contest. While we can\u8217\'20\'19t quite say that Trump achieved that, Biden {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jun/27/presidential-debate-trump-biden-updates?page=with:block-667e26118f081d94ff3d16ba#block-667e26118f081d94ff3d16ba"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 certainly did not}}}\uc2 . The president struggled to land his lines, seemed to stare into space while Trump spoke, and had a cough that marred his answers. It served to further heighten already prominent concerns among voters about the 81-year-old\u8217\'20\'19s ability to do the job, and sparked a panic among Democrats. In the hours after the debate finished, even Biden\u8217\'20\'19s allies {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jun/27/presidential-debate-trump-biden-updates?page=with:block-667ea01d8f086bfb3f8f00f0#block-667ea01d8f086bfb3f8f00f0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 openly wondered}}}\uc2  if the party wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t be better off replacing him, despite the fact that it would be historically short notice. At {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jun/27/presidential-debate-trump-biden-updates?page=with:block-667eedef8f081d94ff3d20fa#block-667eedef8f081d94ff3d20fa"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a rally in North Carolina}}}\uc2  today, a comparatively energetic Biden seemed to acknowledge his poor debate performance, but told the crowd, \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jun/27/presidential-debate-trump-biden-updates?page=with:block-667ef3f58f081787dccaab67#block-667ef3f58f081787dccaab67"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 when you get knocked down, you get back up}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D. In the weeks to come, we\u8217\'20\'19ll see if voters think he can do that.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more about what happened today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Biden{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jun/27/presidential-debate-trump-biden-updates?page=with:block-667eb8148f081787dccaa76f#block-667eb8148f081787dccaa76f"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reportedly}}}\uc2  still plans to participate in a second debate with Trump in September.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The supreme court{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jun/27/presidential-debate-trump-biden-updates?page=with:block-667ed0368f081787dccaa958#block-667ed0368f081787dccaa958"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 will almost certainly}}}\uc2  rule on Trump\u8217\'20\'19s petition for immunity from prosecution for trying to overturn the 2020 election on Monday.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A Biden campaign official{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jun/27/presidential-debate-trump-biden-updates?page=with:block-667f0d0f8f086bfb3f8f077b#block-667f0d0f8f086bfb3f8f077b"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 tried to prevent}}}\uc2  a \uc2 New York Times\uc2  reporter at a \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  event from hearing critical comments from voters about the president\u8217\'20\'19s debate performance.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Mike Johnson, the Republican House speaker and Trump ally, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jun/27/presidential-debate-trump-biden-updates?page=with:block-667ec4e78f086bfb3f8f0320#block-667ec4e78f086bfb3f8f0320"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 called}}}\uc2  last night \u8220\'20\'1Cthe greatest mismatch in the history of presidential debates\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Bad debate nights happen\u8217\'20\'19 \u8211\'20\'13 so {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jun/27/presidential-debate-trump-biden-updates?page=with:block-667f07b38f081d94ff3d2245#block-667f07b38f081d94ff3d2245"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 says}}}\uc2 Barack Obama, who had at least one rough go at it during his presidency.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.49pm BST\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  was among the issues debated by \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  last night, with the Democratic president attempting to channel voters\u8217\'20\'19 frustration at the fall of Roe v Wade against his Republican adversary.\par \par \uc2 This morning, Iowa\u8217\'20\'19s supreme court allowed a six-week ban on the procedure to go into effect, making it the latest Republican-led state to cut off access at a point when many women do not yet know they are pregnant.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what Biden had to say about that, in a statement distributed by the White House:\par \par \uc2 This should never happen in America. Yet, this is exactly what is happening in states across the country since the supreme court overturned Roe v Wade. And it\u8217\'20\'19s not stopping at the state level \u8211\'20\'13 Republican elected officials in Congress have proposed four national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans while refusing to protect nationwide access to IVF and contraception.\par \par \uc2 Vice-President Harris and I believe that women in every state must have the right to make deeply personal decisions about their health. We will continue to call on Congress to restore the protections of Roe v Wade in federal law and stand firm against efforts made by Republican elected officials to undermine Americans\u8217\'20\'19 fundamental freedoms.\par \par \uc2 And here\u8217\'20\'19s more on the court\u8217\'20\'19s ruling:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jun/28/iowa-supreme-court-abortion-ban"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Iowa supreme court allows six-week \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  ban to take effect}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.34pm BST\par \par \uc2 Nevada campaign official blocks reporter from hearing voters' criticism of Biden debate\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is rallying voters this afternoon in Las Vegas, Nevada a critical swing state where polls have lately shown \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  trailing \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 As is often the case when the vice-president travels, she is joined by a pool of reporters, including Simon J. Levien of the \uc2 New York Times\uc2 , who distribute details of their travels to other outlets, through mailing lists maintained by the White House.\par \par \uc2 In his latest report, Levien said he was trying to interview attendees at the event prior to Harris\u8217\'20\'19s speech, but in two instances when someone would express a critical view of the president\u8217\'20\'19s performance at his debate last night, Clio Calvo-Platero, the deputy communications director for Biden\u8217\'20\'19s campaign in the state, would try to stop the interview.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s how Levien said it went:\par \par \uc2 Calvo-Platero followed your pooler as he interviewed voters and recorded the interviews.\par \par \uc2 Twice she tried to end the interviews when the voters began to criticize Biden.\par \par \uc2 Democratic voter Amy Nelson said that the debate was \u8220\'20\'1Cterrible.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou can\u8217\'20\'19t tell me that there\u8217\'20\'19s not anyone better \u8212\'20\'14\u8221\'20\'1D Nelson said, hoping there was another candidate who could take his place.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re at a \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  event, so I\u8217\'20\'19m going to cut you off there, sorry,\u8221\'20\'1D Calvo-Platero said before Nelson finished her statement.\par \par \uc2 Stephen Stubbs, an undecided voter, criticized Mr. Biden\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cmental acuity.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWho\u8217\'20\'19s running the country?\u8221\'20\'1D Stubbs recalled saying after watching the presidential debate. \u8220\'20\'1CLet Kamala in!\u8221\'20\'1D he added, hoping Biden would step down and nominate Harris as president.\par \par \uc2 Calvo-Platero said \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m going to stop it here, sorry. If I can, it\u8217\'20\'19s a Biden event. Is that okay?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.18pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s fellow Democrats are downplaying the president\u8217\'20\'19s stumbles in the debate last night, but government officials at top American allies are less sanguine, the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/patrickwintour"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Patrick Wintour}}}\uc2  reports:\par \par \uc2 European politicians, already drowning in multiple crises of their own, were left shell-shocked and aghast at \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s meandering performance in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jun/28/biden-trump-first-presidential-debate"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Thursday\u8217\'20\'19s presidential debate}}}\uc2 , aware that a second Trump term had drawn that much nearer \u8211\'20\'13 with all that this implies for the rise of populism in the continent, the future of Nato, and for Ukraine and the Middle East.\par \par \uc2 The voices of despair came from across the mainstream political spectrum, interspersed with the odd call for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/europe-news"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Europe}}}\uc2  to prepare even more intensively for a Trump second coming.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAmerican democracy killed before our eyes by gerontocracy,\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 Guy Verhofstadt\uc2 , a member of the European parliament and a former prime minister of Belgium, posted on X.\par \par \uc2 The German CDU foreign policy specialist \uc2 Norbert R\u246\'00\'F6ttgen\uc2  said: \u8220\'20\'1CThis night will not be forgotten. The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/democrats"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Democrats}}}\uc2  have to rethink their choices now. And Germany must prepare at full speed for an uncertain future. If we don\u8217\'20\'19t take responsibility for European security now, no one will.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The Polish foreign minister, Radek Sikorski, issued the most delphic advice about the importance of planning succession. \u8220\'20\'1CMarcus Aurelius was a great emperor but he screwed up his succession by passing the baton to his feckless son Commodus (he from the Gladiator). Whose disastrous rule started Rome\u8217\'20\'19s decline. It\u8217\'20\'19s important to manage one\u8217\'20\'19s ride into the sunset.\u8221\'20\'1D Whether Barack Obama or Biden was cast in the role of Aurelius was unclear.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jun/28/western-politicians-shocked-joe-biden-us-presidential-debate"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Biden can\u8217\'20\'19t do it\u8217\'20\'19: European politicians shocked by US president\u8217\'20\'19s debate flop}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.27pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 Obama after Biden's performance in Atlanta: 'Bad debate nights happen'\par \par \uc2 In a post on X, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s former boss \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  downplayed the importance of his struggles on the debate stage last night:\par \par \uc2 enltrBad debate nights happen. Trust me, I know. But this election is still a choice between someone who has fought for ordinary folks his entire life and someone who only cares about himself. Between someone who tells the truth; who knows right from wrong and will give it to the\u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Barack Obama (@BarackObama) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/BarackObama/status/1806758633230709017?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 28, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 Indeed, Obama knows what he\u8217\'20\'19s talking about when it comes to underperforming in debates as an incumbent president:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2012/oct/04/romney-obama-first-presidential-debate"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Mitt Romney comes out on top as Obama stumbles in first debate}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.09pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.37pm BST\par \par \uc2 After last night\u8217\'20\'19s debate, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s official account on X shared video clips mocking \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , and of the president speaking to supporters in Atlanta.\par \par \uc2 Tellingly, they published nothing showing Biden on the CNN stage, but they\u8217\'20\'19ve now shared a couple clips of his speech this afternoon to supporters in Raleigh. If you caught the debate last night, they\u8217\'20\'19re worth watching, as they show a very different president than the one at the debate.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s the part where he attacks Trump for lying:\par \par \uc2 enltrDonald Trump lied about how great he was for veterans.\par \par \uc2 He called them "suckers and losers."\par \par \uc2 My son was one of those people. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/vUMFbVJgWr"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/vUMFbVJgWr}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  (@JoeBiden) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JoeBiden/status/1806743354316562856?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 28, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 And where Biden dismisses him as having \u8220\'20\'1Cthe morals of an alley cat\u8221\'20\'1D:\par \par \uc2 enltrIn this election, your freedom, your democracy, and America itself is at stake. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/D5ajgd5obp"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/D5ajgd5obp}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  (@JoeBiden) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JoeBiden/status/1806744069147668719?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 28, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.50pm BST\par \par \uc2 The White House pool reporter following Biden says that he was interrupted four times by pro-Palestinian protesters.\par \par \uc2 The president managed to shake off their interruptions and continue his speech, while the crowd drowned them out with chants of \u8220\'20\'1Cfour more years!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 His staff has generally managed to keep such protesters out of Biden\u8217\'20\'19s speeches in recent months, after he was interrupted repeatedly at the start of the year. Nonetheless, opposition to his support for Israel in its war on Gaza is another issue that could sap his support in crucial states. Here\u8217\'20\'19s more on that:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/14/biden-israel-backing-israel-democrats"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Biden\u8217\'20\'19s renewed embrace of Israel threatens to deepen Democratic divide}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.56pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.41pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden is now walking offstage with the first lady as Tom Petty\u8217\'20\'19s I won\u8217\'20\'19t back down plays.\par \par \uc2 Despite dealing with a cough and several interruptions by who appeared to be protesters, Biden pulled off a notably forceful speech that was a far cry from his performance on the debate stage in Atlanta just hours before.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.07pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.37pm BST\par \par \uc2 'When you get knocked down, you get back up': Biden tells supporters after shaky debate performance\par \par \uc2 In comments that came as close as any to addressing his stumbles against Trump in last night\u8217\'20\'19s debate, Biden acknowledged that he is indeed old, but believes he can still beat the former president in the November election.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI know I\u8217\'20\'19m not a young man, to the state the obvious. Well, I know I don\u8217\'20\'19t walk as easy as I used to, I don\u8217\'20\'19t speak as smoothly as I used to, I don\u8217\'20\'19t debate as well as I used to, but I know what I do know. I know how to tell the truth,\u8221\'20\'1D the president said.\par \par \uc2 He went on:\par \par \uc2 I know right from wrong. I know how to do this job. I know how to get things done. I know, like millions of Americans, I know, when you get knocked down, you get back up.\par \par \uc2 Biden then made plain that he believed he can still do the job:\par \par \uc2 Folks, I give you my word as a Biden, I would not be running again if I didn\u8217\'20\'19t believe with all my heart and soul I can do this job. Because, quite frankly, the stakes are too high.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.55pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.30pm BST\par \par \uc2 Crowd chants 'lock him up' as Biden calls Trump a 'one-man crime wave'\par \par \uc2 Biden laid into Trump over his many legal troubles, calling him a \u8220\'20\'1Cone-man crime wave\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 and prompting the Democratic crowd to chant \u8220\'20\'1Clock him up!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 It harkens {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2016/oct/10/debate-donald-trump-threatens-to-jail-hillary-clinton"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 back to 2016}}}\uc2 , when crowds at Trump rallies chanted \u8220\'20\'1Clock her up\u8221\'20\'1D as he attacked his Democratic opponent \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2  for various alleged violations of the law.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe only convicted criminal on stage last night was \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhen I thought about his 34 felony convictions, his sexual assault on a woman in a public place and his being fined $400m for business fraud, I thought to myself, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  isn\u8217\'20\'19t just a convicted felon. \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is a one-man crime wave.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CLock him up! Lock him up!\u8221\'20\'1D the crowd chanted.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.34pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.26pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden says Trump set 'a new record for the most lies told in a single debate'\par \par \uc2 Biden has now shifted to last night\u8217\'20\'19s debate, and is attacking Trump for telling what was, in the president\u8217\'20\'19s view, a record number of lies.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CDid you see Trump last night? \u8230\'20\'26 It\u8217\'20\'19s sincerely a new record for the most lies told in a single debate,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said.\par \par \uc2 He continued the attack:\par \par \uc2 He lied about the great economy he created. He lied about the pandemic he botched, killing millions of people. He closed businesses, he closed schools, losing their homes, people all over this country. America was flat on its back, so I told Trump that it was just one of two presidents in American history who left office at fewer jobs than he started. Herbert Hoover was the other one. That\u8217\'20\'19s why I called him Donald Herbert Hoover Trump.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.29pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.23pm BST\par \par \uc2 The president is going through his staple campaign promises.\par \par \uc2 And though he\u8217\'20\'19s occasionally coughing, and seems to have been interrupted by protesters at least twice, Biden is generally nailing his lines \u8211\'20\'13 something he repeatedly struggled to do when Trump was standing to his right at CNN studios last night.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re going to provide clean drinking water, affordable high-speed internet, quality education for every child in America. We\u8217\'20\'19re going to secure our border and protect legal immigration,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said.\par \par \uc2 And then a sentence delivered with particular force: \u8220\'20\'1CUnlike the other guy, we\u8217\'20\'19re going to stand up to dictators like Putin because America bows to no one, no one, no one ever.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden is at the podium, and greeted the crowd heartily.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThank you, North Carolina!\u8221\'20\'1D the president bellowed.\par \par \uc2 Where was this energy last night? On the debate stage he appeared subdued, and often gave crowded answers to Trump or the moderators\u8217\'20\'19 questions. But at this speech so far, he seems more spirited.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.30pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.17pm BST\par \par \uc2 Up next to introduce Biden is Eric Fitts, an educator in the Raleigh area.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CLast night, I watched with pride as President Biden won the debate and put forward \u8230\'20\'26 a clear vision for making life better for our families, and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  made it very clear he\u8217\'20\'19s focused on retribution and revenge,\u8221\'20\'1D Fitts said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBut what amazed me most was that President Biden that we saw last night on the debate stage was the same Joe I had the pleasure of sharing a meal with a few months ago, right in my home, my sons Christian and Carter, when we sat at my dinner table, I was able to share with him how grateful I was for his leadership and for his compassion.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.31pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.13pm BST\par \par \uc2 Jill Biden is introducing her husband, and implicitly downplaying concerns over his performance against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in last night\u8217\'20\'19s debate.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere is no one that I would rather have sitting in the Oval Office right now than my husband,\u8221\'20\'1D the first lady said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhat you saw last night on the debate stage was \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , a president with integrity and character, who told the truth. And \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  told lie after lie after lie.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.10pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden takes stage in North Carolina for first speech since debate against Trump\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is onstage now in Raleigh, North Carolina for his first campaign speech since his shaky performance last night in his debate against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Jill Biden is revving up the crowd before the president speaks. Don\u8217\'20\'19t go away \u8211\'20\'13 we\u8217\'20\'19re covering it live.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.04pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is once again late for his speech. As you wait, check out what the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/roberttait"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Robert Tait}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/edwardhelmore"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Edward Helmore}}}\uc2  have learned about how the president\u8217\'20\'19s campaign is dealing with the fallout from his debate last night:\par \par \uc2 A defiant {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/joebiden"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Joe Biden}}}\uc2  resisted calls to abandon his re-election effort and step aside for a younger candidate after his calamitous showing in Thursday\u8217\'20\'19s presidential debate with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 As {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/democrats"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Democrats}}}\uc2  panicked and openly talked about replacing the president with another nominee, the Biden campaign unequivocally ruled out that possibility.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COf course he\u8217\'20\'19s not dropping out,\u8221\'20\'1D Lauren Hitt, a campaign spokesperson, said on Friday.\par \par \uc2 Her statement followed Biden\u8217\'20\'19s own resolute comments to downcast supporters shortly after leaving the debate stage in Atlanta. \u8220\'20\'1CLet\u8217\'20\'19s keep going,\u8221\'20\'1D he told them.\par \par \uc2 Biden was also said to be planning to return to the debate stage as planned in September, CNN reported on Friday morning, citing an adviser.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jun/28/debate-replace-biden-drop-out"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Defiant Biden resists call to drop out as campaign surrogates maintain support}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.05pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.46pm BST\par \par \uc2 As we wait for Biden to speak, the \uc2 Washington Post\uc2  reports that \uc2 Jim Clyburn\uc2 , a longtime Democratic congressman from South Carolina who is influential with the president, believes there is no reason for him to exit the race:\par \par \uc2 enltrRep. \uc2 Jim Clyburn\uc2  said he plans to speak to Biden today and tell him to \u8220\'20\'1Cstay the course.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He said \u8220\'20\'1Cthere\u8217\'20\'19s no better Democrat\u8221\'20\'1D and directed nervous Democrats to \u8220\'20\'1Cchill out.\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/QccH95699n"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/QccH95699n}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Dylan Wells (@dylanewells) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/dylanewells/status/1806726066020503925?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 28, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 Clyburn played a crucial role in re-energizing Biden\u8217\'20\'19s campaign in 2020, when the candidate\u8217\'20\'19s support in the Democratic primaries was flagging:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2020/mar/04/joe-biden-jim-clyburn-endorsement-super-tuesday"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18A chain reaction\u8217\'20\'19: how one endorsement set Joe Biden\u8217\'20\'19s surge in motion}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.24pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden to rally in North Carolina amid Democratic panic over debate performance\par \par \uc2 Hours after his debate with \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  went far worse than expected and made Democrats nationwide even more concerned about his ability to campaign for the presidency at the age of 81, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is set to rally supporters in Raleigh, North Carolina, at 12.30pm ET.\par \par \uc2 Biden is hoping to win the southern state in the November election, but it\u8217\'20\'19s been tough territory for Democrats lately \u8211\'20\'13 their Senate candidates have repeatedly lost, Biden is down against Trump in polls of state voters, and Republicans have taken over the state legislature and curbed Democratic governor Roy Cooper \u8217\'20\'19s power.\par \par \uc2 When he takes the stage, all eyes will, once again, be on how Biden talks and acts, after he repeatedly struggled to articulate his arguments against Trump at the debate at CNN\u8217\'20\'19s studios in Atlanta last night.\par \par \uc2 An energetic performance could bolster the argument that the president was just having a bad day, albeit at an incredibly important moment. But if he falters onstage in Raleigh, it could heighten his supporters\u8217\'20\'19 anxiety, and give more ammunition to those who argue he must pass the baton to another candidate, if Trump is to be stopped.\par \par \uc2 Don\u8217\'20\'19t close your browser tab \u8211\'20\'13 we\u8217\'20\'19ll be covering the speech live on this blog.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.27pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.02pm BST\par \par \uc2 Plenty of Americans did not watch last night\u8217\'20\'19s presidential debate, and did not personally witness \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s struggles, or \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s incessant lying and distorting. But many in that group are no doubt digesting headlines from news outlets, indicating the debate did not go well for the president. Here\u8217\'20\'19s more about that, from the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/edwardhelmore"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Edward Helmore}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 US voters woke up to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jun/27/biden-trump-debate-democrats-reaction"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 post-debate reviews}}}\uc2  of the first {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jun/27/biden-trump-presidential-debate-atlanta"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Biden-Trump debate}}}\uc2  with headlines that echoed {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jun/28/biden-trump-first-presidential-debate"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 anxiety}}}\uc2  that the incumbent president is too cognitively weak and physically frail to sustain another five months of political campaigning or another term in office.\par \par \uc2 Those anxieties, multiple outlets reported, were being reflected in pressure from Democratic donors and former Democratic officials who are now openly talking about {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jun/28/who-could-replace-joe-biden-here-are-six-possibilities"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 replacing Biden}}}\uc2  with an alternative presidential candidate at the party\u8217\'20\'19s convention in Chicago in August.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CA Fumbling Performance, and a Panicking Party\u8221\'20\'1D, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2024/06/27/us/politics/biden-debate-democrats.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said the New York Times}}}\uc2  on its front page. Columnist Nicholas Kristof, a centrist Democrat, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2024/06/25/opinion/joe-biden-drop-out.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  that Biden is a \u8220\'20\'1Cgood man\u8221\'20\'1D who had capped his political career with a successful presidential term \u8230\'20\'26 \u8220\'20\'1Cbut I hope he reviews his debate performance Thursday evening and withdraws from the race\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Kristof floated \uc2 Gretchen Whitmer\uc2 , the governor of Michigan, Senator \uc2 Sherrod Brown\uc2  of Ohio and \uc2 Gina Raimondo\uc2 , the US secretary of commerce, as potential candidates \u8220\'20\'1Cin a good position to defeat Trump in November\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jun/28/trump-biden-debate-reaction"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'1810 minutes to destroy a presidency\u8217\'20\'19: how US and global media reviewed the Biden-Trump debate}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.26pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.40pm BST\par \par \uc2 The clever folks at Politico {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2024/06/28/biden-trump-debate-nursing-home-reaction-00165726"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 dispatched a reporter}}}\uc2  to a nursing home to find out what its residents thought of last night\u8217\'20\'19s debate against two historically old candidates.\par \par \uc2 They had plenty of thoughts about \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s troubling performance, as well as how \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  behaved. Here\u8217\'20\'19s a snippet:\par \par \uc2 When Biden, 81, appeared to lose his train of thought and said, inexplicably, \u8220\'20\'1CWe finally beat Medicare,\u8221\'20\'1D Goldberg put her head in her hands again.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe finally beat Medicare?\u8221\'20\'1D she asked.\par \par \uc2 For Biden, it was a disaster. His allies had seen the debate as his best chance yet to ease concerns about his age, a persistent liability for his campaign. And the perception of older voters \u8211\'20\'13 who {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.aarp.org/politics-society/government-elections/info-2018/power-role-older-voters.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 turn up to vote}}}\uc2  at higher levels any other age group \u8211\'20\'13 is critical to the Democratic president. He {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/election/2020/exit-polls/president/national-results"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 lost voters 65 and older to Donald Trump by 5 percentage points in 2020}}}\uc2 , but is courting them aggressively in the run-up to November.\par \par \uc2 Nothing his contemporaries saw here Thursday helped his case.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI think that he is rushing it, and he\u8217\'20\'19s not looking at the camera for the most part,\u8221\'20\'1D said Meg Maguire, 81, who was visiting the facility to watch the debate with her husband.\par \par \uc2 She said, \u8220\'20\'1CIn terms of just physical relationship to the camera, Trump is doing better,\u8221\'20\'1D even if, as she put it, \u8220\'20\'1CTrump says garbage.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI do think Biden\u8217\'20\'19s age is showing at this debate, and it pains me,\u8221\'20\'1D she added.\par \par \uc2 Goldberg agreed. \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t like to see [Biden\u8217\'20\'19s] gaffes, but I don\u8217\'20\'19t like to see Trump going haywire and cockamamie either,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.49pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.19pm BST\par \par \uc2 Much like the rest of last night\u8217\'20\'19s often excruciating debate, the section devoted to the climate crisis struggled to stay on topic and was riddled with falsehoods.\par \par \uc2 It was an hour into the debate before \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  were asked about global heating, arguably the greatest challenge ever faced by humans, and Trump initially refused to answer, instead going on a lengthy monologue about Black people and immigration.\par \par \uc2 Eventually pressed for his climate policies, Trump said he wants \u8220\'20\'1Cabsolutely immaculate, clean water. I want absolutely clean air.\u8221\'20\'1D He added \u8220\'20\'1Cwe had it, we had H 20\u8221\'20\'1D and that his administration oversaw the \u8220\'20\'1Cbest environmental numbers ever\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s unclear what \u8220\'20\'1Cenvironmental numbers\u8221\'20\'1D he\u8217\'20\'19s referring to but, while he was president, Trump {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2020/oct/20/trump-us-dirtier-planet-warmer-75-ways"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 eviscerated}}}\uc2  dozens of clean air and water regulations and strived to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2019/jun/19/trump-climate-crisis-coal-pollution-clean-power-plan"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 bolster}}}\uc2  polluting industries. During this campaign, he has asked the oil and gas industry {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/may/16/donald-trump-big-oil-executives-alleged-deal-explained"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 for donations in return for deleting Biden\u8217\'20\'19s climate policies}}}\uc2 , should he return to the White House.\par \par \uc2 Trump has also vowed to remove the US, again, from the Paris climate accords, which he called a \u8220\'20\'1Cripoff\u8221\'20\'1D and a \u8220\'20\'1Cdisaster\u8221\'20\'1D during the debate. He also claimed the deal cost the US \u8220\'20\'1Ca trillion dollars\u8221\'20\'1D, a baseless assertion.\par \par \uc2 Biden, in response, said that he\u8217\'20\'19d {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/11/biden-climate-bill-inflation-reduction-act"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 passed}}}\uc2  the \u8220\'20\'1Cmost extensive \u8230\'20\'26 climate change legislation in history\u8221\'20\'1D and directly attacked Trump. \u8220\'20\'1CThe only existential threat to humanity is climate change, he didn\u8217\'20\'19t do a damn thing about it and he wants to undo all that I\u8217\'20\'19ve done,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said.\par \par \uc2 Environmental groups were left underwhelmed by the paucity of discussion on climate change, although the differences between Trump and Biden were still starkly apparent.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTonight put on full display how broken our political system is,\u8221\'20\'1D said Stevie O\u8217\'20\'19Hanlon, communications director of the youth-led Sunrise climate group. \u8220\'20\'1COur generation deserves better.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C The debate also made it undeniable that a Trump presidency would be a climate catastrophe.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.22pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.04pm BST\par \par \uc2 Supreme court set to rule on Trump immunity claim on Monday, finds in favor of January 6 rioter in case with wide implications\par \par \uc2 The supreme court has finished issuing its opinions for the day, but did not rule on \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s petition for immunity from charges related to trying to overturn the 2020 election.\par \par \uc2 However, the court announced it will issue more decisions on Monday \u8211\'20\'13 making it certain that the decision on Trump\u8217\'20\'19s fate will be handed down that day.\par \par \uc2 Before it wrapped up, the justices ruled on a case involving a January 6 rioter that could have broad implications for prosecutions related to the attack. Our live blog will tell you more about that:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jun/28/supreme-court-trump-immunity-latest-updates"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US supreme court rules for January 6 rioter challenging obstruction charge \u8211\'20\'13 live}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.05pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.47pm BST\par \par \uc2 Rightwing Republican congressman Chip Roy is leaning into the anxiety consuming Democrats over \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s debate performance last night.\par \par \uc2 He announced this morning that he will propose a resolution asking \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  to attempt to replace Biden as president:\par \par \uc2 enltrI intend to put forth a resolution calling upon the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/VP?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @VP}}}\uc2  to immediately use her powers under section 4 of the 25th Amendment to convene & mobilize the principal officers of the Cabinet to declare the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/POTUS?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @POTUS}}}\uc2  is unable to successfully discharge the duties and powers of his office.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Chip Roy (@chiproytx) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/chiproytx/status/1806680556828082213?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 28, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 It is unclear if this will pass the Republican-dominated House of Representatives, and even if it does, Harris can probably ignore it.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.28pm BST\par \par \uc2 Supreme court's conservatives hand down rulings punishing unhoused, upending federal regulations\par \par \uc2 As we speak, the supreme court is issuing more opinions, and the two that have come out so far have seen its conservative supermajority green-light penalties for people who sleep outside, and overturn a decades-old doctrine dealing with federal regulations that may have reverberations across the country.\par \par \uc2 They\u8217\'20\'19re not yet done for the day, and among the cases they could still rule on is \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s petition for immunity from prosecution for trying to overturn the 2020 election. Follow our supreme court live blog for the latest:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jun/28/supreme-court-trump-immunity-latest-updates"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US supreme court rules 6-3 that unhoused people sleeping outside can be punished \u8211\'20\'13 live}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.45pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.16pm BST\par \par \uc2 Republican House speaker Johnson cheers 'greatest mismatch in the history of presidential debates'\par \par \uc2 Mike Johnson, the Republican speaker of the House and a top ally of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , went in for the kill after \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  stumbled through his parlay with the former president, calling it \u8220\'20\'1Cthe greatest mismatch in the history of presidential debates\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 In an interview with Fox News, he also implied that America\u8217\'20\'19s enemies would interpret Biden\u8217\'20\'19s debate performance as a sign of weakness when it comes to national security:\par \par \uc2 It was sad to watch it. This is dangerous to put this on display for the country. We\u8217\'20\'19re all concerned about this because our adversaries see this as well. We\u8217\'20\'19re in a dangerous moment. We\u8217\'20\'19ve got China, Russia, Iran, North Korea forming a new axis of evil making threats to us and our allies. We can\u8217\'20\'19t afford to have this on the world stage. The only solace we have is that help is on the way. November can\u8217\'20\'19t get here soon enough.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.21pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.58pm BST\par \par \uc2 Minnesota congressman \uc2 Dean Phillips\uc2 , who ran against \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  in the Democratic primary, had just a few words in response to last night\u8217\'20\'19s debate performance:\par \par \uc2 enltrSpeak only if it improves upon the silence. -Gandhi\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Dean Phillips\uc2  (@deanbphillips) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/deanbphillips/status/1806675141352436059?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 28, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.51pm BST\par \par \uc2 Michigan governor \uc2 Gretchen Whitmer\uc2 , who is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jun/28/who-could-replace-joe-biden-here-are-six-possibilities"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 being touted as a possible Biden replacement}}}\uc2  on the Democratic ticket, has defended the president in a statement this morning that failed to mention last night\u8217\'20\'19s debate.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is running to serve the American people,\u8221\'20\'1D Whitmer said in her statement.\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is running to serve \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . The difference between \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s vision for making sure everyone in America has a fair shot and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s dangerous, self-serving plans will only get sharper as we head toward November.\par \par \uc2 From Politico\u8217\'20\'19s Jonathan Martin:\par \par \uc2 enltrWith some chatter speculating about Whitmer, she issues statement this am\u8230\'20\'26w pro Biden talkers and nothing about the elephant in room\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is running to serve the American people. \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is running to serve \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . The difference between \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s vision for\u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Jonathan Martin (@jmart) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/jmart/status/1806675100105642331?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 28, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.36pm BST\par \par \uc2 Pennsylvania governor Josh Shapiro, a Democrat, has spent the morning defending \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s debate performance.\par \par \uc2 Biden \u8220\'20\'1Chad a bad debate night,\u8221\'20\'1D Shapiro acknowledged on MSNBC\u8217\'20\'19s Morning Joe, \u8220\'20\'1Cbut it doesn\u8217\'20\'19t change the fact that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  was a bad president.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThat is what I took away from this debate,\u8221\'20\'1D he continued.\par \par \uc2 That\u8217\'20\'19s what I saw, and I think we still have a clear contrast in this race. Nothing about the debate changed that last night.\par \par \uc2 He added that he has worked closely with both Trump and Biden, \u8220\'20\'1Cand you know what I can tell you, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is up to the job.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden still plans to take part in second debate - report\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  still plans to participate in a second presidential debate in September, CNN is reporting, citing an adviser.\par \par \uc2 The adviser acknowledged that the president\u8217\'20\'19s performance on Thursday was \u8220\'20\'1Clackluster\u8221\'20\'1D but said the campaign is committed to highlighting the moments it believes worked for their candidate \u8212\'20\'14 and then moving on, the outlet states.\par \par \uc2 enltrNEW, as just reported on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/CNN?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @CNN}}}\uc2  : Not only does {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/POTUS?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @POTUS}}}\uc2  not plan to drop out, Biden remains committed to a second debate in September, an adviser tells me\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kayla Tausche (@kaylatausche) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/kaylatausche/status/1806675665845903645?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 28, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.15pm BST\par \par \uc2 Pennsylvania senator \uc2 John Fetterman\uc2  has told fellow Democrats to \u8220\'20\'1Cchill the fuck out\u8221\'20\'1D following reports that the party reacted with panic and dismay after \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s dismal performance on the debate stage.\par \par \uc2 Fetterman, who survived {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2022/oct/27/john-fetterman-dr-oz-pennsylvania-senate-midterms"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 his own disastrous debate }}}\uc2  ahead of the 2022, posted to X this morning:\par \par \uc2 I refuse to join the Democratic vultures on Biden\u8217\'20\'19s shoulder after the debate. No one knows more than me that a rough debate is not the sum total of the person and their record.\par \par \uc2 enltrI refuse to join the Democratic vultures on\par \par \uc2 Biden\u8217\'20\'19s shoulder after the debate.\par \par \uc2 No one knows more than me that a rough debate is not the sum total of the person and their record. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/NjWdUw5ugh"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/NjWdUw5ugh}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 John Fetterman\uc2  (@JohnFetterman) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JohnFetterman/status/1806658909052055762?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 28, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrMorning-after thermonuclear beat downs from my race from the debate and polling geniuses like 538 predicted l\u8217\'20\'19d lose by 2.\par \par \uc2 And what happened?\par \par \uc2 The only seat to flip and won by a historic margin (+5).\par \par \uc2 Chill the fuck out.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 John Fetterman\uc2  (@JohnFetterman) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JohnFetterman/status/1806658911119831457?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 28, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 Fetterman {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/oct/26/fetterman-oz-debate-democrats-pennsylvania-senate"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 struggled}}}\uc2  during his Senate debate with Mehmet Oz, which took place just months after he suffered a stroke.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.03pm BST\par \par \uc2 Hakeem Jeffries\uc2 , the Democratic House minority leader, has said \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  should not step aside after last night\u8217\'20\'19s debate.\par \par \uc2 From Fox News\u8217\'20\'19 Tyler Olson:\par \par \uc2 enltrJeffries to Fox on if Biden should step aside after the debate: \u8220\'20\'1CNo\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Tyler Olson (@TylerOlson1791) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/TylerOlson1791/status/1806672241200943498?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 28, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.49pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s debate performance was a \u8220\'20\'1Cnightmare\u8221\'20\'1D for his Democratic party, the Hill\u8217\'20\'19s Amie Parnes {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thehill.com/homenews/campaign/4745090-biden-debate-disaster-democrats-concerned/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wrote}}}\uc2 , citing one Biden ally who said: \u8220\'20\'1CI am watching us lose this election in slow motion.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Thursday night\u8217\'20\'19s performance sent shudders of anxiety through Democrats who fear a Biden loss could take down other candidates, the Hill\u8217\'20\'19s morning newsletter writes. One House Democrat from a swing state told the outlet:\par \par \uc2 Biden\u8217\'20\'19s team needs to convince him to withdraw and have an open convention.\par \par \uc2 Should Biden decide not to go for reelection in November after all, the Democratic National Convention in Chicago, which takes place 19-22 August, would have to nominate somebody else.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jun/27/presidential-debate-trump-biden-updates?page=with:block-667e6f398f081d94ff3d18e0#block-667e6f398f081d94ff3d18e0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 how Biden could be replaced,}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jun/27/presidential-debate-trump-biden-updates?page=with:block-667e732d8f086bfb3f8efe80#block-667e732d8f086bfb3f8efe80"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 who could replace him.}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.27pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Cstarted off poorly and he ended poorly,\u8221\'20\'1D Punchbowl News writes in its newsletter this morning, noting that Democrats must be \u8220\'20\'1Cvery alarmed\u8221\'20\'1D by the president\u8217\'20\'19s debate performance.\par \par \uc2 It was bad. Biden\u8217\'20\'19s answers were rambling, his voice was raspy and he committed repeated verbal flubs that will be clipped thousands of times between now and Election Day. Democrats wanted Biden to show voters that he\u8217\'20\'19s capable of serving another term. Many Democrats now fear they got the exact opposite.\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  wasn\u8217\'20\'19t great either, with \u8220\'20\'1Crambling, wildly unfocused\u8221\'20\'1D answers that were filled with falsehoods. But \u8220\'20\'1Cthe problem was that Biden was often unable to exploit Trump\u8217\'20\'19s false statements or distortions.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Tthe reality is this: No matter what Democrats say on the record today, they\u8217\'20\'19re privately alarmed and many will want Biden out. They\u8217\'20\'19re worried he will drag them down with him on Nov. 5.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.16pm BST\par \par \uc2 Winning a presidential debate is one thing, but coming out victorious in the meme wars is something else.\par \par \uc2 Both \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  understand how important it is to go viral. According to NBC News, Biden\u8217\'20\'19s campaign headquarters {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/2024-election/biden-campaign-digital-debate-strategy-boost-clips-thursday-rcna159148"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 enlisted}}}\uc2  18 influencers with a combined following of 8 million to post about the event, amounting to a \u8220\'20\'1Cpost-debate social media clip sharing battle\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Though Biden\u8217\'20\'19s voice grew stronger as the debate went on \u8211\'20\'13 a low bar, considering how weak he sounded at the start \u8211\'20\'13 it was impossible for viewers to ignore, especially as concerns about his age are a constant source of stress for Democrats this election.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19ve watched a lot of Biden talks. I\u8217\'20\'19ve never heard him sound this frail,\u8221\'20\'1D Vox correspondent Zack Beauchamp {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/zackbeauchamp/status/1806494228760998284"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wrote}}}\uc2  on X. \u8220\'20\'1CSomeone has to pull a fire alarm and help Biden out here,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/sunraysunray/status/1806497202467901674"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 writer}}}\uc2  Bhaskar Sunkara added, referencing \uc2 Jamaal Bowman\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/dec/07/jamaal-bowman-fire-alarm-censure"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 infamous congressional incident}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 X users wondered: did the president need a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/kyreetyree/status/1806497037514420444"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 cough drop}}}\uc2  ? An energy drink \u8211\'20\'13 maybe Panera\u8217\'20\'19s infamous {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/hunteryharris/status/1806500073527763318"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 charged lemonade}}}\uc2  ? What about the \u8220\'20\'1Csecret sauce\u8221\'20\'1D he posted a photo holding shortly before the debate, a canned water containing, according to the label, \u8220\'20\'1Czero malarky\u8221\'20\'1D? ( {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://shop.joebiden.com/dark-brandons-secret-sauce/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Actual cans}}}\uc2  later hit the Biden campaign\u8217\'20\'19s official store, costing $4.60 each.)\par \par \uc2 enltrI don't know what they've got in these performance enhancers, but I'm feeling pretty jacked up.\par \par \uc2 Try it yourselves, folks.\par \par \uc2 See you in a bit: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/vD3mL9slj1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/vD3mL9slj1}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/Li4EM9mzve"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/Li4EM9mzve}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  (@JoeBiden) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JoeBiden/status/1806486230084812937?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 28, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 On social media, people were obsessed with performance-enhancing drugs \u8211\'20\'13 and how it appeared that Biden needed to take some. \u8220\'20\'1CThe Adderall shortage is tearing this country apart and it has finally hit Biden,\u8221\'20\'1D read one {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/Papapishu/status/1806496135017881653"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 tweet}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CThey accidentally injected Biden with ketamine instead of adrenaline,\u8221\'20\'1D another {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/LolOverruled/status/1806495431746064455"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wrote}}}\uc2 . Some fantasized about feeding Biden Adderall through the TV screen.\par \par \uc2 enltrtrying to give joe an adderall through the tv {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/cd2Lp1OnpB"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/cd2Lp1OnpB}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Sean Morrow (@snmrrw) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/snmrrw/status/1806507500381880788?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 28, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.52pm BST\par \par \uc2 Calls for Biden to stand aside as surrogates double down in support\par \par \uc2 Possible contenders to replace \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  as the Democratic presidential nominee have doubled down on supporting him after a night in which there have been calls for the president to step aside from the 2024 election after a disappointing performance in the first TV debate of the campaign.\par \par \uc2 Democratic senator Claire McCaskill said on MSNBC that she was not sure \u8220\'20\'1Cif things can be done to fix this\u8221\'20\'1D after Biden appeared to have been bested by \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , who despite making numerous false claims nevertheless appeared to be the more coherent of the elderly perspective candidates.\par \par \uc2 Biden\u8217\'20\'19s voice at times sounded raspy, and at times he did not make sense, blurting out \u8220\'20\'1CWe finally beat Medicare\u8221\'20\'1D at one point. Trump regularly answered straightforward questions \u8211\'20\'13 about the economy, or \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , or the opioid crisis \u8211\'20\'13 with non sequiturs, but after the debate it was Democratic commentators who seemed most concerned about the potential impact on voters.\par \par \uc2 Maria Shriver, the former first lady of California, said she loves Biden, but that the evening was \u8220\'20\'1Cheartbreaking in many ways\u8221\'20\'1D and that there was \u8220\'20\'1Cpanic in the Democratic party\u8221\'20\'1D. David Plouffe, a Democratic strategist and former Obama campaign official, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jun/27/biden-trump-debate-democrats-reaction"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 called the debate \u8220\'20\'1Ckind of a Defcon 1 moment\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 There is no easy process in place to replace \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  at this late stage of the process, with him having triumphed mostly unopposed during the primaries and all set to be confirmed as the nominee at the Democratic National Convention in Chicago in August.\par \par \uc2 The only significant change would be if he were to voluntarily step aside, or even step down from the presidency.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jun/28/who-could-replace-joe-biden-here-are-six-possibilities"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Possible alternative names}}}\uc2  being touted include vice-president \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , and California governor \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2 . Michigan governor \uc2 Gretchen Whitmer\uc2 , Illinois governor \uc2 J B Pritzker\uc2  and veteran Ohio senator \uc2 Sherrod Brown\uc2  have also been mooted.\par \par \uc2 But at least on the night of the debate Harris and Newsom seemed foursquare behind the beleaguered president. Harris conceded Biden made \u8220\'20\'1Ca slow start\u8221\'20\'1D, saying \u8220\'20\'1CThat\u8217\'20\'19s obvious to everyone. I\u8217\'20\'19m not going to debate that point.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 However she went on to tell CNN that \u8220\'20\'1Cpeople can debate on style points but ultimately this election and who is the president of the US has to be about substance and the contrast is clear. \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  lied over and over and over again as he is want to do. He would not disavow what happened on January 6. He would not give a clear answer on whether he would stand by the election results.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Newsom said talk of changing nominee was \u8220\'20\'1Cnonsensical speculation\u8221\'20\'1D, adding \u8220\'20\'1CI will never turn my back on President Biden. Never turn my back on President Biden, I don\u8217\'20\'19t know a Democrat in my party that would do so.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.01pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.25pm BST\par \par \uc2 Incidentally \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is due to be campaigning later today in North Carolina. Vice-president \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is expected to be in Nevada.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.59am BST\par \par \uc2 Journalist Jake Sherman has posted to social media claiming to have had a lot of post-debate conversations with congressional Democrats. He writes:\par \par \uc2 Their sense isn\u8217\'20\'19t that this was a bad debate. It is much worse than that. In their view, Biden didn\u8217\'20\'19t even clear the lowest bar. They may agree with him on policy. But Biden wasn\u8217\'20\'19t even able to articulate what his policies are. For Democrats running down ballot, this is an incredibly serious problem.\par \par \uc2 enltrI\u8217\'20\'19ve had a lot of conversations in the last 7 hours with congressional democrats. Their sense isn\u8217\'20\'19t that this was a bad debate. It is much worse than that. In their view, Biden didn\u8217\'20\'19t even clear the lowest bar. They may agree with him on policy. But Biden wasn\u8217\'20\'19t even able to\u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Jake Sherman (@JakeSherman) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JakeSherman/status/1806630737413566706?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 28, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.37am BST\par \par \uc2 Writing for MSNBC, Hayes Brown states that Biden has less than three months to turn this performance around, but does not think it is a completely hopeless case. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.msnbc.com/politics/2024-election/live-blog/presidential-debate-trump-biden-live-updates-rcna157793#rcrd44648"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 He writes}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s clear that Biden\u8217\'20\'19s energy and capability is still there, as he warmed up throughout the night. He even seemed like an entirely different person in an appearance at an Atlanta watch party that MSNBC aired after the debate ended. The question is how to make sure that version of Biden is on full display throughout the remainder of the campaign, countering the image that may unfortunately be locked into many voters\u8217\'20\'19 minds now.\par \par \uc2 The answer may rest with reminding Americans that no matter what concerns they might have had about Biden\u8217\'20\'19s performance tonight, there was nothing that Trump did that made it seem like he is the better choice to return to the White House.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.20am BST\par \par \uc2 One of the odder bits of factchecking last night, via Glenn Kessler of the \uc2 Washington Post\uc2 , is whether \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  was being misleading to claim that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  had said people should inject bleach into their arms during the Covid pnademic. How did we get here? Anyway, to clear up the confusion, Kessler provides the full quote from Trump on 23 April 2020:\par \par \uc2 I see the disinfectant, where it knocks it out in one minute. And is there a way we can do something like that, by injection inside or almost a cleaning, because you see it gets in the lungs and it does a tremendous number on the lungs, so it\u8217\'20\'19d be interesting to check that, so that you\u8217\'20\'19re going to have to use medical doctors with, but it sounds interesting to me.\par \par \uc2 His verdict is that this does not appear to be Trump suggesting people should inject bleach, and that Biden was being misleading.\par \par \uc2 At the time, asked to clarify his comments the next day, the then-president insisted he had been \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2020/apr/24/trump-disinfectant-bleach-sarcastic"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 asking a question sarcastically}}}\uc2  to reporters like you just to see what would happen.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.45am BST\par \par \uc2 Guardian US columnist Rebecca Solnit has also delivered her verdict, saying the American people were the true losers last night:\par \par \uc2 Debates exist so that people can hear from the candidates, which makes sense when they\u8217\'20\'19re relative unknowns. We\u8217\'20\'19ve heard plenty from both of them for 40 years or so, since Biden was a young congressman and Trump was a young attention-seeker in New York City\u8217\'20\'19s nightclubs and tabloids, and both of them have had the most high-profile job on earth for four years.\par \par \uc2 We didn\u8217\'20\'19t need this debate. Because 2024 is not like previous election years, and the reasons it\u8217\'20\'19s not are both that each candidate has had plenty of time to show us who they are and because one of them is a criminal seeking to destroy democracy and human rights along with the climate, the economy and international alliances. If you are too young to remember 2017-2021, this would not help you figure that out.\par \par \uc2 Much has been said about the age of the candidates, but maybe it\u8217\'20\'19s the corporate media whose senility is most dangerous to us. Their insistence on proceeding as though things are pretty much what they\u8217\'20\'19ve always been, on normalizing the appalling and outrageous, on using false equivalencies and bothsiderism to make themselves look fair and reasonable, on turning politics into horseraces and personality contests, is aiding the destruction of the United States.\par \par \uc2 Read more from Rebecca Solnit here: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/article/2024/jun/28/debate-losers-american-people"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The true losers of this presidential debate were the American people}}}\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/article/2024/jun/28/debate-losers-american-people"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The true losers of this presidential debate were the American people | Rebecca Solnit}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.33am BST\par \par \uc2 Jess Bidgood, writing for the \uc2 New York Times\uc2  On Politics newsletter, summed it all up as \u8220\'20\'1CWell, that was ugly\u8221\'20\'1D and said the main takeaway was \u8220\'20\'1Cmostly, they fought about each other.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 She writes:\par \par \uc2 Both Biden and Trump are deeply unpopular, and voters have for months been telling pollsters that they did not want this rematch even as they sent the candidates to the top of the ticket. Watching the debate last night, as each cast the other as the reason that he is running again, it seemed clear that the two Americans who most want this rematch were standing onstage.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI wish he was a great president because I wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t be here right now. I\u8217\'20\'19d be at one of my many places enjoying myself,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said, adding, \u8220\'20\'1CThe only reason I\u8217\'20\'19m here is that he\u8217\'20\'19s so bad as a president\u8221\'20\'1D. Biden portrayed Trump as a unique threat to the country, castigating him in deeply personal terms and repeatedly calling him a liar. The deep enmity on display \u8211\'20\'13 and the messiness of the night \u8211\'20\'13 may have damaged them both.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.20am BST\par \par \uc2 David Smith\uc2  was in Atlanta for the Guardian, and this is his sketch of what was a terrible debate night for the Biden campaign:\par \par \uc2 That sickening thud you heard was jaws hitting the floor. That queasy sound you heard was hearts sinking into boots. That raspy noise you heard was a US president embodying what felt like the last gasp of the ailing republic. Say it ain\u8217\'20\'19t so, Joe.\par \par \uc2 The first US presidential debate in Atlanta on Thursday was the night that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/democrats"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Democrats}}}\uc2  went from \u8220\'20\'1CDon\u8217\'20\'19t panic!\u8221\'20\'1D to \u8220\'20\'1COK, time to panic!\u8221\'20\'1D After months of preparation and expectation, they got to the altar and suddenly realised they were marrying the wrong man.\par \par \uc2 In 90 miserable minutes, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  achieved two things that had seemed impossible. He lived down to expectations that were already rock bottom. And he managed to make {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  sound almost coherent. Trump did not win the debate but Biden certainly lost it.\par \par \uc2 Democrats had been lulled into a false sense of security by Biden\u8217\'20\'19s high energy performance at the State of the Union address. They expected Superman again. Instead they got Clark Kent in his dotage.\par \par \uc2 Read more of \uc2 David Smith\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s verdict here: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jun/28/biden-trump-first-presidential-debate"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18You\u8217\'20\'19re the sucker, you\u8217\'20\'19re the loser\u8217\'20\'19: 90 miserable minutes of Biden v Trump}}}\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jun/28/biden-trump-first-presidential-debate"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18You\u8217\'20\'19re the sucker, you\u8217\'20\'19re the loser\u8217\'20\'19: 90 miserable minutes of Biden v Trump}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.55am BST\par \par \uc2 Who could replace \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  as Democratic presidential nominee?\par \par \uc2 Should \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  decide not to go for reelection in November after all, the Democratic National Convention in Chicago, which takes place 19-22 August, would have to nominate somebody else. There isn\u8217\'20\'19t a clear frontrunner, but there would be some of the potential options.\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\par \par \uc2 The most obvious default pick would be Biden\u8217\'20\'19s vice-president. She has been widely criticised for not carving out her own role in the Biden administration and has poor polling approval ratings, suggesting she would struggle against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in the glare of an election campaign. The 59-year-old was backing Biden after the debate, but would also be maybe the easiest for the party to install as a replacement. She would automatically become president if Biden resigned from the White House, but that would not automatically make her the nominee.\par \par \uc2 Gavin Newsom\par \par \uc2 The 56-year-old California governor was in the spin room last night talking down any alternatives to Biden being the nominee, saying it was \u8220\'20\'1Cnonsensical speculation\u8221\'20\'1D. He had a primetime debate with Florida gov \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  last year, which could be a presidential match-up of the future, and has made a point of supporting Democrats in elections away from his home state, which looked, at times, like a shadow White House campaign.\par \par \uc2 J B Pritzker\par \par \uc2 The 59-year-old governor of Illinois would be one of the wealthiest of potential picks, but also can flourish the credentials of having codified the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Illinois and declaring it a \u8220\'20\'1Csanctuary state\u8221\'20\'1D for women seeking abortions. He has also been strong on gun control, and legalised recreational marijuana.\par \par \uc2 Gretchen Whitmer\par \par \uc2 The Michigan governor was on the shortlist for VP pick for Biden in 2020, and a strong showing in the midterms for the Democratic party was in part put down to her governership. The 52-year-old has been in favor of stricter gun laws, repealing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans and back universal pre-kindergarten.\par \par \uc2 Sherrod Brown\par \par \uc2 The 71-year-old would be the most elderly of the alternate picks, but still seven years younger than \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . It was considered a surprise when he didn\u8217\'20\'19t have a tilt for the Democratic nomination for 2020, at the time saying he saw remaining as Ohio\u8217\'20\'19s senator as \u8220\'20\'1Cthe best place for me to make that fight\u8221\'20\'1D on behalf of working people. A strong voice on labor rights and protections, he has also spoken out on protections for IVF and \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Dean Philips\par \par \uc2 The main contender to \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  during the primaries earlier this year has already demonstrated an inability to appeal to the broader party, and so is unlikely to be a factor.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.01am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.54am BST\par \par \uc2 Democratic strategist Theryn Bond has told Sky News that the party needs to replace \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  as presidential nominee, but that it should not be \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  as the \u8220\'20\'1Ccountry is not ready\u8221\'20\'1D for a Black woman to be president.\par \par \uc2 She said that California governor \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2  and Michigan governor \uc2 Gretchen Whitmer\uc2  could be candidates, explaining:\par \par \uc2 Unfortunately as much as I want the US to be ready for Black woman to be president, they are not ready. This country is not ready. This country is too divisive, unfortunately, we\u8217\'20\'19re just not there. I don\u8217\'20\'19t think she would be the one to take the Democratic Party to victory.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.24am BST\par \par \uc2 How could \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  be replaced as Democratic presidential nominee?\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  does not become the party\u8217\'20\'19s nomination for president until endorsed at the 2024 Democratic National Convention in Chicago, which takes place 19-22 August.\par \par \uc2 There is no formal mechanism to replace him as the presumptive nominee, and it would be the first time a party has attempted to do so in modern times. Effectively the only option is that he would have to agree to step aside.\par \par \uc2 He won through the primaries almost uncontested, and has about 95% of the delegates who choose the nominee pledged to vote for him. There isn\u8217\'20\'19t a legal requirement that they vote for who won in the primaries, but they are asked to vote in a way that \u8220\'20\'1Cin all good conscience reflects the sentiments of those who elected them\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Were Biden to step aside as a candidate, he might try to nominate someone \u8211\'20\'13 most likely vice-president \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 as his preferred alternative, which would carry some weight with delegates, but which would not be binding.\par \par \uc2 The most drastic course of action open to Biden \u8211\'20\'13 resigning the presidency itself \u8211\'20\'13 would make Harris president. But that would not automatically make her the Democratic nominee for 2024.\par \par \uc2 The party would still have to carry out an open, contested convention, leaving about 700 party insiders the choice of picking someone, and then having only three months to unite behind and campaign for them.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.24am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.59am BST\par \par \uc2 And here are the top (by which I mean terrible) moments from that debate.\par \par \uc2 Warning: there\u8217\'20\'19s a lot of golf talk.\par \par \uc2 On that note, this is Helen Sullivan, doing whatever the opposite of teeing off is on this live coverage. My colleague Martin Belam will be with you for the next while.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.45am BST\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s worth watching this from MSNBC analyst Claire McCaskill (you\u8217\'20\'19ll hear her use the word \u8220\'20\'1Csurrogate\u8221\'20\'1D a lot \u8211\'20\'13 that is a person who speaks on behalf of a candidate, usually to promote them):\par \par \uc2 enltrWatch this assessment by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/clairecmc?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @clairecmc}}}\uc2  on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/MSNBC?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @MSNBC}}}\uc2 . All 4 minutes. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/WNFhOKEjG2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/WNFhOKEjG2}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Brian Stelter (@brianstelter) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/brianstelter/status/1806542745307083200?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 28, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.41am BST\par \par \uc2 Politico has this {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2024/06/28/can-democrats-replace-biden-00165684"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 explainer}}}\uc2  for how the Democrats could replace Biden (again: this is extremely unlikely to happen \u8211\'20\'13 not quite as unlikely as it was before this debate):\par \par \uc2 If Biden agreed to decline his party\u8217\'20\'19s nomination, it would kick off an open and unpredictable process of picking his replacement.\par \par \uc2 Other names \u8212\'20\'14 from Vice President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , to Govs. \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2 , \uc2 Gretchen Whitmer\uc2  and JB Pritzker, to numerous others \u8212\'20\'14 could be placed in nomination. The candidates, who could span the Democratic Party\u8217\'20\'19s geographic, ideological and generational wings, would be working to sway the thousands of Democratic delegates to support them on the first ballot.\par \par \uc2 The pledged delegates aren\u8217\'20\'19t the only ones who have a say. The Democratic Party has stripped \u8220\'20\'1Csuperdelegates\u8221\'20\'1D \u8212\'20\'14 elected officials and party leaders who can vote for anyone they please \u8212\'20\'14 of most of their power since the contentious 2016 primary. These superdelegates would be free to vote if no candidate won a majority of delegates on the first ballot. An open, contested convention would give more than 700 party insiders a major role in picking the new nominee.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.34am BST\par \par \uc2 Here is Jon Stewart on how that went:\par \par \uc2 enltrJon Stewart's takeaway from tonight's Biden-Trump debate {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/blfuAAdew8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/blfuAAdew8}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Daily Show (@TheDailyShow) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/TheDailyShow/status/1806538824534639049?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 28, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.25am BST\par \par \uc2 Tim Miller, a former Republican strategist-turned ardent Biden supporter, told the AP in the spin room after the debate, \u8220\'20\'1CThat was the worst performance in the history of televised presidential debates\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.16am BST\par \par \uc2 What Biden had to say after the debate\par \par \uc2 In case you missed this earlier, here is what Biden had to say.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI think we did well,\u8221\'20\'1D he told reporters.\par \par \uc2 Asked whether he had any concerns about his performance, and calls from some supporters for him to drop out, he said: \u8220\'20\'1CNo. It\u8217\'20\'19s hard to debate a liar. \uc2 The New York Times\uc2  pointed out he lied 26 times.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 When asked whether he was sick \u8211\'20\'13 his aides told reporters during the debate that Biden had a cold \u8211\'20\'13 Biden said, \u8220\'20\'1CI have a sore throat.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 At a debate watch party earlier, Biden told supporters: \u8220\'20\'1CLook we\u8217\'20\'19re going to beat this guy, and I need you in order to beat him,\u8221\'20\'1D he said, adding, \u8220\'20\'1CYou are the reason why America is as good as we are.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re the finest nation in the world,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden told supporters energetically a short while later, and \u8220\'20\'1CThank you, thank you, thank you, thank you\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 A \uc2 CBS\uc2  host responded: \u8220\'20\'1CIt appears his cold has been cured.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.10am BST\par \par \uc2 Could the Democrats replace Biden?\par \par \uc2 Under current Democratic Party rules, it would be difficult, if not impossible, to replace Biden as the party\u8217\'20\'19s nominee without his cooperation or without the party officials being willing to rewrite its rules at the August national convention.\par \par \uc2 The president won the overwhelming majority of Democratic delegates during the state-by-state primary process. And party rules state that, \u8220\'20\'1CDelegates elected to the national convention pledged to a presidential candidate shall in all good conscience reflect the sentiments of those who elected them.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 That said, DNC rules don\u8217\'20\'19t have the same strict \u8220\'20\'1Cfaithless delegate\u8221\'20\'1D rules that the \uc2 RNC\uc2  does, which ignore votes against in violation of a delegate\u8217\'20\'19s pledged position.\par \par \uc2 More detail on why it would be hard to replace Biden {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jun/27/presidential-debate-trump-biden-updates?page=with:block-667e4be78f086bfb3f8efd4d#block-667e4be78f086bfb3f8efd4d"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 and some of the names that could (in the also extremely unlikely eventuality of him dropping out of the race) be in the running.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.04am BST\par \par \uc2 Biden and Trump aren\u8217\'20\'19t not scheduled to meet on the debate stage again for another 75 days, so Biden\u8217\'20\'19s performance is likely to linger in people\u8217\'20\'19s minds for a while.\par \par \uc2 Trump co-campaign chief Chris LaCavita told the Associated Press Trump would be at the next debate \u8220\'20\'1Cwith bells on.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.01am BST\par \par \uc2 Biden\u8217\'20\'19s surrogates were slow to enter the post-debate spin room in Atlanta, AP reports.\par \par \uc2 And when they finally emerged, they largely avoided questions from the press. Instead, they railed against Trump\u8217\'20\'19s long list of falsehoods during the debate. Among other things, Trump didn\u8217\'20\'19t disavow those who attacked the Capitol on 6 January.\par \par \uc2 California Governor \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2 , a potential future presidential candidate who was Biden\u8217\'20\'19s most prominent surrogate in the Atlanta spin room, urged Democrats not to panic.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI think it\u8217\'20\'19s unhelpful. And I think it\u8217\'20\'19s unnecessary. We\u8217\'20\'19ve got to go in, we\u8217\'20\'19ve got to keep our heads high,\u8221\'20\'1D Newsom said in an interview on MSNBC. \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19ve got to have the back of this president. You don\u8217\'20\'19t turn back because of one performance. What kind of party does that?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Still, signs of anxiety were apparent as Democrats began to openly encourage the party to find an alternative to Biden. Some party officials pointed to a social media post from former Obama campaign aide Ravi Gupta.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CEvery Democrat I know is texting that this is bad,\u8221\'20\'1D Gupta wrote on X. \u8220\'20\'1CJust say it publicly and begin the hard work of creating space in the convention for a selection process. I\u8217\'20\'19ll vote for a corpse over Trump, but this is a suicide mission.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrEvery Democrat I know is texting that this is bad. Just say it publicly and begin the hard work of creating space in the convention for a selection process. I'll vote for a corpse over Trump, but this is a suicide mission.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Ravi Gupta (@RaviMGupta) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RaviMGupta/status/1806496690683162896?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 28, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 Under current Democratic Party rules, it would be difficult, if not impossible, to replace Biden as the party\u8217\'20\'19s nominee without his cooperation or without the party officials being willing to rewrite its rules at the August national convention.\par \par \uc2 The president won the overwhelming majority of Democratic delegates during the state-by-state primary process. And party rules state that, \u8220\'20\'1CDelegates elected to the national convention pledged to a presidential candidate shall in all good conscience reflect the sentiments of those who elected them.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 But DNC rules don\u8217\'20\'19t have the same strict \u8220\'20\'1Cfaithless delegate\u8221\'20\'1D rules that the \uc2 RNC\uc2  does, which ignore votes against in violation of a delegate\u8217\'20\'19s pledged position.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.54am BST\par \par \uc2 Biden, whose deceased son, Beau, served in Iraq, had one of his most forceful moments when he went on the attack against Trump\u8217\'20\'19s reported comments in 2018 that he declined to visit a US military cemetery in France because veterans buried there were \u8220\'20\'1Csuckers\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Closers.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 It was an argument that Biden, then the Democratic challenger, made against Trump in their first 2020 debate and one that the incumbent president has regularly used against Trump, framing him as a commander in chief who nonetheless disparages veterans. \u8220\'20\'1CMy son was not a loser, was not a sucker,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said. \u8220\'20\'1CYou\u8217\'20\'19re the sucker. You\u8217\'20\'19re the loser.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Trump responded that the publication that initially reported this comments, The Atlantic, \u8220\'20\'1Cwas a third-rate magazine\u8221\'20\'1D and had made up the quotes. But undercutting Trump\u8217\'20\'19s retort is the fact that his former chief of staff, \uc2 John Kelly\uc2 , confirmed those private remarks in a statement last fall.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.51am BST\par \par \uc2 Nicholas Kristof, the leftwing political columnist, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/NickKristof/status/1806508213208248501"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said on Twitter/X}}}\uc2  that he hopes Biden reflects on the debate and decides to withdraw from the race, letting the convention decide who should be the nominee. He suggested someone like Michigan governor \uc2 Gretchen Whitmer\uc2 , Ohio senator \uc2 Sherrod Brown\uc2  or commerce secretary \uc2 Gina Raimondo\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.53am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.44am BST\par \par \uc2 Trump, for his part, stumbled over the question of how he would reassure voters that he would respect his oath of office after the 6 January, 2021, attack on the US Capitol.\par \par \uc2 Trump tried to avoid addressing the issue at all. He defended the people who stormed the Capitol, blaming Biden for prosecuting them. \u8220\'20\'1CWhat they\u8217\'20\'19ve done to some people who are so innocent, you ought to be ashamed of yourself,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump told Biden.\par \par \uc2 More than 1,400 people have been charged with federal offenses stemming from the riot. Of those, more than 850 people have pleaded guilty to crimes, including seditious conspiracy and assaulting police officers. About 200 others have been convicted at trial.\par \par \uc2 Trump warned that the members of the congressional committee that investigated 6 January could face criminal charges, as could Biden himself.\par \par \uc2 Biden shot back: \u8220\'20\'1CThe only person on this stage who\u8217\'20\'19s a convicted felon is the man I\u8217\'20\'19m looking at.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Terump also sought to blame former House Speaker \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2 . She responded on X/\uc2 Twitter\uc2 , saying:\par \par \uc2 enltrI tore up the former president\u8217\'20\'19s State of the Union address because it was a manifesto of lies. Tonight he presented another pack of lies which along, with his candidacy, must be rejected. How dare he place the blame for January 6th on anyone but himself, the inciter of an\u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  (@TeamPelosi) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/TeamPelosi/status/1806525160138445208?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 28, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.37am BST\par \par \uc2 Now for some more reaction to the debate. Tevi Troy, a bipartisan policy center fellow and presidential historian, told Reuters that overall, the debate \u8220\'20\'1Cis going to be a problem for Biden\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Biden had a lot of answers where he looked weak. \u8220\'20\'1CThere were other answers where he was more solid, but it doesn\u8217\'20\'19t matter because the problematic answers are going to live on through \uc2 Twitter\uc2  and social media.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Trump on the other hand was \u8220\'20\'1Cmore restrained\u8221\'20\'1D than in previous debates, Troy said. The rules of the debate where they shut off the mics \u8220\'20\'1Cactually helped him (Trump) so he wasn\u8217\'20\'19t interrupting and didn\u8217\'20\'19t seem quite as rude.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere\u8217\'20\'19s the phenomenon of the double haters, where people like neither candidate... One guy\u8217\'20\'19s crazy, the other guy\u8217\'20\'19s too old. They were definitely validated in thinking the one guy is too old, and in terms of the crazy I think Trump did dial it down.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.29am BST\par \par \uc2 Analysis: Trump-Biden debate likely amplified Americans\u8217\'20\'19 dismay about the election\par \par \uc2 Here is the analysis of tonight\u8217\'20\'19s debate from the Guardian US\u8217\'20\'19s senior political reporter, Joan E Greve:\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  both walked into the presidential debate on Thursday hoping to sway the so-called \u8220\'20\'1Cdouble haters\u8221\'20\'1D, those voters who {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/mar/09/biden-trump-presidential-election-no-one-wants"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 disapprove}}}\uc2  of both candidates and could play a decisive role in the outcome of the election.\par \par \uc2 In the end, those voters probably walked away from the debate with a more visceral understanding of why they hate their options.\par \par \uc2 Trump spent the night spouting lies about immigration, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and foreign policy while deflecting moderators\u8217\'20\'19 questions on the climate crisis and election denialism. But Biden largely failed to capitalize on Trump\u8217\'20\'19s vulnerabilities and struggled to offer concise and coherent answers.\par \par \uc2 Biden\u8217\'20\'19s gravelly voice became such a distraction that the White House had to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/KellyO/status/1806505436457189594"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 clarify}}}\uc2  that he was suffering from a cold. When asked early in the debate about tackling the national debt, Biden offered a rambling answer in which he stumbled through his words before concluding, \u8220\'20\'1CLook: we finally beat Medicare.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The bizarre slip of the tongue caught the attention of Trump, who retorted: \u8220\'20\'1CHe did beat Medicare. He beat it to death, and he\u8217\'20\'19s destroying Medicare.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Trump then pivoted to the subject of immigration, a tactic that he deployed repeatedly throughout the night. Trump\u8217\'20\'19s successful rebuttal may have obscured the fact that his claim about Biden \u8220\'20\'1Cdestroying Medicare\u8221\'20\'1D is false; the president has actually taken steps to expand Medicare benefits, including {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.kff.org/medicare/issue-brief/explaining-the-prescription-drug-provisions-in-the-inflation-reduction-act/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 lowering}}}\uc2  enrollees\u8217\'20\'19 prescription drug costs.\par \par \uc2 That dynamic played out over and over again on Thursday. Biden\u8217\'20\'19s attempts to call out Trump\u8217\'20\'19s endless stream of lies often missed the mark because of his uneven delivery, while CNN moderators Jake Tapper and Dana Bash stuck to the network\u8217\'20\'19s previously stated plan of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jun/27/fact-check-debate-biden-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 not fact-checking the candidates in real time}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jun/28/biden-trump-debate-performance-analysis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump-Biden debate likely amplified Americans\u8217\'20\'19 dismay about the election}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.27am BST\par \par \uc2 Here are some photos of Americans watching the debate:\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.20am BST\par \par \uc2 Margaret Sullivan: 'Even factchecking Trump\u8217\'20\'19s constant lies probably wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t have rescued Biden'\par \par \uc2 From the moment the candidates walked out on to the stage in Atlanta, it was obvious that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jun/27/biden-trump-presidential-debate-atlanta"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 this debate}}}\uc2  was a big mistake for \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 . By the end, it was a train wreck for his campaign.\par \par \uc2 The incumbent president, who desperately needed to show vitality, looked from the start like an old man. His gait was stiff and his voice tentative. His energy was markedly different from his triumphant State of the Union address just a few months ago.\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  had a thuggish look, but he seemed vigorous and energetic. He seemed \u8230\'20\'26 the same.\par \par \uc2 Then the barrage of lies started, as they always do with Trump.\par \par \uc2 Among them: Democrats favor post-birth executions. The former president never slept with a porn star. The 2020 election was riddled with fraud. Trump never called prisoners of war losers and suckers. Biden would quadruple people\u8217\'20\'19s taxes.\par \par \uc2 On and on and on, in nearly every Trump sentence. Biden had occasional moments, too, of exaggeration or misstatement. But there is no comparison.\par \par \uc2 No comparison \u8211\'20\'13 and no fact-checking by the moderators.\par \par \uc2 That was the policy going in. CNN\u8217\'20\'19s political director, David Chalian, made that clear a few days ago when he said that debate moderators shouldn\u8217\'20\'19t make themselves into participants but remain mere facilitators. There would be no live factchecks during the debate.\par \par \uc2 And so, Trump rolled over Biden, landing punch after punch. Not with logic. And certainly not with truth. But with force of personality, and sheer chutzpah.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/article/2024/jun/28/trumps-lies-biden-debate"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Even factchecking Trump\u8217\'20\'19s constant lies probably wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t have rescued Biden | Margaret Sullivan}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.14am BST\par \par \uc2 Summary\par \par \uc2 Here is what you may be thankful you missed in tonight\u8217\'20\'19s debate between US President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 :\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  debated \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and tax policy in the first presidential head-to-head, in which the president struggled to land his lines and Trump countered Biden\u8217\'20\'19s criticism by leaning into falsehoods about the economy, illegal immigration and his role in the Jan. 6, 2021, Capitol insurrection.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Biden\u8217\'20\'19s uneven performance, particularly early in the debate, crystallized the concerns of many Americans that, at 81, he is too old to serve as president. It sparked a fresh round of calls for the Democrat to consider stepping aside as the party\u8217\'20\'19s nominee as members of his party fear a return of Trump to the White House.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Biden repeatedly tore into Trump in an apparent effort to provoke him, bringing up everything from the former president\u8217\'20\'19s recent felony conviction to his alleged insult of World War I veterans to his weight.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The 78-year-old Trump declined to clearly state he would accept the results of the November election, four years after he promoted conspiracy theories about his loss that culminated in the 6 January insurrection, and repeatedly misstated the record from his time in office.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 But Biden\u8217\'20\'19s delivery from the beginning of the debate drew the most attention afterward. Trump\u8217\'20\'19s allies immediately declared victory while prominent Democrats publicly questioned whether Biden could move forward.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI think the panic had set in,\u8221\'20\'1D said David Axelrod, a longtime advisor to former President \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  on CNN, immediately after the debate about Biden\u8217\'20\'19s performance. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd I think you\u8217\'20\'19re going to hear discussions that, I don\u8217\'20\'19t know will lead to anything, but there are going to be discussions about whether he should continue.\u8221\'20\'1D Said Van Jones, another Democratic strategist, on CNN: \u8220\'20\'1CHe did not do well at all.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Vice President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , speaking on CNN afterward, sought to defend the president\u8217\'20\'19s performance while acknowledging the criticism. \u8220\'20\'1CThere was a slow start, but there was a strong finish,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. Asked about his performance in the debate, Biden told reporters early Friday that \u8220\'20\'1CI think we did well,\u8221\'20\'1D but said he has a \u8220\'20\'1Csore throat.\u8221\'20\'1D Pressed about Democratic concerns with his showing that he should consider stepping aside, Biden said, \u8220\'20\'1CNo, it\u8217\'20\'19s hard to debate a liar.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Biden began the night with a hoarse voice as he tried to defend his economic record and criticize Trump. He repeatedly lost his train of thought. A person familiar with the matter said Biden was suffering from a cold during the debate, adding that he tested negative for Covid-19.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Biden appeared to lose his train of thought while giving one answer, drifting from an answer on tax policy to health policy, at one point using the word \u8220\'20\'1CCovid\u8221\'20\'1D and then saying, \u8220\'20\'1Cexcuse me, with, dealing with,\u8221\'20\'1D and he trailed off again. \u8220\'20\'1CLook, we finally beat Medicare,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said, as his time ran out on his answer.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 He also fumbled on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, one of the most important issues for Democrats in this year\u8217\'20\'19s election. He was unable to explain Roe v. Wade, the landmark Supreme Court ruling that legalized \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  nationwide. A conservative Supreme Court with three justices nominated by Trump overturned Roe two years ago. When asked if he supports some restrictions on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Biden said he \u8220\'20\'1Csupports Roe v. Wade, which had three trimesters. The first time is between a woman and a doctor. Second time is between a doctor and an extreme situation. A third time is between the doctor, I mean, between the women and the state.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The current president and his predecessor hadn\u8217\'20\'19t spoken since their last debate weeks before the 2020 presidential election. Trump skipped Biden\u8217\'20\'19s inauguration after leading an unprecedented and unsuccessful effort to overturn his loss that culminated in the Capitol riot by his supporters.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump equivocated on whether he would accept the results of the November election, saying he would accept them if the vote was \u8220\'20\'1Cfair\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Clegal,\u8221\'20\'1D repeating his baseless claims of widespread fraud and misconduct in his 2020 loss to Biden that he still denies.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.17am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.03am BST\par \par \uc2 The Associated Press has spoken to US voters who tuned into the debate. There\u8217\'20\'19s one thing that Trump and Biden supporters can agree on, the AP\u8217\'20\'19s Calvin Woodward writes: Biden had a bad night:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COh, Joe.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 That gasp, from patrons at a Chicago bar when President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  first stumbled verbally in his debate with \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , spoke for a lot of Americans on Thursday night.\par \par \uc2 In watch parties, bars, a bowling alley and other venues where people across the country gathered to tune in, Trump supporters, happily, and Biden supporters, in their angst if not dread, seemed to largely agree they had witnessed a lopsided showdown.\par \par \uc2 Biden \u8220\'20\'1Cjust didn\u8217\'20\'19t have the spark that we needed tonight,\u8221\'20\'1D Rosemarie DeAngelus, a Democrat from South Portland, Maine, said from her watch party at Broadway Bowl. Trump, she said, showed \u8220\'20\'1Cmore spunk or more vigor\u8221\'20\'1D even if, in her view, he was telling a pack of lies.\par \par \uc2 Fellow Biden supporter and bowling alley attendee Lynn Miller, from nearby Old Orchard Beach, said: \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s like somebody gave Trump an Adderall and I don\u8217\'20\'19t think they gave Joe one.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19ve never seen Trump seem so coherent,\u8221\'20\'1D Miller said. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd I hate to say this, but Joe seemed a little bit off. But I still support him over Trump because Trump lied about every single thing that happened.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In McAllen, Texas, near the Mexico border, London\u8217\'20\'19s Bar & Grill is normally loud on a day close to the weekend, but many patrons were quiet as they absorbed the debate from TV screens. Here, Biden supporters, Trump supporters and undecided voters mingled.\par \par \uc2 Virginia Lopez came away still not knowing whom she will support in November. She heard snappy but unsatisfying answers from the Republican. \u8220\'20\'1CTrump is just deflecting in all the answers and he\u8217\'20\'19s just lying,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CIt doesn\u8217\'20\'19t feel like a real debate.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Biden? \u8220\'20\'1CI just feel like he\u8217\'20\'19s too old,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 Sitting up at the bar, Hector Mercado, 72, a veteran wearing a US military beret, was a distinctive patron as he listened intently to the debate. Although he was a Democrat for several years, he switched parties under \uc2 Ronald Reagan\uc2 , a Republican.\par \par \uc2 Mercado heard Biden accuse Trump of making derogatory comments about veterans, but it didn\u8217\'20\'19t sway his support for Trump. \u8220\'20\'1CYeah, he said a few things bad about veterans at one point back in the early days,\u8221\'20\'1D he said of Trump. \u8220\'20\'1CBut now he\u8217\'20\'19s saying, \u8216\'20\'18No, I back up the veterans and I never had any problems with him. I got a raise in my VA disability when Trump was president.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Biden\u8217\'20\'19s performance left him cold. \u8220\'20\'1CI think Trump is stronger,\u8221\'20\'1D he said, \u8220\'20\'1Cand Biden is a little weak.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.54am BST\par \par \uc2 Matt Grossmann, a political science professor at \uc2 Michigan State University\uc2 , told Reuters after the debate:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CObviously the biggest factor is that Biden still seemed old and raspy and less coherent than when he ran last time, and that\u8217\'20\'19s going to be the big story, I think, out of the debate. I don\u8217\'20\'19t think Trump really did anything to help himself beyond his existing supporters, but I think it is eclipsed by people\u8217\'20\'19s impressions of Biden on his biggest vulnerability.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Grossmann said that from the beginning of the debate Biden had trouble getting his points across \u8220\'20\'1Cand just seemed a lot softer.\u8221\'20\'1D He said Biden didn\u8217\'20\'19t really start delivering effective answers until 20 minutes into the debate. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s hard to recover from that.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Grossmann said that debates typically have a small impact on presidential races and that impact dissipates over time.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CDebates do not normally have huge influence on election results. But because we\u8217\'20\'19re at this 50-50 election where the country is divided, any small change can make a difference.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Grossmann said one problem for Biden is that some of his supporters are expressing their concerns about his performance rather than defending it.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSo there\u8217\'20\'19s not a message in his favor. And to the extent that it has an influence, the influence will be to make people\u8217\'20\'19s concerns about Biden\u8217\'20\'19s age even more salient.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.50am BST\par \par \uc2 If you\u8217\'20\'19re just joining us, here is how the debate between \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and US President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  went: badly. For Biden.\par \par \uc2 In a debate that was not fact-checked live, Trump lied repeatedly. But he was energetic, forceful, and fairly clear in the delivery of his responses/lies. Biden was shaky and appeared to struggle to gather his thoughts and, at times, to express them with much clarity. During the debate, aides informed the media that the president had a cold. But this was cold comfort to voters and democrats, who largely seemed to find the debate disastrous for Biden.\par \par \uc2 Vice President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , appearing on CNN after the debate, acknowledged what she called Biden\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cslow start\u8221\'20\'1D but argued that voters should judge him and Trump based on their years in office.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m not going to spend all night with you talking about the last 90 minutes when I\u8217\'20\'19ve been watching the last three-and-a-half years of performance,\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Democrats, the Guardian reports, are \u8220\'20\'1Cin panic mode\u8221\'20\'1D:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jun/27/biden-trump-debate-democrats-reaction"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Defcon 1 moment\u8217\'20\'19: Biden\u8217\'20\'19s debate performance sends Democrats into panic}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.54am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.43am BST\par \par \uc2 Why it would be tough to replace Biden \u8211\'20\'13 and who could be in the running (in the tiny chance that opportunity arose)\par \par \uc2 There is no evidence Biden is willing to end his campaign. And it would be nearly impossible for Democrats to replace him unless he chooses to step aside, AP reports.\par \par \uc2 Every state has already held its presidential primary. Democratic rules mandate that the delegates Biden won remain bound to support him at the party\u8217\'20\'19s upcoming national convention unless he tells them he\u8217\'20\'19s leaving the race.\par \par \uc2 If Biden opts to abandon his reelection campaign, \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  would likely join other top Democratic candidates looking to replace him. But that would probably create a scenario where she and others end up lobbying individual state delegations at the convention for their support.\par \par \uc2 That hasn\u8217\'20\'19t happened for Democrats since 1960, when John F. Kennedy and Lyndon B. Johnson jockeyed for votes during that year\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic convention in Los Angeles.\par \par \uc2 Other Democrats with their own presidential aspirations include:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 California Gov. \uc2 Gavin Newsom\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Michigan Gov. \uc2 Gretchen Whitmer\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Pennsylvania Gov. Josh Shapiro\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Illinois Gov. \uc2 J. B. Pritzker\uc2  and\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 California Rep. \uc2 Ro Khanna\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Still others who Biden bested during the party\u8217\'20\'19s 2020 presidential primary could also try again, including Sens. \uc2 Bernie Sanders\uc2  of Vermont, Elizabeth Warren of Massachusetts and Amy Klobuchar of Minnesota, as well as Transportation Secretary \uc2 Pete Buttigieg\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.34am BST\par \par \uc2 What happens if (IF) Biden drops out?\par \par \uc2 The UK\u8217\'20\'19s Financial Times has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ft.com/content/34ce2774-fb61-4bce-bb4c-62c4d557f94e"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 this}}}\uc2  useful explainer about what would happen if (and it is a huge, huge, IF, but a slightly less huge one after tonight), Biden {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ft.com/content/34ce2774-fb61-4bce-bb4c-62c4d557f94e"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 dropped out}}}\uc2  of the race:\par \par \uc2 Both [Trump and Biden] easily won their party\u8217\'20\'19s primary vote earlier this year. If they dropped out now, it would be up to delegates at the forthcoming Republican and Democratic conventions to find replacements.\par \par \uc2 That would make July\u8217\'20\'19s Republican convention in Milwaukee or the Democratic convention in Chicago in August akin to conventions decades ago, when candidates canvassed each state\u8217\'20\'19s delegation for floor votes.\par \par \uc2 State delegates would be \u8220\'20\'1Cuncommitted\u8221\'20\'1D \u8212\'20\'14 no longer beholden to their state\u8217\'20\'19s primary result \u8212\'20\'14 and able to vote for any candidate they liked, said Elaine Kamarck at the \uc2 Brookings Institution\uc2  think-tank. It might take several rounds of voting to find a nominee.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CPresumably, for Democrats, they would pick [vice-president] \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D said Derek Muller, professor at the \uc2 University of Notre Dame\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s law school.\par \par \uc2 But Harris\u8217\'20\'19s approval rating is just 39.4%, according to FiveThirtyEight \u8212\'20\'14 even lower than Biden\u8217\'20\'19s 39.9%. Other Democrats would almost certainly jump into the race.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.37am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.29am BST\par \par \uc2 Former Obama campaign aide Ravi Gupta on X/\uc2 Twitter\uc2 :\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CEvery Democrat I know is texting that this is bad. Just say it publicly and begin the hard work of creating space in the convention for a selection process. I\u8217\'20\'19ll vote for a corpse over Trump, but this is a suicide mission.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.27am BST\par \par \uc2 Guardian\uc2  columnist Osita Nwanevu writes: Half an hour into the worst presidential debate of all time, Jake Tapper finally put a question to the candidates about \u8220\'20\'1Cthe issue of democracy\u8221\'20\'1D. As president, Tapper said, Trump had sworn an oath to the constitution that many voters believe he violated by instigating the riot on January 6. What would he say to those voters?\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWell, I don\u8217\'20\'19t think too many believe that,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump sniffed. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd let me tell you about January 6th. On January 6th, we had a great border. Nobody coming through. Very few. On January 6th, we were energy independent. On January 6th, we had the lowest taxes ever. We had the lowest regulations ever \u8230\'20\'26 We were respected all over the world.\u8221\'20\'1D He was asked again and babbled about \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s daughter instead.\par \par \uc2 This was Biden\u8217\'20\'19s golden opportunity. Because as stubbornly pessimistic as Americans might be about the economy or Biden\u8217\'20\'19s age, Trump\u8217\'20\'19s efforts to overturn the 2020 election illustrate that democracy itself is at stake. It\u8217\'20\'19s a simple, clear and potent message. Biden failed to deliver it effectively. \u8220\'20\'1CHe talked about these people being great patriots of America,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden rasped. \u8220\'20\'1CIn fact, he says he\u8217\'20\'19ll now forgive them for what they\u8217\'20\'19ve done. He\u8217\'20\'19ll \u8230\'20\'26 and they\u8217\'20\'19ve been convicted. He says he wants to commute their sentences \u8230\'20\'26 and say that \u8230\'20\'26 that no, he went to every single court in the nation, I don\u8217\'20\'19t know how many cases, scores of cases, including the supreme court. And they said, they said: \u8216\'20\'18No, no, this guy, this guy is responsible for doing what is being that was done.\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Unfortunately, it\u8217\'20\'19s doubtful that Biden\u8217\'20\'19s capacities will improve by November. Although he does sometimes have a command of facts and figures, Biden has lost his ability to communicate effectively ?\u8211\'20\'13 not something one wants in a political candidate or, for that matter, a president.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/article/2024/jun/27/trump-biden-presidential-debate-responses"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump v Biden in the first 2024 presidential debate: our panelists\u8217\'20\'19 verdict | Panelists}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.17am BST\par \par \uc2 Biden\u8217\'20\'19s debate performance sends Democrats into panic\par \par \uc2 Could there be a contested Democratic convention? How would that even work? Replacing the president may not be an option, they said, but many acknowledged {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/democrats"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Democrats}}}\uc2  are talking about it, spurred by Biden\u8217\'20\'19s troubling debate performance.\par \par \uc2 MSNBC\u8217\'20\'19s Nicole Wallace laid out how a candidate could release their delegates. \uc2 Joy Reid\uc2  said someone sent her the rules.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe rules are circulating,\u8221\'20\'1D Wallace laughed.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNo one is saying it\u8217\'20\'19s going to happen, it\u8217\'20\'19s very unlikely,\u8221\'20\'1D Reid reiterated.\par \par \uc2 The fact that a liberal network would broach the idea of whether an incumbent president running for re-election could be replaced after they\u8217\'20\'19ve won the nomination shows how Democrats are scrambling after the debate to affirm Biden\u8217\'20\'19s ability to lead the nation. Many are questioning whether the party should have serious conservations about what else could be done instead.\par \par \uc2 David Plouffe, a Democratic strategist and former Obama campaign official, called the debate \u8220\'20\'1Ckind of a Defcon 1 moment\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe biggest thing in this election is voters\u8217\'20\'19 concerns \u8211\'20\'13 and it\u8217\'20\'19s both swing voters and base voters \u8211\'20\'13 with his age, and those were compounded tonight,\u8221\'20\'1D Plouffe said.\par \par \uc2 Read the full story:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jun/27/biden-trump-debate-democrats-reaction"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Defcon 1 moment\u8217\'20\'19: Biden\u8217\'20\'19s debate performance sends Democrats into panic}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.21am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.14am BST\par \par \uc2 Shropshire said one strong moment for Biden was when he pointed out that Trump was a convicted felon and criticized his morality.\par \par \uc2 She also said that Trump\u8217\'20\'19s reference to migrants taking Black jobs had become \u8220\'20\'1Ca hilarious meme all across Black \uc2 Twitter\uc2  right now\u8221\'20\'1D:\par \par \uc2 enltrI\u8217\'20\'19m black\par \par \uc2 My job is \uc2 White Sox\uc2  podcaster\par \par \uc2 So Sox podcaster is a black job?!\par \par \uc2 Are migrants taking my black job?\par \par \uc2 Godspeed??\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Herb Lawrence (@Ecnerwal23) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Ecnerwal23/status/1806509762340655285?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 28, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 She said it showed how Trump was failing to connect with Black voters.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThat there are specific Black jobs for Black people that immigrants are coming to take. Utter nonsense.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.11am BST\par \par \uc2 Adrianne Shropshire, Executive director of Blackpac, an organization that works to mobilize black voters, told Reuters she wrote down two things in her notepad while watching the debate.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COne is that Trump lies,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. The other was that Biden \u8220\'20\'1Cwas not as forceful as I thought he needed to be.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Shropshire criticised the moderators for allowing Trump to make various false claims without any pushback.\par \par \uc2 Trump was essentially allowed to do what he does at his rallies, which is say whatever he wants, regardless of the relationship it has to the truth. And that was really unfortunate.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Shropshire said Biden could have pushed back on Trump\u8217\'20\'19s false claims more forcefully.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI think he tried to take the high road by talking policy. And I think that has its place. But when we think about where our politics are right now, there really is a need to just assert facts and assert them very clearly. And I think that got muddled a bit in his policy responses.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Shropshire said she was not as worried as others who have said Biden had an unsteady performance that could increase about his age. \u8220\'20\'1CHe has great performances that people have talked about just in the past few months,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI also think that it just doesn\u8217\'20\'19t change the dynamics of the race, because they also saw Trump standing next to \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , and I don\u8217\'20\'19t think that they saw someone who was stronger necessarily. I think they saw the same unhinged Trump that they see at every rally and in clips when they\u8217\'20\'19re on social media.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.04am BST\par \par \uc2 Arwa Mahdawi: 'This was not a debate so much as a farce'\par \par \uc2 My expectations for this debate weren\u8217\'20\'19t just low, they were dungeon-in-hell levels of low. I still wasn\u8217\'20\'19t prepared for how shocking it would actually be. Trump lied unashamedly, Biden waffled incoherently, and the moderators just said \u8220\'20\'1Cthank you\u8221\'20\'1D a lot and moved on. This was not a \u8220\'20\'1Cdebate\u8221\'20\'1D so much as a farce.\par \par \uc2 If Biden\u8217\'20\'19s team thought this debate would assuage worries about the president\u8217\'20\'19s age and competence, their plans spectacularly backfired. For the first half of the debate, Biden looked dazed and could barely get his words out. He noticeably improved towards the end; still, this was not a man who instills confidence. Trump blustered and lied and dog-whistled his way through the night, but if you were going on optics alone the convicted felon had the upper hand.\par \par \uc2 For those of us distraught by Gaza, tonight was a gut-wrenching reminder that neither candidate gives a damn about Palestinian lives. Trump used \u8220\'20\'1CPalestinian\u8221\'20\'1D as a slur and Biden, meanwhile, reiterated his support for Israel no matter how many Palestinian kids are killed. Neither candidate answered the question of whether they support a Palestinian state and the moderators didn\u8217\'20\'19t press them on it.\par \par \uc2 Responses to questions about \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  were also bleak. Trump advanced inflammatory misinformation about late-term \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and Biden didn\u8217\'20\'19t seem interested in talking about \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in detail \u8211\'20\'13 he didn\u8217\'20\'19t even mention it in his closing statements. He seemed a lot more interested in talking about golf. Indeed, the only part of the night when both men seemed to really come alive was when they got into a fight about their golf handicaps.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/article/2024/jun/27/trump-biden-presidential-debate-responses"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump v Biden in the first 2024 presidential debate: our panelists\u8217\'20\'19 verdict | Panelists}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.45am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.00am BST\par \par \uc2 Pelosi: 'How dare [Trump] place blame for January 6 on anyone but himself"\par \par \uc2 Former House speaker \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2 , meanwhile, has taken aim at Trump\u8217\'20\'19s claiming \u8211\'20\'13 falsely \u8211\'20\'13during the debate that she was responsible for the January 6 insurrection.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHow dare he place the blame for January 6th on anyone but himself, the inciter of an insurrection?\u8221\'20\'1D she wrote on X:\par \par \uc2 enltrI tore up the former president\u8217\'20\'19s State of the Union address because it was a manifesto of lies. Tonight he presented another pack of lies which along, with his candidacy, must be rejected. How dare he place the blame for January 6th on anyone but himself, the inciter of an\u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  (@TeamPelosi) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/TeamPelosi/status/1806525160138445208?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 28, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.10am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.57am BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s age and acuity took center stage. He looked lost, and the Democrats are almost certainly panicking. At times, the president could barely stitch two coherent sentences together. \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  won the evening, and it wasn\u8217\'20\'19t even close.\par \par \uc2 Trump took command from the outset. He appeared energized and engaged. What Trump said mattered less than how he said it; he forcefully responded to whatever question was posed. He repeatedly mocked, taunted and bludgeoned Biden. If this were a boxing match, the referee would have stopped the match in the third round.\par \par \uc2 Despite Biden\u8217\'20\'19s efforts to nail Trump on his own record as president, Trump was mostly unbowed. He seemingly stood by his picks to the supreme court and the end of Roe v Wade. At one point Trump seemingly mouthed the words \u8220\'20\'1Clet\u8217\'20\'19s not act like children\u8221\'20\'1D, which may be the evening\u8217\'20\'19s most memorable line. He also got away with calling Biden \u8220\'20\'1Cthe Manchurian candidate\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Trump lied aplenty. He acted as if he never had said there were \u8220\'20\'1Cgood people\u8221\'20\'1D on both sides in Charlottesville, and pretended that he hadn\u8217\'20\'19t dissed America\u8217\'20\'19s war dead. But little of that may matter come November. Americans want a president who exudes vigor. And Biden isn\u8217\'20\'19t that.\par \par \uc2 The debate will supply Trump with a wealth of material for campaign ads. It may be time for an open convention. August could be interesting.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.10am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.54am BST\par \par \uc2 Well, that was a disaster.\par \par \uc2 The debate was an unmitigated calamity, especially for Biden. The president was often hard to follow and at times incoherent; he struggled to answer questions that should have been easy gimmes on issues favorable to Democrats. It would be nice if substance mattered more than style, because the substance of Biden\u8217\'20\'19s remarks were important, and promised a more prosperous, secure and free future for Americans than Trump\u8217\'20\'19s. But his delivery made it extremely difficult for even the most plugged-in politics addicts to follow, let alone your average viewer at home.\par \par \uc2 For Trump\u8217\'20\'19s part, what he didn\u8217\'20\'19t say was more telling than what he did. He was unwilling or unable to answer questions on how he would help families with childcare, the costs of which are a drag not only on family budgets, but on the US economy. He was unwilling or unable to answer questions about opioids and the US\u8217\'20\'19s addiction crisis. And, perhaps most importantly, he refused to clearly answer a thrice-asked question about whether he would accept the results of the election \u8211\'20\'13 saying only that he would do so if such an election were fair, and then claimed the 2020 one wasn\u8217\'20\'19t. In other words, Trump will accept the results of the election only if he wins \u8211\'20\'13 and contest it if he doesn\u8217\'20\'19t.\par \par \uc2 That\u8217\'20\'19s remarkably dangerous. And his wholesale lack of interest in the issues that matter most to American families is remarkably negligent. But unfortunately, his would-be foil \u8211\'20\'13 Biden \u8211\'20\'13 proved simply unable to take on even a truly terrible opponent. Neither man came off looking good. But if Americans are counting on Biden to save us, we might want to start making a Plan B.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/article/2024/jun/27/trump-biden-presidential-debate-responses"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump v Biden in the first 2024 presidential debate: our panelists\u8217\'20\'19 verdict | Panelists}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.51am BST\par \par \uc2 Here is what \uc2 Guardian\uc2  columnist and author of How Does It Feel To Be a Problem?: Being Young and Arab in America and This Muslim American Life: Dispatches from the War on Terror, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/article/2024/jun/27/trump-biden-presidential-debate-responses"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Moustafa Bayoumi}}}\uc2  thought of tonight\u8217\'20\'19s debate:\par \par \uc2 What a catastrophe. From the moment the debate started, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  was meandering, confused and charmless. It never improved. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2 , however, was relatively restrained, at least for Trump. Of course, he resorted to lies, insults and exaggerations throughout the 90 minutes. By citing things called \u8220\'20\'1CBlack jobs\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1CHispanic jobs\u8221\'20\'1D and by calling Biden a \u8220\'20\'1Cbad Palestinian\u8221\'20\'1D, Trump managed to hit all his usual racist notes.\par \par \uc2 Yet the whole thing was simply painful to watch, mostly because it was useless on any practical level. This much ballyhooed confrontation between two political foes for the most important office in the world turned out to be featherlight on substance, policy, interest, intellect, imagination, vision, energy, ideas, humor and hope. It was heavy on one thing (besides cringe), though: ego.\par \par \uc2 The presidency should not simply be a vanity project, but that\u8217\'20\'19s exactly what it has become. Biden\u8217\'20\'19s performance was so far below acceptable that the Democratic party should be ashamed of itself for allowing him to stand for re-election. With tonight\u8217\'20\'19s performance as evidence, the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/democrats"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Democrats}}}\uc2  will almost certainly lose. Trump\u8217\'20\'19s narcissism is notorious, and it too has destroyed the Republican party from within. The stakes are much too high to allow the inflated egos of these two men to determine the fates of millions of people here and around the world. If the Democrats truly believe that democracy is on the line during this election, they must select someone other than Biden as their candidate. There\u8217\'20\'19s still time.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.49am BST\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s panellists have also delivered their verdicts. I\u8217\'20\'19ll bring you those imminently. But to make what has been a fun evening even more fun \u8211\'20\'13 first, some clues: \u8220\'20\'1Ccatastrophe\u8221\'20\'1D, \u8220\'20\'1Cdisaster\u8221\'20\'1D, and lower than \u8220\'20\'1Cdungeon-in-hell levels of low\u8221\'20\'1D are some of the words that appear in their analysis.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.50am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.43am BST\par \par \uc2 Prominent political analyst Amy Walter told Reuters the debate \u8220\'20\'1Conly served to remind voters of Biden\u8217\'20\'19s weaknesses, especially his health and stamina\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 She continued, \u8220\'20\'1CTo be sure, Trump did not \u8216\'20\'18win\u8217\'20\'19 this debate as much as Biden lost it. Trump lobbed multiple falsehoods and lies. He failed to make a positive case for his second term, spending more time litigating Biden\u8217\'20\'19s failures. But, Trump is leading in the polls and doesn\u8217\'20\'19t need a \u8216\'20\'18rest\u8217\'20\'19 in the way Biden does.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t think that this debate will sway undecided voters, especially those who say they dislike both candidates. If you came into this debate thinking both men were unsatisfactory choices, their debate performances did not disabuse you of this opinion.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.40am BST\par \par \uc2 The reactions from democrats and democratic voters continue to be excoriating.\par \par \uc2 Julian Castro, Housing and Urban Development secretary under Obama, said on X/\uc2 Twitter\uc2 :\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTonight was completely predictable. Biden had a very low bar going into the debate and failed to clear even that bar\u8230\'20\'26He seemed unprepared, lost, and not strong enough to parry effectively with Trump, who lies constantly.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrBiden had a very low bar going into the debate and failed to clear even that bar. He seemed unprepared, lost, and not strong enough to parry effectively with Trump, who lies constantly.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Juli\u225\'00\'E1n Castro (@JulianCastro) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JulianCastro/status/1806519938984845809?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 28, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.36am BST\par \par \uc2 An unnamed \u8220\'20\'1Ctop\u8221\'20\'1D Biden donor has told Reuters that the president\u8217\'20\'19s performance was \u8220\'20\'1Cdisqualifying\u8221\'20\'1D and that he believes fundraising is going to \u8220\'20\'1Cdry up\u8221\'20\'1D as a result of that performance:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere is no way to spin this. His performance was disqualifying. There is going to be a call for a brokered convention. Whitmer, Pritzker, Newsom, Beshear. Those could all be the options. It\u8217\'20\'19s inevitable.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The donor added that it would likely come down to Jill Biden to convince him. \u8220\'20\'1CHe is a stubborn guy... It cannot be described how bad this performance was.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The donor said they thought \uc2 Andy Beshear\uc2 , the popular Democratic governor of Kentucky, a deeply Republican state at the federal level, would be the likely winner.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHe won red Kentucky. He\u8217\'20\'19ll be a great candidate who can still bring this home. I don\u8217\'20\'19t think Newsom [Democratic governor of California] will win.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Fundraising will \u8220\'20\'1Cdry up,\u8221\'20\'1D the donor predicted.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMoney follows enthusiasm. How can anyone with a straight face say donate to elect Joe?... I will continue to fundraise for him. What else can we all do? There is no option.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.37am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.31am BST\par \par \uc2 Four key takeaways from the debate\par \par \uc2 Here are four key takaways from tonight:\par \par \uc2 One: Biden did badly\par \par \uc2 The president joked about the rightwing conspiracies that he would take some kind of performance-enhancing drugs before the debate, posting a link to a can of water for sale on his campaign website called \u8220\'20\'1CDark Brandon\u8217\'20\'19s Secret Sauce\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 But his low-energy, muted and garbled performance didn\u8217\'20\'19t live up to expectations. And keep in mind: Biden challenged the former president to the debate, which looks like a strategic error in retrospect.\par \par \uc2 Voters regularly say they are concerned about Biden\u8217\'20\'19s age and fitness for office. This debate will not assuage their fears.\par \par \uc2 Two: Trump lied, again and again:\par \par \uc2 Trump repeatedly tried to sell falsehoods and half-truths to voters.\par \par \uc2 When questions were posed that would require tough answers, like one about the January 6 insurrection, he deflected and talked about something he could attack Biden on.\par \par \uc2 CNN\u8217\'20\'19s moderators did not factcheck statements live. At times, when he avoided the question, they would reiterate it \u8211\'20\'13 sometimes successfully getting Trump to answer.\par \par \uc2 He falsely claimed Democrats want abortions up until and after birth. He said without evidence that \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  refused his offer for national guard troops on 6 January 2021 to respond to an insurrection he encouraged. He said his administration had the \u8220\'20\'1Cbest environmental numbers\u8221\'20\'1D, whatever that means.\par \par \uc2 Three: the candidates see America very differently\par \par \uc2 The two men showed the distinctions of the two Americas in which they live.\par \par \uc2 Trump repeatedly talked about how the US had failed, how Biden was the worst president in the country\u8217\'20\'19s history and how the world views the country dismally now.\par \par \uc2 Biden disagreed, offering an optimistic view of the US on the world stage.\par \par \uc2 Four: \u8216\'20\'18I didn\u8217\'20\'19t have sex with a porn star.\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s convictions and varied court cases didn\u8217\'20\'19t come up in the debate until it was well underway, a missed opportunity from Biden to hammer on one of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s key liabilities.\par \par \uc2 When the issue finally surfaced, Biden hit at Trump for having sex with an adult film actor while his wife was pregnant, referring to Stormy Daniels and the hush-money trial that concluded {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/may/30/trump-trial-hush-money-verdict"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in 34 felonies for Trump}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou have the morals of an alley cat,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden quipped at Trump.\par \par \uc2 Trump responded with a line that surely has not been uttered at presidential debates in decades past: \u8220\'20\'1CI didn\u8217\'20\'19t have sex with a porn star.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jun/27/trump-biden-cnn-presidential-debate-reaction-highlights"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Biden\u8217\'20\'19s poor performance and Trump\u8217\'20\'19s lies: four key takeaways from the debate}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.28am BST\par \par \uc2 2020 Presidential candidate \uc2 Andrew Yang\uc2  has come out swinging, using the hashtag #swapjoeout in multiple tweets, and writing, \u8220\'20\'1CLook, I debated Joe 7 times in 2020. He\u8217\'20\'19s a different guy in 2024\u8221\'20\'1D:\par \par \uc2 enltrLook I debated Joe 7 times in 2020. He\u8217\'20\'19s a different guy in 2024. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/swapJoeout?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #swapJoeout}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Andrew Yang\uc2 ???????? (@AndrewYang) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AndrewYang/status/1806510637641564223?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 28, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.21am BST\par \par \uc2 Moira Donegan: 'This debate was a disastrous opening performance for Biden'\par \par \uc2 The Biden campaign is probably hoping that you did not watch {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jun/27/biden-trump-presidential-debate-atlanta"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the first presidential debate}}}\uc2 . Over the course of 90 minutes in Atlanta, the president was only sometimes coherent, delivering meandering statements that were often inaudible, frequently veering off topic, and often running out of his allotted time mid-sentence, so that his message remained unclear or outright incomprehensible to viewers.\par \par \uc2 It was a disastrous opening performance for a president whose greatest electoral vulnerability is his age and perceptions about his fitness for the demands of his office. Biden\u8217\'20\'19s showing at the first presidential debate has placed his campaign\u8217\'20\'19s least favorite issue \u8211\'20\'13 the president\u8217\'20\'19s stamina and acuity \u8211\'20\'13 back at the center of the electoral contest.\par \par \uc2 In one of his more energetic and clear moments, Biden responded to a question about his age by pointing out that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  is only three years younger than he is, \u8220\'20\'1Cand a lot less competent\u8221\'20\'1D. That may be true, but Trump \u8211\'20\'13 the convicted felon who has been found liable for sexual assault, was impeached twice, and attempted to overturn the last election when he lost \u8211\'20\'13 was forceful, alert, and on message, even as he repeatedly lied.\par \par \uc2 In contrast, when the cameras cut to Biden, he was often slack-jawed, his eyes unfocused, seeming to stare into the middle distance with a look of vacant horror. The contrast was stark. Many of the liberal-leaning voters watching no doubt despaired at Biden\u8217\'20\'19s performance, which they feared would permanently cement the popular opinion that he is simply too old for the job.\par \par \uc2 He may well be. Even in response to what should have been easy questions, Biden fumbled:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/article/2024/jun/28/debate-disastrous-biden"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 This debate was a disastrous opening performance for Biden | Moira Donegan}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.19am BST\par \par \uc2 A CNN flash poll has Trump winning the debate 67% to 33%.\par \par \uc2 Trump gave a better performance, voters said. Polled before the debate, the same voters said they thought Trump would give a better performance than Biden, but it was closer: 5% to 45%.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.17am BST\par \par \uc2 Here is a summary \u8211\'20\'13 and snap verdict \u8211\'20\'13after that debate:\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s first debate does not appear to have turned out well for the president, who struggled with a raspy voice, occasional cough and general difficulty landing his lines in the 90-minute face-off. Democrats are now {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jun/27/presidential-debate-trump-biden-updates?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-667e26118f081d94ff3d16ba#block-667e26118f081d94ff3d16ba"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in panic mode}}}\uc2  over his chances in the November election, with one notable strategist calling it \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jun/27/presidential-debate-trump-biden-updates?page=with:block-667e2a9b8f081d94ff3d16d3#block-667e2a9b8f081d94ff3d16d3"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a Defcon 1 moment}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D that will serve to heighten voters\u8217\'20\'19 concerns over his advanced age. Biden showed no sign of changing course, telling supporters \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jun/27/presidential-debate-trump-biden-updates?page=with:block-667e28738f086bfb3f8efc55#block-667e28738f086bfb3f8efc55"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 see you}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D at the next debate scheduled for September, while \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  acknowledged the president had a \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jun/27/presidential-debate-trump-biden-updates?page=with:block-667e2e728f081d94ff3d16e6#block-667e2e728f081d94ff3d16e6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 slow start}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D to what she said was an otherwise successful night. As for Trump, he used the debate as an opportunity to tell a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jun/27/presidential-debate-trump-biden-updates?page=with:block-667e1fc38f081d94ff3d1679#block-667e1fc38f081d94ff3d1679"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 panoply of lies}}}\uc2  about many, many things. Expect Democrats to go on the attack over that in the next couple days, Biden freakout notwithstanding.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s a look back at what happened tonight:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Biden{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jun/27/presidential-debate-trump-biden-updates?page=with:block-667e23028f081787dccaa119#block-667e23028f081787dccaa119"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 is not}}}\uc2  the first incumbent to suffer in his first debate.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The president, who took a whole week to prep for the debate, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jun/27/presidential-debate-trump-biden-updates?page=with:block-667e1e948f086bfb3f8efbfa#block-667e1e948f086bfb3f8efbfa"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reportedly}}}\uc2  came down with a cold beforehand.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jun/27/presidential-debate-trump-biden-updates?page=with:block-667e1f858f086bfb3f8efbfd#block-667e1f858f086bfb3f8efbfd"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 appeared to say}}}\uc2  he would accept the results of the election no matter who wins, but added caveats.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 CNN{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jun/27/presidential-debate-trump-biden-updates?page=with:block-667e16d28f081787dccaa0ab#block-667e16d28f081787dccaa0ab"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 may be in for it}}}\uc2  over a debate format that allowed Trump to spew falsehoods unchecked by the moderators.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The debate{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jun/27/presidential-debate-trump-biden-updates?page=with:block-667e1ca68f086bfb3f8efbec#block-667e1ca68f086bfb3f8efbec"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 highlighted}}}\uc2  the candidates\u8217\'20\'19 very different visions of America. To Trump, it\u8217\'20\'19s a nation that has been \u8220\'20\'1Cdestroyed\u8221\'20\'1D, while to Biden, it is \u8220\'20\'1Cthe most admired country in the world\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.14am BST\par \par \uc2 Republican senator Marco Rubio of Florida is on CBS right now.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CPresident Biden looked ways that are concerning not just for democrats but for America,\u8221\'20\'1D he says. He says there is \u8220\'20\'1Cno choice\u8221\'20\'1D and that the US was \u8220\'20\'1Cstronger and better\u8221\'20\'1D under Trump he says.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.15am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.07am BST\par \par \uc2 Biden supporters chant in response: \u8220\'20\'1CWe need you.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re the finest nation in the world,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden says energetically, and \u8220\'20\'1CThank you, thank you, thank you, thank you\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 CBS responds: \u8220\'20\'1CIt appears his cold has been cured.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.14am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.05am BST\par \par \uc2 Biden is speaking to supporters after the debate. He is using a John Wayne reference and has, quoting Wayne, called Trump a \u8220\'20\'1Clying dog-faced pony soldier\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.03am BST\par \par \uc2 Here is what the stock market thinks of the debate:\par \par \uc2 US stock futures and the dollar rose in early Asian trading on Friday as 2024, which means Trump was viewed by investors as putting in a stronger showing than his opponent.\par \par \uc2 While the election is four months away, investors anticipate a Trump presidency would mean lower corporate taxes, tougher trade relations and therefore higher stock prices and bond yields.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.02am BST\par \par \uc2 Hi, this is Helen Sullivan bringing you the latest reaction and analysis after that debate for the next while.\par \par \uc2 If you have questions about the debate or the election, get in touch on Twitter {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/helenrsullivan"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @helenrsullivan}}}\uc2  or email: helen.sullivan[at]theguardian.com and I\u8217\'20\'19ll do my best.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.52am BST\par \par \uc2 CNN\u8217\'20\'19s deliberate decision to forgo live factchecking evokes a bit of dread and d eja vu from the 2016 election.\par \par \uc2 David Chalian, CNN\u8217\'20\'19s political director, told {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/cnn-presidential-debate-biden-trump-930d00479cd07b4069aff36d556b05b2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Associated Press}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CObviously, if there is some egregious fact that needs to be checked or the record needs to be made clear, Jake and Dana can do that. But that\u8217\'20\'19s not their role. They are not here to participate in this debate. They are here to facilitate a debate between Trump and Biden.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Indeed, neither host pushed back on the barrage of false and misleading claims from Donald Trump, nor did they the fumbles by Joe Biden. This debate over how to moderate the debate \u8211\'20\'13 and whether networks should offer fact checks \u8211\'20\'13 was also raging back in 2016.\par \par \uc2 After a televised debacle in which then-NBC host Matt Lauer failed to push back on Trump\u8217\'20\'19s falsehoods in a commander-in-chief forum, networks declined the Hillary Clinton campaign\u8217\'20\'19s requests for debate fact checks. On NBC, Lester Holt was under {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2016/sep/26/lester-holt-debate-moderator-trump-clinton-fact-check-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 immense pressure}}}\uc2  at that point to do some live fact checks and pushback, which he did to some extent \u8211\'20\'13 but ultimately stayed {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/news/the-fix/wp/2016/09/26/how-lester-holt-handled-the-first-big-fact-check-moment-of-the-presidential-debate/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 focused}}}\uc2  on keeping the conversation going. When Trump won that election, media organizations were {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2020/jan/06/sleepwalking-into-2020-media-missed-donald-trump-rise-lessons-learned-2016"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 left to grapple with}}}\uc2  how they failed to take seriously his political rise \u8211\'20\'13 and weight of his lies.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.46am BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden has staked much of his candidacy on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights \u8211\'20\'13 but he didn\u8217\'20\'19t mention the issue in his closing statement.\par \par \uc2 Across the US, but especially in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jun/18/arizona-abortion-latino-vote"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 swing states like Arizona}}}\uc2 , organizers are hoping that the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights issue will galvanize voters who have started to cool on Biden. But the president didn\u8217\'20\'19t do much to return to the issue after answering the one debate question tonight that focused on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 Though Donald Trump claimed that overturning Roe v Wave was \u8220\'20\'1Csomething everybody wanted\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 numerous polls have found that Roe was popular when it was in place and the majority of Americans disagree with the decision to overturn in. Republicans who have advanced harsh \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions have been increasingly out of touch with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/article/2024/may/14/abortion-rights-support-poll"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 what most voters want}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.39am BST\par \par \uc2 Pressed by CNN anchor Anderson Cooper, Kamala Harris again acknowledged that Joe Biden had a \u8220\'20\'1Cslow start\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt was a slow start, that\u8217\'20\'19s obvious to everyone. I\u8217\'20\'19m not going to debate that point,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m talking about the choice in November. I\u8217\'20\'19m talking about one of the most important elections in our collective lifetime. And do we want to look at what November will bring and go on a course for America that is about a destruction of democracy, electing a man who has said he\u8217\'20\'19ll be a dictator on day one? Or do we want to continue on a course that\u8217\'20\'19s about strengthening America\u8217\'20\'19s economy, building and creating 15m American jobs, over 800,000 manufacturing jobs?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.36am BST\par \par \uc2 Harris acknowledges Biden's 'slow start' as she defends debate performance\par \par \uc2 In an interview with CNN, Kamala Harris defended Joe Biden \u8217\'20\'19s debate performance, and pointed out that Donald Trump spent plenty of time distorting facts and dodging questions.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhat we saw tonight is the President making a very clear contrast with Donald Trump on all of the issues that matter to the American people. Yes, there was a slow start, but it was a strong finish,\u8221\'20\'1D said Harris. \u8220\'20\'1CJoe Biden is extraordinarily strong on substance and policy and performance.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Pressed to comment on Biden\u8217\'20\'19s performance and Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 concerns that it only heightened voters\u8217\'20\'19 apprehension over his age, Harris said:\par \par \uc2 Ultimately, this election and who is the president of the United States has to be about substance. And the contrast is clear. Look at what happened during the course of the debate. Donald Trump lied over and over and over again, as he is wont to do.\par \par \uc2 He would not disavow what happened on January 6. He would not give a clear answer on whether he would stand by the election results this November, he went back and forth about where he stands on one of the most critical issues of freedom in America, which is the right of women to make decisions about their own body. He has been completely ambiguous and all over the place about where he stands on that issue, despite the fact that he hand-selected three members of the United States supreme court with the intention that they would undo the protections of Roe v Wade.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.25am BST\par \par \uc2 The decision of CNN hosts Dana Bash and Jake Tapper to altogether forgo fact-checking is being widely panned by journalists and political commentators:\par \par \uc2 enltrCNN = not meeting the moment.\par \par \uc2 The absence of real-time fact checking is the biggest failure of this debate.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Anthony Coley (@AnthonyColey) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AnthonyColey/status/1806503594805305474?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 28, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrSo much general angst about the lack of fact checking tonight. The after-the-debate correction of many misstatements (mostly Trump\u8217\'20\'19s) won\u8217\'20\'19t be heard by a lot of people who need to know that.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Not THAT Karen, thank you (@karenbates) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/karenbates/status/1806519224501997718?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 28, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrCNN's lack of fact checking and wooden questions are just as bad for democracy as everything else that's happening\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Will Bunch (@Will_Bunch) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Will_Bunch/status/1806500507319734582?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 28, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.19am BST\par \par \uc2 Former Obama campaign manager says Biden's debate performance 'a Defcon 1 moment'\par \par \uc2 In an interview on MSNBC, David Plouffe, a Democratic strategist who managed Barack Obama \u8217\'20\'19s 2008 campaign and worked in his White House, warned that Joe Biden \u8217\'20\'19s debate performance drew attention to his advanced age, which is one of his biggest weaknesses.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s kind of a Defcon 1 moment,\u8221\'20\'1D Plouffe said. \u8220\'20\'1CThe biggest thing in this election is voters\u8217\'20\'19 concerns, and it\u8217\'20\'19s both swing voters and base voters, with his age, and those were compounded tonight.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Though Biden is only three years older than Trump, Plouffe said, \u8220\'20\'1CThey seemed about 30 years apart tonight. And I think that\u8217\'20\'19s going to be the thing that voters really wrestle with coming out of this.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltr\u8220\'20\'1CDEFCON 1 moment\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Obama campaign vet David Plouffe on the fallout from Biden\u8217\'20\'19s debate performance.\par \par \uc2 Plouffe adds Biden did \u8220\'20\'1Chave a couple of good moments\u8221\'20\'1D but the \u8220\'20\'1Cconcern level is quite high.\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/SPi1pcIlDy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/SPi1pcIlDy}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 MSNBC (@MSNBC) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/MSNBC/status/1806526878720639419?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 28, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.21am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.08am BST\par \par \uc2 Biden says 'see you at the next one' despite Democratic worries over debate performance\par \par \uc2 While many of his allies were expressing concerns over his debate performance, Joe Biden headed over to speak to supporters at a watch party, and showed no indication of pulling out of the second debate scheduled for early September.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHe\u8217\'20\'19s just a liar,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said of Trump. \u8220\'20\'1C I can\u8217\'20\'19t think of one thing he said that was true, not being facetious. But look, we\u8217\'20\'19re going to beat this guy. We need to beat this guy, and I need you in order to beat him.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He concluded with: \u8220\'20\'1CLet\u8217\'20\'19s keep going. See you at the next one.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.03am BST\par \par \uc2 Trump hammered the issue of immigration.\par \par \uc2 Nearly every question detoured back to the topic.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s his signature issue, and his strongest issue with voters. Americans consistently tell pollsters that they believe Trump is better equipped to handle the border than Biden.\par \par \uc2 Voters rank immigration as a top issue, sometimes the top issue. Unprecedented migration at the US-Mexico border, and the sense that the Biden administration has failed to address it, has alarmed many Americans, including Democrats.\par \par \uc2 But for much of the debate, Trump simply played on those fears. He continued to wrongly {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politifact.com/factchecks/2017/aug/03/antonio-villaraigosa/mostly-true-undocumented-immigrants-less-likely-co/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 conflate crime and border crossings}}}\uc2 . He has vowed to carry out the \u8220\'20\'1Clargest\u8221\'20\'1D deportation campaign in American history.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.02am BST\par \par \uc2 Incumbents usually start off rusty.\par \par \uc2 There is no downplaying the full-blown panic within the Democratic party right now. But, if any are searching for a silver lining, they may remember that incumbent presidents often perform poorly in the first debate of their re-election campaign.\par \par \uc2 The reason? Presidents are the boss, the commander in chief. For nearly the past four years, they have given the orders and often aren\u8217\'20\'19t challenged. A debate puts them in a new, uncomfortable setting.\par \par \uc2 President Barack Obama famously had a terrible first debate against Republican nominee Mitt Romney in 2012, but came back to deliver a much stronger performance in the second debate and of course was re-elected.\par \par \uc2 Will Biden get a second chance to debate Trump this cycle? If worried Democrats have their way, probably not.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.59am BST\par \par \uc2 Democrats lament 'really disappointing' Biden debate \u8211\'20\'13 reports\par \par \uc2 The reviews from Democrats of Joe Biden \u8217\'20\'19s debate performance against Donald Trump are in, and they are not good.\par \par \uc2 The president\u8217\'20\'19s raspy voice, tendency to meander and difficulty finishing his answers have his allies deeply worried about his ability to beat Trump in the November elections, multiple media outlets have reported.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s how his former communications director Kate Bedingfield put it:\par \par \uc2 enltrJoe Biden's former communications director Kate Bedingfield, on CNN: "It was a really disappointing debate performance from Joe Biden."\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Sahil Kapur (@sahilkapur) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/sahilkapur/status/1806519605910802694?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 28, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 The Hill received an ominous text from a swing state Democrat:\par \par \uc2 enltrHoo boy. From one House Dem who hails from a swing state:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis was a disaster. Biden\u8217\'20\'19s team needs to convince him to withdraw and have an open convention.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Al Weaver (@alweaver22) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/alweaver22/status/1806519380626326014?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 28, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 Former top Barack Obama strategist David Axlerod said Democrats are so worried they may wonder if Biden should continue his campaign:\par \par \uc2 enltr. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/davidaxelrod?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @davidaxelrod}}}\uc2  on CNN post-debate, \u8220\'20\'1C there are gonna be discussions on if he should continue.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Andy Kaczynski (@KFILE) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/KFILE/status/1806519333398458865?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 28, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.21am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.52am BST\par \par \uc2 As expected, Donald Trump is far, far outpacing Joe Biden in making false and misleading statements.\par \par \uc2 (Trump even lied, at one point, about how much Biden lies \u8230\'20\'26)\par \par \uc2 This was also the case during the last two election cycles, when candidate Trump flooded debate stages with so many lies and so much misinformation that it became almost impossible for journalists and factcheckers to keep up. Tonight, he repeated several false statements, including that the US has the biggest deficit ever under Biden (Trump had larger deficits).\par \par \uc2 He pulled out of thin air the idea that Biden \u8220\'20\'1Cwants to raise your taxes by four times\u8221\'20\'1D (actually Biden proposed a tax increase of about 7% over the next 10 years), that Biden has been paid by China (there\u8217\'20\'19s absolutely no evidence of this). He claimed that 18m migrants entered the country during the Biden administration, not including the \u8220\'20\'1Cgotaways\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 citing a number he seems to have pulled out of thin air. (It\u8217\'20\'19s impossible to know exactly how many people entered the country without authorization but the total number of migrants entering both at ports of entry and apprehensions oustide of ports was under 10m. Some may have tried to enter more than once and about 4m were turned back.)\par \par \uc2 The former president also said that Biden has \u8220\'20\'1Cdestroyed our country\u8221\'20\'1D. That\u8217\'20\'19s a bit subjective \u8211\'20\'13 but given that I am fact checking this debate from an intact North American land mass in California, suggests the United States has not, in fact, been destroyed.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.46am BST\par \par \uc2 Trump attacks Biden as 'complainer' as debate concludes\par \par \uc2 The former president used his closing argument to attack Biden as having failed to change anything as president.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CLike so many politicians, this man is just a complainer. He said, we want to do this, we want to do that, we want to get rid of this tax, that tax. But he doesn\u8217\'20\'19t do anything,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said.\par \par \uc2 And then he shifted to his tried-and-true tactic of tying that to all his favored campaign subjects:\par \par \uc2 All he does is make our country unsafe by allowing millions and millions of people to pour in. Our military doesn\u8217\'20\'19t respect him. We look like fools in Afghanistan. We didn\u8217\'20\'19t stop Israel. It was such a horrible thing that would have never happened. It should have never happened.\par \par \uc2 Trump concluded by saying: \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re in a failing nation, but it\u8217\'20\'19s not going to be failing any more. We\u8217\'20\'19re going to make it great again.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.51am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.42am BST\par \par \uc2 Biden-Trump debate concludes\par \par \uc2 The debate is now over after 90 minutes of back and forth between Trump and Biden.\par \par \uc2 Trump walked off the stage, while Biden was joined by Jill Biden, and appeared to go down to speak to moderators Dana Bash and Jake Tapper.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.45am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.40am BST\par \par \uc2 Biden touts 'significant progress' after Trump's 'debacle' in closing statement\par \par \uc2 The candidates are now on to closing statements, with Biden up first and arguing that he had cleaned up a mess left behind by his predecessor.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19ve made significant progress from the debacle that was left by President Trump in his last term,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said.\par \par \uc2 He went on to say Trump \u8220\'20\'1Cincreased your taxes because of the deficit. Number one, he\u8217\'20\'19s increased inflation because of the debacle he left after where he handled the pandemic, and he finds himself in a position where he now wants to tax you more by putting a 10% tariff on everything that comes into the United States of America.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Biden ended by pledging to \u8220\'20\'1Ccontinue to fight to bring down inflation and give people a break.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.34am BST\par \par \uc2 Trump seems to indicate he will accept election results, with conditions\par \par \uc2 After trying twice more, moderator Dana Bash finally got Trump to say he will accept the election results. But in typical form for the former president, he included caveats.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf it\u8217\'20\'19s a fair and legal and good election, absolutely,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.30am BST\par \par \uc2 Trump declines to say if he will accept election results\par \par \uc2 Moderator Dana Bash asked Trump if he would accept the election results, and rather than answer, Trump more or less dodged the question by rambling about a variety of things.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWill you pledge tonight that once all legal challenges have been exhausted, that you will accept the results of this election, regardless of who wins? And you will say right now that political violence in any form is unacceptable?\u8221\'20\'1D Bash asked.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWell, I shouldn\u8217\'20\'19t have to say that, but of course, I believe that it\u8217\'20\'19s totally unacceptable,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said, seemingly in response to the question about political violence.\par \par \uc2 But he had more difficulty answering if he would accept the election, and never quite completed his response:\par \par \uc2 But the answer is, if the election is fair, free, and I want that more than anybody, and I\u8217\'20\'19ll tell you something, I wish he was a great president, because I wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t be here right now. I\u8217\'20\'19d be at one of my many places, enjoying myself.\par \par \uc2 He then went on to attack Biden and accuse him of putting the country on course for a third world war.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.25am BST\par \par \uc2 Fact check: Trump on the environment\par \par \uc2 Trump claimed he \u8220\'20\'1Chad the best environmental numbers ever\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 a vague statement that is impossible to fact check (what environmental numbers?).\par \par \uc2 However, here the many ways that Trump\u8217\'20\'19s policies made the environment dirtier and the climate warmer, compiled by the Guardian in 2020:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2020/oct/20/trump-us-dirtier-planet-warmer-75-ways"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 75 ways Trump made America dirtier and the planet warmer}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.23am BST\par \par \uc2 Biden has a cold \u8211\'20\'13 report\par \par \uc2 CBS News reports that Biden\u8217\'20\'19s doctor recently diagnosed him with a cold \u8211\'20\'13 which may explain his raspy voice and occasional coughing during this debate:\par \par \uc2 enltrWhite House official says POTUS was examined by his doctor, Kevin O'Connor, at Camp David in recent days, and O'Connor determined it was a cold. POTUS tested negative for COVID.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Nancy Cordes (@nancycordes) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/nancycordes/status/1806510506624311392?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 28, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.27am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.22am BST\par \par \uc2 Fact check: Trump accuses Biden of using the phrase \u8220\'20\'1Csuper predator\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Trump said that Biden called Black Americans \u8220\'20\'1Csuper predators\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The super predator theory in the 1990s suggested that a growing number of unusually violent young people, especially Black boys, posed a threat to the country. The theory capitalized on racialized fear and was used to encourage policies that led to the disproportionate incarceration of Black youth. There is no evidence Biden used the phrase or ascribed to the theory behind it.\par \par \uc2 However, his endorsement of the 1994 crime bill has justifiably come under scrutiny. Biden has defended the bill, and said that aspects of it were wrongly implemented. Here\u8217\'20\'19s context from 2020, when Trump made the same false claim about Biden:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2020/oct/17/joe-biden-race-crime-bill-1994-policing"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Things have changed\u8217\'20\'19: can Biden overcome the racist legacy of the crime bill he backed?}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.51am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.19am BST\par \par \uc2 'Destroyed our country' v 'most admired country in the world': debate highlights starkly different views of US power\par \par \uc2 A question about childcare led to a back and forth between Trump and Biden in which the Republican insisted that the country had been \u8220\'20\'1Cdestroyed\u8221\'20\'1D, while the president argued that things had never been better.\par \par \uc2 It was a clear encapsulation of the very different messages each campaign is pushing to voters as they seek to win their allegiance in November.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what Trump had to say:\par \par \uc2 Joe, our country is being destroyed. As you and I sit up here and waste a lot of time on this debate. This shouldn\u8217\'20\'19t be a debate. He is the worst president, he just said about me because I said it. But look, he\u8217\'20\'19s the worst president in the history of our country. He\u8217\'20\'19s destroyed our country.\par \par \uc2 Contrast that with Biden:\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19re the most admired country in the world. We\u8217\'20\'19re the United States of America. There\u8217\'20\'19s nothing beyond our capacity. We have the finest military in the history of the world, the finest in the history of the world. No one thinks we\u8217\'20\'19re weak. No one wants to screw around with us, nobody.\par \par \uc2 Both candidates have been saying variations of these themes for months, and will undoubtedly do so right up to election day.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.23am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.13am BST\par \par \uc2 Looming over the debate is a rightwing manifesto that will inform a potential second term for Trump.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/may/26/what-is-project-2025-trump#:~:text=Project%202025%20details%20across%20more,beholden%20to%20Trump's%20policy%20prescriptions."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Project 2025}}}\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1CMandate for Leadership,\u8221\'20\'1D an effort by the conservative think tank Heritage Foundation, outlines agency-by-agency policies that should be undertaken, if a Republican president wins. The project includes a lengthy playbook and a personnel database that hopes to set the government on a more conservative path immediately, should Trump win.\par \par \uc2 Democrats have highlighted the massive changes Project 2025 would entail, like staffing the government with political appointees, dismantling entire agencies, hindering reproductive rights and overturning policies that protect LGBTQ rights or advance diversity. Searches for the project have surged in recent weeks, and it\u8217\'20\'19s been the subject of a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/tv-and-radio/article/2024/jun/17/john-oliver-trump-second-term"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 John Oliver}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/tv-and-radio/article/2024/jun/17/john-oliver-trump-second-term"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  segment}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\u8217\'20\'19 s campaign signaled earlier today that the president could bring up the project this evening. The campaign sent out a press release announcing {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://joebiden.com/project2025/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a new website}}}\uc2  set up to explain Project 2025 and how it would affect the daily lives of Americans. The campaign also is running digital and outdoor ads in Atlanta to direct voters to its webpage about the project.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CProject 2025 is the plan by Donald Trump \u8217\'20\'19s MAGA Republican allies to give Trump more power over your daily life, gut democratic checks and balances, and consolidate power in the Oval Office if he wins,\u8221\'20\'1D the new webpage says. \u8220\'20\'1CTrump\u8217\'20\'19s campaign advisors and close allies wrote it \u8211\'20\'13 and are doing everything they can to elect him so he can execute their playbook immediately.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Trump has previously sought to distance himself from Project 2025, saying he isn\u8217\'20\'19t working with or tied to any one organization or its goals. But much of what\u8217\'20\'19s included in the playbook aligns with Trump\u8217\'20\'19s own plans, dubbed Agenda 47, that he\u8217\'20\'19s announced on the campaign trail or on his campaign website.\par \par \uc2 The Heritage Foundation has a history of getting its preferred policies enacted - its influence was cemented after Ronald Reagan used a previous version of its Mandate for Leadership as a policy Bible, of sorts. And Heritage has previously {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.heritage.org/impact/trump-administration-embraces-heritage-foundation-policy-recommendations"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 claimed credit}}}\uc2  for a bevy of Trump policy proposals in his first term, based on the group\u8217\'20\'19s 2017 version of the Mandate for Leadership.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.11am BST\par \par \uc2 Fact check: Trump\u8217\'20\'19s claim about the national guard on January 6\par \par \uc2 When asked about the January 6 riot, Trump deflected, blaming Nancy Pelosi for turning down a chance to deploy the national guard.\par \par \uc2 This is false. There is no evidence Pelosi got an offer to deploy national guard troops, and even if she did, she wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t have the power to turn it down. The president, defense secretary and army secretary have command of the Washington DC national guard.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.07am BST\par \par \uc2 The commercial break lasted about four minutes, and for that time only, the pool reporters who travel with Biden were allowed into the studio.\par \par \uc2 They report that the two candidates were staring silently straight ahead at their lecterns as photographers took pictures.\par \par \uc2 Trump took a sip of water, while Biden cracked a smile as the cameras flashed.\par \par \uc2 The debate resumed shortly after.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.17am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.05am BST\par \par \uc2 Biden has at times struggled to land his lines this debate, but managed to strongly defend his handling of the economy from Trump\u8217\'20\'19s attack.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C There was no inflation when I became president. You know why? The economy was flat on its back, 15% unemployment, he decimated the economy, absolutely decimated the economy. That\u8217\'20\'19s why there was no inflation at the time. There were no jobs. We provided 1000s and millions of jobs for individuals who are involved in communities, including minority communities. We made sure that they have health insurance,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.02am BST\par \par \uc2 Again and again, Trump has found a way to bring up immigration in response to just about any question.\par \par \uc2 Moderator Dana Bash asked both Trump and Biden about their plan to address racial inequities in the economy, particularly when it came to Black and Hispanic Americans.\par \par \uc2 Biden talked about his policies, while Trump brought up inflation \u8230\'20\'26 before, once again, bringing up the border:\par \par \uc2 He caused inflation, as sure as you\u8217\'20\'19re sitting there. The fact is that his big kill on the Black people is the millions of people that he\u8217\'20\'19s allowed to come in through the border. They\u8217\'20\'19re taking Black jobs now, and it could be 18, it could be 19, and even 20 million people, they\u8217\'20\'19re taking Black jobs, and they\u8217\'20\'19re taking Hispanic jobs. And you haven\u8217\'20\'19t seen it yet, but you\u8217\'20\'19re going to see something that\u8217\'20\'19s going to be the worst in our history.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.58am BST\par \par \uc2 CNN could face moderation scrutiny as Trump's false claims go unchecked\par \par \uc2 CNN could face scrutiny for deciding that moderators Jake Tapper and Dana Bash would not be fact-checking Donald Trump.\par \par \uc2 David Chalian, CNN\u8217\'20\'19s political director, had explained to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/cnn-presidential-debate-biden-trump-930d00479cd07b4069aff36d556b05b2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Associated Press}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CObviously, if there is some egregious fact that needs to be checked or the record needs to be made clear, Jake and Dana can do that. But that\u8217\'20\'19s not their role. They are not here to participate in this debate. They are here to facilitate a debate between Trump and Biden.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 But so far Trump has made false claims about January 6 and the national debt, about Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 plans to abort babies in the eighth or ninth month or even after birth, and that he presided over the \u8220\'20\'1Cgreatest economy in the history of our country\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Tapper and Bash have failed to push back, and it\u8217\'20\'19s difficult for Biden alone to counter every lie. The unfortunate upshot is false equivalence: Trump\u8217\'20\'19s lies seem to have just as much weight as Biden\u8217\'20\'19s truths, especially to viewers who might just be tuning into the election. It\u8217\'20\'19s a potential repeat of the disastrous CNN town hall with Trump last year.\par \par \uc2 Political commentator David Rothkopf tweeted: \u8220\'20\'1CThe lack of challenges from moderators has the effect of making it appear that the lies flowing from Trump\u8217\'20\'19s mouth are the same as the facts in which Biden is dealing.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.05am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.57am BST\par \par \uc2 And we are back.\par \par \uc2 The debate has resumed, after its first commercial break.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.56am BST\par \par \uc2 If this debate was an opportunity for Joe Biden to dispel concerns about his age, it will probably be a missed one.\par \par \uc2 While Donald Trump speaks, Biden, on the other side of the split screen, sways and closes his eyes. He speaks quietly and at times uncomfortably \u8211\'20\'13 and Trump is taking every opportunity to pounce.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, Trump has unleashed an ongoing stream of misleading and false statements, from his claims of broad approval for overturning Roe v Wade (\u8220\'20\'1Cthis is something that everybody wanted\u8221\'20\'1D) to claiming his administration oversaw the strongest economy in US history.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.59am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.53am BST\par \par \uc2 Fact check: Trump on the border\par \par \uc2 Trump said that when he left the presidency, the US had the most secure border in history, and later said \u8220\'20\'1Chardly\u8221\'20\'1D anyone was coming through. That\u8217\'20\'19s not true.\par \par \uc2 While migrant apprehensions have spiked under Trump, the increases began in 2020, during Trump\u8217\'20\'19s presidency. The reasons people were seeking to migrate include economic stress caused by the pandemic and natural disasters, long-running issues, including violence and political instability.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.52am BST\par \par \uc2 And now we have started our first commercial break, about 52 minutes into the debate.\par \par \uc2 The showdown wraps up at 10.30pm ET.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.53am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.52am BST\par \par \uc2 Trump says Biden 'could be a convicted felon as soon as he gets out of office'\par \par \uc2 Trump was asked if he would prosecute his political opponents, like Biden, if he returns to the presidency.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWell, I said my retribution is going to be success. We\u8217\'20\'19re going to make this country successful again, because right now, it\u8217\'20\'19s a failing nation,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said at the start of his answer.\par \par \uc2 But then he seemed to indicate that he would target Biden:\par \par \uc2 But when he talks about a convicted felon. His son is a convicted felon at a very high level. His son is convicted, going to be convicted probably numerous other times. Should have been convicted before, but his justice department let the statute of limitations lapse on the most important things. But he could be a convicted felon as soon as he gets out of office. Joe could be a convicted felon with all of the things that he\u8217\'20\'19s done. He\u8217\'20\'19s done horrible things.\par \par \uc2 That\u8217\'20\'19s partially a reference to Biden, and also to his son, Hunter, who was recently convicted on federal gun charges.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.47am BST\par \par \uc2 Now they\u8217\'20\'19re getting into it over Trump\u8217\'20\'19s recent felony conviction in New York City on charges related to making hush-money payments.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe only person on this stage is a convicted felon, is the man I\u8217\'20\'19m looking at right now,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said as he glanced at Trump.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.52am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.45am BST\par \par \uc2 Trump deflects when asked about role in January 6 attack\par \par \uc2 Trump was asked directly about his role in the January 6 insurrection, during which hordes of his supporters sacked the US Capitol in an effort to block Biden from becoming president.\par \par \uc2 The former president did not have much substantive to say in response, but instead tried to steer attention to his campaign planks:\par \par \uc2 Let me tell you about January 6. On January 6, we had a great border. Nobody coming through, very few. On January 6, we were energy independent. On January 6, we had the lowest taxes ever. We had the lowest regulations ever. On January 6, we were respected over the world, all over the world. We were respected.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.49am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.44am BST\par \par \uc2 Fact check: both candidates on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 Trump and Biden both repeatedly misconstrued or failed to accurately convey the reality of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law and medicine.\par \par \uc2 When moderator Dana Bash asked the candidates about \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Trump rushed to frame the Democrats as \u8220\'20\'1Cradicals,\u8221\'20\'1D falsely claiming that they support \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  up to birth. This is a common line of attack among Republicans \u8211\'20\'13 but it\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/sep/27/abortion-myths-republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 based on a myth}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Trump also repeatedly insisted that, by overturning Roe, the supreme court returned the issue of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  to the states, which \u8220\'20\'1Ceverybody wanted\u8221\'20\'1D. Roe remained popular throughout the half-century it was in effect. Some anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  activists have also argued that the federal government can use an existing law to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/article/2024/jun/20/comstock-act-democrats"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 implement a federal ban on \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2 . The US supreme court has also dealt with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/jun/27/supreme-court-allows-emergency-abortions-idaho"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 two \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  cases}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/jun/13/supreme-court-abortion-pill-access"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 so far this year}}}\uc2  \u8212\'20\'14 evidence that the issue is far from settled at the national level.\par \par \uc2 Biden also seemed to fumble his explanation of how Roe v Wade, which was overturned thanks to supreme court justices appointed by Trump, regulated \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . By the time it was overturned, Roe and its line of jurisprudence blocked states from totally banning \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  prior to fetal viability, the point at which a fetus can survive outside the womb and a benchmark that generally occurs around 24 weeks of pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.57am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.40am BST\par \par \uc2 Biden accuses Trump of wanting to pull out of Nato after Trump reveals Ukraine proposal\par \par \uc2 Biden hit back at Trump\u8217\'20\'19s proposal for Ukraine, accusing him of wanting to pull the US out of Nato and spark a broader war in Europe.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19ve never heard so much foolishness. This is a guy who wants to get out of Nato,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhat happens if, in fact, you have Putin continue to go into Nato? We have an Article Five agreement, attack on one is attack on all. You want to start the nuclear war, he keeps talking about, go ahead, let Putin go in and control Ukraine, and then move on to Poland and other places. What happens then?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.04am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.37am BST\par \par \uc2 Trump says he will get Ukraine war 'settled fast before I take office'\par \par \uc2 Trump claimed he could somehow resolve Russia\u8217\'20\'19s invasion of Ukraine prior to taking office, assuming he wins the November election.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI will have that war settled between Putin and Zelenskiy as president-elect before I take office on January 20. I\u8217\'20\'19ll have that war settled, people being killed so needlessly, so stupidly, and I will get it settled, and I\u8217\'20\'19ll get it settled fast before I take office,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.52am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.33am BST\par \par \uc2 Fact check: Biden on jobs\par \par \uc2 Biden said the economy had \u8220\'20\'1Ccollapsed\u8221\'20\'1D and that there were no jobs when Trump left office. That\u8217\'20\'19s a bit misleading \u8211\'20\'13 employment rates began to tick up pretty quickly after an initial dip at the beginning of the pandemic, before Biden took office.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.31am BST\par \par \uc2 Biden calls Trump 'loser' 'sucker' over reported comments on soldiers\par \par \uc2 Biden attacked Trump over his {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2020/sep/03/trump-american-war-dead-losers-suckers-report"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported comments}}}\uc2  that he called American war dead \u8220\'20\'1Csuckers\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Closers\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou\u8217\'20\'19re the sucker. You\u8217\'20\'19re the loser,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said.\par \par \uc2 Trump then denied that he ever made such a remark:\par \par \uc2 First of all, that was a made-up quote, suckers and losers. They made it up. It was in a third rate magazine that\u8217\'20\'19s failing, like many of these magazines, he made that up. He put it in commercials. We\u8217\'20\'19ve notified them.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.36am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.25am BST\par \par \uc2 Fact check: Trump on tax cuts\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump argued in favor of his tax cut, which he falsely claimed was the largest in history. In inflation-adjusted dollars, it was the fourth-largest since 1940, according to PolitiFact.\par \par \uc2 He also claimed he was ready to start paying down debt. According to the non-profit Committee for a Responsible Federal Budget\u8217\'20\'19s recent {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.crfb.org/papers/trump-and-biden-national-debt"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 report}}}\uc2 , Trump created about twice as much debt ($8.4tn) as Biden ($4.3th).\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.29am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.24am BST\par \par \uc2 'It's been a terrible thing what you've done': Biden attacks Trump over \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 Biden and Trump got into it over \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , with the president telling off his predecessor for his hand in the supreme court decision overturning Roe v Wade, and allowing states to ban the procedure.\par \par \uc2 Trump appointed three of the justices who supported that decision, and Biden told him: \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s been a terrible thing what you\u8217\'20\'19ve done.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The president went on to argue politicians should not have a part in women\u8217\'20\'19s health care":\par \par \uc2 The idea that the politicians, the founders, wanted the politicians to be the ones making decisions about my woman\u8217\'20\'19s health is ridiculous \u8230\'20\'26 no politician should be making that decision. A doctor should be making those decisions. That\u8217\'20\'19s how it should be.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.31am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.19am BST\par \par \uc2 Biden appeared to have trouble completing one of his answers, and then made a gaffe.\par \par \uc2 He was laying into Trump over his tax policies, which he said gave the wealthy a tax cut and deprived the government of revenue it could use to improve its safety net. The president then stumbled as he was running out of time to speak, before blurting out, \u8220\'20\'1CWe finally beat Medicare.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Trump immediately seized on it in his rebuttal to argue undocumented immigrants will bankrupt social security and Medicare, two major federal-run welfare programs for the elderly:\par \par \uc2 He did beat Medicare. He beat it to death, and he\u8217\'20\'19s destroying Medicare. Because all of these people are coming in, they\u8217\'20\'19re putting them on Medicare. They\u8217\'20\'19re putting them on Social Security. They\u8217\'20\'19re going to destroy Social Security. This man is going to single handedly destroy Social Security\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.21am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.15am BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump \u8211\'20\'13 as he\u8217\'20\'19s done several times in the past \u8211\'20\'13 re-upped his baseless claim of having the \u8220\'20\'1Cgreatest economy in the history of our country\u8221\'20\'1D during his presidency \u8211\'20\'13 especially before the pandemic set it back. That\u8217\'20\'19s not true.\par \par \uc2 Before the pandemic hit, economic growth during his presidency averaged at about 2.7% \u8211\'20\'13 that\u8217\'20\'19s good but not as good as the 4% average growth during Bill Clinton \u8217\'20\'19s administration.\par \par \uc2 Unemployment before the pandemic was as low as 3.5% \u8211\'20\'13 again, not as low as during Clinton\u8217\'20\'19s presidency.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.13am BST\par \par \uc2 Biden cracked a smile as Trump insisted that he had done \u8220\'20\'1Ca very poor job\u8221\'20\'1D of handling the Covid-19 pandemic during his term.\par \par \uc2 The former president turned to attacking Biden over what he said was an erosion of America\u8217\'20\'19s global standing during his presidency \u8211\'20\'13 before pivoting to other issues:\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19re no longer respected as a country. They don\u8217\'20\'19t respect our leadership. They don\u8217\'20\'19t respect the United States anymore. We\u8217\'20\'19re like a third-world nation. Between weaponization of his election, trying to go after his political opponent, all of the things he\u8217\'20\'19s done, we\u8217\'20\'19ve become like a third-world nation, and it\u8217\'20\'19s a shame the damage he\u8217\'20\'19s done to our country.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.24am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.10am BST\par \par \uc2 Jake Tapper then asked Trump about his proposal for a blanket 10% tariff on imports, and how he could prevent that from driving prices higher.\par \par \uc2 Trump replied:\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s not going to drive them higher, it\u8217\'20\'19s just going to cause countries that have been ripping us off for years, like China and many others, in all fairness to China. It\u8217\'20\'19s going to just force them to pay us a lot of money, reduce our deficit tremendously, and give us a lot of power for other things.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.07am BST\par \par \uc2 Biden spoke more quickly than usual as he answered that first question \u8211\'20\'13 perhaps because he has a limited amount of time to answer.\par \par \uc2 Now Trump is up, with his rebuttal:\par \par \uc2 We had the greatest economy in the history of our country. We have never done so well. Every, everybody was amazed by it. Other countries were copying us. We got hit with Covid, and when we did, we spent the money necessary so we wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t end up in a Great Depression, the likes of which we had in 1929 by the time we finished. So we finished, so we did a great job. We got a lot of credit for the economy, a lot of credit for the military and no wars and so many other things.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.05am BST\par \par \uc2 Biden answers first question by pointing finger at Trump\par \par \uc2 The first question from moderator Jake Tapper is about the economy, and specifically the inflation that has gripped the US during Biden\u8217\'20\'19s term.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhat do you say to voters who feel they are worse off under your presidency than they were under President Trump?\u8221\'20\'1D Tapper asked.\par \par \uc2 Biden immediately blamed Trump:\par \par \uc2 We got to take a look at what I was left when I became president, what Mr Trump left me. We had an economy that was in freefall. The pandemic was so badly handled, many people were dying. All he said was not that serious, just inject a little bleach into your arm, you\u8217\'20\'19ll be all right. The economy collapsed, there were no jobs, unemployment rate rose to 15%, it was terrible. And so, what we had to do is try to put things back together again. That\u8217\'20\'19s exactly what we began to do.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.12am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.03am BST\par \par \uc2 Biden, Trump take stage as debate begins\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden and Donald Trump have now both taken the stage at CNN studios in Atlanta to begin debating.\par \par \uc2 After winning a coin flip, Biden\u8217\'20\'19s team opted for the president to stand at the podium of his choice, and he will be on the right side of the screen. Trump will stand on the left, and has chosen to give the final remarks of the 90-minute debate.\par \par \uc2 Follow this blog for live updates, and you can also watch it below:\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.58am BST\par \par \uc2 With about two minutes until the presidential debate starts, here\u8217\'20\'19s the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/lauren-gambino"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Lauren Gambino}}}\uc2  with everything you need to know about how tonight\u8217\'20\'19s showdown will be run:\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/joebiden"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Joe Biden}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  will hold the first of two scheduled US presidential debates on Thursday, a high-stakes rematch between two well-defined political foes.\par \par \uc2 The earlier-than-usual confrontation will give both men a chance to make their case for a second-term to what could be one of the largest television \u8211\'20\'13 and internet \u8211\'20\'13 audiences of the election cycle.\par \par \uc2 Thursday\u8217\'20\'19s show down also carries the risk that Americans already dissatisfied with their options will come away even more dismayed. Polls show an extremely {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2024/06/25/upshot/introducing-2024-poll-tracker.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 tight race}}}\uc2  between the 81-year-old incumbent and the 78-year-old former US president \u8211\'20\'13 and both candidates remain broadly unpopular.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what to know and what to watch during the 90-minute primetime event, scheduled to start at 9pm ET inside a CNN studio in Atlanta.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jun/27/biden-trump-debate-what-to-know"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Biden v Trump: the first presidential debate of 2024, explained}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.53am BST\par \par \uc2 Political parties usually run someone fresh when they\u8217\'20\'19re trying to take down the sitting president \u8211\'20\'13 but that\u8217\'20\'19s not the case this year. The Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/alice-herman"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Alice Herman}}}\uc2  took a trip down memory lane to explore what happened the last time something similar to the Trump-Biden rematch took place:\par \par \uc2 When {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/joebiden"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Joe Biden}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  secured enough delegates to lead the Democratic and Republican party presidential tickets in November, they confirmed what many voters expected but fewer actually wanted: a redo of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2020/sep/29/us-debate-trump-biden-latest-2020-presidential-news"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 2020 election}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Republicans skeptical about giving Trump a second shot tried in vain to elevate a viable primary opponent. Powerful donors, including the Koch-aligned Americans for Prosperity Action, poured money into former South Carolina governor Nikki Haley\u8217\'20\'19s campaign, but Haley was unable to claw enough support away from Trump to pose a threat to the former president.\par \par \uc2 So for the first time in more than 50 years, the Republican party will rerun a candidate who already lost a general presidential election \u8211\'20\'13 the last time that happened was in 1968, when Richard Nixon, who had lost the 1960 general presidential election, ran again and won.\par \par \uc2 It has been even longer since a presidential candidate faced a true rematch.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jun/27/biden-trump-rematch-history"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 When was the last time two US presidents faced each other in an election?}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.57am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.46am BST\par \par \uc2 Several hundred protest ers have taken over a street corner across the I-85 connector in midtown Atlanta.\par \par \uc2 Most were calling for an end to American involvement in the Gaza war and for the president \u8211\'20\'13 or his successor \u8211\'20\'13 to call for an immediate ceasefire.\par \par \uc2 The protest at 10th and West Peachtree was organized by the Atlanta chapter of the Democratic Socialists of America.\par \par \uc2 zxxltr {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/ZVR67utQZy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/ZVR67utQZy}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 George Chidi (@neonflag) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/neonflag/status/1806481046176772106?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 28, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re joining with 15 other organizations who are united, standing in solidarity with the Palestinian people,\u8221\'20\'1D said Nate Knauf, a DSA organizer in Atlanta. \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re calling on both major presidential candidates Biden and Trump to support free Palestine to support an immediate ceasefire to end all military aid to Israel, to force Israel to end the genocide in Gaza. We know that the president of the United States has the power to end the genocide.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 A second protest is brewing closer to Turner studios across the highway. The organizer of that event is unclear; Knauf said his group was not involved.\par \par \uc2 Supporters of Robert Kennedy Jr. were also engaged in protest at the site, along with members of Peta, police accountability organizations and others.\par \par \uc2 enltrJawahir Kamil, 51, of Atlanta, leading protest chants ahead of the presidential debate in Atlanta. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/Qa0RnWeBOI"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/Qa0RnWeBOI}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 George Chidi (@neonflag) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/neonflag/status/1806480973480993029?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 28, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrA Jewish group protesting American involvement in the Gaza War. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/WzHr9VPuCP"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/WzHr9VPuCP}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 George Chidi (@neonflag) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/neonflag/status/1806481763403002001?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 28, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.56am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.41am BST\par \par \uc2 Republicans have lately been claiming, without evidence, that Biden will take some sort of performance-enhancing drug to make it through the debate.\par \par \uc2 The president is now dragging them for it:\par \par \uc2 enltrI don't know what they've got in these performance enhancers, but I'm feeling pretty jacked up.\par \par \uc2 Try it yourselves, folks.\par \par \uc2 See you in a bit: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/vD3mL9slj1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/vD3mL9slj1}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/Li4EM9mzve"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/Li4EM9mzve}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Joe Biden (@JoeBiden) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JoeBiden/status/1806486230084812937?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 28, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 Perhaps this will be the next Dark Brandon:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/may/03/joe-biden-tiktok"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Dark Brandon popping off: is Joe Biden\u8217\'20\'19s \u8216\'20\'18cringe\u8217\'20\'19 TikTok helping or hurting him?}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.38am BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden is on his way to CNN studios in Atlanta for the debate.\par \par \uc2 He had been at a nearby hotel for the past few hours ahead of the parlay with Donald Trump.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.31am BST\par \par \uc2 One question that will be on many viewers minds tonight: who will be Donald Trump\u8217\'20\'19s running mate?\par \par \uc2 Trump is expected to make the announcement any time between now and the Republican national convention in Milwaukee, starting on 15 July.\par \par \uc2 As the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/davidsmith"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 David Smith}}}\uc2  put it:\par \par \uc2 He has said his top consideration for a vice-president is whether they are qualified to take over as commander-in-chief. But history suggests that he will have five priorities: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jun/17/donald-trump-vice-president-criteria"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a \u8220\'20\'1Cfighter\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2  who can take on Democrats; a person who displays absolute loyalty; a candidate from \u8220\'20\'1Ccentral casting\u8221\'20\'1D who performs well on television and will be effective on the debate stage against Kamala Harris; a number two who knows their place and will not outshine him on the campaign trail; a go-getter able to raise vast sums of money for the campaign.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s who\u8217\'20\'19s likely on his shortlist:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/21/trump-vp-pick-shortlist"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Who will Trump pick as his 2024 running mate? A VP shortlist}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.56am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.21am BST\par \par \uc2 Trump and Biden seek breakthrough in deadlocked race\par \par \uc2 A feeling of stalemate has taken over the presidential contest thus far: polls have for months shown a very tight race between Trump and Biden, as well as an unusually low amount of enthusiasm for both candidates among the voting public.\par \par \uc2 The two campaigns are hoping that tonight\u8217\'20\'19s debate will bring the sort of breakthrough moment \u8211\'20\'13 a pithy remark, a catastrophic misstep by their opponent \u8211\'20\'13 that has catapulted others to the White House. Here\u8217\'20\'19s more on that dynamic, from the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/roberttait"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Robert Tait}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 It could be the moment when a rematch that few seem to want finally comes to life: like two ageing prizefighters, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/joebiden"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Joe Biden}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  will enter the arena of political bloodsport on Thursday evening to resume a verbal sparring bout that will revive memories of the ugly exchanges when the two {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2020/sep/29/us-debate-trump-biden-latest-2020-presidential-news"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 debated face to face four years ago}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 A CNN studio in Atlanta will host the first presidential debate of the campaign between the same two candidates who contested the last election, which Biden won.\par \par \uc2 With more than four months to go until polling day in November, it is the earliest in any US {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-elections-2024"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 presidential campaign}}}\uc2  that a debate between the two main candidates has ever been staged.\par \par \uc2 While some see the timing as premature, it could provide a chance to open up a contest that has become overshadowed by, among other things, Trump\u8217\'20\'19s recent felony conviction, as well as assorted other legal travails that see him facing 54 criminal charges for trying to overturn the last election and for retaining classified documents.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jun/27/biden-trump-presidential-debate"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Biden and Trump look to debate to open up race currently in a dead heat}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.56am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.11am BST\par \par \uc2 Debates are a fixture of presidential election cycles in the US, with unpredictable effects on campaigns, and popular culture. The Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/davidsmith"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 David Smith}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/rachel-leingang"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Rachel Leingang}}}\uc2  took a look back at some of the most memorable moments:\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/joebiden"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Joe Biden}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  will {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jun/22/biden-trump-presidential-debate"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 debate on Thursday for the first time}}}\uc2  this election cycle, and it holds the potential for some history-making moments.\par \par \uc2 Debates can inform voters on both the issues and temperaments of the candidates, potentially swaying an undecided voter toward one candidate\u8217\'20\'19s direction. They can also make for good TV, creating soundbites that resonate for decades to come.\par \par \uc2 From the candidates\u8217\'20\'19 physical appearances to gaffes to planned attacks to off-the-cuff retorts, here are some memorable moments from US presidential debate history.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jun/27/famous-us-presidential-debate-moments"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US presidential debates: the 10 most memorable moments}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.59am BST\par \par \uc2 The debate hasn't started, but the spin room is already spinning\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19re still more than an hour away from the start of CNN\u8217\'20\'19s presidential debate in Atlanta, but various besuited, well-coiffed, seemingly all male politicians are already in the spin room the network has set up, where they are \u8230\'20\'26 well, they\u8217\'20\'19re spinning reporters.\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19re talking about people like California\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic governor Gavin Newsom, who is thought to be a presidential contender some day:\par \par \uc2 And Republican congressman Byron Donalds, a potential vice-presidential pick for Trump:\par \par \uc2 As well as Corey Lewandowski, who was Trump\u8217\'20\'19s campaign manager for part of his first run for the White House:\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.45am BST\par \par \uc2 No audience, muted mics and commercial breaks: the rules and quirks of tonight's debate\par \par \uc2 There are a few aspects of this debate that are different from Biden and Trump\u8217\'20\'19s previous encounters, which were organized by the non-profit Commission on Presidential Debates.\par \par \uc2 For this election, the two campaigns opted to sideline the nonprofit and attend an event hosted by CNN, and the network\u8217\'20\'19s rules are a little different than those of previous years.\par \par \uc2 For one, there will be two commercial breaks during the event, but Biden and Trump\u8217\'20\'19s staff cannot interact with them while the cameras are off (one wonders if there will be any small talk between the two adversaries).\par \par \uc2 And then there\u8217\'20\'19s the fact that the CNN control room has the option of muting either man\u8217\'20\'19s microphone if they interrupt the other \u8211\'20\'13 which could change things for Trump, in particular, since he likes to talk over people.\par \par \uc2 Finally, there will be no audience in the studio, which means that if Trump or Biden lands a zinger, or flubs a line, you won\u8217\'20\'19t hear applause, gasps or laughs.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more from CNN on how this evening\u8217\'20\'19s debate will work:\par \par \uc2 enltrInside the first presidential debate: How exactly is this going to work?\par \par \uc2 We walk you through it all, from the stage, here: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/K5o6isqCPV"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/K5o6isqCPV}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Phil Mattingly (@Phil_Mattingly) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Phil_Mattingly/status/1806081626339975388?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 26, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.50am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.37am BST\par \par \uc2 When, and how, to tune in to the debate\par \par \uc2 The presidential debate starts at 9pm ET, and is being held at CNN\u8217\'20\'19s studios in Atlanta.\par \par \uc2 Just about every major broadcaster will be carrying it \u8211\'20\'13 or you can watch it on the home of the OG politics nerds, CSPAN:\par \par \uc2 enltrTONIGHT -- CNN Presidential Debate Simulcast \u8211\'20\'13 LIVE at 9pm ET on C-SPAN2 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/wNiRUGU77C"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/wNiRUGU77C}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/3hg8NNFUHE"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/3hg8NNFUHE}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 CSPAN (@cspan) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/cspan/status/1806278802567516528?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 27, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.47am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.31am BST\par \par \uc2 Biden and Trump to face off in first presidential debate in Atlanta\par \par \uc2 Good evening, US politics blog readers. All eyes are on CNN studios in Atlanta this evening, where Donald Trump and Joe Biden will be holding the first of two debates scheduled before the 5 November presidential election. Polls show that the candidates are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://projects.fivethirtyeight.com/2024-election-forecast/?cid=rrpromo"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 nearly neck-in-neck}}}\uc2  in the race for the White House, and that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.pewresearch.org/short-reads/2024/06/14/biden-trump-are-least-liked-pair-of-major-party-presidential-candidates-in-at-least-3-decades/sr_24-06-13_historical-favorability_1/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 many Americans are not pleased}}}\uc2  at having to put up with a rematch of the 2020 election, where Biden bested Trump. Since then, the Democratic president has seen his job approval sink, while Trump has been criminally indicted {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jul/28/donald-trump-investigations-criminal-charges-tracker"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 four separate times}}}\uc2 , with one of those cases resulting in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/may/30/trump-trial-hush-money-verdict"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 his conviction}}}\uc2  on 34 felony charges last month. There will be plenty to see in tonight\u8217\'20\'19s 90-minute showdown, but both campaigns are hoping for one specific event: a breakthrough moment that captures the public\u8217\'20\'19s attention, and gives Trump or Biden renewed momentum. We will see if that happens.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else we are watching out for:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Make no mistake: Biden can sometimes {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/mar/07/joe-biden-state-of-the-union-address"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 still give a good speech}}}\uc2 . But at 81, he is also the oldest president to ever serve, and has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/feb/08/joe-biden-surprise-speech-white-house-memory"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a tendency}}}\uc2  to garble his words and mix up facts. Will it undermine him on the debate stage?\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump, who, at 78, is similarly old, can also flop when it comes to speechmaking \u8211\'20\'13 just look at how he {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/may/31/trump-guilty-verdict-speech"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 rambled on}}}\uc2  after being convicted in his New York hush-money trial last month. How might he stack up against Biden, who always aims to stay on message?\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The format of this debate is unique in a few ways, since CNN is hosting instead of the non-profit Commission on Presidential Debates, which was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/may/15/biden-trump-debate-date"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 spurned}}}\uc2  by both campaigns. There will be commercial breaks, for one, and, in a break from Biden and Trump\u8217\'20\'19s previous encounters in 2020, when the then-president\u8217\'20\'19s over-the-top attacks {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2020/sep/29/us-debate-trump-biden-latest-2020-presidential-news"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 didn\u8217\'20\'19t do him any favors}}}\uc2 , CNN has the power to turn off their microphones if they start arguing. What might that lead to when the two men, who do not like each other at all, are in the same room for the first time in four years?\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.45am BST\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240628ek6r00002\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
