\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Joe Biden \u8216\'20\'18really fumbled\u8217\'20\'19 a winning issue for Democrats \u8211\'20\'13  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 Carter Sherman \par \uc2 1,071 \uc2 words\par \uc2 28 June 2024\par 20:11 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Far from delivering a slam dunk, the president couldn\u8217\'20\'19t provide a single coherent answer about the procedure\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden went into the Thursday presidential debate with one ace in the hole: \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . And somehow, in a fumbling and frail performance, the president managed to blow even that.\par \par \uc2 In the two years since the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  overturned Roe v Wade, a decision joined by three justices nominated by \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , support for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/article/2024/may/14/abortion-rights-support-poll"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 climbed even in red states}}}\uc2 . Republican strongholds like Kansas, Kentucky and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/nov/07/ohio-issue-1-abortion-rights-vote-result"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ohio have voted}}}\uc2  in favor of maintaining or even strengthening \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights; purple Michigan, a state Biden desperately needs to win, has too. The Biden campaign knows that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is a winning issue \u8211\'20\'13 that\u8217\'20\'19s why it has dispatched the vice-president, \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , on a nationwide, months-long tour to talk about it.\par \par \uc2 But instead of hammering Trump, whose administration paved the way for Roe\u8217\'20\'19s demise and whose potential return to power could lead to federal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions, Biden stumbled to give a single coherent answer about the procedure.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI supported Roe v Wade, which had three trimesters. First time is between a woman and a doctor. Second time is between the doctor and an extreme situation. And a third time is between the doctor \u8211\'20\'13 I mean, it\u8217\'20\'19d be between the woman and the state,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/nov/07/ohio-issue-1-abortion-rights-vote-result"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to a CNN transcript of the debate}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CThe idea that the politicians \u8211\'20\'13 that the founders wanted the politicians to be the ones making decisions about women\u8217\'20\'19s health is ridiculous. That\u8217\'20\'19s the last \u8211\'20\'13 no politician should be making that decision.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He continued: \u8220\'20\'1CA doctor should be making those decisions. That\u8217\'20\'19s how it should be run. That\u8217\'20\'19s what you\u8217\'20\'19re going to do.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 When the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  first decided Roe in 1973, legalizing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  nationwide, the justices implemented a kind of sliding scale of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, on which a patient\u8217\'20\'19s right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  could vary depending on their trimester of pregnancy. This may have been the framework that Biden was referring to, although his articulation of it is not exactly accurate (or possible to follow).\par \par \uc2 Biden abandoned his party\u8217\'20\'19s vigorous and effective attempts to frame \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  as a matter of freedom and rights\par \par \uc2 In any case, by the time the supreme court overturned Roe in 2022, federal law around \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions had changed. \u8220\'20\'1CRoe\u8221\'20\'1D, which is really more of the popular term for both the original Roe decision and the line of cases that followed, had come to essentially block states from totally banning \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  prior to fetal viability, a benchmark that generally occurs around 24 weeks of pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 By making it sound as though the state and doctors \u8211\'20\'13 whom Biden kept referring to using male pronouns \u8211\'20\'13 should get to decide whether a woman can have an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Biden abandoned his party\u8217\'20\'19s vigorous and effective attempts to frame \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  as a matter of freedom and rights.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThat was really fumbled,\u8221\'20\'1D said Tresa Undem, who has been polling people on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  for more than two decades. \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is, she continued, \u8220\'20\'1Cvery easy to communicate on right now, because a majority of the public is pro-choice, majority of voters are pro-choice. It\u8217\'20\'19s very easy. They don\u8217\'20\'19t want politicians involved in this decision at all. That\u8217\'20\'19s the bottom line.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 US elections 2024: a guide to the first presidential debate\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Biden v Trump: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jun/28/biden-trump-first-presidential-debate"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 90 miserable minutes}}}\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Who won the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jun/28/trump-biden-debate-memes-social-media"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 meme wars}}}\uc2  ?\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Biden\u8217\'20\'19s performance {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jun/27/biden-trump-debate-democrats-reaction"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sends Democrats into panic}}}\par \par \uc2 *\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jun/28/who-could-replace-joe-biden-here-are-six-possibilities"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Six who could replace Biden}}}\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump and Biden\u8217\'20\'19s claims \u8211\'20\'13 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jun/27/fact-check-debate-biden-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 factchecked}}}\par \par \uc2 Part of Biden\u8217\'20\'19s issue may be that the devout Catholic \u8211\'20\'13 who once said he was personally not \u8220\'20\'1Cbig on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/jan/26/biden-abortion-rights-expand-protections"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 does not have a track record}}}\uc2  of promoting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights. While he was on the campaign trail in 2020, his reluctance to even say the word \u8220\'20\'1C\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D frustrated \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights activists.\par \par \uc2 Trump, in contrast, stayed disciplined on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  during the Thursday debate. He repeatedly called it a states\u8217\'20\'19 rights issue and demurred on whether it should be legal in cases of rape, incest or medical emergencies. He glided past the fact that many states with near-total \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans do not permit the procedure in cases of rape or incest, and that a supreme court stacked with his justices had just {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jun/27/ketanji-brown-jackson-dissent-idaho-abortion-ban"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 punted on the legal question}}}\uc2  of whether states can {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/jun/27/supreme-court-allows-emergency-abortions-idaho"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ban abortions in some emergencies}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The former president also avoided mentioning that some anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  activists believe he could {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/article/2024/jun/20/comstock-act-democrats"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 use a 151-year-old law}}}\uc2  to enact a total \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban nationwide.\par \par \uc2 During another exchange, Trump spoke forcefully about how restoring Roe would mean that Biden \u8220\'20\'1Ccan take the life of the baby in the ninth month and even after birth\u8221\'20\'1D, as well as \u8220\'20\'1Crip the baby out of the womb in the ninth month and kill the baby\u8221\'20\'1D. It was language that Trump had deployed during a presidential debate with \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2 , to the delight of the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  movement.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/sep/27/abortion-myths-republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 These claims are based on myths}}}\uc2 . Infanticide is obviously illegal. The vast majority of abortions occur in the first trimester of pregnancy; those that happen after that point are often due to a medical issue. The \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights movement has worked for years to destigmatize these procedures and eradicate the phrase \u8220\'20\'1Clate-term \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D, which is not a phrase doctors use.\par \par \uc2 But Biden couldn\u8217\'20\'19t seem to figure out if he wanted to correct Trump\u8217\'20\'19s falsehoods or confirm them.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThat is simply not true. That Roe v Wade does not provide for that. That\u8217\'20\'19s not the circumstance. Only when the woman\u8217\'20\'19s life is in danger, if she\u8217\'20\'19s going to die \u8211\'20\'13 that\u8217\'20\'19s the only circumstance in which that can happen,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CBut we are not for late-term \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , period \u8211\'20\'13 period, period.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 There\u8217\'20\'19s little danger that staunchly pro-choice voters will leave Biden, according to Undem, since Democrats are so associated with \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights while Republicans are so linked to restrictions. But Biden\u8217\'20\'19s inability to talk about what should be a slam-dunk issue for Democrats may bolster concerns that he\u8217\'20\'19s just not up for a second presidency.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt was pretty dismal,\u8221\'20\'1D Undem said. \u8220\'20\'1CIt just seemed incoherent, not clear. At one point, he got the message in that politicians shouldn\u8217\'20\'19t be making this decision at all. But it was not great.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240628ek6s0025y\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
