\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Iowa supreme court allows six-week  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  ban to take effect\b0\par\par\uc2 Guardian staff and agencies \par \uc2 357 \uc2 words\par \uc2 28 June 2024\par 15:36 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Ruling reverses lower court decision that blocked 2023 law, exclusively backed by Republicans, from going into effect\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/iowa"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Iowa}}}\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s state supreme court on Friday told a lower court to let a strict \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law take effect.\par \par \uc2 The court\u8217\'20\'19s 4-3 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.iowacourts.gov/courtcases/20698/embed/SupremeCourtOpinion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ruling}}}\uc2  held that the law \u8211\'20\'13 which bans most abortions after about six weeks of pregnancy \u8211\'20\'13 does not violate citizens\u8217\'20\'19 fundamental rights under the state constitution, rejecting a lawsuit by \uc2 Planned Parenthood\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The decision reversed a lower court order that blocked the 2023 law from going into effect. The law {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jul/12/iowa-passes-six-week-abortion-ban"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 passed with exclusively Republican support}}}\uc2  in a one-day special session last July, making Friday\u8217\'20\'19s ruling a win for the GOP in Iowa.\par \par \uc2 Most women do not know they are pregnant at six weeks.\par \par \uc2 Republican-led states across the country have limited \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access since 2022, when the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  overturned the federal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights previously established by Roe v Wade.\par \par \uc2 For now, 14 states have near-total bans on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and four \u8211\'20\'13 now including Iowa \u8211\'20\'13 have implemented six-week bans.\par \par \uc2 Representing Iowa during oral arguments in April, attorney Eric Wessan said that the state supreme court had already indicated what is appropriate in this case when the justices ruled that there\u8217\'20\'19s no \u8220\'20\'1Cfundamental right\u8221\'20\'1D to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the state constitution.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis court has never before recognized a quasi-fundamental or a fundamental-ish right,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 But Planned Parenthood attorney Peter Im countered that there were core constitutional rights at stake that merit the court\u8217\'20\'19s consideration of whether there is too heavy a burden on people seeking \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt is emphatically this court\u8217\'20\'19s role and duty to say how the Iowa constitution protects individual rights, how it protects bodily autonomy, how it protects Iowans\u8217\'20\'19 rights to exercise dominion over their own bodies,\u8221\'20\'1D he argued.\par \par \uc2 Iowa\u8217\'20\'19s law had previously been in effect for a few days before a district court judge halted it. The state\u8217\'20\'19s Republican governor, \uc2 Kim Reynolds\uc2 , appealed, setting the stage for Friday\u8217\'20\'19s ruling.\par \par \uc2 The Associated Press contributed reporting\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240628ek6s00231\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
