\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Factchecked: Trump and Biden\u8217\'20\'19s presidential debate claims\b0\par\par\uc2 Rachel Leingang, Chris Stein,Maanvi Singh and Carter Sherman \par \uc2 919 \uc2 words\par \uc2 28 June 2024\par 15:13 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Moderators for CNN\u8217\'20\'19s debate took a hands-off approach, letting lies and half-truths remain unchallenged. Here are the facts on some of the false claims\par \par \uc2 Moderators in the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jun/27/biden-trump-debate-what-to-know"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 first presidential debate}}}\uc2  in 2024 took a completely hands-off approach to factchecking the candidates, letting lies and half-truths, most frequently from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2 , remain unchallenged.\par \par \uc2 The former president frequently ignored the questions posed by CNN moderators Jake Tapper and Dana Bash, instead talking about whatever he wanted. In a few instances, they reiterated the question and gave Trump a chance to answer it again.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/joebiden"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Joe Biden}}}\uc2  sometimes pushed back on Trump\u8217\'20\'19s claims, and vice versa, though not always with specificity beyond saying the other was lying.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-elections-2024"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US elections 2024}}}\uc2  : a guide to the first presidential debate\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Biden v Trump: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jun/28/biden-trump-first-presidential-debate"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 90 miserable minutes}}}\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Who won the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jun/28/trump-biden-debate-memes-social-media"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 meme wars}}}\uc2  ?\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Biden\u8217\'20\'19s performance {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jun/27/biden-trump-debate-democrats-reaction"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sends Democrats into panic}}}\par \par \uc2 *\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jun/28/who-could-replace-joe-biden-here-are-six-possibilities"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Six who could replace Biden}}}\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump and Biden\u8217\'20\'19s claims \u8211\'20\'13 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jun/27/fact-check-debate-biden-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 factchecked}}}\par \par \uc2 The light moderation left lingering lies, though the network said before the debate that the moderators wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t intercede.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CObviously, if there is some egregious fact that needs to be checked or the record needs to be made clear, Jake and Dana can do that,\u8221\'20\'1D David Chalian, CNN\u8217\'20\'19s political director, told {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/cnn-presidential-debate-biden-trump-930d00479cd07b4069aff36d556b05b2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Associated Press}}}\uc2  before the debate. \u8220\'20\'1CBut that\u8217\'20\'19s not their role. They are not here to participate in this debate. They are here to facilitate a debate between Trump and Biden.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Here are the facts on some of the false claims offered during Thursday\u8217\'20\'19s debate.\par \par \uc2 Abortion\par \par \uc2 The claim: Trump says Democrats support \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  until birth and that \u8220\'20\'1Ceverybody\u8221\'20\'1D wanted to overturn Roe v Wade.\par \par \uc2 The facts: Later abortions are a common line of attack among Republicans \u8211\'20\'13 but it\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/sep/27/abortion-myths-republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 based on a myth}}}\uc2 . Less than 1% of abortions in the US are performed at or past 21 weeks, largely because of fetal abnormalities or lack of access to care earlier in pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 And Roe remained popular throughout the half-century it was in effect. Some anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  activists have also argued that the federal government can use an existing law to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/article/2024/jun/20/comstock-act-democrats"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 implement a federal ban on \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2 . The \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  has also dealt with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/jun/27/supreme-court-allows-emergency-abortions-idaho"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 two \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  cases}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/jun/13/supreme-court-abortion-pill-access"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 so far this year}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 evidence that the issue is far from settled at the national level.\par \par \uc2 The environment\par \par \uc2 The claim: Trump had \u8220\'20\'1Cthe best environmental numbers ever\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The facts: It\u8217\'20\'19s not clear what \u8220\'20\'1Cenvironmental numbers\u8221\'20\'1D Trump is referring to, making it impossible to factcheck. But the \uc2 Guardian\uc2  has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2020/oct/20/trump-us-dirtier-planet-warmer-75-ways"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 compiled}}}\uc2  75 ways Trump made the country dirtier and the climate warmer.\par \par \uc2 Prescription drug reform\par \par \uc2 The claim: Biden oversold his prescription drug reforms.\par \par \uc2 The facts: Biden said seniors\u8217\'20\'19 out-of-pocket costs were capped at $200, but it\u8217\'20\'19s $2,000. The cap on insulin costs out of pocket are $35 a month, more than the $15 Biden claimed.\par \par \uc2 The border\par \par \uc2 The claim: Trump\u8217\'20\'19s border was the most secure in history.\par \par \uc2 The facts: Trump said that when he left the presidency, the US had the most secure border in history, and later said \u8220\'20\'1Chardly\u8221\'20\'1D anyone was coming through.\par \par \uc2 While migrant apprehensions have surged under Biden, the increases began in 2020, during Trump\u8217\'20\'19s presidency. The reasons people were seeking to migrate include economic stress caused by the pandemic and natural disasters, as well as long-running issues including violence and political instability.\par \par \uc2 The economy\par \par \uc2 The claim: Biden said the economy had \u8220\'20\'1Ccollapsed\u8221\'20\'1D and there were no jobs when Trump left office.\par \par \uc2 The facts: That\u8217\'20\'19s a bit misleading \u8211\'20\'13 employment rates began to tick up pretty quickly after an initial dip at the beginning of the pandemic, before Biden took office.\par \par \uc2 January 6\par \par \uc2 The claim: Trump deflected a question about the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-capitol-breach"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 6 insurrection}}}\uc2 , blaming \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  for turning down a chance to deploy the national guard.\par \par \uc2 The facts: This is false. There is no evidence Pelosi got an offer to deploy national guard troops, and even if she did, she wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t have the power to turn it down. The president, defense secretary and army secretary have command of the Washington DC national guard.\par \par \uc2 Tax cuts\par \par \uc2 The claim: Trump claimed his {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2019/oct/09/trump-tax-cuts-helped-billionaires-pay-less"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 tax cuts}}}\uc2  were the largest in history and that his administration had the greatest economy in history.\par \par \uc2 The facts: His tax cut was the fourth-largest since 1940, according to PolitiFact. According to the non-profit Committee for a Responsible Federal Budget\u8217\'20\'19s recent {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.crfb.org/papers/trump-and-biden-national-debt"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 report}}}\uc2 , Trump created about twice as much debt ($8.4tn) as Biden ($4.3tn). Before the pandemic hit, economic growth during his presidency averaged at about 2.7% \u8211\'20\'13 that\u8217\'20\'19s good but not as good as the 4% average growth during \uc2 Bill Clinton\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s administration. Unemployment before the pandemic was as low as 3.5% \u8211\'20\'13 again, not as low as during Clinton\u8217\'20\'19s presidency.\par \par \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Superpredators\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 The claim: Trump said that Biden called Black Americans \u8220\'20\'1Csuperpredators\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The facts: The superpredator theory in the 1990s suggested that a growing number of unusually violent young people, especially Black boys, posed a threat to the country. The theory capitalized on racialized fear and was used to encourage policies that led to the disproportionate incarceration of Black youth. There is no evidence Biden used the phrase or ascribed to the theory behind it.\par \par \uc2 However, Biden\u8217\'20\'19s endorsement of the 1994 crime bill has justifiably {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2020/oct/17/joe-biden-race-crime-bill-1994-policing"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 come under scrutiny}}}\uc2 . Biden has defended the bill, and said that aspects of it were wrongly implemented.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240628ek6s0008d\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
