\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Ketanji Brown Jackson\uc2  pens fiery dissent in  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  ruling: \u8216\'20\'18Facilitating suffering of people\u8217\'20\'19\b0\par\par\uc2 Carter Sherman \par \uc2 784 \uc2 words\par \uc2 27 June 2024\par 21:07 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18We cannot simply wind back the clock\u8217\'20\'19, the supreme court justice said of her colleagues\u8217\'20\'19 6-3 decision to dismiss suitUS supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s decision in Idaho \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  case\par \par \uc2 In a searing dissent Thursday, Justice \uc2 Ketanji Brown Jackson\uc2  slammed her fellow justices\u8217\'20\'19 decision to dismiss the case over whether a state can ban abortions to protect women\u8217\'20\'19s health, pointing out that the dismissal will drag out the case \u8211\'20\'13 and potentially endanger Americans.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWill this court just have a do-over, rehearing and rehashing the same arguments we are considering now, just at a comparatively more convenient point in time?\u8221\'20\'1D Jackson asked in a dissent read from the bench, a move justices tend to only make when they feel particularly fired up.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COr maybe we will keep punting on this issue altogether, allowing chaos to reign wherever lower courts enable states to flagrantly undercut federal law, facilitating the suffering of people in need of urgent medical treatment.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/jun/27/supreme-court-allows-emergency-abortions-idaho"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 case}}}\uc2  deals with whether Idaho\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, which only permits abortions in cases where a woman\u8217\'20\'19s life is in danger, violates a federal law known as Emergency Medical Treatment and Labor Act (Emtala). That law, which dates back the 1980s, requires hospitals that receive federal dollars \u8211\'20\'13 which is virtually all of them \u8211\'20\'13 to stabilize the health of patients who show up at their emergency rooms in the midst of medical emergencies.\par \par \uc2 The Biden administration had {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/02/idaho-abortion-ban-justice-department-sues"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sued Idaho}}}\uc2 , arguing that its \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban forced doctors to break federal law by leading them to withhold abortions until women were on the verge of death. The supreme court initially issued an order allowing Idaho\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban to take full effect but, in its Thursday dismissal of the case as \u8220\'20\'1Cimprovidently granted\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 indicating they should have never taken it on \u8211\'20\'13 the justices agreed to let Idaho doctors resume performing emergency abortions.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe cannot simply wind back the clock to how things were before the court injected itself into this matter. Our intervention has already distorted this litigation process,\u8221\'20\'1D Jackson said in her dissent. \u8220\'20\'1CWe permitted Idaho\u8217\'20\'19s law to go into effect by staying the district court\u8217\'20\'19s injunction in the first place, then allowed this matter to sit on our merits docket for five months while we considered the question presented.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Letting the Idaho case continue to play out will also impact the rest of the US, Jackson added. Although many states that ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  permit the procedure to protect women\u8217\'20\'19s health, a handful do have bans on the books that, like Idaho, only allow abortions to save a patient\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Clife\u8221\'20\'1D. These bans could conflict with Emtala, according to briefing in the supreme court case by the Biden administration.\par \par \uc2 Notably, Texas has also already sued the Biden administration over Emtala. The state\u8217\'20\'19s claim in that suit was that the landmark law protecting emergency \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access was \u8220\'20\'1Can attempt to use federal law to transform every emergency room in the country into a walk-in \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinic\u8221\'20\'1D. Courts have since sided with Texas, blocking Biden administration guidance about Emtala and emergency abortions from taking effect in Texas.\par \par \uc2 The dismissal in the Idaho case does not impact the Texas litigation. The Texas Emtala case could land in front of the supreme court as early as next term, \uc2 Nancy Northup\uc2 , the president of the \uc2 Center for Reproductive Rights\uc2 , told reporters in a call on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 A final decision in the case may not arrive until after the November elections. If \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  wins the presidency, his administration could decide to shift its priorities, change the executive branch\u8217\'20\'19s interpretation of Emtala and stop litigating the case, according to Nicole Huberfeld, a health law professor at Boston University\u8217\'20\'19s School of Public Health. If that happens, Idaho\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban may end up remaining as is.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAs someone who cares about access to care, this decision is just a temporary reprieve,\u8221\'20\'1D Huberfeld said. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s not the end of the line.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Jackson effectively sided with the 6-3 vote to dismiss the case, in that she agreed with the move to let emergency abortions resume in Idaho but said she would not have dismissed it as improvidently granted. To the extent that Emtala is in conflict with Idaho\u8217\'20\'19s ban, she wrote, the federal law trumps state law.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis months-long catastrophe was completely unnecessary,\u8221\'20\'1D Jackson said.\par \par \uc2 She continued: \u8220\'20\'1CThis court had a chance to bring clarity and certainty to this tragic situation and we have squandered it. And for as long as we refuse to declare what the law requires, pregnant patients in Idaho, Texas and elsewhere will be paying the price.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240627ek6r00335\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
