\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Supreme court says Idaho  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  ruling \u8216\'20\'18inadvertently\u8217\'20\'19 published online \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Chris Stein (now) and L\u233\'00\'E9onie Chao-Fong (earlier) \par \uc2 6,181 \uc2 words\par \uc2 26 June 2024\par 20:11 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 This live blog is now closed. For the latest on this \u8216\'20\'18inadvertently\u8217\'20\'19 published opinion, read our full report:\uc2 US supreme court\uc2  set to allow emergency abortions in Idaho \u8211\'20\'13 report\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.01pm BST\par \par \uc2 Closing summary\par \par \uc2 The supreme court {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jun/26/supreme-court-decisions-today-trump-abortion-updates?page=with:block-667c1f808f08fb1b8fd1727c#block-667c1f808f08fb1b8fd1727c"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 turned down an attempt}}}\uc2  by Republican-led states to block the Biden administration\u8217\'20\'19s coordination with social media companies on fighting disinformation, one of only two decisions the conservative-dominated panel released today. They still have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jun/26/supreme-court-decisions-today-trump-abortion-updates?page=with:block-667c181d8f0839bc2f003cac#block-667c181d8f0839bc2f003cac"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 yet to rule on cases}}}\uc2  concerning \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s prosecution for trying to overturn the 2020 election and the scope of federal government regulations, but will issue more opinions {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jun/26/supreme-court-decisions-today-trump-abortion-updates?page=with:block-667c24388f08fb1b8fd172c6#block-667c24388f08fb1b8fd172c6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 on Thursday and Friday}}}\uc2 . But perhaps an even bigger story than what the court actually decided is what it inadvertently decided. Bloomberg Law noticed that the court had accidentally posted its opinion in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jun/26/supreme-court-decisions-today-trump-abortion-updates?page=with:block-667c48888f08db81fc3252f1#block-667c48888f08db81fc3252f1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a closely watched case}}}\uc2  pitting Idaho against the Biden administration, and a 6-3 majority was going to require the Republican-led state to allow emergency abortions \u8211\'20\'13 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jun/26/supreme-court-decisions-today-trump-abortion-updates?page=with:block-667c4efb8f0879fc3d68dc1e#block-667c4efb8f0879fc3d68dc1e"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 at least for now}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else happened today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 House Republicans {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jun/26/supreme-court-decisions-today-trump-abortion-updates?page=with:block-667c33b18f08fb1b8fd1743d#block-667c33b18f08fb1b8fd1743d"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 convened}}}\uc2  a little-known congressional body to intervene on behalf of top Trump adviser \uc2 Steve Bannon\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s attempts to stay out of jail.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The supreme court once again overturned the ultra-conservative fifth circuit court of appeals, in its ruling over social media disinformation. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jun/26/supreme-court-decisions-today-trump-abortion-updates?page=with:block-667c272f8f08fb1b8fd1730a#block-667c272f8f08fb1b8fd1730a"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s why}}}\uc2  that\u8217\'20\'19s significant.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jun/26/supreme-court-decisions-today-trump-abortion-updates?page=with:block-667c3c7b8f08a8aaa70e4333#block-667c3c7b8f08a8aaa70e4333"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 claims}}}\uc2  he can get detained US journalist \uc2 Evan Gershkovich\uc2  out of jail in Russia, if he wins the November election. The Wall Street Journal reporter\u8217\'20\'19s trial began behind closed doors today.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Encounters at the southern border {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jun/26/supreme-court-decisions-today-trump-abortion-updates?page=with:block-667c6b828f0879fc3d68dd69#block-667c6b828f0879fc3d68dd69"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 dropped}}}\uc2  by 40% after \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  imposed restrictions that will temporarily restrict access to asylum seekers, the homeland security department said.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Progressives{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jun/26/supreme-court-decisions-today-trump-abortion-updates?page=with:block-667c520f8f08db81fc325383#block-667c520f8f08db81fc325383"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 are not pleased}}}\uc2  after congressman \uc2 Jamaal Bowman\uc2  lost his Democratic primary yesterday, and are training their ire on the influence of the \uc2 American Israel Public Affairs Committee\uc2  (\uc2 Aipac\uc2 ).\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.37pm BST\par \par \uc2 A group of Black campaign surrogates for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  met at a barbershop in Atlanta\u8217\'20\'19s Buckhead neighborhood Wednesday, ahead of the head-to-head between Trump and \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  here tomorrow.\par \par \uc2 Trump made a phone appearance to tout his accomplishments for the Black community while in office and his proposal to end taxation on tips.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CLet the people earn what they earn,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said, adding that he was aware he was talking to people in a barbershop who do tipped service work. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd it has been so popular beyond anything.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Both Trump and Biden are blitzing metro Atlanta with events leading up to the debate. Rocky\u8217\'20\'19s Barber Shop, a Black-owned business in Atlanta\u8217\'20\'19s more affluent neighborhood, hosted conservative Black leaders from metro Atlanta. Shelley Winter, a conservative talk show host here, asked Trump if he thought that CNN debate moderators Jake Tapper and Dana Bash would treat him fairly.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWell, I think it would be good for them if they did,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump replied. \u8220\'20\'1CI think probably not,\u8221\'20\'1D he added, expressing lingering ire about Tapper cutting off his televised victory speech after winning the primaries.\par \par \uc2 So they cover the whole primary, but they don\u8217\'20\'19t cover my victory speech. So am I going to get it fair? Probably not, but it would be very good for CNN. They\u8217\'20\'19re having a lot of ratings problems.\par \par \uc2 Two potential choices for vice president who did not need a haircut found themselves at the shop anyway Wednesday: congressman Byron Donalds (R-Fla.) and former housing and urban development secretary Dr. Ben Carson.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI just want to encourage you to continue to speak out because the attacks on you have been absolutely ridiculous,\u8221\'20\'1D Carson said. \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re praying that God will give you the strength to bear it because you\u8217\'20\'19re standing in there for all of us.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Donalds said we would see if he was Trump\u8217\'20\'19s vice presidential pick. Does he want to be vice president? \u8220\'20\'1COf course!\u8221\'20\'1D he replied.\par \par \uc2 Trump said on Saturday that he had already made up his mind about who he would choose to be vice president, and that his choice would be present in Atlanta for the debate.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.27pm BST\par \par \uc2 The number of encounters at the south-west border was down 40% in the three weeks since \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  announced new rules restricting asylum, the \uc2 Department of Homeland Security\uc2  announced on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 According to a DHS fact sheet, the average daily arrests over a seven-day period has fallen to under 2,400 encounters per day, the lowest level of encounters since January 2021. It is still not low enough to lift the order. Asylum processing resumes when encounters fall to an average of 1,500 encounters across a seven-day period.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s a remarkable feat that our personnel have accomplished in just such a short period of time,\u8221\'20\'1D DHS secretary Alejandro Mayorkas said in an interview on MSNBC\u8217\'20\'19s Morning Joe Wednesday. \u8220\'20\'1CCongress failed to act. The president has acted.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 But he said congressional action was needed to send more resources to border patrol and that without legislation the order could be lifted or reversed by the courts or a future administration.\par \par \uc2 Last week, CBP said encounters fell by 25%, meaning illegal border crossings dropped significantly since then.\par \par \uc2 Encounters were already on a downward trend before Biden\u8217\'20\'19s asylum order, due in part to a crackdown on northward migration by Mexican officials. Seasonal patterns also affect crossings.\par \par \uc2 Opponents have sued the administration to block the order.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.37pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.11pm BST\par \par \uc2 Cori Bush\uc2 , the Democratic congresswoman of Missouri and another prominent member of the progressive \u8220\'20\'1CSquad\u8221\'20\'1D, has issued a statement calling \uc2 Jamaal Bowman\uc2  her \u8220\'20\'1Cbrother-in-service\u8221\'20\'1D and attacking \uc2 Aipac\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s role in his primary defeat last night.\par \par \uc2 Bowman is the \u8220\'20\'1Ctrue representation of transformational leadership and brings \u8230\'20\'26 the power of everyday people from our communities to Congress each and every day,\u8221\'20\'1D Bush wrote.\par \par \uc2 AIPAC\uc2  and their allies\u8212\'20\'14backed by far-right \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  megadonors\u8212\'20\'14poured a tidal wave of cash into this primary race showing us just how desperate these billionaire extremists are in their attempts to buy our democracy, promote their own gain, and silence the voices of progress and justice. There should be no question about the need to get Big Money out of politics.\par \par \uc2 A recent {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/f/?id=00000190-5299-d9a9-a3b3-d2dfee860000&nname=playbook&nid=0000014f-1646-d88f-a1cf-5f46b7bd0000&nrid=974c5257-6792-4469-8156-8ab1101b4442&nlid=630318"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 poll }}}\uc2  shows Bush at risk of losing in her own primary contest for Missouri\u8217\'20\'19s 1st congressional district, one point behind challenger Wesley Bell. The pollster, The Mellman Group, said:\par \par \uc2 Bush is still seen favorably, but assessments of her and her performance are moving in a negative direction, while Bell\u8217\'20\'19s image is improving, leaving him with an underlying image advantage. With some six weeks to go and 11% [of voters surveyed] still undecided, this race can go either way, but Bell has achieved a slight advantage.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.58pm BST\par \par \uc2 Jamaal Bowman\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s primary defeat on Tuesday was a \u8220\'20\'1Closs for young people and anyone who cares about our continued movement toward justice, peace, and building a multiracial democracy,\u8221\'20\'1D Protect Our Power said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 The progressive group blamed \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Aipac\uc2  and the Maga billionaires who recruited and paid for George Latimer \u8217\'20\'19s campaign from start to finish\u8221\'20\'1D for the defeat, and vowed \u8220\'20\'1Cto tell \uc2 Aipac\uc2  they have no business creating division in our democracy\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 In a separate letter of protest, Jewish Voice for Peace Action (JVP) said it was \u8220\'20\'1Csaddened\u8221\'20\'1D by the results that had unseated a congressman who \u8220\'20\'1Chas been one of the few members of Congress committed to defending Palestinian human rights\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CToday is a sad day for American democracy,\u8221\'20\'1D said \uc2 JVP\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s political director, Beth Miller. She added:\par \par \uc2 To protect progressive candidates moving forward it is essential that Democrats reject \uc2 Aipac\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.46pm BST\par \par \uc2 Jamaal Bowman\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s primary defeat leaves progressives angry at role of \uc2 Aipac\par \par \uc2 Progressive groups are calling on House Democratic leader \uc2 Hakeem Jeffries\uc2  to reject the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://candidates.aipacpac.org/page/featured/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 endorsement}}}\uc2  and donations from the \uc2 American Israel Public Affairs Committee\uc2  (\uc2 Aipac\uc2 ) in the wake of congressman \uc2 Jamaal Bowman\uc2  \u8216\'20\'18s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jun/25/new-york-democratic-primary-jamaal-bowman"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 primary loss}}}\uc2  in New York.\par \par \uc2 The United Democracy Project, a super Pac affiliated with \uc2 Aipac\uc2 , dumped {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jun/23/democratic-house-primary-new-york-jamaal-bowman"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 nearly $15m}}}\uc2  into Bowman\u8217\'20\'19s district as part of its successful effort to elevate George Latimer to the Democratic nomination.\par \par \uc2 A coalition of progressive groups, outraged over \uc2 Aipac\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s involvement in the race, sent {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://drive.google.com/file/d/1ndE3VbfkBvPcqopFHHbpWRMSiEKLqeOa/view"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a letter}}}\uc2  to Jeffries today demanding that he reconsider his association with the group and denounce its tactics.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAIPAC turned the NY16 race into the most expensive Democratic primary in history, waging an\par \par \uc2 unacceptable assault on our democracy, our communities, and our shared future. We call on you to take action to address this threat,\u8221\'20\'1D the letter reads.\par \par \uc2 AIPAC\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s interference in Democratic politics poses a grave danger to the vision our organizations fight for every day: a future in which everyone can access a high quality education, comprehensive healthcare, a liveable climate, affordable housing, good jobs for good pay, humane immigration policies, human rights centered foreign policy \u8212\'20\'14 and more.\par \par \uc2 Latimer defeated Bowman by 17 points yesterday, and he is now heavily favored to win the seat in November, as the Cook Political Report {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cookpolitical.com/ratings/house-race-ratings"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 rates}}}\uc2  the district as solid Democrat.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.28pm BST\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights group \uc2 Reproductive Freedom for All\uc2  has said it agrees with Justice Kentanji Brown Jackson \u8217\'20\'19s reported reservations in the copy of the opinion briefly posted on the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s website.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is not a victory but a delay,\u8221\'20\'1D the group said in a statement responding to the court\u8217\'20\'19s reported decision to permit abortions in medical emergencies in Idaho.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans that are putting people\u8217\'20\'19s lives on the line in the first place will continue to remain on the books. We\u8217\'20\'19re grateful that the Biden administration is fighting to preserve the shreds of access possible in states where anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  extremists are doing everything in their power to block people from the care they need, even under the most dire of circumstances.\par \par \uc2 The group said it will not forget that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and the Maga Republicans are responsible for those bans, adding:\par \par \uc2 Our rights are on the line, and we must send President Biden back to the White House to restore the federal right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and end these bans once and for all.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.22pm BST\par \par \uc2 The copy of the opinion suggesting that the supreme court may rule to permit abortions in medical emergencies in Idaho may not be final and could be changed.\par \par \uc2 According to the copy {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2024-06-26/us-supreme-court-poised-to-allow-emergency-abortions-in-idaho?cmpid=socialflow-twitter-business&utm_source=twitter&utm_campaign=socialflow-organic&utm_medium=social&utm_content=business&sref=fqqmZ8gi"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 obtained}}}\uc2  by \uc2 Bloomberg\uc2 , a majority of justices will reportedly dismiss the case as \u8220\'20\'1Cimprovidently granted\u8221\'20\'1D, meaning the supreme court should not have accepted the case.\par \par \uc2 The ruling would reinstate a lower court\u8217\'20\'19s order that had allowed Idaho hospitals to perform abortions in cases where a woman\u8217\'20\'19s health may be endangered, according to the outlet.\par \par \uc2 Currently, the state\u8217\'20\'19s law only allows abortions when a woman\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Clife\u8221\'20\'1D is in danger. Idaho has sought to have \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  exempted from the Emergency Medical Treatment and Labor Act (Emtala), a precedent critics said would endanger pregnant people in any state that has \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions.\par \par \uc2 Although many states allow doctors to perform an emergency \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  when a woman\u8217\'20\'19s life or health is at risk, effectively mirroring Emtala, Idaho only allowed doctors to intervene when a woman was on the brink of death, a much higher bar for intervention. The Biden administration sued Idaho to enforce the law.\par \par \uc2 The Emtala law, signed by \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  opponent \uc2 Ronald Reagan\uc2 , sought to protect pregnant women in active labor in particular. Until its passage, hospitals often transferred or \u8220\'20\'1Cdumped\u8221\'20\'1D women who could not pay when they suffered an emergency on public hospitals, even when in advanced stages of labor.\par \par \uc2 Emtala had endured a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://immigrationforum.org/article/fact-sheet-undocumented-immigrants-and-federal-health-care-benefits/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 series of attacks}}}\uc2 , including by some hospital administrators who viewed it as an \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://westjem.com/editorial/why-the-emtala-mandate-for-emergency-care-does-not-equal-healthcare-coverage.html#:~:text=EMTALA%20was%20passed%20in%201986,be%20an%20%E2%80%9Cunfunded%20mandate.%E2%80%9D"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 unfunded mandate}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D. Although the federal government required hospitals to treat sick patients, it never provided money to care for indigent patients.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.06pm BST\par \par \uc2 Bernie Sanders has joined those blaming the \uc2 American Israel Public Affairs Committee\uc2  (\uc2 Aipac\uc2 ) for congressman \uc2 Jamaal Bowman\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s primary loss in New York last night.\par \par \uc2 Bowman, whose criticism of Israel\u8217\'20\'19s war on Gaza made him a target for pro-Israel lobbying groups, was defeated by George Latimer, a pro-Israel centrist, after \uc2 Aipac\uc2  and an affiliated group spent almost $15m to defeat him.\par \par \uc2 Sanders, in a statement today, said it was an \u8220\'20\'1Coutrage and an insult to democracy that we maintain a corrupt campaign finance system which allows billionaire-funded super PACs to buy elections.\u8221\'20\'1D He added:\par \par \uc2 AIPAC\uc2  and other super PACs spent over $23 million to defeat Bowman. He spent $3 million. That is a spending gap which is virtually impossible to overcome.\par \par \uc2 It is not a coincidence that with our corrupt campaign finance system we also have a rigged economy that allows the very rich to get much richer while many working people are falling further behind. Big Money buys politicians who will do their bidding, and the results are clear.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.16pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.51pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Congressional Pro-Choice Caucus has responded to the news that the supreme court {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jun/26/supreme-court-decisions-today-trump-abortion-updates?page=with:block-667c48888f08db81fc3252f1#block-667c48888f08db81fc3252f1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 may be poised}}}\uc2  to allow abortions in medical emergencies in Idaho.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe are all watching,\u8221\'20\'1D the caucus posted to X, adding:\par \par \uc2 With lives hanging in the balance, we hope this indicates a step forward for patients\u8217\'20\'19 access to emergency \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care.\par \par \uc2 Now, it is up to #SCOTUS to confirm that this is true and they will indeed protect that right and uphold federal law.\par \par \uc2 enltrWe are all watching. With lives hanging in the balance, we hope this indicates a step forward for patients' access to emergency \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care.\par \par \uc2 Now, it is up to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/SCOTUS?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #SCOTUS}}}\uc2  to confirm that this is true and they will indeed protect that right and uphold federal law. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/1KrfNLdhLs"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/1KrfNLdhLs}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Pro-Choice Caucus (@ProChoiceCaucus) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ProChoiceCaucus/status/1806011715932336524?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 26, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 Alexis McGill Johnson\uc2 , the head of \uc2 Planned Parenthood\uc2 , the country\u8217\'20\'19s largest \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  provider, writes that any decision that falls short of guaranteeing patients\u8217\'20\'19 access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care in emergencies would be \u8220\'20\'1Ccatastrophic\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 enltrWe're watching \uc2 SCOTUS\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 any decision that falls short of guaranteeing patients' access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care in emergencies would be catastrophic. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/ePzAf70bqq"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/ePzAf70bqq}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Alexis McGill Johnson\uc2  (@alexismcgill) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/alexismcgill/status/1806013474541092967?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 26, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.29pm BST\par \par \uc2 Supreme court says Idaho \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ruling 'inadvertently' published - report\par \par \uc2 The supreme court has acknowledged {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2024-06-26/us-supreme-court-poised-to-allow-emergency-abortions-in-idaho?cmpid=socialflow-twitter-business&utm_source=twitter&utm_campaign=socialflow-organic&utm_medium=social&utm_content=business&sref=fqqmZ8gi"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 to Bloomberg Law}}}\uc2  that the ruling in a case over whether hospitals in Idaho can be required to carry out abortions in emergencies was published by accident.\par \par \uc2 The court\u8217\'20\'19s public information officer Patricia McCabe told the outlet: \u8220\'20\'1CThe Court\u8217\'20\'19s Publications Unit inadvertently and briefly uploaded a document to the Court\u8217\'20\'19s website. The Court\u8217\'20\'19s opinion in Moyle v. United States and Idaho v. United States will be issued in due course.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Bloomberg Law goes on to report that the ruling is 6-3 in favor of the Biden administration, with conservative justices \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2 , \uc2 Neil Gorsuch\uc2  and \uc2 Samuel Alito\uc2  dissenting. However, the ruling is structured to allow litigation over the issue to continue, and not resolve the broader question of whether the federal government can require emergency abortions be performed in states where the procedure is banned:\par \par \uc2 The high court decision \u8220\'20\'1Cwill prevent Idaho from enforcing its \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban when the termination of a pregnancy is needed to prevent serious harms to a woman\u8217\'20\'19s health,\u8221\'20\'1D Justice \uc2 Elena Kagan\uc2  said in a concurring opinion.\par \par \uc2 Justice \uc2 Ketanji Brown Jackson\uc2  wrote separately to say that she wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t have dismissed the case, according to the copy that was briefly online.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CToday\u8217\'20\'19s decision is not a victory for pregnant patients in Idaho. It is delay,\u8221\'20\'1D she wrote. \u8220\'20\'1CWhile this court dawdles and the country waits, pregnant people experiencing emergency medical conditions remain in a precarious position, as their doctors are kept in the dark about what the law requires.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The posted decision indicates the court won\u8217\'20\'19t resolve broader questions about the intersection of state \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans and a federal law designed to ensure hospitals treat patients who arrive in need of emergency care.\par \par \uc2 The case is the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s first look at a state \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban since the conservative majority overturned Roe v Wade in 2022. The court on 13 June preserved full access to the widely used \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill mifepristone, saying anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  doctors and organizations lacked legal standing to press a lawsuit.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.24pm BST\par \par \uc2 A supreme court opinion in a high-profile \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  case that is revealed to the public before it is supposed to be?\par \par \uc2 If this sounds familiar, that\u8217\'20\'19s because it is.\par \par \uc2 Just over a month and a half before the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s ruling in Dobbs v Jackson Women\u8217\'20\'19s Health Organization, in which five conservative justices overturned the 49-year-old constitutional protections on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  created by Roe v Wade, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/may/03/supreme-court-abortion-law-leak-roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 someone leaked}}}\uc2  the majority\u8217\'20\'19s draft opinion.\par \par \uc2 To this day, it has not been revealed who was behind the disclosure, though there {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/2023/04/28/alito-leaker-dobbs-wsj/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 are}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://davidlat.substack.com/p/my-latest-theory-about-the-scotus"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 plenty}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2023/12/15/us/supreme-court-dobbs-roe-abortion.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 of}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.usatoday.com/story/news/politics/2024/03/24/stephen-breyer-leaked-supreme-court-opinion/73085383007/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 theories}}}\uc2  as to why someone would want to leak it.\par \par \uc2 In that case, the leaked draft generally lined up with how the court ended up ruling, and gave the public early warning that Roe was poised to fall. And indeed it did, setting the stage for states to ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and an array of legal battles to play out over circumstances in which the procedure should remain available \u8211\'20\'13 which is what {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/2024/apr/24/us-supreme-court-abortion-rights-emtala"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Idaho case}}}\uc2  is about.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more on the unsuccessful investigation into the Dobbs leak:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/2023/jan/19/us-supreme-court-leaked-dobbs-draft-opinion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US supreme court says it has not determined who leaked Dobbs draft}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.11pm BST\par \par \uc2 According to the eagle-eyed sleuths at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2024-06-26/us-supreme-court-poised-to-allow-emergency-abortions-in-idaho?cmpid=socialflow-twitter-business&utm_source=twitter&utm_campaign=socialflow-organic&utm_medium=social&utm_content=business&sref=fqqmZ8gi"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bloomberg Law}}}\uc2 , who somehow spotted the apparently erroneously published opinion in the Idaho \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  case, or had someone give it to them, the supreme court will dismiss the state\u8217\'20\'19s case as \u8220\'20\'1Cimprovidently granted \u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 That would reinstate a lower court decision allowing hospitals to perform abortions when the health of the mother is at risk.\par \par \uc2 The court did not respond to a request for comment from Bloomberg Law, which notes that the copy of the ruling is not necessarily the final decision.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.50pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.02pm BST\par \par \uc2 Supreme court inadvertently releases opinion requiring abortions in medical emergencies in Idaho - report\par \par \uc2 The supreme court today published an opinion, apparently by accident, that shows the justices will rule in favor of the Biden administration in a dispute with Idaho over whether hospitals there can be required to carry out abortions in emergencies, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2024-06-26/us-supreme-court-poised-to-allow-emergency-abortions-in-idaho?cmpid=socialflow-twitter-business&utm_source=twitter&utm_campaign=socialflow-organic&utm_medium=social&utm_content=business&sref=fqqmZ8gi"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bloomberg Law reports}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The opinion, which was later taken down, indicates the court will dismiss Idaho\u8217\'20\'19s challenge to the regulations and require federally funded hospitals to perform the procedure in emergencies, despite the state\u8217\'20\'19s strict ban on abortions.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.56pm BST\par \par \uc2 The day so far\par \par \uc2 The supreme court {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jun/26/supreme-court-decisions-today-trump-abortion-updates?page=with:block-667c1f808f08fb1b8fd1727c#block-667c1f808f08fb1b8fd1727c"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 turned down an attempt}}}\uc2  by Republican-led states to block the Biden administration\u8217\'20\'19s coordination with social media companies to fight disinformation, one of only two decisions the conservative-dominated panel released today. They still have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jun/26/supreme-court-decisions-today-trump-abortion-updates?page=with:block-667c181d8f0839bc2f003cac#block-667c181d8f0839bc2f003cac"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 yet to rule on cases}}}\uc2  concerning \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s prosecution for trying to overturn the 2020 election, the scope of federal government regulations, or emergency abortions, but answers could come soon: the court is set to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jun/26/supreme-court-decisions-today-trump-abortion-updates?page=with:block-667c24388f08fb1b8fd172c6#block-667c24388f08fb1b8fd172c6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 issue more decisions}}}\uc2  on Thursday and Friday.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else has happened today so far:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 House Republicans {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jun/26/supreme-court-decisions-today-trump-abortion-updates?page=with:block-667c33b18f08fb1b8fd1743d#block-667c33b18f08fb1b8fd1743d"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 convened}}}\uc2  a little-known congressional body to intervene on behalf of top Trump adviser \uc2 Steve Bannon\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s attempts to stay out of jail.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The supreme court once again overturned the ultra-conservative fifth circuit court of appeals in its ruling over social media disinformation. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jun/26/supreme-court-decisions-today-trump-abortion-updates?page=with:block-667c272f8f08fb1b8fd1730a#block-667c272f8f08fb1b8fd1730a"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s why}}}\uc2  that\u8217\'20\'19s significant.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jun/26/supreme-court-decisions-today-trump-abortion-updates?page=with:block-667c3c7b8f08a8aaa70e4333#block-667c3c7b8f08a8aaa70e4333"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 claims}}}\uc2  he can get detained US journalist \uc2 Evan Gershkovich\uc2  out of jail in Russia, if he wins the November election. The Wall Street Journal reporter\u8217\'20\'19s trial begins behind closed doors today.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is gearing up for his debate with \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  tomorrow in Atlanta, as are his allies.\par \par \uc2 In remarks to reporters today, Republican House speaker Mike Johnson made the argument, often repeated among conservatives, that Biden\u8217\'20\'19s energy levels are no match for Trump\u8217\'20\'19s:\par \par \uc2 enltr. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SpeakerJohnson?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @SpeakerJohnson}}}\uc2  on President Biden in the CNN Presidential Debate: "It doesn't matter if he drinks a whole gallon of energy drinks, he's not going to be able to match the acumen and the readiness of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , and that is what we expect." {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/iIrCEoG8x9"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/iIrCEoG8x9}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 CSPAN (@cspan) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/cspan/status/1805982555595759832?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 26, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19ll see who\u8217\'20\'19s right when the parlay kicks off tomorrow at 9pm ET.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.12pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump claims Russia will release jailed reporter \uc2 Evan Gershkovich\uc2  if he wins November election\par \par \uc2 The behind-closed-doors trial of Wall Street Journal reporter \uc2 Evan Gershkovich\uc2  begins today in Ekaterinburg, Russia, and the \uc2 US government\uc2  has decried it as politically motivated.\par \par \uc2 To \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , it\u8217\'20\'19s yet another thing he can use to convince voters to elect him over \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  in November. On Truth Social, the former president has alleged that he can somehow get Russia to release Gershkovich if he wins the election:\par \par \uc2 enltrEVAN GERSHKOVICH, the young Wall Street Journal reporter who is being harshly detained in Russia as his ESPIONAGE TRIAL is about to begin, will be released prior to my taking office if I WIN the Election on NOVEMBER 5th. Crooked Joe can\u8217\'20\'19t do anything right, although it is likely\u8230\'20\'26 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/qWdyz1vhu4"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/qWdyz1vhu4}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Donald J. Trump\uc2  Posts From His Truth Social (@TrumpDailyPosts) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/TrumpDailyPosts/status/1805980010370720104?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 26, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more on the start of the trial:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/article/2024/jun/26/evan-gershkovich-us-reporter-appears-court-closed-trial-russia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Closed-door trial of US journalist Evan Gershkovich begins in Russia}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.52pm BST\par \par \uc2 Shortly before a judge confirmed that he must indeed report to prison by Monday, \uc2 Steve Bannon\uc2  spoke for a very long time to the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/davidsmith"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 David Smith}}}\uc2 . Here\u8217\'20\'19s what he said:\par \par \uc2 It is not your typical man cave. Christian iconography. A bust of Julius Caesar. A painting of John Paul Jones, the revolutionary war naval officer. A book, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.penguinrandomhouse.com/books/131488/the-russian-revolution-by-richard-pipes/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The Russian Revolution}}}\uc2  by Richard Pipes, sitting on a crowded desk. A sign resting on the mantelpiece declares: \u8220\'20\'1CThere are no conspiracies, but there are no coincidences.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Welcome to the War Room, where the classical, contemporary and conspiratorial nourish {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2019/dec/17/steve-bannon-working-class-republicans-labour"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Steve Bannon\u8217\'20\'19s}}}\uc2  grand vision of himself as a historical figure. Each day he holds court in this basement on Capitol Hill to plot not only \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s return to power but the next American revolution. Screens, microphones and other podcasting paraphernalia sit above piles of books and newspapers, namely the Financial Times and New York Times.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI was a paper boy so I love papers,\u8221\'20\'1D explains Bannon, picking up his phone as he continues: \u8220\'20\'1CYou can\u8217\'20\'19t read it on here. It\u8217\'20\'19s not the same. First off, one of the most important things is the editorial choices. Very important how they place it, how they do it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The 70-year-old \u8211\'20\'13 once featured on the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://time.com/magazine/us/4657637/february-13th-2017-vol-189-no-5-u-s/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 front of Time magazine}}}\uc2  with the headlines \u8220\'20\'1CThe Great Manipulator\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1CIs \uc2 Steve Bannon\uc2  the Second Most Powerful Man in the World?\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 is constantly thinking about the media and shaping narratives. He believes that he wields more influence through his War Room show, which launched in October 2019, than he did working on Trump\u8217\'20\'19s first election campaign or during a brief, ill-fated spell as White House chief strategist.\par \par \uc2 His impact on the 2024 election is about to be severely disrupted: Bannon must report to prison by 1 July to serve a four-month sentence for defying a subpoena from the congressional committee that investigated {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-capitol-breach"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the 6 January 2021 insurrection}}}\uc2  at the US Capitol. That means he should be back on air just before the 5 November presidential election.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/jun/24/steve-bannon-war-room-republican"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Steve Bannon on how his War Room is shaping Republican narratives: \u8216\'20\'18We\u8217\'20\'19re relentless. I will never back off\u8217\'20\'19}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 House Republicans attempt unusual intervention as \uc2 Steve Bannon\uc2  fights to stay out of jail\par \par \uc2 Ever heard of the Bipartisan Legal Advisory Group (Blag)? Many people who watch Congress have not, but the panel has received an injection of prominence today from the Republican leaders of the House, who are attempting to use its powers to help influential \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  strategist \uc2 Steve Bannon\uc2  appeal his contempt of Congress conviction.\par \par \uc2 Bannon is supposed to report to prison by 1 July, after being convicted of charges related to defying a subpoena from the House committee investigating the January 6 insurrection in 2022. He is nonetheless {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jun/21/steve-bannon-prison"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 continuing to appeal}}}\uc2  his conviction, and that\u8217\'20\'19s where the Blag comes in.\par \par \uc2 The five-member panel \u8220\'20\'1Cis responsible for articulating the House\u8217\'20\'19s institutional position in legal filings with federal, state, and local courts\u8221\'20\'1D, and is composed of the top Republicans and Democrats in the chamber. Today, House speaker Mike Johnson, majority leader Steve Scalise and whip \uc2 Tom Emmer\uc2  voted to intervene in the case, over the objections of Democratic minority leader \uc2 Hakeem Jeffries\uc2  and whip Katherine Clark. Here\u8217\'20\'19s what the GOP had to say about that:\par \par \uc2 The Bipartisan Legal Advisory Group voted 3-2 to file a brief with the D.C. Circuit in the case against \uc2 Steve Bannon\uc2 . The amicus brief will be submitted after Bannon files a petition for rehearing en banc and will be in support of neither party. It will withdraw certain arguments made by the House earlier in the litigation about the organization of the Select Committee to Investigate the January 6 Attack on the U.S. Capitol during the prior Congress. House Republican Leadership continues to believe Speaker Pelosi abused her authority when organizing the Select Committee.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.36pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.14pm BST\par \par \uc2 Jerrold Nadler\uc2 , the top Democrat on the judiciary committee, saw the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s decision in Murthy v Missouri as a direct rebuke of Jim Jordan\u8217\'20\'19s campaign to characterize social media firms as complicit in censorship.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAs expected, the Supreme Court has issued a stinging rebuke to Jim Jordan and his multimillion-dollar conspiracy theory fueled witch hunt,\u8221\'20\'1D Nadler said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 He continued:\par \par \uc2 The Court concluded that the social media platforms \u8216\'20\'18exercised their own judgement\u8217\'20\'19 with regards to content moderation\u8212\'20\'14which is precisely what we have heard from the dozens of witnesses that Jim Jordan has dragged before this committee. The Court also pointed out that the basis for House Republicans\u8217\'20\'19 partisan reign of harassment against social media companies was inaccurate and outright false. I hope that after this humiliating defeat Chairman Jordan and his colleagues will end their failed investigation into the companies, universities, and individuals who have been trying to stop the spread of harmful misinformation and disinformation on social media.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.57pm BST\par \par \uc2 Jim Jordan, the rightwing Republican chair of the House judiciary committee, has been a prominent voice alleging that the Biden administration is censoring conservatives on social media.\par \par \uc2 The supreme court did not exactly weigh in on that claim, but did find that the Republican-led states who challenged the White House\u8217\'20\'19s contacts with social media companies in Murthy v Missouri did not have standing to sue. Here\u8217\'20\'19s what Jordan, who also chairs the subcommittee on the \u8220\'20\'1Cweaponization of government\u8221\'20\'1D, had to say about that:\par \par \uc2 The First Amendment is first for a reason, and the freedom of expression should be protected from any infringement by the government. Our country benefits when ideas can be tested and debated fairly on their merits, whether online or in the halls of Congress.\par \par \uc2 The Committee and the Select Subcommittee on the Weaponization of the Federal Government have uncovered how and the extent to which the Biden Administration engaged in a censorship campaign in violation of the First Amendment. While we respectfully disagree with the Court\u8217\'20\'19s decision, our investigation has shown the need for legislative reforms, such as the Censorship Accountability Act, to better protect Americans harmed by the unconstitutional censorship-industrial complex. Our important work will continue.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.41pm BST\par \par \uc2 An emerging pattern: ultra-right fifth circuit court of appeals v \uc2 US supreme court\par \par \uc2 With the Murthy v Missouri ruling, we are seeing the emergence of an interesting and potentially critical pattern involving relations between the ultra-right fifth circuit court of appeals and the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In both today\u8217\'20\'19s decision and the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/jun/13/supreme-court-abortion-pill-access"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 momentous opinion}}}\uc2  earlier this month to allow continued access to the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill mifepristone, the supreme court slapped down the fifth circuit on grounds of standing. They found that the appeals court had been mistaken in allowing the cases to proceed, because the challengers in each case were not directly injured by the actions to which they objected.\par \par \uc2 The fifth circuit is the most hard rightwing court in the country \u8211\'20\'13 of its 17 active judges, six were appointed by \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . As a result, it has become a channel for Maga legal actions, with rightwing activists creating extreme cases designed expressly for the court.\par \par \uc2 Take the mifepristone case. Anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  activists picked a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/feb/10/judge-abortion-pill-ruling-trump-appointed-matthew-kacsmaryk"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 particular judge in Texas}}}\uc2  with a known hard-right track record, knowing that he would side with them and that the case would then go through the fifth circuit up to the supreme court.\par \par \uc2 That a majority of the court has seen through this tactic and rebuffed it in both the mifepristone and today\u8217\'20\'19s Murthy ruling is a sign that the wildest extremities of far-right legal thinking are not yet upon us. But watch this space.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.13pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.24pm BST\par \par \uc2 More supreme court rulings expected on Thursday, Friday\par \par \uc2 The supreme court has just wrapped up releasing decisions for the day, but they\u8217\'20\'19re far from finished.\par \par \uc2 There are just under a dozen matters the nine justices have yet to weigh in on, but we will hear from them soon: the court has scheduled tomorrow and Friday as days to release more opinions.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.22pm BST\par \par \uc2 The last opinion of the day is Snyder v US, which deals with federal bribery law, and is not among the politically charged matters the court is considering.\par \par \uc2 The court\u8217\'20\'19s six conservatives have found in favor of the former mayor of an Indiana city, who challenged his conviction for bribery by arguing the money he was prosecuted for receiving does not violate federal law. The three liberals dissented.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.10pm BST\par \par \uc2 Here is the lineup of justices that concurred and dissented in Murthy v Missouri:\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://interactive.guim.co.uk/uploader/embed/2024/06/archive-zip/giv-13425fIrVY8X2xiqz/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Interactive}}}\uc2  The majority and minority in Murthy v Missouri.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.09pm BST\par \par \uc2 Much as with the conservative attempt to roll back the availability of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  medication mifepristone, the decision in Murthy v Missouri over the Biden administration\u8217\'20\'19s contacts with social media firms hinged on whether the justices believed the plaintiffs had standing to sue.\par \par \uc2 Writing for the majority, conservative justice \uc2 Amy Coney Barrett\uc2  found that they did not:\par \par \uc2 The plaintiffs, two States and five social-media users, sued dozens of Executive Branch officials and agencies, alleging that they pressured the platforms to suppress protected speech in violation of the First Amendment. The Fifth Circuit agreed, concluding that the officials\u8217\'20\'19 communications rendered them responsible for the private platforms\u8217\'20\'19 moderation decisions. It then affirmed a sweeping preliminary injunction.\par \par \uc2 The Fifth Circuit was wrong to do so. To establish standing, the plaintiffs must demonstrate a substantial risk that, in the near future, they will suffer an injury that is traceable to a Government defendant and redressable by the injunction they seek. Because no plaintiff has carried that burden, none has standing to seek a preliminary injunction.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.05pm BST\par \par \uc2 Supreme court rejects conservative challenge to Biden administration's contacts with social media companies\par \par \uc2 In their first decision of the day, the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s liberals and some conservatives banded together to reject a challenge, brought by Republican-led states, to efforts by the Biden administration to work with social media companies in combatting misinformation over the coronavirus.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more on the case:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2024/mar/18/us-supreme-court-social-media-case-free-speech-covid"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US supreme court hears case on government\u8217\'20\'19s power over online misinformation}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.56pm BST\par \par \uc2 New supreme court decisions are imminent\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s almost 10am in Washington DC, when the supreme court will begin issuing decisions.\par \par \uc2 We don\u8217\'20\'19t know which cases they will rule on in advance, but will let you know what they are as they come out.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.56pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.46pm BST\par \par \uc2 Guns, Trump and \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 : the supreme court's major decisions thus far\par \par \uc2 In about half an hour, the supreme court may release one or multiple decisions with major impact on US politics and policies. But the conservative-dominated panel has already handed down several important rulings this term so far. Here are a few of them:\par \par \uc2 In March, it rejected a challenge to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s presence on Colorado\u8217\'20\'19s ballot, putting an end to efforts by advocacy groups to bar him from running for trying to overturn the 2020 election. The decision was unanimous, and in their opinions, the justices avoided weighing on whether they believed he was guilty of insurrection:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/2024/mar/04/us-supreme-court-14th-amendment-key-takeaways"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US supreme court ruling on Trump ballot ban: five key takeaways}}}\par \par \uc2 Earlier this month, the court rejected a challenge to the availability of mifepristone, a common \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill, again unanimously. That all the justices signed on to the decision wasn\u8217\'20\'19t an indication of broad agreement over \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but rather the view that the groups who brought the case did not have standing to sue:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/jun/13/supreme-court-abortion-pill-access"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US supreme court unanimously upholds access to \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  pill mifepristone}}}\par \par \uc2 Last week, the court\u8217\'20\'19s three liberals and five of its six conservatives joined together to uphold a federal law that prohibited gun possession by people under a domestic violence restraining order, in a case gun control advocates feared could be used to further erode controls on firearms:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/jun/21/supreme-court-domestic-violence-gun-ban"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US supreme court upholds ban on domestic abusers possessing guns}}}\par \par \uc2 But the three liberals were in the minority earlier in the month, when the conservatives overturned a Trump-era ban on \u8220\'20\'1Cbump stocks\u8221\'20\'1D, a device that can make weapons fire rapidly, and was used in the deadliest mass shooting in US history:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/ng-interactive/2024/jun/14/supreme-court-bump-stock-ban-decision"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US supreme court strikes down federal ban on \u8216\'20\'18bump stock\u8217\'20\'19 devices for guns}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.25pm BST\par \par \uc2 Supreme court may issue potentially blockbuster decisions on Trump, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and federal regulation\par \par \uc2 Good morning, US politics blog readers. We are bracing for a morning that begins with a relative bang, when the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 supreme court }}}\uc2  releases another batch of opinions at 10am ET. The court, where conservatives have a six-justice supermajority and liberals a three-justice minority, has been steadily working through its backlog of undecided cases over the past weeks \u8211\'20\'13 meaning that most of the outstanding matters carry significant political weight. Among these are \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/25/supreme-court-trump-immunity-claim"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 petition for immunity}}}\uc2  from the federal charges brought against him for trying to overturn the 2020 election, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/2024/apr/24/us-supreme-court-abortion-rights-emtala"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the squabble}}}\uc2  between the Biden administration and Idaho over whether states can be required to carry out emergency abortions, and cases that could {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/article/2024/may/31/chevron-deference-doctrine-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 upend federal regulations}}}\uc2 , and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2024/feb/26/social-media-moderation-us-supreme-court-case"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 social media moderation}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 It is unlikely that decisions on all of these cases will come out today, since the court has also scheduled Thursday and Friday to release more opinions. We won\u8217\'20\'19t know in advance how many cases have been decided, or on which subjects, but chances seem good for at least one major decision to be published. We will be blogging live as they are released.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else is going on today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Washington DC will be digesting the fallout from yesterday\u8217\'20\'19s primaries in Colorado, Utah and New York, as well as runoffs in South Carolina. Progressive {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jun/25/new-york-democratic-primary-jamaal-bowman"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Jamaal Bowman}}}\uc2  is on his way out of the House of Representatives after losing his primary, rightwing star {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jun/25/colorado-primary-election-boebert"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Lauren Boebert}}}\uc2  has succeeded in winning the GOP primary in a deeply conservative Colorado district, and several Trump-backed candidates were turned away by voters in different states.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 House Republicans are attempting an unusual procedural tactic to prevent top Trump ally {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/jun/24/steve-bannon-war-room-republican"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Steve Bannon}}}\uc2  from having to report to prison by Monday to serve his four-month sentence for contempt of Congress.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Julian Assange is back in Australia, ending the \uc2 WikiLeaks\uc2  founder\u8217\'20\'19s long and controversial entanglement with the US justice system. Follow {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/media/live/2024/jun/26/julian-assange-live-news-wikileaks-founder-lands-on-us-island-of-saipan-for-district-court-sentencing"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 our live blog}}}\uc2  for the latest.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.59pm BST\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240626ek6q001s1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
