\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18A healthcare crisis\u8217\'20\'19: Harris takes aim at Trump on anniversary of Roe\u8217\'20\'19s fall\b0\par\par\uc2 Robert Tait in Washington, Lauren Gambino in College Park, Maryland, and Carter Sherman in New York \par \uc2 1,096 \uc2 words\par \uc2 24 June 2024\par 20:59 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Biden and Harris give forceful campaign statements blaming Trump for ending right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  marked the second anniversary of the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  ruling that overturned {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Roe v Wade}}}\uc2  with forceful campaign statements that laid the blame squarely on \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  for ending the national right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In a video released on Monday, Biden pledged to restore the right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and \u8220\'20\'1Cprotect American freedom\u8221\'20\'1D if he is re-elected.\par \par \uc2 The video, along with a campaign event headlined by the vice-president, came two years to the day since the court\u8217\'20\'19s decision in Dobbs v Jackson Women\u8217\'20\'19s Health Organization reversed nearly half a century of guaranteed federal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, and reflect the centrality of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Biden\u8217\'20\'19s presidential campaign.\par \par \uc2 In College Park, Maryland, Harris took the stage to chants of \u8220\'20\'1Cfour more years\u8221\'20\'1D. In her remarks, Harris laid out what she said were the stakes for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access if Trump is re-elected.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CUnderstand as much harm as he has already caused, a second Trump term would be even worse,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CHis friends in the \uc2 United States Congress\uc2  are trying to pass a national ban that would outlaw \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in every single state \u8211\'20\'13 in states like New York and California, and even right here in Maryland.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Nodding to her background as a prosecutor, Harris called Trump\u8217\'20\'19s attack on women\u8217\'20\'19s reproductive rights \u8220\'20\'1Cpremeditated\u8221\'20\'1D and said he has \u8220\'20\'1Cnot denied, much less shown remorse, for his actions\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn the case of the stealing of reproductive freedom from the women of America, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is guilty,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 Harris called Republicans who have passed state-level bans Trump\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Caccomplices\u8221\'20\'1D and warned that he would go even further by curtailing access to contraception and IVF.\par \par \uc2 "Enough with the gaslighting," Harris says of Trump's wavering stance on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\u8212\'20\'14 Lauren Gambino (@laurenegambino) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/laurenegambino/status/1805270599234654545?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 24, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 Pointing to the statistic that one in three American women live in a state with \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions, she said: \u8220\'20\'1CToday our daughters know fewer rights than their grandmothers. This is a healthcare crisis, and we all know who to blame: \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Kate Cox, the Texas woman who was denied an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  under the state\u8217\'20\'19s near-total ban last year despite a fatal fetal anomaly, introduced Harris in Maryland.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMy state chose to drive me out of my home, my community, away from my children and my doctors, rather than to let me access care,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CI will never again miss an opportunity to vote. I will cast my ballot in every election like my life depends on it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Cox {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/dec/11/texas-abortion-kate-cox-lawsuit"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ultimately left }}}\uc2  Texas to receive care. Growing emotional from the stage on Monday, she shared that she is pregnant again, expecting a child in January. The crowd erupted in applause. \u8220\'20\'1CI hope that by then, when we welcome our baby into the world, we will have a world led by \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou are a hero of this movement,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris told Cox.\par \par \uc2 In Biden\u8217\'20\'19s video, the president, too, placed the responsibility for reversing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights on Trump, quoting him boasting about the decision and taking credit for putting three conservative justices on the court.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHere\u8217\'20\'19s what \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  says about your freedom: \u8216\'20\'18After 50 years of failure, with nobody coming even close, I was able to kill Roe v Wade,\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D Biden says, quoting a Trump statement last year.\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is proud to have overturned Roe v. Wade.\par \par \uc2 We know what will happen if he gets another four years in the White House: He\u8217\'20\'19ll try to ban the right to choose nationwide.\par \par \uc2 This November, we must stop him. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/Pj4a0uFA8b"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/Pj4a0uFA8b}}}\uc2  \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  (@JoeBiden) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JoeBiden/status/1805209488506392855?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 24, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTwo years ago, the supreme court justices that Trump handpicked helped overturn Roe v Wade,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden continues. \u8220\'20\'1CDecades of progress shattered just because the last guy got four years in the White House.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re up against extremism. Send me back to the White House and I\u8217\'20\'19ll fight like hell to restore Roe v Wade and protect American freedom.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The offensive comes amid polling evidence that with consistently {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/mar/02/joe-biden-disapproval-rating-new-low"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 weak approval ratings}}}\uc2  for Biden, concerns over reproductive rights represent Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 best hope of retaining the White House in November.\par \par \uc2 Since Roe v Wade was overthrown in 2022, ballot measures in several states \u8211\'20\'13 including ones that tend to vote Republican \u8211\'20\'13 have upheld or enshrined \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights locally, signalling that the issue has popular resonance particularly among female voters.\par \par \uc2 On Friday, a group of Montana \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights supporters {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://flatheadbeacon.com/2024/06/23/abortion-rights-group-says-it-has-signatures-to-qualify-initiative-for-ballot/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 became the latest to announce}}}\uc2  that they had secured enough signatures to hold a November ballot measure asking voters to enshrine the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the state constitution. Although that measure has not yet been confirmed by state officials, voters in roughly a dozen states are expected to weigh in directly on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights this year, including in battleground states such as Nevada and Arizona.\par \par \uc2 Democrats are hoping that these measures will boost turnout in their favor.\par \par \uc2 Several groups \u8211\'20\'13 including \uc2 the American Civil Liberties Union\uc2 , the Center for Reproductive Rights and \uc2 Reproductive Freedom for All\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 announced on Monday a $100m {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://abortionaccessnowcampaign.org/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22  Access Now}}}\uc2  campaign across several states.\par \par \uc2 Since Roe fell, Biden has frequently promised to \u8220\'20\'1Ccodify\u8221\'20\'1D Roe\u8217\'20\'19s protections into law. Although his administration has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/03/biden-executive-order-protect-abortion-access"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 issued executive orders}}}\uc2  aimed at boosting access to reproductive healthcare, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jun/23/joe-biden-abortion-reproductive-rights-roe-2024-campaign"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 including contraception}}}\uc2 , as well as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/jun/13/supreme-court-abortion-pill-access"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 defended \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  access}}}\uc2  in two supreme court cases this year, Biden cannot re-establish a federal right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  without congressional support. Congress has repeatedly failed to pass the Women\u8217\'20\'19s Health Protection Act, a bill that blocks states from totally banning \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  before fetal viability, or the point at which a fetus can survive outside the womb.\par \par \uc2 In a call with reporters on Monday, White House officials declined to reveal any plans for future \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -related executive actions. Jennifer Klein, assistant to the president and director of the Gender Policy Council, also acknowledged that, if the supreme court rules against the Biden administration in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/2024/apr/24/us-supreme-court-abortion-rights-emtala"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 highly anticipated case over emergency abortions}}}\uc2 , \u8220\'20\'1Cour options on emergency medical care are likely to be limited\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Trump has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/08/trump-abortion-states"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sought to backpedal on his stance}}}\uc2  in recent months, telling congressional Republicans in a meeting on Capitol Hill this month that the matter should be left to the states and warning them against pursuing a national ban.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240624ek6o001us\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
