\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  says Trump \u8216\'20\'18guilty\u8217\'20\'19 of \u8216\'20\'18stealing\u8217\'20\'19  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  rights at rally \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Chris Stein (now) and L\u233\'00\'E9onie Chao-Fong (earlier) \par \uc2 5,628 \uc2 words\par \uc2 24 June 2024\par 20:08 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 This live blog is now closed. For the latest on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  news in the US, read our coverage here.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 Closing summary\par \par \uc2 Democrats went on the attack as they marked the second anniversary of the Dobbs decision, in which the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s conservative justices overturned the constitutional protections on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  guaranteed by Roe v Wade. At a speech near Washington DC, \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  said \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jun/24/biden-trump-debate-abortion-roe-updates?page=with:block-667996518f081b914d711aff#block-667996518f081b914d711aff"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Cguilty\u8221\'20\'1D of \u8220\'20\'1Cstealing\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2  reproductive rights from American women with his appointment of three of the justices who supported doing away with the precedent. \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , who is days away from his Thursday presidential debate with Trump, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jun/24/biden-trump-debate-abortion-roe-updates?page=with:block-6679753e8f089e1574dbd59c#block-6679753e8f089e1574dbd59c"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 called}}}\uc2  his predecessor the \u8220\'20\'1Csole person responsible for this nightmare\u8221\'20\'1D. Meanwhile, neither Trump nor any top Republicans in Congress {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jun/24/biden-trump-debate-abortion-roe-updates?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-667987cf8f082b117834902a#block-667987cf8f082b117834902a"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said anything}}}\uc2  about the anniversary of the court\u8217\'20\'19s decision.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else happened today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jun/24/biden-trump-debate-abortion-roe-updates?page=with:block-6679c0d78f082b117834930d#block-6679c0d78f082b117834930d"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 plans to rally}}}\uc2  in Chesapeake, Virginia, the day after his debate with Biden. His campaign believes the state is winnable in November, even though it voted overwhelmingly for Biden in 2020.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The supreme court{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jun/24/biden-trump-debate-abortion-roe-updates?page=with:block-66797bfe8f081b914d71193f#block-66797bfe8f081b914d71193f"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 will hear}}}\uc2  a challenge brought by the Biden administration against state-level bans on gender-affirming care for minors \u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 \u8230\'20\'26 but first{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jun/24/biden-trump-debate-abortion-roe-updates?page=with:block-6679c5618f081b914d711d7d#block-6679c5618f081b914d711d7d"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 it will release}}}\uc2  decisions on Wednesday, Thursday and Friday, almost certainly on at least some of the high-profile cases the justices have yet to decide.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The fall of Roe{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jun/24/biden-trump-debate-abortion-roe-updates?page=with:block-66798d978f081b914d711a79#block-66798d978f081b914d711a79"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 upended life}}}\uc2  for aspiring doctors who hoped to provide abortions.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A top White House official{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jun/24/biden-trump-debate-abortion-roe-updates?page=with:block-667981bf8f082b1178348fcd#block-667981bf8f082b1178348fcd"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 signaled}}}\uc2  that Biden supports an effort by Senate Democrats to repeal the Comstock Act, a 19th-century law that a second Trump administration might use to ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  nationwide.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, in Florida, the judge handling \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s stalled prosecution over the classified documents found at his Mar-a-Lago resort is in the midst of a major hearing that could determing the case\u8217\'20\'19s trajectory. Here\u8217\'20\'19s the latest on what the two sides are arguing, from the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/hugo-lowell"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Hugo Lowell}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 The federal judge overseeing {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump\u8217\'20\'19s}}}\uc2  prosecution for retaining classified documents is expected on Monday to consider modifying his conditions of release to include a prohibition on making statements that could endanger the safety of \uc2 FBI\uc2  agents involved in the case.\par \par \uc2 The request to the US district judge, Aileen Cannon \u8211\'20\'13 the first time prosecutors have sought to limit Trump\u8217\'20\'19 public remarks in this case \u8211\'20\'13 raises the stakes for Trump. Unlike in his other cases, where prosecutors sought {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jun/21/trump-trial-alvin-bragg-death-threats"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 gag orders}}}\uc2 , a violation of release conditions carries a risk of jail.\par \par \uc2 The latest dispute over Trump\u8217\'20\'19s inflammatory statements stems from his blatantly false characterization of the \uc2 FBI\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s use-of-deadly force policy when they executed a search warrant at the Mar-a-Lago club in August 2022 and retrieved more than {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jun/14/trump-classified-documents-case"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 100 classified documents}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The order, which limits \uc2 FBI\uc2  agents to use deadly force only if they face extreme danger and became public after the \uc2 FBI\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s operational plan for the search was unsealed, used standard language that is routinely used in hundreds of warrants executed across the country.\par \par \uc2 But Trump and some allies twisted the limiting language to claim the \uc2 FBI\uc2  was authorized by the Biden administration to shoot him when they searched {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/mar-a-lago"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Mar-a-Lago}}}\uc2 , even though Trump was not there during the search and the language is standard US justice department policy.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jun/24/trump-classified-documents-case"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Judge in classified files case to consider reining in Trump attacks on FBI}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.25pm BST\par \par \uc2 Supreme court expected to issue more decisions Thursday, Friday\par \par \uc2 The supreme court has indicated that the justices may release more decisions on Thursday and Friday, as several politically weighty cases await rulings.\par \par \uc2 The justices were already expected to issue decisions on Wednesday, thus bringing to three the number of days this week that we can expect to hear from the court. The conservative-dominated body has a bunch of matters outstanding, which touch on everything from \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s legal fate, to the scope of government regulation. Here are a few:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/25/supreme-court-trump-immunity-claim"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 petition for immunity}}}\uc2  from the federal charges brought against him by special prosecutor \uc2 Jack Smith\uc2  for attempting to overturn the 2020 election.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Where the Biden administration can require federally funded hospitals to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/2024/apr/24/us-supreme-court-abortion-rights-emtala"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 perform emergency abortions}}}\uc2 , even in states like Idaho, which the case centers on, that have strict \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A challenge to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/society/2024/apr/22/homelessness-us-supreme-court-case"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a longstanding doctrine}}}\uc2  underpinning many federal regulatory decisions.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Whether municipalities {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/society/2024/apr/22/homelessness-us-supreme-court-case"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 can make it illegal}}}\uc2  for people to sleep outside, even when there is insufficient shelter space, in a case that could upend homeless policies nationwide.\par \par \uc2 Decisions on some, all, or theoretically none of these cases could come before the end of the week.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.02pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will hold the first of two debates they have scheduled on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 The day after, the former president is scheduled to hold a rally in Chesapeake, Virginia, a state that Biden won overwhelmingly in 2020, but which Trump\u8217\'20\'19s campaign argues is within his grasp this year.\par \par \uc2 Trump will \u8220\'20\'1Cspeak with the people of Virginia about how he will reverse the devastating effects of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s failed presidency,\u8221\'20\'1D his campaign announced.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CPresident Trump will ease the financial pressures placed on households and re-establish law and order in this country! We can Make America Great Again by tackling lawlessness head-on, ceasing the endless flow of illegal immigrants across our southern border, and reversing the detrimental effects of inflation by restoring people\u8217\'20\'19s wealth.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://projects.fivethirtyeight.com/polls/president-general/2024/virginia/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Polls}}}\uc2  have lately showed a close, perhaps tied, race between Trump and Biden in Virginia, though there have been none released so far showing the former president with the advantage.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.38pm BST\par \par \uc2 Democrats are continuing to press their message against Republicans over their support for the Dobbs decision, which overturned Roe v Wade, and allowed states to ban abortions.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTwo years ago, the extreme right-wing Supreme Court majority issued one of the most egregious rulings in our nation\u8217\'20\'19s history,\u8221\'20\'1D the Democratic House minority leader \uc2 Hakeem Jeffries\uc2  said.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more:\par \par \uc2 The Dobbs decision undermined reproductive freedom for women all across America as part of the extreme MAGA Republican plan to criminalize reproductive health care, outlaw contraception and march us toward a nationwide \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban.\par \par \uc2 The decision by the out of control Supreme Court majority to take away the long-held right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  represents an assault on freedom, the Constitution and the values shared by a majority of Americans. House Democrats will continue to fight until reproductive freedom is the law of the land and the extreme MAGA Republican effort to impose a nationwide \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban is crushed.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 Still not a peep from \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and most leading Republicans on the second anniversary of Roe v Wade\u8217\'20\'19s overturning, but that\u8217\'20\'19s not stopping the Biden campaign.\par \par \uc2 Their official account has spent the day tweeting out past instances where Trump has taken credit for orchestrating the downfall of the precedent, which prevented the sorts of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions now commonplace in Republican-controlled states.\par \par \uc2 From his town hall in Iowa earlier this year:\par \par \uc2 enltrTrump brags about overturning Roe v. Wade: I did it. I\u8217\'20\'19m proud to have done it. It was a miracle {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/cVk7w1VF9k"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/cVk7w1VF9k}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Biden-Harris HQ (@BidenHQ) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/BidenHQ/status/1805263420582678555?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 24, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 And what appears to be one of the many videos Trump has posted on his Truth Social account:\par \par \uc2 enltrTrump: I was proudly the person responsible for the ending of Roe v. Wade {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/Xjzv6YOyia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/Xjzv6YOyia}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Biden-Harris HQ (@BidenHQ) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/BidenHQ/status/1805288595281891479?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 24, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.01pm BST\par \par \uc2 Former Maryland governor \uc2 Larry Hogan\uc2 , the GOP nominee for a Senate seat in the state, was one of the few Republicans to mark the second anniversary of the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  ruling that overturned Roe v Wade.\par \par \uc2 Hogan, in a statement shared by the \uc2 Washington Post\uc2 , said that if elected, he would work on bipartisan legislation to \u8220\'20\'1Ccodify Roe v. Wade as the law of the land.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He noted that as governor, he \u8220\'20\'1Creaffirmed my commitment to uphold Maryland law protecting access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D adding that he was \u8220\'20\'1Cproud to make Maryland the first state in America to provide over-the-counter birth control covered by insurance.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Hogan, who last week tried to reject \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s endorsement in his Senate race, also promised to protect women\u8217\'20\'19s reproductive rights.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CA woman\u8217\'20\'19s health care decisions are her own,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 Whether it be the decision to start a family with the help of IVF, or exercise her reproductive rights, nothing and no one \u8212\'20\'14 especially partisan politics \u8212\'20\'14 should come between a woman and her doctor.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.51pm BST\par \par \uc2 Planned Parenthood\uc2  will spen d $40m ahead of November\u8217\'20\'19s elections to bolster \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and leading congressional Democrats.\par \par \uc2 The group will initially target eight states: Arizona, Georgia, Pennsylvania, Wisconsin, where Biden is seeking to defend 2020 victories, as well as North Carolina, which the Biden campaign to flip, and Montana, New Hampshire and New York, which have races that could help determine control of the Senate and House, it told Associated Press.\par \par \uc2 Jenny Lawson, executive director of Planned Parenthood Votes, said:\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  will be the message of this election, and it will be how we energize voters. It will be what enables us to win.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.07pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.32pm BST\par \par \uc2 Texas \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban linked to increase in infant deaths, new study finds\par \par \uc2 A six-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban in Texas was linked to a 13% increase in the number of infants who died in their first year of life, a new study published Monday in JAMA Pediatrics suggests.\par \par \uc2 The study, published {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/article/2024/jun/24/abortion-training-doctors-ban-roe"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 two years to the day}}}\uc2  since the supreme court overturned Roe v Wade and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2023/nov/10/state-abortion-laws-us"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 permitted more than a dozen states}}}\uc2  across the country to outlaw almost all abortions, is one of the first glimpses into how strict \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans impact babies\u8217\'20\'19 health.\par \par \uc2 The study also estimated that the ban may have led the number of infants in Texas who died within their first month of life to rise more than 10%.\par \par \uc2 Because Texas enacted its {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/01/texas-abortion-law-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 six-week \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  ban}}}\uc2  in September 2021, months before Roe\u8217\'20\'19s demise, scholars have studied what has happened in Texas for clues about how post-Roe \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans are now affecting the rest of the nation. Some of the researchers involved in the Monday study have previously concluded that the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://jamanetwork.com/journals/jama/article-abstract/2806878"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Texas ban also led to 10,000 additional births}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The study found a 23% jump in infant deaths due to congenital anomalies \u8211\'20\'13 the kind of conditions that are often identified in utero and lead to abortions in states where the procedure is legal, since they can be incompatible with life. But that choice is no longer available to pregnant Texans.\par \par \uc2 Two hundred and sixteen more infant deaths occurred due to the Texas six-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, the researchers estimated.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jun/24/texas-abortion-ban-infant-deaths"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Texas \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  ban linked to increase in infant deaths, new study finds}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  has warned that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans in states across the country are cutting women off from essential reproductive care and causing a \u8220\'20\'1Chealth care crisis\u8221\'20\'1D,\par \par \uc2 In an interview with MSNBC aired today alongside reproductive rights advocate Hadley Duvall, Harris reflected on her experience visiting a reproductive care clinic in Minnesota in March.\par \par \uc2 In those clinics that are trusted in the community, there is \u8212\'20\'14 you can get a Pap [smear]... breast cancer screening, HIV screening, the things that where people want to be able to walk into a health care facility and be treated with dignity and without judgment so they can address their health care concerns.\par \par \uc2 She continued:\par \par \uc2 That\u8217\'20\'19s what these clinics do. And in states where they have passed these Trump \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans, these clinics are closing, which means that there is a reduction of very essential health care across the board for a lot of people.\par \par \uc2 enltrVP Harris blames Trump & SCOTUS for rollbacks of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  protections since Roe was overturned:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe are seeing what I call 'Trump \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans,' including states...with a 6-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban... These legislators clearly don't know how a woman's body works, or they don't care.\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/3bgCsHnC2b"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/3bgCsHnC2b}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1805259929575379189?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 24, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 The day so far\par \par \uc2 Democrats are on the attack as they mark the second anniversary of the Dobbs decision, in which the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s conservative justices overturned the constitutional protections on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  guaranteed by Roe v Wade. At a speech outside Washington DC, \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  said \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jun/24/biden-trump-debate-abortion-roe-updates?page=with:block-667996518f081b914d711aff#block-667996518f081b914d711aff"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Cguilty\u8221\'20\'1D of \u8220\'20\'1Cstealing\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2  reproductive rights from American women with his appointment of three of the justices who supported doing away with the precedent. \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , who is three days away from his Thursday presidential debate with Trump, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jun/24/biden-trump-debate-abortion-roe-updates?page=with:block-6679753e8f089e1574dbd59c#block-6679753e8f089e1574dbd59c"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 called}}}\uc2  his predecessor the \u8220\'20\'1Csole person responsible for this nightmare\u8221\'20\'1D. Meanwhile, neither Trump nor any top Republicans in Congress {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jun/24/biden-trump-debate-abortion-roe-updates?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-667987cf8f082b117834902a#block-667987cf8f082b117834902a"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 have said anything}}}\uc2  about the anniversary of the court\u8217\'20\'19s decision.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else has happened today so far:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The supreme court{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jun/24/biden-trump-debate-abortion-roe-updates?page=with:block-66797bfe8f081b914d71193f#block-66797bfe8f081b914d71193f"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 will hear}}}\uc2  a challenge brought by the Biden administration against state-level bans on gender-affirming care for minors.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The fall of Roe{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jun/24/biden-trump-debate-abortion-roe-updates?page=with:block-66798d978f081b914d711a79#block-66798d978f081b914d711a79"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 upended life}}}\uc2  for aspiring doctors who hoped to provide abortions.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A top White House official{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jun/24/biden-trump-debate-abortion-roe-updates?page=with:block-667981bf8f082b1178348fcd#block-667981bf8f082b1178348fcd"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 signaled}}}\uc2  that Biden supports an effort by Senate Democrats to repeal the Comstock Act, a 19th-century law that a second Trump administration might use to ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  nationwide.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.50pm BST\par \par \uc2 Kate Cox, the Texas mother who was denied an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  under the state\u8217\'20\'19s near-total ban last year, introduced \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  at her speech in Maryland.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CEvery minute that I stayed pregnant, the risk to my health and to a future pregnancy were growing,\u8221\'20\'1D Cox said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMy state chose to drive me out of my home, my community, away from my children and my doctors, rather than to let me access care,\u8221\'20\'1D she said, adding: \u8220\'20\'1CI never imagined having to fight for something so basic as a procedure to save my health.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 As a young student and mother \u8220\'20\'1Cjust trying to stay afloat,\u8221\'20\'1D Cox said she didn\u8217\'20\'19t always make time to vote.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI will never again miss an opportunity to vote. I will cast my ballot in every election like my life depends on it,\u8221\'20\'1D Cox said.\par \par \uc2 Growing emotional, Cox then shared that she is pregnant again, expecting a child in January. The crowd erupted in applause, as many stood to cheer for her.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAnd I hope that by then, when we welcome our baby into the world, we will have a world led by \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 She then welcomed Harris on to the stage as a \u8220\'20\'1Cchampion of the cause\u8221\'20\'1D for reproductive freedom.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou are a hero of this movement,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris told Cox.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 Harris emphasized the importance of turning out to vote in November to protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access so that places like Maryland remain havens for reproductive healthcare.\par \par \uc2 Pointing to the statistic that one-in-three American women live in a state with \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions, she said: \u8220\'20\'1CToday our daughters know fewer rights than their grandmothers. This is a healthcare crisis, and we all know who to blame: \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Making her case that Trump was \u8220\'20\'1Cguilty\u8221\'20\'1D of stripping \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access, which was previewed by the campaign before her appearance, Harris said Trump appointed three supreme court justices with the intention of overturning Roe v Wade.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt was premeditated,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris said from a stage, where a sign that said \u8220\'20\'1CTrust Women\u8221\'20\'1D hung behind her.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTrump has not denied, much less shown remorse, for his actions,\u8221\'20\'1D she added.\par \par \uc2 Later this afternoon, Harris will go to battleground state Arizona for a second event marking the Dobbs anniversary.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.14pm BST\par \par \uc2 Harris took the stage to chants of \u8220\'20\'1Cfour more years.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 She then said Trump was \u8220\'20\'1Cguilty\u8221\'20\'1D in \u8220\'20\'1Cthe case of the stealing of reproductive freedom from the women of America\u8221\'20\'1D, and went on to lay out what she said are the stakes for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access if Trump is re-elected.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CUnderstand as much harm as he has already caused, a second Trump term will be even worse,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CHis friends in the \uc2 United States Congress\uc2  are trying to pass a national ban that would outlaw \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in every single state in states like New York and California, and even right here in Maryland.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 She called Republicans who have passed state-level bans Trump\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Caccomplices\u8221\'20\'1D, and said voters shouldn\u8217\'20\'19t be fooled by Trump\u8217\'20\'19s wavering on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but should focus on what he has said. And she warned that he would go even further, curtailing access to contraception and IVF.\par \par \uc2 enltr"Enough with the gaslighting," Harris says of Trump's wavering stance on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Lauren Gambino (@laurenegambino) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/laurenegambino/status/1805270599234654545?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 24, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf there were a second Trump term, he has admitted that he is \u8216\'20\'18looking at restrictions on contraception,\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd pay close attention to how his friends in the \uc2 United States Senate\uc2  obstructed a bill to protect the right to contraception, not once, not twice, but three times.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.19pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.03pm BST\par \par \uc2 Vice President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  just took the stage to address a crowd at the University of Maryland, her first event of the day to mark the second anniversary of the Dobbs decision.\par \par \uc2 Maryland is a deep-blue state with an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  referendum on the ballot and a surprisingly competitive Senate race that could help determine the balance of power in Congress. Ahead of Harris\u8217\'20\'19s remarks, Maryland Democrats and reproductive rights leaders emphasized the stakes in November.\par \par \uc2 Angela Alsobrooks, the Democratic nominee for the state\u8217\'20\'19s open seat, said Trump was \u8220\'20\'1Cproud as a peacock\u8221\'20\'1D for setting in motion the fall of Roe, and warned that Republicans saw the state as an opportunity to win back control of the chamber.\par \par \uc2 Speaking before Harris, she said of Republicans: \u8220\'20\'1CMake no mistake about it. They would take the first opportunity to ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  nationwide.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Alsobrooks faces \uc2 Larry Hogan\uc2 , the state\u8217\'20\'19s former two-term Republican governor, who, in a sign of the fast-shifting politics of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , has recast himself as \u8220\'20\'1Cpro-choice\u8221\'20\'1D and said he supports the state\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  referendum.\par \par \uc2 Maryland senator \uc2 Chris Van Hollen\uc2 , a Democrat, urged voters who want to protect access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  to send Alsobrooks with him to the Senate.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Larry Hogan\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s undergoing some election year conversion like none other I\u8217\'20\'19ve ever seen,\u8221\'20\'1D the senator said, pointing to Hogan\u8217\'20\'19s record as governor, when he vetoed a law that would have expanded \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CA vote for \uc2 Larry Hogan\uc2  is a vote to put the Maga Republicans in charge of the \uc2 United States Senate\uc2 .\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In November, Maryland voters will decide whether to approve a constitutional amendment enshrining the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and \u8220\'20\'1Creproductive freedom,\u8221\'20\'1D in the state\u8217\'20\'19s constitution. It is widely expected to pass because of broad support for protecting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access, which is legal in the state.\par \par \uc2 Mini Timmaraju\uc2 , president of \uc2 Reproductive Freedom for All\uc2 , called it a \u8220\'20\'1Csolemn anniversary\u8221\'20\'1D but said there was also reason to hope.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe poured the pain that we felt into action,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CElection after election, voters showed up motivated by that grief by that pain, but also by that anger and they sent Maga extremists packing.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.58pm BST\par \par \uc2 At rally marking Dobbs anniversary, Harris to say Trump 'guilty' of 'stealing' \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is holding a rally in Washington DC\u8217\'20\'19s Maryland suburbs to mark two years since the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s Dobbs decision, which overturned constitutional protections on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In excerpts of the speech shared by the White House, the vice-president will accuse \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  of \u8220\'20\'1Cstealing of reproductive freedom from the women of America\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is a health care crisis, and we know who is to blame: \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 How do we know? Well, I\u8217\'20\'19m a former prosecutor. So let\u8217\'20\'19s look at the facts.\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  hand-picked three members of the \uc2 United States Supreme Court\uc2  because he intended for them to overturn Roe. So it was premeditated,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris will say.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more:\par \par \uc2 Trump has not denied, much less shown remorse, for his actions. Instead, he proudly takes credit for overturning Roe.\par \par \uc2 In a court of law, that would be called an admission. Some would say, a confession.\par \par \uc2 \u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 In the case of the stealing of reproductive freedom from the women of America, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is guilty.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.36pm BST\par \par \uc2 The end of Roe v Wade, and moves by Republican-controlled states to ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , have made life particularly complicated for women on probation and parole, according to recently published research. From the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/jessica-glenza"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Jessica Glenza}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 The number of women on probation or parole who must seek permission to travel for an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  more than doubled to 635,000 in two years since the supreme court overturned the federal right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.prisonpolicy.org/blog/2024/06/18/dobbs/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 new report}}}\uc2  finds.\par \par \uc2 Fourteen states have near-total \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans and 21 restrict the procedure. Together with near ubiquitous travel restrictions imposed by probation and parole, more than half of women on probation or parole in the US must seek permission to travel before obtaining an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The policies are a \u8220\'20\'1Cone-two punch\u8221\'20\'1D for women caught in the criminal justice system, the report\u8217\'20\'19s author said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CDoing the math I was shocked it was so many,\u8221\'20\'1D said Wendy Sawyer, research director at the Prison Policy Initiative, which published the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.prisonpolicy.org/blog/2024/06/18/dobbs/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 new report}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The research came just ahead of today \u8211\'20\'13 the second anniversary of the Dobbs decision, which the supreme court used to overturn {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Roe v Wade}}}\uc2  in 2022.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAn additional 400,000 women is a lot of additional women to be put in this very precarious situation,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jun/24/abortion-probation-parole-permission-travel-report"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Over half of US women on probation or parole need permission to travel for \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  \u8211\'20\'13 study}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.19pm BST\par \par \uc2 Beyond its massive impact in American politics, the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/carter-sherman"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Carter Sherman}}}\uc2  reports that the fall of Roe v Wade upended the education of aspiring doctors who were looking to provide abortions:\par \par \uc2 The fall of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Roe v Wade}}}\uc2  upended Dr Jasmine Chan\u8217\'20\'19s career.\par \par \uc2 As a medical student, the Texas native wanted to provide abortions as an OB-GYN. But in 2022, as Chan prepared to apply for residency \u8211\'20\'13 a kind of years-long apprenticeship after medical school \u8211\'20\'13 she worried that the quirks of the residency placement process would keep her in Texas, which banned abortions after the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  overturned Roe.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI met with my advisers and I had very strong heart-to-heart conversations about how I couldn\u8217\'20\'19t see myself practicing medicine if it didn\u8217\'20\'19t include me getting to do abortions,\u8221\'20\'1D Chan said. Instead of becoming an OB-GYN, she decided to become a family medicine doctor \u8211\'20\'13 a less competitive specialty that increased her chances of finding a residency in a state that protects \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access.\par \par \uc2 Now, two years into her residency program in New Jersey, Chan is preparing to finally get the training that she\u8217\'20\'19s longed for her entire career. But, like many other doctors seeking \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  training after Roe\u8217\'20\'19s demise, she will still have to overcome hurdles that didn\u8217\'20\'19t exist just two years ago.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/article/2024/jun/24/abortion-training-doctors-ban-roe"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US doctors struggle to get basic \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  training two years after fall of Roe}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.57pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump, Republicans, don't have much to say on Dobbs anniversary\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and his allies have seized on the second anniversary of the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s Dobbs ruling to attack \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and his allies as threats to reproductive freedom. And, so far today, the GOP is not saying much back.\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://truthsocial.com/@realDonaldTrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 feed}}}\uc2  on Truth Social is full of posts about {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jun/23/trumps-sledgehammer-message-to-philadelphia-is-light-on-facts-heavy-on-fear"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 his rally in Philadelphia}}}\uc2  this weekend, with not a peep about the overturning of Roe v Wade, or his role in it. Meanwhile, top Republican officials in Congress, including Senate minority leader \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  and speaker of the House Mike Johnson, have not commented either, nor has \uc2 Lindsey Graham\uc2 , who has introduced legislation to ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  nationwide. That could change in the course of the day.\par \par \uc2 However, veteran anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  groups are marking the occasion, with warnings that a second Biden term could lead to the re-establishment of nationwide access to the procedure. Here\u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 Susan B. Anthony\uc2  Pro-Life America:\par \par \uc2 enltrWill This Be Our Last {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/Dobbs?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #Dobbs}}}\uc2  Anniversary?\par \par \uc2 Every pro-life state could be stripped of its pro-life laws if Biden, Harris, and the Democrats win.\par \par \uc2 Give life a fighting chance. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/Apw6w771GA"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/Apw6w771GA}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 SBA Pro-Life America (@sbaprolife) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/sbaprolife/status/1805244238470205669?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 24, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.31pm BST\par \par \uc2 In the ongoing call with reporters marking the two-year anniversary of the Dobbs decision, the director of the White House\u8217\'20\'19s gender policy council Jennifer Klein signaled that \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  supports efforts in Congress to repeal the Comstock Act.\par \par \uc2 That is the obscenity law passed in 1873 that remains on the books, and which productive rights advocates fear could be used by a second Trump administration to ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  nationwide.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe support all actions by Democrats in Congress to protect reproductive freedom, including this one, and the president has been quite clear that what we need, ultimately, is a federal law restoring the protections of Roe v Wade, which is the only way we can ensure that women in every state are going to be able to make the decisions that are right for them and their families, to stop the erosion of reproductive rights that we are seeing across the country, and to stop the other side from attempting to roll us back to the 1800s,\u8221\'20\'1D Klein said.\par \par \uc2 She also noted that though Biden\u8217\'20\'19s justice department does not believe Comstock could be used to outlaw \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  by criminalizing the mailing and transportation of material used in the procedure, officials in a second Trump administration could reverse that:\par \par \uc2 Our department of justice has issued a binding opinion that Comstock is not a barrier to the shipment, the mailing, the transport, for lawful purposes, for lawful \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . And so their view, the other side\u8217\'20\'19s view, is draconian and inconsistent with longstanding interpretation of the Comstock Act by courts for decades \u8230\'20\'26 and they\u8217\'20\'19ve been quite clear what a future administration could and would do. They would use Comstock to go after the mailing of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  medication and even potentially other supplies used in \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . And they\u8217\'20\'19ve been quite clear that, you know, that\u8217\'20\'19s why they don\u8217\'20\'19t think they need to pass a national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban \u8230\'20\'26 They\u8217\'20\'19ve got a backdoor ban on the books.\par \par \uc2 Last week, Democratic senator Tina Smith introduced legislation to repeal the Comstock Act:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/article/2024/jun/20/comstock-act-democrats"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Democrats move to repeal 1873 law they say could pave way for national \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  ban}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.16pm BST\par \par \uc2 White House says GOP attacks on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , IVF 'should never happen in America'\par \par \uc2 In a call with reporters, White House press secretary \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2  hit out Republicans for their efforts to ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and accused them of moving to curb access to in vitro fertilization treatment, and contraception.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTwo years ago today, the Supreme Court overturned a woman\u8217\'20\'19s constitutional right to make deeply Personal health care decisions free from the interference of politicians. The aftermath has been devastating for women\u8217\'20\'19s health and lives,\u8221\'20\'1D Jean-Pierre said.\par \par \uc2 She continued:\par \par \uc2 Already this year, Republican elected officials and states have filed more than 300 bills to restrict access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care. And, on Capitol Hill, congressional Republicans have proposed three national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans, and, despite having had every opportunity to protect reproductive freedom since the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s decision to overturn Roe, Republican officials have blocked attempts led by Democratic elected officials and refused to do so.\par \par \uc2 Just earlier this month, Senate Republicans once again refused to protect access to IVF for women who are desperately trying to get pregnant, and Republicans in Congress blocked a bill that would protect a woman\u8217\'20\'19s right to access contraception.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s extreme, it\u8217\'20\'19s out of touch, and it\u8217\'20\'19s wrong \u8230\'20\'26 This should never happen in America.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.04pm BST\par \par \uc2 Supreme court to hear Biden administration challenge to state bans on gender-affirming care for minors\par \par \uc2 The supreme court has agreed to hear a challenge brought by the Biden administration against Republican-backed bans on gender-affirming care for minors, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/supreme-court-transgender-health-tennessee-kentucky-75e3b446513f61281013a2bf86248044"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Associated Press reports}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The case will be heard in the court\u8217\'20\'19s forthcoming term, with arguments expected later this year. Conservatives hold a supermajority of seats on the high court, and the petition gives them the opportunity to issue a ruling that could green-light such bans nationwide.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more, from the AP:\par \par \uc2 The justices\u8217\'20\'19 action comes as Republican-led states have enacted a variety of restrictions on health care for transgender people, school sports participation, bathroom usage and drag shows. The administration and Democratic-led states have extended protections for transgender people, including {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/title-ix-lawsuit-states-bathrooms-lawsuit-f731ff2f1afd24a1f246443f12053bcc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a new federal regulation}}}\uc2  that seeks to protect transgender students.\par \par \uc2 The case before the high court involves a law in Tennessee that restrict puberty blockers and hormone therapy for transgender minors. The federal appeals court in Cincinnati allowed laws in Tennessee and Kentucky to take effect after they had been blocked by lower courts. (The high court did not act on a separate appeal from Kentucky.)\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWithout this Court\u8217\'20\'19s prompt intervention, transgender youth and their families will remain in limbo, uncertain of whether and where they can access needed medical care,\u8221\'20\'1D lawyers for the transgender teens in Tennessee told the justices.\par \par \uc2 Actor Elliot Page, the Oscar-nominated star of \u8220\'20\'1CJuno,\u8221\'20\'1D \u8220\'20\'1CInception\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1CThe Umbrella Academy,\u8221\'20\'1D was among 57 transgender people who joined a legal filing in support of Supreme Court review.\par \par \uc2 Arguments will take place in the fall.\par \par \uc2 Last week, South Carolina became {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/transgender-care-minors-gender-affirming-south-carolina-49edeee22eab31574316a13ab874b623"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the 25th state}}}\uc2  to adopt a law restricting or banning gender-affirming medical care for transgender minors, even though such treatments have been available in the United States for more than a decade and are endorsed by major medical associations.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.42pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden calls Trump 'sole person responsible for this nightmare' on anniversary of Dobbs decision\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has marked the second anniversary of the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s Dobbs decision by issuing a statement reminding voters of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s involvement in the ruling, which gave state the green-light to ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Since then, 14 states have implemented total \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans, and 27 others have banned the procedure after a certain number of weeks of gestation, according to the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.guttmacher.org/state-policy/explore/state-policies-abortion-bans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Guttmacher Institute}}}\uc2 . In his statement, Biden described the situation as a \u8220\'20\'1Cnightmare\u8221\'20\'1D that can only be blamed on Trump:\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is the sole person responsible for this nightmare. For him, these cruel state bans are a \u8216\'20\'18beautiful thing to watch\u8217\'20\'19 \u8211\'20\'13 and they\u8217\'20\'19re just beginning. This is a man who brags about overturning Roe v. Wade, has called for women who access reproductive health care to be punished \u8212\'20\'14 and says he would rule as a dictator on day one. If given the chance, there is no question he will ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  nationwide, with or without the help of Congress. You don\u8217\'20\'19t have to take my word for it \u8211\'20\'13 his advisors have already laid out the plans to do it.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden and Democrats pummel Trump on anniversary of supreme court decision overturning Roe v Wade\par \par \uc2 Good morning, US politics blog readers. Today is the two-year anniversary of the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s decision in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jun/24/roe-v-wade-overturned-abortion-summary-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Dobbs v Jackson Women\u8217\'20\'19s Health Organization}}}\uc2 , which overturned the 49-year-old precedent set in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Roe v Wade}}}\uc2  and allowed states to ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Since then, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights advocates have succeeded in getting voters to approve measures protecting access to the procedure in states as conservative as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/03/kansas-abortion-vote-state-constitution"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kansas}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/nov/07/ohio-issue-1-abortion-rights-vote-result"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ohio}}}\uc2 , while Democratic candidates across the country have campaigned on reproductive rights to win office. Now, the party is looking to continue that momentum going into the November {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-elections-2024"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 presidential election}}}\uc2 , with an eye towards focusing the ire of pro-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights voters on \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 who appointed to the court three of the justices that supported the Dobbs decision.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTwo years ago today, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s supreme court majority ripped away the fundamental freedom for women to access the health care they need and deserve,\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  said in a statement released this morning to mark the occasion. While he remains ensconced at the Camp David presidential retreat ahead of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jun/22/biden-trump-presidential-debate"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Thursday\u8217\'20\'19s debate with Trump}}}\uc2 , \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  will hold a campaign event today in Maryland, where she\u8217\'20\'19ll no doubt address the issue.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else is going on today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump continued his tactic of campaigning in inner cities over the weekend, holding his first rally in Philadelphia with a speech that focused on blaming undocumented migrants for crime, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jun/23/trumps-sledgehammer-message-to-philadelphia-is-light-on-facts-heavy-on-fear"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 facts be damned}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Same-sex marriage, which is protected by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/society/2015/jun/26/gay-marriage-legal-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a supreme court ruling}}}\uc2  and also by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/dec/13/biden-signs-law-protecting-same-sex-interracial-marriages"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a recently passed federal law}}}\uc2 , remains broadly popular, though its support is slipping among Republicans, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://news.gallup.com/poll/646202/sex-relations-marriage-supported.aspx?utm_source=alert&utm_medium=email&utm_content=morelink&utm_campaign=syndication"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Gallup finds}}}\uc2  in a new poll.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Neither the Housenor Senate are in session today, but the lower chamber will be back tomorrow, with its Republican majority focused on passing spending bills that will likely contain a number of rightwing demands to be used as bargaining chips with the Democrats.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240624ek6o001pa\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
