\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Anger, fear and desperation: people reflect on two years since fall of Roe\b0\par\par\uc2 Clea Skopeliti \par \uc2 1,534 \uc2 words\par \uc2 24 June 2024\par 17:04 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 The Dobbs decision has forced patients to travel out of their state to access \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care, others have carried unwanted pregnancies, while for some it was a call to action\par \par \uc2 After Roe v Wade was overturned in June 2022, Daphne did not want to leave anything to chance.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is currently legal until 18 weeks in Utah, where the 38-year-old lives \u8211\'20\'13 but the state {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.acluutah.org/en/news/understanding-ongoing-litigation-abortion-care-utah#:~:text=Soon%20after%20the%20June%202022,place%20while%20the%20litigation%20continued."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has a 2020 trigger law banning almost all \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  care}}}\uc2  that is currently under appeal.\par \par \uc2 Daphne knew she didn\u8217\'20\'19t want children so she decided to undergo surgical sterilization in October 2022, to have \u8220\'20\'1Cpeace of mind that [she] physically cannot become pregnant\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMy husband could have gotten a vasectomy for less money and an easier recovery time. However, that doesn\u8217\'20\'19t change the outcome if I were to be assaulted. Living in Utah, I could not and would not risk having to seek an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , likely having to leave the state to do so, after an already traumatic event,\u8221\'20\'1D Daphne said.\par \par \uc2 The procedure, which was not fully covered by her health insurance, left her around $1,000 out of pocket.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m lucky I was able to take these measures, and most cannot,\u8221\'20\'1D she added.\par \par \uc2 Almost two years after the supreme court decided there is no constitutional right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the Dobbs v Jackson Women\u8217\'20\'19s Health Organization case, patients have increasingly been forced to travel out of their state in order to access \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care, while others have carried unwanted pregnancies to term. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://edition.cnn.com/2024/01/24/health/rape-pregnancy-abortion/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 A study earlier published in January}}}\uc2  estimated there have been nearly 65,000 pregnancies from rape in states with \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans.\par \par \uc2 Interstate travel for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care in the US {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.guttmacher.org/news-release/2023/new-data-show-interstate-travel-abortion-care-united-states-has-doubled-2020#:~:text=The%20latest%20study%20findings%20show,a%20similar%20period%20in%202020."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 doubled between 2020 and 2023}}}\uc2 , from one in 10 to almost one in five people leaving their state to access treatment, data from the \uc2 Guttmacher Institute\uc2  shows.\par \par \uc2 In states where it is possible, many go to neighboring states. Hanz, a 30-year-old who works as a clinical social worker in an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinic in Illinois, but lives in Missouri, found out they were pregnant in late July 2022, they recalled: \u8220\'20\'1CAs soon as I saw the two lines on the test, I knew I had more rights standing in Illinois than I would when I got home that night. \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights had already got so much worse in recent years \u8211\'20\'13 and then Roe was overturned.\u8221\'20\'1D (Missouri passed a trigger law in 2019 that banned abortions except in medical emergencies.)\par \par \uc2 Hanz wanted a child, but felt it wasn\u8217\'20\'19t the right time. \u8220\'20\'1CI was really weighing what I wanted and what felt like the right decision. It was very hard for me to terminate the pregnancy, but I had a difficult time growing up and didn\u8217\'20\'19t feel I could bring a child into the world and not be able to give them the quality of life I wanted to,\u8221\'20\'1D they said.\par \par \uc2 After spending a month carefully weighing their options, they crossed into Illinois to terminate the pregnancy at the beginning of September at nine weeks.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMaking the decision was much harder than having the actual \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D Hanz said, adding that fears remain about crossing the border to receive care.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19ve talked to people who thought they may be arrested when they returned to their home state \u8211\'20\'13 you\u8217\'20\'19re not breaking the law by crossing the state,\u8221\'20\'1D Hanz said.\par \par \uc2 For others, the introduction of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions has meant they are not having children they may have had. Over the last few years, Brie, 41, had been considering having another child \u8211\'20\'13 but after Dobbs, she felt she could not undergo the risk of a pregnancy at her age in the state of Texas.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMy husband and I had dreamt of a third child. Now, I know it\u8217\'20\'19s definitely not going to happen,\u8221\'20\'1D Brie said, adding that she felt she could not risk a pregnancy in Texas, which {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/may/31/texas-abortion-ban-medical-exceptions-supreme-court-ruling"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has a near-total \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  ban}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Her medical history adds to her fears: she had a complicated first pregnancy, including experiencing pre-eclampsia, and needed an emergency C-section.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt was scary and dangerous,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CWith my history, there\u8217\'20\'19s no way I\u8217\'20\'19d trust having this pregnancy in Texas or the south. I\u8217\'20\'19d have to move.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The loss of the constitutional right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  has taken the choice out of her hands, she feels. \u8220\'20\'1COur seven-year-old son is asking for a younger sibling,\u8221\'20\'1D Brie said. \u8220\'20\'1CI know I\u8217\'20\'19m in a privileged position \u8211\'20\'13 we have two wonderful, healthy kids \u8211\'20\'13 but I don\u8217\'20\'19t appreciate the state making my family planning decisions.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is an issue that divides her family. \u8220\'20\'1CThe last two years have been a very volatile time, even having these discussions within my extended family,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. The issue is at odds with other values prized in Texas, she believes: \u8220\'20\'1CPeople here are very concerned with freedom. But there\u8217\'20\'19s this huge conflict here between concern with personal freedom, and the approach to women and fertility. The only acceptable carveout is women that are pregnant.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Every month, she feels anxious about the chance of pregnancy. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s constantly on my mind and has been since Dobbs: am I going to be thrown under the bus by my state this month?\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou play scenarios out, what if, where would I go, who would I tell. It\u8217\'20\'19s a big wall of separation between who could you trust. I think that\u8217\'20\'19s the goal: to isolate and put women in a position of insecurity.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 For some, the fall of Roe was a call to action. Paul, in his mid-50s and living in North Carolina, knew little about \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights when he heard the news two years ago.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CUp until then, it was not something I cared about \u8211\'20\'13 it was obvious that women should have the right to choose,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. He had thought \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  was a \u8220\'20\'1Csettled issue\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 When he heard the news, he remembers that he and his wife \u8220\'20\'1Cstared at each other in silence, and thought, what the hell happens next? It doesn\u8217\'20\'19t affect us personally, but it does affect millions of women. I went in completely blind.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Compelled by a need to take action, by November 2022, Paul had begun volunteering with a group that offered logistical assistance to people requiring abortions, often picking up patients who had travelled from states with more restrictive laws and driving them to clinics.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19ve driven young teens with their parents who are absolutely petrified; women in their 20s who accept it\u8217\'20\'19s something they have to do, and others to whom it\u8217\'20\'19s no big deal. Everyone has a different set of circumstances \u8211\'20\'13 you don\u8217\'20\'19t have to explain your reason to me,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 After North Carolina reduced the limit from 20 to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/may/16/north-carolina-abortion-ban-veto-override"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 12 weeks in May 2023}}}\uc2 , the number of patients traveling to the state dwindled until the service disbanded. Now, Paul volunteers most weeks as a clinic escort.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMore Saturdays than not, I can be found wearing a rainbow-striped vest, shielding women behind umbrellas as I walk them into the clinic. I have been called a murderer, a baby killer \u8230\'20\'26 And I\u8217\'20\'19ll happily do it again next weekend as well,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CA lot of men don\u8217\'20\'19t want to acknowledge that men have a role to play in fixing this \u8211\'20\'13 it\u8217\'20\'19s not up to just women.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 For Jane*, a woman from Texas in her 60s, the writing was on the wall before Dobbs as she watched restrictions chip away at \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights year after year. ?Between 1973 and May 2022, 1,380 \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions were enacted in states, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.guttmacher.org/article/2021/11/resources-journalists-15-points-consider-when-covering-abortion-supreme-court-and"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to the Guttmacher Institute}}}\uc2 , with more than 630 of these enacted since 2011.\par \par \uc2 Jane became involved in direct action in 2018, driving people in need of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  to appointments: \u8220\'20\'1CI became involved because I realised pro-choice is just that \u8211\'20\'13 it doesn\u8217\'20\'19t address access. It\u8217\'20\'19s a limited way at looking at reproductive justice. Seeing the impact of restrictions on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , I felt that to do nothing is to be complicit.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 After {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/mar/15/idaho-abortion-ban-texas-law-six-weeks"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Texas passed a bill outlawing \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  following the detection of cardiac activity \u8211\'20\'13 usually around six weeks \u8211\'20\'13 in 2021, Jane was galvanized to take further action. Toward the end of that year, she reached out to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://theguardian.com/world/2022/jun/10/mexico-abortion-access-americans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Las Libres, a Mexican network}}}\uc2  that mails pills for self-managed medical \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe inhumanity of restrictions just raised my temperature and made me increasingly angry and willing to stick my neck out and do something to help,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CDobbs was the logical next step after increasing regulations permitted under Roe. [Access] was very effectively overturned before Dobbs.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Jane has been packaging and posting pills to states with \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans for the last two years.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt is empowering and effective to fight back,\u8221\'20\'1D Jane said. \u8220\'20\'1CPerhaps I am in denial about my own risk, but I have had a good life, I enjoy relative financial stability in my retirement, and who better than me to be in a position to fight back? Small actions matter, and allow me to maintain hope.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 *Name has been changed\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240624ek6o002be\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
