\par\par \uc2 World news\par \b \uc2 Monday briefing: Strap in or run for the hills \u8211\'20\'13 it\u8217\'20\'19s the return of the Biden v Trump debates\b0\par\par\uc2 Nimo Omer \par \uc2 2,435 \uc2 words\par \uc2 24 June 2024\par 09:04 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 In today\u8217\'20\'19s newsletter: So much has changed since the two least popular presidential candidates in decades last faced off. Here\u8217\'20\'19s what to look out for when they share a stage this week\u8226\'20\'22 Sign up here for our daily newsletter, First Edition\par \par \uc2 Good morning\par \par \uc2 The last time \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  were on stage together feels like a lifetime ago. The pandemic was at the very top of the agenda, Russia had not yet invaded Ukraine and the US election was coming on the back of a wave of historic civil rights protests. Four years later, we somehow find ourselves facing a historic rematch but the context could not feel more different and, alarmingly, more fraught. On Thursday, at 9pm EST, CNN will host the first presidential debate of the election race from Atlanta, Georgia.\par \par \uc2 Though there will be some new issues on the agenda \u8211\'20\'13 \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access and the mental competence of the candidates chief among them \u8211\'20\'13 perennial themes like the economy and immigration will still dominate the discussion.\par \par \uc2 The 90-minute debate, moderated by CNN\u8217\'20\'19s Jake Tapper and Dana Bash, will not have a studio audience, a request from the Biden team and a departure from previous debate setups. To avoid {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2020/sep/30/trump-debate-national-humiliation-analysis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 another frustrated outburst}}}\uc2 , Biden\u8217\'20\'19s team also asked for the candidates\u8217\'20\'19 microphones to be muted when it is not their turn to speak, which Trump\u8217\'20\'19s campaign agreed to. Only Trump and Biden will be on stage, with Biden on the right podium and Trump on the left \u8211\'20\'13 even this needed to be decided by coin flip lest one side felt their positioning unfair. And unlike their last debate, Trump will get the final word during closing statements (this was also decided by coin flip).\par \par \uc2 In today\u8217\'20\'19s newsletter I\u8217\'20\'19ll run through what to look out for later this week if you are planning on tuning into (or out of) the debate. That\u8217\'20\'19s right after the headlines.\par \par \uc2 Five big stories\par \par \uc2 Conservatives\par \par \uc2 | \uc2 Rishi Sunak\uc2  is facing a growing clamour to come clean about the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/politics/article/2024/jun/23/pressure-on-rishi-sunak-as-election-betting-scandal-grows"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 betting scandal engulfing Westminster}}}\uc2  after a fifth figure was drawn into the row. Nick Mason, a senior Conservative official, was the latest to be drawn into investigations by the gambling watchdog, amid reports he placed dozens of bets on the timing of the UK general election before it was announced.\par \par \uc2 The hajj\par \par \uc2 | At least {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/article/2024/jun/23/hajj-pilgrimage-death-toll-extreme-heat-mecca-saudi-arabia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 1,300 people have died during the hajj pilgrimage}}}\uc2 , which took place during intense heat, Saudi Arabia has said, adding that most of the deceased did not have official permits.\par \par \uc2 Environment\par \par \uc2 | A huge citizen testing blitz of rivers across Britain this summer has found {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/article/2024/jun/24/citizen-testing-rivers-britain-poor-ecological-health-pollution"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 75% are in poor ecological health}}}\uc2  as a result of pollution from water companies and agricultural runoff.\par \par \uc2 Labour\par \par \uc2 | Labour is to appoint dozens of peers if it wins the election, to push through its policies and improve the representation of women {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/politics/article/2024/jun/23/labour-add-dozens-peers-back-policies-improve-gender-balance"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in the House of Lords}}}\uc2 , the \uc2 Guardian\uc2  has learned. The plan comes despite \uc2 Keir Starmer\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s pledge to eventually abolish the Lords and amid growing concerns over the ballooning size and cost of the chamber.\par \par \uc2 Housing\par \par \uc2 | The monthly mortgage of a first-time buyer has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/money/article/2024/jun/24/mortgage-of-first-time-buyer-tops-1000-a-month-as-house-prices-and-rates-rise"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 soared by more than 60% to exceed \u163\'00\'A31,000 a month}}}\uc2  since the last general election. The financial squeeze has forced many younger borrowers to either look for smaller properties or to take out an ultra-long mortgage.\par \par \uc2 In depth: What to look out for between the low blows and embarrassing gaffes\par \par \uc2 Despite the criminal convictions and standard controversy surrounding \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , extensive polling shows the presidential race is still close \u8211\'20\'13 with many indicating Trump has the edge. So there is no doubt that both sides are taking this upcoming debate very seriously: \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has reportedly run away to the mountains with a close circle of advisers to tighten his argument and prepare retorts to the inevitable personal smears, while Trump is likely workshopping said insults and other attack lines with his vice-presidential hopefuls.\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s campaign so far has been focused on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jun/02/trump-social-media-threats"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 revenge, retribution}}}\uc2  and apocalyptic narratives about what will happen if Biden is re-elected. A rally in Wisconsin perhaps gives some insight into where he plans to take the debate: \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re going to end up in world war three with this person. He\u8217\'20\'19s the worst president ever.\u8221\'20\'1D Biden\u8217\'20\'19s team are hoping to remind the public of the kind of demagogic figure Trump has been and is vowing to be again if he returns to office \u8211\'20\'13 banking on the notion that the more the American public see of Trump the less they like him. The president will be hoping that this debate will be the turning point in the race, a reminder to the country of why Trumpism was rejected four years ago.\par \par \uc2 ***\par \par \uc2 The age factor\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s important to remember that while all the attention seems to be on Biden, most Americans {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ipsos.com/en-us/majority-americans-think-both-biden-and-trump-are-too-old-serve-second-terms"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 think both candidates are too old to serve}}}\uc2  second terms according to an Ipsos poll. When Biden was sworn in he became the oldest president in history, although at 77 Trump is hot on his heels. Together the pair make the oldest presidential matchup ever, so the health and competence of both nominees will be a heated topic.\par \par \uc2 The Trump campaign {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/2024/02/09/trump-classified-documents-charges-biden/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told}}}\uc2  a crowd earlier this year: ?\u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t think [Biden] knows he\u8217\'20\'19s alive.\u8221\'20\'1D Meanwhile, the current president has not been above age-related digs, frequently calling Trump \u8220\'20\'1Cconfused\u8221\'20\'1D, accusing the former president of \u8220\'20\'1Cunhinged ramblings\u8221\'20\'1D and seizing on every opportunity to highlight Trump\u8217\'20\'19s mix-ups. A verbal slip here \u8211\'20\'13 something {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/video/2024/mar/02/joe-biden-twice-confuses-gaza-with-ukraine-announces-plans-airdrop-aid-video"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 both candidates}}}\uc2  have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/mar/17/trump-verbal-gaffes-ohio-rally-bloodbath"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 been prone to}}}\uc2  in recent months \u8211\'20\'13 could prove fatal to their electoral hopes.\par \par \uc2 ***\par \par \uc2 Immigration\par \par \uc2 When Biden ran for office in 2020, reversing Trump\u8217\'20\'19s punitive and haphazard immigration policy was a central plank of his campaign. But as this election draws closer he has changed his tune, taking a more {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jun/03/biden-close-mexico-border-immigration-executive-order"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 restrictive stance after signing an executive order}}}\uc2  that temporarily closed the southern border to asylum seekers to shore up support from voters who have consistently shown disapproval of how he has handled the situation there. The move received significant {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jun/12/biden-border-executive-order-climate-risks"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pushback}}}\uc2  from the left so, to appease his progressive critics, Biden has since {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jun/18/us-citizenship-pathway-spouses-children-immigrants-joe-biden"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 announced another policy }}}\uc2  granting some undocumented migrants a path to citizenship if they have an American spouse, giving 550,000 people protection from deportation. He has also been keen to denounce the Republican-controlled House of Representatives for blocking long-term immigration reform, at Trump\u8217\'20\'19s behest. Biden\u8217\'20\'19s camp is hoping that this will lure Trump into a trap: discussing one of his most contentious policies, family separation at the border. Biden will probably try to make himself a firm but fair figure on immigration, while portraying Trump\u8217\'20\'19s past and future agendas as extreme and cruel.\par \par \uc2 Since he entered politics in 2016, Trump has always centred immigration. A second Trump term will see the resurrection of some of his old favourites, like the \u8220\'20\'1CRemain in Mexico\u8221\'20\'1D policy which forces non-Mexican asylum seekers to stay in Mexico and restarting construction of the border wall between the two countries. He also has vowed to launch the biggest \u8220\'20\'1Cdomestic deportation operation\u8221\'20\'1D ever and has said that he will seek to limit legal migration in to the US too.\par \par \uc2 Trump will wield the immigration debate like a hammer against Biden, likely pointing to the record-breaking number of border crossings as a reason not to trust Biden with immigration. At a rally earlier this month, Trump summarised his position like this: \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  wants an invasion. I want a deportation\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 ***\par \par \uc2 Abortion\par \par \uc2 In April the former president bragged about his central role in overturning the constitutional right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 : \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/12/donald-trump-abortion-roe-v-wade-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 we broke Roe v Wade}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D he told the press. But Trump\u8217\'20\'19s team has since come to realise that he is walking a fine line when it comes to reproductive rights. Republican efforts to restrict or completely ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  have backfired significantly in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/article/2024/may/14/abortion-rights-support-poll"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the polls}}}\uc2 , energising voters to turn out and vote Democrat. Trump has to balance the support of his evangelical and anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  base with the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.pewresearch.org/politics/2024/05/13/broad-public-support-for-legal-abortion-persists-2-years-after-dobbs/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 general public who broadly support \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  access}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The Democratic party believe \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is their magic bullet. Biden will be reminding everyone on Thursday that the rollback of reproductive rights is all Trump\u8217\'20\'19s fault. The party has united around a message of protecting what is left of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access and strengthening support on other reproductive health measures like contraception. Not only do they believe it is the most effective stick to beat Trump with and galvanise their base further, it also holds the chance of bringing back voters who are disaffected with Biden\u8217\'20\'19s other policies.\par \par \uc2 ***\par \par \uc2 Economy\par \par \uc2 American voters aren\u8217\'20\'19t giving the president any credit for the robust economic recovery that Biden claims to have delivered for them. It turns out quarterly GDP figures are not enough to make the public feel good, with Americans pointing to unaffordable rents, mortgages and goods. Biden will probably come out with all of the relevant indicators to try to convince the public, as he has been for the last year, that \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/mar/08/biden-strong-economy-stephen-moore-republican#:~:text=%E2%80%9COne%20thing%20that%20Biden%20said,%2C%20they're%20not%20growing."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 America has the best economy in the world}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 while attempting to draw attention to his legislative success such as the Inflation Reduction Act, which provided much needed investment in the country\u8217\'20\'19s infrastructure. Trump however has been painting a very different picture \u8211\'20\'13 one of a country that \u8220\'20\'1Cis collapsing into a cesspool of ruin, whose supply chain is broken, whose stores are not stocked, whose deliveries are not coming\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 while claiming the US was booming during his last term in office.\par \par \uc2 The candidates will also touch on a host of other issues including foreign policy, healthcare, Trump\u8217\'20\'19s trials, education and crime. There will be zingers, sneering personal attacks and embarrassing blunders, but neither side is underestimating the challenge of convincing the American public to vote for one of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.pewresearch.org/short-reads/2024/06/14/biden-trump-are-least-liked-pair-of-major-party-presidential-candidates-in-at-least-3-decades/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  the two most unpopular presidential candidates in decades}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 What else we\u8217\'20\'19ve been reading\par \par \uc2 *\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/tv-and-radio/article/2024/jun/22/radiant-charm-scene-stealing-tears-and-steamy-kisses-ncuti-gatwa-is-the-new-golden-age-of-doctor-who"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHe could have chemistry with a lamp-post\u8221\'20\'1D:}}}\uc2  as his maiden voyage in the Tardis comes to an end, Leila Latif has written about how Ncuti Gatwa\u8217\'20\'19s Time Lord has brought \u8220\'20\'1Ctelevisual dopamine\u8221\'20\'1D to Doctor Who. Hannah J Davies, deputy editor, newsletters\par \par \uc2 *\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/politics/article/2024/jun/22/you-asked-me-questions-ive-never-asked-myself-keir-starmers-most-personal-interview-yet"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Charlotte Edwardes\u8217\'20\'19 interview}}}\uc2  with \uc2 Keir Starmer\uc2  is one of the most revealing portraits I\u8217\'20\'19ve ever read of the man. He has no favourite novel or poem, there were no phobias when he was a child \u8211\'20\'13 he doesn\u8217\'20\'19t even dream, perhaps a gloomy indication of what his government will look like. Edwardes followed Starmer around for two months to get a sense of who the man is, and the conclusions are fascinating. Nimo\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Amelia Abraham offers {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/lifeandstyle/article/2024/jun/23/maybe-baby-could-a-fertility-coach-help-you-make-an-easier-parenting-decision"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a candid look}}}\uc2  at fertility coaching and how to deal with the pressure and uncertainty around whether to become a parent. Hannah\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Mass tourism to a number of picturesque, remote Italian villages has begun to wear on residents. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/article/2024/jun/23/were-not-anti-tourist-italys-picturesque-villages-struggle-to-cope-with-deluge-of-insta-visitors"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Angela Giuffrida}}}\uc2  finds out how locals are trying to keep \u8220\'20\'1CInsta-visitors\u8221\'20\'1D at bay. Nimo\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Another week, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/lifeandstyle/article/2024/jun/24/james-cracknell-olympic-rower-catastrophe-comas-comebacks-tories-partygate"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 another moving entry}}}\uc2  in this series on outstanding Olympians, as Simon Hattenstone meets James Cracknell or \u8211\'20\'13 as he sometimes refers to himself after a traumatic brain injury \u8211\'20\'13 \u8220\'20\'1Cthe man who used to be James Cracknell\u8221\'20\'1D. Hannah\par \par \uc2 Sport\par \par \uc2 Euros\par \par \uc2 | It took {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/football/article/2024/jun/23/scotland-hungary-euro-2024-match-report"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  Hungary until the 100th-minute of play }}}\uc2  to score the goal that sent Scotland out of the competition. Germany\u8217\'20\'19s Euro 2024 journey stuttered and slowed after the team fell {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/football/article/2024/jun/23/switzerland-germany-euro-2024-match-report"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 one goal behind Switzerland}}}\uc2 , but an equaliser from Niclas F\u252\'00\'FCllkrug in injury time was enough to send them through to the final 16.\par \par \uc2 Euros\par \par \uc2 | Harry Kane has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/football/article/2024/jun/23/harry-kane-hits-back-at-ex-player-critics-and-brings-up-their-past-england-failures"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 hit back at Gary Lineker}}}\uc2  by saying that pundits and former players need to show more responsibility, remember that they wore the shirt and were part of England\u8217\'20\'19s \u173\'00\'ADfailures at previous tournaments. It comes after Lineker caused a stir within the England camp after describing the team\u8217\'20\'19s performance against Denmark as \u8220\'20\'1Cshit\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Cricket\par \par \uc2 | Fast bowler Chris Jordan got a hat-trick and the American cricket team lost five wickets in six balls as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/sport/article/2024/jun/23/chris-jordan-basks-in-a-special-one-after-hat-trick-sets-up-england-rout"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 England secured its spot in the semi-finals of the Twenty20}}}\uc2  World Cup. Defending champion England crushed the United States by 10 wickets with 62 balls remaining in their last Super Eight game.\par \par \uc2 The front pages\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2  leads with \u8220\'20\'1CSunak urged to drop candidates as betting investigation widens\u8221\'20\'1D. The i follows the same story with \u8220\'20\'1CTories question Sunak\u8217\'20\'19s leadership as he resists calls to suspend betting scandal suspects\u8221\'20\'1D. The Financial Times reports \u8220\'20\'1CConservatives lose a third of their voters since January, survey finds\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The Telegraph leads with \u8220\'20\'1CLabour to rip up school trans ban\u8221\'20\'1D, while the Times has \u8220\'20\'1CLabour plan for changing gender with less evidence\u8221\'20\'1D. The Mail carries an \u8220\'20\'1Cexclusive\u8221\'20\'1D, reporting that \uc2 Rishi Sunak\uc2  is set to warn of \u8220\'20\'1CTen days left to stop \u8216\'20\'18disaster\u8217\'20\'19 of a Starmer supermajority\u8221\'20\'1D. Finally, the Mirror leads with \u8220\'20\'1CFrozen out by Sunak for telling the truth\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Today in Focus\par \par \uc2 New towns and old ideas: Labour\u8217\'20\'19s housing plan\par \par \uc2 What are Labour\u8217\'20\'19s proposals for fixing the housing crisis? {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/news/audio/2024/jun/24/new-towns-and-old-ideas-labours-housing-plan-podcast"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Robert Booth}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/news/audio/2024/jun/24/new-towns-and-old-ideas-labours-housing-plan-podcast"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  reports from Hitchin, North Hertfordshire}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Cartoon of the day | Edith Pritchett\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://ablink.email.theguardian.com/ss/c/TBl-lE0k4WbTlFRn6v-lQXxTpTslqnvUsR2ofAkC00vqkHXqakTSxrykj9mrdACFM7X02zB_4eaUcPGwGF8aSdwRgVGO90P9jWCTAme32U5T-vnI6XmWDMj3FJwYRpoHkFNbLC7gF6lJtLXkZEafGPr91zCNJfd75y4srJK7hF9rC7DtMprXX9waLOo6IasUuyiX2WyLj6_QAr2Er-sZ3pUo1lqR8H7xRgc_wdPt5vw6OZTdkayzug3kU3s7Kcsk-XG5uIH5ajjQ81Ur4lb9OdVIWg1quQfk4HV_8czlpcY/3om/atajwSjOR9WSWjozGj9ciw/h43/pcnM5h3gNALOSgMA7uWqlQhxgBX88j6XLDvP4QIlMes"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Sign up for Inside Saturday}}}\uc2  to see more of Edith Pritchett\u8217\'20\'19s cartoons, the best Saturday magazine content and an exclusive look behind the scenes\par \par \uc2 The Upside\par \par \uc2 A bit of good news to remind you that the world\u8217\'20\'19s not all bad\par \par \uc2 What should you do when your children move out? It\u8217\'20\'19s a familiar question to thousands of parents, but Kitty Johnson took an unusual path: she became an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/lifeandstyle/article/2024/jun/24/new-start-after-60-rescuing-injured-hedgehogs"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ambulance driver for hedgehogs}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CI had a friend whose son was leaving home and she was so terrified of it happening, I knew I needed to plan ahead and keep myself occupied to avoid feeling the same,\u8221\'20\'1D she says. \u8220\'20\'1CA few members of my Women\u8217\'20\'19s Institute group had been volunteering with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://hodmedods.org.uk/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Hodmedods Hedgehog Support}}}\uc2 , and it seemed like a worthy cause. I decided to join them.\u8221\'20\'1D Her first rescue came in May 2023, with some latex gloves and a box filled with newspaper, and she now spends her weekends driving around Norwich, hunting in bins, cemeteries and alleyways for injured animals. Kitty reckons she has completed close to 30 rescues in the year since.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2018/feb/12/the-upside-sign-up-for-our-weekly-email"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Sign up here}}}\uc2  for a weekly roundup of The Upside, sent to you every Sunday\par \par \uc2 Bored at work?\par \par \uc2 And finally, the \uc2 Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s puzzles are here to keep you entertained throughout the day. Until tomorrow.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/crosswords/quick/16890"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Quick crossword}}}\par \par \uc2 *\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/crosswords/cryptic/29417"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Cryptic crossword}}}\par \par \uc2 *\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wordiply.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Wordiply}}}\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240624ek6o000jh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
