\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 In Trump we trust: religious right on crusade to make their man president\b0\par\par\uc2 David Smith in Washington \par \uc2 1,587 \uc2 words\par \uc2 22 June 2024\par 19:21 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 America\u8217\'20\'19s evangelicals sense a chance to impose a radical agenda and resist what they see as a tide of liberal secularism\par \par \uc2 God\u8217\'20\'19s army is on the march. And many of its foot soldiers are wearing \u8220\'20\'1CMake America great again\u8221\'20\'1D regalia, sensing that their unlikely standard-bearer, former US president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , is once again close to the promised land.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI do not believe that America can survive another four years of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 Ralph Reed\uc2 , founder and chair of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ffcoalition.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Faith & Freedom Coalition}}}\uc2 , told a gathering of the religious right in Washington on Friday. \u8220\'20\'1CI haven\u8217\'20\'19t felt this way since \uc2 Jimmy Carter\uc2  was president.\u8221\'20\'1D The audience burst into knowing laughter.\par \par \uc2 Reed promised they would knock on 10m doors of Christian and conservative voters in every battleground state, make 10m phone calls, send 25m text messages and put 30m voter guides in 113,000 churches, producing \u8220\'20\'1Cthe biggest turnout of Christian voters in American history\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The election result will be clear, he added. \u8220\'20\'1CThis time there aren\u8217\'20\'19t gonna need to be any lawsuits. We\u8217\'20\'19re not going to have to go to court and we\u8217\'20\'19re not going to have to wait until 2.30 in the morning for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  to declare victory. He\u8217\'20\'19s going to do it at 9 o\u8217\'20\'19clock at night!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 With Trump running ahead of Biden in many swing state polls, religious right voters scent a historic opportunity to impose a radical agenda that could ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  nationwide, curb LGBTQ+ rights and blur the separation of church and state. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.c-span.org/video/?536527-1/republican-officials-address-faith-freedom-coalition-conference"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 At Friday\u8217\'20\'19s conference}}}\uc2 , speaker after speaker framed it as righteous crusade and the only way to resist a tide of liberal secularism sweeping America.\par \par \uc2 Ben Carson, a former housing secretary in Trump\u8217\'20\'19s first term, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/FaithandFreedom/status/1804149049903190385"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 praised Republican-dominated Louisiana}}}\uc2  for becoming the first state to require that the Ten Commandments be displayed in every government school classroom.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAren\u8217\'20\'19t you glad that yesterday the governor of Louisiana signed into law \u8211\'20\'13 put the Ten Commandments back in the schools?\u8221\'20\'1D he said to cheers and applause before warning of a 60-year communist project to change America by taking over schools, churches and Hollywood and removing God from the public square.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/feb/23/josh-hawley-anti-abortion-arguments-embryo-ruling"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Josh Hawley}}}\uc2 , a Republican senator for Missouri, warned of a \u8220\'20\'1Cradical anti-faith agenda\u8221\'20\'1D gripping the country. He said: \u8220\'20\'1CWho\u8217\'20\'19s dividing America is the radical left and that\u8217\'20\'19s why I say to you we don\u8217\'20\'19t need less Christian influence in our society, we don\u8217\'20\'19t need less Christian witness in our society; we need more in every part of government, in every part of society.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 To approving roars from the audience, Hawley added: \u8220\'20\'1CWe ought to take {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.hrc.org/resources/lgbtq-pride-flags"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Pride flag}}}\uc2  out of schools and put the Bible back in. You know what? We ought to take the trans flag down from all of our federal buildings and over every federal building in America write the words: \u8216\'20\'18In God we trust.\u8217\'20\'19 In God we trust. Amen. \u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The couching of an Armageddon election, in which religious truth itself is at stake, with victory representing divine providence and defeat spelling total catastrophe, was crystallised by Monica Crowley, a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://rumble.com/user/TheMonicaCrowleyPodcast"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 rightwing political commentator}}}\uc2  and former assistant secretary of the treasury.\par \par \uc2 She described the election as a \u8220\'20\'1Chinge moment\u8221\'20\'1D comparable to the American revolution, American civil war, second world war and September 11 terrorist attacks. She spoke of a \u8220\'20\'1Cwar\u8221\'20\'1D against \u8220\'20\'1Cthe enemy within\u8221\'20\'1D that has spent nearly half a century \u8220\'20\'1Cinfiltrating, undermining and destroying\u8221\'20\'1D America with \u8220\'20\'1Cgodless philosophies\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Crowley lamented that Hollywood no longer produces \u8220\'20\'1Cpatriotic films\u8221\'20\'1D like those of John Wayne and, extraordinarily, defended the communist witch-hunts of the 1950s. \u8220\'20\'1CSenator {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.npr.org/2021/10/18/1046648461/decades-before-trumps-election-lies-mccarthys-anti-communist-fever-gripped-the-g"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Joe McCarthy}}}\uc2  was right, and he was trying to ring the bell in the 1950s about communist infiltration in our government and the same deep state that is now going after \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe same deep state that removed {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/books/2021/jun/05/richard-nixon-tapes-michael-dobbs-book-donald-trump-impeachment"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Richard Nixon}}}\uc2 , the same deep state that went after \uc2 Ronald Reagan\uc2  and anybody else who stood up to them. That deep state became very insidious and in the 1950s smeared and attacked Joe McCarthy for speaking the truth about godless communism in very halls of our government.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Notably, little was said by the dozen main stage speakers about \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , a live political grenade for which Republicans have struggled find a coherent message since the supreme court overturned the landmark Roe v Wade precedent two years ago.\par \par \uc2 Religious conservatives\u8217\'20\'19 pact with Trump appears to be holding. Some were sceptical about the thrice-married reality TV star when he first ran for president in 2016 but the concerns were assuaged by his running mate, born-again evangelical Christian \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2 , and by a first term that saw him shift the judiciary to the right.\par \par \uc2 Not even Trump\u8217\'20\'19s conviction in New York last month on 34 felony counts in a trial involving hush-money payments to an adult film star has shaken his grip on this constituency. Many who complain that their faith is under siege regard him as a blunt instrument with which to fight back against the radical left.\par \par \uc2 They often rationalise their vote by saying they are choosing a president, not a pastor. Some evangelicals have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2018/12/31/opinion/trump-evangelicals-cyrus-king.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 likened him to Cyrus the Great}}}\uc2 , the Persian king who, according to the Bible, enabled Jews to return to Israel from their exile in Babylon.\par \par \uc2 Robert P Jones, the president and founder of the Public Religion Research Institute thinktank in Washington, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.whitetoolong.net/p/trump-the-totem?campaign_id=93&emc=edit_fb_20240620&instance_id=126741&nl=frank-bruni&regi_id=73407093&segment_id=170087&te=1&user_id=757069e6d408ae27eaeb8ed46f31e703"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wrote on Substack recently}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CThe transformation of Trump from a person to a symbol is the key to understanding the power of the Maga movement and the internal logic of the upside-down world where a unanimous guilty verdict in a fair trial results in solidified support, record fundraising, and desperate Christian defenses of a convicted felon.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The presumptive Republican nominee has exploited this totemic status. Earlier this year, he launched his own brand of Bible, selling for $59.99 each. During the trial, he shared social media posts comparing himself to Jesus Christ.\par \par \uc2 At Friday\u8217\'20\'19s Road to Majority policy conference, it was not uncommon to hear of the Almighty and Trump spoken in the same breath. Crowley said: \u8220\'20\'1CWe do have a fearless leader in \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , where they have thrown the kitchen sink at this man over nine years and they cannot believe that he is still standing. Hand of God!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/nov/03/kari-lake-trump-arizona-maga-republicanism-midterms"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kari Lake}}}\uc2 , a senate candidate in Arizona, said: \u8220\'20\'1CWe gotta bring Him back into our culture, into our lives, into our hearts and souls \u8211\'20\'13 and then also let\u8217\'20\'19s work to bring Donald J Trump back on November 5 .\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Inside the upmarket Washington hotel hosting the conference, there were vendors selling Maga merchandise, lifesize cardboard cutouts of Trump and an area where attendees could pose with head shots of their choice for his running mate.\par \par \uc2 Stephen Sandrelli, 60, posed with a picture of the US representative {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/jan/30/elise-stefanik-trump-republican-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Elise Stefanik}}}\uc2  against an Oval Office backdrop. \u8220\'20\'1CFirst of all, we\u8217\'20\'19ve got to deport millions \u8211\'20\'13 at least 15 million people,\u8221\'20\'1D he said of a second Trump term. \u8220\'20\'1CThe Democrats are terrorists. They hate our nation. They hate humankind.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey\u8217\'20\'19re trying to replace us \u8211\'20\'13 replacement theory, whatever you want to call it \u8211\'20\'13 and Trump cares about us. I believe he\u8217\'20\'19s a man that God has touched and he\u8217\'20\'19s doing the right thing. He\u8217\'20\'19s only blessed our country. He\u8217\'20\'19s only helped people.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Sandrelli, a former Democrat and federal government officer from Fitchburg, Massachusetts, added: \u8220\'20\'1CAnybody who supports \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is supporting murder .\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 But {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/sep/17/evangelical-christians-religious-right-republican-party-2024"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sensing political danger}}}\uc2 , Trump has refused to endorse a national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban. Some here felt let down. Wearing a red Maga cap, Thomas Dinkel, 16, who goes to a school in Morgantown, West Virginia, said: \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m going to be honest with you: as a pro-life Christian, it hurts. I see why he and a lot of other national Republicans are doing it. They\u8217\'20\'19re slowly backing away from the issue. It\u8217\'20\'19s ruffled some feathers.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI do back an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban. For right now, it\u8217\'20\'19s at the state level, and I respect that, but if it ever went as a federal ban, I would back that. I understand why Trump is having a stance on that, just like some other stances he\u8217\'20\'19s been taking lately. I pray that when he gets in, the least he can do for the pro-life communities is continue to back and appoint pro-life justices.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 But {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wvforlife.org/teen-resources/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Dinkel}}}\uc2  is supporting Trump and is willing to overlook his moral shortcomings, saying: \u8220\'20\'1CListen, I\u8217\'20\'19m a Christian. I mess up, you mess up. Everyone in this room messes up. We sin, we fall short, we turn away from God, and Trump has admitted to that. He\u8217\'20\'19s not the best person. He\u8217\'20\'19s not a perfect person. None of us are. He says that he\u8217\'20\'19s repented of his sins, and I\u8217\'20\'19m called to forgive Trump. \u8221\'20\'1D\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/dharpe45?ref_src=twsrc%5Egoogle%7Ctwcamp%5Eserp%7Ctwgr%5Eauthor"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Dorothy Harpe}}}\uc2 , an African American woman who is retired from a church in Atlanta, Georgia, was wearing a Maga cap and badge that said: \u8220\'20\'1CTrump was right!\u8221\'20\'1D The 74-year-old said: \u8220\'20\'1CHe tells the truth. People don\u8217\'20\'19t want to believe him, they think he always doing something wrong, but he\u8217\'20\'19s not. He\u8217\'20\'19s innocent of all the bogus charges they brought against him. God knows every man\u8217\'20\'19s heart, and I believe he is a Christian.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240622ek6m001e2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
