\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Supreme court to release more decisions Friday after upholding Trump-era tax rule on foreign income \u8211\'20\'13 live\b0\par\par\uc2 L\u233\'00\'E9onie Chao-Fong (now) and Chris Stein (earlier) \par \uc2 3,234 \uc2 words\par \uc2 20 June 2024\par 17:29 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Court delivers rulings on lower-profile cases as decisions on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, social media and Trump\u8217\'20\'19s prosecution for election meddling remain pendingUS supreme court rules against Washington couple in foreign investment taxation case\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.29pm BST\par \par \uc2 The White House has hit back {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/article/2024/jun/19/biden-netanyahu-us-arms-shipments"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 again }}}\uc2  against accusations by Israel\u8217\'20\'19s prime minister, \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2 , that the US is holding back weapons and ammunition from Israel in its war in Gaza.\par \par \uc2 The Israeli leader made the claims of a supposedly deliberate weapons delay {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/netanyahu/status/1803064164539081120?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw%7Ctwcamp%5Etweetembed%7Ctwterm%5E1803064164539081120%7Ctwgr%5Ee9d0d3ed46a73d9ca05eea98971f3490eb3c3954%7Ctwcon%5Es1_&ref_url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.theguardian.com%2Fworld%2Farticle%2F2024%2Fjun%2F19%2Fbiden-netanyahu-us-arms-shipments"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in a video posted on social media}}}\uc2  in which he implied that Israel\u8217\'20\'19s ability to prevail in the nine-month war with \uc2 Hamas\uc2  was being hampered as a result. Netanyahu said:\par \par \uc2 I said it\u8217\'20\'19s inconceivable that in the past few months the administration has been withholding weapons and ammunitions to Israel \u8211\'20\'13 Israel, America\u8217\'20\'19s closest ally, fighting for its life, fighting against Iran and our other common enemies.\par \par \uc2 The White House\u8217\'20\'19s spokesperson John Kirby, speaking to reporters today, said he had \u8220\'20\'1Cno idea\u8221\'20\'1D what Netanyahu\u8217\'20\'19s motivation was in making the statement.\par \par \uc2 We didn\u8217\'20\'19t know that video was coming. It was perplexing to say the least.\par \par \uc2 Kirby described Netanyahu\u8217\'20\'19s comments as \u8220\'20\'1Cdeeply disappointing and vexing\u8221\'20\'1D, adding:\par \par \uc2 [There\u8217\'20\'19s] no other country that\u8217\'20\'19s done more or will continue to do more than the United States to help Israel defend itself.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.13pm BST\par \par \uc2 The day so far\par \par \uc2 The supreme court put out a batch of new opinions this morning, none of which dealt with hotly anticipated cases on emergency abortions, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s immunity petition, or federal regulations that the conservative-dominated body has pending before it, though the justices did allow {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jun/20/abortion-trump-immunity-supreme-court-ruling-biden-politics-latest-updates?page=with:block-667436b18f083e48d0c657eb#block-667436b18f083e48d0c657eb"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a Trump-era tax provision}}}\uc2  on foreign investments to stand. However, we\u8217\'20\'19re not done hearing from the court this week: the justices {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jun/20/abortion-trump-immunity-supreme-court-ruling-biden-politics-latest-updates?page=with:block-667440a68f083e48d0c658e7#block-667440a68f083e48d0c658e7"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 will release more}}}\uc2  opinions on Friday. Meanwhile, the contours of next Thursday\u8217\'20\'19s presidential debate {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jun/20/abortion-trump-immunity-supreme-court-ruling-biden-politics-latest-updates?page=with:block-667454788f0816d8381404f8#block-667454788f0816d8381404f8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 are shaping up}}}\uc2 , with Trump opting to get the last word, and Biden the podium of his choosing. \uc2 Robert F Kennedy Jr\uc2  won\u8217\'20\'19t be on the debate stage, and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jun/20/abortion-trump-immunity-supreme-court-ruling-biden-politics-latest-updates?page=with:block-66745dd88f089e1574dbab6d#block-66745dd88f089e1574dbab6d"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 is not happy about it}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else has happened today so far:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump has the edge over Biden in several swing states, and is tied with him in Democratic stronghold Minnesota, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jun/20/abortion-trump-immunity-supreme-court-ruling-biden-politics-latest-updates?page=with:block-667458b68f0816d838140533#block-667458b68f0816d838140533"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a new poll found}}}\uc2 . However, the results are in the margin of error, and the survey also found support slipping for the former president among crucial independents.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2 , the Israeli prime minister, will make a joint address to Congress on 24 July at 2pm, Republican House speaker Mike Johnson{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jun/20/abortion-trump-immunity-supreme-court-ruling-biden-politics-latest-updates?page=with:block-66744ed28f0816d83814049b#block-66744ed28f0816d83814049b"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 announced}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Jeff Landry\uc2 , the Republican governor of Louisiana, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jun/20/abortion-trump-immunity-supreme-court-ruling-biden-politics-latest-updates?page=with:block-667449f48f0892b1922beb09#block-667449f48f0892b1922beb09"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 signed legislation}}}\uc2  mandating that the Ten Commandments be displayed in public classrooms.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.56pm BST\par \par \uc2 Independent presidential candidate Kennedy blames Trump, Biden for failure to qualify for debate\par \par \uc2 Robert F Kennedy Jr\uc2  has hit out at both \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , after the independent presidential candidate failed to qualify for the first presidential debate, to be hosted by CNN next Thursday.\par \par \uc2 The network said only Trump and Biden met their criteria for the debate. But in a statement, Kennedy blamed the two leading presidential contenders for keeping him off the debate stage:\par \par \uc2 Presidents Biden and Trump do not want me on the debate stage and CNN illegally agreed to their demand. My exclusion by Presidents Biden and Trump from the debate is undemocratic, un-American, and cowardly. Americans want an independent leader who will break apart the two-party duopoly. They want a President who will heal the divide, restore the middle class, unwind the war machine, and end the chronic disease epidemic.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2024/06/20/politics/cnn-debate-trump-biden/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 what CNN said}}}\uc2  about their qualifications to make the debate:\par \par \uc2 In order to qualify for participation, candidates had to satisfy the requirements outlined in Article II, Section 1 of the US Constitution to serve as president, as well as file a formal statement of candidacy with the \uc2 Federal Election Commission\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 According to parameters set by CNN in May, all participating debaters had to appear on a sufficient number of state ballots to reach the 270 electoral vote threshold to win the presidency and receive at least 15% in four separate national polls of registered or likely voters that meet CNN\u8217\'20\'19s standards for reporting.\par \par \uc2 Polls that meet those standards are those sponsored by CNN, ABC News, CBS News, Fox News, Marquette University Law School, \uc2 Monmouth University\uc2 , NBC News, The New York Times/Siena College, \uc2 NPR\uc2 /PBS NewsHour/Marist College, \uc2 Quinnipiac University\uc2 , The Wall Street Journal and \uc2 The Washington Post\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Biden and Trump were the only candidates to meet those requirements.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 New poll shows Trump with edge in swing states, tied with Biden in Democratic stronghold Minnesota\par \par \uc2 A new poll of swing states shows \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  with the edge over \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , and tied with the president in Minnesota, which has not supported a Republican presidential candidate in 52 years.\par \par \uc2 The poll was conducted by Emerson College, and lines up with other surveys that have indicated Biden faces uphill battle for re-election in November:\par \par \uc2 enltrJUNE STATE POLLS with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/thehill?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @thehill}}}\par \par \uc2 AZ: 47% Trump, 43% Biden\par \par \uc2 GA: 45% Trump, 41% Biden\par \par \uc2 MI: 46% Trump, 45% Biden\par \par \uc2 MN: 45% Trump, 45% Biden\par \par \uc2 NV: 46% Trump, 43% Biden\par \par \uc2 PA: 47% Trump, 45% Biden\par \par \uc2 WI: 47% Trump, 44% Biden {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/JvHu3EZT4M"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/JvHu3EZT4M}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/P6MuS7JNvT"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/P6MuS7JNvT}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Emerson College Polling (@EmersonPolling) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/EmersonPolling/status/1803805856523321626?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 20, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 Spencer Kimball, the executive director of Emerson College Polling, said the data indicates little movement in overall support for the two candidates since Trump was convicted of felony business fraud last month.\par \par \uc2 However, Kimball noted that \u8220\'20\'1Cresults fall within the poll\u8217\'20\'19s margin of error,\u8221\'20\'1D and that there have been signs of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s support declining with independent voters, who may play the deciding role in this election:\par \par \uc2 In Arizona, Trump\u8217\'20\'19s support among independents dropped five points, from 48% to 43%. In Michigan, Trump\u8217\'20\'19s support dropped three, from 44% to 41%, and in Pennsylvania, Trump dropped eight points, from 49% to 41%. Biden lost support among independents in Georgia, by six points, 42% to 36% and Nevada, by five, 37% to 32%.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.14pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump gets last word, Biden preferred podium placement at next week's CNN debate\par \par \uc2 The Trump and Biden campaigns flipped a coin to sort out some of the lingering issues ahead of next Thursday\u8217\'20\'19s first presidential debate, and CNN has announced the results.\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  won the coin flip, and opted to choose a specific podium. That left \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  to specify if he would have the last word of the debate, or leave that to Biden.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what the two candidates chose, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2024/06/20/politics/cnn-debate-closing-statements-podiums/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 from CNN}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 The coin landed on the Biden campaign\u8217\'20\'19s pick \u8211\'20\'13 tails \u8211\'20\'13 which meant his campaign got to choose whether it wanted to select the president\u8217\'20\'19s podium position or the order of closing statements.\par \par \uc2 Biden\u8217\'20\'19s campaign chose to select the right podium position, which means the Democratic president will be on the right side of television viewers\u8217\'20\'19 screens and his Republican rival will be on viewers\u8217\'20\'19 left.\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s campaign then chose for the former president to deliver the last closing statement, which means Biden will go first at the conclusion of the debate.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.52pm BST\par \par \uc2 Israeli prime minister Netanyahu to address Congress on 24 July\par \par \uc2 Republican speaker of the House Mike Johnson has announced that Israeli prime minister \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2  will address a joint session of Congress on 24 July.\par \par \uc2 Netanyahu\u8217\'20\'19s 2pm address will take place in the House chamber, and comes amid tensions with the Biden administration and some Democrats over the Israeli leader\u8217\'20\'19s handling of the invasion of Gaza. Earlier this year, \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2 , the Democratic Senate majority leader, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/mar/14/chuck-schumer-israel-speech"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 called for}}}\uc2  Israel to hold new elections, and said Netanyahu \u8220\'20\'1Chas lost his way\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more on Netanyahu\u8217\'20\'19s planned speech:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jun/03/netanyahu-congress-joint-session"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu set to address joint session of US Congress for fourth time}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.30pm BST\par \par \uc2 Louisiana\u8217\'20\'19s governor \uc2 Jeff Landry\uc2  just signed legislation to require public classrooms display the Ten Commandments \u8211\'20\'13 setting up a clash over the separation of church and state that seems destined for the courts.\par \par \uc2 The Republican governor invoked Moses yesterday, as he signed the bill:\par \par \uc2 enltrLouisiana Gov. \uc2 Jeff Landry\uc2  (R) invokes biblical figures as he signs a law requiring public school classrooms in the state to display the Ten Commandments:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf you want to respect the rule of law, you\u8217\'20\'19ve got to start from the original lawgiver, which was Moses." {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/3BywlBDmno"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/3BywlBDmno}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1803802937715495213?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 20, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 The supreme court has struck down previous attempts by states to mandate the Ten Commandments be displayed in classrooms, but they last ruled on the issue four decades ago:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jun/19/ten-commandments-louisiana-public-schools"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ten Commandments to be displayed in Louisiana public school classrooms}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.10pm BST\par \par \uc2 The supreme court weighed in today on a case regarding a provision of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s 2017 tax code overhaul dealing with foreign investments. But, as the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/lauren-aratani"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Lauren Aratani}}}\uc2  reports, the case was part of a larger battle over proposals to tax billionaires, and the court\u8217\'20\'19s decisions signaled that future skirmishes are to come:\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  on Thursday ruled against a Washington couple who argued they were unconstitutionally taxed $15,000 for their investment in a foreign company \u8211\'20\'13 in a case some have argued was a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/25/us-thinktank-billionaires-supreme-court-wealth-tax-lobbying"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 backdoor attempt}}}\uc2  to ban future wealth taxes.\par \par \uc2 The case, Moore v US, put into question what assets are considered taxable income. Some experts say the case was used as a vehicle to give the supreme court an opportunity to weigh in on a hypothetical billionaire\u8217\'20\'19s tax, which would raise similar questions on what assets can be taxed.\par \par \uc2 As the court {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/2023/12/05/supreme-court-trump-wealth-tax-offshore-earnings/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 was hearing}}}\uc2  the case in December, experts were worried that it put into question the long-established tax code, threatening to wreak havoc on what Americans may be taxed for.\par \par \uc2 The vote was 7-2 with Justice \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2  and Justice \uc2 Neil Gorsuch\uc2  dissenting. In his opinion, Justice \uc2 Brett Kavanaugh\uc2  described the ruling as \u8220\'20\'1Cnarrow\u8221\'20\'1D, leaving an opening for future challenges.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/ng-interactive/2024/jun/20/supreme-court-foreign-investment-tax-ruling"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US supreme court rules against Washington couple in foreign investment taxation case}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.51pm BST\par \par \uc2 Supreme court expected to release more decisions on Friday\par \par \uc2 The supreme court this morning issued four decisions dealing with less well-known criminal justices matters, as well as an aspect of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s 2017 tax code overhaul that covers shares in foreign companies.\par \par \uc2 The justices are expected to tomorrow release more opinions, and the chances that they will weigh in on the high-profile \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , federal regulation or Trump-related cases are high.\par \par \uc2 Among the cases they have left to decide is Trump\u8217\'20\'19s petition for immunity from the federal charges brought against him for trying to overturn the 2020 election:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/25/supreme-court-trump-immunity-claim"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US supreme court eyes returning Trump immunity claim to lower court after arguments}}}\par \par \uc2 As well as whether the Biden administration can force federally funded hospitals in Idaho to carry out emergency abortions, despite the state\u8217\'20\'19s strict ban:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/2024/apr/24/us-supreme-court-abortion-rights-emtala"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US supreme court appears divided after hearing arguments on emergency \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  care}}}\par \par \uc2 And a case that could upend a swath of federal regulations:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/article/2024/may/31/chevron-deference-doctrine-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 A supreme court case about fishermen could throw government into chaos}}}\par \par \uc2 The court may release their opinions on one, some, all, or perhaps even none of these cases tomorrow, starting at 10am ET. We\u8217\'20\'19ll be watching out for them on this blog.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.30pm BST\par \par \uc2 The supreme court issued two more opinions, both on comparatively obscure matters, and is now done releasing decisions for today.\par \par \uc2 One was Diaz v United States, which centered on a drug trafficking prosecution, and dealt with expert witness testimony. You can read their opinion {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.supremecourt.gov/opinions/23pdf/23-14_d1o2.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The second was Gonzalez v Trevino, a fairly convoluted case dealing with the evidence a plaintiff requires to prove that they were wrongfully arrested in Texas. That opinion can be found {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.supremecourt.gov/opinions/23pdf/22-1025_1a72.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.18pm BST\par \par \uc2 The second supreme court decision of today is Chiaverini v City of Napoleon, Ohio, which deals with situations in which someone who believes they have been wrongfully charged may bring a malicious-prosecution claim.\par \par \uc2 This is one of the lower-profile cases the court dealt with, and you can read how they ruled {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.supremecourt.gov/opinions/23pdf/23-50_n648.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.05pm BST\par \par \uc2 Supreme court upholds Trump-era tax rule on foreign income\par \par \uc2 The first case is Moore v United States, which deals with whether a one-time tax on Americans who hold shares in foreign corporations is legal.\par \par \uc2 The tax was created under the 2017 tax code overhaul enacted under \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . In a 7-2 vote, the court {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.supremecourt.gov/opinions/23pdf/22-800_jg6o.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 held}}}\uc2  that it is legal.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.24pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.59pm BST\par \par \uc2 Supreme court to release latest opinions\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s almost 10am here in Washington DC, which means the supreme court will soon release opinions.\par \par \uc2 As always, we do not know in advance how many opinions will be released, or on which cases. While the court, which is current composed of six conservative justices and three liberals, has cases pending that touch on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, federal regulations, social media and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s prosecution for election meddling, it also has to decide matters dealing with lower-profile aspects of federal law.\par \par \uc2 Either way, we\u8217\'20\'19ll let you know what the decisions are as they come out.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.46pm BST\par \par \uc2 The supreme court is the highest court in the United States, but their rulings are not always the final word on contentious legal topics. Case in point: mifepristone, the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  medication that the justices unanimously ruled last week could remain on the market. \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/carter-sherman"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Carter Sherman}}}\uc2  reports that, despite their failure at the court this time, conservatives are pursuing other legal challenges to the drug:\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/jun/13/supreme-court-abortion-pill-access"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 rejected an effort by anti-\b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  activists}}}\uc2  to roll back access to a common \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill \u8211\'20\'13 but the battle over the pill is far from over, both in the courts and in legislatures.\par \par \uc2 In a 9-0 unanimous decision on Thursday, the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/us-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US supreme court}}}\uc2  ruled that anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  activists did not have standing, or the legal right to sue, over the \uc2 Food and Drug Administration\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s (\uc2 FDA\uc2 ) regulation of mifepristone, one of two drugs typically used in a US medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . But because the case turns on an interpretation of legal doctrine, the justices left open the possibility that someone else may challenge mifepristone in the future.\par \par \uc2 Judge Matthew Kacsmaryk, a federal judge in Texas who first heard arguments in the case, has allowed Missouri, Idaho and Kansas to join the case as plaintiffs. Although the supreme court declined to let those states join the case once it was before \uc2 Scotus\uc2 , the states may continue litigating it at a lower-court level and evade the standing defects that doomed the case\u8217\'20\'19s original plaintiffs.\par \par \uc2 The powerful anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  group, SBA Pro-Life America, already emphasized that possibility in the organization\u8217\'20\'19s statement on the Thursday ruling.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe pro-life states of Idaho, Kansas and Missouri are seeking to take up the challenge based on harms suffered by women in their states,\u8221\'20\'1D the group said.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/article/2024/jun/13/supreme-court-abortion-pill-mifepristone"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Despite the supreme court ruling for the \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  pill, the battle is far from over}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.27pm BST\par \par \uc2 Independent Robert F Kennedy fails to qualify for first presidential debate\par \par \uc2 The window to qualify for the first presidential debate closed today at midnight, and CNN says that only \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  will appear on the debate stage next Thursday at their studios in Atlanta.\par \par \uc2 That is bad news for Robert F Kennedy, the independent who has campaigned as an alternative to both Democrats and Republicans, while facing controversy for his doubts over the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/06/robert-kennedy-jr-announces-run-for-president-anti-vaccine-activist"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 efficacy of vaccines}}}\uc2 , and belief in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/sep/26/robert-kennedy-jr-september-11-podcast-peter-bergen"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 other conspiracy theories}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2024/06/20/politics/cnn-debate-trump-biden/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 an article}}}\uc2  about the debate, CNN does not mention Kennedy or any other third-party candidate, but notes that only the current and former president met their criteria to qualify:\par \par \uc2 In order to qualify for participation, candidates had to satisfy the requirements outlined in Article II, Section 1 of the US Constitution to serve as president, as well as file a formal statement of candidacy with the \uc2 Federal Election Commission\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 According to parameters set by CNN in May, all participating debaters had to appear on a sufficient number of state ballots to reach the 270 electoral vote threshold to win the presidency and receive at least 15% in four separate national polls of registered or likely voters that meet CNN\u8217\'20\'19s standards for reporting.\par \par \uc2 Polls that meet those standards are those sponsored by CNN, ABC News, CBS News, Fox News, Marquette University Law School, \uc2 Monmouth University\uc2 , NBC News, The New York Times/Siena College, \uc2 NPR\uc2 /PBS NewsHour/Marist College, \uc2 Quinnipiac University\uc2 , The Wall Street Journal and \uc2 The Washington Post\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Biden and Trump were the only candidates to meet those requirements.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.09pm BST\par \par \uc2 Major \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and Trump cases remain undecided as supreme court set to issue latest batch opinions\par \par \uc2 Good morning, US politics blog readers. The big event for today comes first thing in the morning, when the supreme court releases another batch of opinions at 10am ET. While there\u8217\'20\'19s no telling which cases they will decide, the matters pending before the court give its conservative supermajority opportunities to upend \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access, federal regulations and the prosecution of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  for his alleged plot to overturn the 2020 election. The court has decided several cases so far this term, including {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/jun/13/supreme-court-abortion-pill-access"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 unanimously allowing}}}\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill mifepristone to remain on the market, and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/ng-interactive/2024/jun/14/supreme-court-bump-stock-ban-decision"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 doing the same}}}\uc2  for \u8220\'20\'1Cbump stocks\u8221\'20\'1D, the modification that allows firearms to fire rapidly and was banned under the Trump administration.\par \par \uc2 The latest batch of decisions comes amid questions over the justices\u8217\'20\'19 ethics, particularly conservatives \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2  and \uc2 Samuel Alito\uc2 . The former has been caught up {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jun/13/clarence-thomas-harlan-crow-trips#:~:text=The%20document%20shows%20private%20jet,DC%20and%20San%20Jose%2C%20California."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in a furor}}}\uc2  over his habit of traveling with a conservative billionaire, which he has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jun/07/clarence-thomas-harlan-crow-trips"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 only partially}}}\uc2  acknowledged, and the latter {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jun/11/samuel-martha-ann-alito-recording"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 flew flags}}}\uc2  sympathetic to rightwing causes at his properties. But neither justice has heeded Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 calls to recuse from deciding cases, and are expected to have their names on the opinions released today.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else is happening:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has a light schedule today, with little other than a trip to Camp David in the evening on his schedule. Perhaps he\u8217\'20\'19s busy preparing for his debate with Trump, set to take place in Atlanta on 27 June.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Mike Turner, the Republican chair of the House intelligence committee, will at 11am give a speech where he will call on Biden to declassify information about Russia\u8217\'20\'19s nuclear anti-satellite weaponry, warning it presents a grave threat to national security, Politico reports.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Fox News released {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.foxnews.com/official-polls/fox-news-poll-three-point-shift-biden-trump-matchup-since-may"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a poll}}}\uc2  showing Biden overtaking Trump in the support of national registered voters for the first time since last October. However, the president\u8217\'20\'19s support remains within its margin of error.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240620ek6k001uz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
