\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Battle over  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  rights in South Dakota constitution intensifies\b0\par\par\uc2 Carter Sherman \par \uc2 525 \uc2 words\par \uc2 18 June 2024\par 21:57 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  activists sue over ballot measure, leading group behind measure to ask federal judge to step in\par \par \uc2 Anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  activists in South Dakota have sued over a ballot measure to enshrine \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in the state constitution, leading the group behind the measure to ask a federal judge to step in and block the activists\u8217\'20\'19 effort.\par \par \uc2 Last week, South Dakota\u8217\'20\'19s Life Defense Fund filed a lawsuit accusing Dakotans for Health of fraud, turning in invalid signatures and failing to abide by the state rules that govern signature-gathering for ballot measures. Life Defense Fund has asked a South Dakota circuit court to take the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights measure off the November ballot.\par \par \uc2 In response, Dakotans for Health on Tuesday filed a motion in federal court arguing that Life Defense Fund\u8217\'20\'19s argument is faulty, because it relies on a law that has been blocked by a separate court order.\par \par \uc2 Life Defense Fund \u8220\'20\'1Care wrong on the facts and wrong on the law,\u8221\'20\'1D Rick Weiland, co-founder of Dakotans for Health, said in a statement. \u8220\'20\'1CThey aren\u8217\'20\'19t even aware that the law they are trying to use to claim our petition should be invalidated was itself invalidated over a year and half ago and no longer exists.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re reviewing the complaint, and we will continue to fight to protect mothers and babies from the atrocities of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in our state,\u8221\'20\'1D Jon Hansen, co-chair of Life Defense Fund and a Republican South Dakota state legislator, said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 Currently, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2023/nov/10/state-abortion-laws-us"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 South Dakota bans \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  except in cases of medical emergencies. The ballot measure would restore the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the first trimester of pregnancy, as well as require that \u8220\'20\'1Cregulation of a pregnant woman\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  decision, or of an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , during the second trimester must be reasonably related to the physical health of the pregnant woman\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 South Dakota would still be allowed to ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the third trimester of pregnancy, unless a doctor decides that an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is necessary to protect a patient\u8217\'20\'19s life or health.\par \par \uc2 Dakotans for Health turned in more than 50,000 signatures in support of putting the measure on the ballot.\par \par \uc2 The lawsuit is only the latest effort to stop the state\u8217\'20\'19s ballot measure from moving forward. In March, the South Dakota governor, \uc2 Kristi Noem\uc2 , signed into law a bill that would allow people to remove their signatures from ballot measure petitions, a move widely seen as an attack on the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights measure, which had not yet qualified for the ballot. Then, in May, the South Dakota secretary of state, Monae L Johnson, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://sdsos.gov/about-the-office/assets/Press%20Releases/SOSWarnsCitizensToRemainVigilantOnElectionCalls.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 released a statement warning voters}}}\uc2  about \u8220\'20\'1Cscammers\u8221\'20\'1D calling people and, while pretending to be officials from Johnson\u8217\'20\'19s office, urging them to take their names off petitions supporting the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights ballot measure.\par \par \uc2 South Dakota is one of at least three states where residents will be able to vote directly on whether to enshrine \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in the state constitution. Similar ballot measures are still pending in several other states, including electoral battlegrounds like Arizona and Nevada.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240618ek6i003jw\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
