\par\par \uc2 World news\par \b \uc2 G7\uc2  summit: Biden says lasting peace for Ukraine must be underwritten by Kyiv\u8217\'20\'19s ability to defend itself \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 L\u233\'00\'E9onie Chao-Fong (now); Martin Belam and Tom Bryant (earlier) \par \uc2 11,066 \uc2 words\par \uc2 13 June 2024\par 20:04 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 This live blog is now closed. For the latest on the \uc2 G7\uc2  summit, read more of our coverage here.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.39pm BST\par \par \uc2 Closing summary\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s a recap of the first day of the \uc2 G7\uc2  summit in Puglia, Italy:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The US and Ukraine signed a 10-year bilateral security agreement seen by Kyiv as a stopgap on the road to joining the Nato alliance. Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s president \uc2 Volodymyr Zelenskiy\uc2 , at a press conference, called it a \u8220\'20\'1Chistoric day\u8221\'20\'1D and thanked \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and \u8220\'20\'1Ceveryone in America\u8221\'20\'1D for the US\u8217\'20\'19s continued support.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  said the security pact would make Ukraine \u8220\'20\'1Cstrong, sustainable and resilient\u8221\'20\'1D. Russia\u8217\'20\'19s war has been a test of the world, the US president said at the joint presser, adding that the Russian leader, \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Ccannot wait us out. He cannot divide us.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Ukraine also signed a bilateral security deal with Japan on Thursday, providing Ukraine with $4.5bn this year and support for the next decade. Zelenskiy hailed the \u8220\'20\'1Cunique document with one of the world\u8217\'20\'19s most economically and technologically advanced countries\u8221\'20\'1D and thanked Tokyo for its \u8220\'20\'1Cunwavering support\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Italy has been accused of scrapping a reference guaranteeing access to \u8220\'20\'1Csafe and legal\u8221\'20\'1D abortions in the text of the \uc2 G7\uc2  summit\u8217\'20\'19s final declaration. The US and France have pushed back on the reported attempt by Italy\u8217\'20\'19s prime minister, Georgia Meloni, with the French president \uc2 Emmanuel Macron\uc2  expressing regret at Rome\u8217\'20\'19s position.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Ursula von der Leyen\uc2 , the president of the \uc2 European Commission\uc2 , has praised an agreement reached on guaranteeing a $50bn loan to Ukraine using profits from frozen \uc2 Russian central bank\uc2  assets held in Europe. \u8220\'20\'1CIt is a strong signal that we are sending to Ukraine that we will support Ukraine in its fight for freedom for as long as it takes,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CIt is also a strong signal to Putin that Putin cannot outlast us.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Russia has said that the \uc2 G7\uc2  agreement to provide Ukraine with $50bn in loans by using interest from frozen Russian assets would be criminal. \uc2 Russian foreign ministry\uc2  spokesperson, \uc2 Maria Zakharova\uc2 , said attempts by the west to take the income from frozen Russian assets would lead to a response from Moscow that would be very painful for the EU.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The UK, US and Canada have accused Russia of a plot to interfere in Moldova\u8217\'20\'19s presidential election and referendum on EU membership later this year. In a pointed joint statement issued on the first day of the \uc2 G7\uc2  summit in Italy, the three governments accused Russian actors of \u8220\'20\'1Cspreading lies\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cseeking to undermine Moldovan democratic institutions\u8221\'20\'1D in a campaign of political interference stretching back years.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.16pm BST\par \par \uc2 Zelenskiy: US-Ukraine security agreement 'benefits everyone in the world'\par \par \uc2 Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s president, \uc2 Volodymyr Zelenskiy\uc2 , warns that Russia is a \u8220\'20\'1Creal global threat\u8221\'20\'1D and notes that the security agreement between his country and the US is an agreement on \u8220\'20\'1Chow our nations will become stronger\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 This is an agreement on steps to guarantee sustainable peace and therefore it benefits everyone in the world.\par \par \uc2 Zelenskiy also notes that the agreement is a \u8220\'20\'1Cbridge\u8221\'20\'1D to Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s membership in Nato.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.09pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , answering a question from a reporter, says the US has not changed its position on providing longer-range weapons that would go further into Russia.\par \par \uc2 Biden also expresses his support for his son, \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2 , who was convicted of thee felony gun charges this week. He reiterates that he will not pardon his son.\par \par \uc2 I\u8217\'20\'19m not going to do anything. I said I\u8217\'20\'19d abide by the jury decision. I will do that.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.28pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.06pm BST\par \par \uc2 Volodymyr Zelenskiy\uc2  also thanks Biden for his leadership on the \uc2 G7\uc2  decision on a $50bn loan for Ukraine, and says it is a vital step forward in providing sustainable support for Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.27pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.02pm BST\par \par \uc2 Zelenskiy says this is a 'historic day' after signing security agreement with US\par \par \uc2 Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s president, \uc2 Volodymyr Zelenskiy\uc2 , says today is a historic day, and that the deal is an agreement \u8220\'20\'1Con security and thus, on the protection of human life\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Zelenskiy says the security deal with the US is the strongest agreement since Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s independence, as he thanks \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  for his leadership and for his years of support for Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 I\u8217\'20\'19m proud of our people and what Ukraine can do. And I\u8217\'20\'19m very grateful to all Americans, to everyone in America, who stresses American leadership.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.26pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.59pm BST\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 G7\uc2  has achieved \u8220\'20\'1Csignificant\u8221\'20\'1D outcomes in the matter of Russia\u8217\'20\'19s frozen assets, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  says.\par \par \uc2 He says the steps taken by the \uc2 G7\uc2  will create a stronger foundation for Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s success.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.53pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden: Lasting peace for Ukraine must be underwritten by Ukraine's ability to defend itself\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and \uc2 Volodymyr Zelenskiy\uc2  are holding a joint press conference, just over two hours behind schedule, after signing a 10-year bilateral security agreement at the \uc2 G7\uc2  summit.\par \par \uc2 Biden begins by saying that lasting peace for Ukraine must be underwritten by Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s ability to defend itself now and to deter future aggression anytime in the future.\par \par \uc2 The US is going to help ensure Ukraine can do both by sending American troops, funding new weapons and ammunition, expanding intelligence sharing, continuing to train Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s troops and bases in Europe and the US, and investing in Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s defense industrial base, Biden says.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.25pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.41pm BST\par \par \uc2 Macron deplores lack of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  reference in \uc2 G7\uc2  declaration\par \par \uc2 France\u8217\'20\'19s president, \uc2 Emmanuel Macron\uc2 , has said \u8220\'20\'1CI regret this\u8221\'20\'1D when asked about the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/article/2024/jun/13/giorgia-meloni-italy-accused-of-scrapping-safe-abortion-guarantee-from-g7-declaration"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 lack of reference to \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  in the text of the \uc2 G7\uc2  summit\u8217\'20\'19s final declaration.\par \par \uc2 France does not share the same sensitivites regarding \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  as Italy, Macron told reporters.\par \par \uc2 France \u8220\'20\'1Chas included women\u8217\'20\'19s right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the freedom of decision on one\u8217\'20\'19s own body, into its constitution,\u8221\'20\'1D he said, adding France defends \u8220\'20\'1Cthis vision of equality between women and men\u8221\'20\'1D, AP reported.\par \par \uc2 Addressing an Italian reporter on the sidelines of the \uc2 G7\uc2  summit, the French leader said:\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s not a vision that\u8217\'20\'19s shared across all the political spectrum \u8230\'20\'26 I regret it, but I respect it because it was the sovereign choice of your people.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.52pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.27pm BST\par \par \uc2 Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s president, \uc2 Volodymyr Zelenskiy\uc2 , has called on the \uc2 G7\uc2  leaders to approve \u8220\'20\'1CMarshall Plan\u8221\'20\'1D for Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s recovery after the war.\par \par \uc2 A readout of his speech posted on the Ukrainian president\u8217\'20\'19s website referenced the multi-billion dollar programme between the US and Europe after the second world war. Zelenskiy said:\par \par \uc2 We need a clear plan for the recovery of Ukraine. Similar to what the Marshall Plan was for Europe after the war.\par \par \uc2 Zelenskiy called on the group to agree on a recovery plan \u8220\'20\'1Cin time for the Nato summit in Washington,\u8221\'20\'1D which will take place in early July.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.34pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.05pm BST\par \par \uc2 All \uc2 G7\uc2  countries will contribute to a loan package worth some $50bn to Ukraine backed by proceeds from frozen Russian assets, \uc2 Ursula von der Leyen\uc2 , the president of the \uc2 European Commission\uc2 , has said.\par \par \uc2 Speaking to reporters on the sidelines of the \uc2 G7\uc2  summit, she said:\par \par \uc2 All \uc2 G7\uc2  are contributing to this loan. It is the windfall profits from the Russian immobilised assets in Europe that will serve it.\par \par \uc2 She added:\par \par \uc2 The finance ministers are now going through the details \u8211\'20\'13 for example, the topic of backstops that are necessary \u8211\'20\'13 and (will) clarify this as soon as possible.\par \par \uc2 enltrThe \uc2 G7\uc2  has agreed to provide Ukraine with loans worth around $50 bn by end of year.\par \par \uc2 We'll use the windfall profits from Russia\u8217\'20\'19s sovereign assets to repay them.\par \par \uc2 This builds on EU action, where we are already directing these windfall profit to Ukraine's defence & reconstruction. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/nYu2g78X18"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/nYu2g78X18}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Ursula von der Leyen\uc2  (@vonderleyen) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/vonderleyen/status/1801307519845077291?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 13, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.18pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.54pm BST\par \par \uc2 Germany\u8217\'20\'19s chancellor \uc2 Olaf Scholz\uc2  has described a deal by \uc2 G7\uc2  leaders to lend $50bn to Ukraine from the proceeds of frozen Russian assets as a \u8220\'20\'1Chistoric step\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Scholz, speaking to reporters at the \uc2 G7\uc2  summit in Italy, said the deal is \u8220\'20\'1Ca very strong commitment\u8221\'20\'1D that gives Ukrainians \u8220\'20\'1Cthe courage to do what is now necessary for them to defend their independence and sovereignty\u8221\'20\'1D, AP reported.\par \par \uc2 The agreement is also \u8220\'20\'1Ca clear signal\u8221\'20\'1D to the Russian president, \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2 , that he \u8220\'20\'1Ccannot simply take advantage of a situation and hope that he will succeed in winning this war\u8221\'20\'1D because some countries supporting Ukraine are now facing fiscal problems, he said.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden and Zelenskiy to hold joint news conference after signing 10-year security agreement\par \par \uc2 The presidents of the US and Ukraine, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and \uc2 Volodymyr Zelenskiy\uc2 , are about to hold a joint press conference after signing a 10-year bilateral security agreement at the \uc2 G7\uc2  summit in Italy.\par \par \uc2 The agreement is meant to be a step towards Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s eventual Nato membership, according to the text of the deal, Reuters reports. The text reads:\par \par \uc2 The parties recognize this agreement as supporting a bridge to Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s eventual membership in the \uc2 NATO\uc2  alliance.\par \par \uc2 It states that in the event of an armed attack or threat of such against Ukraine, top US and Ukrainian officials will meet within 24 hours to consult on a response and determine what additional defense needs are required for Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 Under the agreement, the US restates its support for Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s defense of its sovereignty and territorial integrity, amid a renewed push by Russia on Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s eastern front.\par \par \uc2 To ensure Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s security, both sides recognize Ukraine needs a significant military force, robust capabilities, and sustained investments in its defense industrial base that are consistent with \uc2 North Atlantic Treaty Organization (NATO)\uc2 standards.\par \par \uc2 The United States intends to provide long-term materiel, training and advising, sustainment, intelligence, security, defense industrial, institutional, and other support to develop Ukrainian security and defense forces that are capable of defending a sovereign, independent, democratic Ukraine and deterring future aggression.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.38pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.28pm BST\par \par \uc2 US president \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  briefly spoke to reporters after posing for photos following a skydiving demonstration.\par \par \uc2 Asked if the leaders discussed the Gaza ceasefire deal, Biden said, \u8220\'20\'1CYes,\u8221\'20\'1D per pool report.\par \par \uc2 Asked if he was confident they would get a deal soon, he said \u8220\'20\'1CNo,\u8221\'20\'1D adding \u8220\'20\'1CI haven\u8217\'20\'19t lost hope.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Hamas\uc2  has to move,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden added.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 G7\uc2  leaders have been pictured attending a skydiving demonstration on the first day of the summit in Savelletri, Italy.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.30pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.17pm BST\par \par \uc2 Italy has demanded to remove reference to \u8220\'20\'1Csafe and legal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D from the text of the \uc2 G7\uc2  summit\u8217\'20\'19s final declaration, Reuters reported, citing diplomats.\par \par \uc2 Italian media have reported that a sidebar clause on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights had been left out of a last draft of the final declaration circulated on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 The clause had been intended to reinforce an agreement by the \uc2 G7\uc2  members in Japan last year that they would guarantee \u8220\'20\'1Ceffective and safe access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 It also committed to sexual and reproductive health rights for all, \u8220\'20\'1Cincluding by addressing access to safe and legal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and post-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 One diplomat was cited as saying:\par \par \uc2 All the other countries backed them, but it was a red line for Meloni so it is absent from the final text.\par \par \uc2 A senior US official told reporters that the US president, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , \u8220\'20\'1Cfelt very strongly\u8221\'20\'1D that he did not want the reference to disappear from the text.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/article/2024/jun/13/giorgia-meloni-italy-accused-of-scrapping-safe-abortion-guarantee-from-g7-declaration"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Italy accused of scrapping safe \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  guarantee from G7 declaration}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.07pm BST\par \par \uc2 Unsurprisingly, the former Ukrainian minister of the economy and now president of the Kyiv School of Economics, Tymofiy Mylovanov, said the government was keen to move on from the sound and fury around both men\u8217\'20\'19s departures, and to present instead, its Ukraine Investment Guide, a glossy brochure which, over 238 pages highlights the 95 projects worth more than $27bn for investors including detailed information on Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s vast \u8220\'20\'1Cinvestment landscape\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 This, say others close to the government, is attestation to the \u8220\'20\'1Ccommitment the government has for the reconstruction process\u8221\'20\'1D, in contrast to what Nayyem\u8217\'20\'19s allies are saying.\par \par \uc2 According to the conference organisers, deals worth $16bn in relation to these investments, were sealed at the two day event. Mylovanov said:\par \par \uc2 If you look at actual evidence, Ukraine is moving according to the plan.\par \par \uc2 Returning briefly to talk about Mustafa Nayyem, who he described as a friend, he referred to his key role in the Maidan revolution of 2014, after he called for street protests which eventually became the the revolution which toppled Viktor Yanukovych and his government, and said that was what he would be remembered for.\par \par \uc2 He is the one who triggered the revolution in 2014. He\u8217\'20\'19ll be in the history books, I probably won\u8217\'20\'19t.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.29pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.05pm BST\par \par \uc2 Former Ukrainian minister of the economy Tymofiy Mylovanov, who is now president of the Kyiv School of Economics, told the Guardian in an interview on the sidelines of the Ukraine Recovery conference in Berlin that the dismissal of Kubanov and the subsequent resignation of Mustafa Nayyem was a \u8220\'20\'1Cnormal part\u8221\'20\'1D of the cut and thrust of a healthy democratic administration and an unsurprising component in any organisational switch.\par \par \uc2 Mylovanov said:\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s the friction you get in a democracy but not in a dictatorship. It\u8217\'20\'19s like getting the flu, which ultimately strengthens your immune system.\par \par \uc2 Recalling when he had entered his post as economy minister in 2019, he said:\par \par \uc2 I had no time to care about whether people (in the ministry) were corrupt or not, I just fired everyone who was in the way. I was not cleaning up the ministry, I was getting land market reform through. That was my goal.\par \par \uc2 Had he had longer in the job (he held the post until 2020) he might have taken it slower. \u8220\'20\'1CI would probably say, let\u8217\'20\'19s take it slow \u8230\'20\'26 let\u8217\'20\'19s engage people, let\u8217\'20\'19s train, upskill \u8230\'20\'26 and then go for the reforms.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He said Nayyem had arguably concentrated too much on fundamental change and whilst he did not deny that tackling corruption was important, often more urgent, practical progress, especially at this, a time of war, was needed.\par \par \uc2 In that job people judge you every two weeks, especially when they don\u8217\'20\'19t have the buildings they need because you\u8217\'20\'19re concentrating on reforming the environment, on tackling corruption on a local level, which is all well and good, but not when you need the buildings.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.22pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.55pm BST\par \par \uc2 Following recent reports over differences of opinion in the Ukrainian government over its reconstruction procedures, including suggestions that some of its foreign partners had expressed misgivings over the Kyiv administration\u8217\'20\'19s direction and reliability, as well as concerns about centralising tendencies in \uc2 Volodymyr Zelenskiy\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s administration, there has been considerable pushback on the sidelines of negotiations both at the Ukraine Recovery Conference (URC) and in briefings leading up to the current \uc2 G7\uc2  meeting and the upcoming Peace Summit in Switzerland.\par \par \uc2 Existing concerns were brought to a head following the recent firing of \uc2 Oleksandr Kubrakov\uc2  as infrastructure minister and the subsequent resignation of Mustafa Nayyem, who Kubrakov had hired as the head of Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s agency for infrastructure and redevelopment.\par \par \uc2 Kyiv sources had suggested that the men had been thought to be too free-spirited in their thinking and at the same time had been too close to their western donors. Nayyem stands accused by some of focusing too much on anti-corruption efforts and was therefore too slow delivering on recovery, even though many argue the two go hand in hand.\par \par \uc2 The Guardian{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/article/2024/jun/10/ukraine-reconstruction-agency-chief-quits-recovery-conference-mustafa-nayyem"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported this week}}}\uc2  that Nayyem felt he had been systematically undermined by the government from doing his job and had been prevented from attending the URC.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.40pm BST\par \par \uc2 Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s president \uc2 Volodymyr Zelenskiy\uc2  and his US counterpart, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , are scheduled to deliver a press conference from Italy shortly.\par \par \uc2 The two leaders are slated to sign a 10-year bilateral security agreement at the \uc2 G7\uc2  summit, a deal that Zelenskiy has described as \u8220\'20\'1Cunprecedented\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Kyiv has signed 15 bilateral security agreements with other countries since the full-scale Russian invasion began in 2022, including with the UK, France, Germany and Italy. As with the other bilateral pacts, the agreement with the US will not require America to come to Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s defence if attacked. But it could make it easier for Ukraine to enter into peace negotiations with Russia, as Kyiv would have some assurance about the help it would receive in the event of a further Russian attack.\par \par \uc2 The US-Ukraine agreement does not require the authorisation of Congress and could be undone by a future Trump administration.\par \par \uc2 Biden has said previously that guarantees for Ukraine would be equivalent to those to Israel, covering financial and military assistance as well as the possibility of the joint weapons production.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.02pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.26pm BST\par \par \uc2 Pope Francis\uc2  is expected to met with the leaders of the US, Ukraine, France and India, among others, on the sidelines of the \uc2 G7\uc2  summit, the Vatican has said.\par \par \uc2 Francis, who has previously warned against the \u8220\'20\'1Cperverse\u8221\'20\'1D dangers of artificial intelligence, will take part in leaders\u8217\'20\'19 talks on AI on Friday.\par \par \uc2 Francis is the first pope to participate in \uc2 G7\uc2  discussions, Reuters reported.\par \par \uc2 The Vatican said he will have a bilateral meeting with \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , as well as one-on-one meetings with Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 Volodymyr Zelenskiy\uc2 , France\u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 Emmanuel Macron\uc2 , India\u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 Narendra Modi\uc2 , Brazil\u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva\uc2 , Canada\u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 Justin Trudeau\uc2 , Turkey\u8217\'20\'19s Recep \uc2 Tayyip Erdogan\uc2 , Kenya\u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 William Ruto\uc2 , Algeria\u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 Abdelmadjid Tebboune\uc2 , and the head of the \uc2 International Monetary Fund\uc2 , \uc2 Kristalina Georgieva\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.11pm BST\par \par \uc2 G7\uc2  leaders 'concerned' about Israel's ongoing ground operations in Rafah \u8211\'20\'13 draft statement\par \par \uc2 G7\uc2  leaders are preparing to express their concerns about Israel\u8217\'20\'19s ongoing ground operations in Rafah, but will not explicitly call on Israel to stop their current actions or set out any consequences if they do not.\par \par \uc2 The draft statement reads:\par \par \uc2 We are concerned about the consequences of the ongoing ground operations in Rafah on the civilian population and the possibility of a large-scale military offensive that would have further disastrous consequences on civilians. We call on the Government of Israel to refrain from such an offensive, in line with its obligations under international law.\par \par \uc2 It also urges \u8220\'20\'1Call parties must refrain from any unilateral action that undermines the prospect of a two-state solution, including Israeli settlement expansion and the \u8216\'20\'18legalization\u8217\'20\'19 of settlement outposts. We condemn the increase in extremist settler violence committed against Palestinians, which undermines security and stability in the West Bank and threatens the prospects for lasting peace.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 We reiterate our firm commitment to the vision of a two-state solution in which two democratic states, Israel and Palestine, coexist side by side in peace within secure and recognized borders, in line with international law and relevant resolutions of United Nations, and in this regard we underline the importance of unifying the Gaza Strip with the West Bank under the \uc2 Palestinian Authority\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Predictably it backs the peace plan outlined by \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , but gives no interpretation on the issues \uc2 Hamas\uc2  is seeking further clarification including the withdrawal of \uc2 Israeli Defence Forces\uc2  troops.\par \par \uc2 On humanitarian aid the \uc2 G7\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Cwill urge all parties to facilitate the rapid and unhindered passage of humanitarian aid to civilians in need, especially women and children\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 It says Israel should \u8220\'20\'1Censure full, rapid, safe and unhindered humanitarian access in all its forms, in line with international humanitarian law, and through all relevant land crossings, including the Rafah crossing, through maritime delivery routes, including the port of Ashdod, and throughout Gaza, remains an absolute priority\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 It sets no date for the recognition of a Palestinian state, saying \u8220\'20\'1CWe note that mutual recognition, including the recognition of a Palestinian state, at the appropriate time, would be a crucial component of such a political process.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 It also calls for the unification of Gaza and the West Bank under the rule of the \uc2 Palestinian Authority\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.04pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.57pm BST\par \par \uc2 At the interim hearing on Thursday, Jemima Stratford KC for \uc2 Amnesty International\uc2  and \uc2 HRW\uc2  argued the organisations have broad international experience on state compliance with international humanitarian law that differs from Al-Haq\u8217\'20\'19s.\par \par \uc2 Sean Aughey for \uc2 Oxfam\uc2  argued that as an agency working on the ground in Gaza, they have witnessed first-hand, the devastation the \uc2 IDF\uc2  has caused on life-saving aid and vital infrastructure.\par \par \uc2 Jessica Wells KC on behalf of the secretary of state for business and trade said: \u8220\'20\'1CIt needs to be established that anything \uc2 HRW\uc2 , Amnesty or \uc2 Oxfam\uc2  are adding is really necessary,\u8221\'20\'1D adding, \u8220\'20\'1CThe court won\u8217\'20\'19t be assisted by further untargeted evidence.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 At the hearing\u8217\'20\'19s outset, Justice Farbey expressed concern at the length of Amnesty and \uc2 HRW\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s submission, including 265 footnoted documents and a 42-paged annex, of open source evidence of Israel\u8217\'20\'19s actions including forced displacement, targeting practices and the provision of access to aid.\par \par \uc2 Justice Fabey granted the organisations the opportunity to provide a shorter document, and permitted \uc2 Oxfam\uc2  a written and oral intervention in the substantive case, due to be heard in mid October. The organisation\u8217\'20\'19s chief executive, Halima Begum, said:\par \par \uc2 Oxfam\uc2  has been systematically prevented from getting life-saving aid into the enclave, and our staff and partners face a constant threat to their lives while trying to sustain basic humanitarian operations.\par \par \uc2 Welcoming the decision, \uc2 Amnesty International\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s UK chief executive, Sacha Deshmukh, said he believed it \u8220\'20\'1Cvital\u8221\'20\'1D the court has the opportunity to review human rights evidence from themselves and \uc2 HRW\uc2 . Deshmukh said:\par \par \uc2 Our evidence demonstrates the gap between the Israeli military and political leadership\u8217\'20\'19s policies and practices and their legal obligations,.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.04pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.51pm BST\par \par \uc2 The UK high court has granted international human rights organisations permission to intervene in an ongoing legal challenge to suspend UK arms sales to Israel.\par \par \uc2 Oxfam\uc2 , \uc2 Amnesty International\uc2  and \uc2 Human Rights Watch\uc2  (\uc2 HRW\uc2 ) on Thursday joined the case being brought by the Palestinian human rights organisation Al-Haq and the UK-based Global Legal Action Network (Glan), who applied for a judicial review of the government\u8217\'20\'19s export licences for the sale of British weapons capable of being used in Israel\u8217\'20\'19s action in Gaza, which has killed more than 36,000 Palestinians.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn my judgement \uc2 Oxfam\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s evidence is ready, concise and targeted at matters that concern its own experience as a humanitarian organisation operating in Gaza,\u8221\'20\'1D Justice Farbey said, adding that \uc2 Amnesty International\uc2  and \uc2 Human Rights Watch\uc2  would be allowed to provide written evidence to the court.\par \par \uc2 The two intervention applications put forward by \uc2 Oxfam\uc2 , and \uc2 Human Rights Watch\uc2  and \uc2 Amnesty International\uc2  are expected to bring more legal firepower to the legal challenge which has called for a review of the \uc2 UK Department for Business and Trade\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s export licences for the sale of British weapons capable of being used in Israel\u8217\'20\'19s action in Gaza.\par \par \uc2 Recent government figures have revealed that the UK has issued {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/article/2024/jun/11/more-than-100-arms-export-licences-to-israel-issued-by-uk-since-7-october"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 more than 100 arms export licences to Israel}}}\uc2  between 7 October and 31 May. Last month, the \uc2 UK government\uc2  announced they had found no reason to suspend arms exports to Israel upon further review of the \uc2 Israel Defense Force\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s presence in Gaza. The latest government review examined the \uc2 IDF\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s behaviour until 24 April, including an Israeli airstrike that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/politics/article/2024/may/02/david-cameron-backed-israel-arms-sales-two-days-after-death-of-uk-aid-workers"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 killed three British aid workers on 1 April}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.39pm BST\par \par \uc2 The joint statement by the US, UK and Canada accuses Russia of \u8220\'20\'1Cconsistently\u8221\'20\'1D attempting to \u8220\'20\'1Cinfluence, subvert, and undermine democratic elections in order to secure results favorable to the Kremlin.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The three \uc2 G7\uc2  nations are \u8220\'20\'1Cstand firmly against persistent Kremlin attempts to use disinformation, criminal and covert activities, and corruption to undermine sovereignty and democratic processes,\u8221\'20\'1D the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.state.gov/joint-statement-exposing-russias-subversive-activity-and-electoral-interference-targeting-moldova/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 statement}}}\uc2  reads.\par \par \uc2 The Kremlin relies on lies, deceit, corruption and disinformation to undermine sovereignty and democracy. While democracy thrives on openness and truth-telling, authoritarianism and disinformation depend on secrecy and deception.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.23pm BST\par \par \uc2 UK, US and Canada accuse Russia of interfering in Moldovan elections\par \par \uc2 Three countries at the \uc2 G7\uc2  summit \u8211\'20\'13 the US, UK and Canada \u8211\'20\'13 have issued a joint statement claiming that Russia is interfering with Moldova\u8217\'20\'19s October election.\par \par \uc2 The three countries warn that \u8220\'20\'1CRussian actors are carrying out a plot to influence outcomes of Moldova\u8217\'20\'19s 2024 presidential election\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cintend to incite protests in Moldova should a pro-Russia candidate not win.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The statement claims Russian actors are \u8220\'20\'1Cspreading lies about the incumbent president\u8217\'20\'19s character and intentions, and about supposed electoral irregularities\u8221\'20\'1D and intend to whip up protests.\par \par \uc2 The US, UK and Canada say they are working with Moldovan authorities and sanctioning those behind the attempted interference.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBy revealing the Kremlin\u8217\'20\'19s plot, we are making it clear to Moscow that we stand for free and fair elections and will not tolerate its attempts to meddle and undermine democratic processes,\u8221\'20\'1D the statement says.\par \par \uc2 The breakaway Moldovan region of Transnistria, which has Russian troops stationed in it, borders Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.16pm BST\par \par \uc2 Ukraine and Japan sign $4.5bn security agreement\par \par \uc2 Ukraine and Japan have signed a security agreement on the sidelines of the \uc2 G7\uc2  summit, \uc2 Volodymyr Zelenskiy\uc2  has confirmed.\par \par \uc2 The Ukrainian leader had earlier said he would sign bilateral security agreements with Japan\u8217\'20\'19s prime minister, \uc2 Fumio Kishida\uc2 , and US president \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Under the \u8220\'20\'1Cunique\u8221\'20\'1D agreement, Japan has agreed to provide Ukraine with $4.5bn and will \u8220\'20\'1Ccontinue to support us throughout the agreement\u8217\'20\'19s entire 10-year term\u8221\'20\'1D, Zelenskiy said.\par \par \uc2 enltrJapan\u8217\'20\'19s Prime Minister \uc2 Fumio Kishida{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/kishida230?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @kishida230}}}\uc2  and I have just signed a security agreement between Ukraine and Japan. A unique document with one of the world\u8217\'20\'19s most economically and technologically advanced countries. ????????\par \par \uc2 In 2024, Japan will provide Ukraine with $4.5 billion\u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Volodymyr Zelenskyy\uc2  / ????????? ?????????? (@ZelenskyyUa) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ZelenskyyUa/status/1801268384182526460?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 13, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.08pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.47pm BST\par \par \uc2 Patrick Wintour, the \uc2 Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s diplomatic editor, is in Puglia\par \par \uc2 Britain has been urged to lead in persuading their fellow \uc2 G7\uc2  leaders to insert some badly needed reality into the search for a two state solution by providing funding to rescue the process of civilian society reconciliation in Israel and Palestine.\par \par \uc2 Britain has been seen as the country most likely to push an agenda that is seen as critical if support for a two state solution is not to erode in both communities. The call, originally tabled by the Alliance for Middle East Peace (Allmep) has been backed by \uc2 Pope Francis\uc2  and more than 360 NGOs. The Pope is due to attend the \uc2 G7\uc2  summit on Friday.\par \par \uc2 G7\uc2  leaders on Wednesday discussed the Middle East for over two hours in the company of Jordanian leaders, but neither the Emirati leader Mohammed bin Zayed or the Saudi Crown Prince \uc2 Mohammed bin Salman\uc2  in the end joined.\par \par \uc2 The meeting was held against the backdrop of Israeli-\uc2 Hamas\uc2  peace talks hanging by a thread and a dangerous upsurge in violence in northern Israel caused by what \uc2 Hezbollah\uc2  described as its largest attack on Israel since the conflict broke out in October.\par \par \uc2 There has been no mention of the Palestinian conflict in four of the last five \uc2 G7\uc2  communiques, even though there has been references in all previous communiques from 2000 to 2017. The current commmunique is certain to back the latest peace plan outlined by the US President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , and will place the onus on \uc2 Hamas\uc2  to accept the deal.\par \par \uc2 Allmep\u8217\'20\'19s executive director John Lyndon said \u8220\'20\'1CIf a renewed diplomatic process is to succeed where all its predecessors have failed, then it must be very different to what has come before. Civil society must be put at the core of any strategy, rather than at the margins \u8211\'20\'13 as an afterthought or absent altogether. The requirement now is that the \uc2 G7\uc2  communique highlights the role of civil society, or else there is no realistic path to peace.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.38pm BST\par \par \uc2 Here is an indication of some of the security precautions being taken in Brindisi where \uc2 G7\uc2  leaders are scheduled to have dinner with Italy\u8217\'20\'19s president tonight.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.34pm BST\par \par \uc2 The social media account of India\u8217\'20\'19s prime minister \uc2 Narendra Modi\uc2  has shown him departing to head to the \uc2 G7\uc2  summit.\par \par \uc2 enltrPM {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/narendramodi?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @narendramodi}}}\uc2  emplanes for Italy, where he will attend the G7 Summit. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/JnWcQzfY7R"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/JnWcQzfY7R}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 narendramodi_in (@narendramodi_in) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/narendramodi_in/status/1801252923256775120?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 13, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.57pm BST\par \par \uc2 Russia: 'painful' response for EU if it uses frozen Russian assets to fund Ukraine\par \par \uc2 Russian foreign ministry\uc2  spokesperson \uc2 Maria Zakharova\uc2  said on Thursday that attempts by the west to take the income from frozen Russian assets was criminal and would lead to a response from Moscow that would be very painful for the \uc2 European Union\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Earlier Reuters reported that a senior US official had told it the \uc2 G7\uc2  has reached agreement on using frozen Russian assets to fund a $50bn loan to Ukraine to support budget, military, reconstruction, humanitarian purposes.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 Draft G7 communique to support US Gaza ceasefire plan and express concern about conflict bordering Israel and Lebanon\par \par \uc2 G7\uc2  leaders are very concerned by the situation in northern Israel and southern Lebanon, and endorse US efforts to secure a ceasefire in the Gaza Strip, according to a draft communique due to be released after this week\u8217\'20\'19s G7 summit.\par \par \uc2 Reuters reports the statement is expected to add that western leaders reiterate their commitment to a two-state solution for Israelis and Palestinians to live in peace, side-by-side.\par \par \uc2 In addition, they are expected called on Israel to refrain from a full-scale offensive in Rafah, \u8220\'20\'1Cin line with their obligations under international law\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Israel and anti-Israeli forces including \uc2 Hezbollah\uc2  have exchanged near constant fire across the \uc2 UN\uc2 -drawn blue line that separates Israel and Lebanon. Tens of thousands of people in southern Lebanon and northern Israel have been displaced from their homes\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.37pm BST\par \par \uc2 G7\uc2  reaches agreement on $50bn loan to Ukraine using frozen Russian assets \u8211\'20\'13 reports\par \par \uc2 Reuters reports a senior US official has told it the \uc2 G7\uc2  has reached agreement on using frozen Russian assets to fund a $50bn loan to support budget, military, reconstruction, humanitarian purposes.\par \par \uc2 More details soon \u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.17pm BST\par \par \uc2 Russian foreign ministry\uc2  spokesperson \uc2 Maria Zakharova\uc2  said on Thursday that the West was escalating the conflict in Ukraine by encouraging Kyiv to strike deep into Russia.\par \par \uc2 In a message posted to her Telegram channel, Zakharova said:\par \par \uc2 Do the EU countries understand that Washington is dragging them into a direct clash with Russia under the Nato flag? The hysterical pumping of the western public with the thesis about Russia\u8217\'20\'19s supposed \u8220\'20\'1Cimminent aggression against western countries\u8221\'20\'1D means only one thing \u8211\'20\'13 the Biden administration needs even more bloodletting on the European continent to keep both its own government and the American economy from collapsing.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.06pm BST\par \par \uc2 Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s president \uc2 Volodymr Zelenskiy\uc2  has arrived at the \uc2 G7\uc2  summit and has been greeted by Italy\u8217\'20\'19s prime minister \uc2 Giorgia Meloni\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 Russian diplomats and their families should be denied free movement rights around the \uc2 EU\uc2  to protect the bloc against propaganda and sabotage, eight foreign ministers have written.\par \par \uc2 In a letter to the \uc2 EU\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s high representative for foreign policy, \uc2 Josep Borrell\uc2 , foreign ministers from eight \uc2 EU\uc2  member states call for an end to free movement rights for Russian diplomats, saying it makes \u8220\'20\'1Cmalign activities\u8221\'20\'1D easier.\par \par \uc2 The letter states:\par \par \uc2 Intelligence, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/article/2024/may/18/disappearing-ink-fake-polls-and-voter-eu-fears-as-russian-propaganda-ads-target-euro-elections"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 propaganda}}}\uc2  or {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/article/2024/may/30/europe-on-high-alert-after-suspected-moscow-linked-arson-and-sabotage"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  even preparation of sabotage acts }}}\uc2  are the main workload for a large number of Russian \u8220\'20\'1Cdiplomats\u8221\'20\'1D in the EU. A huge blow to Russian intelligence presence done through {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/apr/05/eu-allies-expel-over-120-russian-diplomats-in-two-days-after-bucha-killings"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a wave of expulsions }}}\uc2  in recent years was crucial. However, the threat persists as the continuation of the need to expel Russian embassy staff from various EU countries demonstrates.\par \par \uc2 Russian diplomats and their families, instead, should be restricted to the state of their accreditation, the ministers say, adding:\par \par \uc2 This measure will significantly narrow operational space for Russian agents.\par \par \uc2 The letter has been signed by the foreign ministers of the Baltic States, the Czech Republic, Poland, Romania, the Netherlands and Denmark.\par \par \uc2 The signatories argue the restriction would not violate the Vienna convention on diplomatic relations, arguing that free movement \u8220\'20\'1Cis not a diplomatic privilege but a collateral benefit\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The Schengen area covers most \uc2 EU\uc2  member states, plus Iceland, Norway, Liechtenstein and Switzerland.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.46pm BST\par \par \uc2 Away from the \uc2 G7\uc2  summit, Germany and Denmark have signed a letter of intent to strengthen their military cooperation in the face of what they perceive as an increasing Russian hostility.\par \par \uc2 Denmark is supporting Germany\u8217\'20\'19s initiative to supply Ukraine with air defences with \u8364\'20\'AC125m (\u163\'00\'A3105m/$135m), Reuters reports.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.46pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.39pm BST\par \par \uc2 UK announces new Russia sanctions targeting Putin's 'shadow fleet'\par \par \uc2 The UK has announced it will target ships in \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s shadow fleet with new sanctions to support Ukraine as part of co-ordinated action with \uc2 G7\uc2  partners.\par \par \uc2 Rishi Sunak\uc2  has also announced another \u163\'00\'A3242m in bilateral funding for Ukraine as he meets his counterparts from Italy, Canada, France, Germany, Japan and the United States at the \uc2 G7\uc2  summit in Puglia.\par \par \uc2 The 50 new sanctions are the UK\u8217\'20\'19s first to target vessels in Putin\u8217\'20\'19s shadow fleet, which Russia uses to circumvent UK and \uc2 G7\uc2  sanctions to trade in Russian oil, PA Media reports Downing Street as saying.\par \par \uc2 Suppliers of munitions, machine tools and logistics based in China, Israel, Kyrgyzstan and Turkey that support Russia\u8217\'20\'19s military production are also among those sanctioned, Downing Street said.\par \par \uc2 The sanctions also take aim at the Moscow Stock Exchange and other institutions at the heart of Russia\u8217\'20\'19s financial system. The US designated the Moscow Stock Exchange on 12 June.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe UK will always stand shoulder to shoulder with Ukraine in its fight for freedom,\u8221\'20\'1D said Sunak. \u8220\'20\'1CToday we are once more ramping up economic pressure through sanctions to bear down on Russia\u8217\'20\'19s ability to fund its war machine. Putin must lose, and cutting off his ability to fund a prolonged conflict is absolutely vital.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Sunak has also committed to providing \u163\'00\'A3242m to Ukraine for the immediate humanitarian, energy and stabilisation needs and to lay the foundations for longer term economic and social recovery and reconstruction.\par \par \uc2 He and other \uc2 G7\uc2  leaders are also seeking to agree on a mechanism that will allow profits stemming from immobilised Russian sovereign assets to be used to support Ukraine. Some $285bn (\u163\'00\'A3222bn) worth of immobilised Russian assets are held in \uc2 G7\uc2  jurisdictions.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.42pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.15pm BST\par \par \uc2 Kate Connolly reports for the Guardian from Berlin\par \par \uc2 Ahead of the \uc2 G7\uc2  summit, Kyiv mayor \uc2 Vitali Klitschko\uc2  expressed his hope that the result of the European elections on Sunday, in which parties which oppose military support for Ukraine and back a friendlier approach towards Moscow gained ground, would not undermine the effort to aid his country.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C The risk is there, and life is divided,\u8221\'20\'1D he told the Guardian after addressing the Ukraine Recovery Conference in Berlin. \u8220\'20\'1CRight now the world is black and white for many people \u8211\'20\'13 right now you are either for the war or against the war. Right now you are for democracy or for authoritarianism. Which is all the more reason why we have to defend our values, our democratic values, fight for our mission,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 The former heavyweight boxing champion who has been mayor of the Ukrainian capital since 2014, said the fight for Ukraine was integral to the fight for democracy.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C We have to save the future of democratic Europe. Ukraine is an important part of Europe, even as Putin says: no, it\u8217\'20\'19s part of the Russian Empire, that\u8217\'20\'19s why our fight is also a European fight, a fight for European values, and the success of Ukraine will be a success for all of Europe.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Klitschko, surrounded by many Ukrainians and other participants seeking a selfie with him, after holding a discussion with other mayors from across Europe, said the desire for peace harboured by Ukrainians was no different to the desire expressed by many who went to the polls calling for an end to the war.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C The next task for the European parliament has to be to bring peace back to Europe, which is the main wish not just in Ukraine, but everywhere in Europe,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 His wish for the \uc2 G7\uc2  summit and this weekend\u8217\'20\'19s international peace summit \u8220\'20\'1CPeace in Ukraine\u8221\'20\'1D in B\u252\'00\'FCrgenstock, Switzerland, was for \u8220\'20\'1Ca more proactive position to be taken by many countries, and unity in their approach on Ukraine, because this is the key to peace and freedom.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He said the reconstruction and recovery of Ukraine, which had been the focus of the Berlin conference, were \u8220\'20\'1Cimportant questions,\u8221\'20\'1D but added: \u8220\'20\'1Chowever, my main priority right now is to stop the war.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C We need political support, we need military support, we need to save our country\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Klitschko also expressed his disdain towards members of the far-right populist AfD party and MPs from the far-left bloc of \uc2 Sahra Wagenknecht\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s BSW, who boycotted a speech to the Bundestag by Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s president \uc2 Volodymyr Zelenskiy\uc2  earlier this week, calling him a \u8220\'20\'1Cwar president\u8221\'20\'1D who was unwilling to negotiate peace. \u8220\'20\'1CIt is a slur against all Ukrainians that they deliberately kept their distance,\u8221\'20\'1D Klitschko said.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.59pm BST\par \par \uc2 Meloni: \uc2 G7\uc2  summit to bring 'concrete and measurable results' on Ukraine, Middle East, AI and migration\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 G7\uc2  has issued a video clip of \uc2 Giorgia Meloni\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s opening address, in which she said she believed that the next two days would bring \u8220\'20\'1Cconcrete and measurable results\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 She told the other \uc2 G7\uc2  leaders \u8220\'20\'1CThe \uc2 G7\uc2  is not a self-enclosed fortress, which needs to defend itself against others. It is a container of values, and we want to open to the world in order to have shared development and growth as our goal.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Highlighting what is on the agenda for the summit, Meloni said:\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19re talking about the current crises, Ukraine and Middle East, and we\u8217\'20\'19ll also build on what the Japanese presidency did in order to guarantee that we have solid supplies.\par \par \uc2 Responding also to one of the major challenges of our times, generative AI and clearly the need to make use of its opportunities and governance risks. And also give greater attention to the Indo-Pacific region.\par \par \uc2 The Italian presidency also decided to give special attention to another continent which is fundamental to the future, which is Africa with its opportunities. And this requires a different approach than we\u8217\'20\'19ve shown in the past. Often, Africa is linked to another issue \u8211\'20\'13 not just Africa \u8211\'20\'13 which is the issue of migration and the worrying dimension of smuggling and trafficking organisations.\par \par \uc2 enltrPresident \uc2 Giorgia Meloni\uc2 's opening remarks during the first session of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/G7?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #G7}}}\uc2  Summit in Borgo Egnazia. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/G7Italy?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #G7Italy}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/XD5I0Y5dZ2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/XD5I0Y5dZ2}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 G7 Italy (@G7) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/G7/status/1801214226305802723?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 13, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.46pm BST\par \par \uc2 Countries supporting Ukraine must speed up their decision making, outgoing Dutch prime minister \uc2 Mark Rutte\uc2  said on Thursday, Reuters reports.\par \par \uc2 Rutte, a leading candidate to become \uc2 Nato\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s next secretary general, was speaking at a conference in Finland.\par \par \uc2 Earlier, Finnish president Alexander Stubb told a press conference Rutte will likely become \uc2 Nato\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s next secretary general. Last year the current secretary general, \uc2 Jens Stoltenberg\uc2 , was persuaded to extend his term until October 2024 due to ongoing impact of the war in Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 We mentioned earlier that while she was left waiting for US president \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  to arrive, Italy\u8217\'20\'19s prime minister \uc2 Giorgia Meloni\uc2  took a selfie of herself showing the press pack who were watching the arrivals of the \uc2 G7\uc2  leaders. The selfie has just appeared on the news wires.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.19pm BST\par \par \uc2 Ursula von der Leyen\uc2 , president of the \uc2 European Commission\uc2 , has said this week\u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 G7\uc2  is about showing unity. She said in a message posted to social media:\par \par \uc2 In turbulent times the strongest message we can send is unity. Today the \uc2 G7\uc2  in Bari will show unity. Unity for Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s freedom. We work on further financial support. Unity for a peaceful and stable Middle East and the three-phase plan. Unity on a free and open Indo-Pacific.\par \par \uc2 enltrIn turbulent times the strongest message we can send is unity.\par \par \uc2 Today the \uc2 G7\uc2  in Bari will show unity.\par \par \uc2 Unity for Ukraine's freedom. We work on further financial support.\par \par \uc2 Unity for a peaceful and stable Middle East and the three-phase plan.\par \par \uc2 Unity on a free and open Indo-Pacific. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/vCszrXfC3F"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/vCszrXfC3F}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Ursula von der Leyen\uc2  (@vonderleyen) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/vonderleyen/status/1801203138239529271?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 13, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.17pm BST\par \par \uc2 Kate Connolly reports for the Guardian from Berlin\par \par \uc2 The Ukraine Recovery Conference has just concluded in Berlin, where the main focus was on how to raise money for short and long-term reconstruction, even as the country remains under vicious attack, with many participants acknowledging that \u8220\'20\'1CUkraine Resilience\u8221\'20\'1D would right now be a more fitting title. On the sidelines, Tymur Pistriuha, head of the NGO Ukrainian Deminers Association, spoke to the Guardian about the urgent, ongoing need to put de-mining at the centre of any talk of recovery.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAs our deputy prime minister (and minister of economic development and trade) \uc2 Yulia Svyrydenko\uc2  has pointed out, without humanitarian de-mining, so-called mine action, recovery cannot happen. It\u8217\'20\'19s good that this is understood, but it has not been as prominent on the agenda here in Berlin as much as in the past, and it\u8217\'20\'19s the absolute starting point for any recovery and reconstruction. We need to scale up,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 At the previous recovery conference in London last year the issue was more widely discussed, Pistriuha said. Currently 144,000 square kilometres of Ukrainian territory counts as potentially dangerous due to landmines and unexploded ordnance (UXO), and requires urgent intervention.\par \par \uc2 The speed with which this is happening has improved over time. Pistriuha pointed out that around six months ago the affected area was 174,000 square kilometres. \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19ve already released 30,000 square kilometres,\u8221\'20\'1D he said \u8211\'20\'13 referring to the term according to which land is deemed safe, after being inspected and cleared of UXO \u8211\'20\'13 \u8220\'20\'1Cwhich is like the size of the territory of Albania.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s tremendous, but the scale of the problem is still huge.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The day to day impact of this he said, is measured by the \u8220\'20\'1Ccrucial statistic\u8221\'20\'1D of human victims. Officially, there have been around 1000 victims \u8211\'20\'13 both killings and injuries \u8211\'20\'13 from mine and explosive ordnance, since the start of the full-blown invasion in 2022. But according to the Ukrainian Demining Association\u8217\'20\'19s own database, the real figure is far higher, at about 2,500, due to underreporting, and a lack of access to some areas.\par \par \uc2 The problem greatly affects everything from Ukrainian agriculture to critical infrastructure, spanning \u8220\'20\'1Ceverything from the energy sector to the forest to underwater areas,\u8221\'20\'1D Pistriuha said.\par \par \uc2 He recently took part in a mine action symposium in Croatia \u8211\'20\'13 itself still affected by landmines and explosive remnants of war as a legacy of the conflict there in the early 90s \u8211\'20\'13 and in October a donor conference to raise funds for demining activities in Ukraine will take place in Lausanne. \u8220\'20\'1CSo it is on the agenda,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 One of the most crucial strands of his association\u8217\'20\'19s work is explosive ordnance risk education. \u8220\'20\'1CI have 60 mobile teams travelling throughout Ukraine to provide face to face instruction sessions. But Ukraine is a huge country and it\u8217\'20\'19s not enough.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.41am BST\par \par \uc2 Georgia Meloni \u8217\'20\'19s social media account has posted to reiterate that the location of the \uc2 G7\uc2  summit, Puglia, was a deliberate choice. She said:\par \par \uc2 We did it because Puglia is a region of southern Italy and the message we want to give is of a \uc2 G7\uc2  who under the Italian presidency wants strengthen its dialogue with the nations of the global south.\par \par \uc2 We did it because this land is historically a bridge between West and East, it is a land of dialogue at the centre of the Mediterranean, of that middle sea that connects the two great maritime spaces of the globe, the Atlantic and the Indo-Pacific.\par \par \uc2 itltrL'Italia ha scelto di ospitare il summit dei leader in Puglia, non \u232\'00\'E8 stata una scelta casuale: lo abbiamo fatto perch\u233\'00\'E9 la Puglia \u232\'00\'E8 una regione del Sud Italia e il messaggio che vogliamo dare \u232\'00\'E8 di un {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/G7?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #G7}}}\uc2  che sotto presidenza italiana vuole rafforzare il suo dialogo con le Nazioni\u8230\'20\'26 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/YaAD6sV1iP"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/YaAD6sV1iP}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Giorgia Meloni\uc2  (@GiorgiaMeloni) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/GiorgiaMeloni/status/1801201948273594696?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 13, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.32am BST\par \par \uc2 Italy accused of scrapping safe \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  guarantee from \uc2 G7\uc2  declaration\par \par \uc2 Angela Giuffrida in Rome and Ashifa Kassamin Madrid report for the Guardian\par \par \uc2 Giorgia Meloni\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s government has been accused of scrapping a reference guaranteeing access to \u8220\'20\'1Csafe and legal\u8221\'20\'1D abortions in the text of the \uc2 G7\uc2  summit\u8217\'20\'19s final declaration.\par \par \uc2 Citing sources from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/g7"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 G7}}}\uc2  member delegations, the Italian media reported on Thursday that a sidebar clause on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights had been left out of a last draft of the final declaration circulated on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 The clause, pushed especially by France and Canada, had been intended to reinforce an agreement by the \uc2 G7\uc2  members in Japan last year that they would guarantee \u8220\'20\'1Ceffective and safe access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 It also committed to sexual and reproductive health rights for all, \u8220\'20\'1Cincluding by addressing access to safe and legal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and post-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Sources in Meloni\u8217\'20\'19s office denied the reference had been removed, telling Ansa news agency the declaration was still being negotiated and that \u8220\'20\'1Ceverything that will be included in the final document will be final points resulting from the negotiations\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Antonio Tajani\uc2 , the deputy prime minister, told Sky TG24: \u8220\'20\'1CThe various delegations are in talks, and it is premature to make an analysis and useless to make predictions. We will see what the agreement will be.\u8221\'20\'1D He emphasised that while \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  would be discussed at the \uc2 G7\uc2 , Ukraine and the Middle East were priorities.\par \par \uc2 A source close to the negotiations told AFP that since 2021 there had \u8220\'20\'1Cbeen a mention of \u8216\'20\'18safe access\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D, but \u8220\'20\'1CMeloni doesn\u8217\'20\'19t want it\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Read more of Angela Giuffrida and Ashifa Kassam\u8217\'20\'19s report here: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/article/2024/jun/13/giorgia-meloni-italy-accused-of-scrapping-safe-abortion-guarantee-from-g7-declaration"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Italy accused of scrapping safe \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  guarantee from G7 declaration}}}\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/article/2024/jun/13/giorgia-meloni-italy-accused-of-scrapping-safe-abortion-guarantee-from-g7-declaration"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Italy accused of scrapping safe \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  guarantee from G7 declaration}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.30am BST\par \par \uc2 Here are some more images issued from inside the room where the \uc2 G7\uc2  summit meeting is taking place.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.24am BST\par \par \uc2 Patrick Wintour is in Puglia for the \uc2 Guardian\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and \uc2 Volodymyr Zelenskiy\uc2  will sign a 10 year bilateral security agreement on behalf of their two countries at the \uc2 G7\uc2  summit as arguments continued on the sidelines about how the West is to deliver on its plan to provide a Trump-proof $50bn loan to the Ukrainian government.\par \par \uc2 The bilateral security agreement is the 16th such bilateral security agreements that Ukraine has signed, and will help to speed the modernisation of the Ukrainian army. Ukraine had hoped for more than two years that the US would be the first to sign, but in the end the talks took more than a year, and the US is now the last of the \uc2 G7\uc2  countries along with Japan to sign.\par \par \uc2 The agreement is not a treaty that requires the authorisation of Congress and could be undone by a future Trump administration. Biden has previously said the gauarantees for Ukraine are equivalent to those enjoyed by Israel, so covering financial and military assistance, as well as the possibility of the joint production of weapons\par \par \uc2 The two leaders will to stage a press conference to hail the agreement where differences over a timetable for Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s bid to join \uc2 Nato\uc2 , and the introduction of foreign military trainers inside Ukraine are likely to be on view. The bilateral agreements have also been viewed Ukraine as a stopgap before joining \uc2 Nato\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.29am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.48am BST\par \par \uc2 Here are some pictures of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s arrival at the \uc2 G7\uc2 , and an image that has been issued from the room where the leaders are having discussion.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.41am BST\par \par \uc2 White House national security adviser Jake Sullivan has been speaking to the media at the sidelines of the \uc2 G7\uc2  summit, Reuters reports, and he said that during discussions today \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will encourage other nations to support ceasefire negotiations trying to end fighting in Gaza.\par \par \uc2 Sullivan said \uc2 Hamas\uc2  had submitted an amended proposal with some minor changes that could be worked out, as well as others that were not in line with what Biden had laid out or that had been embraced by the \uc2 UN\uc2  security council.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COur goal is to figure out how we bridge the remaining gaps and get to a deal,\u8221\'20\'1D he said, adding that discussions would continue with Qatar and Egypt, who, in turn, would work with \uc2 Hamas\uc2  to reach agreement as quickly as possible.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.37am BST\par \par \uc2 Here is the group shot from the \uc2 G7\uc2  summit, from left-right: \uc2 Charles Michel\uc2 , \uc2 Olaf Scholz\uc2 , \uc2 Justin Trudeau\uc2 , \uc2 Emmanuel Macron\uc2 , \uc2 Giorgia Meloni\uc2 , \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , \uc2 Fumio Kishida\uc2 , \uc2 Rishi Sunak\uc2  and \uc2 Ursula von der Leyen\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.31am BST\par \par \uc2 In the group photo lineup Meloni is flanked by Macron and Biden. The attendees have now gone indoors.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.29am BST\par \par \uc2 After a short delay, US president \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has arrived at the \uc2 G7\uc2  summit. While she was waiting for him, at one point Italy\u8217\'20\'19s prime minister \uc2 Giorgia Meloni\uc2  posed for her own selfie in front of the media. The \uc2 G7\uc2  leaders are now gathering for a group photo.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.12am BST\par \par \uc2 Japan\u8217\'20\'19s prime minister \uc2 Fumio Kishida\uc2 , Canada\u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 Justin Trudeau\uc2  and French president \uc2 Emmanuel Macron\uc2  have all arrived, and the news wires are beginning to carry pictures of the leaders being greeted by \uc2 Giorgia Meloni\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.54am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.04am BST\par \par \uc2 As the leaders began to gather at the \uc2 G7\uc2  summit, Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s president \uc2 Volodymyr Zelenskiy\uc2  has issued a lengthy message on social media ahead of today\u8217\'20\'19s discussions. In it, he said:\par \par \uc2 For us, the main issues are developing fighter jet coalition, expediting pilot training, and accelerating aircraft delivery. Development of the Ukrainian air defense system based on the most powerful western systems, as well as an increase in long-range capability.\par \par \uc2 Bilateral security agreements will be signed during meetings with US President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and Japanese prime minister \uc2 Fumio Kishida\uc2 . The document with the United States will be unprecedented, as it should be for leaders who support Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 The entire Ukrainian people, including our warriors, see that the \uc2 G7\uc2  will always support Ukraine. I am grateful to our partners for their belief in us and our victory.\par \par \uc2 enltrToday is the G7 Summit in Italy, a meeting of our closest partners. Much of it will be dedicated to Ukraine, our defense, and economic resilience. And we look forward to important decisions today.\par \par \uc2 For us, the main issues are developing fighter jet coalition, expediting pilot\u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Volodymyr Zelenskyy\uc2  / ????????? ?????????? (@ZelenskyyUa) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ZelenskyyUa/status/1801175795223626079?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 13, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.01am BST\par \par \uc2 The first arrivals have been \uc2 Ursula von der Leyen\uc2  and \uc2 Charles Michel\uc2  representing the \uc2 European Union\uc2 , prime minister \uc2 Rishi Sunak\uc2  of the UK, and \uc2 Olaf Scholz\uc2 , chancellor of Germany.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.47am BST\par \par \uc2 Here is a picture of \uc2 Giorgia Meloni\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s arrival at the \uc2 G7\uc2  summit.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.46am BST\par \par \uc2 While we wait for other \uc2 G7\uc2  leaders to arrive, Reuters is carrying a quick snap that Ukraine and Japan are expected to sign a security agreement later today. At the same time Reuters reports Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s foreign minister \uc2 Dmytro Kuleba\uc2  said on Thursday he welcomed a sweeping new set of US sanctions imposed on Russia and praised the measures taken against its defence industrial base.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.44am BST\par \par \uc2 Italy\u8217\'20\'19s prime minister \uc2 Giorgia Meloni\uc2  has just arrived at the venue.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.29am BST\par \par \uc2 This is the scene at the Borgo Egnazia resort as \uc2 G7\uc2  leaders are scheduled to begin arriving.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.14am BST\par \par \uc2 Patrick Wintour is in Puglia for the Guardian, and overnight he had this curtain raiser\par \par \uc2 A dramatic expansion of entities exposed to US sanctions for helping the Russian economy and an EU-led $50bn loan to ease the financial burden on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/ukraine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ukraine}}}\uc2  will be at the centre of discussions at a summit of the leaders of wealthy \uc2 G7\uc2  nations in Puglia, Italy, starting on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 The leaders, facing unprecedented challenges from discontented electorates, will be under heightened pressure to provide concrete results as their three days of discussion range across an interlinked agenda encompassing the war in Ukraine, migration, Africa, the Middle East, the climate crisis and harnessing artificial intelligence (AI).\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 G7\uc2  was once a cloistering of western leaders in informal conversation, but host countries can invite outside guests to join some of the sessions. Italy has thrown open the doors and will welcome \uc2 Pope Francis\uc2 ; \uc2 Javier Milei\uc2 , the populist president of Argentina; \uc2 Narendra Modi\uc2 , the Indian prime minister; and \uc2 Luiz In\u225\'00\'E1cio Lula da Silva\uc2 , the Brazilian president. Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s president, \uc2 Volodymyr Zelenskiy\uc2 , will stage a joint press conference with the US president, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 . The aim is to show the west remains determined to confront Russia\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Carsenal of autocracy\u8221\'20\'1D, but is not preoccupied with its own problems.\par \par \uc2 The meeting is also billed by the US state department as the best opportunity to ease Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s financial burdens before the US\u8217\'20\'19s presidential elections in November and send a message to Russia of western stamina. As much as feasible the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/g7"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 G7}}}\uc2  would like its decisions to be Trump-proof.\par \par \uc2 Read more of Patrick Wintour\u8217\'20\'19s article here: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/article/2024/jun/12/g7-countries-head-to-italy-for-summit-as-ukraine-and-russia-top-the-agenda"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 G7 leaders head to Italy for summit as Ukraine and Russia top the agenda}}}\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/article/2024/jun/12/g7-countries-head-to-italy-for-summit-as-ukraine-and-russia-top-the-agenda"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 G7 leaders head to Italy for summit as Ukraine and Russia top the agenda}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.03am BST\par \par \uc2 As well as the \uc2 G7\uc2  summit in Italy today, there is also a high profile meeting of the Ukraine Defense Contact Group, hosted by the US at \uc2 Nato\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Headquarters in Brussels.\par \par \uc2 Going into the event secretary general \uc2 Jens Stoltenberg\uc2  said members are set to take tougher action against Russian spies across the alliance in response to a campaign of hostile activities by Moscow that includes acts of sabotage and cyberattacks.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe have seen several examples of sabotage, of arson attempts, of cyber attacks, of disinformation,\u8221\'20\'1D he told reporters, adding \uc2 Nato\uc2  defence ministers meeting in Brussels later in the day would \u8220\'20\'1Caddress the Russian campaign of hostile activities.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.48am BST\par \par \uc2 Good progress has been made on international efforts to unlock the value of frozen Russian assets to help fund Ukraine, Reuters reports US national security adviser Jake Sullivan said on Thursday, adding he hoped for agreement by the time \uc2 G7\uc2  leaders meet.\par \par \uc2 He said \uc2 G7\uc2  leaders were more unified than ever on major issues, including Chinese industrial overcapacity\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.28am BST\par \par \uc2 Overnight Angela Giuffrida in Rome teed up the event for us with a look at what it means for \uc2 Giorgia Meloni\uc2 :\par \par \uc2 When {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/giorgia-meloni"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Giorgia Meloni}}}\uc2  met \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  at the White House in March, he played Ray Charles\u8217\'20\'19s Georgia on My Mind as she entered the room. \u8220\'20\'1CWe have each other\u8217\'20\'19s backs,\u8221\'20\'1D he later told reporters, before planting a tender kiss on her forehead as the meeting wrapped up.\par \par \uc2 The cosy get-together was the clearest sign yet that the Italian prime minister, a chameleon of a communicator, had been able to cultivate warm relations with the US president, who had previously expressed concerns about her Brothers of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/italy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Italy}}}\uc2  party\u8217\'20\'19s neofascist history.\par \par \uc2 As {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/europe-news"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Europe}}}\uc2  reels from the far-right\u8217\'20\'19s advances in the European parliamentary elections, the pair will reunite among the olive trees of a secluded resort in the southern Italian region of Puglia on Thursday, when Italy hosts the \uc2 G7\uc2  summit. It is an event Meloni intends to use to burnish her image on the international scene, even as her government draws criticism at home for its hardline approach on numerous issues.\par \par \uc2 Read more of Angela Giuffrida\u8217\'20\'19s piece here: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/article/2024/jun/12/all-eyes-are-on-her-italys-far-right-chameleon-giorgia-meloni-prepares-to-host-the-g7"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18All eyes are on her\u8217\'20\'19: Italy\u8217\'20\'19s far-right chameleon, Giorgia Meloni, prepares to host the G7}}}\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/article/2024/jun/12/all-eyes-are-on-her-italys-far-right-chameleon-giorgia-meloni-prepares-to-host-the-g7"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18All eyes are on her\u8217\'20\'19: Italy\u8217\'20\'19s far-right chameleon, Giorgia Meloni, prepares to host the G7}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.16am BST\par \par \uc2 Giorgia Meloni\uc2 , Italy\u8217\'20\'19s prime minister, set out the countries aims for their year holding the presidency of the \uc2 G7\uc2  and hosting the summit in a promo video.\par \par \uc2 In it she said the \uc2 G7\uc2  had \u8220\'20\'1Ctaken on an irreplaceable role in defending freedom and democracy and managing global challenges.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 She continued:\par \par \uc2 Italy has taken on this historic responsibility at a particularly complex time. Russia\u8217\'20\'19s war of aggression against Ukraine has challenged the international system based on the rule of law. And the violation of those principles holding the international community together is triggering hotbeds of conflict in various parts of the world.\par \par \uc2 We will return reiterate our support for Ukraine and we will continue to work towards an end to a war and to achieve a just and lasting peace. We will also address the conflict in the Middle East, and other crisis on the agenda over the course of the year.\par \par \uc2 We will focus on relations with developing nations and emerging economies, paying particular attention to Africa. We have set ourselves the goal of building an equal cooperation model that rejects a predatory approach and is able to offer benefits for all. That is also why we will be paying great attention to migration issues, the climate-energy nexus and food security.\par \par \uc2 The Italian presidency will also focus on a challenge that many consider to be the most decisive of our time: artificial intelligence. This technology can create great opportunities, but also huge risks and affect global balances. We are committed to developing governance mechanisms and ensuring that artificial intelligence is both human centred and human controlled.\par \par \uc2 Gioria Meloni G7 promo video.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.12am BST\par \par \uc2 Here is a glimpse at the press centre that has been set up for the \uc2 G7\uc2  summit in Bari.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.04am BST\par \par \uc2 What's happening today?\par \par \uc2 The agenda for today\u8217\'20\'19s summit features Italy\u8217\'20\'19s president of the council of ministers \uc2 Giorgia Meloni\uc2  greeting delegation leaders from 10.30am local time (9.30am BST / 4.30am EDT). There will then be the traditional opening family photo of the delegation leaders.\par \par \uc2 The discussion sessions set for today are about:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Africa, climate change and development\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Middle East (with working lunch)\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Ukraine (\uc2 G7\uc2  + Ukraine format)\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Ukraine (\uc2 G7\uc2  format)\par \par \uc2 There will also be an evening flag ceremony and photo opportunity.\par \par \uc2 Tomorrow\u8217\'20\'19s sessions include discussion on migration, AI, energy, and the Indo-Pacific and economic security.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.02am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.00am BST\par \par \uc2 Welcome and opening summary\par \par \uc2 It is 9am in Borgo Egnazia in the Puglia region, Italy\u8217\'20\'19s south. Welcome to our live coverage of this year\u8217\'20\'19s G7 summit. I am Martin Belam and I\u8217\'20\'19ll be with you for the next while.\par \par \uc2 G7\uc2  leaders are gathering for the first day the summit, hosted by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/article/2024/jun/12/all-eyes-are-on-her-italys-far-right-chameleon-giorgia-meloni-prepares-to-host-the-g7"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Italy\u8217\'20\'19s prime minister, Giorgia Meloni}}}\uc2 , and are seeking to seal a deal on using frozen Russian assets to help war-torn Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 Ukrainian President \uc2 Volodymyr Zelenskiy\uc2  will join US President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and leaders from Italy, Britain, France, Germany, Canada and Japan at the luxury Borgo Egnazia resort in Puglia.\par \par \uc2 The leaders are hoping to agree on a $50bn loan for Kyiv, secured against the future profits from interest on 300bn euros ($325bn) of \uc2 Russian central bank\uc2  assets frozen after the February 2022 invasion, reports Agence France-Presse.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 European Union\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 where most of the funds are being held \u8211\'20\'13 agreed earlier this year to use the profits for Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 But the idea at the \uc2 G7\uc2  is to use this to provide more, faster help in the form of a massive upfront loan \u8211\'20\'13 although key questions such as who issues the debt and who shares the risk are still being hammered out.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 G7\uc2  summit opens Thursday morning with a short session on Africa, development and climate change, before turning to the Middle East.\par \par \uc2 The leaders have already announced their support for a Gaza truce deal outlined by Biden, which would also see the release of hostages taken in \uc2 Hamas\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s 7 October attack on Israel.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 G7\uc2  comprises the United States, Japan, Canada, Germany, France, Italy and Britain. Russia was suspended from the then-styled G8 indefinitely from 2014 after it unilaterally annexed Crimea.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 European Union\uc2  participates in all discussions and is represented by the presidents of both the European Council and the \uc2 European Commission\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The host country traditionally invites outside guests to join some of the sessions. Among those invited are \uc2 Pope Francis\uc2 , the King of Jordan as well as the leaders of Ukraine, India, Brazil, Argentina, Turkey, the United Arab Emirates, Kenya, Algeria, Tunisia and Mauritania, which holds the presidency of the \uc2 African Union\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 More on that in a moment but first, here\u8217\'20\'19s a summary of the latest developments:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A dramatic expansion of entities exposed to US sanctions for helping the Russian economy will also be {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/article/2024/jun/12/g7-countries-head-to-italy-for-summit-as-ukraine-and-russia-top-the-agenda"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 at the centre of discussions}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The meeting is being billed by the US state department as an opportunity to send a message to Russia of western stamina ; the \uc2 G7\uc2  would also like to \u8220\'20\'1CTrump-proof\u8221\'20\'1D its decisions as much as possible ahead of the US election in November.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The British prime minister \uc2 Rishi Sunak\uc2  will announce up to 242m pounds ($309.69m) in bilateral assistance to Ukraine in the \uc2 G7\uc2  summit, his office said on Wednesday, to support immediate humanitarian, energy and stabilisation needs for Ukraine. \u8220\'20\'1CWe must be decisive and creative in our efforts to support Ukraine and end Putin\u8217\'20\'19s illegal war at this critical moment,\u8221\'20\'1D Sunak said ahead of the summit.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The Saudi Crown Prince \uc2 Mohammed bin Salman\uc2  has apologised for not attending the G7 Summit in Italy according to the state news agency. Zelenskiy said on Wednesday he had held \u8220\'20\'1Cproductive and energetic\u8221\'20\'1D talks with the CrownPrince focusing on this week\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1CPeace Summit\u8221\'20\'1D in Switzerland and improving bilateral ties.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 On the first evening, the leaders will attend a dinner in their honour in the nearby city of Brindisi. The media centre is in the city of Bari, 80 km (50 miles) from the summit venue.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The Borgo Egnazia resort, where the summit is being held, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/article/2024/jun/12/all-eyes-are-on-her-italys-far-right-chameleon-giorgia-meloni-prepares-to-host-the-g7"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Angela Giuffrida writes}}}\uc2 , is frequented by celebrities such as Madonna and David Beckham: \u8220\'20\'1CWith its stone villas, replete with almond-filled baskets, and narrow, winding alleys, the resort, which opened in 2010, is modelled on an ancient Puglian village \u8230\'20\'26 However, one detail of history the brochures fail to mention is that the land on which the resort stands was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://bari.repubblica.it/cronaca/2016/08/19/news/borgo_egnazia_madonna_savelletri_aldo_melpignano-146235621/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 razed during Benito Mussolini\u8217\'20\'19s fascist rule}}}\uc2  to build an airbase.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 China will be discussed at length, reports Reuters. The leaders are likely to issue a statement expressing concern on Chinese industrial overcapacity, particularly in green energy and technology sectors such as solar panels and electric vehicles.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The US, \uc2 EU\uc2  and Japan have all voiced concern that generous subsidies from Beijing are resulting in a flood of cheap goods hitting the global market, threatening western firms, and will also look at the possibility of imposing additional measures to level the field with heavily subsidised Chinese companies.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 G7\uc2  leaders are likely to express their resolve in addressing the heavy debt burden faced by many emerging market and developing countries, says Reuters, but it is not clear what this commitment will mean in real terms.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Italy is still pushing for an accord on a global minimum tax on multinationals, even if it said last month that a deal would not be finalised by June as previously planned.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Many \uc2 G7\uc2  countries are also in political flux, reports Agence France-Presse. Everyone in Puglia is aware this could be Biden\u8217\'20\'19s last \uc2 G7\uc2  summit if he loses to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in November US elections. Britain\u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 Rishi Sunak\uc2  is tipped to be ousted in July 4 elections, while France\u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 Emmanuel Macron\uc2  and Germany\u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 Olaf Scholz\uc2  are both under pressure after gains by the far right in EU elections last weekend.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240613ek6d00108\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
