\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 ACLU\uc2  hails supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s mifepristone decision: \u8216\'20\'18This fight is far from over\u8217\'20\'19 \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Maya Yang \par \uc2 3,836 \uc2 words\par \uc2 13 June 2024\par 20:11 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 This live blog is now closed. For more on the latest supreme court decision, read our full report:\uc2 US supreme court\uc2  allows continued access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.02pm BST\par \par \uc2 Summary\par \par \uc2 It is just past 4pm in Washington DC. Here is a wrap-up of the day\u8217\'20\'19s key events:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The supreme court has rejected a bid to restrict access to the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill mifepristone. The decision overturned an appeals court ruling that would have restricted mail-order prescriptions of the common \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  drug. The nation\u8217\'20\'19s highest court arrived at the decision unanimously, in turn marking a win for reproductive rights across the country.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  released the following statement on the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s decision to uphold mifepristone: \u8220\'20\'1CToday\u8217\'20\'19s decision does not change the fact that the fight for reproductive freedom continues. It does not change the fact that the supreme court overturned Roe v Wade two years ago, and women lost a fundamental freedom. It does not change the fact that the right for a woman to get the treatment she needs is imperiled if not impossible in many states.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The American Civil Liberties Union\uc2  hailed the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s decision on mifepristone, saying: \u8220\'20\'1C The supreme court just unanimously rejected a request by anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  extremists to impose medically unnecessary restrictions on mifepristone, a safe and effective medication used in most abortions nationwide.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  visited Capitol Hill for the first time since the January 6 insurrection in 2021. Trump was invited to address House Republicans at the Capitol Hill Club and also meet with Senate Republicans at the National Republican Senatorial Committee headquarters.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Ahead of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s visit to Capitol Hill, former House speaker \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  said: \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  comes to Capitol Hill today with the same mission of dismantling our democracy. But make no mistake \u8211\'20\'13 Trump has already cemented his legacy of shame in our hallowed halls.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 That\u8217\'20\'19s it as we wrap up the blog for today. Thank you for following along.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.11pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.19pm BST\par \par \uc2 When voters are asked to sum up \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  in one word, the most popular response is \u8220\'20\'1Cold\u8221\'20\'1D, according to a survey by polling firm JL Partners.\par \par \uc2 Facing the same question with regard to Biden\u8217\'20\'19s election-challenger \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/SmithInAmerica/status/1801289408873685464"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the word \u8220\'20\'1Ccriminal\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2  comes up more than any other.\par \par \uc2 The poll also found that voters expect Trump to perform better in the first presidential debate later this month in Atlanta. Some 70% expect \u8220\'20\'1CBiden to mess up his words\u8221\'20\'1D and 49% even expect \u8220\'20\'1CBiden to forget where he is\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Responding to the findings at a panel discussion in Washington on Thursday, political consultant and pollster {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://echeloninsights.com/about/patrick-ruffini/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Patrick Ruffini}}}\uc2  said: \u8220\'20\'1CThis age issue for Biden really ties into voter perceptions of his competence and his ability to get things done.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI think why that has proven to be a such a devastating issue for him, that has really underlied the failure to message around accomplishments, is that when people look at him they don\u8217\'20\'19t see somebody who is going to [have] the ability to do a whole lot to actively change the course of events in a potential second term.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 JL Partners, using a representative sample size of 500 people and conducting fieldwork on 10 and 11 June, asked: \u8220\'20\'1CThinking about anyone alive today, who would be your dream President?\u8221\'20\'1D In the resulting word cloud, \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D loomed largest, followed by \u8220\'20\'1CObama\u8221\'20\'1D - a combination of both Barack and Michelle.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.59pm BST\par \par \uc2 Mini Timmaraju\uc2 , president and CEO of \uc2 Reproductive Freedom for All\uc2 , joined the Biden campaign press call and warned that anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  advocates would likely pursue other means to block access to mifepristone after the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s decision.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CRegardless of today\u8217\'20\'19s ruling, Trump and his allies are laying the groundwork to ban medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  nationwide,\u8221\'20\'1D Timmaraju said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey want to try and use executive power to jail doctors and patients for sending or receiving \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  medication in the mail, and they could extend that strategy to try to jail those mailing anything intended for producing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  advocates have already tried to argue that the Comstock Act, an 1873 anti-obscenity law, bans the mailing of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -related materials, and Trump could use that strategy to threaten reproductive rights across the country, Timmaraju said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe road ahead is long. The fight to restore rights will be hard,\u8221\'20\'1D she told reporters. \u8220\'20\'1CBut we know President Biden and Vice-President Harris are on our side. So that\u8217\'20\'19s why I\u8217\'20\'19m so proud to be fighting alongside them.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.08pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.43pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s campaign officials celebrated the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s ruling preserving access to the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  medication mifepristone, but they emphasized that the case was \u8220\'20\'1Conly one tactic in a broader relentless strategy to strip away access to reproductive freedom\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf Trump regains power in November, Trump\u8217\'20\'19s allies will be ready to deploy their plans to ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access nationwide without the help of Congress or the court,\u8221\'20\'1D Julie Ch\u225\'00\'E1vez Rodriguez, Biden\u8217\'20\'19s campaign manager, said on a press call.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CPresident Biden is going to make \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  answer for the state of reproductive rights in this country. There\u8217\'20\'19s so much at stake in 2024, and we\u8217\'20\'19re going to continue to make sure that every single voter knows it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 As the country marks two years since Roe v Wade was overturned, Rodriguez indicated that Biden would make the issue of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access a central focus of the first general election debate, which will take place later this month.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThat\u8217\'20\'19s the contrast we will continue to highlight leading into the debate, using the Dobbs anniversary as another core inflection point,\u8221\'20\'1D Rodriguez said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.32pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.18pm BST\par \par \uc2 Here are some images coming through the newswires from Capitol Hill, where \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  made his first visit since the January 6 riots in 2021:\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.27pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.58pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Senate minority leader, \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2 , said that the Trump meeting was \u8220\'20\'1Centirely positive\u8221\'20\'1D, Punchbowl News reported.\par \par \uc2 McConnell specified that he and Trump \u8220\'20\'1Cgot a chance to talk\u8221\'20\'1D, adding that their meeting was policy focused.\par \par \uc2 The meeting between McConnell and Trump is the first time the two have spoken since December 2020.\par \par \uc2 enltrNEW \u8212\'20\'14 McConnell says Trump meeting was \u8220\'20\'1Centirely positive\u8221\'20\'1D and says he and Trump \u8220\'20\'1Cgot a chance to talk.\u8221\'20\'1D Didn\u8217\'20\'19t elaborate. Said meeting was policy focused.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Andrew Desiderio (@AndrewDesiderio) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AndrewDesiderio/status/1801310129335214140?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 13, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrFor context, McConnell and Trump hadn\u8217\'20\'19t spoken since December 2020.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Andrew Desiderio (@AndrewDesiderio) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AndrewDesiderio/status/1801310988353855714?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 13, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.43pm BST\par \par \uc2 The US House speaker, Mike Johnson, has issued a statement declaring that Republicans will win the White House, Senate and House of Representatives after he and other party members hosted \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Johnson said that Trump brought \u8220\'20\'1Can extraordinary amount of energy and excitement and enthusiasm\u8221\'20\'1D during the morning meeting.\par \par \uc2 Johnson said: \u8220\'20\'1CWe believe we are going to win back the White House, and the Senate, and grow the House majority, and when we do that, we will not waste a moment.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The House speaker promised an \u8220\'20\'1Caggressive agenda\u8221\'20\'1D with the new Congress in January. So far, such an agenda could look like pushing far-right legislation around immigration, gun control and other policies.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.50pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.30pm BST\par \par \uc2 Interim summary\par \par \uc2 Hello, US politics readers, it\u8217\'20\'19s been a busy morning in Washington with an important decision from the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  relating to reproductive rights and the first visit to Capitol Hill by \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  since some of his extremist supporters stormed the Capitol on January 6, 2021.\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19ll have much more news for you coming up.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s where things stand:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 American Civil Liberties Union (ACLU)\uc2  hailed the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/jun/13/supreme-court-abortion-pill-access"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 decision}}}\uc2  on mifepristone, while warning: \u8220\'20\'1CThis fight isn\u8217\'20\'19t over. Anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  politicians have already pledged to continue their efforts in this case to deny people access to medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  took a similar stance and said, in part: \u8220\'20\'1CToday\u8217\'20\'19s decision does not change the fact that the fight for reproductive freedom continues. It does not change the fact that the supreme court overturned Roe v Wade two years ago, and women lost a fundamental freedom. It does not change the fact that the right for a woman to get the treatment she needs is imperiled if not impossible in many states.\u8221\'20\'1D He additionally warned of \u8220\'20\'1CRepublican elected officials\u8217\'20\'19 extreme and dangerous agenda to ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  nationwide\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  has rejected a bid to restrict access to the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill mifepristone, with a unanimous decision from the nine-member bench that, essentially, the plaintiff did not have standing. \uc2 FDA\uc2 -approved mifepristone therefore continues to be available.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  visited Capitol Hill for the first time since the January 6 insurrection in 2021. Trump was invited to address House Republicans at the Capitol Hill Club and also meet with Senate Republicans at the National Republican Senatorial Committee headquarters.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A crowd of reporters, protesters and aides gathered outside the Capitol Hill Club. Former House speaker and sitting California congresswoman \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  said Trump\u8217\'20\'19s visit was with the \u8220\'20\'1Cmission of dismantling our democracy\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.37pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.58pm BST\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Democratic National Committee\uc2  has echoed similar sentiments as other Democratic leaders including \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  following the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s decision on mifepristone.\par \par \uc2 In a statement on Thursday, the DNC said:\par \par \uc2 The supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s unanimous ruling that the Maga extremists who sued the \uc2 FDA\uc2  in an attempt to ban medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  nationwide lacked standing does not change the dire stakes of this election for reproductive freedom.\par \par \uc2 It does not change the fact that because of Trump, millions of women in states across the country cannot access the health care they need. It does not change the fact that Trump bragged about overturning Roe and thinks women suffering extreme physical, mental, and emotional harm because they can\u8217\'20\'19t access reproductive health care is a \u8216\'20\'18 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://democrats.org/news/trump-thinks-its-beautiful-that-women-are-dying-because-of-the-extreme-abortion-bans-he-made-possible/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 beautiful thing to watch}}}\uc2 .\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 And it does not change the fact that if elected, Trump and his allies want to effectively ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  nationwide with or without the help of Congress and the courts \u8230\'20\'26 The only way to stop the Maga movement\u8217\'20\'19s attacks on our freedoms is to turn out the vote in November to win Democratic majorities in Congress and reelect President Biden and Vice President Harris \u8211\'20\'13 who will never stop fighting to guarantee women in every state have access to the care they need.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.07pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.25pm BST\par \par \uc2 In a statement on the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s ruling, \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  said that it \u8220\'20\'1Cdoes not change the fact that millions of American women are today living under cruel \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans because of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The vice-president went on to add:\par \par \uc2 Nor does this ruling change the threat to medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . We know the Trump team has a plan to try to end access to medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and carry out a Trump \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban in all 50 states, with or without Congress, if they get the chance. We cannot and will not let that happen.\par \par \uc2 The contrast is stark: while Trump relentlessly attacks reproductive freedoms, President Biden and I will never stop fighting to protect them. Americans have repeatedly made it clear they want more freedom, not less, and they will make their voices heard at the ballot box once again this November.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.05pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.57pm BST\par \par \uc2 ACLU\uc2  hails supreme court's mifepristone decision: 'This fight is far from over'\par \par \uc2 The American Civil Liberties Union\uc2  hailed the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s decision on mifepristone, saying:\par \par \uc2 The supreme court just unanimously rejected a request by anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  extremists to impose medically unnecessary restrictions on mifepristone, a safe and effective medication used in most abortions nationwide.\par \par \uc2 This fight isn\u8217\'20\'19t over. Anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  politicians have already pledged to continue their efforts in this case to deny people access to medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrThis fight isn\u8217\'20\'19t over. Anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  politicians have already pledged to continue their efforts in this case to deny people access to medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 ACLU (@ACLU) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ACLU/status/1801265307119481299?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 13, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 : 'Fight for reproductive freedom continues'\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has released the following statement on the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s decision to uphold mifepristone:\par \par \uc2 Today\u8217\'20\'19s decision does not change the fact that the fight for reproductive freedom continues. It does not change the fact that the supreme court overturned Roe v Wade two years ago, and women lost a fundamental freedom. It does not change the fact that the right for a woman to get the treatment she needs is imperiled if not impossible in many states.\par \par \uc2 It does mean that mifepristone, or medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , remains available and approved. Women can continue to access this medication \u8211\'20\'13 approved by the \uc2 FDA\uc2  as safe and effective more than 20 years ago.\par \par \uc2 But let\u8217\'20\'19s be clear: attacks on medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  are part of Republican elected officials\u8217\'20\'19 extreme and dangerous agenda to ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  nationwide \u8230\'20\'26 The stakes could not be higher for women across America.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.11pm BST\par \par \uc2 Washington\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic representative \uc2 Pramila Jayapal\uc2  echoed similar sentiments as other Democrats following the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s mifepristone decision.\par \par \uc2 In a tweet on X, Jayapal wrote:\par \par \uc2 This is a massive victory for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access, but there is no question \u8211\'20\'13 we must codify access to reproductive care nationwide.\par \par \uc2 enltrBREAKING: The Supreme Court just rejected an attempt to ban mifepristone.\par \par \uc2 This is a massive victory for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access, but there is no question \u8212\'20\'14 we must codify access to reproductive care nationwide. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/i0ec7v0rS4"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/i0ec7v0rS4}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Rep. \uc2 Pramila Jayapal\uc2  (@RepJayapal) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RepJayapal/status/1801257705195131179?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 13, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.57pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Massachusetts Democratic senator Elizabeth Warren hailed the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s decision to uphold mifepristone access, calling the challenge to reject it \u8220\'20\'1Cmeritless from the start \u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Warren, an outspoken reproductive rights activist, wrote on X:\par \par \uc2 This challenge to mifepristone was meritless from the start. \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  medication is safe and effective. Make no mistake: \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and Republican politicians will not stop marching us toward a nationwide \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban. We must protect reproductive freedom everywhere.\par \par \uc2 enltrThis challenge to mifepristone was meritless from the start. \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  medication is safe and effective.\par \par \uc2 Make no mistake: \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and Republican politicians will not stop marching us toward a nationwide \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban.\par \par \uc2 We must protect reproductive freedom everywhere. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/4sBBcwUruU"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/4sBBcwUruU}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Elizabeth Warren (@SenWarren) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SenWarren/status/1801260630202007915?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 13, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.03pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.41pm BST\par \par \uc2 The supreme court also issued another decision today in which it sided with \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  over the firing of seven pro-union workers in Memphis.\par \par \uc2 Reuters has more:\par \par \uc2 The justices threw out a lower court\u8217\'20\'19s approval of an injunction sought by the US National Labor Relations Board (\uc2 NLRB\uc2 ) ordering \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  to reinstate the workers while the agency\u8217\'20\'19s in-house administrative case against the Seattle-based company proceeds.\par \par \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  had argued that the judge in the Memphis case should have used a stringent four-factor test to weigh the bid for an injunction, similar to the standard used by some other courts and in non-labor legal disputes. This test includes an assessment of whether the side seeking relief would suffer irreparable harm and is likely to succeed on the merits of the case.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 In another decision on Thursday, the supreme court barred a federal trademark for the phrase \u8220\'20\'1CTrump too small.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The court\u8217\'20\'19s decision rejects a claim from a California lawyer that the trademark denial violated his constitutional free speech.\par \par \uc2 Reuters further reports:\par \par \uc2 The justices overturned a lower court\u8217\'20\'19s decision that the \uc2 US Patent and Trademark Office\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s rejection of Steve Elster\u8217\'20\'19s application to register the trademark to exclusively use it on t-shirts violated the US constitution\u8217\'20\'19s first amendment.\par \par \uc2 The case centered on a provision in a 1946 federal trademark law that bans the registration of any trademark that uses a living individual\u8217\'20\'19s name without their written consent. At issue was whether free speech protections for criticism of public figures outweigh the \uc2 US Patent and Trademark Office\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s concerns over Trump\u8217\'20\'19s rights, as the lower court found.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.23pm BST\par \par \uc2 New York\u8217\'20\'19s attorney general has hailed the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s decision to uphold mifepristone access.\par \par \uc2 In a tweet following the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s decision, Letitia James wrote:\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 US supreme court\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s decision to maintain access to medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is a major victory for reproductive rights across our nation. I fought to protect access to mifepristone in this case because it\u8217\'20\'19s your body, and it should always be your choice.\par \par \uc2 enltrThe \uc2 U.S. Supreme Court\uc2 's decision to maintain access to medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is a major victory for reproductive rights across our nation.\par \par \uc2 I fought to protect access to mifepristone in this case because it's your body, and it should always be your choice.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 NY AG James (@NewYorkStateAG) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/NewYorkStateAG/status/1801254707299532805?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 13, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.24pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.07pm BST\par \par \uc2 Supreme court rejects bid to restrict mifepristone\par \par \uc2 The supreme court has rejected a bid to restrict access to the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill mifepristone.\par \par \uc2 The decision overturned an appeals ruling that would have restricted mail-order prescriptions of the common \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  drug.\par \par \uc2 The nation\u8217\'20\'19s highest court arrived at the decision unanimously, in turn marking a win for reproductive rights across the country.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 Supreme court to issue at least one decision with major Trump and \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  cases outstanding\par \par \uc2 The supreme court is set to issue at least one decision on Thursday, with major cases on \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights still outstanding.\par \par \uc2 It remains to be seen whether the nation\u8217\'20\'19s highest court will decide if Trump is immune to criminal charges in the election interference case surrounding him.\par \par \uc2 The supreme court still also has to issue decisions on two key \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  cases involving mifepristone pill access as well as Idaho\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban amid federal emergency room care requirements.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.03pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.46pm BST\par \par \uc2 Should \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  win the 2024 presidential election , the state department may likely see a mass purge.\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Julian Borger reports:\par \par \uc2 America\u8217\'20\'19s career diplomats are braced for the threat of a mass purge if {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  wins the November election and for the potential flooding of the state department with loyalty-tested political appointees.\par \par \uc2 Rather than leading to a seamless change of course in a rightward Trumpist direction, the diplomats\u8217\'20\'19 union and former ambassadors argue, such an attempted takeover would be much more likely to end in legal challenges, gridlock and chaos.\par \par \uc2 If elected, Trump has threatened to reinstate a policy he unsuccessfully attempted in his first term with the creation of \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jun/11/trump-project-2025-wrecking-ball#:~:text=limit%20executive%20power.-,%E2%80%9CYou%20can%20look%20at%20what%20they're%20going%20to%20do,on%20political%20loyalty%20to%20Donald"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Schedule F}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D, a new category of federal employees which would be applied to tens of thousands of civil servants in \u8220\'20\'1Cpolicy-related\u8221\'20\'1D jobs, robbing them of legal protections and making them liable to be fired at will.\par \par \uc2 For the full story, click here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jun/13/trump-state-department-project-2025-purge"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump win could see mass purge of state department, US diplomats fear }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.04pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.26pm BST\par \par \uc2 A crowd of reporters, along with protesters and aides, appears to have gathered outside the Capitol Hill Club \u8211\'20\'13 a national social club for Republicans \u8211\'20\'13 ahead of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s visit to Capitol Hill:\par \par \uc2 enltrJust a small sample of how many reporters, protestors and staffers are outside the Capitol Hill Club where former President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  will meet with House Republicans this morning. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/2Uz966zFA9"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/2Uz966zFA9}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kyle Stewart (@KyleAlexStewart) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/KyleAlexStewart/status/1801240743266107721?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 13, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.09pm BST\par \par \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  on Trump's Capitol Hill visit: 'Mission of dismantling our democracy'\par \par \uc2 Here is former House speaker \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s full statement that the she released ahead of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s visit to Capitol Hill on Thursday:\par \par \uc2 Today, the instigator of an insurrection is returning to the scene of the crime. January 6th was a crime against the Capitol, that saw Nazi and Confederate flags flying under the dome that Lincoln built.\par \par \uc2 It was a crime against the constitution and its peaceful transfer of power, in a desperate attempt to cling to power. And it was a crime against Members, heroic police officers and staff, that resulted in death, injury and trauma that endure to this day.\par \par \uc2 With his pledges to be a dictator on day one and seek revenge against his political opponents, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  comes to Capitol Hill today with the same mission of dismantling our democracy. But make no mistake \u8211\'20\'13 Trump has already cemented his legacy of shame in our hallowed halls.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.07pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.02pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  to visit Capitol Hill for first time since January 6\par \par \uc2 Good morning,\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is set to visit Capitol Hill for the first time since the January 6 riots in 2021.\par \par \uc2 Trump is expected to address House Republicans at the Capitol Hill Club and also meet with Senate Republicans at the National Republican Senatorial Committee headquarters, Politico {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/newsletters/playbook/2024/06/13/what-trump-wants-from-capitol-hill-00163125"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports.}}}\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/donald-trump/trump-meeting-republicans-first-visit-capitol-hill-jan-6-rcna156779"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Speaking to}}}\uc2  NBC, Mississippi\u8217\'20\'19s Republican senator Roger Wicker said the visit from Trump \u8220\'20\'1Cwill be an expression of unity\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, Democrats including the former House speaker, \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2 , have hit back at Trump\u8217\'20\'19s upcoming visit. In a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thehill.com/homenews/house/4719535-nancy-pelosi-donald-trump-congress-meeting-democracy/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 statement}}}\uc2  on Thursday, Pelosi accused the former president of being on a mission of \u8220\'20\'1Cdismantling our democracy\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s visit comes after he was found guilty last month of 34 counts of falsifying business records in his historic hush-money trial involving the adult film star Stormy Daniels.\par \par \uc2 Here are other developments in US politics:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The Republican-led House has voted to hold the attorney general, \uc2 Merrick Garland\uc2 , in contempt for withholding audio recordings of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  in his classified-documents case.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The Democrat-led Senate is set to vote on a bill that would enshrine IVF access and protection across the country.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The supreme court is expected to announce several decisions today as Republicans blocked an ethics bill surrounding the nation\u8217\'20\'19s highest court amid a series of scandals involving justices accepting luxury gifts.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.41pm BST\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240613ek6d001xl\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
