\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Nancy Mace beats Kevin McCarthy-backed challenger in South Carolina primary\b0\par\par\uc2 Joan E Greve and George Chidi \par \uc2 1,108 \uc2 words\par \uc2 12 June 2024\par 02:09 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Congresswoman leads by 29 points, surviving McCarthy\u8217\'20\'19s grudge after she voted to oust ex-House speaker last year\par \par \uc2 The South Carolina congresswoman Nancy Mace easily survived a primary challenge on Tuesday, against Kevin McCarthy-backed \uc2 Catherine Templeton\uc2 , while a much closer than expected special election in Ohio offered warning signs for Republicans ahead of November.\par \par \uc2 In Ohio\u8217\'20\'19s sixth district, candidate Michael Rulli prevailed in the special election to replace fellow Republican \uc2 Bill Johnson\uc2 , who resigned from Congress in January. Rulli\u8217\'20\'19s victory will help expand his party\u8217\'20\'19s razor-thin majority in the House, but his nine-point win over Democratic contender Michael Kripchak may unnerve Republicans, given that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , who resigned from Congress in January. Rulli\u8217\'20\'19s victory will help expand his party\u8217\'20\'19s razor-thin majority in the House, but his nine-point win over Democratic contender Michael Kripchak may unnerve Republicans, given that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.dailykos.com/stories/2022/11/14/1163009/-Daily-Kos-Elections-presidential-results-by-congressional-district-for-2020"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 carried }}}\uc2  the district by 29 points in 2020.\par \par \uc2 In South Carolina, McCarthy, the former House speaker, attempted to oust Mace by backing her rival, but the the two-term incumbent received a crucial endorsement from Trump. The grudge match was personal for McCarthy, as Mace was one of the eight Republicans who {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/oct/03/kevin-mccarthy-oust-republican-house-speaker-vote-result-matt-gaetz"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 voted to oust }}}\uc2  the then speaker last year.\par \par \uc2 The high stakes made the race a costly one, with outside groups dumping millions of dollars into the district. The South Carolina Patriots Pac {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.opensecrets.org/races/outside-spending?cycle=2024&id=SC01"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 spent }}}\uc2  nearly $4m backing Templeton\u8217\'20\'19s primary bid, while the Win It Back Pac and Club for Growth Action {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.opensecrets.org/political-action-committees-pacs//C00844613/independent-expenditures/2024"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 collectively }}}\uc2  nearly $4m backing Templeton\u8217\'20\'19s primary bid, while the Win It Back Pac and Club for Growth Action {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.opensecrets.org/political-action-committees-pacs//C00487470/independent-expenditures/2024"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 invested }}}\uc2  roughly $2.5m supporting Mace. Despite Templeton\u8217\'20\'19s external support, Mace led by 29 points when the Associated Press called the first congressional district race about an hour and a half after polls closed in South Carolina.\par \par \uc2 Mace was not the only South Carolina Republican facing a primary threat on Tuesday. Over in the fourth district, the Republican congressman William Timmons was running neck and neck with state representative Adam Morgan, who leads the South Carolina legislature\u8217\'20\'19s freedom caucus. Like Mace, Timmons had the benefit of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s endorsement, but the race was still too close to call three hours after polls closed.\par \par \uc2 And at least one of South Carolina\u8217\'20\'19s House Republican primaries will advance to a runoff later this month. In the reliably Republican third district, Trump-backed pastor Mark Burns and Air National Guard Lt Col Sheri Biggs will compete again on 25 June to determine who will have the opportunity to succeed Jeff Duncan, the retiring representative.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the fate of South Carolina\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws rests in part on the results of three Republican primaries in state senate races. State senators Katrina Shealy, Margie Bright Matthews, Mia McLeod, Sandy Senn and Penry Gustafson collectively blocked a near-total \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban in South Carolina earlier this year. The \u8220\'20\'1CSister Senators\u8221\'20\'1D were feted as a profile in courage by the Kennedy Center, but the three Republicans among them \u8211\'20\'13 Shealy, Senn and Gustafson \u8211\'20\'13 face primary challengers from their right on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . If two of the three lose to challengers, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  foes will have the votes to restrict \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  beyond the current six-week ban.\par \par \uc2 In addition to South Carolina, three other states held primaries on Tuesday. In Maine\u8217\'20\'19s second congressional district, the former Nascar driver turned state representative Austin Theriault resoundingly defeated fellow state representative Michael Soboleski in the Republican primary. Theriault will advance to the general election against Democratic congressman Jared Golden, who faces yet another difficult re-election campaign.\par \par \uc2 Republicans are hopeful that Theriault has the r\u233\'00\'E9sum\u233\'00\'E9 to defeat Golden, but the Democrat has proven politically resilient since he was first elected to Congress in 2018, when he narrowly defeated the Republican incumbent, \uc2 Bruce Poliquin\uc2 , thanks to Maine\u8217\'20\'19s ranked-choice voting system. In 2022, Golden again defeated Poliquin by six points in the second round of voting, even though Trump had carried the second district by seven points two years earlier.\par \par \uc2 The Cook Political Report {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cookpolitical.com/ratings/house-race-ratings"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 rates }}}\uc2  Golden\u8217\'20\'19s seat as a toss-up, so Theriault\u8217\'20\'19s victory will kick off what is expected to be a heated and closely contested race in the general election. Just minutes after the AP made Theriault\u8217\'20\'19s primary win official, the left-leaning Pac American Bridge 21st Century {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/American_Bridge/status/1800695073597960537"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 began }}}\uc2  attacking him over his views on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access.\par \par \uc2 In Nevada, a dozen Republicans are vying for their party\u8217\'20\'19s Senate nomination, but the primary appears to have become a two-person race between the retired army captain Sam Brown and former US ambassador to Iceland Jeff Gunter. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thenevadaindependent.com/article/gop-pollster-sam-brown-still-leads-nevada-senate-primary-in-internal-poll-despite-gunters-late-push"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Polling }}}\uc2  indicates Brown has a significant lead over Gunter, and Brown has received a last-minute boost from Trump, who made a much-awaited {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://truthsocial.com/@realDonaldTrump/posts/112589851588761769"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 endorsement }}}\uc2  in the race on Sunday.\par \par \uc2 The winner of the Republican primary will go on to face the Democratic incumbent, Jackie Rosen, in one of the most closely watched Senate races this year, as the Cook Political Report {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cookpolitical.com/ratings/senate-race-ratings"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 rates }}}\uc2  the seat as a toss-up.\par \par \uc2 Further down the ballot, the Democratic congresswoman Susie Lee faces a tough re-election campaign in Nevada\u8217\'20\'19s third congressional district. Seven Republicans \u8211\'20\'13 including video game music composer Marty O\u8217\'20\'19Donnell and former state treasurer Dan Schwartz \u8211\'20\'13 are running for the chance to face off against Lee, but Trump has stayed out of the primary so far. The former president\u8217\'20\'19s only House primary endorsement in Nevada went to the former North Las Vegas mayor John Lee in the fourth district, but the winner of that race will face a much steeper climb to defeat the Democratic incumbent, Steven Horsford, in the general election.\par \par \uc2 Over in North Dakota, five Republicans and two Democrats are running to replace the Republican congressman Kelly Armstrong representing the state\u8217\'20\'19s at-large congressional district, but no Democrat has won the seat since 2008. Rather than seeking re-election, Armstrong has launched a gubernatorial bid, and he won his primary on Tuesday. Armstrong is widely favored to replace the outgoing governor, \uc2 Doug Burgum\uc2 , who has been named as a potential running mate for Trump.\par \par \uc2 North Dakota voters also weighed in on a ballot measure regarding age limits for congressional candidates. If approved by a majority of North Dakota voters, the measure would prevent candidates from running for Congress if they would turn 81 during their term. Although the policy would only apply to congressional candidates, the age cutoff is noteworthy considering \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , who is four years older than Trump, turned 81 in November.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240611ek6b001ut\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
