\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 DeSantis \u8216\'20\'18freedom fund\u8217\'20\'19 Pac targets  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  and marijuana ballot initiatives\b0\par\par\uc2 Gloria Oladipo \par \uc2 449 \uc2 words\par \uc2 11 June 2024\par 20:43 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Group, known as Florida Freedom Fund, launched in May and will also be involved in school board races\par \par \uc2 The Florida governor, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ron-desantis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ron DeSantis}}}\uc2 , has launched a political action committee that is targeting popular ballot amendments on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access and marijuana legalization that will be voted on in November.\par \par \uc2 The group, known as the Florida Freedom Fund, launched in May, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2024/06/10/desantis-target-abortion-pot-amendments-florida-ballot-00162567"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Politico first reported}}}\uc2 . The committee is chaired by James Uthmeier, DeSantis\u8217\'20\'19s chief of staff who was previously the Republican\u8217\'20\'19s campaign manager during his unsuccessful presidential primary run.\par \par \uc2 In addition to targeting ballot initiatives, the committee will get involved in school board races, Politico reported, citing an individual who is familiar with the group\u8217\'20\'19s plans.\par \par \uc2 Florida Republicans have attempted to maximize their political control of local school boards, especially amid book bans and far-right education laws banning discussions of race and sexual identity being passed in the state, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wuft.org/politics/2024-04-24/florida-republicans-eye-control-of-more-county-school-boards-in-november-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 WUFT reported}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 A spokesperson for the governor told Politico that the goal of the political action committee is to support issues and candidates that are \u8220\'20\'1Ccommitted to preserving Floridians\u8217\'20\'19 freedom\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFrom up and down ballot races to critical amendments, we\u8217\'20\'19re steadfast in our mission to keep Florida free,\u8221\'20\'1D a DeSantis spokesperson, Taryn Fenske, said.\par \par \uc2 Reproductive-rights activists have been pushing for voters to support an upcoming ballot initiative that would enshrine broader \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access in Florida\u8217\'20\'19s constitution, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.axios.com/2024/06/09/florida-abortion-ban-clinic-access-vote-2024"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Axios reported}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Since Florida\u8217\'20\'19s six-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban went into effect in June, fewer abortions have been performed in the state. Activists have also seen more people seeking care in states on the east coast with broader \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access.\par \par \uc2 Amending Florida\u8217\'20\'19s constitution is a difficult task \u8211\'20\'13 60% of voters will have to approve the ballot initiative.\par \par \uc2 But support for the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access measure, known as Amendment 4, has been picking up steam before the November vote.\par \par \uc2 Supporters of the constitutional amendment have raised more than $12m in two months since the state\u8217\'20\'19s supreme court approved the measure in April, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tampabay.com/news/florida-politics/elections/2024/06/10/florida-abortion-amendment-ban-pregnancy-marijuana-desantis/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Tampa Bay Times reported}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSeeing increased financial support for the Yes on 4 effort provides us a glimmer of hope. Regardless of income or background, every Floridian deserves the freedom to make their own healthcare decisions without government interference, including \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and we\u8217\'20\'19ll keep up the fight to make that a reality,\u8221\'20\'1D the campaign director for Yes on 4 Florida, Lauren Brenzel, said to the Times.\par \par \uc2 Both amendments appear to be garnering widespread support. Recent {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.fox13news.com/news/fox-polling-shows-support-florida-abortion-marijuana-amendments-november"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 polling by Fox News}}}\uc2  predicted that both amendments would overwhelmingly pass, with 69% of voters supporting the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -access initiative and 66% favoring the marijuana-legalization amendment.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240611ek6b0035y\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
