\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 US reportedly considers deal with \uc2 Hamas\uc2 ; Blinken arrives in Israel to meet Netanyahu \u8211\'20\'13 live\b0\par\par\uc2 L\u233\'00\'E9onie Chao-Fong (now) and Erum Salam (earlier) \par \uc2 4,645 \uc2 words\par \uc2 10 June 2024\par 18:57 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Biden administration considers deal with \uc2 Hamas\uc2  that doesn\u8217\'20\'19t include Israel, NBC News reports; secretary of state in Israel to meet with PMUS to ask \uc2 UN\uc2  security council to back \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Gaza peace deal\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.57pm BST\par \par \uc2 US and allies stand behind Biden's Gaza ceasefire proposal, Blinken tells Netanyahu\par \par \uc2 The US secretary of state, \uc2 Antony Blinken\uc2 , met with Israel\u8217\'20\'19s prime minister, \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2 , in Jerusalem today where he reiterated that America \u8220\'20\'1Cand other world leaders will stand behind the comprehensive proposal outlined by President Biden\u8221\'20\'1D for an immediate ceasefire in Gaza and release of hostages.\par \par \uc2 Blinken told Netanyahu that \u8220\'20\'1Cthe proposal on the table would unlock the possibility of calm along Israel\u8217\'20\'19s northern border and further integration with countries in the region,\u8221\'20\'1D according to a US state department readout of the meeting.\par \par \uc2 The Secretary updated the prime minister on ongoing diplomatic efforts to plan for the post-conflict period, emphasizing the importance of those efforts to providing long-term peace, security, and stability to Israelis and Palestinians alike. Secretary Blinken also emphasized the importance of preventing the conflict from spreading.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.49pm BST\par \par \uc2 Closing arguments have begun in Hunter Biden\u8217\'20\'19s gun trial, beginning with the prosecutors.\par \par \uc2 Prosector Leo Wise said \u8220\'20\'1Cno one is above the law\u8221\'20\'1D and added the testimonies from Biden\u8217\'20\'19s high-profile family members don\u8217\'20\'19t matter.\par \par \uc2 Biden\u8217\'20\'19s lawyer Abbe Lowell said \u8220\'20\'1Cit\u8217\'20\'19s time to end this case,\u8221\'20\'1D arguing the burden of proof against her client has not been met.\par \par \uc2 The judge in this trial has instructed jurors to only consider whether or not the president\u8217\'20\'19s son was using drugs at the time he filled out the federal forms to purchase his firearm.\par \par \uc2 Jury deliberation will begin after both sides have rested their cases.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden\u8217\'20\'19s criticism of Trump, who recently became the first former American president to be convicted of felony crimes, has become increasingly sharper.\par \par \uc2 Today the Biden campaign dropped a new campaign ad featuring a Trump gaffe, in which his opponent in the upcoming 2024 presidential election says:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe need every voter. I don\u8217\'20\'19t care about you. I just want your vote. I don\u8217\'20\'19t care.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrI approve this message. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/IajfDVy72C"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/IajfDVy72C}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  (@JoeBiden) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JoeBiden/status/1800188776074924223?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 10, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.06pm BST\par \par \uc2 In a subsequent post to X, Brown thanked Trump for the endorsement and for his \u8220\'20\'1Cleadership\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI look forward to working with you to bring a better future to every Nevadan and American when we both win in November!!,\u8221\'20\'1D Brown said.\par \par \uc2 Read the full post below:\par \par \uc2 enltrThank you, President Trump, for your leadership. I'm honored to have your endorsement.\par \par \uc2 I look forward to working with you to bring a better future to every Nevadan and American when we both win in November!! {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/GCi2Uf2In1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/GCi2Uf2In1}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Sam Brown (@CaptainSamBrown) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/CaptainSamBrown/status/1799988190113325531?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 10, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  endorsed retired Army captain Sam Brown in the Nevada Senate race in a Truth Social post late Sunday, giving Brown a crucial boost two days before the state primary.\par \par \uc2 Trump, who described Brown as a \u8220\'20\'1CFEARLESS AMERICAN PATRIOT\u8221\'20\'1D, posted after he spent the day in Las Vegan holding a rally, where several of the GOP Senate candidates were in attendance, AP reported. Trump chose Brown over several other candidates with close ties to the former president, including Jeff Gunter, his former ambassador to Iceland.\par \par \uc2 The winner of Tuesday\u8217\'20\'19s Republican primary will face off with Democratic senator \uc2 Jacky Rosen\uc2  in what is likely to be one of the closest Senate races in the country.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.30pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Kennedy name looms large over American politics. \uc2 John F Kennedy\uc2 , despite serving only two and a half years as president before his assassination, is frequently ranked among the top 10 US leaders; his brother, \uc2 Robert F Kennedy\uc2 , seemed set for his own spell in the White House until he too was killed in 1968.\par \par \uc2 Enter: \uc2 Robert F Kennedy Jr\uc2 , nephew of the former, son of the latter and increasingly, persona non grata of the surviving Kennedy clan.\par \par \uc2 Part-time environmental lawyer, full-time conspiracy theorist, an animal enthusiast who owned a pet lion at his elite boarding school and who, in his telling, had {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2024/05/08/us/rfk-jr-brain-health-memory-loss.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 part of his brain eaten by a worm}}}\uc2 , Kennedy entered the 2024 presidential race as a Democrat running against Biden, before switching to an independent in October last year. The 70-year-old, who also has a history of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jul/19/robert-kennedy-jr-racist-antisemitic-xenophobic-views"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 associating with white supremacists}}}\uc2 , is an unknown quantity in the 2024 election race, with both parties worried about the havoc he could wreak.\par \par \uc2 Five months out from perhaps the most consequential election in recent US history, Biden and Trump continue to be unpopular with the American public. Kennedy\u8217\'20\'19s ability to be neither of those men, and his willingness to lean into his family name, have positioned him as a spanner in the works of American democracy.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/jun/09/rfk-biden-trump-2024-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Read the full story here: }}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/jun/09/rfk-biden-trump-2024-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Could RFK swing enough votes from Trump and Biden to decide the election?}}}\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/jun/09/rfk-biden-trump-2024-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Could RFK swing enough votes from Trump and Biden to decide the election?}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.27pm BST\par \par \uc2 As we {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jun/10/trump-probation-blinken-israel-gaza-updates?page=with:block-6666fce48f082d17177667b4#block-6666fce48f082d17177667b4"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported earlier,}}}\uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  was scheduled today to make a virtual address to an event by the Danbury Institute, a Christian group that calls for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  to be \u8220\'20\'1Ceradicated entirely\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Hours before Trump\u8217\'20\'19s expected address, the former president\u8217\'20\'19s campaign said he will deliver a pre-recorded message in which he does not say the word \u8220\'20\'1C\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D at all, according to a Politico, which has obtained a script of his two-minute speech.\par \par \uc2 According to the script, Trump is expected to say:\par \par \uc2 We have to defend religious liberty, free speech, innocent life and the heritage and traditions that built America into the greatest nation in the history of the world. I know that each of you is protecting those values every day \u8212\'20\'14 and I hope we\u8217\'20\'19ll be defending them side by side for the next four years.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.04pm BST\par \par \uc2 Dozens of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s supporters have been requiring medical help at his rallies in the scorching US south-west but it seems lost on him that his plans to reverse climate policies and \u8220\'20\'1Cdrill, baby, drill\u8221\'20\'1D for fossil fuels will only worsen extreme weather, campaigners say.\par \par \uc2 A total of 24 people at a Trump rally in Las Vegas on Sunday required medical attention due to the heat, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ktnv.com/news/six-people-taken-to-the-hospital-after-las-vegas-trump-rally"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to the Clark county fire department}}}\uc2 , with six taken to hospital for treatment. The hospitalizations come after a further 11 people needed to be admitted to hospital for heat exhaustion as they waited for Trump to speak at a rally in Phoenix on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 Trump himself noted the severe heat during his speech on Sunday, with the Las Vegas rally starting around noon when the temperature was about 90F (32C) and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://world-weather.info/forecast/usa/las_vegas_1/09-june/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 climbed}}}\uc2  to around 102F (38C). The rally was held in a park with little shade, although organizers provided water and cooling tents, and allowed attendees to hold shading umbrellas.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s 110, but it doesn\u8217\'20\'19t feel it to me,\u8221\'20\'1D said Trump, who wore a suit jacket and signature red baseball cap.\par \par \uc2 I\u8217\'20\'19m up here sweating like a dog. They don\u8217\'20\'19t think about me. This is hard work.\par \par \uc2 enltrDonald Trump: \u8220\'20\'1CI don't care about you. I just want your vote. I don't care.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Once in a while, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  slips up and tells the truth.\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/urNUA0s8WA"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/urNUA0s8WA}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Republicans against Trump (@RpsAgainstTrump) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RpsAgainstTrump/status/1799953634631061940?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 9, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 Trump then said:\par \par \uc2 I don\u8217\'20\'19t want anybody going on me. We need every voter. I don\u8217\'20\'19t care about you. I just want your vote. I don\u8217\'20\'19t care.\par \par \uc2 He later said he was joking about not caring about his own voters and complained the media would criticize him for this.\par \par \uc2 Record-breaking heat {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jun/07/us-south-west-heatwave"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 enveloped much of the US south-west last week}}}\uc2 , with temperatures soaring beyond 110F (43C) in areas stretching from California to Arizona. Roughly half of Arizona and Nevada were under an excessive heat alert, even though the official start of summer is still a week away, with Las Vegas hitting 110F on Friday and Phoenix reaching 113F (45C).\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.47pm BST\par \par \uc2 Antony Blinken\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s meetings with Israeli officials on Monday and the US push for a Gaza ceasefire deal comes after Israel\u8217\'20\'19s former army chief of staff, \uc2 Benny Gantz\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/article/2024/jun/09/moderate-politician-benny-gantz-resigns-israeli-war-cabinet"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 resigned from the war cabinet.}}}\par \par \uc2 The resignation by Gantz, leader of the centre-right National Unity party and a major rival to \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2 , followed through on a threat to resign after he gave Israel\u8217\'20\'19s prime minister an ultimatum of 8 June to present concrete \u8220\'20\'1Cday after\u8221\'20\'1D plans for the Gaza Strip.\par \par \uc2 The withdrawal of his party also means Gadi Eisenkot, an \uc2 Israel Defense Forces\uc2  (\uc2 IDF\uc2 ) general and war cabinet observer, and the minister without portfolio, Chili Tropper, are also stepping down.\par \par \uc2 The departure of Gantz leaves Netanyahu with enough seats in his coalition but has made him even more reliant on the support of far-right allies including \uc2 Bezalel Smotrich\uc2  and Itamar Ben-Gvir, the national security minister. Smotrich and Ben-Gvir have repeatedly threatened to walk away over any deal for a ceasefire in exchange for hostages.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.21pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has been compared to Jesus Christ by the far-right Georgia congresswoman \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene\uc2  at a campaign rally for the former president in Las Vegas, a city more renowned for evoking images of gambling than biblical scenes.\par \par \uc2 Greene, who makes frequent references to her Christian faith, cited Trump\u8217\'20\'19s supposed Christ-like qualities to challenge the Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 efforts to capitalise on the presumptive Republican presidential nominee\u8217\'20\'19s status as a convicted felon following his recent conviction in a case involving hush money paid to an adult film actor and falsified business records in a New York court.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe Democrats and the fake news media want to constantly talk about \u8216\'20\'18President Trump is a convicted felon\u8217\'20\'19,\u8221\'20\'1D she {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.rollingstone.com/politics/politics-news/mtg-jesus-convicted-felon-like-trump-1235036256/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told}}}\uc2  a crowd that waited in soaring early-summer temperatures.\par \par \uc2 Well, you want to know something? The man that I worship is also a convicted felon. And he was murdered on a Roman cross.\par \par \uc2 enltrMarjorie Taylor Greene in Vegas compares Trump to Jesus {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/R8l3fGUO0B"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/R8l3fGUO0B}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Aaron Rupar (@atrupar) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/atrupar/status/1799865854630199452?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 9, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 It is not the first time Greene has drawn parallels between Trump and Christ \u8211\'20\'13 whom Christians consider to be the messiah and son of God \u8211\'20\'13 as well as other historical martyr figures.\par \par \uc2 When he was arrested in New York on corruption charges in April last year, she likened Trump to Jesus and \uc2 Nelson Mandela\uc2 , who became South Africa\u8217\'20\'19s first post-apartheid president after being jailed for 27 years by the racist regime.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.02pm BST\par \par \uc2 A Georgia congressional candidate convicted for participating in the January 6th insurrection walked out of a televised Republican debate on Sunday.\par \par \uc2 Chuck Hand is one of at least four people convicted of January 6 crimes running for Congress this year, according to AP. All are running as Republicans. Hand was sentenced to 20 days in federal prison and six months of probation.\par \par \uc2 Hand is running against Wayne Johnson ahead of a 18 June primary runoff for southwest Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s 2nd congressional district.\par \par \uc2 During the debate, Hand said he was refusing to debate Johnson afte r Michael Nixon, who finished third in an earlier primary, endorsed Johnson. Nixon brought up a 2005 criminal trespass charge and a 2010 DUI charge against Hand, both of which were dismissed, and also cited federal court documents to argue Hand\u8217\'20\'19s participation in the January 6 riot was more serious than Hand had claimed.\par \par \uc2 Hand, walking out of the studio, said:\par \par \uc2 This is where I get back in my truck and go back to southwest Georgia because I\u8217\'20\'19ve got two races to win.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou\u8217\'20\'19re not staying?\u8221\'20\'1D asked anchor Donna Lowry. \u8220\'20\'1CYou\u8217\'20\'19re leaving, sir? OK.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrChuck Hand, a Georgia congressional candidate who was convicted of a misdemeanor for participating in the January 6th insurrection, walked off stage during a Republican debate on Sunday:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is where I get back in my truck and head back to southwest Georgia.\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/FHgRzwfBRc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/FHgRzwfBRc}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1800192063864021187?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 10, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.43pm BST\par \par \uc2 US considering unilateral deal with \uc2 Hamas\uc2  - report\par \par \uc2 The Biden administration is considering entering into a deal with \uc2 Hamas\uc2  that does not include Israel, according to a NBC report.\par \par \uc2 Citing two current and two former US officials, the American broadcaster said a deal to free five US hostages would be hammered out through Qatari mediation if current ceasefire talks involving Israel fail.\par \par \uc2 The officials did not know what the US could offer \uc2 Hamas\uc2  in return, but argued there was an incentive for \uc2 Hamas\uc2  to drive a deeper wedge between \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and the Israeli leader, \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Parts of the Biden administration would like to see the Netanyahu coalition government collapse, leading to fresh elections and the formation of an Israeli government more willing to seek an understanding with the Palestinians. They believe the complete obliteration of \uc2 Hamas\uc2  militarily is a mirage and say Netanyahu has no realistic plan for Gaza\u8217\'20\'19s future governance.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.43pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.36pm BST\par \par \uc2 Mitch Landrieu, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s campaign chair, has told MSNBC that it is \u8220\'20\'1Castounding\u8221\'20\'1D that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , the presumptive Republican presidential nominee, \u8220\'20\'1Cfirst has to go {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jun/10/trump-probation-blinken-israel-gaza-updates?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-6666ef808f082d17177666d8#block-6666ef808f082d17177666d8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  sit down with his probation officer\u8221\'20\'1D.}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrBiden campaign national co-chair Mitch Landrieu: "A guy that wants to be president of the United States first has to go sit down with his probation officer. That is just an astounding statement that sometimes people walk by." {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/MSNBC?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @MSNBC}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kyle Griffin (@kylegriffin1) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/kylegriffin1/status/1800187559651553483?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 10, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.19pm BST\par \par \uc2 Antony Blinken\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jun/10/trump-probation-blinken-israel-gaza-updates?page=with:block-666714738f082d1717766915#block-666714738f082d1717766915"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 visit to Israel }}}\uc2  comes as the \uc2 UN\uc2  security council in New York is scheduled to vote on a US-drafted resolution backing its proposed Gaza ceasefire deal.\par \par \uc2 Washington is struggling to gain the unequivocal backing of Israel or \uc2 Hamas\uc2  for a three-stage deal proposed by \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , that would lead to the release of all the remaining hostages in return for Israel accepting steps towards a permanent ceasefire and the eventual withdrawal of its forces from Gaza \u8211\'20\'13 two key \uc2 Hamas\uc2  demands.\par \par \uc2 The draft \uc2 UN\uc2  resolution backing Biden\u8217\'20\'19s proposal suggests the move to phase two and the permanent end of hostilities will occur \u8220\'20\'1Con the agreement of both parties\u8221\'20\'1D, but says if the negotiations to reach that stage take longer than six weeks, \u8220\'20\'1Cthe ceasefire will continue as long as the negotiations continue\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 It says the US, Qatar and Egypt will work to ensure the negotiations keep going until all the agreements are reached and phase two is able to begin.\par \par \uc2 A vote is expected later today, after the US finalized its text on Sunday after six days of negotiations among the 15-member council. It was not immediately clear whether Russia and China would veto the draft, which needs nine votes and no vetoes to pass.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.04pm BST\par \par \uc2 Blinken arrives in Israel to meet Netanyahu\par \par \uc2 Anthony Blinken\uc2  is scheduled today to meet with Israel\u8217\'20\'19s prime minister, \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2 , in Jerusalem as he kicks off a Middle East trip where he is expected to urge leaders to support a three-stage Gaza ceasefire deal proposed by \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The US secretary of state met with Egypt\u8217\'20\'19s president, \uc2 Abdel Fattah al-Sisi\uc2 , in Cairo earlier today before traveling on to Israel. Blinken is also meeting with Israeli defence minister Yoav Gallant later today.\par \par \uc2 Blinken, speaking to reporters, said \uc2 Hamas\uc2  was the only outlier in not accepting the proposal for a ceasefire deal, to which he said Israel had agreed.\par \par \uc2 My message to governments throughout the region, to people throughout the region, is if you want a ceasefire, press \uc2 Hamas\uc2  to say yes.\par \par \uc2 A senior \uc2 Hamas\uc2  official said Blinken\u8217\'20\'19s comments were \u8220\'20\'1Cbiased to Israel\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.10pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 The South Dakota governor, \uc2 Kristi Noem\uc2 , said on Sunday that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  should pick a woman to be his running mate amid reports that her fellow Republican\u8217\'20\'19s shortlist is nearly all men.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI think that that would be beneficial, according to the polling that I\u8217\'20\'19ve seen for him and a lot of swing states, is that having a woman that is helping his campaign makes a difference,\u8221\'20\'1D she told Dana Bash during an interview on CNN\u8217\'20\'19s State of the Union.\par \par \uc2 One in four Republican women haven\u8217\'20\'19t made up their minds because they want to have a woman talking to them about the issues they care about. And women aren\u8217\'20\'19t monolithic. They don\u8217\'20\'19t care about just one issue.\par \par \uc2 Noem\u8217\'20\'19s comments come amid reports that the former president\u8217\'20\'19s campaign for a second term in the White House {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cbsnews.com/news/trump-vetting-vice-presidential-candidates/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 is vetting possible picks}}}\uc2 . Only one of them, congresswoman \uc2 Elise Stefanik\uc2  of New York, is a woman.\par \par \uc2 Others include senators JD Vance, \uc2 Marco Rubio\uc2 , Tim Scott and Tom Cotton. The North Dakota governor, \uc2 Doug Burgum\uc2 , congressman Byron Donalds, and Ben Carson, the former secretary of housing and urban development, are also reportedly under consideration.\par \par \uc2 Until recently, Noem was considered a top possible pick for the No 2 spot on the Republican ticket for November\u8217\'20\'19s election. But her chances reportedly fell significantly after she published a story in her recently published memoir {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/books/2024/apr/26/trump-kristi-noem-shot-dog-and-goat-book"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 about killing her dog}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.34pm BST\par \par \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2  gun trial resumes with president's son not expected to testify\par \par \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s federal trial resumed on Monday in Wilmington, Delaware, with closing arguments expected as soon as today.\par \par \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2 , the only surviving son of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , faces three felony charges tied to a 2018 firearm purchase while using narcotics. He is accused of making false statements on a gun-purchase form when he said he was not illegally using or addicted to drugs, and then unlawfully possessing the gun for 11 days. He has pleaded not guilty.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jun/07/hunter-biden-trial-takeaways-first-week"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Here are }}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jun/07/hunter-biden-trial-takeaways-first-week"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 some key takeaways from the trial\u8217\'20\'19s first week\u8217\'20\'19s proceedings.}}}\par \par \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s lawyer, Abbe Lowell, indicated in court this morning that his client will not testify, allowing the judge, Maryellen Noreika, to give the jury an instruction that they should not hold it against Biden that he did not testify in the case.\par \par \uc2 This is not the same as announcing definitively that \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2  will not testify. The instruction will be given later today.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jun/07/hunter-biden-trial-takeaways-first-week"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Hunter Biden gun trial: key takeaways from the first week}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.10pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is determined to avoid jail, but if he does get handed a prison sentence after his conviction on 34 felony counts in New York last week, the former president\u8217\'20\'19s inner circle is certain he will lay the blame squarely at the judge\u8217\'20\'19s feet, sources familiar with the matter said.\par \par \uc2 The precise way Trump might blame the judge, Juan Merchan, remains unclear because Trump has been avoidant of the issue and the matter was not resolved when he huddled with his top advisers at a Trump Tower meeting immediately after the verdict on Thursday, the sources said.\par \par \uc2 But Trump is likely to double down on his attacks against Merchan, directing his supporters at rallies and in Truth Social posts to take up their grievances with the judge, one of the sources added.\par \par \uc2 The consequences of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s likely rhetoric are difficult to predict. Trump has been railing against Merchan for months as being unfair and in conspiracy cahoots with the Biden administration to prevent him from campaigning \u8211\'20\'13 and nothing concrete has happened.\par \par \uc2 Still, Trump\u8217\'20\'19s supporters have a history of making threats against judges Trump has assailed, including death threats to \uc2 Tanya Chutkan\uc2 , the US district judge who is presiding in his federal 2020 election interference case, and to the chambers of the New York judge who oversaw his civil fraud trial.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.55pm BST\par \par \uc2 More than half of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s supporters are primarily motivated to cast their vote for the president in order to prevent a return of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  to the White House, according to a new poll.\par \par \uc2 Opposing Trump is the main reason to back Biden for 54% of the Democratic incumbent\u8217\'20\'19s voters, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.scribd.com/document/740568401/Cbsnews-20240609-SUN-NAT#1fullscreen=1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the new CBS/YouGov poll found}}}\uc2 , up from 47% in a similar survey conducted in March, which was prior to the presumptive Republican nominee being found guilty of business fraud by a New York jury.\par \par \uc2 A further 27% of Biden voters are supporting the president because they like him \u8211\'20\'13 down from 31% in March \u8211\'20\'13 while 19% say that they are backing him because he is the Democratic nominee for president.\par \par \uc2 The poll comes as the Biden campaign has ramped up its rhetoric in attacking Trump directly in recent weeks, pointing to the former president\u8217\'20\'19s felony conviction and string of past controversies. Last week, Biden said his predecessor is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jun/04/biden-trump-trial-verdict"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Creckless and dangerous\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2  for complaining that his New York trial was rigged and claimed that he had been driven \u8220\'20\'1Ccrazy\u8221\'20\'1D by his 2020 election loss.\par \par \uc2 The outcome of this year\u8217\'20\'19s presidential election remains in the balance, with the new \uc2 CBS\uc2  poll finding Biden and Trump are essentially tied nationally and in key swing states. Trump is on 50% of support among likely voters, and Biden is on 49%, with these figures switched for likely voters in battleground states.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s longtime refusal to admit wrongdoing in his hush-money case and repeated attacks on the presiding judge, Juan Merchan, and the trial could hurt him at his sentencing next month.\par \par \uc2 The former president has repeatedly claimed that the case against him was \u8220\'20\'1Crigged\u8221\'20\'1D, called Justice Merchan a \u8220\'20\'1Cdevil\u8221\'20\'1D who was \u8220\'20\'1Chighly conflicted\u8221\'20\'1D, and claimed, without evidence, that \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  was behind the production.\par \par \uc2 The ultimate {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/may/29/what-if-trump-guilty-prison-fine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 decision with sentencing rests with Merchan}}}\uc2 , who has wide discretion to sentence him to fines or probation on the low end, to a carceral sentence on the high end, regardless of what prosecutors might request. Much could depend on how Merchan interprets Trump\u8217\'20\'19s conduct, including any lack of remorse.\par \par \uc2 Jeffrey Cohen, an associate professor at Boston College Law School and a former federal prosecutor in Massachusetts, told AP:\par \par \uc2 The fact, I think, that he has no remorse \u8211\'20\'13 quite the opposite, he continues to deny his guilt \u8211\'20\'13 is going to hurt him at sentencing. It\u8217\'20\'19s one of the things that the judge can really point to that everybody is aware of \u8212\'20\'14 that he just denies this \u8212\'20\'14 and can use that as a strong basis for his sentence.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.26pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump to address Christian group that calls for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  to be 'eradicated entirely\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  will address a Christian group that calls for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  to be \u8220\'20\'1Ceradicated entirely\u8221\'20\'1D and calls it \u8220\'20\'1Cchild sacrifice\u8221\'20\'1D, as the presumptive Republican nominee tries to navigate between appeasing parts of his base who favor strict \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws and a broader electorate that largely supports some access to the procedure.\par \par \uc2 Trump is scheduled to make a virtual appearance on Monday at an event hosted by the Danbury Institute, which believes \u8220\'20\'1Cthat the greatest atrocity facing our generation today is the practice of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D and it \u8220\'20\'1Cmust be ended\u8221\'20\'1D, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.danburyinstitute.org/who-we-are"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according }}}\uc2  to its website. The group\u8217\'20\'19s statement reads:\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  must be ended. We will not rest until it is eradicated entirely.\par \par \uc2 Trump has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/12/donald-trump-abortion-roe-v-wade-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  repeatedly claimed credit }}}\uc2  for overturning Roe v Wade but has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/08/trump-abortion-states"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 declined to endorse}}}\uc2  a national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban and says he wants to leave the issue to the states. Both the Southern Baptists whom Trump will address Monday and the GOP at large are split on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  politics, with some calling for immediate, complete \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans and others more open to incremental tactics, according to AP.\par \par \uc2 In a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2024/06/06/trump-danbury-institute-abortion-event-00162203"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  statement}}}\uc2  to Politico, the Biden campaign blasted Trump\u8217\'20\'19s decision to speak at today\u8217\'20\'19s event, saying the presumptive Republican nominee \u8220\'20\'1Cloves campaigning with \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban extremists.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.09pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is scheduled to be interviewed by New York probation officials Monday, a required step before his July sentencing in his criminal hush-money case, according to three people familiar with the plan.\par \par \uc2 The former president will do the interview via a computer video conference from his residence at the Mar-a-Lago club in Palm Beach, Florida, the people told the Associated Press. They spoke on condition of anonymity because they weren\u8217\'20\'19t authorized to disclose the plans publicly.\par \par \uc2 One of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s lawyers, Todd Blanche, will be present for the interview. People convicted of crimes in New York usually meet with probation officials without their lawyers, but the judge in Trump\u8217\'20\'19s case, Juan Merchan, said in a letter Friday that he would allow Blanche\u8217\'20\'19s presence.\par \par \uc2 The usual purpose of a pre-sentencing probation interview is to prepare a report that will tell the judge more about the defendant, and potentially help determine the proper punishment for the crime.\par \par \uc2 Such reports are typically prepared by a probation officer, a social worker or a psychologist working for the probation department who interviews the defendant and possibly that person\u8217\'20\'19s family and friends, as well as people affected by the crime.\par \par \uc2 Present reports include a defendant\u8217\'20\'19s personal history, criminal record and recommendations for sentencing. It will also include information about employment and any obligations to help care for a family member. It is also a chance for a defendant to say why they think they deserve a lighter punishment.\par \par \uc2 Merchan has scheduled Trump\u8217\'20\'19s sentencing for 11 July. He has discretion to impose a wide range of punishments, ranging from probation and community service to up to four years in prison.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.59pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump to face probation interview in hush-money case\par \par \uc2 Good morning {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-politics"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US politics}}}\uc2  readers. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jun/10/trump-probation-officials-interview-hush-money-trial"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jun/10/trump-probation-officials-interview-hush-money-trial"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  is scheduled for a pre-sentencing interview}}}\uc2  with New York probation officials today, according to reports.\par \par \uc2 The former president will hold a virtual interview from his home at the Mar-a-Lago club in Palm Beach, Florida, alongside his lawyer Todd Blanche, sources told the Associated Press. It comes after Trump was convicted last month on all {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/may/30/trump-trial-hush-money-verdict"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 34 felony counts}}}\uc2  of falsifying business records.\par \par \uc2 The probation interview is used to prepare a report that will include a defendant\u8217\'20\'19s personal history, criminal record and recommendations for sentencing. It is also a chance for a defendant to say why they think they deserve a lighter punishment.\par \par \uc2 Trump is also expected on Monday to address a Christian group that calls for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  to be \u8220\'20\'1Ceradicated entirely\u8221\'20\'1D and calls the procedure \u8220\'20\'1Cchild sacrifice\u8221\'20\'1D. Trump is scheduled to speak virtually at an event hosted by the Danbury Institute, an organization that also seeks to ban same-sex marriage and use the Bible to guide public policy.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else we\u8217\'20\'19re watching:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/antony-blinken"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Antony Blinken}}}\uc2  returned to the Middle East today as a proposed Israel-\uc2 Hamas\uc2  ceasefire hangs in the balance. The US secretary of state met with Egypt\u8217\'20\'19s president, \uc2 Abdel Fattah\uc2  el-Sissi, in Cairo earlier, and is scheduled to meet with Israel\u8217\'20\'19s prime minister, \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2 , and defence minister Yoav Gallant later today.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jun/07/hunter-biden-trial-takeaways-first-week"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Hunter Biden}}}\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s lawyers are expected to wrap up arguments in his federal gun trial in Delaware today, with jury deliberations potentially to begin at the end of the day.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240610ek6a001uv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
