\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Steve Bannon\uc2  vows to appeal jail sentence and says order about \u8216\'20\'18shutting down the Maga movement\u8217\'20\'19 \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Chris Stein (now) and Gloria Oladipo (earlier) \par \uc2 5,646 \uc2 words\par \uc2 6 June 2024\par 20:03 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 This live blog is now closed. For the latest on Bannon\u8217\'20\'19s jail order, you can read our full report:Trump ally \uc2 Steve Bannon\uc2  told to begin four-month contempt sentence by 1 July\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.01pm BST\par \par \uc2 Closing summary\par \par \uc2 Almost two years after he was first found guilty of contempt of Congress for defying a subpoena from the January 6 committee, a federal judge today {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jun/06/biden-supreme-court-trump-abortion-politics-latest-updates?page=with:block-6661e2fb8f0872aaf435ba69#block-6661e2fb8f0872aaf435ba69"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ordered}}}\uc2 Steve Bannon\uc2 , an influential figure in \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s Maga movement, to begin serving his four-month sentence by 1 July. In a defiant speech outside the courthouse, he {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jun/06/biden-supreme-court-trump-abortion-politics-latest-updates?page=with:block-6661eac88f0872aaf435bb1d#block-6661eac88f0872aaf435bb1d"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 accused}}}\uc2  the justice department of using his case to retaliate against Trump, and predicted a big win for Republicans in the November presidential election. Speaking of Trump, the former president {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jun/06/biden-supreme-court-trump-abortion-politics-latest-updates?page=with:block-6661cbab8f082030798b1bc4#block-6661cbab8f082030798b1bc4"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 gave an interview}}}\uc2  to Fox News last night, where he argued he \u8220\'20\'1Cwould have every right to go after\u8221\'20\'1D political adversaries like \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , if he is returned to the White House. In response, the Biden campaign said Trump was \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jun/06/biden-supreme-court-trump-abortion-politics-latest-updates?page=with:block-6661ce2a8f08a6bac2fa9afe#block-6661ce2a8f08a6bac2fa9afe"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 visibly rattled}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D by his conviction last week on felony business fraud charges.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else happened today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The supreme court{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jun/06/biden-supreme-court-trump-abortion-politics-latest-updates?page=with:block-6661c7318f08ee6323fd8cfb#block-6661c7318f08ee6323fd8cfb"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 released}}}\uc2  a new batch of opinions, which did not include much-awaited decisions on Trump\u8217\'20\'19s petition for immunity from federal prosecution over his 2020 election meddling, and two cases dealing with \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The American Civil Liberties Union\uc2  is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jun/06/biden-supreme-court-trump-abortion-politics-latest-updates?page=with:block-66620c1d8f085d7b4203743d#block-66620c1d8f085d7b4203743d"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 suing}}}\uc2  Milwaukee over restrictions on protesters ahead of the Republican National Convention.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jun/06/biden-supreme-court-trump-abortion-politics-latest-updates?page=with:block-6661b87f8f08a6bac2fa9992#block-6661b87f8f08a6bac2fa9992"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 called for}}}\uc2  the supreme court to overturn his conviction on felony charges connected to falsifying documents related to hush-money payments made ahead of the 2016 election.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s federal gun charges trial {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jun/06/biden-supreme-court-trump-abortion-politics-latest-updates?page=with:block-6661dabf8f08a6bac2fa9bd5#block-6661dabf8f08a6bac2fa9bd5"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 continues}}}\uc2  in Delaware, with testimony from the widow of his late brother, \uc2 Beau Biden\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 NAACP\uc2  civil rights group {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jun/06/biden-supreme-court-trump-abortion-politics-latest-updates?page=with:block-6661f1878f0826e9b0f8578c#block-6661f1878f0826e9b0f8578c"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 asked}}}\uc2  Biden to halt all shipments of weapons to Israel.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.51pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  does not do too many sit down interviews with reporters, but took questions from ABC News during his visit to France for the D-day anniversary.\par \par \uc2 He was asked about his recent decision to allow Ukraine to use US-supplied weaponry to strike inside Russia. Here\u8217\'20\'19s what he had to say:\par \par \uc2 enltr\u8220\'20\'1C[Putin's] concerned me for 40 years. He's not a decent man.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 President Biden, in an ABC News exclusive, when asked whether he's concerned about Putin vowing retaliation for \uc2 NATO\uc2  allies allowing Ukraine to use their arms inside Russia {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/ipfOFMNVjT"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/ipfOFMNVjT}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1798796386005340636?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 6, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more on the president\u8217\'20\'19s decision, which comes as Russia steps up attacks aimed at the city of Kharkiv:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/article/2024/may/30/biden-ukraine-weapons-strike-russia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Biden changes stance to allow Ukraine to fire US-supplied weapons into Russia}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.53pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.29pm BST\par \par \uc2 Rights group announces lawsuit against Milwaukee over \uc2 RNC\uc2  protest restrictions\par \par \uc2 The American Civil Liberties Union\uc2  said this morning it has filed a lawsuit against the city of Milwaukee over restrictions on protesters at the Republican National Convention that it says violate the first amendment.\par \par \uc2 The convention, beginning on 15 July, will see thousands of delegates converge on the city\u8217\'20\'19s Fiserv Forum and culminate in \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  formally accepting the party\u8217\'20\'19s nomination. Various groups have already announced plans to protest the event, and the \uc2 ACLU\uc2  claims the city\u8217\'20\'19s restrictions on where they can do that are not in line with the constitution.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more:\par \par \uc2 enltrBREAKING: We sued the City of Milwaukee for establishing unconstitutional protest rules that violate the First Amendment rights of people planning to protest during the Republican National Convention next month. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/FQXjL3b83f"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/FQXjL3b83f}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 ACLU of Wisconsin (@ACLUofWisconsin) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ACLUofWisconsin/status/1798736474650890735?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 6, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrWe\u8217\'20\'19re representing the Coalition to March on the \uc2 RNC\uc2 , a group of protesters that applied for a parade permit over a year ago. With just six weeks before the \uc2 RNC\uc2 , Milwaukee has neither approved the permit nor identified a parade route whatsoever.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 ACLU of Wisconsin (@ACLUofWisconsin) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ACLUofWisconsin/status/1798736477196886068?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 6, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrBut the city is limiting demonstrators to an undisclosed parade route somewhere in a 90-square block area around Fiserv Forum. Protesters have a right to demonstrate within \u8220\'20\'1Csight and sound\u8221\'20\'1D of an event, and these additional rules will render them unseen and unheard.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 ACLU of Wisconsin (@ACLUofWisconsin) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ACLUofWisconsin/status/1798736478996177177?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 6, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.36pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.11pm BST\par \par \uc2 You\u8217\'20\'19re not hearing too much about \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  on this blog today, because the US president is in France to mark the anniversary of D-day, and call for support for Ukraine. The Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/leonie-chao-fong"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Leonie Chao-Fong}}}\uc2  has the scoop:\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has marked the 80th anniversary of the D-day landings in Normandy with an impassioned call to western allies to continue supporting Ukraine in the face of the \u8220\'20\'1Cunending struggle between dictatorship and freedom\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Speaking on Thursday at a ceremony at the Normandy American cemetery attended by his French counterpart, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/emmanuel-macron"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Emmanuel Macron}}}\uc2 , and dozens of surviving veterans from the second world war, Biden drew parallels between the Allied troops who fought to free Europe and the alliance of nations that came together to defend Ukraine against Russian aggression.\par \par \uc2 The president warned that democracy was under great threat than at any time since the end of second world war. Describing \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  as a \u8220\'20\'1Ctyrant bent on domination\u8221\'20\'1D, Biden said the Russian leader and \u8220\'20\'1Cthe autocrats of the world are watching closely to see what happens in Ukraine, to see if we let this illegal aggression go unchecked.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTo surrender to bullies, to bow to dictators, is simply unthinkable,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said. \u8220\'20\'1CIf we do, Ukraine will be subjugated and it will not end there, Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s neighbours will be threatened, all of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/europe-news"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Europe}}}\uc2  will be threatened.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/article/2024/jun/06/d-day-anniversary-biden"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 D-day: Biden calls for supporting Ukraine in struggle against \u8216\'20\'18dark forces\u8217\'20\'19}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  criticized the international criminal court last month, after its chief prosecutor, Karim Kham, requested arrest warrants for two of Israel\u8217\'20\'19s top leaders over their actions during the war in Gaza.\par \par \uc2 That did not sit well with actor George Clooney, whose wife, \uc2 Amal Clooney\uc2 , worked on the case. He called up the White House to make his displeasure known, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/2024/06/06/george-clooney-biden-criminal-court-israel/?utm_campaign=wp_main&utm_medium=social&utm_source=twitter"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Washington Post reports}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 Clooney called Steve Ricchetti, counselor to the president, to express concern about Biden\u8217\'20\'19s denunciation of arrest warrants sought by \uc2 ICC\uc2  prosecutors for Israeli Prime Minister \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2  and Defense Minister Yoav Gallant, especially his use of the word \u8220\'20\'1Coutrageous.\u8221\'20\'1D The prosecutors also sought warrants for top \uc2 Hamas\uc2  leaders.\par \par \uc2 The actor was also upset about the administration\u8217\'20\'19s initial openness to imposing sanctions on the \uc2 ICC\uc2  because his wife might be subject to the penalties, the people said, speaking on the condition of anonymity to discuss a private conversation.\par \par \uc2 Clooney\u8217\'20\'19s call came just weeks before he is set to appear at a fundraiser for Biden\u8217\'20\'19s reelection campaign next Saturday in Los Angeles. His concerns spread throughout Biden\u8217\'20\'19s orbit, leaving some officials to worry that the high-profile actor would withdraw from participating in the marquee fundraiser, which will also feature former president \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2 , late-night TV host Jimmy Kimmel and actress Julia Roberts.\par \par \uc2 Biden has supported Israel\u8217\'20\'19s response to the 7 October 2023 \uc2 Hamas\uc2  attack, despite a wave of protests from activists upset by the civilian toll caused the invasion of Gaza. Here\u8217\'20\'19s more about why the president objected to the \uc2 ICC\uc2  chief prosecutor\u8217\'20\'19s arrest warrant application:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/may/20/biden-icc-warrant-netanyahu"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Biden attacks request by ICC prosecutor for Netanyahu arrest warrant}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.50pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.23pm BST\par \par \uc2 Johnson\u8217\'20\'19s statement comes after a recent report {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/world/2024/06/06/israel-hamas-war-news-gaza-palestine-rafah/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 from the Washington Post}}}\uc2  which revealed that Israeli fighter jets used US munitions to strike a \uc2 UN\uc2  school located in Gaza on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 Two weapons experts verified the weapons\u8217\'20\'19 type to the Post, using footage of debris from the attack.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more from the Post\u8217\'20\'19s Louisa Loveluck, Niha Masih, Hajar Harb, Kyle Melnick and Miriam Berger:\par \par \uc2 Israeli fighter jets appear to have used US-made munitions in a strike that killed dozens of people inside a \uc2 UN\uc2  school in the central {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/world/2023/10/09/gaza-strip-israel-hamas-explained/?itid=lk_inline_manual_2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Gaza Strip}}}\uc2  on Thursday, according to two weapons experts who examined verified footage from the debris.\par \par \uc2 The nose cones of two GBU-39 small diameter bombs were visible in footage taken by an eyewitness, Emad Abu Shawish, in the aftermath of the strike in the Nuseirat refugee camp. His images were verified by Storyful and independently geolocated by the \uc2 Washington Post\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 An \uc2 Israel Defense Forces\uc2  spokesman said the strikes targeted a gathering of militants at the school. But the facility was also packed with thousands of civilians displaced by the war, according to the \uc2 United Nations Relief and Works Agency\uc2 , which aids Palestinian refugees.\par \par \uc2 The Gaza Health Ministry said 40 people were killed, including 14 children and nine women, and 74 others were wounded. Khalil al-Degran, spokesman for the al-Aqsa Martyrs Hospital in nearby Deir al-Balah, said that the bodies of children killed in the strike were brought to his facility.\par \par \uc2 Read the full article {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/world/2024/06/06/israel-hamas-war-news-gaza-palestine-rafah/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2  (paywall).\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.25pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.02pm BST\par \par \uc2 Johnson\u8217\'20\'19s demand for Biden came after Israel launched airstrikes against a refugee camp in Rafah during the Memorial Day weekend, an attack that killed dozens of people and was widely condemned by the international community.\par \par \uc2 Here are Johnson\u8217\'20\'19s full remarks, available {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://naacp.org/articles/naacp-calls-biden-harris-administration-halt-weapons-shipments-israel-push-immediate-and"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 NAACP\uc2  has, and continues to express our profound sympathy to civilians whose lives have been unjustly impacted in the crossfire of conflict. What happened on October 7 was a tragedy, and it is our hope that those with loved ones still in captivity are reunited as expeditiously as possible.\par \par \uc2 As the nation\u8217\'20\'19s leading civil rights organization, it is our responsibility to speak out in the face of injustice and work to hold our elected officials accountable for the promises they\u8217\'20\'19ve made. Over the past months, we have been forced to bear witness to unspeakable violence, affecting innocent civilians, which is unacceptable. The most recent statement from the Biden administration is useful but does not go far enough. It is one thing to call for a ceasefire, it is another to take the measures necessary to work towards liberation for all. Decades of conflict reflect that factions inside Israel and \uc2 Hamas\uc2  actively work against resolution of the conflict. The latest proposal must clarify the consequences of continued violence. The United States and the international community must be willing to pull the levers of power when appropriate to advance liberation for all.\par \par \uc2 The Middle East conflict will only be resolved when the \uc2 US government\uc2  and international community take action, including limiting access to weapons used against civilians. The \uc2 NAACP\uc2  calls on President Biden to draw the red line and indefinitely end the shipment of weapons and artillery to the state of Israel and other states that supply weapons to \uc2 Hamas\uc2  and other terrorist organizations. It is imperative that the violence that has claimed so many civilian lives, immediately stop. \uc2 Hamas\uc2  must return the hostages and stop all terrorist activity. Israel must commit to an offensive strategy that is aligned with international and humanitarian laws. Peace and security for Israelis and Palestinians can only align when the humanity and common needs of people within the region are respected. Centuries of conflict reflect that violence results in more violence. The spillover effect in the United States is more racism, antisemitism and Islamophobia.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.13pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.37pm BST\par \par \uc2 The president of the \uc2 NAACP\uc2  (\uc2 National Association for the Advancement of Colored People\uc2 ) has asked \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  to end the shipment of all weapons and artillery to Israel, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/DerrickNAACP/status/1798735604487766283"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in a new post to X}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Derrick Johnson\uc2 , who has led the civil rights organization since 2017, made the demand as more than 35,000 Palestinian people have been killed by Israel\u8217\'20\'19s attacks against the territory.\par \par \uc2 Johnson said:\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19re calling on [Biden] to draw the red line and end the shipment of all weapons and artillery to Israel. It is imperative that the violence that has claimed so many civilian lives comes to an end immediately.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.22pm BST\par \par \uc2 The day so far\par \par \uc2 Almost two years after he was first found guilty of contempt of Congress for defying a subpoena from the January 6 committee, a federal judge today {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jun/06/biden-supreme-court-trump-abortion-politics-latest-updates?page=with:block-6661e2fb8f0872aaf435ba69#block-6661e2fb8f0872aaf435ba69"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ordered}}}\uc2 Steve Bannon\uc2 , an influential figure in \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s Maga movement, to begin serving his four-month sentence by 1 July. In a defiant speech outside the courthouse, he {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jun/06/biden-supreme-court-trump-abortion-politics-latest-updates?page=with:block-6661eac88f0872aaf435bb1d#block-6661eac88f0872aaf435bb1d"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 accused}}}\uc2  the justice department of using his case to retaliate against Trump, and predicted a big win for Republicans in the November presidential election. Speaking of Trump, the former president {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jun/06/biden-supreme-court-trump-abortion-politics-latest-updates?page=with:block-6661cbab8f082030798b1bc4#block-6661cbab8f082030798b1bc4"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 gave an interview}}}\uc2  to Fox News last night, where he argued he \u8220\'20\'1Cwould have every right to go after\u8221\'20\'1D political adversaries like \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , if he is returned to the White House. In response, the Biden campaign said Trump was \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jun/06/biden-supreme-court-trump-abortion-politics-latest-updates?page=with:block-6661ce2a8f08a6bac2fa9afe#block-6661ce2a8f08a6bac2fa9afe"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 visibly rattled}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D by his conviction last week on felony business fraud charges.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else has happened today so far:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The supreme court{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jun/06/biden-supreme-court-trump-abortion-politics-latest-updates?page=with:block-6661c7318f08ee6323fd8cfb#block-6661c7318f08ee6323fd8cfb"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 released}}}\uc2  a new batch of opinions, which did not include much-awaited decisions on Trump\u8217\'20\'19s petition for immunity from federal prosecution over his 2020 election meddling, and two cases dealing with \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jun/06/biden-supreme-court-trump-abortion-politics-latest-updates?page=with:block-6661b87f8f08a6bac2fa9992#block-6661b87f8f08a6bac2fa9992"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 called for}}}\uc2  the supreme court to overturn his conviction on felony charges connected to falsifying documents related to hush-money payments made ahead of the 2016 election.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s federal gun charges trial {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/jun/06/biden-supreme-court-trump-abortion-politics-latest-updates?page=with:block-6661dabf8f08a6bac2fa9bd5#block-6661dabf8f08a6bac2fa9bd5"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 continues}}}\uc2  in Delaware, with testimony from the widow of his late brother, \uc2 Beau Biden\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.04pm BST\par \par \uc2 'This is about shutting down the Maga movement,' Bannon says after judge orders him to jail\par \par \uc2 Speaking outside the courthouse, \uc2 Steve Bannon\uc2  vowed to appeal his jail sentence to the supreme court, and accused the justice department of pursuing him as a way to retaliate against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey\u8217\'20\'19re not going to shut up Trump, they\u8217\'20\'19re not going to shut up Navarro, they\u8217\'20\'19re not going to shut up Bannon, and they\u8217\'20\'19re certainly not going to shut up Maga,\u8221\'20\'1D said Bannon. He was referring to \uc2 Peter Navarro\uc2 , a former Trump White House trade adviser, who is serving {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/mar/19/trump-adviser-peter-navarro-prison"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a similar prison sentence}}}\uc2  on contempt of Congress charges.\par \par \uc2 Bannon went on to predict an overwhelming victory in the November presidential election:\par \par \uc2 All of this is about one thing. This is about shutting down the Maga movement, shutting down grassroots conservatives, shutting down President Trump. Not only are we winning, we are going to prevail, and every number and every poll shows that. There\u8217\'20\'19s nothing that can shut me up and nothing that will shut me up \u8230\'20\'26 There\u8217\'20\'19s not a prison built, or a jail built that will ever shut me up.\par \par \uc2 All victory to Maga. We\u8217\'20\'19re going to win this, we\u8217\'20\'19re going to win at the supreme court, and more importantly, we\u8217\'20\'19re going to win on November 5 an amazing landslide, with the Senate, the House and also \uc2 Donald J Trump\uc2  back as president United States.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.22pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.54pm BST\par \par \uc2 After a federal judge revoked \uc2 Steve Bannon\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s bail and ordered him to begin serving his prison term by 1 July, he held a brief press conference outside Washington DC\u8217\'20\'19s federal courthouse.\par \par \uc2 Before he began speaking, a protester holding up a sign reading \u8220\'20\'1Clock him up\u8221\'20\'1D shouted \u8220\'20\'1CGet out of my way\u8221\'20\'1D at Bannon\u8217\'20\'19s security guards, who were keeping him away from the former Donald Trump White House adviser.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.58pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.27pm BST\par \par \uc2 Judge orders \uc2 Steve Bannon\uc2  to begin prison sentence by 1 July\par \par \uc2 A federal judge has ordered \uc2 Steve Bannon\uc2 , a far-right strategist and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  ally, to report to prison by 1 July to begin serving his sentence for contempt of Congress, Reuters reports.\par \par \uc2 Bannon was convicted in 2022 for ignoring a summons from the bipartisan House committee that investigated the January 6 insurrection, and his four-month sentence was upheld by an appeals court last month. Here\u8217\'20\'19s more on the long-running legal saga:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/may/10/steve-bannon-january-6-appeal-conviction"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Court upholds Steve Bannon\u8217\'20\'19s January 6 contempt of Congress conviction}}}\par \par \uc2 This post has been corrected to note that Bannon must begin serving his sentence by 1 July, not on 1 July.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.27pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.14pm BST\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, in Congress, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has orchestrated the appointment of two allies to the House intelligence committee, which deals with some of the most sensitive information the \uc2 US government\uc2  possesses. Here\u8217\'20\'19s more, from the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/roberttait"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Robert Tait}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 Two far-right Republicans have been appointed to the highly sensitive House of Representatives intelligence committee at the direction of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , a move likely to antagonise the security establishment.\par \par \uc2 Representatives Scott Perry of Pennsylvania and \uc2 Ronny Jackson\uc2  of Texas, known for their fierce loyalty to Trump and vocal support of his efforts to overturn the 2020 presidential election result, were installed by the House speaker, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/mike-johnson"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Mike Johnson}}}\uc2 , ahead of other qualified GOP members and apparently without consulting the body\u8217\'20\'19s chair, \uc2 Mike Turner\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Turner has sought to restore the committee\u8217\'20\'19s bipartisan character following years of bitter party infighting between {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republicans}}}\uc2  and Democrats.\par \par \uc2 The appointments of Perry and Jackson to a committee that helps to shape US foreign policy and oversees intelligence agencies such as the \uc2 FBI\uc2  and the CIA has caused consternation on Capitol Hill. It also signals Trump\u8217\'20\'19s hostility to organisations that he has vowed to purge if he is re-elected.\par \par \uc2 Adam Kinzinger\uc2 , a former Republican congressman who served on the House select committee that investigated the 6 January 2021 attack on the US Capitol, called the move \u8220\'20\'1Cinsane\u8221\'20\'1D on a social media post.\par \par \uc2 The pair were appointed to slots opened up by the resignations from Congress of \uc2 Mike Gallagher\uc2  of Wisconsin and Chris Stewart of Utah.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jun/06/house-intelligence-committee-far-right-republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 House speaker appoints two Trump loyalists to intelligence committee}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.18pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.53pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is also dealing with some unwelcome legal attention. His son, \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2 , is on trial in Delaware on federal gun charges, and the Associated Press reports that the widow of the president\u8217\'20\'19s late son \uc2 Beau Biden\uc2  took the stand today:\par \par \uc2 Testifying in \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s federal gun trial, Hallie Biden \u8211\'20\'13 the widow of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s oldest son, Beau \u8211\'20\'13 described panicking after finding a gun in his truck.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI panicked and I wanted to get rid of them,\u8221\'20\'1D she testified about finding a gun and ammunition in the console of \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s truck in October 2018.\par \par \uc2 Prosecutor Leo Wise asked why she panicked, and Hallie responded: \u8220\'20\'1CBecause I didn\u8217\'20\'19t want him to hurt himself, and I didn\u8217\'20\'19t want my kids to find it and hurt themselves.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Hallie said she considered hiding the gun but thought her kids might find it. She then decided to throw it away.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI was afraid to touch it. I didn\u8217\'20\'19t know if it was loaded,\u8221\'20\'1D Hallie said.\par \par \uc2 She put the gun in a leather pouch, stuffed it in a shopping bag, and tossed it in a trash can outside an upscale grocery market near her house.\par \par \uc2 The prosecution played surveillance footage showing Hallie dumping the gun in the trash.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jun/06/hallie-biden-testifies-hunter-biden-gun-trial"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Hallie Biden, widow of president\u8217\'20\'19s elder son, testifies in Hunter Biden gun trial}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.32pm BST\par \par \uc2 While \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s felony business fraud trial in New York concluded last week with a guilty verdict, other prosecutions of the former president have stalled. Yesterday, an appeals court in Georgia put his trial on election fraud charges on hold, likely until after the 2024 election, the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/george-chidi"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 George Chidi}}}\uc2  reports:\par \par \uc2 The Georgia court of appeals has put a hold on the trial of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  and other defendants while it considers whether to disqualify the Fulton county district attorney, \uc2 Fani Willis\uc2 , the lead prosecutor in the case.\par \par \uc2 Trump {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/may/08/fani-willis-georgia-trump-case-appeal"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 had appealed}}}\uc2  an order by the Fulton county superior court judge Scott McAfee that declined to disqualify Willis after bombshell revelations about a romantic relationship with her chosen special prosecutor. As part of their effort to dismiss the case, Trump and his co-defendants alleged Willis\u8217\'20\'19s relationship meant she should be recused from the case.\par \par \uc2 On Monday, the appeals court selected a three-judge panel to hear the appeal and docketed the case to be heard in October. Then on Wednesday, the court paused the case while this argument plays out.\par \par \uc2 Both Trump\u8217\'20\'19s attorney Steve Sadow and a spokesperson for Willis\u8217\'20\'19s office declined to comment on the court\u8217\'20\'19s order.\par \par \uc2 The order staying the case in Fulton county essentially ensures that the former president will not be tried on charges of election interference and racketeering in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/state-of-georgia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Georgia}}}\uc2  before the November election.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe history books will look back on what the country lost by not having a televised trial before November 2024 and historians will wonder what Fani Wills was thinking. And they\u8217\'20\'19ll just scratch their heads,\u8221\'20\'1D said Anthony Michael Kreis, a constitutional law professor in Georgia and a close observer of the case. \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t know how much Judge McAfee could have done between now and the appeal\u8217\'20\'19s pendency anyway. But the real loss is McAfee\u8217\'20\'19s ability to deal with the question of presidential immunity and the supremacy clause over the summer.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jun/05/trump-georgia-appeals-court-pauses-election-interference-case"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Court pauses Trump\u8217\'20\'19s Georgia election case as it mulls disqualifying prosecutor}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.37pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.08pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden campaign says Trump 'visibly rattled following his felony conviction'\par \par \uc2 In response to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s insistence that he could \u8220\'20\'1Cgo after\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and other political adversaries if re-elected, the Democratic president\u8217\'20\'19s campaign said it indicated that the former president was \u8220\'20\'1Cvisibly rattled\u8221\'20\'1D by his felony conviction last week.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTonight in prime time, America saw \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  consumed by rage and visibly rattled following his felony conviction; a man who has clearly snapped and whose candidacy is becoming more dangerous by the day,\u8221\'20\'1D said Michael Tyler, the Biden campaign\u8217\'20\'19s communications director.\par \par \uc2 He continued:\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is so consumed with personal grievance that he does not care who he hurts so long as \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  benefits. That\u8217\'20\'19s why he sicced a violent mob on the Capitol in an attempt to overturn the 2020 election he lost; that\u8217\'20\'19s why he\u8217\'20\'19s pledging to rule as a dictator and calling for a bloodbath; that\u8217\'20\'19s why he thinks the extreme state level \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans he made possible are \u8216\'20\'18a beautiful thing to watch\u8217\'20\'19. It\u8217\'20\'19s why the American people voted for \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  over \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  to begin with and why Trump can never step foot back in the Oval Office ever again.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.38pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.51pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump says 'I would have every right to go after' adversaries if re-elected\par \par \uc2 Days after a New York City jury {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/may/30/trump-trial-hush-money-verdict"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 found him guilty}}}\uc2  of 34 felony charges for falsifying his business records to conceal hush-money payments made ahead of the 2016 election, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  on Wednesday said he would have the power to retaliate against \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and other political adversaries, if he returns to the presidency.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CLook, when this election is over, based on what they\u8217\'20\'19ve done, I would have every right to go after them, and it\u8217\'20\'19s easy, because it\u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and you see all the criminality, all of the money that\u8217\'20\'19s going into the family and him, all of this money from China, from Russia, from Ukraine,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.foxnews.com/media/trump-addresses-concerns-he-would-seek-retribution-i-would-have-every-right-go-after-them"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in an interview}}}\uc2  with Fox News conservative commentator \uc2 Sean Hannity\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Trump appears to suggest he would pursue corruption charges against Biden. House Republicans have tried for years to prove that the president has profited illicitly from his family\u8217\'20\'19s overseas business dealings, but {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/sep/28/biden-impeachment-hearing-house-republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 have yet to turn up proof}}}\uc2 . Last year, they {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/dec/13/biden-impeachment-house-vote-republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 began the process}}}\uc2  of impeaching Biden, but have yet to bring the charges up for a vote, in part because they have not been able to find evidence to support them.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.54pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.32pm BST\par \par \uc2 The opinions released by the supreme court today concerned lower -profile matters before the justices.\par \par \uc2 They have yet to weigh in on \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s claim of immunity from the federal charges brought against him for trying to overturn the 2020 election, conservative challenges to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  drug mifepristone, and the Biden administration\u8217\'20\'19s policy that federally funded hospitals must carry out emergency abortions, even in states with bans on the procedure.\par \par \uc2 The supreme court has lately been issuing batches of opinions once per week, and we will let you know when we find out the date of its next release.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.36pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.13pm BST\par \par \uc2 The final opinion of the day is Becerra v San Carlos Apache Tribe, which deals with the \uc2 Indian Health Service\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s financial obligations.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.supremecourt.gov/opinions/23pdf/23-250_2dp3.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The decision}}}\uc2  brought together an ideologically motley group of justices: the chief justice, \uc2 John Roberts\uc2 , wrote the opinion, which was joined by fellow conservative \uc2 Neil Gorsuch\uc2 . The court\u8217\'20\'19s three liberals, \uc2 Sonia Sotomayor\uc2 , Elana Kagan and \uc2 Ketanji Brown Jackson\uc2 , also signed on.\par \par \uc2 The other conservatives, \uc2 Amy Coney Barrett\uc2 , \uc2 Samuel Alito\uc2  and \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2 , dissented in an opinion written by \uc2 Brett Kavanaugh\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.24pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.07pm BST\par \par \uc2 The second case is Connelly v United States, which deals with taxation and life insurance.\par \par \uc2 Conservative justice \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2  wrote {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.supremecourt.gov/opinions/23pdf/23-146_i42j.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the court\u8217\'20\'19s opinion}}}\uc2 , which was unanimous.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.04pm BST\par \par \uc2 The first case is Truck Insurance Exchange v Kaiser Gypsum Company, which deals with US bankruptcy law.\par \par \uc2 Liberal justice \uc2 Sonia Sotomayor\uc2  wrote {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.supremecourt.gov/opinions/23pdf/22-1079_868c.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the court\u8217\'20\'19s opinion}}}\uc2 , which all justices joined except for conservative \uc2 Samuel Alito\uc2 , who did not take part in deciding the case.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.08pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 Supreme court to release latest batch of decisions\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s almost 10am in Washington DC, which means the supreme court will release its latest decision, or decisions.\par \par \uc2 As always, we do not know in advance which cases they will release their opinions on, but we will follow the decisions\u8217\'20\'19 release on this live blog.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.53pm BST\par \par \uc2 Top Senate Republican suggests Democratic lawmakers should face 'discipline' for pressuring court\par \par \uc2 As Senate majority leader, \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  played a major role in creating the conservative supermajority on the supreme court, by confirming \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s rightwing justices and blocking Barack Obama from appointing a liberal judge in 2016.\par \par \uc2 Republicans are now in the minority in the Senate, but McConnell still leads the party, and he is not happy with Democratic senators who have called for \uc2 Samuel Alito\uc2  to recuse himself from cases concerning the 2020 election, or for the chief justice, \uc2 John Roberts\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/live/2024/may/30/supreme-court-trump-immunity-abortion-biden-updates?page=with:block-6658c81e8f08834dc312857a#block-6658c81e8f08834dc312857a"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 to sit down}}}\uc2  for a meeting to discuss the court\u8217\'20\'19s ethics.\par \par \uc2 In a speech on the chamber\u8217\'20\'19s floor yesterday, McConnell warned that two of the Democratic senators calling for the court to (so far unsuccessfully) act, Sheldon Whitehouse of Rhode Island and Richard Blumenthal of Connecticut, could face \u8220\'20\'1Cdiscipline\u8221\'20\'1D because they are lawyers who have been admitted to the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s bar.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more from McConnell:\par \par \uc2 Three of our colleagues have taken it upon themselves to write to the chief justice and demand Justice Alito\u8217\'20\'19s recusal in cases. One went so far as to tell the chief that he should strip Justices Alito and Thomas of the ability to write majority opinions unless they recuse from the cases liberals don\u8217\'20\'19t want them hearing.\par \par \uc2 This goes beyond the standard disgraceful bullying my Democratic colleagues have perfected. Recusal is a judicial act.\par \par \uc2 These senators are telling the chief justice, privately, to change the course of pending litigation. This is known as ex parte communication and it is frowned upon by the ABA\u8217\'20\'19s Model Code of Judicial Conduct.\par \par \uc2 This matters because at least two of these colleagues of ours, the junior senator from Rhode Island and the senior senator from Connecticut, seem to be members of the supreme court bar. If so, they are, therefore, potentially engaged in unethical professional conduct before the court.\par \par \uc2 They may be under the mistaken impression that their persistent attempts to threaten the federal courts are a permissible use of their legislative office.\par \par \uc2 But they are officers of the court and bound by a different set of rules than a mere senator. These rules provide for discipline against those who engage in \u8216\'20\'18conduct unbecoming\u8217\'20\'19 an officer of the court.\par \par \uc2 I might suggest to our colleagues that unethical ex parte communications seeking to change the course of pending litigation is such conduct. And that the court should take any remedial action it feels to be appropriate.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.57pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.30pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump calls on supreme court to intervene after felony conviction\par \par \uc2 As president, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  created the conservative supermajority on the supreme court by appointing three rightwing justices who have since supported decisions overturning the constitutional right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and weakening firearm protections and environmental regulations.\par \par \uc2 When the court heard arguments over Trump\u8217\'20\'19s petition for immunity from the federal charges against him for allegedly conspiring to overturn the election, those same justices {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/25/supreme-court-trump-immunity-claim"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 seemed open}}}\uc2  to a ruling that will likely have the net effect of further delaying his federal trial, perhaps until after the November election. And after he was convicted last week of felony business fraud charges, the president openly appealed to the court to throw the conviction out. \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/roberttait"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Robert Tait}}}\uc2  has more:\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has called on the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/us-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US supreme court}}}\uc2  to step in and annul his guilty verdict in a hush-money trial that left him with the unwanted distinction of being the first former US president to be a convicted felon.\par \par \uc2 The 2024 presumptive Republican nominee made his plea in a typically florid post on his Truth Social site, highlighting that a sentencing hearing scheduled for 11 July falls just four days before the GOP\u8217\'20\'19s national convention in Milwaukee, when his nomination is expected to become official.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe \u8216\'20\'18Sentencing\u8217\'20\'19 for not having done anything wrong will be, conveniently for the Fascists, 4 days before the Republican National Convention,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump wrote. \u8220\'20\'1CA Radical Left Soros backed D.A., who ran on a platform of \u8216\'20\'18I will get Trump,\u8217\'20\'19 reporting to an \u8216\'20\'18Acting\u8217\'20\'19 Local Judge, appointed by the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.huffpost.com/news/topic/democratic-party"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Democrats}}}\uc2 , who is HIGHLY CONFLICTED, will make a decision which will determine the future of our Nation?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 A jury in Manhattan found the ex-president guilty last Thursday on all 34 counts of falsifying documents to conceal a sexual liaison with an adult film actor, Stormy Daniels, in the run-up to the 2016 presidential election, which Trump won over \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The verdict, which Trump has pledged to appeal, raised the atmosphere in this year\u8217\'20\'19s presidential campaign to fever pitch more than five months before polling day, with Republicans circling the wagons while Democrats sought ways to exploit it.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jun/03/trump-conviction-supreme-court-annul"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump calls on supreme court to annul his guilty verdict in hush-money case}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.09pm BST\par \par \uc2 Supreme court could upend \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access and give Trump immunity with new rulings\par \par \uc2 Good morning, US politics blog readers.\par \par \uc2 The supreme court will issue another batch of decisions this morning at 10am ET, and a host of hot-button issues are pending before the conservative-dominated bench. While there is no telling in advance which cases the justices will weigh in on, they have yet to decide a case that could see the availability of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/mar/26/us-supreme-court-abortion-pill-case-mifepristone"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  drug mifepristone}}}\uc2  rolled back, and another over whether the Biden administration can require states with bans on the procedure to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/2024/apr/24/us-supreme-court-abortion-rights-emtala"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 perform emergency abortions}}}\uc2  at federally funded hospitals. But perhaps the most controversial case pending before the supreme court is \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/25/supreme-court-trump-criminal-trial-immunity-key-takeaways"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 petition for immunity}}}\uc2  from the federal election meddling charges brought against him by special prosecutor Jack Smith. It is a divisive matter not only because the case involves the former president and presumptive Republican nominee, but also because one of the justices on the bench, \uc2 Samuel Alito\uc2 , was reported to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/article/2024/may/29/samuel-alito-upside-down-flag"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 have flown flags}}}\uc2  sympathetic to Trump\u8217\'20\'19s cause at two of his properties.\par \par \uc2 Democrats are outraged by Alito\u8217\'20\'19s conduct, but last week the conservative justice said he {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/article/2024/may/29/samuel-alito-flag-jan-6-recusal"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 would not recuse himself}}}\uc2  from that case or any other dealing with the 2020 election. Should the Trump case be decided today, how Alito rules will be one of the most closely watched elements. We\u8217\'20\'19ll let you know if that happens.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else is going on today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2 , the Republican Senate minority leader, suggested Democratic senators who pressured the supreme court to act on Alito\u8217\'20\'19s flag flap should face \u8220\'20\'1Cdiscipline\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is marking the 80th anniversary of D-day with a visit to Normandy. He\u8217\'20\'19s speaking now, and you can follow it live {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2024/jun/06/d-day-80th-anniversary-2024-veterans-second-world-war-normandy-joe-biden"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump once again made clear that he would use his powers \u8220\'20\'1Cto go after\u8221\'20\'1D his political opponents, if elected, in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.foxnews.com/media/trump-addresses-concerns-he-would-seek-retribution-i-would-have-every-right-go-after-them"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 an interview}}}\uc2  yesterday with Fox News.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.30pm BST\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240606ek66002by\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
