\par\par \uc2 Law\par \b \uc2 Supreme court chief justice declines to meet US senators about Alito upside-down flag furor \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Chris Stein \par \uc2 5,462 \uc2 words\par \uc2 30 May 2024\par 20:26 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 This live blog is now closed. You can read our latest US politics coverage hereSee all our US politics coverage\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 Closing summary\par \par \uc2 The Biden campaign {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/live/2024/may/30/supreme-court-trump-immunity-abortion-biden-updates?page=with:block-6658ac2f8f08834dc31283b6#block-6658ac2f8f08834dc31283b6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 launched a new attack}}}\uc2  against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , accusing him of racism after a former producer on The Apprentice {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/live/2024/may/30/supreme-court-trump-immunity-abortion-biden-updates?page=with:block-66589b288f086b8009a03ef2#block-66589b288f086b8009a03ef2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said he used}}}\uc2  an anti-Black slur on the set. Meanwhile, jury deliberations {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/live/2024/may/30/supreme-court-trump-immunity-abortion-biden-updates?page=with:block-6658834a8f08834dc31280f5#block-6658834a8f08834dc31280f5"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 are ongoing}}}\uc2  in Trump\u8217\'20\'19s business fraud trial in New York City, and a verdict could be delivered at anytime. Earlier in the day, the supreme court {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/live/2024/may/30/supreme-court-trump-immunity-abortion-biden-updates?page=with:block-6658a8c78f08b090cee99a9f#block-6658a8c78f08b090cee99a9f"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 released a batch}}}\uc2  of new opinions, covering topics from banking regulation to free speech rights. But the conservative-dominated court did not yet weigh in on Trump\u8217\'20\'19s claim of immunity from prosecution over the 2020 election, or two \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -related cases, all of which remain pending before the justices. Another batch of opinions {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/live/2024/may/30/supreme-court-trump-immunity-abortion-biden-updates?page=with:block-6658a4958f08834dc3128332#block-6658a4958f08834dc3128332"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 is expected}}}\uc2  next Thursday.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else happened today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Jamie Raskin, a Democratic congressman and Trump antagonist, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/live/2024/may/30/supreme-court-trump-immunity-abortion-biden-updates?page=with:block-66587d188f08b090cee997d2#block-66587d188f08b090cee997d2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 proposed}}}\uc2  a way to force conservative justices \uc2 Samuel Alito\uc2  and \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2  to recuse themselves from January 6 cases.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 John Roberts\uc2 , the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s chief justice, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/live/2024/may/30/supreme-court-trump-immunity-abortion-biden-updates?page=with:block-6658c1808f08b090cee99c38#block-6658c1808f08b090cee99c38"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 declined a request}}}\uc2  for a meeting from two Democratic senators concerned over Alito\u8217\'20\'19s flag flap.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Do swing state voters care if Trump is convicted in his New York business fraud trial? Our reporters {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/live/2024/may/30/supreme-court-trump-immunity-abortion-biden-updates?page=with:block-66589fe08f08b090cee999c9#block-66589fe08f08b090cee999c9"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 searched}}}\uc2  for the answer.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Most evidence in the New York case {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/live/2024/may/30/supreme-court-trump-immunity-abortion-biden-updates?page=with:block-6658834a8f08834dc31280f5#block-6658834a8f08834dc31280f5"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 seems to point}}}\uc2  to Trump\u8217\'20\'19s guilt, but the jury could reach a variety of conclusions.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump can sue his niece Mary Trump for potentially violating the terms of a settlement over his father\u8217\'20\'19s estate, a New York state appeals court {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/live/2024/may/30/supreme-court-trump-immunity-abortion-biden-updates?page=with:block-6658b2958f08b090cee99b42#block-6658b2958f08b090cee99b42"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ruled}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.01pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.43pm BST\par \par \uc2 Should \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  win the November election, the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/roberttait"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Robert Tait}}}\uc2  reports that his ally, speaker of the House Mike Johnson, is prepared to move quickly to pass his agenda through Congress. Here\u8217\'20\'19s what Johnson told Semafor he is looking at:\par \par \uc2 Mike Johnson, the speaker of the US {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/house-of-representatives"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 House of Representatives}}}\uc2 , is planning a sweeping ideological legislative drive that aims to make \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Cthe most consequential president of the modern era\u8221\'20\'1D if the Republicans win power in November.\par \par \uc2 A far-reaching bill containing a range of policy priorities at once \u8211\'20\'13 including tax cuts worth trillions, border security and rolling back Obamacare \u8211\'20\'13 is being prepared to avoid the mistakes the GOP believed happened early in Trump\u8217\'20\'19s first term, when Johnson says the party wasted time because its victory over Hillary Clinton took it by surprise.\par \par \uc2 In an interview with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.semafor.com/article/05/29/2024/speaker-mike-johnson-promises-a-republican-mega-bill-that-would-define-donald-trumps-second-term"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Semafor}}}\uc2 , Johnson said he had already spoken to Trump about introducing an omnibus package immediately after he retakes office.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI told him that I believe he can be the most consequential president of the modern era, if we are focused on a policy and agenda-driven administration and Congress \u8211\'20\'13 and that\u8217\'20\'19s our intention,\u8221\'20\'1D Johnson said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe don\u8217\'20\'19t want to make the mistake that we made in the past. Back in the 2017 timeframe and in previous years, we {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republicans}}}\uc2  kind of took a single-subject approach. We did one round of healthcare reform, one round of tax reform. But for [fiscal year 2025], we want to have a much larger scope, multiple issues to address in addition to the expiration of the Tax Cuts and Jobs Act.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/may/30/mike-johnson-republican-bill-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Mike Johnson plans Republican mega-bill ready to push through if Trump wins}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.29pm BST\par \par \uc2 For the second time in as many days, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has defended supreme court justice \uc2 Samuel Alito\uc2  amid criticism from Democrats over his display of flags associated with rightwing causes.\par \par \uc2 Alito, an appointee of Republican president \uc2 George W Bush\uc2 , is a reliably conservative vote on the court, and Trump has loudly denounced the Democratic lawmakers who have called for him to recuse himself from cases dealing with January. Here\u8217\'20\'19s what the ex-president wrote, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://truthsocial.com/@realDonaldTrump/posts/112531120840909855"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 on Truth Social}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Playing the Ref\u8217\'20\'19 with Justice Alito doesn\u8217\'20\'19t work. It works with many others, but not with him!\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.32pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.07pm BST\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more from the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/edpilkington"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ed Pilkington}}}\uc2  about the firestorm around conservative supreme court justice \uc2 Samuel Alito\uc2 , and the rightwing flags found flying at his residences:\par \par \uc2 Justice \uc2 Samuel Alito\uc2  is rejecting calls to step aside from supreme court cases involving the former president {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  and January 6 defendants because of the controversy over flags that flew over his homes.\par \par \uc2 In letters to members of Congress on Wednesday, Alito says his wife was responsible for flying an upside-down US flag over his home in 2021 and an \u8220\'20\'1CAppeal to Heaven\u8221\'20\'1D flag at his New Jersey beach house last year.\par \par \uc2 Neither incident merits his recusal, he wrote.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI am therefore duty-bound to reject your recusal request,\u8221\'20\'1D he wrote.\par \par \uc2 The court is considering two major cases related to the 6 January 2021 attack by a mob of Trump supporters on the Capitol, including charges faced by the rioters and whether the former president has immunity from prosecution on election-interference charges.\par \par \uc2 Alito has rejected calls from Democrats in the past to recuse on other issues.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/article/2024/may/29/samuel-alito-flag-jan-6-recusal"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Alito refuses to step aside from Trump supreme court cases amid flag scandal}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.46pm BST\par \par \uc2 In his letter to the Democratic leaders of the Senate judiciary committee, supreme court chief justice \uc2 John Roberts\uc2  argued it would be inappropriate to meet with them.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI must respectfully decline your request for a meeting,\u8221\'20\'1D wrote Roberts, who was appointed by Republican president \uc2 George W Bush\uc2 , and is considered among the more moderate of the court\u8217\'20\'19s conservative justices.\par \par \uc2 He continued in the letter addressed to the committee\u8217\'20\'19s chair Dick Durbin and senator Sheldon Whitehouse, who chairs the subcommittee on federal courts:\par \par \uc2 As noted in my letter to Chairman Durbin last April, apart from ceremonial events, only on rare occasions in our Nation\u8217\'20\'19s history has a sitting Chief Justice met with legislators, even in a public setting (such as a Committee hearing) with members of both major political parties present. Separation of powers concerns and the importance of preserving judicial independence counsel against such appearances. Moreover, the format proposed \u8211\'20\'13 a meeting with leaders of only one party who have expressed an interest in matters currently pending before the Court \u8211\'20\'13 simply underscores that participating in such a meeting would be inadvisable.\par \par \uc2 Last week, the two Democrats {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.durbin.senate.gov/newsroom/press-releases/durbin-whitehouse-request-meeting-with-chief-justice-roberts-urge-roberts-to-ensure-justice-alito-recuses-himself-in-2020-election-cases#:~:text=Durbin%2C%20Whitehouse%20Request%20Meeting%20With,Himself%20In%202020%20Election%20Cases"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 had requested a meeting}}}\uc2  with Roberts, after reports emerged that conservative justice \uc2 Samuel Alito\uc2  had flown flags associated with rightwing causes at two of his properties.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe therefore call for Justice Alito to recuse himself from certain proceedings as outlined above, renew our call for the Supreme Court to adopt an enforceable code of conduct for Supreme Court justices, and request a meeting with you as soon as possible. Until the Court and the Judicial Conference take meaningful action to address this ongoing ethical crisis, we will continue our efforts to enact legislation to resolve this crisis,\u8221\'20\'1D Durbin and Whitehouse wrote to Roberts.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.55pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.29pm BST\par \par \uc2 Supreme court chief justice declines request from US senators to meet about Alito conduct\par \par \uc2 John Roberts\uc2 , the chief justice of the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2 , has rebuffed a request from senior Democratic US senators to meet as the lawmakers push for supreme court justice \uc2 Samuel Alito\uc2  to recuse himself from cases before the court that relate to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and will ripple into the 2024 presidential election.\par \par \uc2 Roberts declined an invitation to talk about supreme court ethics and the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/article/2024/may/25/samuel-alito-upside-down-us-flag"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 controversy over flags}}}\uc2  that flew outside homes owned by Alito, the Associated Press further reports.\par \par \uc2 Roberts\u8217\'20\'19 response came in a letter to Democratic senators Dick Durbin a day after Alito separately wrote to them and House of Representatives members to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/article/2024/may/29/samuel-alito-flag-jan-6-recusal"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reject their demands}}}\uc2  that he recuse himself from major cases involving Trump and the January 6 rioters because of the flags, which are like those carried by some rioters at the 6 January 2021 attack on the US Capitol.\par \par \uc2 Senate judiciary committee chair Dick Durbin of Illinois and senator and committee member Sheldon Whitehouse of Rhode Island had written Roberts a week ago to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/may/23/aoc-samuel-alito-flag-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ask for the meeting}}}\uc2  and ask that Roberts take steps to ensure that Alito recuses himself from any cases before the court concerning the January 6 attack or former president Trump\u8217\'20\'19s attempts to overturn his 2020 election defeat.\par \par \uc2 Trump, the \uc2 Guardian\uc2  adds, is being prosecuted in a federal criminal case on charges relating to election interference and obstructing an official proceeding. The supreme court will rule next month on two cases before it that have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/mar/19/trump-lawyers-us-supreme-court-immunity"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 grave implications}}}\uc2  in that case, and for the election.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.07pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.11pm BST\par \par \uc2 A recap that a year ago a judge in New York {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/may/03/donald-trump-lawsuit-new-york-times-mary-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 threw out}}}\uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s 2021 lawsuit accusing New York Times reporters of an \u8220\'20\'1Cinsidious plot\u8221\'20\'1D to obtain his tax records.\par \par \uc2 Trump was ordered to pay all attorneys\u8217\'20\'19 fees and legal expenses that the Times and its reporters had incurred. The lawsuit alleged that the newspaper sought out Trump\u8217\'20\'19s niece Mary Trump and persuaded her \u8220\'20\'1Cto smuggle the records out of her attorney\u8217\'20\'19s office\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 At the time, Trump\u8217\'20\'19s claim against his niece had not been ruled on. Today, we learned that Donald is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/live/2024/may/30/supreme-court-trump-immunity-abortion-biden-updates?page=with:block-6658b2958f08b090cee99b42#block-6658b2958f08b090cee99b42"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 permitted to proceed}}}\uc2  with suing Mary.\par \par \uc2 The Times\u8217\'20\'19s 2018 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2018/10/02/us/politics/donald-trump-tax-schemes-fred-trump.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Pulitzer-winning}}}\uc2  stories relied on information from Mary Trump to cast doubt on the ex-president\u8217\'20\'19s claims that he was a self-made millionaire, showing that he had inherited hundreds of millions through \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2019/05/07/us/politics/donald-trump-taxes.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 dubious tax schemes}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D. The series also revealed a history of tax avoidance.\par \par \uc2 Robert Reed, the New York supreme court justice, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.documentcloud.org/documents/23796793-trump-v-trump-decision"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  at the time of his ruling, in May 2023, that Trump\u8217\'20\'19s claims \u8220\'20\'1Cfail as a matter of constitutional law\u8221\'20\'1D, which allows for reporters to engage in legal, ordinary news-gathering. \u8220\'20\'1CThese actions are at the very core of protected first amendment activity,\u8221\'20\'1D Reed wrote.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.17pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 Alina Habba, a lawyer for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , said the former president looked forward to holding his niece, Mary Trump, \u8220\'20\'1Cfully accountable for her blatant and egregious breach of contract\u8221\'20\'1D in her exchanges with \uc2 New York Times\uc2  journalists for a story about her uncle\u8217\'20\'19s finances and evasive tax habits.\par \par \uc2 Thursday\u8217\'20\'19s decision upheld a June 2023 ruling by Justice Robert Reed of the New York state supreme court.\par \par \uc2 Also, Reed had dismissed \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s claims against the \uc2 New York Times\uc2  and three reporters, and in January ordered him to pay $392,639 of their legal fees, Reuters reports.\par \par \uc2 In November 2022, Reed dismissed Mary Trump\u8217\'20\'19s separate lawsuit accusing her uncle and two of his siblings of defrauding her out of a multimillion-dollar inheritance.\par \par \uc2 The New York Times\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 reporting challenged \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s claim that he was a self-made billionaire. It said he received the equivalent of $413m from his father, largely the result of \u8220\'20\'1Cdubious\u8221\'20\'1D tax schemes in the 1990s, including undervaluing his family\u8217\'20\'19s real estate holdings. \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has denied wrongdoing.\par \par \uc2 Mary Trump previously identified herself as a Times source in her 2020 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2020/jul/07/donald-trump-abuse-father-niece-mary-book"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 tell-all bestseller}}}\uc2  Too Much and Never Enough: How My Family Created the World\u8217\'20\'19s Most Dangerous Man.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.31pm BST\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more on the news that a court has said \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  can sue his niece Mary Trump.\par \par \uc2 The court in New York ruled that the former president can sue Mary Trump, 59, a psychologist and writer, for supplying information to the \uc2 New York Times\uc2  as part of its coverage into the then president\u8217\'20\'19s finances and his alleged effort to avoid taxes. The coverage won the Pulitzer prize.\par \par \uc2 The appellate division in Manhattan found a \u8220\'20\'1Csubstantial\u8221\'20\'1D legal basis for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  to claim that his niece violated confidentiality provisions of a 2001 settlement over the estate of his father, \uc2 Fred Trump Sr\uc2 , Reuters reports.\par \par \uc2 A five-judge panel said it was unclear whether Mary Trump\u8217\'20\'19s disclosures were subject to confidentiality, or how long both sides intended the provisions to remain in effect. It also signaled that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  might deserve only minimal damages, not the $100m he sought.\par \par \uc2 The court said:\par \par \uc2 At a minimum, nominal damages may still be available on the breach of contract claim even in the absence of actual damages.\par \par \uc2 Lawyers for Mary Trump said the lawsuit violated a state law barring frivolous cases designed to silence critics and \u8220\'20\'1Cchill and retaliate against\u8221\'20\'1D their free speech. These cases are called strategic lawsuits against public participation, or Slapps.\par \par \uc2 Anne Champion, Mary Trump\u8217\'20\'19s lawyer, said in a statement:\par \par \uc2 Mary has made valuable contributions to the public\u8217\'20\'19s knowledge of the former president with her unique perspective as a family member. We are confident she will be vindicated as the case proceeds.\par \par \uc2 Champion also said \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Ccan claim no injury for the publication of truthful information.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.18pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  can sue niece over NY Times article, court rules\par \par \uc2 A New York state appeals court said \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  can sue his niece Mary Trump for giving the \uc2 New York Times\uc2  information for its Pulitzer Prize-winning 2018 probe into his finances and his alleged effort to avoid taxes.\par \par \uc2 The appellate division in Manhattan found a \u8220\'20\'1Csubstantial\u8221\'20\'1D legal basis for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  to claim that his niece violated confidentiality provisions of a 2001 settlement over the estate of his father, \uc2 Fred Trump Sr\uc2 , Reuters reports.\par \par \uc2 More to come on this. Adding from the Guardian, Trump originally {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/22/donald-trump-sues-niece-new-york-times-tax-story"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sued}}}\uc2  his estranged niece and the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/media/new-york-times"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 New York Times}}}\uc2  in 2021 over a 2018 story about his family\u8217\'20\'19s wealth and tax practices that was partly based on confidential documents she provided to the newspaper\u8217\'20\'19s reporters, and there has been a whole legal odyssey ever since.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.22pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.05pm BST\par \par \uc2 The day so far\par \par \uc2 The Biden campaign has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/live/2024/may/30/supreme-court-trump-immunity-abortion-biden-updates?page=with:block-6658ac2f8f08834dc31283b6#block-6658ac2f8f08834dc31283b6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 launched a new attack}}}\uc2  against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , accusing him of racism after a former producer on The Apprentice {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/live/2024/may/30/supreme-court-trump-immunity-abortion-biden-updates?page=with:block-66589b288f086b8009a03ef2#block-66589b288f086b8009a03ef2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said he used}}}\uc2  an anti-Black racial slur on the set. Meanwhile, jury deliberations {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/live/2024/may/30/supreme-court-trump-immunity-abortion-biden-updates?page=with:block-6658834a8f08834dc31280f5#block-6658834a8f08834dc31280f5"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 are ongoing}}}\uc2  in Trump\u8217\'20\'19s business fraud trial in New York City, and a verdict could be delivered at anytime. Earlier in the day, the supreme court {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/live/2024/may/30/supreme-court-trump-immunity-abortion-biden-updates?page=with:block-6658a8c78f08b090cee99a9f#block-6658a8c78f08b090cee99a9f"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 released a batch}}}\uc2  of new opinions, covering topics from banking regulation to free speech rights. But the conservative-dominated court did not yet weigh in on Trump\u8217\'20\'19s claim of immunity from prosecution over the 2020 election, or two \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -related cases, all of which remain pending before the justices. Another batch of opinions {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/live/2024/may/30/supreme-court-trump-immunity-abortion-biden-updates?page=with:block-6658a4958f08834dc3128332#block-6658a4958f08834dc3128332"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 is expected}}}\uc2  next Thursday.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else has happened today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Jamie Raskin, a Democratic congressman and Trump antagonist, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/live/2024/may/30/supreme-court-trump-immunity-abortion-biden-updates?page=with:block-66587d188f08b090cee997d2#block-66587d188f08b090cee997d2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 proposed}}}\uc2  a way to force conservative justices \uc2 Samuel Alito\uc2  and \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2  to recuse themselves from January 6 cases.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Do swing state voters care if Trump is convicted in his New York business fraud trial? Our reporters {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/live/2024/may/30/supreme-court-trump-immunity-abortion-biden-updates?page=with:block-66589fe08f08b090cee999c9#block-66589fe08f08b090cee999c9"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 searched}}}\uc2  for the answer.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Most evidence in the New York case {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/live/2024/may/30/supreme-court-trump-immunity-abortion-biden-updates?page=with:block-6658834a8f08834dc31280f5#block-6658834a8f08834dc31280f5"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 seems to point}}}\uc2  to Trump\u8217\'20\'19s guilt, but the jury could rule in any direction.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.43pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden campaign slams Trump as 'textbook racist' after reported use of slur on Apprentice set\par \par \uc2 In a statement, the Biden campaign\u8217\'20\'19s Black media director, Jasmine Harris, accused \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  of racism after a former producer on The Apprentice accused him of using a racial slur on set:\par \par \uc2 No one is surprised that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , who entered public life by falsely accusing Black men of murder and entered political life spreading lies about the first Black president, reportedly used the N-word to casually denigrate a successful Black man. Anyone notice a pattern? \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is exactly who Black voters know him to be: a textbook racist who disrespects and attacks the Black community every chance he gets, and the most ignorant man to ever run for president. It\u8217\'20\'19s why Black voters kicked him out of the White House in 2020, and it\u8217\'20\'19s why they\u8217\'20\'19ll make him a loser a second time this November.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.47pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.28pm BST\par \par \uc2 In addition to handing the \uc2 National Rifle Association\uc2  a lifeline in its lawsuit against New York state, the supreme court also denied resentencing to an Arizona man on death row, the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/joannawalters"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Joanna Walters}}}\uc2  reports:\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/us-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US supreme court}}}\uc2  issued opinions on Thursday relating to free speech and the death penalty, in one case clearing the way for a \uc2 National Rifle Association\uc2  ( {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/nra"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 NRA}}}\uc2  ) lawsuit against a former New York state official.\par \par \uc2 The court gave a boost to the influential gun rights group that has accused the official of coercing banks and insurers to avoid doing business with it and, in the process, violating the \uc2 NRA\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s free speech rights.\par \par \uc2 The justices, in a unanimous decision from the nine-member bench, threw out a lower court\u8217\'20\'19s ruling that dismissed the \uc2 NRA\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s 2018 lawsuit against \uc2 Maria Vullo\uc2 , a former superintendent of New York\u8217\'20\'19s department of financial services.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 NRA\uc2 , in the case \uc2 NRA\uc2  v Vullo, claimed that Vullo unlawfully retaliated against it following a mass shooting in which 17 people were {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/florida-school-shooting"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 killed at a high school in Parkland}}}\uc2 , Florida.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 NRA\uc2  was represented by the \uc2 American Civil Liberties Union (ACLU)\uc2 , and the Biden administration argued some of its claims should go forward, an unusual alliance between often opposing parties considering the \uc2 NRA\uc2  is a strongly Republican-aligned organization.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the supreme court, in a 6-3 decision, struck down an appeals court ruling giving Danny Lee Jones a new sentencing hearing in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cronkitenews.azpbs.org/2024/04/17/state-asks-supreme-court-to-reject-new-trial-for-arizona-death-row-inmate/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 death penalty case}}}\uc2  in Arizona. The conservative supermajority decided that errors in Jones\u8217\'20\'19s legal defense, in the case Thornell v Jones, did not justify him having a chance at resentencing.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/article/2024/may/30/us-supreme-court-nra-free-speech"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US supreme court boosts NRA in free speech ruling while denying man on death row resentencing}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.32pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.10pm BST\par \par \uc2 The supreme court just scheduled its next opinion release day.\par \par \uc2 The court is expected to issue more decisions on Thursday, 6 June. Among the pending cases is \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s claim of immunity from prosecution over trying to overturn the 2020 election, and two lawsuits related to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.53pm BST\par \par \uc2 If a New York jury finds Trump guilty of business fraud charges, what impact would it have on the election? Reporting from two swing states, the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/alice-herman"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Alice Herman}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/george-chidi"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 George Chidi}}}\uc2  looked for the answer:\par \par \uc2 For Josh Ellis, a refrigerator technician from southern Wisconsin, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s trial in New York is a sideshow. He\u8217\'20\'19s not convinced of the prosecution\u8217\'20\'19s narrative, or the former president\u8217\'20\'19s \u8211\'20\'13 and the verdict will not likely affect his vote in November, anyway.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBiden\u8217\'20\'19s running this country into the ground,\u8221\'20\'1D said Ellis, who said the economy is his main concern. At 49, Ellis has long viewed politicians as out-of-touch on economic issues; he used to vote for Democrats, but switched in 2016 to vote for Trump, who he saw as possibly offering a change.\par \par \uc2 The jurors in Trump\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/new-york"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 New York}}}\uc2  trial are deliberating over the question of whether or not Trump unlawfully falsified business records to hide a sex scandal before the 2016 election \u8211\'20\'13 and it\u8217\'20\'19s not clear how much of an impact their verdict will have on voters, despite the historic nature of a possible conviction.\par \par \uc2 Like Ellis, voters across the country seem ambivalent about Trump\u8217\'20\'19s criminal charges.\par \par \uc2 Denise White, who helps manage a social services agency in Atlanta, wears her cynicism about the trial like armor.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CPrivilege,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CPatriarchy. All of that is on full display right now. And I am not confident that there will be a just outcome.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/may/30/trump-hush-money-trial-voters-opinions"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18It\u8217\'20\'19s bullshit\u8217\'20\'19: voters on what Trump\u8217\'20\'19s hush-money case means to them}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.54pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 Former Apprentice producer accuses Trump of using racial slur\par \par \uc2 A former producer on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2020/sep/29/trump-tax-returns-the-apprentice-empire"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The Apprentice}}}\uc2 , the reality show \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  hosted prior to going into politics, recounted that the then New York real estate mogul used a racial slur in a recorded conversation.\par \par \uc2 Trump used the word when discussing Kwame Jackson, a Black finalist on the show who at the time was working at investment bank \uc2 Goldman Sachs\uc2 , writes Bill Pruitt in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://slate.com/culture/2024/05/donald-trump-news-2024-trial-verdict-apprentice.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a piece for Slate}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18I think Kwame would be a great addition to the organization,\u8217\'20\'19 Kepcher says to Trump, who winces while his head bobs around in reaction to what he is hearing and clearly resisting.\par \par \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Why didn\u8217\'20\'19t he just fire her?\u8217\'20\'19 Trump asks, referring to Omarosa. It\u8217\'20\'19s a reasonable question. Given that this the first time we\u8217\'20\'19ve ever been in this situation, none of this is something we expected.\par \par \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18That\u8217\'20\'19s not his job,\u8217\'20\'19 Bienstock says to Trump. \u8216\'20\'18That\u8217\'20\'19s yours.\u8217\'20\'19 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s head continues to bob.\par \par \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18I don\u8217\'20\'19t think he knew he had the ability to do that,\u8217\'20\'19 Kepcher says. Trump winces again.\par \par \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Yeah,\u8217\'20\'19 he says to no one in particular, \u8216\'20\'18but, I mean, would America buy a [N-word] winning?\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 Kepcher\u8217\'20\'19s pale skin goes bright red. I turn my gaze toward Trump. He continues to wince. He is serious, and he is adamant about not hiring Jackson.\par \par \uc2 Pruitt says he is coming forward with his story now because a non-disclosure agreement he signed when coming onto the show expired. For his part, a spokesman for Trump, \uc2 Steven Cheung\uc2 , told Slate, \u8220\'20\'1CThis is a completely fabricated and bullshit story that was already peddled in 2016\u8221\'20\'1D and which is only coming to light now because Democrats are \u8220\'20\'1Cdesperate\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.45pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.11pm BST\par \par \uc2 The supreme court will likely announce more opinions sometime in June. Meanwhile, in New York City, jurors are on their second day of deliberations in \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s business fraud trial. \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/victoria-bekiempis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Victoria Bekiempis}}}\uc2  reports on two notes sent by the jury to the court, that may offer hints at how their discussions are going:\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s criminal hush-money case in New York enters its second day of jury deliberations on Thursday with panelists weighing whether a payment to the adult film star Stormy Daniels was part of a plot to sway the 2016 election.\par \par \uc2 The jurors deliberated for approximately four and a half hours on Wednesday after beginning their discussions at about 11.30am.\par \par \uc2 Outside of the courtroom on Wednesday, Trump ranted about the proceedings and likened himself to a saint, claiming in the hallway: \u8220\'20\'1CMother Teresa could not beat these charges. The charges are rigged. The whole thing is rigged.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Earlier in the day, the jury sent two notes to the court in the afternoon. One missive was a request to hear some trial testimony from two key witnesses. The second message was a request to re-hear Judge Juan Merchan\u8217\'20\'19s instructions to them.\par \par \uc2 After receiving more information from jurors about which instructions they wanted re-read, Merchan went through the requested directives: they wanted guidance about how to interpret evidence and draw inferences from facts.\par \par \uc2 The jurors seemed attentive during Merchan\u8217\'20\'19s re-reading. Some scribbled on notepads. Others eyed Merchan intently as he read through the instructions. One sometimes handled a pen in a way that seemingly hearkened back to the purpose of a fidget spinner; using the writing implement as passive physical activity while paying attention to Merchan and jotting notes.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/may/30/trump-trial-jury"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump trial jury continues deliberations in New York hush-money case}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.49pm BST\par \par \uc2 In a unanimous opinion, the supreme court allowed a lawsuit brought against the New York state government by the \uc2 National Rifle Association\uc2  to proceed on free speech grounds.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/nra-aclu-parkland-shooting-lawsuit-supreme-court-953424f3fd33f279b0cc2ce050069d48"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 from the Associated Press}}}\uc2  on the court\u8217\'20\'19s decision in \uc2 National Rifle Association\uc2  of America v Vullo:\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/hub/us-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The Supreme Court}}}\uc2  on Thursday cleared the way for a \uc2 National Rifle Association\uc2  lawsuit against a former New York state official over claims she violated its free-speech rights.\par \par \uc2 The unanimous opinion reverses a lower-court decision tossing out the gun rights group\u8217\'20\'19s lawsuit against ex-\uc2 New York state Department of Financial Services\uc2  Superintendent \uc2 Maria Vullo\uc2 . It does not, however, shield the \uc2 NRA\uc2  and other advocacy groups from regulation, Justice \uc2 Sonia Sotomayor\uc2  said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CUltimately, the critical takeaway is that the First Amendment prohibits government officials from wielding their power selectively to punish or suppress speech, directly or (as alleged here) through private intermediaries,\u8221\'20\'1D she wrote.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 NRA\uc2  said Vullo pressured banks and insurance companies to blacklist it after {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/hub/parkland-florida-school-shooting"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the school shooting}}}\uc2  in Parkland, Florida, that left 17 people dead in 2018. The group was represented by \uc2 the American Civil Liberties Union\uc2 , and the Biden administration argued some of its claims should go forward.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.53pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump immunity and \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  decisions yet to come after supreme court rules on three other cases\par \par \uc2 The supreme court has finished releasing opinions for the day, without weighing in on \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s immunity claim, or the two \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -related cases pending before the justices.\par \par \uc2 The court issued two unanimous decisions, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.supremecourt.gov/opinions/23pdf/22-529_1b7d.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 one dealing}}}\uc2  with banking regulations, and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.supremecourt.gov/opinions/23pdf/22-842_6kg7.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the other}}}\uc2  regarding a free speech claim made in a lawsuit between the \uc2 National Rifle Association\uc2  and the New York department of financial services.\par \par \uc2 Its {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.supremecourt.gov/opinions/23pdf/22-982_bq7d.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 third decision}}}\uc2  was a 6-3 split between the conservative supermajority and the liberal minority, and reversed an appeals court decision in a death penalty case.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.45pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.12pm BST\par \par \uc2 The supreme court has issued two opinions so far, both on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.supremecourt.gov/opinions/23pdf/22-529_1b7d.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 less}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.supremecourt.gov/opinions/23pdf/22-842_6kg7.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 politically charged}}}\uc2  matters before the court.\par \par \uc2 Further decisions are expected, and we will let you know what they are.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.57pm BST\par \par \uc2 Supreme court to begin release of opinions\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s nearly 10am in Washington DC, which means the supreme court will begin releasing opinions or, at least, an opinion, shortly.\par \par \uc2 We only find out which cases they have decided when the opinions come out. While the conservative-dominated court could issue its much-awaited decisions on \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s immunity claim, emergency abortions or the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill mifepristone, it could also issue opinions on other less anticipated \u8211\'20\'13 but still important \u8211\'20\'13 cases.\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19ll know for sure in a few minutes.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.59pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, in New York City, jurors will continue deliberating over whether \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is guilty of falsifying business records to conceal hush-money payments ahead of the 2016 election. \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/hugo-lowell"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Hugo Lowell}}}\uc2  reports that prosecutors have presented a mass of evidence pointing to his guilt \u8211\'20\'13 but whether jurors will agree is, as always, an open question:\par \par \uc2 As the jury began deliberations on Wednesday, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  appeared to have little room to extricate himself from the mass of evidence presented in the weeks-long case.\par \par \uc2 A recording of Trump directing hush money to be paid in cash. Handwritten notes by Trump\u8217\'20\'19s ex-chief financial officer about how to reimburse Cohen. A parade of witnesses who testified the Trump campaign was desperate to suppress the story of his affair with the adult film star {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/stormy-daniels"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Stormy Daniels}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 That evidence fitted in to the Manhattan district attorney\u8217\'20\'19s case that Trump caused false entries to be made in the \uc2 Trump Organization\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s business records and that the falsifications were done as part of a plot to influence the outcome of the 2016 presidential election.\par \par \uc2 Trump has pleaded not guilty to 34 counts of felony falsification of business records. And the jury will now have to decide whether prosecutors proved their case beyond a reasonable doubt, or whether the Trump\u8217\'20\'19s defense lawyers poked enough holes in the prosecution\u8217\'20\'19s case.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/may/30/trump-jurors-hush-money-case"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump with little room to extricate himself from mass of evidence in hush-money case}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.56pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.28pm BST\par \par \uc2 Top Democratic congressman proposes way to force Alito, Thomas off January 6 cases\par \par \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/dec/13/clarence-thomas-trump-immunity-case-conflict-of-interest"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wife called}}}\uc2  for the 2020 election to be overturned. \uc2 Samuel Alito{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/article/2024/may/29/samuel-alito-flag-jan-6-recusal"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 had rightwing flags flying}}}\uc2  at two of his properties. Yet both conservative justices are set to rule on \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s claim of immunity from prosecution for his election meddling, despite calls from Democrats that they step back from that and other cases because they are conflicted.\par \par \uc2 In {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/article/2024/may/29/samuel-alito-flag-jan-6-recusal"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 an opinion essay}}}\uc2  published in the \uc2 New York Times\uc2 , Democratic congressman Jamie Raskin, a prominent Trump antagonist in the House of Representatives, proposed a novel way to force the two justices off the case:\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 US Department of Justice\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 including the US attorney for the District of Columbia, an appointed US special counsel and the solicitor general, all of whom were involved in different ways in the criminal prosecutions underlying these cases and are opposing Mr Trump\u8217\'20\'19s constitutional and statutory claims \u8211\'20\'13 can petition the other seven justices to require Justices Alito and Thomas to recuse themselves not as a matter of grace but as a matter of law.\par \par \uc2 The Justice Department and Attorney General \uc2 Merrick Garland\uc2  can invoke two powerful textual authorities for this motion: the Constitution of the United States, specifically the due process clause, and the federal statute mandating judicial disqualification for questionable impartiality, 28 USC Section 455. The Constitution has come into play in several recent Supreme Court decisions striking down rulings by stubborn judges in lower courts whose political impartiality has been reasonably questioned but who threw caution to the wind to hear a case anyway. This statute requires potentially biased judges throughout the federal system to recuse themselves at the start of the process to avoid judicial unfairness and embarrassing controversies and reversals.\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19ll have to see if the justice department takes him up on this strategy. Meanwhile, the Trump immunity case could be among those released at 10am ET, when the supreme court issues decisions.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.37pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.05pm BST\par \par \uc2 Supreme court to release opinions with Trump immunity, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  cases pending\par \par \uc2 Good morning, US politics blog readers. Right off the bat this morning, at 10am ET, the supreme court will issue opinions, potentially on some of the closely watched cases the justices have yet to rule on. Among these is \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/25/supreme-court-trump-criminal-trial-immunity-key-takeaways"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 petition for immunity}}}\uc2  from the federal charges brought against him for trying to overturn the 2020 election, as well as a pair of cases dealing with \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access. One concerns whether the Biden administration {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/2024/apr/24/us-supreme-court-abortion-rights-emtala"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 can require}}}\uc2  hospitals in states with strict bans on the procedure to perform the procedure in emergencies, and the other deals with a conservative effort to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/mar/26/us-supreme-court-abortion-pill-case-mifepristone"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 roll back the availability}}}\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill mifepristone. With six conservative justices and three liberal justices, the court has a pronounced rightwing tilt, but plenty of uncertainty remains, and, as alway, we do not know in advance which cases they will rule on, or how many opinions they will issue.\par \par \uc2 A ruling in the Trump case would present an interesting split-screen with the scene in New York, where jurors are beginning their second day of deliberations in his business fraud trial. There\u8217\'20\'19s no telling when they will reach a verdict, but however they find the former president will undoubtedly send shockwaves through the 2024 election campaign.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else is happening today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A group of Senate Democrats are demanding the justice department investigate oil companies and executives after the \uc2 Federal Trade Commission\uc2  accused a former petroleum executive of colluding to raise gas prices.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is spending the day in his home state of Delaware, after yesterday making a push to rally Black voters by holding a rare joint rally with \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  in Philadelphia.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Jamie Raskin, a Democratic congressman, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2024/05/29/opinion/alito-thomas-recuse-trump-jan-6.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 argued in the New York Times}}}\uc2  that there is a way to force conservative supreme court justices \uc2 Samuel Alito\uc2  and \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2  to recuse themselves from cases dealing with the 2020 election, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/dec/13/clarence-thomas-trump-immunity-case-conflict-of-interest"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 amid}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/article/2024/may/29/samuel-alito-flag-jan-6-recusal"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports}}}\uc2  of their connections to rightwing causes.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.06pm BST\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240530ek5u001ut\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
