\par\par \uc2 World news\par \b \uc2 Texas Republicans open to death penalty for  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  providers\b0\par\par\uc2 Carter Sherman \par \uc2 631 \uc2 words\par \uc2 30 May 2024\par 20:13 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 GOP convention votes on wide-ranging platform including striking law protecting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers from being charged with murder\par \par \uc2 Texas Republicans are open to applying the death penalty to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers, a new proposal from the state party indicates.\par \par \uc2 Over the weekend, during the Texas GOP convention, Republican delegates voted on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.texastribune.org/2024/05/28/texas-gop-convention-elections-religion-delegates-platform/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a party platform for 2024}}}\uc2  that proclaims \u8220\'20\'1C\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is not healthcare, it is homicide\u8221\'20\'1D and suggests striking a state law that protects \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers from being charged with homicide. In Texas, capital murder is punishable by the death penalty. Killing a child under the age of 15 can {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://statutes.capitol.texas.gov/Docs/PE/htm/PE.19.htm"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 qualify as capital murder}}}\uc2 , the most severe form of homicide.\par \par \uc2 Elsewhere in the platform, the Texas GOP calls for \u8220\'20\'1Clegislation to abolish \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  by immediately securing the right to life and equal protection of the laws to all preborn children from the moment of fertilization\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 That language, as highlighted by the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://jessica.substack.com/p/texas-gop-platform-endorses-death?utm_source=post-email-title&publication_id=11153&post_id=145040863&utm_campaign=email-post-title&isFreemail=true&r=39sef&triedRedirect=true&utm_medium=email"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 feminist writer Jessica Valenti}}}\uc2 , who first called attention to it earlier this week, draws from the rhetoric of \u8220\'20\'1C\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  abolitionists\u8221\'20\'1D, a fringe, hardline segment of the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  movement that has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/dec/14/abortion-abolitionist-oklahoma-fringe-victory-roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 inched closer to the mainstream in recent years}}}\uc2 . While the mainstream anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  movement typically supports exempting women seeking abortions from punishment, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  abolitionists adhere to what they consider a more consistent line of logic: if a fetus is a person and \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is murder, then \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  patients deserve to be punished like murderers.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  patients are not mentioned in the provision in the proposed platform that redefines \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  as homicide, making its implications for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  seekers unclear. \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans typically target \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers for punishment, not patients.\par \par \uc2 Punishing women for abortions is a politically toxic stance, particularly as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/article/2024/may/14/abortion-rights-support-poll"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 support for \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  rights has surged}}}\uc2  in the wake of the overturning of Roe v Wade. Even before Roe fell, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.texastribune.org/2021/03/09/texas-legislature-abortion-criminalize-death-penalty/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Texas lawmakers repeatedly introduced}}}\uc2  bills that would have instituted the death penalty for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  patients. They all stalled out in the Republican-dominated state legislature.\par \par \uc2 Regardless of the platform\u8217\'20\'19s implications for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  patients, adding language that in effect defines fetuses as people, complete with full legal rights and protections, could have vast implications for wide swaths of Texas law, including cutting off access to in vitro fertilization. Efforts to establish \u8220\'20\'1Cfetal personhood\u8221\'20\'1D have sped up in anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  circles in recent years, but {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/society/2024/mar/20/states-fetal-personhood-bill"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 experts say that the full implications}}}\uc2  of this ideology have never been realized. Earlier this year, IVF treatments in Alabama temporarily ground to a halt after the state supreme court {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/feb/21/alabama-ivf-embryo-extrauterine-children-ruling"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ruled frozen embryos}}}\uc2  were \u8220\'20\'1Cintrauterine children\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 As the home to one in 10 American women of reproductive age, Texas has long been a key laboratory for activists and lawmakers looking to fine-tune bills that restrict reproductive rights \u8211\'20\'13 many of which are exported to other state legislatures across the country.\par \par \uc2 In the 50-page platform, the Texas GOP also calls homosexuality an \u8220\'20\'1Cabnormal lifestyle choice\u8221\'20\'1D and says providing gender-affirming care to minors is \u8220\'20\'1Cchild abuse\u8221\'20\'1D. The platform demands that the recent renaming of military bases be reversed in order to \u8220\'20\'1Cpublicly honor the southern heroes\u8221\'20\'1D, and confirms the platform supports \u8220\'20\'1Caffirmation of God, including prayer, the Bible, and the Ten Commandments being returned to our schools, courthouses, and other government buildings\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Although Republicans voted over the weekend on the proposed platform, the votes were {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.texastribune.org/2024/05/25/texas-republican-party-convention-platform/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 set to be tallied this week}}}\uc2 . The Texas GOP did not immediately respond to a request for comment on whether the platform has been formally adopted or on its approach to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The party platform is not a legislative slate; these proposals may never make their way into bills, much less pass.\par \par \uc2 The Texas state legislature, which meets only in odd-numbered years, will open for business in January 2025.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240530ek5u002xq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
