\par\par \uc2 Opinion\par \b \uc2 Louisiana\u8217\'20\'19s move to criminalize  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  pills is cruel and medically senseless\b0\par\par\uc2 Moira Donegan \par \uc2 893 \uc2 words\par \uc2 29 May 2024\par 21:49 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Louisiana, with one of the US\u8217\'20\'19s worst maternal mortality rates, wants to make \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  medication a \u8216\'20\'18controlled substance\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 This week, Louisiana moved to expand the criminalization of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  further than any state has since before Roe v Wade was decided. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2024/05/23/us/politics/louisiana-abortion-pills-controlled-substances.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 On Thursday}}}\uc2 , the state legislature passed a bill that would reclassify mifepristone and misoprostol \u8211\'20\'13 the two drugs used in a majority of American abortions \u8211\'20\'13 as dangerous controlled substances.\par \par \uc2 Under both state and federal classifications, the category of controlled substances includes those medications known to cause mind-altering effects and create the potential for addictions, such as sedatives and opioids; \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  medications carry none of this potential for physical dependence, habit-forming or abuse. The move from Louisiana lawmakers runs counter to both established medical opinion and federal law. \uc2 Jeff Landry\uc2 , the anti-choice Republican governor, is expected to sign the bill. When he does, possession of mifepristone or misoprostol in Louisiana will come to carry large fines and up to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2024/05/23/louisiana-abortion-pill-criminal-penalties-00159735#:~:text=Louisiana%20lawmakers%20on%20Thursday%20approved,to%2010%20years%20in%20prison."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 10 years in prison}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Louisiana already has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://states.guttmacher.org/policies/louisiana/abortion-policies"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a total \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  ban}}}\uc2 , with no rape or incest exceptions. But the Louisiana lawmakers are pursuing this new additional criminalization measure because while \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans are very good at generating suffering for women, they are not very good at actually preventing abortions. Data from the \uc2 Guttmacher Institute\uc2  suggests that the United States saw an 11% increase in abortions between 2020 and 2023 \u8211\'20\'13 a possible indication that pregnant people are still managing to obtain abortions in spite of post-Dobbs bans. As was the case in the pre-Roe era, women have continued to seek out ways to end their pregnancies, even in defiance of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban laws.\par \par \uc2 In the pre-Roe era, illegal abortions were often unsafe, and \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans caused a public health crisis: many hospitals had to open {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.latimes.com/archives/la-xpm-2003-jan-21-me-patt21-story.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 septic \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  wards}}}\uc2 , where women who had had incompetent or careless illegal abortions were treated for frequently life-threatening conditions. But the post-Dobbs reality is that advances in communications technology and medicine mean that illegal abortions need no longer be unsafe ones. Now, women living in states with \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans can access safe, effective \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care in the comfort of their own homes, and often law enforcement and anti-choice zealots are none the wiser. Women can perform their own abortions, safely and effectively, without regard to the law\u8217\'20\'19s opinion on whether they should be free to. They can do this because they can access the pills.\par \par \uc2 The criminalization measure, then, is part of an expanding horizon of invasive, sadistic and burdensome state interventions meant to do the impossible: to stop women from trying to control their own lives. The Louisiana bill nominally will not apply to pregnant women \u8211\'20\'13 they\u8217\'20\'19re exempted from criminal punishments for possession of the medications. But it will take square aims at the vital, heroic efforts of feminists, medical practitioners and mutual aid networks that have been distributing the pills in Louisiana: the people who have adhered to the principles of bodily autonomy and women\u8217\'20\'19s self-determination even amid a hostile climate. These people\u8217\'20\'19s courage and integrity is the greatest threat to the anti-choice regime, and so it is these people whom Louisiana\u8217\'20\'19s new medical criminalization law will be used against first.\par \par \uc2 But pro-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights and women\u8217\'20\'19s rights activists are not the only ones who will be hurt by the new law. For one thing, the criminalization of possession is likely to scare many Louisiana \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  seekers out of ordering the pills online, even if the bill itself technically excludes them from prosecution. These \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  seekers, dissuaded and threatened out of seeking the most reliable and safe method of self-managed \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , may then turn to less safe options.\par \par \uc2 But the new drug classification also has implications for a wide array of healthcare treatments. Mifepristone and misoprostol are not only used in elective abortions. They are also the standard of care for spontaneous miscarriages \u8211\'20\'13 the management of which has already become {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.npr.org/sections/health-shots/2024/03/19/1239376395/louisiana-abortion-ban-dangerously-disrupting-pregnancy-miscarriage-care#:~:text=In%20the%20wake%20of%20Louisiana's,first%20made%20available%20to%20NPR."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 legally fraught}}}\uc2  for doctors in Louisiana, causing women to suffer needlessly and endanger their health. Misoprostol is used in labor, too, and in the treatment of some ulcers. The drugs\u8217\'20\'19 needless, cruel and medically senseless reclassification as \u8220\'20\'1Ccontrolled\u8221\'20\'1D substances will make these medical practices more difficult in a state that already has one of the worst rates of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2022/05/19/why-louisianas-maternal-mortality-rates-are-so-high-00033832"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 maternal mortality}}}\uc2  in the country. That\u8217\'20\'19s part of why more than {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://kyma.com/decision-2024/national-politics/2024/05/22/louisiana-state-representatives-passes-abortion-pill-bill/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 200 Louisiana physicians}}}\uc2  signed a letter opposing the bill.\par \par \uc2 The Republican legislators who have pushed the new criminalization do not pretend to actually believe that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  drugs are habit-forming. Thomas Pressly, the state senator who introduced the bill, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2024/05/23/louisiana-abortion-pill-criminal-penalties-00159735#:~:text=Louisiana%20lawmakers%20on%20Thursday%20approved,to%2010%20years%20in%20prison."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 frankly said}}}\uc2  that his aim was to \u8220\'20\'1Ccontrol the rampant illegal distribution of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -inducing drugs\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 But there is something to the notion that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access might be \u8220\'20\'1Chabit-forming\u8221\'20\'1D. In the Roe era, after all, women began to conceive of themselves as full persons, able to exercise control over their own destinies \u8211\'20\'13 as adults, that is, with all the privileges and entitlements of citizenship. They formed a habit of independence, a habit of imagining themselves as people entitled to freedom, equality, self-determination and respect. It is these habits that the Republican party is trying to break them of.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Moira Donegan is a Guardian US columnist\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240529ek5t001gv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
