\par\par \uc2 Opinion\par \b \uc2 Louisiana descends into dystopia with historic law on  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  pills\b0\par\par\uc2 Arwa Mahdawi \par \uc2 1,373 \uc2 words\par \uc2 25 May 2024\par 13:33 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 The state wasn\u8217\'20\'19t the best place to get pregnant in the first place, with some of the highest maternal mortality rates in the US\par \par \uc2 There\u8217\'20\'19s something rotten in the state of Louisiana\par \par \uc2 Louisiana is not a great place to get pregnant. If you need an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , a near-total ban means {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nola.com/news/healthcare_hospitals/abortion-is-now-banned-in-louisiana-here-s-what-you-need-to-know/article_ba416134-e8e7-11ec-b6e2-8f8cd0d27442.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 it\u8217\'20\'19s almost impossible}}}\uc2  to get one, even in cases of rape or incest \u8211\'20\'13 anyone who provides an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  deemed illegal can go to jail {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://phr.org/our-work/resources/louisiana-abortion-bans/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 for 15 years}}}\uc2 . And if you plan on having the baby, you have to deal with some of the highest {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2022/05/19/why-louisianas-maternal-mortality-rates-are-so-high-00033832"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 maternal mortality rates}}}\uc2  in the US. Although, as Senator \uc2 Bill Cassidy{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/news/nbcblk/cassidy-defends-statements-louisianas-black-maternal-health-statistics-rcna30166"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has helpfully noted}}}\uc2 , \u8220\'20\'1Cif you correct our population for race, we\u8217\'20\'19re not as much of an outlier as it\u8217\'20\'19d otherwise appear\u8221\'20\'1D. In other words, if you ignore Black people (a third of his constituents), things look a little better. So that\u8217\'20\'19s OK then!\par \par \uc2 This week, Louisiana decided to descend further into dystopia and passed a first-of-its-kind law {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/article/2024/may/23/mifepristone-misoprostol-abortion-pills-louisiana"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 making \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  pills a controlled substance}}}\uc2 . Senate Bill 276 makes possession of the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills mifepristone and misoprostol without a prescription punishable by up to 10 years in prison.\par \par \uc2 Republicans excel at using {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.rollingstone.com/politics/political-commentary/conservatives-rebranding-pro-life-abortion-1235018370/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sneaky}}}\uc2  tactics to undermine our rights, and this bill is no exception. When it was originally put forward, you see, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.legis.la.gov/legis/BillInfo.aspx?i=246533"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the bill}}}\uc2  didn\u8217\'20\'19t include the amendment that turns \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills into Schedule IV drugs \u8211\'20\'13 a classification normally given to dangerous or addictive substances. Rather, the bill was positioned as a way to protect pregnant people by making it a crime to intentionally give an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -inducing drug to a pregnant woman without her consent. Everyone can get behind that idea, right?\par \par \uc2 There was also an emotional story behind the legislation that made it easy to sell. Senator Thomas Pressly, the author of the bill, explained that his sister, Catherine Herring, had been slipped the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill by her soon-to-be-ex-husband. Various outlets have said that Herring then managed to save the baby through a \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.shreveporttimes.com/story/news/2024/03/06/shreveport-senator-files-bill-after-sisters-husband-tried-to-secretly-abort-baby-with-abortion-pill/72863621007/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 medical \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  reversal process}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D. KTBS, for example, a Louisiana media outlet, reported that Herring \u8220\'20\'1Cused a pill-reversal regimen and her baby is still alive\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 I\u8217\'20\'19m sorry \u8230\'20\'26 what? I\u8217\'20\'19m not a doctor but this story sounds medically implausible. Sara Pentlicky, who is a doctor (a gynecologist) and an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  provider, told me much the same thing.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf [Herring] took medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills and was still pregnant with a baby, the only explanation is that the pills didn\u8217\'20\'19t work, which is a possibility,\u8221\'20\'1D Pentlicky said when I ran the scenario past her. There are, however, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.acog.org/advocacy/facts-are-important/medication-abortion-reversal-is-not-supported-by-science"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 she notes}}}\uc2 , organizations that \u8220\'20\'1Cprescribe progesterone to people who have taken medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills with the false information that it can reverse the medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D. The New York {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2024/05/08/us/new-york-abortion-pill-lawsuit?cid=ios_app"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 attorney general}}}\uc2  is currently cracking down on these organizations, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.acog.org/advocacy/facts-are-important/medication-abortion-reversal-is-not-supported-by-science"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 and the American College of Obstetricians and Gynecologists}}}\uc2  has said the procedures are \u8220\'20\'1Cunproven and unethical\u8221\'20\'1D. They\u8217\'20\'19re also dangerous: a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/31809439/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 recent}}}\uc2  study looking at the effects of progesterone on people who had taken mifepristone was halted after \u8220\'20\'1Cthe third hemorrhage\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 To be clear, I\u8217\'20\'19m not saying Pressly is lying about what his sister went through: Herring\u8217\'20\'19s husband {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/abortion-texas-guilty-plea-sentence-c5e6a1b71ddf8cfdcf0258fb5b7bff23"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pleaded guilty}}}\uc2  to injuring a child and the assault of a pregnant person and was sentenced to six months in jail. But it does rather feel like Pressly has weaponized elements of his sister\u8217\'20\'19s story to position a regressive law as a way to protect women. That\u8217\'20\'19s certainly how it\u8217\'20\'19s being defended following a backlash to the law, anyway. On Friday, for example, Landry {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/JeffLandry/status/1794026844968145046"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 tweeted}}}\uc2  that safety was the motivation behind the bill. \u8220\'20\'1CProud to stand with our legislature to ensure this drug can be obtained legally and safely \u8211\'20\'13 ensuring the protection of all women. Without this bill, women and the unborn are more susceptible to predators,\u8221\'20\'1D Landry said.\par \par \uc2 Let\u8217\'20\'19s be very clear here: this isn\u8217\'20\'19t about protecting women at all. Rather it\u8217\'20\'19s about making \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills even more difficult to access in Louisiana than they already are. More than 200 doctors in Louisiana have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.axios.com/local/new-orleans/2024/05/23/louisiana-abortion-pills-controlled-substance"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 signed a letter}}}\uc2  to lawmakers warning that reclassification could provide a \u8220\'20\'1Cbarrier to physicians\u8217\'20\'19 ease of prescribing appropriate treatment\u8221\'20\'1D and cause unnecessary fear and confusion among patients and doctors. Which, of course, is exactly what anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  activists want.\par \par \uc2 Perhaps the most depressing aspect of all this is that it\u8217\'20\'19s almost certain that Louisiana has just set a dangerous new trend. As Pentlicky notes: \u8220\'20\'1CEvery time a state succeeds in passing any type of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restriction, we see other states follow suit \u8211\'20\'13 it just becomes more and more egregious.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In short, expect Louisiana\u8217\'20\'19s crackdown on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills to come to a red state near you soon.\par \par \uc2 Texas doctor who said nine-year-olds can safely give birth now on maternal mortality committee\par \par \uc2 Looks like Texas is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/may/23/texas-anti-abortion-activist"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 giving Louisiana a run for its money}}}\uc2  when it comes to the worst US state to be female.\par \par \uc2 British teacher charged with hate crime for calling Rishi Sunak and \uc2 Suella Braverman\uc2  \u8216\'20\'18coconuts\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 Marieha Hussain {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2024/5/21/uk-police-charge-pro-palestine-protester-behind-divisive-coconut-placard"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has been charged}}}\uc2  with a racially aggravated public order offence for a placard at a pro-Palestinian demonstration poking fun at the British prime minister and former home secretary by depicting them as coconuts. It\u8217\'20\'19s fair to debate whether the term \u8220\'20\'1Ccoconut\u8221\'20\'1D (which is used in British ethnic minority communities to mean someone brown outside and white inside) is offensive, but criminalizing a brown woman for using it to criticize two brown politicians who have thrown their weight behind racist policies is outrageous. Let\u8217\'20\'19s not forget that Sunak wants to deport {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/uk-news/2024/apr/22/rwanda-deportations-bill-passes-parliament-sunak#:~:text=Rishi%20Sunak's%20Rwanda%20deportation%20bill,dozens%20of%20people%20seeking%20asylum."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 asylum seekers to Rwanda}}}\uc2 , and, during her stint as home secretary, Braverman brought in dystopian anti-protest legislation that has just been {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/article/2024/may/21/suella-braverman-unlawfully-curbed-protest-protect-rights"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ruled unlawful and undemocratic}}}\uc2 . I can think of a lot worse things to call the pair of them than \u8220\'20\'1Ccoconuts\u8221\'20\'1D. This feels a lot like yet another way of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2024/5/21/uk-police-charge-pro-palestine-protester-behind-divisive-coconut-placard"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 punishing pro-Palestinian speech}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 What does \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  think about birth control?\par \par \uc2 On Tuesday, Trump suggested that he would be open to restricting access to birth control and would have a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/trump-contraception-birth-control-abortion-2024-8f73bb1b3a5864b24157f15eb272a3e6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 policy on that \u8220\'20\'1Cvery shortly\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2 . After a lot of alarmed headlines, he announced on Truth Social that: \u8220\'20\'1CI DO NOT SUPPORT A BAN ON BIRTH CONTROL.\u8221\'20\'1D The all-caps do not make this assurance any more convincing.\par \par \uc2 There\u8217\'20\'19s a new reality TV dating show called \u8216\'20\'18Virgin Island\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 You will be able to guess from the name {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/tv-and-radio/article/2024/may/23/virgin-island-dating-show-hulu-tv"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 exactly what Virgin Island is about}}}\uc2 . In other abstinence-related news, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/article/2024/may/21/celibacy-hetrosexual-women-boysober-4b-sex-positive-feminism"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 celibacy is very hot right now}}}\uc2 . And if a President Trump does outlaw birth control, I imagine it will become even more popular.\par \par \uc2 Epidural in labour can reduce risk of serious complications by 35%\par \par \uc2 A new study suggests expanding access to epidurals, particularly in women who are delivering prematurely, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/lifeandstyle/article/2024/may/22/epidural-in-labour-can-reduce-risk-of-serious-complications-by-35-study-finds"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 could improve maternal health}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Nicola Coughlan shows that you don\u8217\'20\'19t need to sacrifice your morals for success\par \par \uc2 I\u8217\'20\'19ve been delighted to watch {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/culture/nicola-coughlan"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Bridgerton actor}}}\uc2  (who got her big break in the amazing {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/tv-and-radio/2018/jan/19/derry-girls-channel-4-the-funniest-thing-on-tv-lisa-mcgee"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Derry Girls}}}\uc2  ) go from strength to strength. Unlike a lot of other celebrities, the 37-year-old isn\u8217\'20\'19t a cowardly {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.refinery29.com/en-gb/nicola-coughlan-ageism-entertainment-industry-interview"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 nepo baby}}}\uc2  : the self-made actor has consistently spoken out about the humanitarian crisis in Gaza despite being warned that calling for a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.teenvogue.com/story/nicola-coughlan-cover-interview-april-2024"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ceasefire could harm her career}}}\uc2 . Just take that in for a moment, will you? We live in a world where calling for a ceasefire in the middle of a genocide can hurt your career. Meanwhile, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.thedailybeast.com/amy-schumer-needs-to-stop"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Amy Schumer}}}\uc2 , the self-proclaimed \u8220\'20\'1Cmost successful female comedian of all time\u8221\'20\'1D, has shared outrageously racist statements about Palestinians without facing any career consequences whatsoever.\par \par \uc2 The week in pawtriarchy\par \par \uc2 Spotted a cute, bandit-faced critter out and about? Then it\u8217\'20\'19s time to dial 1-800-BAD-RACCOON! Tokyo is currently at war with its raccoon population, which grew out of control after a 1970s TV show reportedly led to people importing the animals and keeping them as pets. Now they\u8217\'20\'19ve gone from pets to pests and certain areas of the city are launching hotlines for people to call and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/article/2024/may/17/tokyo-japan-raccoons-numbers-increase"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 report naughty raccoons}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240525ek5p001e3\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
