\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Texas doctor who said nine-year-olds can safely give birth appointed to maternal mortality committee\b0\par\par\uc2 Mary Tuma \par \uc2 1,046 \uc2 words\par \uc2 24 May 2024\par 01:29 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Dr Ingrid Skop called the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s overturning of Roe v Wade \u8216\'20\'18a victory\u8217\'20\'19 and has argued in favor of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans\par \par \uc2 One of the US\u8217\'20\'19s leading anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  activists has been appointed to a Texas health committee tasked with reviewing maternal deaths.\par \par \uc2 The move worries reproductive justice advocates who say the state\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban \u8211\'20\'13 among the strictest in the US \u8211\'20\'13 has placed {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jul/13/texas-abortion-ban-maternal-health-risk"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pregnant women\u8217\'20\'19s lives in jeopardy}}}\uc2 . The appointment could undermine the committee\u8217\'20\'19s ability to accurately examine the impact of the law on deaths during and in the immediate aftermath of pregnancy, they say.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis appointment speaks volumes about how seriously certain state leaders are taking the issue of maternal mortality,\u8221\'20\'1D said Kamyon Conner, executive director of the Texas Equal Access Fund, an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  assistance group that advocates for reproductive health equity. \u8220\'20\'1CIt is another sign that the state is more interested in furthering their anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  agenda than protecting the lives of pregnant Texans.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Dr Ingrid Skop, a San Antonio-based OB-GYN, has long been vocal about her views on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Skop serves as vice-president and director of medical affairs for the national anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  research group {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://lozierinstitute.org/team-member/ingrid-skop-m-d-facog/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Charlotte Lozier Institute}}}\uc2  and is a member of the American Association of Pro-Life Obstetricians and Gynecologists. She is also a plaintiff in a \uc2 US supreme court{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/mar/26/us-supreme-court-abortion-pill-case-mifepristone"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 lawsuit}}}\uc2  seeking to revoke the \uc2 Food and Drug Administration\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s approval of the key \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  drug mifepristone, which she argues is \u8220\'20\'1Cdangerous\u8221\'20\'1D despite {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2023/04/01/health/abortion-pill-safety.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 years of evidence}}}\uc2  showing the drug is safe. She has authored a number of research papers that were ultimately retracted for misleading errors.\par \par \uc2 Skop \u8211\'20\'13 who has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=aGwbDNWaPOk"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 called}}}\uc2  the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s overturning of Roe v Wade \u8220\'20\'1Ca victory in the battle but not the end of the war\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 has argued in favor of forcing rape and incest victims as young as nine or 10 to carry pregnancies to term. \u8220\'20\'1CIf she is developed enough to be menstruating and become pregnant and reach sexual maturity, she can safely give birth to a baby,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2021/11/26/health/texas-abortion-law-risky-pregnancy.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Skop told}}}\uc2  the House oversight committee in 2021. Pregnancy at such a young age is shown to carry {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://utswmed.org/medblog/early-teen-pregnancy-health-risks/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 significant health risks}}}\uc2 , including {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.who.int/news-room/fact-sheets/detail/adolescent-pregnancy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pre-eclampsia and infections}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In Texas, Skop has repeatedly testified at the legislature and in court in support of state \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans, most recently in a hearing {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://reproductiverights.org/wp-content/uploads/2023/12/State-Response-Cox-v-Texas.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 opposing}}}\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/dec/05/texas-woman-emergency-abortion-lawsuit"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kate Cox}}}\uc2 , a Dallas woman who petitioned a judge for emergency access after receiving a lethal fetal diagnosis.\par \par \uc2 Texas has seen a number of instances of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jul/20/texas-women-pregnancy-abortion-ban"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pregnant women being denied emergency abortions}}}\uc2 , despite, in some cases, life-threatening {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ansirh.org/sites/default/files/2023-05/Care%20Post-Roe%20Preliminary%20Findings.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pregnancy complications}}}\uc2 . Studies have shown that some patients are being forced to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nejm.org/doi/full/10.1056/NEJMp2207423?query=TOC&cid=NEJM%20eToc,%20June%2023,%202022%20DM1181466_NEJM_Non_Subscriber&bid=1036921651"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wait at \u8220\'20\'1Cdeath\u8217\'20\'19s door\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2  before doctors, who face criminal penalties under the state\u8217\'20\'19s ban, intervene. But Skop has argued that the problem rests with the judgment of individual physicians, not the law itself.\par \par \uc2 Contrary to the arguments of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/27/roe-v-wade-overturned-maternal-mortality-rate-will-rise"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 many experts}}}\uc2 , Skop believes that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans not only {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://lozierinstitute.org/response-to-media-allegations-that-abortion-restrictions-cause-maternal-mortality-and-female-suicides/?utm_source=substack&utm_medium=email"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 will not lead}}}\uc2  to an increase in maternal deaths, but {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://lozierinstitute.org/twelve-reasons-womens-health-and-maternal-mortality-will-not-worsen-and-may-improve-in-states-with-abortion-limitations/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 may actually help}}}\uc2  reduce those rates. She calls the link between \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions and risks to maternal mortality \u8220\'20\'1Cfallacious\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Maternal mortality rates in Texas \u8211\'20\'13 among {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://kffhealthnews.org/morning-breakout/texas-has-worst-maternal-mortality-rate-births-among-over-30s-slip/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the worst}}}\uc2  in the US \u8211\'20\'13 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://jamanetwork.com/journals/jama/article-abstract/2806661"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 more than doubled}}}\uc2  between 1999 and 2019. Skop told {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.houstonchronicle.com/news/houston-texas/health/article/anti-abortion-maternal-mortality-deaths-19468740.php"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Houston Chronicle}}}\uc2  the state\u8217\'20\'19s high rate of maternal death \u8220\'20\'1Cdeserves rigorous discourse\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere are complex reasons for these statistics, including chronic illnesses, poverty and difficulty obtaining prenatal care, and I have long been motivated to identify ways women\u8217\'20\'19s care can be improved,\u8221\'20\'1D said Skop. \u8220\'20\'1CFor over 30 years, I have advocated for both of my patients, a pregnant woman and her unborn child, just like the overwhelming majority of OB-GYNs who don\u8217\'20\'19t perform elective abortions.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.acog.org/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 American College of Obstetricians and Gynecologists }}}\uc2  questioned Skop\u8217\'20\'19s appointment, saying it was \u8220\'20\'1Ccrucial\u8221\'20\'1D that maternal review committee members be informed by \u8220\'20\'1Cdata, not ideology\u8221\'20\'1D. Her bias is relevant because \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , they note, is inherently tied to maternal health.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe believe that all members of the MMRC should be unbiased, free of conflicts of interest, and focused on the appropriate standards of care when evaluating maternal mortality and morbidity in Texas, which were already at unacceptably high levels even before Texas passed its \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans and restrictions,\u8221\'20\'1D said \uc2 ACOG\uc2  in a statement.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBias against \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  has already led to compromised analysis and, ultimately, dangerously flawed data,\u8221\'20\'1D said \uc2 ACOG\uc2 , citing three research papers critical of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  that Skop co-authored. The studies were {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://journals.sagepub.com/doi/10.1177/23333928231216699"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ultimately retracted}}}\uc2  by the academic publisher for \u8220\'20\'1Cunjustified or incorrect factual assumptions\u8221\'20\'1D, as well as errors and misleading presentations of the data that showed a \u8220\'20\'1Clack of scientific rigor and invalidate the authors\u8217\'20\'19 conclusions in whole or in part\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Skop did not respond to a request from the Guardian for comment.\par \par \uc2 The 23-member {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.dshs.texas.gov/maternal-child-health/maternal-mortality-morbidity-review-committee"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Texas maternal mortality and review committee}}}\uc2 , created in 2013 amid a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/may/30/texas-maternal-mortality-crisis-black-women-medicaid"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 maternal healthcare crisis}}}\uc2 , gathers data on pregnancy-related deaths.\par \par \uc2 The committee\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.dshs.texas.gov/sites/default/files/legislative/2022-Reports/2022-MMMRC-DSHS-Joint-Biennial-Report.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 latest report}}}\uc2  showed that 90% of maternal deaths in the state were probably preventable. It is now reviewing pregnancy-related deaths from 2020 and plans to examine the impact of state \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws on maternal health in the coming years.\par \par \uc2 Nakeenya Wilson, who {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/global-development/2023/mar/17/texas-black-women-maternal-healthcare-crisis-medicaid"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 nearly lost her life}}}\uc2  giving birth in Texas, sat on the committee as an outspoken community advocate, pushing for the release of data when the state health commissioner {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.houstonchronicle.com/politics/texas/article/Texas-delays-publication-of-maternal-death-data-17439477.php"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 delayed publication}}}\uc2  of the report in 2022. As a voice for people of color, Wilson championed the stories of black women, who are disproportionately affected by maternal mortality rates both {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cdc.gov/reproductivehealth/maternal-mortality/disparities-pregnancy-related-deaths/infographic.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 nationally}}}\uc2  and in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.dshs.texas.gov/sites/default/files/legislative/2022-Reports/Joint-Biennial-MMMRC-Report-2022.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Texas}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 After legislation in 2023 eliminated her \u8220\'20\'1Ccommunity advocate\u8221\'20\'1D role, Wilson applied to a different role on the committee, but did not get the job.\par \par \uc2 While Skop\u8217\'20\'19s role is meant for a rural community member, she has spent her career working in San Antonio, a major Texas city. Skop, who is one of seven {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.dshs.texas.gov/news-alerts/dshs-commissioner-appoints-seven-maternal-mortality-and-morbidity-review-committee"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 new appointees}}}\uc2 , will begin her six-year term on 1 June.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAs a black mother who went through a traumatic pregnancy first-hand, I think I provided that necessary lived experience and could represent my community well,\u8221\'20\'1D Wilson said. \u8220\'20\'1CWe need to ask, what community is [Skop] representing?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240523ek5n002gy\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
