\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Senate Democrats investigate Trump\u8217\'20\'19s reported offer to oil bosses of climate rules rollback for donations \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Chris Stein (now) and Gloria Oladipo (earlier) \par \uc2 5,435 \uc2 words\par \uc2 23 May 2024\par 21:39 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 This live blog is now closed. You can read our latest US politics coverage here:Read all our US politics coverage\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.01pm BST\par \par \uc2 Closing summary\par \par \uc2 The supreme court allowed South Carolina\u8217\'20\'19s Republican-drawn congressional map to stay, at least for now, after the panel\u8217\'20\'19s conservative majority {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/may/23/supreme-court-alito-biden-trump-republicans-latest-updates?page=with:block-664f514c8f086914c5b64dba#block-664f514c8f086914c5b64dba"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ruled against}}}\uc2  a lower court\u8217\'20\'19s finding that they discriminated against Black voters. The decision, which \uc2 Joe Biden{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/may/23/supreme-court-alito-biden-trump-republicans-latest-updates?page=with:block-664f9e028f0891c9817ac2a9#block-664f9e028f0891c9817ac2a9"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 called}}}\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Cwrong\u8221\'20\'1D, was authored by \uc2 Samuel Alito\uc2 , a conservative justice who was yesterday revealed to have flown a flag associated with Christian extremism at a vacation property. It was the second rightwing banner to have reportedly been displayed at one of his homes, prompting the House\u8217\'20\'19s top Democrat, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/may/23/supreme-court-alito-biden-trump-republicans-latest-updates?page=with:block-664f59248f083be58d8ea379#block-664f59248f083be58d8ea379"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Hakeem Jeffries}}}\uc2  , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/may/23/supreme-court-alito-biden-trump-republicans-latest-updates?page=with:block-664f474f8f08d0608a291d90#block-664f474f8f08d0608a291d90"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 among}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/may/23/supreme-court-alito-biden-trump-republicans-latest-updates?page=with:block-664f5ed58f083be58d8ea3d1#block-664f5ed58f083be58d8ea3d1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 others}}}\uc2 , to call for him to recuse himself from cases dealing with January 6. Alito has not commented on whether he will do that.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else happened:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Senate Democrats have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/may/23/supreme-court-alito-biden-trump-republicans-latest-updates?page=with:block-664f73f98f08b23bf2415879#block-664f73f98f08b23bf2415879"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 launched}}}\uc2  an investigation into \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s reported offer to roll back environmental regulations if oil executives raise $1b for him.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Biden and attorney general \uc2 Merrick Garland\uc2  both {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/may/23/supreme-court-alito-biden-trump-republicans-latest-updates?page=with:block-664f629e8f08f4cfe4696630#block-664f629e8f08f4cfe4696630"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 declined to comment}}}\uc2  on Alito\u8217\'20\'19s flag preferences.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Elena Kagan\uc2 , a liberal supreme court justice, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/may/23/supreme-court-alito-biden-trump-republicans-latest-updates?page=with:block-664f55b38f080aff756aad23#block-664f55b38f080aff756aad23"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 dissented}}}\uc2  from the conservative ruling in the South Carolina case, and warned it would undermine future attempts to challenge racial gerrymanders.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Mike Johnson, the Republican House speaker, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/may/23/supreme-court-alito-biden-trump-republicans-latest-updates?page=with:block-664f9aaf8f08f9a1e7a08aac#block-664f9aaf8f08f9a1e7a08aac"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 squabbled}}}\uc2  with Biden after Senate Democrats tried and failed again to pass a bill to tighten immigration policy.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Louisiana \u8217\'20\'19s Republican-dominated legislature {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/may/23/supreme-court-alito-biden-trump-republicans-latest-updates?page=with:block-664f89b78f0891c9817ac202#block-664f89b78f0891c9817ac202"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 moved}}}\uc2  to restrict \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  medication \u8211\'20\'13 which the Biden campaign {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/may/23/supreme-court-alito-biden-trump-republicans-latest-updates?page=with:block-664f8e028f08f9a1e7a08a58#block-664f8e028f08f9a1e7a08a58"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 blamed}}}\uc2  on Trump.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.32pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.53pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden calls supreme court's ruling on South Carolina congressional map 'wrong'\par \par \uc2 In a just-released statement, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  decried the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s ruling earlier today that South Carolina\u8217\'20\'19s Republican leaders do not need to redraw their congressional map, despite claims that it excludes Black voters.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe right to vote is the foundation of American democracy. Key to that right is ensuring that voters pick their elected officials \u8211\'20\'13 not the other way around. The Supreme Court\u8217\'20\'19s decision today undermines the basic principle that voting practices should not discriminate on account of race and that is wrong,\u8221\'20\'1D the president said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis decision threatens South Carolinians\u8217\'20\'19 ability to have their voices heard at the ballot box, and the districting plan the Court upheld is part of a dangerous pattern of racial gerrymandering efforts from Republican elected officials to dilute the will of Black voters.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more on the court\u8217\'20\'19s finding:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/article/2024/may/23/south-carolina-redistricting-case-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Supreme court rules South Carolina doesn\u8217\'20\'19t need to redraw congressional map to consider Black voters}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.29pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.50pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden, Johnson squabble after GOP torpedoes Senate immigration bill\par \par \uc2 Senate Democrats tried once again this afternoon to pass legislation tightening immigration policy, with the goal of curbing the flow of people crossing the southern border. But, just as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/feb/07/us-senate-vote-bipartisan-border-bill"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 when they first tried}}}\uc2  to move the legislation in February in a gambit to win approval of a new military aid infusion for Israel and Ukraine, the attempt failed, thanks to the opposition of Republicans who say they want even stronger anti-immigration measures.\par \par \uc2 In a statement following the vote, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  accused the GOP of indifference to the issue of border security:\par \par \uc2 Congressional Republicans do not care about securing the border or fixing America\u8217\'20\'19s broken immigration system. If they did, they would have voted for the toughest border enforcement in history. Instead, today, they put partisan politics ahead of our country\u8217\'20\'19s national security.\par \par \uc2 By blocking the bipartisan border agreement, Republicans in Congress said no to legislation that would hire more Border Patrol Agents, add more immigration judges and asylum officers to process cases in months and not years. They said no to new technology to detect and stop fentanyl from entering the United States, and no to resources to go after drug traffickers. They rejected an agreement that would give me, as President, a new emergency authority to temporarily shut down the border when the system is overwhelmed.\par \par \uc2 Republican House speaker Mike Johnson alleged that Biden and his allies in the Senate are faking concern for immigration, and just want to shore up support before November\u8217\'20\'19s election.\par \par \uc2 After more than three years of claiming the situation at our southern border was not a crisis while millions of illegals poured in, Congressional Democrats are attempting to throw an election year Hail Mary to cover for their embrace of President Biden\u8217\'20\'19s open border policies. In the absence of a substantive legislative solution, Senator Schumer should join House Republicans in demanding President Biden reverse course and use his executive authority to finally secure the border and protect American families.\par \par \uc2 Left unmentioned by both parties were {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/jan/25/congress-mexico-border-ukraine-israel-aid-mcconnell"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the well-documented efforts}}}\uc2  by \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  to torpedo the legislation earlier this year, reportedly so he could campaign on frustration over immigration.\par \par \uc2 Another issue Democrats face is that the party isn\u8217\'20\'19t united on how to handle immigration. Yesterday, Congressional Progressive Caucus chair \uc2 Pramila Jayapal\uc2  and \uc2 Nanette Barrag\u225\'00\'E1n\uc2 , leader of the \uc2 Congressional Hispanic Caucus\uc2 , called the bill \u8220\'20\'1Cinhumane\u8221\'20\'1D:\par \par \uc2 This framework, which was constructed under Republican hostage-taking, does nothing to address the longstanding updates needed to modernize our outdated immigration system, create more legal pathways, and recognize the enormous contributions of immigrants to communities and our economy.\par \par \uc2 While the investments in asylum officers and immigration judges are welcome and needed, these alone cannot address the negative effects of a new Title 42-like expulsion authority that will close the border and turn away people seeking asylum without due process. Such a policy will be a boon to cartels who prey on migrants and would do nothing to address the root causes of migration \u8211\'20\'13 which will continue to send immigrants to the border. It is worth remembering that under \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , such a policy was not only declared unlawful by the courts, but it also led to increases \u8211\'20\'13 not decreases \u8211\'20\'13 in illegal border crossing.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.28pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.26pm BST\par \par \uc2 While \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has already effectively clinched the Republican presidential nomination, the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/wilson-jason"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Jason Wilson}}}\uc2  reports that rightwing lobbyists are working behind the scenes to cement deeper ties between GOP lawmakers and groups supporting the ex-president\u8217\'20\'19s agenda:\par \par \uc2 A powerful, rightwing lobbying group is promoting a hard-right policy agenda and cementing ties between the Republican party and the far right at at least 21 events involving senators, members of Congress, and both junior and senior political aides, documents obtained by the Guardian show.\par \par \uc2 The documents offer previously unreported details of Conservative Partnership Institute (CPI) trainings and \u8220\'20\'1Cbootcamps\u8221\'20\'1D for congressional staff at CPI\u8217\'20\'19s sprawling Maryland ranch, and lavish, star-studded retreats for members of Congress \u8211\'20\'13 mostly members of the far-right Freedom caucus \u8211\'20\'13 at a string of Florida resorts.\par \par \uc2 They also show how CPI, widely described as the \u8220\'20\'1Cnerve center of the Maga movement\u8221\'20\'1D, enlisted its own network of affiliated organizations along with like-minded far-right organizations \u8211\'20\'13 some classified as hate groups by experts \u8211\'20\'13 as well as individual extremists to promote anti-immigrant, anti-LGBTQ+ and anti-vaccine policies, along with others premised on the false claim that the 2020 election was stolen from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The revelations raise further questions about the powerful influence exercised on Capitol Hill staffers by the well-heeled NGO, and the extent of its successes in moving Republican elected officials even further to the right.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/may/23/conservative-partnership-institute-republican-laws"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Revealed: the extremist Maga lobbying group driving far-right Republican policies}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.06pm BST\par \par \uc2 Attorney general Garland says Trump claim the justice department was authorized to kill him during Mar-a-Lago search is 'extremely dangerous'\par \par \uc2 At a press conference today, attorney general \uc2 Merrick Garland\uc2  repudiated a claim by \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  that the federal agents who searched his Mar-a-Lago resort in Florida two years ago were given the authority to kill him.\par \par \uc2 The former president made the allegation in a fundraising email, but the attorney general said it was an \u8220\'20\'1Cextremely dangerous\u8221\'20\'1D distortion of the department\u8217\'20\'19s policies, which were also followed when \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s home was searched for classified material:\par \par \uc2 enltrAttorney General Garland on former President Trump's claim that the Justice Department had authorization to kill him during the Mar-a-Lago raid: "That allegation is false and it is extremely dangerous." {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/mAEfeCejwF"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/mAEfeCejwF}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 CSPAN (@cspan) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/cspan/status/1793685630855020804?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 23, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 And here\u8217\'20\'19s a recap of what exactly Trump was alleging:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/may/22/trump-fbi-doj-lethal-force"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump falsely claims US justice department was ready to kill him}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.46pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s re-election campaign says \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is to blame for the move by Louisiana Republicans to tighten access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  medication.\par \par \uc2 From spokesperson Lauren Hitt :\par \par \uc2 enltrThis Louisiana bill also creates a registry, on which every single person who is prescribed \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  medication will be listed - truly state monitoring of pregnancies.\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  did this. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/DytQ0V04YD"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/DytQ0V04YD}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Lauren Hitt (@LaurenHitt) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/LaurenHitt/status/1793708109946638754?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 23, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 The Biden campaign has banked on rising public support for access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  to translate into votes for the president in November. Here\u8217\'20\'19s more on the latest opinion polls on the issue:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/article/2024/may/14/abortion-rights-support-poll"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US support for \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  rights up four points to 60% since fall of Roe v Wade}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.50pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.30pm BST\par \par \uc2 Louisiana Republicans move to tighten access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  medication\par \par \uc2 Louisiana\u8217\'20\'19s Republican-dominated state legislature has moved to further tighten access to two prescription drugs used in medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the Associated Press reports.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more on the move, which comes {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/mar/26/us-supreme-court-abortion-pill-case-mifepristone"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 as we await}}}\uc2  a ruling from the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  on whether mifepristone, one of the drugs targeted by the new Louisiana law, can remain available nationwide:\par \par \uc2 Two \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -inducing drugs could soon be reclassified as controlled and dangerous substances in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/louisiana"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Louisiana}}}\uc2  under a first-of-its-kind bill that received final legislative passage Thursday and is expected to be signed into law by the governor.\par \par \uc2 Supporters of the reclassification of mifepristone and misoprostol, commonly known as \u8220\'20\'1C\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills\u8221\'20\'1D, say it would protect expectant mothers from coerced abortions. Numerous doctors, meanwhile, have said it will make it harder for them to prescribe the medicines they use for other important reproductive healthcare needs, and could delay treatment.\par \par \uc2 Louisiana currently has a near-total \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban in place, applying both to surgical and medical abortions. The GOP-dominated legislature\u8217\'20\'19s push to reclassify mifepristone and misoprostol could possibly open the door for other Republican states with \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans that are seeking tighter restrictions on the drugs.\par \par \uc2 Current Louisiana law already requires a prescription for both drugs and makes it a crime to use them to induce an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in most cases. The bill would make it harder to obtain the pills by placing them on the list of Schedule IV drugs under the state\u8217\'20\'19s Uniform Controlled Dangerous Substances Law.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/article/2024/may/23/mifepristone-misoprostol-abortion-pills-louisiana"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Louisiana expected to classify \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  pills as controlled and dangerous substances}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.51pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.08pm BST\par \par \uc2 The investigation into the 11 April dinner comes a day after Trump attended a Houston lunch to ask oil executives for more campaign money.\par \par \uc2 Trump attended the invitation-only meeting at Houston\u8217\'20\'19s ritzy Post Oak hotel. The lunch was organized by three major oil executives, and came only a week after severe thunderstorms hit the Houston area.\par \par \uc2 Climate advocates in Texas have condemned Trump\u8217\'20\'19s pleas to the oil industry as the state struggles with extreme weather exacerbated by the climate crisis.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHoustonians are staring at Trump in disbelief as he flies in to beg big oil for funds just days after the city\u8217\'20\'19s climate disaster,\u8221\'20\'1D said Alex Glass, communications director at the climate advocacy organization Climate Power, and a former Houston resident.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/may/22/trump-oil-industry-campaign"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump attends Houston lunch to ask oil bosses for more campaign cash}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.46pm BST\par \par \uc2 The 11 April dinner was reportedly called an \u8220\'20\'1Cenergy round table\u8221\'20\'1D, the Times reported.\par \par \uc2 Executives from major oil companies including \uc2 ExxonMobil\uc2  and \uc2 EQT Corporation\uc2  were in attendance.\par \par \uc2 The event was organized by oil tycoon \uc2 Harold Hamm\uc2 , the \uc2 Washington Post\uc2  first {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/2024/05/09/trump-oil-industry-campaign-money/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2 . Hamm and others are reportedly organizing another fundraiser for Trump later this year, which is expected to bring high donations.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more from the Times:\par \par \uc2 Over a dinner of chopped steak, Mr. Trump repeated his public promises to delete Mr. Biden\u8217\'20\'19s pollution controls, telling the attendees that they should donate heavily to help him beat Mr. Biden because his policies would help their industries.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThat has been his pitch to everybody,\u8221\'20\'1D said Michael McKenna, who worked in the Trump White House but did not attend the event in Florida.\par \par \uc2 Mr. McKenna said the former president\u8217\'20\'19s appeal to the fossil fuel industry could be summed up as: \u8220\'20\'1CLook, you want me to win. You might not even like me, but your other choice is four more years of these guys,\u8221\'20\'1D referring to the Biden administration. He added, \u8220\'20\'1CThe uniform sentiment of guys in the business community is \u8216\'20\'18We don\u8217\'20\'19t want four more years of Team Biden.\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.22pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Senate Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 investigation into Trump\u8217\'20\'19s alleged quid-pro-quo suggestion to oil executives stems from an 11 April dinner at Mar-a-Lago, the \uc2 New York Times{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2024/05/23/climate/trump-oil-democrats.html?unlocked_article_code=1.uE0.Fzsy.7j3A29T-iAB6&smid=nytcore-ios-share&referringSource=articleShare&sgrp=c-cb"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Trump reportedly told 20 oil executives that they should donate $1b to his campaign as they would save more than that amount in \u8220\'20\'1Ctaxes and legal fees\u8221\'20\'1D once Trump was elected as he would repeal Biden\u8217\'20\'19s restrictions on drilling that hurt their industries.\par \par \uc2 Read the full article {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2024/05/23/climate/trump-oil-democrats.html?unlocked_article_code=1.uE0.Fzsy.7j3A29T-iAB6&smid=nytcore-ios-share&referringSource=articleShare&sgrp=c-cb"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2  (pay wall).\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.19pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.06pm BST\par \par \uc2 The day so far\par \par \uc2 The supreme court has allowed South Carolina\u8217\'20\'19s Republican-drawn congressional maps to stay, at least for now, after the panel\u8217\'20\'19s conservative majority {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/may/23/supreme-court-alito-biden-trump-republicans-latest-updates?page=with:block-664f514c8f086914c5b64dba#block-664f514c8f086914c5b64dba"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 turned away}}}\uc2  a request from challengers that they be thrown out for discriminating against Black voters. The decision was authored by \uc2 Samuel Alito\uc2 , a conservative justice who was yesterday revealed to have flown a flag associated with Christian extremism at a vacation property. It was the second rightwing flag to have reportedly been displayed at his properties, prompting the House\u8217\'20\'19s top Democrat {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/may/23/supreme-court-alito-biden-trump-republicans-latest-updates?page=with:block-664f59248f083be58d8ea379#block-664f59248f083be58d8ea379"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Hakeem Jeffries}}}\uc2  , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/may/23/supreme-court-alito-biden-trump-republicans-latest-updates?page=with:block-664f474f8f08d0608a291d90#block-664f474f8f08d0608a291d90"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 among}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/may/23/supreme-court-alito-biden-trump-republicans-latest-updates?page=with:block-664f5ed58f083be58d8ea3d1#block-664f5ed58f083be58d8ea3d1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 others}}}\uc2 , to call for him to recuse himself from cases dealing with January 6. Alito has not commented on if he will do that.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else is going on:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Senate Democrats have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/may/23/supreme-court-alito-biden-trump-republicans-latest-updates?page=with:block-664f73f98f08b23bf2415879#block-664f73f98f08b23bf2415879"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 launched}}}\uc2  an investigation into \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s reported offer to roll back environmental regulations if oil executives raise $1bn for him.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and attorney general \uc2 Merrick Garland\uc2  both {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/may/23/supreme-court-alito-biden-trump-republicans-latest-updates?page=with:block-664f629e8f08f4cfe4696630#block-664f629e8f08f4cfe4696630"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 declined to comment}}}\uc2  on Alito\u8217\'20\'19s flag preferences.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Elena Kagan\uc2 , a liberal supreme court justice, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/may/23/supreme-court-alito-biden-trump-republicans-latest-updates?page=with:block-664f55b38f080aff756aad23#block-664f55b38f080aff756aad23"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 dissented}}}\uc2  from the conservative ruling in the South Carolina case, and warned it would undermine future attempts to challenge racial gerrymanders.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.32pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.56pm BST\par \par \uc2 Senate Democrats launch investigation into Trump's reported offer to oil executives of regulatory rollback in exchange for donations\par \par \uc2 Senate Democrats have launched an investigation into \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/may/09/trump-oil-ceo-donation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported offer}}}\uc2  to oil executives that if they donated $1bn to his campaign, he would roll back environmental regulations, if elected.\par \par \uc2 The joint investigation by the Senate budget and finance committees is targeted at the petroleum firms whose top executives were said to have attended that April dinner.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTime and time again, both Mr. Trump and the US oil and gas industry have proved they are willing to sell out Americans to pad their own pockets,\u8221\'20\'1D finance committee chair \uc2 Ron Wyden\uc2  and budget committee chair Sheldon Whitehouse said {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.finance.senate.gov/chairmans-news/finance-budget-committees-launch-joint-investigation-into-donald-trumps-quid-pro-quo-offer-to-big-oil"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in a joint statement}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more:\par \par \uc2 As Mr. Trump funnels campaign money into his businesses and uses it as a slush fund to pay his legal fees, Big Oil has been lobbying aggressively to protect and expand its profits at the expense of the American taxpayer. And now, emboldened by impunity, Mr. Trump and Big Oil are flaunting their indifference to U.S. citizens\u8217\'20\'19 economic well-being for all to see, conferring on how to trade campaign cash for policy changes. Such potential abuses must be scrutinized.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.59pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.40pm BST\par \par \uc2 A former White House lawyer for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  says he should already be on trial for the classified documents discovered at Mar-a-Lago, the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/roberttait"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Robert Tait}}}\uc2  reports:\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s former White House lawyer has attacked Aileen Cannon, the judge handling the ex-president\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/may/22/trump-classified-documents-case-hearing"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 classified documents charges}}}\uc2 , for repeated delays, attributing her rulings to \u8220\'20\'1Cincompetence\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cperceived bias\u8221\'20\'1D and saying the case should have already come to trial.\par \par \uc2 Ty Cobb\uc2 , the luxuriantly whiskered attorney who served as Trump\u8217\'20\'19s counsel during former \uc2 FBI\uc2  director \uc2 Robert Mueller\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s investigation into Russian interference in the 2016 presidential election, said decisions taken by Cannon, a Trump-appointed judge in the US district court in Florida, virtually guaranteed that the case would not be tried before November\u8217\'20\'19s presidential poll.\par \par \uc2 In an interview with CNN, Cobb said Cannon had delayed on issues that most federal judges would have long since dealt with.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t think this case will move at all,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd I think the fact that she\u8217\'20\'19s scheduling hearings, multiple hearings, sort of one or two motions at a time is compelling evidence of that. Most federal judges would have long ago ruled on all the pending motions.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAnd frankly, this is a case that should\u8217\'20\'19ve started trial yesterday or two days ago when the original trial date was set. This case could have easily gotten to trial. Only her incompetence and perceived bias has prevented that.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/may/23/trump-classified-documents-case-delays"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ex-Trump lawyer blames documents case delays on judge\u8217\'20\'19s incompetence}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.23pm BST\par \par \uc2 Republican congresswoman Nancy Mace\u8217\'20\'19s district is at the heart of the supreme court case in which the challengers to legislative maps drawn by the state\u8217\'20\'19s Republican lawmakers argued that they constituted an illegal racial gerrymander.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what Mace had to say after the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s conservative majority today ruled against the challengers:\par \par \uc2 enltrToday the Supreme Court affirmed what everyone in the state of South Carolina already knew: redistricting was not racially motivated and served in the best interest of constituencies of South Carolina. ???? {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/LowcountryFirst?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #LowcountryFirst}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Nancy Mace (@NancyMace) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/NancyMace/status/1793676105750364251?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 23, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 And here\u8217\'20\'19s a recap of the decision, which could have ripple effects on congressional maps across the south:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/article/2024/may/23/south-carolina-redistricting-case-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Supreme court rules South Carolina doesn\u8217\'20\'19t need to redraw congressional map to consider Black voters}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.03pm BST\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2024/05/23/supreme-court-south-carolina-redistricting-map-00159666"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Politico reports}}}\uc2  that \uc2 Samuel Alito\uc2  seemed brusque when he announced the opinion he authored that essentially allows South Carolina to use Republican-drawn congressional maps, even though challengers claimed they discriminated against African Americans:\par \par \uc2 Alito, who has been under fire in recent days over claims that the display of flags at his Virginia home and New Jersey shore house reflected bias and violated judicial ethics, delivered an unusually short, almost perfunctory summary of his opinion when the court announced its decisions from the bench Thursday morning.\par \par \uc2 Reporters in the court\u8217\'20\'19s press room had only just begun to read the voting-rights ruling when he moved on to an unrelated, criminal-justice opinion he also wrote.\par \par \uc2 However, the court\u8217\'20\'19s ruling, which was joined by all six conservative justices, did not completely end the challenge to South Carolina\u8217\'20\'19s maps, Politico notes:\par \par \uc2 The high court\u8217\'20\'19s ruling did not entirely foreclose the possibility that civil rights groups might eventually prevail in their challenge to the map on what Alito said was a distinct theory under the Voting Rights Act of diluting minority votes.\par \par \uc2 The majority ordered the case returned to the lower court for a fresh look at that issue by the panel that earlier ruled the map unconstitutional. All of those judges are Democratic appointees.\par \par \uc2 But with the state\u8217\'20\'19s congressional primaries looming on June 11, and the lower court already having given the green light to use the legislature\u8217\'20\'19s map this year, the chances of any changes in the map this year seem vanishingly remote.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 National Public Radio\uc2  reports that attorney general \uc2 Merrick Garland\uc2  declined to comment on supreme court justice \uc2 Samuel Alito\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s display of rightwing flags:\par \par \uc2 enltrAttorney General \uc2 Merrick Garland\uc2 , asked about the Alito flag issue, and two Jan. 6 cases before the Supreme Court, replies, "As you rightly point out, the Justice Department has cases before the Supreme Court so I can't comment about any justice."\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Carrie Johnson (@johnson_carrie) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/johnson_carrie/status/1793665673966829613?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 23, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 So, too, did \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , when reporters shouted questions about the matter at him, as he welcomed Kenyan president \uc2 William Ruto\uc2  to the White House:\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.23pm BST\par \par \uc2 In an appearance on MSNBC yesterday, progressive Democratic congresswoman \uc2 Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez\uc2  accused supreme court justice \uc2 Samuel Alito\uc2  of siding with the people who attacked the Capitol on January 6.\par \par \uc2 She also signaled that Democrats would investigate Alito if they retook the House majority, and argued that the Senate \u8211\'20\'13 where the party currently has control \u8211\'20\'13 should do the same immediately:\par \par \uc2 enltrAOC: \uc2 Samuel Alito\uc2  has identified himself with the same people who raided the Capitol on January 6\u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 In the Senate, we have gavels. There should be subpoenas going out. There should be active investigations that are happening. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/S7E22iZTbA"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/S7E22iZTbA}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Acyn (@Acyn) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Acyn/status/1793439852421398906?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 23, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 Top House Democrat Jeffries calls on Alito to recuse himself from January 6 cases over rightwing flags\par \par \uc2 House minority leader \uc2 Hakeem Jeffries\uc2  has become the highest-ranking Democrat to call for supreme court justice \uc2 Samuel Alito\uc2  to recuse himself over the two rightwing flags reported to have flown over his properties.\par \par \uc2 At a press conference today, Jeffries called on Alito, a conservative stalwart on the court, to step back from cases concerning the January 6 insurrection, and warned that the party could work to pass legislation imposing an enforceable code of ethics on the court:\par \par \uc2 enltr. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RepJeffries?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @RepJeffries}}}\uc2  : "\uc2 Samuel Alito\uc2  and \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2  are totally out of control...In the case of \uc2 Samuel Alito\uc2 , he definitively needs to recuse himself from any matter pending before the \uc2 United States Supreme Court\uc2  that has to do with the January 6th violent insurrection." {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/JrxMSnXdKp"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/JrxMSnXdKp}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 CSPAN (@cspan) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/cspan/status/1793642208911826981?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 23, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 The justices still have not released their opinion on \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s petition for immunity from the federal charges brought against him for attempting to overturn the 2020 election \u8211\'20\'13 which culminated in his supporters\u8217\'20\'19 attack on the US Capitol.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 In her dissent, liberal justice \uc2 Elena Kagan\uc2  accused the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s conservatives of green lighting racial gerrymanders of congressional districts with their ruling in favor of South Carolina\u8217\'20\'19s Republican-drawn map:\par \par \uc2 What a message to send to state legislators and mapmakers about racial gerrymandering. For reasons I\u8217\'20\'19ve addressed, those actors will often have an incentive to use race as a proxy to achieve partisan ends. And occasionally they might want to straight-up suppress the electoral influence of minority voters. Go right ahead, this Court says to States today. Go ahead, though you have no recognized justification for using race, such as to comply with statutes ensuring equal voting rights. Go ahead, though you are (at best) using race as a short-cut to bring about partisan gains \u8211\'20\'13 to elect more Republicans in one case, more Democrats in another. It will be easy enough to cover your tracks in the end: Just raise a \u8220\'20\'1Cpossibility\u8221\'20\'1D of non-race-based decision-making, and it will be \u8220\'20\'1Cdispositive\u8221\'20\'1D. And so this \u8220\'20\'1Codious\u8221\'20\'1D practice of sorting citizens, built on racial generalizations and exploiting racial divisions, will continue. In the electoral sphere especially, where \u8220\'20\'1Cugly patterns of pervasive racial discrimination\u8221\'20\'1D have so long governed, we should demand better \u8211\'20\'13 of ourselves, of our political representatives, and most of all of this Court.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.51pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.26pm BST\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more from the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/sam-levine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Sam Levine}}}\uc2  on the decision by the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s conservative supermajority to allow South Carolina\u8217\'20\'19s congressional map to stand, despite claims that they amount to a racial gerrymander, and what that means for voting rights in the south:\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/south-carolina"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 South Carolina}}}\uc2  Republicans do not need to redraw their congressional map, the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  ruled on Thursday, saying that a lower court had not properly evaluated the evidence when it ruled that the lawmakers had discriminated against Black voters.\par \par \uc2 In a 6-3 decision, the justices sent the case back to the lower court for further consideration.\par \par \uc2 The decision in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/oct/11/supreme-court-south-carolina-congressional-map-case"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Alexander v South Carolina Conference of the NAACP}}}\uc2  is a major win for Republicans, who hold a slim margin in the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/house-of-representatives"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US House}}}\uc2  with six of South Carolina\u8217\'20\'19s seven congressional seats. It also could give lawmakers more leeway to discriminate in redistricting and use partisanship as a proxy for race. That could be enormously powerful in the US south, where voting is often racially polarized.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/article/2024/may/23/south-carolina-redistricting-case-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Supreme court rules South Carolina doesn\u8217\'20\'19t need to redraw congressional map to consider Black voters}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.27pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.19pm BST\par \par \uc2 Supreme court allows South Carolina to use congressional map accused of racial gerrymander\par \par \uc2 The supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s conservative supermajority has turned back a challenge to South Carolina\u8217\'20\'19s congressional maps on the grounds that they were a racial gerrymander.\par \par \uc2 In a 6-3 ruling, the court\u8217\'20\'19s conservatives rejected a lower court ruling that found the state\u8217\'20\'19s Republican leadership had undertaken an \u8220\'20\'1Ceffective bleaching\u8221\'20\'1D of a congressional district, by drawing lines to exclude Black voters.\par \par \uc2 The decision\u8217\'20\'19s effect is to deny Democrats the potential opportunity to pick up a seat in a state as they aim to retake the majority in the House in November\u8217\'20\'19s elections.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.22pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.57pm BST\par \par \uc2 Supreme court to release decisions with \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and Trump immunity cases pending\par \par \uc2 The supreme court will in a few minutes release its latest batch of opinions.\par \par \uc2 We do not know how many they will release, or which cases, but there are several key issues pending the before the court, including conservative attempts to limit access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill mifepristone, and to strike down a Biden administration policy that requires federally funded hospitals perform the procedure in emergencies, even in states where \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is banned.\par \par \uc2 The justices are also considering \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s petition for immunity from charges related to attempting to overturn the 2020 election, as well as a challenge to South Carolina\u8217\'20\'19s congressional maps. Here is more on the latter:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/oct/11/supreme-court-south-carolina-congressional-map-case"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Supreme court conservatives appear skeptical South Carolina Republicans discriminated against Black voters}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.15pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 A growing chorus of Democratic lawmakers is demanding supreme court justice \uc2 Samuel Alito\uc2  recuse himself from cases dealing with January 6 or the 2020 election, after the \uc2 New York Times\uc2  reported his homes flew flags associated with rightwing causes.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s Katherine Clark, the Democratic House whip:\par \par \uc2 Justice Alito has displayed flags at his homes that support insurrection against our government, promote religious nationalism, and attack free and fair elections.\par \par \uc2 This is not just another example of extremism that has overtaken conservatism. This is a threat to the rule of law and a serious breach of ethics, integrity, and Justice Alito\u8217\'20\'19s oath of office.\par \par \uc2 At minimum, he must recuse himself from any cases involving January 6th, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , and the security of our elections. Anything less will tarnish our judicial system and democracy.\par \par \uc2 Over in the Senate, Sheldon Whitehouse, a member of the judiciary committee, referenced Alito\u8217\'20\'19s explanation last week that an upside-down American flag that hung outside his Virginia home was put up by his wife:\par \par \uc2 enltrDid another neighbor make Alito\u8217\'20\'19s wife mad?\par \par \uc2 How many MAGA battle flags does Alito need to fly for the Court or the Judicial Conference to see there\u8217\'20\'19s a problem? {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/YTo3AUCFQ9"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/YTo3AUCFQ9}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Sheldon Whitehouse (@SenWhitehouse) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SenWhitehouse/status/1793396847446274427?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 22, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 While Richard Blumenthal demanded Alito offer \u8220\'20\'1Can explanation\u8221\'20\'1D for the flags:\par \par \uc2 enltrFlying this flag is a political statement that is a clear & compelling reason for Alito\u8217\'20\'19s recusal. He cannot responsibly sit on Trump-related cases when he has already signaled his sympathy with January 6th rioters. He owes the American people an explanation. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/g8hSr7Sqww"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/g8hSr7Sqww}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Richard Blumenthal (@SenBlumenthal) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SenBlumenthal/status/1793401774671385065?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 22, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.24pm BST\par \par \uc2 Alito's vacation residence flew flag linked to Christian extremists - report\par \par \uc2 The New York Times\uc2  found conservative supreme court justice \uc2 Samuel Alito\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s New Jersey vacation home flying the \u8220\'20\'1CAppeal to Heaven\u8221\'20\'1D flag, which dates back to the Revolutionary War, and has been adopted by far-right Christians:\par \par \uc2 enltrA second provocative flag linked to Jan. 6 was flown at a home of the Supreme Court justice \uc2 Samuel Alito\uc2 . {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/BuXufAjOgJ"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/BuXufAjOgJ}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The \uc2 New York Times\uc2  (@nytimes) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/nytimes/status/1793461975290192383?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 23, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 Among those who have flown it is Republican speaker of the House Mike Johnson, who flew the flag outside his Capitol office.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s the second controversial flag found outside an Alito residence. Last week, the Times reported that shortly before \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  took office, Alito\u8217\'20\'19s home in Virginia flew an upside-down American flag, which had been adopted as a symbol by those who believed \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s false claims of election fraud.\par \par \uc2 Alito told the Times his wife had put that flag up after a dispute with their neighbor, but he declined to comment about the banner found at his vacation home in New Jersey. Here\u8217\'20\'19s more on this:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/may/22/samuel-alito-flag"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Another provocative flag flown at Samuel Alito residence, report says}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.01pm BST\par \par \uc2 Supreme court to issue more decisions as Democrat calls for Alito to recuse himself over second rightwing flag flown at house\par \par \uc2 Good morning, US politics blog readers.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/may/22/samuel-alito-flag"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Conservative supreme court justice }}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/may/22/samuel-alito-flag"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Samuel Alito}}}\uc2  flew a rightwing Christian flag carried by insurrectionists on January 6 outside a vacation home, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2024/05/22/us/justice-alito-flag-appeal-to-heaven.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the New York Times reported yesterday}}}\uc2 . The story came a week after the Times revealed that a different flag associated with \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s election lies appeared outside his suburban Washington DC residence shortly before \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  took office. The justice blamed his wife for the first episode, and had no comment on the flag flown outside the New Jersey vacation property, but to top Democrats, it is clear that Alito needs to step back from cases involving the attack on the Capitol and the 2020 election. Dick Durbin, the chair of the Senate judiciary committee, made the demand, while calling the flag \u8220\'20\'1Capparent ethical misconduct\u8221\'20\'1D, and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/may/23/aoc-samuel-alito-flag-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 progressive congresswoman }}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/may/23/aoc-samuel-alito-flag-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez}}}\uc2  said the matter should be investigated.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the supreme court is scheduled to, at 10am ET, issue another batch of decisions. There is no telling which cases they may weigh in on, but pending on their docket is Trump\u8217\'20\'19s attempt to be {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/25/supreme-court-trump-criminal-trial-immunity-key-takeaways"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 granted immunity}}}\uc2  from prosecution for his 2020 election meddling attempt as well as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/2024/apr/24/us-supreme-court-abortion-rights-emtala"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 two}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/mar/26/us-supreme-court-abortion-pill-case-mifepristone"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 cases}}}\uc2  dealing with access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  that came after the court overturned Roe v Wade in 2022 \u8211\'20\'13 with an opinion Alito authored.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else is going on today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Biden is spending much of the day with Kenyan president \uc2 William Ruto\uc2 , who is on an official visit to Washington DC. The president hosts the East African leader for a state dinner in the evening \u8211\'20\'13 the first for any African leader since \uc2 George W Bush\uc2  dined with Ghana\u8217\'20\'19s John Kufuor in 2008.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Republican House speaker Mike Johnson wants to invite Israeli prime minister \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2  to give an address to Congress, but is waiting to hear from Senate majority leader \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2 . Perhaps the Democrat will make his decision known today.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The House is expected to vote on Republican-backed legislation to repeal a Washington DC law allowing non-citizens to vote in its local elections.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.37pm BST\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240523ek5n0020c\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
