\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 US prefers two-state talks to unilateral declarations of Palestinian state, says White House \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Chris Stein \par \uc2 5,357 \uc2 words\par \uc2 22 May 2024\par 20:22 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 This live blog is now closed. For the latest on the Israel-Gaza war, you can read our coverage here.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 Closing summary\par \par \uc2 Democrats {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/live/2024/may/22/biden-trump-latest-alito-flag-supreme-court?page=with:block-664e12b08f0862e793a9fd83#block-664e12b08f0862e793a9fd83"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 are planning an offensive}}}\uc2  against the GOP over access to contraception, and have seized on a vote by Louisiana\u8217\'20\'19s Republican state lawmakers to tighten access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  medication and argue that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , the party\u8217\'20\'19s presumptive presidential nominee, will undermine reproductive rights, if elected. The party is also {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/live/2024/may/22/biden-trump-latest-alito-flag-supreme-court?page=with:block-664de4308f0808638b6465f6#block-664de4308f0808638b6465f6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 mulling a response}}}\uc2  to last week\u8217\'20\'19s report that conservative supreme court justice \uc2 Samuel Alito\uc2  once flew a flag associated with Trump\u8217\'20\'19s lies about the 2020 election, though top Senate Republican \uc2 Mitch McConnell{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/live/2024/may/22/biden-trump-latest-alito-flag-supreme-court?page=with:block-664e07d28f0859c6d0840e41#block-664e07d28f0859c6d0840e41"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 defended the court}}}\uc2 . The nine justices are still considering cases concerning Trump\u8217\'20\'19s immunity on charges related to meddling in the 2020 election, and on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access. The court announces {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/live/2024/may/22/biden-trump-latest-alito-flag-supreme-court?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-664def948f0862e793a9faf5#block-664def948f0862e793a9faf5"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 more decisions}}}\uc2  tomorrow, and those issues could be among them.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else happened today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Jake Sullivan, the US national security adviser, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/live/2024/may/22/biden-trump-latest-alito-flag-supreme-court?page=with:block-664e2da28f0859c6d0841120#block-664e2da28f0859c6d0841120"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reiterated}}}\uc2  that the United States supports a two-state solution to the Israel-Palestine crisis after three European allies unilaterally recognized a Palestinian state.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A Guardian {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/live/2024/may/22/biden-trump-latest-alito-flag-supreme-court?page=with:block-664e1aaa8f0862e793a9fe09#block-664e1aaa8f0862e793a9fe09"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 poll}}}\uc2  conducted by Harris found a majority of voters think the economy is in worse shape than it actually is, and are blaming \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Rudy Giuliani{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/live/2024/may/22/biden-trump-latest-alito-flag-supreme-court?page=with:block-664dfe3d8f0862e793a9fbe6#block-664dfe3d8f0862e793a9fbe6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reportedly agreed}}}\uc2  to stop attacking two Georgia election workers who last year won a major defamation judgment against him.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Republican House speaker Mike Johnson{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/live/2024/may/22/biden-trump-latest-alito-flag-supreme-court?page=with:block-664e22ab8f0862e793a9fed7#block-664e22ab8f0862e793a9fed7"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wants}}}\uc2  to \u8220\'20\'1Cpunish\u8221\'20\'1D the international criminal court for its chief prosecutor\u8217\'20\'19s request for arrest warrants against Israeli leaders.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s laptop will soon {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/live/2024/may/22/biden-trump-latest-alito-flag-supreme-court?page=with:block-664e45f08f0859c6d084123f#block-664e45f08f0859c6d084123f"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 get its day}}}\uc2  in court.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.07pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.49pm BST\par \par \uc2 Republican House speaker Mike Johnson wants to invite Israeli prime minister \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2  to make a joint address to Congress, but is waiting to hear from the Senate\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic leader \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  before sending the invitation, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://abcnews.go.com/Politics/speaker-johnson-moving-ahead-netanyahu-invite-address-congress/story?id=110443536"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ABC News reports}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 If he does not hear from Schumer, Johnson said: \u8220\'20\'1CWe were going to proceed and invite Netanyahu just to the House.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Schumer is publicly open to the idea, saying: \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m discussing that now with the speaker of the House, and as I\u8217\'20\'19ve always said, our relationship with Israel is ironclad and transcends any one prime minister or president.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Netanyahu {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2015/mar/03/binyamin-netanyahu-speech-congress-long-on-terror-short-on-substance"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 last addressed}}}\uc2  Congress in 2015. A meeting between Schumer and Netanyahu could be a little awkward, since the Senate leader recently called him \u8220\'20\'1Can obstacle to peace\u8221\'20\'1D in Gaza and said Israel should hold new elections:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/mar/14/chuck-schumer-israel-speech"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Schumer faces backlash after calling for new Israeli elections to oust Netanyahu}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.52pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.27pm BST\par \par \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/sep/26/hunter-biden-sues-rudy-giuliani-laptop-hard-drive"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 infamous}}}\uc2  laptop will get its day in court, literally.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2024/05/22/politics/hunter-biden-laptop-gun-trial-special-counsel?cid=ios_app"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 CNN reports}}}\uc2  that David Weiss, the special counsel who is pursuing charges against the president\u8217\'20\'19s son related to his allegedly lying about his drug use when buying a firearm, will introduce the laptop\u8217\'20\'19s contents in court when the trial begins on 3 June.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe defendant\u8217\'20\'19s laptop is real (it will be introduced as a trial exhibit) and it contains significant evidence of the defendant\u8217\'20\'19s guilt,\u8221\'20\'1D prosecutors wrote today in a filing, according to CNN.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more:\par \par \uc2 Weiss plans to use the laptop to back up his narrow claim that Biden was addicted to illegal drugs when he bought a gun in 2018, allegedly in violation of federal law. Weiss has not addressed the unproven allegation from Republicans that emails on the laptop prove that Biden and his father were involved in corrupt foreign deals.\par \par \uc2 Biden has pleaded not guilty to three gun crimes. The trial is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2024/05/21/politics/appeals-court-hunter-biden-gun-trial/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 set to begin}}}\uc2  June 3 at the federal court in Delaware.\par \par \uc2 In their own court filings earlier this week, \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s lawyers said they want to contest the authenticity of the materials from the laptop if Weiss brings it up at trial.\par \par \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Defense counsel has numerous reasons to believe the data had been altered and compromised before investigators obtained the electronic material,\u8217\'20\'19 his lawyers wrote.\par \par \uc2 Biden {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2020/10/16/politics/russian-disinformation-investigation/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 dropped off the laptop}}}\uc2  at a Delaware repair shop in April 2019. His lawyers said in the filing that the shop owner admitted in his memoir that he \u8216\'20\'18began accessing sensitive, private material in the data\u8217\'20\'19 right away, and continued to potentially tamper with the data throughout the five months before the \uc2 FBI\uc2  seized the device.\par \par \uc2 Prosecutors counter by saying that some of the people who exchanged these messages with Biden {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2024/05/20/politics/hunter-biden-exes-addiction-gun-trial/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 will testify}}}\uc2  and assert that the messages are real. They also say the laptop materials are only a fraction of the digital evidence they have collected against Biden, including messages subpoenaed directly from \uc2 Apple\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18He has not shown any of the actual evidence in this case is unreliable or inauthentic, because there is none,\u8217\'20\'19 Weiss\u8217\'20\'19 team wrote in a Wednesday filing. \u8216\'20\'18Instead, the defendant\u8217\'20\'19s theory about the laptop is a conspiracy theory with no supporting evidence.\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 While Biden has written publicly of his struggles with addiction, his defense attorney recently accused federal prosecutors of not getting their evidence quite right:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/feb/21/hunter-biden-sawdust-cocaine-photo"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Hunter Biden lawyers say prosecutors confused photo of sawdust for cocaine}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.09pm BST\par \par \uc2 While some of its allies are moving to unilaterally recognize a Palestinian state, Washington DC is worried that Benajmin Netanyahu may undermine a deal to normalize relations between Israel and Saudi Arabia, the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/bethan-mckernan"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bethan McKernan}}}\uc2  reports:\par \par \uc2 The US is worried that Israel\u8217\'20\'19s prime minister, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/benjamin-netanyahu"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu}}}\uc2 , may be willing to torpedo a potential normalisation deal with Saudi Arabia if it entails ending the war in Gaza and committing to working towards a two-state solution to the decades-old Israeli-Palestinian conflict.\par \par \uc2 The US secretary of state, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/antony-blinken"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Antony Blinken}}}\uc2 , told the Senate\u8217\'20\'19s foreign relations committee on Tuesday: \u8220\'20\'1CWe have sought to move forward in negotiating the bilateral aspects, but even if we were to conclude those agreements \u8211\'20\'13 and I believe we could, relatively quickly \u8211\'20\'13 it could not go forward absent other things that need to happen for normalisation to proceed.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere\u8217\'20\'19s an opportunity for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/israel"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Israel}}}\uc2  to become integrated in the region, to get the fundamental security it needs and wants, to have the relationships it\u8217\'20\'19s wanted since its founding. The Saudis have been clear that this would require calm in Gaza and a credible pathway to a Palestinian state,\u8221\'20\'1D he said, adding: \u8220\'20\'1CIt may well be at this moment, Israel is not able or willing to proceed down this pathway.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The Biden administration has been {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/sep/21/saudi-arabia-getting-closer-to-normalising-relations-with-israel-crown-prince-says"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 working for some time}}}\uc2  on a plan in which Riyadh would normalise relations with Israel in return for a formal defence pact with the US and assistance in developing a civilian nuclear programme.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/article/2024/may/22/us-israel-netanyahu-normalisation-deal-saudi-arabia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US worried Netanyahu may torpedo normalisation deal with Saudi Arabia }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.51pm BST\par \par \uc2 While the international criminal court has attracted opprobrium from both sides of the aisle for chief prosecutor \uc2 Karim Khan\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s request for arrest warrants against top Israeli officials, it does have some defenders in Washington.\par \par \uc2 Independent senator Bernie Sanders delivered an address on the Senate floor yesterday arguing that Khan\u8217\'20\'19s investigation was in the interest of justice, and argued that the United States cannot object to the conduct of authoritarian rivals such as Russia and China if it does not hold Israel \u8211\'20\'13 a top ally \u8211\'20\'13 to the same standard:\par \par \uc2 What the \uc2 ICC\uc2  is doing is important for the world. It\u8217\'20\'19s [a message] to leaders all over the world \u8211\'20\'13 dictators, people in democratic countries \u8211\'20\'13 that if you go to war you cannot wage all-out war against civilians. That\u8217\'20\'19s what the \uc2 ICC\uc2  is doing, that\u8217\'20\'19s important. But it is also important, Mr. President, for those of us in the United States. Our nation claims to be the leader of the free world, and at our best we try to mobilize countries to uphold international law and prevent crimes against humanity. That is what we try to do and have done.\par \par \uc2 You can see Sanders\u8217\'20\'19s full speech here:\par \par \uc2 enltrLIVE: Even democratically-elected officials can commit war crimes. We cannot apply international law only when it\u8217\'20\'19s convenient. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/0arq3ensqH"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/0arq3ensqH}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Bernie Sanders (@SenSanders) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SenSanders/status/1793059371993235649?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 21, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.34pm BST\par \par \uc2 Israeli leaders updated the White House national security adviser, Jake Sullivan, on its intentions to minimize civilian harm in the southern Gaza city of Rafah when he visited the region last weekend, he said at the White House media briefing a little earlier.\par \par \uc2 We now have to see what unfolds from here. What we\u8217\'20\'19re going to be looking at is whether there is a lot of death and destruction from this operation or if it is more precise and proportional,\u8221\'20\'1D he said, Reuters reports.\par \par \uc2 Sullivan said Israeli operations to date in the area have been targeted and limited. He also said aid is flowing from a pier in Gaza to the Palestinians there, and that it was wrong for Israel to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2024/05/22/world/middleeast/israel-reacts-palestinian-finance.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 withhold funds}}}\uc2  from the Palestinian authority in the West Bank.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.36pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.19pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  plans to visit Africa as president, national security adviser Jake Sullivan said.\par \par \uc2 The president would look forward to visiting Africa. He intends to do so as president of the United States,\u8221\'20\'1D Sullivan told reporters at the White House briefing, Reuters reports.\par \par \uc2 Sullivan said he had no formal announcement to make of a Africa visit by Biden.\par \par \uc2 Adding from the Guardian: there has been chat about Biden \u8220\'20\'1Cbreaking his promise\u8221\'20\'1D, made early in his administration, to visit the continent while president, with assumptions that there would be no time for such a visit prior to the presidential election in November and, obviously, no guarantee that he will win a second term in the White House.\par \par \uc2 The Associated Press continues, with reporting that Biden is welcoming the president of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/kenya"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kenya}}}\uc2 , \uc2 William Ruto\uc2 , to the White House later today to kick off a three-day state visit.\par \par \uc2 Ruto comes to Washington as his country is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/article/2024/may/21/kenya-haiti-mission"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 preparing to deploy}}}\uc2  1,000 police officers to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/haiti"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Haiti}}}\uc2  to take part in a United Nations-led security effort in the Caribbean nation.\par \par \uc2 The White House press briefing has just ended.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.10pm BST\par \par \uc2 National security advisor Jake Sullivan just said he was surprised by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/politics/article/2024/may/22/rishi-sunak-will-call-general-election-for-july-in-surprise-move-sources"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the announcement}}}\uc2  of UK prime minister \uc2 Rishi Sunak\uc2  that Britain will hold its general election on July 4.\par \par \uc2 There were no jokes about loss of empire or anything like that, the annual Fourth of July holiday marking independence day, where the US celebrates declaring independence from Great Britain in 1776 after the American revolution, throwing off British rule.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI was surprised to see it today,\u8221\'20\'1D Sullivan said, adding: \u8220\'20\'1CBut I do not have any real comment on it. We have a very strong, maybe that\u8217\'20\'19s an understatement, alliance with the UK, regardless of elections and prime ministers. We wish them well.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Sullivan said it would not affect the 50th {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/g7"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 G7}}}\uc2  summit, due to be held in Italy June 13 to 15, which Sunak is expected to attend.\par \par \uc2 Sullivan said the summit would be about strategy, not politics.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.55pm BST\par \par \uc2 US prefers two-state talks to unilateral declarations of Palestinian state - White House\par \par \uc2 The US is sticking to its policy of favoring talks leading to a two-state solution in the Middle East that guarantees the status of Israel and \u8220\'20\'1Csecurity for the Palestinian people\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 not declaring recognition for Palestine as three European countries did earlier today.\par \par \uc2 At the White House press briefing that\u8217\'20\'19s underway, with press secretary \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2  and national security advisor Jake Sullivan, in Washington, Sullivan was asked about Ireland, Spain and Norway {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/article/2024/may/22/palestinian-state-recognition-ireland-spain-recognise-palestine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 announcing}}}\uc2  they will formally recognize a Palestinian state on 28 May.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe believe in a two-state solution that should be brought about by direct talks between parties, not unilateral declarations,\u8221\'20\'1D Sullivan said.\par \par \uc2 He added moments later: \u8220\'20\'1CWe believe the only way we are going to achieve a two-state solution is through direct negotiations.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Sullivan did not say the word Palestine at any point.\par \par \uc2 He also said, when asked about Israel\u8217\'20\'19s growing diplomatic isolation in relation to its military offensive in Gaza, that \u8220\'20\'1Cwe certainly have seen a growing chorus of voices that had previously been in support of Israel drifting in another direction. That concerns us.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Sullivan added that it only boosted the US desire to see greater \u8220\'20\'1Cregional integration\u8221\'20\'1D, with a two state solution for Israelis and Palestinians and Israel \u8220\'20\'1Cbeing integrated with the modern Arab states,\u8221\'20\'1D which he had been discussing most recently with Saudi Arabia.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.25pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.26pm BST\par \par \uc2 The day so far\par \par \uc2 Democrats {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/live/2024/may/22/biden-trump-latest-alito-flag-supreme-court?page=with:block-664e12b08f0862e793a9fd83#block-664e12b08f0862e793a9fd83"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 are planning an offensive}}}\uc2  against the GOP over access to contraception, and have seized on a vote by Louisiana\u8217\'20\'19s Republican state lawmakers to tighten access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  medication and argue that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , the party\u8217\'20\'19s presumptive presidential nominee, will undermine reproductive rights, if elected. The party is also {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/live/2024/may/22/biden-trump-latest-alito-flag-supreme-court?page=with:block-664de4308f0808638b6465f6#block-664de4308f0808638b6465f6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 mulling a response}}}\uc2  to last week\u8217\'20\'19s report that conservative supreme court justice \uc2 Samuel Alito\uc2  once flew a flag associated with Trump\u8217\'20\'19s lies about the 2020 election, though top Senate Republican \uc2 Mitch McConnell{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/live/2024/may/22/biden-trump-latest-alito-flag-supreme-court?page=with:block-664e07d28f0859c6d0840e41#block-664e07d28f0859c6d0840e41"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 defended the court}}}\uc2 . The nine justices are still considering cases concerning Trump\u8217\'20\'19s immunity on charges related to meddling in the 2020 election, and on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access. The court announces {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/live/2024/may/22/biden-trump-latest-alito-flag-supreme-court?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-664def948f0862e793a9faf5#block-664def948f0862e793a9faf5"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 more decisions}}}\uc2  tomorrow, and those issues could be among them.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else is going on today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A Guardian {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/live/2024/may/22/biden-trump-latest-alito-flag-supreme-court?page=with:block-664e1aaa8f0862e793a9fe09#block-664e1aaa8f0862e793a9fe09"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 poll}}}\uc2  conducted by Harris found a majority of voters think the economy is in worse shape than it actually is, and are blaming \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Rudy Giuliani{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/live/2024/may/22/biden-trump-latest-alito-flag-supreme-court?page=with:block-664dfe3d8f0862e793a9fbe6#block-664dfe3d8f0862e793a9fbe6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reportedly agreed}}}\uc2  to stop attacking two Georgia election workers who last year won a major defamation judgment against him.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Republican House speaker Mike Johnson{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/live/2024/may/22/biden-trump-latest-alito-flag-supreme-court?page=with:block-664e22ab8f0862e793a9fed7#block-664e22ab8f0862e793a9fed7"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wants}}}\uc2  to \u8220\'20\'1Cpunish\u8221\'20\'1D the international criminal court for its chief prosecutor\u8217\'20\'19s request for arrest warrants against Israeli leaders.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.02pm BST\par \par \uc2 Mike Johnson, the Republican House speaker, says the United States should \u8220\'20\'1Cpunish\u8221\'20\'1D the international criminal court and its chief prosecutor, \uc2 Karim Khan\uc2 , who earlier this week requested arrest warrants for top Israeli and \uc2 Hamas\uc2  leaders:\par \par \uc2 Neither the US nor Israel are parties to the Rome Statute that governs the court, and \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has objected to Khan\u8217\'20\'19s applications for warrants against Israel\u8217\'20\'19s prime minister, \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2 , and the defense minister, Yoav Gallant.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, in Gaza, the humanitarian situation is on the verge of collapse despite the installation of a US-funded floating pier on its shoreline:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/article/2024/may/22/humanitarian-operations-near-collapse-in-gaza-says-wfp"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Humanitarian operations \u8216\'20\'18near collapse\u8217\'20\'19 in Gaza, says World Food Programme}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.56pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.41pm BST\par \par \uc2 Economic concerns loom large in the minds of voters nationwide, including in Georgia, a state \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  won in 2020, the first Democrat to do so in decades, But polls have shown the president\u8217\'20\'19s support slipping in the state, and as the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/michael-sainato"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Michael Sainato}}}\uc2  reports from rural Peach county, concerns over the availability of jobs and the affordability of essentials are one reason why:\par \par \uc2 Rows of pecan and peach trees frame the scenery throughout Peach county, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/state-of-georgia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Georgia}}}\uc2 , a rural area of central Georgia, about 100 miles south of Atlanta. A field of yellow school buses pack a lot on the way into Fort Valley, the county\u8217\'20\'19s seat, where the buses used across the US are manufactured.\par \par \uc2 Peach county is a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ajc.com/politics/in-georgias-bellwether-peach-county-divide-over-pandemic-and-president-trumps-all/MDZYUOIIAZCUZIILFS5VVPSD4A/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 swing county}}}\uc2  in what has emerged as one of the most important swing states in the presidential election. And, according to a March 2024 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://emersoncollegepolling.com/georgia-2024-poll-trump-46-biden-42/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 poll}}}\uc2  conducted by Emerson College, the economy is the most important issue to Georgia voters. About 32% of those polled said the economy was their top priority, trailed by immigration at 14% and healthcare at 12%.\par \par \uc2 In 2020, \uc2 Joe Biden{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/2020-election/results/georgia/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 won}}}\uc2  the state of Georgia by 0.2 percentage points. \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  won Peach county by just over 500 votes, 51.8% to 47.2%. Emerson\u8217\'20\'19s last poll found 46% of voters in Georgia currently support Trump to 42% supporting Biden, with 12% undecided \u8211\'20\'13 setting the state, and Peach county, on course for another nail-biting election where views on the economy will be key.\par \par \uc2 For Victoria Simmons, a retired local newspaper editor who lives in Byron, the economy is a top issue. \u8220\'20\'1CPeople can hardly afford to buy groceries and are losing hope,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CWe need to be focusing more on our own country rather than sending millions to places like Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf the election is fair and there is no tampering, I believe we will see a Trump victory,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/may/22/biden-trump-election-georgia-economy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Inflation, election lies and racial tension weigh on voters in Georgia swing county: \u8216\'20\'18We all got to eat\u8217\'20\'19}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.23pm BST\par \par \uc2 Guardian\uc2  poll draws worrying conclusion for Democrats about voters' perception of the economy\par \par \uc2 Democrats are having increasing trouble convincing voters that the US economy is in a healthy state, a new Harris poll conducted for the Guardian found.\par \par \uc2 Despite months of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/article/2024/may/03/us-april-jobs-report"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 strong job growth}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/article/2024/may/15/us-inflation-drops-slightly#:~:text=Inflation%20across%20the%20US%20eased,of%203.5%25%20the%20previous%20month."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 declines}}}\uc2  in the rate of inflation and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/article/2024/may/16/dow-jones-record-high"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 record highs}}}\uc2  in stock indices, the survey indicated that a majority of Americans wrongly believe the country is in a recession. More worryingly for \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s re-election prospects, nearly 60% blame \u8220\'20\'1Cmismanagement\u8221\'20\'1D from his administration for making the situation worse. Those findings line up with other polls that have shown voters giving the president poor marks for his handling of the economy.\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/lauren-aratani"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Lauren Aratani}}}\uc2  has a full breakdown of the survey\u8217\'20\'19s findings:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/may/22/poll-economy-recession-biden"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Majority of Americans wrongly believe US is in recession \u8211\'20\'13 and most blame Biden}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.57pm BST\par \par \uc2 Democrats go on the offensive against Trump, GOP, over contraception access\par \par \uc2 Democrats are looking for an edge against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , and are moving forward with plans to tie the ex-president and his Republican allies to efforts to cut off access to contraception.\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s campaign has seized on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/abortion-pills-louisiana-bill-advanced-77e2eb0320cbc56e89cec1b8ce694be8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a vote by Louisiana\u8217\'20\'19s Republican state lawmakers}}}\uc2  to reclassify two \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  drugs in a way that would make possessing them without a prescription a crime, calling it is a sign of policies to come if Trump is returned to the White House.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhat\u8217\'20\'19s happening right here in Louisiana is just one example of this dystopian agenda Trump and his allies are pushing,\u8221\'20\'1D Mitch Landrieu, the former New Orleans mayor who is a co-chair of Biden\u8217\'20\'19s campaign, said in a call with reporters. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s a far cry from \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , who are standing up for women\u8217\'20\'19s fundamental freedoms and leading a whole-of-government effort to protect and strengthen access to reproductive health care in the face of extreme Republican attacks. They are going to fight like hell to restore protections of Roe v Wade, and they will never allow a national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban to become law.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In the \uc2 US Senate\uc2 , Democratic majority leader \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  announced the chamber would on Thursday vote on the Right to Contraception Act, which is intended to protect access to the medication.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNow more than ever, contraception is a critical piece of protecting women\u8217\'20\'19s reproductive freedoms, standing as nothing short of a vital lifeline for millions of American women across the country,\u8221\'20\'1D Schumer said today in announcing the push. Senate legislation needs 60 votes to pass, and it is unclear if the measure will attract the Republican support necessary to clear that bar.\par \par \uc2 Democrats have benefited from public concern over reproductive rights generated by the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s 2022 ruling overturning Roe v Wade and allowing states to ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . They are banking on that support emerging again in the November presidential election, though, as the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/carter-sherman"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Carter Sherman}}}\uc2  reports, not all \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights supporters are comfortable with that strategy:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/may/09/florida-abortion-democrats-voting"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22  rights activists worry about Democrats piggybacking on the cause: \u8216\'20\'18This is not a ploy\u8217\'20\'19}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.23pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.34pm BST\par \par \uc2 Mike Johnson has his own problems, particularly when it comes to maintaining staff, the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/roberttait"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Robert Tait}}}\uc2  reports:\par \par \uc2 The Republican speaker of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/house-of-representatives"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 House of Representatives}}}\uc2 , Mike Johnson, is reeling from a sudden staff exodus as he struggles to keep his position and the GOP\u8217\'20\'19s tiny majority in the run-up to November\u8217\'20\'19s elections.\par \par \uc2 In the latest in a spate of resignations, Johnson\u8217\'20\'19s well-connected communications director, \uc2 Raj Shah\uc2 , a former White House deputy press secretary under \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , has confirmed he is leaving, Axios reported. He is expected to depart by the end of the summer.\par \par \uc2 News of his impending departure comes a day after it was announced that three top policy staff members, Brittan Specht, Jason Yaworske and Preston Hill, had quit and would leave by the end of May.\par \par \uc2 All three worked for the previous speaker, Kevin McCarthy, who was ousted in an internal party coup last October, but were retained by Johnson when he ascended to the speaker\u8217\'20\'19s chair.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/may/22/mike-johnson-staff-resignation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Mike Johnson\u8217\'20\'19s woes continue after exodus of staff in run-up to elections}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.17pm BST\par \par \uc2 Next week, jurors in New York City will begin deliberating over whether \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is guilty of charges related to falsifying business documents to conceal hush money payments ahead of the 2016 election.\par \par \uc2 Earlier today Mike Johnson, the Republican House speaker, was asked for his thoughts on the allegation that Trump was trying to cover up extra-martial affairs. Johnson is a longtime ally of the former president, and indicated nothing he had heard from the trial had shaken his faith:\par \par \uc2 enltrCNN's {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/mkraju?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @mkraju}}}\uc2  : "You've been very clear about your disdain for the hush money case, but what about the underlying alleged conduct of paying off a porn star to keep this extramarital affair allegedly quiet?"\par \par \uc2 Speaker Mike Johnson: "I'm not gonna comment on that." {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/G9BPWLwxhU"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/G9BPWLwxhU}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1793297763863601585?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 22, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s defense attorneys concluded their arguments yesterday, without calling him as a witness to testify. Closing arguments are scheduled for next Tuesday and the jury is expected to begin deliberating the following day. Here\u8217\'20\'19s a look back at the trial\u8217\'20\'19s conclusion:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/may/21/trump-hush-money-trial-defense-final-stretch"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Mr Trump, why won\u8217\'20\'19t you testify?\u8217\'20\'19: hush-money trial nears end with a fizzle, not a bang}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.45pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.59pm BST\par \par \uc2 Republicans are standing behind \uc2 Samuel Alito\uc2  after the \uc2 New York Times\uc2  reported that a flag associated with \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s lies about the 2020 election flew outside his home shortly before \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  took office.\par \par \uc2 The Senate minority leader \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2 , who together with Trump was instrumental in creating the six-justice conservative supermajority on the court, was asked about the Times\u8217\'20\'19s story yesterday. Here\u8217\'20\'19s what he had to say:\par \par \uc2 enltrCNN's {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/mkraju?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @mkraju}}}\uc2  : "Should [Justice Alito] recuse himself in any cases related to the election?"\par \par \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2 : "It seems to me they're just nonstop attacks on the Supreme Court, week after week... We need to leave the Supreme Court alone." {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/ZSokCjYWFo"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/ZSokCjYWFo}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1793000124907450656?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 21, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.43pm BST\par \par \uc2 A handful of states held primaries last night, including Georgia, where Democrats in the Atlanta-area Fulton county made \uc2 Fani Willis\uc2  their nominee for district attorney once again. You may remember her as the prosecutor who brought charges against Trump and 18 others for trying to overturn the state\u8217\'20\'19s 2020 election. Here\u8217\'20\'19s more about her primary win, from the Associated Press:\par \par \uc2 Fani Willis\uc2 , the Fulton county district attorney overseeing Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s expansive criminal case against {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  and his allies for attempting to overturn the 2020 election, has won her Democratic primary bid for re-election with nearly 90% of the vote.\par \par \uc2 Willis and Judge Scott McAfee \u8211\'20\'13 who won his primary election on Tuesday \u8211\'20\'13 are central figures in the prosecution against the former president and associates in his orbit accused of conspiring to overturn the 2020 presidential election.\par \par \uc2 Willis will now face the Republican lawyer Courtney Kramer in November. With her high name recognition, the advantages of incumbency and a hefty fundraising haul, Willis\u8217\'20\'19s victory in the primary was not terribly surprising.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/may/21/fani-willis-georgia-election-result"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump prosecutor Fani Willis wins Georgia primary election}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.22pm BST\par \par \uc2 Giuliani agrees to stop fraud accusations against Georgia election workers - report\par \par \uc2 Rudy Giuliani\uc2  has agreed to stop accusing two Georgia election workers of fraud, according to a court filing {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/politics-news/giuliani-stop-defaming-georgia-election-workers-trump-rcna153449?taid=664dfa93d9bd10000192545d&utm_campaign=trueanthem&utm_medium=social&utm_source=twitter"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 seen by NBC News}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Ruby Freeman and Shaye Moss won a more than $148m judgment against Giuliani last year after a jury found he defamed them with untrue statements about their conduct during the 2020 election. Giuliani filed for bankruptcy following the judgment, and NBC News reports he has agreed to no longer attack them, and to comply with the judgment.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more about the very expensive case for the former New York City mayor:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/dec/15/rudy-giuliani-pay-damages-election-workers-defamation-trial"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Rudy Giuliani ordered to pay $148.1m in damages for lies about election workers}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.04pm BST\par \par \uc2 Steve Cohen\uc2 , a Democratic congressman, has introduced {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cohen.house.gov/media-center/press-releases/congressman-cohen-introduces-resolution-censure-against-justice-alito"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a resolution}}}\uc2  to censure \uc2 Samuel Alito\uc2  over the flag flown outside his house that was associated with \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s baseless election fraud claims.\par \par \uc2 The conservative supreme court justice has said the banner was raised after his wife got into a dispute with their neighbor. Cohen\u8217\'20\'19s resolution demands Alito recuse himself from considering cases dealing with the January 6 insurrection or 2020 election.\par \par \uc2 It also censures him \u8220\'20\'1Cfor knowingly violating the federal recusal statute and binding ethics standards and calling the impartiality of the supreme court of the United States into question by continuing to participate in cases in which his prior public conduct could be reasonably interpreted to demonstrate bias\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 In a statement, Cohen, of Tennessee, accused Alito of showing support for those who attacked the Capitol:\par \par \uc2 Beyond poor judgment, Justice Alito\u8217\'20\'19s misuse of the American flag is a knowing and shameless demonstration of his political bias. He literally flew a flag in front of his house showing the world he supported the January 6 th insurrectionists. What\u8217\'20\'19s more, he continues to participate in litigation directly related to the 2020 election and the insurrection, in direct violation of the federal recusal statute and the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s own ethics rules.\par \par \uc2 Republicans control the House, and it is unlikely they will allow Cohen\u8217\'20\'19s resolution to pass.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.51pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.42pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s legal troubles have made their way into a variety of courtrooms, including Aileen Cannon\u8217\'20\'19s chambers in Florida. She is the Trump-appointed federal judge handling his case on charges related to possessing classified documents, and recently postponed his trial indefinitely. Today, she is hearing arguments over whether to dismiss his case, the Associated Press reports:\par \par \uc2 Prosecutors and defense lawyers in the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/trump-justice-department-indictment-classified-documents-miami-8315a5b23c18f27083ed64eef21efff3"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 classified documents case}}}\uc2  against the former president are due in court on Wednesday for the first time since the judge indefinitely postponed the trial earlier this month.\par \par \uc2 The case, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/projects/trump-investigations-civil-criminal-tracker/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 one of four criminal prosecutions against Trump}}}\uc2 , had been set for trial on 20 May but {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/trump-trial-classified-documents-judge-cannon-6f910c3cbe8d91e493ab5fb13019d45f"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US district judge Aileen Cannon cited numerous issues}}}\uc2  she had yet to resolve as a basis for canceling the trial date.\par \par \uc2 On Wednesday, Cannon was scheduled to hear arguments on a Trump request to dismiss the indictment on grounds that it fails to clearly articulate a crime and instead amounts to \u8220\'20\'1Ca personal and political attack against President Trump\u8221\'20\'1D with a \u8220\'20\'1Clitany of uncharged grievances both for public and media consumption\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Prosecutors on special counsel \uc2 Jack Smith\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s team, which brought the case, will argue against that request. Trump is not expected to be present for the hearing.\par \par \uc2 The motion is one of several that Trump\u8217\'20\'19s lawyers have filed to dismiss the case, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/trump-classified-documents-maralago-presidential-records-200d4c73d7c7dd75d9c9d878b77d05ce"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 some of which have already been denied}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/may/22/trump-classified-documents-case-hearing"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump classified documents case: judge holds hearing on dismissing charges}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.52pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.26pm BST\par \par \uc2 Supreme court to issue more decisions on Thursday with \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and Trump immunity cases pending\par \par \uc2 The supreme court is set to issue its latest decisions on Thursday, potentially on some of the hot-button topic pending before the conservative-dominated body.\par \par \uc2 While there\u8217\'20\'19s no telling in advance which cases the nine justices may rule on, two suits dealing with \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and one directly with \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  have yet to be resolved.\par \par \uc2 We will start with the one concerning the former president. He has asked the justices to rule that he is immune from federal prosecution for attempting to overturn the 2020 election, and in oral arguments, several conservative justices sounded partial to that argument. If they indeed reach that conclusion, it could further delay a trial that may prove pivotal to his chances of winning the 2024 election. Here\u8217\'20\'19s more on that:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/25/supreme-court-trump-immunity-claim"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US supreme court eyes returning Trump immunity claim to lower court after arguments}}}\par \par \uc2 The other two cases deal with \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , an issue that polls have shown is a top concern for voters, and one in which Democrats have had an edge ever since the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s conservatives overturned Roe v Wade two years ago, and allowed states to ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  doctors have asked the justices to roll back the availability of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill mifepristone but, in their oral arguments, the justices sounded skeptical:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/mar/26/us-supreme-court-abortion-pill-case-mifepristone"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US supreme court seems skeptical of arguments against \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  drug mifepristone}}}\par \par \uc2 The outcome was less apparent in a clash between the Biden administration and Idaho over whether federally funded hospitals could be required to perform abortions in emergencies, even in states that ban the procedure:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/2024/apr/24/us-supreme-court-abortion-rights-emtala"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US supreme court appears divided after hearing arguments on emergency \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  care}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.31pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.02pm BST\par \par \uc2 House Democrat proposes censuring supreme court justice Alito after reports of flag connected to Trump election lies\par \par \uc2 Good morning, US politics blog readers. It has been nearly a week since the \uc2 New York Times{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2024/05/16/us/justice-alito-upside-down-flag.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 broke the news}}}\uc2  that a flag associated with \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s baseless fraud claims about the 2020 election flew outside the house of the conservative supreme court justice \uc2 Samuel Alito\uc2 , and Democrats appear to be gearing up to respond. Congressman \uc2 Steve Cohen\uc2  has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cohen.house.gov/media-center/press-releases/congressman-cohen-introduces-resolution-censure-against-justice-alito"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 proposed}}}\uc2  censuring Alito, while yesterday \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2 , the Senate\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic leader, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/ReedReports/status/1792993580341977243"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  flying the flag \u8220\'20\'1Ccasts some doubt on [his] impartiality\u8221\'20\'1D, and added he would be looking for ways to respond. Last year, Democrats {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/may/02/republicans-democrats-supreme-court-ethics-rules"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 convened}}}\uc2  the Senate judiciary committee to try to build support for legislation requiring the court to impose an enforceable code of ethics following earlier reports of ties between conservative justices and wealthy parties with interests before the court. But that legislation went nowhere in the face of Republican opposition, and there is no sign of that calculus changing today. Meanwhile, the conservative-dominated court is considering cases whose outcomes could weigh on the November presidential election, including Trump\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/25/supreme-court-trump-criminal-trial-immunity-key-takeaways"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 bid for immunity}}}\uc2  from charges related to his attempt to stop \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  from taking office. We\u8217\'20\'19ll let you know if Democrats elaborate on their next steps today.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else is going on:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Most Americans wrongly believe the country is in a recession, and put the blame on Biden, a new Harris poll conducted for the Guardian {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/may/22/poll-economy-recession-biden"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 finds}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Aileen Cannon, the judge in Trump\u8217\'20\'19s classified documents case who recently delayed his trial indefinitely, will {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/may/22/trump-classified-documents-case-hearing"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 hold a hearing}}}\uc2  on motions from his lawyers to dismiss the charges.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Biden welcomes Kenya\u8217\'20\'19s president \uc2 William Ruto\uc2  to the White House at 4pm, where they will meet with CEOs and business leaders.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240522ek5m001s3\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
