\par\par \uc2 World news\par \b \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Meet Baby Olivia\u8217\'20\'19: spate of new bills would require showing anti- \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  video in schools\b0\par\par\uc2 Carter Sherman \par \uc2 1,598 \uc2 words\par \uc2 21 May 2024\par 17:31 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Video of fetus in disembodied womb required viewing for students in two states, as classroom becomes latest front in post-Roe \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  wars\par \par \uc2 Awash in soft, peach-colored light, the infant yawns, sticks her thumb in her mouth and flutters her eyes at the camera. As the camera pulls away from her, an umbilical cord and the fleshy tunnel surrounding the infant comes into focus. This isn\u8217\'20\'19t a newborn baby: it\u8217\'20\'19s a fetus in a disembodied womb.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is Olivia,\u8221\'20\'1D a British female voice narrates. \u8220\'20\'1CThough she has yet to greet the outside world, she has already completed an amazing journey.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Say hello to \u8220\'20\'1CMeet Baby Olivia\u8221\'20\'1D, an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=S-lQOooYAs8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 animated video}}}\uc2  made by an American anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  group that purports to depict humans\u8217\'20\'19 embryonic and fetal development in an alleged effort to convert young people to the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  cause. The video \u8211\'20\'13 or something very close to it \u8211\'20\'13 will be required viewing for public school students in two states, with several more potentially on the way.\par \par \uc2 Last year, North Dakota became the first state in the nation to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://ndlegis.gov/assembly/68-2023/regular/bill-overview/bo1265.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pass a law}}}\uc2  mandating that schools screen \u8220\'20\'1CMeet Baby Olivia\u8221\'20\'1D or a similar video. This year, Tennessee enacted its own \u8220\'20\'1CMeet Baby Olivia\u8221\'20\'1D law, requiring that \u8220\'20\'1CMeet Baby Olivia\u8221\'20\'1D or something like it be shown as part of schools\u8217\'20\'19 sex education curriculum.\par \par \uc2 So far in 2024, legislators in at least 10 other states have introduced bills that would require schools to show students \u8220\'20\'1CMeet Baby Olivia\u8221\'20\'1D or, in language that appears repeatedly throughout the bills, a similar \u8220\'20\'1Chigh-quality, computer-generated rendering or animation\u8221\'20\'1D that shows \u8220\'20\'1Cevery stage of human development inside the uterus, noting significant markers in cell growth and organ development for every significant marker of pregnancy until birth\u8221\'20\'1D. Including Tennessee\u8217\'20\'19s legislation, bills in at least five of the states cite \u8220\'20\'1CMeet Baby Olivia\u8221\'20\'1D by name.\par \par \uc2 Classrooms are a burgeoning front in the post-Roe v Wade \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  wars, as conservative activists have increasingly intertwined their attacks on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  with their distaste for sex ed that discusses alternatives to premarital abstinence. But medical professionals have accused the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  group behind \u8220\'20\'1CMeet Baby Olivia\u8221\'20\'1D of spreading propaganda and even misinformation in order to convert young people to their cause.\par \par \uc2 Seven of the 12 states where the bills have been introduced or passed ban almost all abortions. So far this year, state legislatures have considered at least 135 sex-ed bills \u8211\'20\'13 a record number, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2024/05/16/politics/sex-education-bills-united-states-dg/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to a CNN analysis}}}\uc2 . Sixty per cent of them would restrict sex ed in some way.\par \par \uc2 Live Action has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.liveaction.org/news/baby-olivia-medically-accurate-fetal-development-media/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 denied accusations}}}\uc2  that any sentence of \u8220\'20\'1CMeet Baby Olivia\u8221\'20\'1D is inaccurate.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\u8216\'20\'18Baby Olivia\u8217\'20\'19 isn\u8217\'20\'19t about \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . It never says the word \u8216\'20\'18\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19,\u8221\'20\'1D said Noah Brandt, Live Action\u8217\'20\'19s vice-president of communications. \u8220\'20\'1C\u8216\'20\'18Baby Olivia\u8217\'20\'19 is an important place for states like Tennessee and North Dakota to turn to next, to continue to do work to educate on both biology and life, because they\u8217\'20\'19ve already protected life so now it\u8217\'20\'19s about teaching people when life begins and to respect that.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 A quiet success story\par \par \uc2 The emergence of the \u8220\'20\'1CMeet Baby Olivia\u8221\'20\'1D legislation comes at a precarious time for the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  movement. Since the overturning of Roe, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/article/2024/may/14/abortion-rights-support-poll"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 support for \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  rights has mounted}}}\uc2  even in conservative states. Some Republicans have tried to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/10/arizona-republicans-against-state-abortion-ban"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 downplay their opposition}}}\uc2  to the procedure or {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/may/02/arizona-1864-abortion-ban-repealed-governor"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 even supported efforts}}}\uc2  to protect it, in a sharp departure from decades of marching in lock step with the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  movement.\par \par \uc2 But as the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  movement flounders, the \u8220\'20\'1CMeet Baby Olivia\u8221\'20\'1D bills are a quiet success story. \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  opponents overturned Roe by spending years pushing for state-level \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions; if a restriction was successful in one state, lawmakers in other states would copy-paste its language and introduce their own versions. This strategy gnawed away access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In the \u8220\'20\'1CMeet Baby Olivia\u8221\'20\'1D bills, observers see a similar strategy at play \u8211\'20\'13 and evidence of mission creep.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAnti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , anti-sexual and [anti]-reproductive health movements have been focusing on other areas and expanding their scope in terms of what is relevant to them and what they\u8217\'20\'19re working on,\u8221\'20\'1D said Kimya Forouzan, principal policy associate of state issues at the \uc2 Guttmacher Institute\uc2 , which supports \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights. Although Guttmacher tracks restrictions on sexual and reproductive health, Forouzan said that she had never before seen legislation quite like the \u8220\'20\'1CMeet Baby Olivia\u8221\'20\'1D bills.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19ve seen a lot of attempts at omitting information from sex ed,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CBut this is such an explicit effort to put misleading curriculum into sex ed.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 American College of Obstetricians and Gynecologists\uc2 , the pre-eminent US membership organization for OB-GYNs, issued a statement denouncing \u8220\'20\'1CMeet Baby Olivia\u8221\'20\'1D as \u8220\'20\'1Cdesigned to manipulate the emotions of viewers rather than to share evidence-based, scientific information about embryonic and fetal development\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The organization continued: \u8220\'20\'1CMany of the claims made in this video are not aligned with scientific fact, but rather reflect the biased and ideologic perspectives of the extremists who created the video.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In \u8220\'20\'1CMeet Baby Olivia\u8221\'20\'1D, the narrator says that life begins when a sperm fertilizes an egg, but there is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.npr.org/sections/health-shots/2022/08/27/1119684376/when-does-life-begin-as-state-laws-define-it-science-politics-and-religion-clash"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 no scientific consensus}}}\uc2  on when life starts \u8211\'20\'13 and it is as much a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2022/12/31/us/human-life-begin.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 philosophical and religious question}}}\uc2  as a scientific one. The narrator also says that \u8220\'20\'1COlivia\u8217\'20\'19s heartbeat can be detected\u8221\'20\'1D roughly three weeks after fertilization, or five weeks after the first day of a woman\u8217\'20\'19s last menstrual period, which is what the medical establishment uses to calculate a pregnancy\u8217\'20\'19s length. At that point in pregnancy, the embryo does not yet have a fully developed heart.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI would say we could start to see activity that could be a cardiac activity, maybe around six weeks to seven weeks of pregnancy,\u8221\'20\'1D said Dr Stacy Sun, a New York-based OB-GYN and fellow with Physicians for Reproductive Health. \u8220\'20\'1CThe question is whether or not that\u8217\'20\'19s a heartbeat as another question, because that\u8217\'20\'19s not really a fully formed heart.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf we\u8217\'20\'19re getting down to the nitty-gritty of what\u8217\'20\'19s medically accurate, those words aren\u8217\'20\'19t medically accurate,\u8221\'20\'1D she added.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMeet Baby Olivia\u8221\'20\'1D also claims that, 20 weeks after fertilization \u8211\'20\'13 or 22 weeks of pregnancy \u8211\'20\'13 \u8220\'20\'1Cwith a lot of help, babies have survived outside the womb\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Fetal viability, or the point at which an infant can survive outside the womb, is typically dated at around 22 weeks after fertilization, or 24 weeks of pregnancy. While there have been cases of babies surviving after being born just 20 weeks after fertilization, fetal viability is attenuated to each individual pregnancy, particularly since many regions of the United States lack adequate OB-GYN facilities or expertise, which could help women who give birth too early. The most premature baby to ever survive, according to Guinness World Records, was born 19 weeks and 1 day after fertilization. He {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.uab.edu/news/health/item/12427-uab-hospital-delivers-record-breaking-premature-baby#:~:text=Guinness%20World%20Records%20%E2%80%93%20The%20most,making%20him%20132%20days%20premature."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 stayed in an Alabama hospital}}}\uc2  for 275 days.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere\u8217\'20\'19s so many nuances when it comes to whether or not a baby can survive, especially when they\u8217\'20\'19re that young,\u8221\'20\'1D Sun said. \u8220\'20\'1CEven if they do survive, they don\u8217\'20\'19t have a great quality of life. The effect of it can be devastating on the person carrying the pregnancy, the baby.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 On the \u8220\'20\'1CMeet Baby Olivia\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 YouTube\uc2  page, Live Action says that the video has been \u8220\'20\'1Creviewed by accredited medical professionals\u8221\'20\'1D. Two of the professionals who are cited as reviewing \u8220\'20\'1CMeet Baby Olivia\u8221\'20\'1D work for the Charlotte Lozier Institute, the research arm of the powerful anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  group Susan B Anthony Pro-Life America. Another is a doctor who is credited as, at the time, working for the American College of Pediatricians, an organization that the \uc2 Southern Poverty Law Center\uc2  has labeled an anti-LGBTQ+ hate group.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COur medical recommendations are evidence-based and focused on fostering children\u8217\'20\'19s optimal physical and emotional health and well-being. Any label to the contrary is simply false,\u8221\'20\'1D the American College of Pediatricians said in a statement. On its website, which says the group is not anti-LGBTQ+, the organization says that children are better off when raised by married heterosexual couples rather than same-sex couples and that \u8220\'20\'1Csame-sex sexual behavior is associated with serious physical and psychological health risks at significantly high rates\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 In at least two states, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wvlegislature.gov/Bill_Status/bills_text.cfm?billdoc=sb468%20sub2%20eng.htm&yr=2024&sesstype=RS&i=468"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 West Virginia}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.legis.iowa.gov/legislation/BillBook?ga=90&ba=HF%202617"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Iowa}}}\uc2 , \u8220\'20\'1CMeet Baby Olivia\u8221\'20\'1D bills passed one legislative chamber, but both state legislatures have now shuttered for the year. Most of the legislatures that introduced \u8220\'20\'1CMeet Baby Olivia\u8221\'20\'1D bills have either ended their 2024 sessions or are set to do so in the next few weeks.\par \par \uc2 Compared to the rest of the country, the states that have introduced \u8220\'20\'1CMeet Baby Olivia\u8221\'20\'1D bills this year \u8211\'20\'13 which also include Georgia, Hawaii, Kentucky, Michigan, Missouri, Pennsylvania, and South Carolina \u8211\'20\'13 have less comprehensive sex-ed policies, according to Siecus: Sex Ed for Social Change, a decades-old organization that issues best practice guidelines for comprehensive sex ed. (None of the states garnered more than a C grade in the Siecus ranking system.) Most states do not require public school sex ed to be medically accurate, culturally appropriate or unbiased, according to Guttmacher. Only four states say that sex ed cannot promote religion.\par \par \uc2 Brandt argues that information about \u8220\'20\'1Chuman development\u8221\'20\'1D needs to be included in sex ed, because \u8220\'20\'1Cthe creation of a new human\u8221\'20\'1D is a potential consequence of sex.\par \par \uc2 Asked if the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  movement should get more involved in shaping sex ed, Brandt answered: \u8220\'20\'1CYeah, definitely, yes.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240521ek5l001b9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
