\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Nevada activists secure signatures for vote on  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  access in November\b0\par\par\uc2 Carter Sherman \par \uc2 681 \uc2 words\par \uc2 20 May 2024\par 20:25 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Nearly double number of signatures needed turned in to get measure to enshrine \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in constitution on ballot\par \par \uc2 Activists in Nevada, a key state in the upcoming US presidential elections, announced on Monday afternoon that they had turned in nearly double the number of signatures they need to get an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -related measure on the November ballot.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2023/nov/10/state-abortion-laws-us"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Nevada currently allows abortions}}}\uc2  up until fetal viability, or the point at which an infant can survive outside the womb, which is generally pegged to around 24 weeks of pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 Activists are hoping that, by enshrining the right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the state constitution, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access will be protected from any legislative attempts to limit it.\par \par \uc2 State officials still need to verify the signatures before confirming the measure will appear on the ballot. If the measure moves forward, Democrats are hoping that it will boost their candidates in the battleground state \u8211\'20\'13 particularly Joe Biden, who is currently trailing \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in Nevada polling.\par \par \uc2 Ultimately, about a dozen states may vote on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights come November, a prospect that could radically rewrite the map of US \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access. Organizers in several states \u8211\'20\'13 including Arizona, another state that will be hotly contested in presidential election \u8211\'20\'13 are still collecting signatures for ballot measures, or have turned in signatures and are waiting for confirmation that their measure will advance to the ballot. At least one measure has already stumbled: in New York, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/may/07/new-york-abortion-rights-amendment-blocked"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a judge has knocked an \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  rights measure}}}\uc2  off the November ballot, ruling that state legislators who championed the measure failed to follow protocol.\par \par \uc2 But in the last few weeks, officials and organizers in several states have announced that voters will get a direct say on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 Colorado\par \par \uc2 On Friday, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/may/17/colorado-abortion-rights-ballot"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a Colorado state official confirmed}}}\uc2  that voters will get to decide whether to add \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights into the state\u8217\'20\'19s constitution. A deep-blue state, Colorado already permits \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after fetal viability. That\u8217\'20\'19s later than most states \u8211\'20\'13 and has made Colorado a haven for both women who are fleeing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans and women who are seeking abortions later on in pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 Only a fraction of abortions occur after the first trimester of pregnancy. When women do get abortions past that point, they may be facing a medical emergency or learned of a fetal anomaly (many of which can only be detected later on in pregnancy). \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers have also said that, since Roe fell, bans have delayed people\u8217\'20\'19s ability to get abortions and thus pushed them later into pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 Florida\par \par \uc2 On 1 May, Florida {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/may/03/florida-abortion-ban-clinic"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 outlawed \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  past six weeks of pregnancy}}}\uc2 , in effect demolishing the last stronghold of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access in the deep south. Now, Florida activists are hoping to enshrine \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in the state constitution and restore providers\u8217\'20\'19 ability to help \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  seekers fleeing southern \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans.\par \par \uc2 To succeed, they will need 60% of the vote. That may be a tall order in an increasingly red state.\par \par \uc2 Maryland\par \par \uc2 Like Nevada and Colorado, Maryland already permits \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . However, if voters pass a measure to enshrine the right to \u8220\'20\'1Creproductive freedom\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 a potentially broad phrase \u8211\'20\'13 into the state constitution, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  will be shielded the procedure from legislative attacks.\par \par \uc2 South Dakota\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights activists in South Dakota, which currently bans \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/may/17/south-dakota-abortion-vote-rights-ban"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 hoping to revive the right to \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  in the first trimester of pregnancy. Notably, they may face one of the greatest uphill battles out of any ballot measure campaign in the country. \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights are generally popular and have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/article/2024/may/14/abortion-rights-support-poll"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 only grown more so}}}\uc2  in the wake of Roe\u8217\'20\'19s fall, but there are a handful of states where most residents do not support legalizing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . South Dakota is one of them, according to recent research from the Public Religion Research Institute.\par \par \uc2 The measure proposed in South Dakota does not go as far as those of other states. Rather than protecting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access until fetal viability, its proposal would allow states to regulate it in the second trimester of pregnancy and prohibit it in the third.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240520ek5k002ux\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
