\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Colorado voters to decide on  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  rights after measure qualifies for ballot\b0\par\par\uc2 Guardian staff and agencies \par \uc2 280 \uc2 words\par \uc2 20 May 2024\par 13:40 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Supporters gather enough valid signatures to put measure \u8211\'20\'13 that would enshrine \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights into constitution \u8211\'20\'13 on to ballot\par \par \uc2 Voters in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/colorado"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Colorado}}}\uc2  will have a say on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights this fall after supporters collected enough valid signatures to put a measure on the ballot, part of a national push to pose \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights questions to voters since the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  removed the nationwide right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The Colorado measure officially made the ballot on Friday and would enshrine \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights into the constitution in a state which already allows \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  at all stages of pregnancy despite the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s overturning of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Roe v Wade}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Since that 2022 decision, most Republican-controlled states have new \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions in effect, including 14 that ban it at every stage of pregnancy. Most Democratic-led states have laws or executive orders to protect access.\par \par \uc2 The announcement on Friday about Colorado\u8217\'20\'19s measure making the November ballot came from the state\u8217\'20\'19s top election official. It would also include requirements that Medicaid and private health insurers cover abortions.\par \par \uc2 Supporters had said they gathered more than 225,000 signatures to put the issue on the ballot, nearly double the requirement of more than 124,000 signatures.\par \par \uc2 Amending the state constitution requires the support of 55% of voters.\par \par \uc2 Those backing a dueling measure \u8211\'20\'13 a law to ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 did not turn in signatures, and that measure will not go before voters.\par \par \uc2 The news in Colorado came a day after South Dakota {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/may/17/south-dakota-abortion-vote-rights-ban"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 announced}}}\uc2  voters would decide on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights there this fall as well.\par \par \uc2 The Associated Press contributed reporting\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240520ek5k002h6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
