\par\par \uc2 World news\par \b \uc2 More than half of US Black women aged 15-49 live under  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  bans \u8211\'20\'13 report\b0\par\par\uc2 Gloria Oladipo \par \uc2 498 \uc2 words\par \uc2 15 May 2024\par 16:35 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Study finds 57% of Black women of reproductive age live in the 26 states with \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans or restrictions\par \par \uc2 More than half of Black women in the US who are of reproductive age live in states with \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans or restrictions, according to a new report.\par \par \uc2 The study, by the \uc2 National Partnership for Women & Families\uc2  (NPWF) and the non-profit In Our Own Voice, shows the stark impact of overturning Roe v Wade on Black women, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/news/nbcblk/57-percent-black-women-abortion-bans-restictions-rcna151972"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 NBC News reported}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 More than 6.7 million Black women \u8211\'20\'13 nearly 57% of Black women in the US between the ages of 15 and 49 \u8211\'20\'13 live in the 26 states that have restricted or banned \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  since Roe was overturned in June 2022.\par \par \uc2 According to polling from Our Own Voice, Black women living in states with recent \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans or restrictions reported thinking about not having children, relocating to states with fewer restrictions, and other concerns.\par \par \uc2 A majority of Black mothers also live in states with \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans or restrictions, the study found. Previous research has found that mothers unable to access \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/30389101/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 experienced}}}\uc2  increased financial challenges for themselves and their children.\par \par \uc2 The study also found that 2.7 million Black women who live in states that restrict \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  are \u8220\'20\'1Ceconomically insecure\u8221\'20\'1D, making them more likely to lack financial resources to travel to receive \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care.\par \par \uc2 Seventy per cent of Black women who are uninsured and 49.8% who use Medicaid as their primary insurance also live in states with \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions or bans, which can impede access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  services.\par \par \uc2 Jocelyn Frye, president of the NPWF, told NBC that understanding the concerns of Black women can help address barriers to care facing other demographics of women.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhen you look at the experiences of Black women, you can address a lot of different barriers that women face, whether it\u8217\'20\'19s from race, gender \u8211\'20\'13 there are also women with disabilities,\u8221\'20\'1D Frye said. \u8220\'20\'1CBlack women are often the bellwether of how well things are working. So when we fix things for Black women, we fix them for a lot of people.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The report also shows the intersection between \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions and states with higher maternal mortality rates, a health crisis {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jul/23/america-black-maternal-mortality-crisis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 disproportionately}}}\uc2  affecting Black women. According to the study, 17 of the 26 states that have restricted \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access also have above-average maternal mortality rates.\par \par \uc2 The report comes as Black women increasingly say \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access is their top voting issue ahead of the 2024 presidential election.\par \par \uc2 A {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.kff.org/womens-health-policy/poll-finding/kff-health-tracking-poll-march-2024-abortion-in-the-2024-election-and-beyond/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 March poll}}}\uc2  from KFF, a health policy research organization, found that 28% of Black women voters said \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  was the most important issue to their vote in 2024, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/black-women-abortion-top-issue-election-voters-da88c34a9390732b89f25c9c11f262f0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Associated Press reported}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The Our Own Voice report also found that the majority of Black adults support reproductive rights and access, with 77% of those polled saying they believe \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  should be legal in all or most cases.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240515ek5f002be\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
