\par\par \uc2 World news\par \b \uc2 US support for  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  rights up four points to 60% since fall of Roe v Wade\b0\par\par\uc2 Carter Sherman \par \uc2 591 \uc2 words\par \uc2 14 May 2024\par 11:17 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 New polling data from \uc2 Pew\uc2  shows shift in Americans\u8217\'20\'19 opinion since loss of constitutional right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in June 2022\par \par \uc2 In the two years after the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  overturned Roe v Wade, leading to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans across many parts of the south and midwest, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights have only grown more popular, new polling from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.pewresearch.org/politics/2024/05/13/broad-public-support-for-legal-abortion-persists-2-years-after-dobbs/?utm_source=AdaptiveMailer&utm_medium=email&utm_campaign=24-05-13%20Abortion%20GEN%20DISTRO&org=982&lvl=100&ite=13991&lea=3375400&ctr=0&par=1&trk=a0DQm000001nkFdMAI"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Pew research}}}\uc2  Center has found.\par \par \uc2 A majority of Americans has long supported \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights. But more than 60% of Americans now believe \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  should be legal in all or most cases \u8211\'20\'13 a four percentage-point jump from 2021, the year before Roe fell.\par \par \uc2 This support transcends numerous demographic divides in US society: most men, women, white people, Black people, Hispanic people and Asian people believe \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  should be legal in all or most cases. It extends to majorities of all age groups and education levels, although 18-to-29-year-olds and people with more education are more likely than other cohorts to believe \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  should be legal in all or most cases.\par \par \uc2 People who live under \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans have also become increasingly supportive of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access since the overturning of Roe in June 2022. In August 2019, only 30% of people who live in states where \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is now outlawed said they believed it should be easier to access \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Today, 42% of people in the same states say that.\par \par \uc2 The broad support for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  may prove pivotal in the upcoming US elections \u8211\'20\'13 Joe Biden\u8217\'20\'19s re-election campaign has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/apr/13/democrats-abortion-voter-arizona-florida"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 zeroed in on \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  as a winning issue}}}\uc2  as the president continues to trail \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in polls. Battleground states such as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/may/02/arizona-1864-abortion-ban-repealed-governor"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Arizona}}}\uc2  and Nevada are expected to hold ballot measures to protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, which {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/may/09/florida-abortion-democrats-voting"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Democrats hope will boost}}}\uc2  both voter turnout and their own chances.\par \par \uc2 Democrats are far more likely than Republicans to support \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, with 85% of Democrats and Democratic-leaning voters believing that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  should be legal in all or most circumstances. By contrast, 41% of Republican or Republican-leaning voters said the same.\par \par \uc2 GOP opposition to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is largely fueled by conservative Republicans, since more than 70% who identify as such think \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  should be illegal in all or most circumstances. More than two-thirds of moderate and liberal Republicans support \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, Pew found.\par \par \uc2 Among the groups measured by Pew, conservative Republicans and white evangelical Protestants were the only groups with majorities that opposed \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access. Nearly three-quarters of white evangelical Protestants think \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  should be illegal in all or most circumstances.\par \par \uc2 Some people\u8217\'20\'19s views of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  did grow more complex the deeper Pew inquired. Most groups that support \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights ultimately thought \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  should be legal in \u8220\'20\'1Cmost\u8221\'20\'1D circumstances, rather than \u8220\'20\'1Call\u8221\'20\'1D. In other polling on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , support for the procedure tends to dwindle when people are asked whether they would back abortions in the second or third trimester of pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 More strikingly, \uc2 Pew\uc2  also asked Americans to evaluate how much they agreed with certain statements about \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . More than half of Americans agreed with the statement that \u8220\'20\'1Cthe decision about whether to have an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  should belong solely to the pregnant woman\u8221\'20\'1D, while only 35% of Americans say they agreed that \u8220\'20\'1Chuman life begins at conception, so an embryo is a person with rights\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 a stance that would logically lead them to oppose \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Yet a third of Americans said that both statements describe their views to some extent, even though those statements clash.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240514ek5e0018m\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
