\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Katie Britt proposes federal database to collect data on pregnant people\b0\par\par\uc2 L\u233\'00\'E9onie Chao-Fong \par \uc2 596 \uc2 words\par \uc2 11 May 2024\par 23:52 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Republican US senator from Alabama best known for delivering widely ridiculed State of the Union speech in March\par \par \uc2 Katie Britt, the Republican US senator from Alabama best known for delivering a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/mar/08/katie-britt-sotu-reaction"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 widely ridiculed}}}\uc2  State of the Union speech in March, marked the run-up to Mother\u8217\'20\'19s Day on Sunday by introducing a bill to create a federal database to collect data on pregnant people.\par \par \uc2 The More Opportunities for Moms to Succeed (Moms) act proposes to establish an online government database called \u8220\'20\'1Cpregnancy.gov\u8221\'20\'1D listing resources related to pregnancy, including information about adoption agencies and pregnancy care providers, except for those that provide \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -related services.\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.britt.senate.gov/wp-content/uploads/2024/05/MOMS-Act_FINAL-Britt_Rubio_Cramer1.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 bill}}}\uc2  specifically forbids any entity that \u8220\'20\'1Cperforms, induces, refers for, or counsels in favor of abortions\u8221\'20\'1D from being listed in the database, which would in effect eliminate swaths of OB-GYN services and sexual health clinics across the country.\par \par \uc2 The website would direct users to enter their personal data and contact information, and although Britt\u8217\'20\'19s communications director said the site would not collect data on pregnant people, page three of the bill states that users can \u8220\'20\'1Ctake an assessment through the website and provide consent to use the user\u8217\'20\'19s contact information\u8221\'20\'1D which government officials may use \u8220\'20\'1Cto conduct outreach via phone or email to follow up with users on additional resources that would be helpful for the users to review\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Britt introduced the legislation on Thursday alongside two co-sponsors: fellow Republican senators \uc2 Marco Rubio\uc2  of Florida and \uc2 Kevin Cramer\uc2  of North Dakota.\par \par \uc2 In a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.britt.senate.gov/news/press-releases/u-s-senators-katie-britt-marco-rubio-kevin-cramer-introduce-moms-act-to-help-build-culture-of-life-support-women-strengthen-families/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 statement}}}\uc2 , Britt said the bill was proof that \u8220\'20\'1Cyou can absolutely be pro-life, pro-woman, and pro-family at the same time\u8221\'20\'1D, adding that the legislation \u8220\'20\'1Cadvances a comprehensive culture of life\u8221\'20\'1D for mothers and children to \u8220\'20\'1Clive their American Dreams\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Today, I\u8217\'20\'19m proud to introduce the More Opportunities for Moms to Succeed (MOMS) Act along with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SenMarcoRubio?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @SenMarcoRubio}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SenKevinCramer?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @SenKevinCramer}}}\uc2 , and a group of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SenateGOP?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @SenateGOP}}}\uc2  colleagues.\par \par \uc2 You can learn more here: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/L1mZmoYoQ5"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/L1mZmoYoQ5}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/kAmX2Up7Yr"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/kAmX2Up7Yr}}}\uc2  \u8212\'20\'14 Senator Katie Boyd Britt (@SenKatieBritt) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SenKatieBritt/status/1788636760672497882?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 9, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 Critics have noted that the database of \u8220\'20\'1Cpregnancy support centers\u8221\'20\'1D would provide misleading information in an effort to dissuade women from seeking abortions. Axios {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.axios.com/2024/05/09/senate-republicans-pregnant-women-moms-katie-britt"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 noted}}}\uc2  that the bill would also provide grants to anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  non-profit organizations.\par \par \uc2 The state of Alabama, which Britt represents, already has one of the strictest \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans in the country. After the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  eliminated federal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights by overturning Roe v Wade in 2022, the state banned \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  except in cases where there is a serious health risk to the mother.\par \par \uc2 Britt\u8217\'20\'19s party is in the minority in the \uc2 US Senate\uc2  and has only a slim majority in the House. Her bill would need to be approved in both chambers and then be signed by Democratic president \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  to become law, giving her proposal virtually no chance of making meaningful progress in the legislative process as-is.\par \par \uc2 The speech Britt gave to rebut Biden\u8217\'20\'19s State of the Union was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/mar/11/katie-britt-speech-victim-cnn-interview"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 panned}}}\uc2  by both parties after she invoked a story about child rape that she implied had resulted from the president\u8217\'20\'19s handling of immigration at the US\u8217\'20\'19s southern border. The abuse actually occurred years earlier in Mexico while a Republican was president, \uc2 George W Bush\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Britt\u8217\'20\'19s delivery \u8211\'20\'13 which oscillated between smiling and sounding as if she were on the verge of tears \u8211\'20\'13 was also a target of ridicule, though she {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/mar/10/katie-britt-state-of-the-union-rebuttal"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 defended}}}\uc2  her performance.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240511ek5b002e5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
