\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Texas man seeks to have ex-partner investigated for out-of-state  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 Carter Sherman \par \uc2 962 \uc2 words\par \uc2 11 May 2024\par 14:11 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Collin Davis asks court to green light investigation as experts call case a \u8216\'20\'18coordinated fear campaign\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 As soon as the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  overturned Roe v Wade two years ago, anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  activists started debating if and how they could limit Americans\u8217\'20\'19 ability to cross state lines for legal abortions. Now, a Texas man has asked a court to greenlight an investigation into the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  his former partner allegedly received in a state where the procedure remains legal.\par \par \uc2 The man, Collin Davis, said in court records that when he learned his former partner planned to get an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in February 2024, he hired an attorney who would \u8220\'20\'1Cpursue wrongful-death claims against anyone involved in the killing of his unborn child\u8221\'20\'1D. According to the records, the woman proceeded to get an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Colorado, a state that has become an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  haven as laws banning the procedure have taken effect across much of the US midwest and south.\par \par \uc2 Davis\u8217\'20\'19s petition, filed in March and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/investigations/2024/05/03/texas-abortion-investigations/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 first reported by the Washington Post}}}\uc2  last week, seeks to use a Texas law that allows people to request legal depositions before potentially filing a lawsuit, in order to ascertain who may have \u8220\'20\'1Caided or abetted\u8221\'20\'1D the woman\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Davis argues that, if the investigation uncovers wrongdoing, he can sue under Texas\u8217\'20\'19s wrongful-death statute or under a state law that permits private individuals to sue one another on suspicion of \u8220\'20\'1Caiding or abetting\u8221\'20\'1D an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  past six weeks of pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 Davis does not intend to sue the woman who got the alleged \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but is evaluating whether to go after \u8220\'20\'1Cco-conspirators and accomplices\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 a seemingly broad range of people that could include \u8220\'20\'1Cany individual \u8230\'20\'26 involved in the murder of Mr Davis\u8217\'20\'19 unborn child\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 It is legal for people to cross state lines for abortions in states that still permit the procedure. However, activists determined to end \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  nationwide have launched a series of legislative and legal volleys to undermine that right, often by targeting groups and individuals who may help patients travel.\par \par \uc2 Idaho has passed a law banning people from helping minors leave the state for legal abortions \u8211\'20\'13 an act that the state has labeled \u8220\'20\'1C\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  trafficking\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 unless they have parental consent. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/oct/25/texas-abortion-travel-ban-lubbock-county"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Small Texas localities have passed}}}\uc2  a series of ordinances to restrict people\u8217\'20\'19s ability to transport others along local roads for out-of-state abortions. Alabama\u8217\'20\'19s attorney general has threatened to prosecute groups that help women leave the state for abortions \u8211\'20\'13 a threat that a federal judge {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.al.com/politics/2024/05/judge-skewers-alabama-attorney-general-in-ruling-allowing-abortion-travel-lawsuit-to-proceed.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 beat back forcefully earlier this week}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAlabama can no more restrict people from going to, say, California to engage in what is lawful there than California can restrict people from coming to Alabama to do what is lawful here,\u8221\'20\'1D US district judge Myron Thompson wrote in a preliminary ruling in a lawsuit brought by Alabama \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers and their supporters.\par \par \uc2 Davis is being represented by Jonathan Mitchell, a prominent anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  attorney and architect of the Texas law that permits people to sue over suspected illegal abortions. Mitchell, who is also representing another Texas man who is currently suing his ex-wife\u8217\'20\'19s friends for allegedly helping her get an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , believes current law allows for holding people liable for helping procure out-of-state abortions.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFathers of aborted fetuses can sue for wrongful death in states with \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans, even if the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  occurs out-of-state,\u8221\'20\'1D Mitchell said in a statement. \u8220\'20\'1CThey can sue anyone who paid for the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , anyone who aided or abetted the travel, and anyone involved in the manufacture or distribution of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  drugs.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Molly Duane\uc2 , a senior staff attorney with the Center for Reproductive Rights, which is representing the woman, said \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  foes want to use Davis\u8217\'20\'19s filing to sow confusion and terror.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt has never been the case that a state can prohibit its citizens from leaving the state. That would be absurd,\u8221\'20\'1D Duane said. \u8220\'20\'1CThis is a coordinated fear campaign. If they can\u8217\'20\'19t prohibit them from traveling, well, then they want to scare them, and make them think that they\u8217\'20\'19re doing something wrong.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Since Roe fell, several states, including Colorado, have enacted so-called \u8220\'20\'1Cshield laws\u8221\'20\'1D to generally protect people from being investigated or prosecuted by states that ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . It is not yet clear what role, if any, Colorado\u8217\'20\'19s shield law may play in Davis\u8217\'20\'19s case.\par \par \uc2 Court records in Davis\u8217\'20\'19s case also repeatedly cite the Comstock Act, a 19th-century anti-vice law that, in the eyes of some \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  opponents, bans the mailing of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -related materials nationwide. Such an interpretation of the Comstock Act, which the Biden administration disagrees with, would result in a de facto national ban on abortions, because clinics rely on the mail to obtain the drugs and equipment they need to do their jobs.\par \par \uc2 Davis is waiting for a ruling from the state district court, which the \uc2 Center for Reproductive Rights\uc2  may in turn appeal. If the case proceeds, Mitchell wants to depose the woman who had the alleged \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and others connected to it, with questioning about \u8220\'20\'1Call sources of financial support for the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D, and to obtain records of any communications with \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers and funds. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/sep/28/texas-lawyer-abortion-ban-procedure-patient-information"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Mitchell has previously asked Texas \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  funds}}}\uc2  for information about recent abortions that they have \u8220\'20\'1Cassisted or facilitated in any way\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Although Duane is steadfast in her belief that Texas law does not prohibit people from helping one another leave the state for abortions, she still fears for the future.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNothing is safe. No one is safe,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CI cannot guarantee anyone, really, that they won\u8217\'20\'19t be pursued for harassing or frivolous legal actions.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240511ek5b001p5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
