\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  rights activists worry about Democrats piggybacking on the cause: \u8216\'20\'18This is not a ploy\u8217\'20\'19\b0\par\par\uc2 Carter Sherman \par \uc2 1,209 \uc2 words\par \uc2 9 May 2024\par 13:07 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 glee about \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  becoming an electoral weapon could hurt key ballot initiatives, say advocates\par \par \uc2 Amy knows that a lot of people hate every candidate on the ballot this November.\par \par \uc2 As a nurse who has worked for more than a decade at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/may/03/florida-abortion-ban-clinic"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bread and Roses Women\u8217\'20\'19s Health Center}}}\uc2 , an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinic in Gainesville, Florida, Amy has dealt with both patients and friends who feel so disillusioned about partisan politics that they don\u8217\'20\'19t want to vote at all in the 2024 elections. She gets it: the mere thought of the last few elections makes her grimace.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou don\u8217\'20\'19t have to vote for the candidates if you don\u8217\'20\'19t want to,\u8221\'20\'1D she said in an interview the day before Florida outlawed \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  past six weeks of pregnancy. (Amy asked to be identified only by her first name, for privacy reasons.) \u8220\'20\'1CBut please just vote for the ballot measure.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Come November, Florida will be one of roughly a dozen states anticipated to hold a ballot measure asking voters to decide whether \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights should be protected or decimated. Florida\u8217\'20\'19s ballot measure, however, may have higher stakes than any other in the country: if voters don\u8217\'20\'19t support the measure to enshrine \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights into the state constitution, they will be left with a six-week ban \u8211\'20\'13 which prohibits \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  before many people even know they are pregnant.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights supporters have won every ballot measure since the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  overturned Roe v Wade two years ago, and outrage over Roe\u8217\'20\'19s demise is believed to have cost the Republicans a much-heralded \u8220\'20\'1Cred wave\u8221\'20\'1D in the 2022 elections. Those successes have convinced Democrats that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is their silver bullet in the 2024 elections, particularly since \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  consistently trails \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in polling and is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/may/05/democrats-white-house-antiwar-protests-1968-2024"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 at risk of losing the youth vote}}}\uc2  over the war in Gaza. Democrats across the country are now regularly blasting Republicans for their complicity in \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans.\par \par \uc2 But Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 spotlight on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights has also pushed the organizers of the nonpartisan campaign behind the Florida ballot initiative into an awkward position. They need 60% of the vote to win \u8211\'20\'13 and with almost a million more registered Republicans than Democrats in Florida, as well as more than 3 million independents, organizers can\u8217\'20\'19t afford to appear too cozy with Democrats, especially at a time of unparalleled political discord.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI understand the knee-jerk reaction, because it was a Republican governor that signed the six-week ban. It was a Republican-majority house and senate that created the bill itself,\u8221\'20\'1D said Trenece Robertson, a Florida reproductive justice activist who helped collect signatures to get the measure on the ballot. \u8220\'20\'1CBut also, we need to do our best to make sure we as a state are unified and that we do not alienate anyone at this point, because we need as many votes as we can get.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 An April poll by Emerson College found that 42% of Florida voters plan to vote for the ballot measure. Fifty-six per cent of Democrats and 44% of independents plan to vote for it, while just 30% of Republicans said the same.\par \par \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18The Democrats are cynically using these initiatives\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 Despite their party\u8217\'20\'19s long-standing support for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, the Democrats in Congress and the White House largely spent the Roe era sidestepping the issue. Biden, a Catholic, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/jan/26/biden-abortion-rights-expand-protections"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 once declared}}}\uc2  that he was not \u8220\'20\'1Cbig on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D; reproductive justice advocates famously tracked what seemed like an inability to even say the word \u8220\'20\'1C\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Now that anger over Roe\u8217\'20\'19s demise has proved to be an electoral weapon, the president has begun to talk more openly about \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . His campaign has pumped out multiple ads about the consequences of banning the procedure, while \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is on a nationwide tour focused on the issue. In a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/may/01/florida-six-week-abortion-ban-takes-effect"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 speech in Jacksonville}}}\uc2 , Florida, last week, the vice-president brought up \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -related ballot measures.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMomentum is on our side. Just think about it. Since Roe was overturned, every time reproductive freedom has been on the ballot, the people of America voted for freedom,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris told the crowd. \u8220\'20\'1CFrom Kansas to California to Kentucky, in Michigan, Montana, Vermont, and Ohio, the people of America voted for freedom \u8211\'20\'13 and not by little but often by overwhelming margins, proving also that this is not a partisan issue \u8211\'20\'13 it\u8217\'20\'19s not a partisan issue \u8211\'20\'13 and proving that the voice of the people has been heard and will be heard.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Yet even as Harris insisted that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights are a nonpartisan issue, she also referred to state-level \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans as \u8220\'20\'1CTrump \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans\u8221\'20\'1D five times.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COf course they\u8217\'20\'19re trying to use the process. The Democrats are cynically using these initiatives to try to turn people out,\u8221\'20\'1D said the \uc2 Arizona State University\uc2  political sociologist Benjamin Case, who studies ballot measures. \u8220\'20\'1CThey\u8217\'20\'19re hoping that will be a boon to Biden, because those people might be more likely to vote for Biden.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 As part of his research, Case interviewed professional political operatives after Arizona\u8217\'20\'19s state supreme court ruled a 1864 \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban could be enforced. Their main response, according to Case: \u8220\'20\'1COh, this is really great. Biden will win Arizona because it will piss people off.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 That sense of glee, however, contrasts sharply with the real-world consequences of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans. \u8220\'20\'1CThat sentiment predominates among the professional political class,\u8221\'20\'1D Case said. \u8220\'20\'1CAmong organizers in Arizona, it was a lot different, for obvious reasons.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Arizona\u8217\'20\'19s state legislature, which has a razor-thin Republican majority, has since {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/may/02/arizona-1864-abortion-ban-repealed-governor"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 moved to repeal that ban}}}\uc2 , and \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is currently legal in the state until 15 weeks of pregnancy. Arizona is likely to hold an initiative in November to protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  until fetal viability.\par \par \uc2 Julie Cantillo, a volunteer coordinator with the Gainesville Radical Reproductive Rights! Network, which helped gather signatures for the Florida ballot initiative, said that national Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 talk of using ballot measures to bring out voters leaves her \u8220\'20\'1Cscared\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt makes it gimmicky. Also, it doesn\u8217\'20\'19t acknowledge that real people\u8217\'20\'19s lives are at stake here,\u8221\'20\'1D Cantillo said. \u8220\'20\'1CThis is about everyone having access to their human rights and healthcare. I don\u8217\'20\'19t want to minimize it by saying this is a ploy to turn people out. That\u8217\'20\'19s not why so many Floridians have been putting so much effort into this.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -related ballot measures have never been put to the test in a presidential campaign. And despite Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 hopes for boosted turnout, it is not clear that support for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, which are broadly popular, will translate to support for Biden or any other Democratic candidate. Whenever voters are asked to decide big ballot measures, votes on the measure often outnumber votes for candidates, indicating that people are showing up only to vote on the measure, according to Case.\par \par \uc2 Ultimately, if voters are resorting to a ballot measure, Case said, it\u8217\'20\'19s an indictment of elected politicians\u8217\'20\'19 failure to do their job.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf they were really governing in the popular interest and there\u8217\'20\'19s some policy that 65% of people want and they haven\u8217\'20\'19t passed it yet,\u8221\'20\'1D he said, \u8220\'20\'1Cthat should raise questions about why not.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240509ek59001bi\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
