\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  says \u8216\'20\'18we must give hate no safe harbor\u8217\'20\'19 in speech condemning antisemitism \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Richard Luscombe \par \uc2 4,877 \uc2 words\par \uc2 7 May 2024\par 20:15 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 This live blog is now closed. You can read our latest report here:Biden warns against \u8216\'20\'18surge of antisemitism\u8217\'20\'19 at Holocaust event\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.03pm BST\par \par \uc2 Closing summary\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19re closing our US politics blog now, but you can continue to follow coverage of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s hush-money trial in New York in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/may/07/donald-trump-hush-money-trial-fine-gag-order-violations-live"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 our live blog here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what we followed today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  spoke at the \uc2 US Holocaust Memorial Museum\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Day of Remembrance ceremony, honoring Second War War victims of the Nazis, condemning the \uc2 Hamas\uc2  attacks of 7 October, and denouncing violence during pro-Palestinian demonstrations on US college campuses. \u8220\'20\'1CWe have an obligation to learn the lessons of history \u8230\'20\'26 to not surrender our future to the horrors of the past. We must give hate no safe harbor against anyone,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 New York supreme court justice Daniel Doyle blocked an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights amendment from appearing on the November ballot, a significant setback for Democrats hoping to use the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2023/nov/10/state-abortion-laws-us"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  access debate}}}\uc2  to galvanize voters.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Speaker Mike Johnson dismissed a threat to his position from rebel Republican congress members \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene\uc2  and \uc2 Thomas Massie\uc2 , insisting at a press conference: \u8220\'20\'1CI intend to lead this conference in the future.\u8221\'20\'1D Johnson is meeting the duo again this lunchtime as they decide whether to advance a vote for his removal after he colluded with Democrats to pass a Ukraine funding bill.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Texas Democratic congressman \uc2 Henry Cuellar\uc2  faced pressure to resign from the Citizens for Responsibility and Ethics in Washington (Crew) group. Cuellar and his wife Imelda were {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/may/03/henry-cuellar-doj-indict"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 indicted last week for bribery}}}\uc2  over their connections with Azerbaijan. \u8220\'20\'1CWhile [he] deserves a fair trial and the presumption of innocence, the serious charges \u8230\'20\'26 make it inappropriate for him to remain in office,\u8221\'20\'1D Crew president Noah Bookbinder said.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2 , the White House press secretary, pushed back on a reporter\u8217\'20\'19s suggestions the Biden administration wasn\u8217\'20\'19t fully forthcoming about its knowledge of ceasefire talks in Gaza. Israel, according to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.axios.com/2024/05/07/us-israel-hamas-hostage-ceasefire-talks"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  Axios, }}}\uc2  was upset the US apparently knew about a proposal by Egypt, but hadn\u8217\'20\'19t briefed Israel. Jean-Pierre insisted at her daily press briefing that no administration official was involved in secret discussion or deceit.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.06pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.41pm BST\par \par \uc2 Jean-Pierre was also asked about the behavior captured on video of counter-protesters at a pro-Palestinian rally {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/may/04/university-of-mississippi-counter-protesters"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 at the University of Mississippi}}}\uc2  last week.\par \par \uc2 One white student was accused of making monkey noises at a Black protester, and has been {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.al.com/news/2024/05/ole-miss-phi-delta-theta-fraternity-member-suspended-for-racist-protest-actions.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 suspended by his Ole Miss fraternity}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The behavior was \u8220\'20\'1Cundignified and racist\u8221\'20\'1D, Jean-Pierre said. \u8220\'20\'1CThe actions in the video are beneath any American.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.31pm BST\par \par \uc2 The White House press conference has just wrapped up, a little later than advertised. \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2 , the White House press secretary, has been pushing back on some reporters\u8217\'20\'19 suggestions that the Biden administration hasn\u8217\'20\'19t been fully forthcoming about its involvement in, or knowledge of, ceasefire talks over the war in Gaza.\par \par \uc2 Hamas\uc2  agreed to an Egyptian ceasefire proposal on Monday that would have seen the release of hostages it still holds from the 7 October attack. But Israel, according to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.axios.com/2024/05/07/us-israel-hamas-hostage-ceasefire-talks"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 an Axios report}}}\uc2  on Monday, was upset the US apparently knew about the proposal by Egypt, but hadn\u8217\'20\'19t briefed Israel on it. And Israel says the terms \uc2 Hamas\uc2  accepted weren\u8217\'20\'19t those it had agreed to.\par \par \uc2 Jean-Pierre insisted no administration official was involved in any secret discussions, or had any intent to deceive. But she didn\u8217\'20\'19t directly address Israel\u8217\'20\'19s reported frustration.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere are talks happening in Cairo, and that\u8217\'20\'19s incredibly important,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1COur assessment is the two sides should be able to come to a deal, or at least close the gaps to get to a deal.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.57pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.09pm BST\par \par \uc2 They may officially be two days late, but White House staff laid on an official Cinco de Mayo celebration this morning for Mexico\u8217\'20\'19s independence day.\par \par \uc2 enltrHappy Cinco de Mayo from the White House! Our Administration is proud to celebrate the history, heritage, and rich contributions of Mexican-Americans. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/tpPGkyjug4"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/tpPGkyjug4}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The White House (@WhiteHouse) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/WhiteHouse/status/1787859951630626841?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 7, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 First lady Jill Biden addressed a large gathering of Mexican-Americans:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C[We] pay tribute to a long line of Mexican-Americans who have added their own threads to our rich American tapestry with bravery and vision. Writers whose poems trace the contours of our sorrows and joys. Activists whose movements for justice achieved hard-won progress. Trailblazers in every career and calling who have led us toward a more perfect union.\par \par \uc2 And as we recognize the Mexican-Americans who have so profoundly shaped this country, and are continuing to shape it, we also remember that the first step to progress is dreaming \u8211\'20\'13 creating those images in our own heads, even if the odds are against us, reaching for the stars, even if we may miss, sculpting the world we see when we close our eyes and imagine.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.45pm BST\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s the video of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s address to the \uc2 US Holocaust Memorial Museum\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Day of Remembrance ceremony earlier.\par \par \uc2 enltrTune in as I deliver the keynote address at the \uc2 U.S. Holocaust Memorial Museum\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Annual Days of Remembrance ceremony in Washington, D.C. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/u2B6FOU92y"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/u2B6FOU92y}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 President Biden (@POTUS) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/POTUS/status/1787869769921626314?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 7, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNever again simply translated for me means: Never forget. Never forgetting means we must keep telling the story, we must keep teaching the truth,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said as he addressed a bipartisan memorial held at the US Capitol\u8217\'20\'19s Emancipation Hall.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe truth is we\u8217\'20\'19re at risk of people not knowing the truth.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Biden spoke seven months to the day after \uc2 Hamas\uc2  attacked {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/israel"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Israel}}}\uc2  on 7 October, killing 1,200 by Israeli tallies, in what Biden has called the deadliest day for Jews since the Holocaust.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis hatred [of Jews] continues to lie deep in the hearts of too many people in the world and requires our continued vigilance and outspokenness,\u8221\'20\'1D the president said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.46pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.22pm BST\par \par \uc2 A furore over the killing of a puppy by South Dakota Republican governor \uc2 Kristi Noem\uc2 , a story first reported by the Guardian, shows no sign of abating, as my colleague Martin Pengelly reports:\par \par \uc2 Asked if a story about killing a dog and a goat as well as a false claim to have met Kim Jong-un could have been put in her book by an editor acting as \u8220\'20\'1Ca liberal plant\u8221\'20\'1D, the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/south-dakota"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 South Dakota}}}\uc2  governor and Republican vice-presidential hopeful \uc2 Kristi Noem\uc2  seemed to realise such a claim would be too outlandish even for her.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe buck always stops with me,\u8221\'20\'1D Noem {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.mediaite.com/tv/newsmax-host-asks-kristi-noem-if-her-book-editor-was-a-liberal-plant-who-inserted-unflattering-stories/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told}}}\uc2 Newsmax\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CI take my own full responsibility. I wrote this book.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 No Going Back was published in the US on Tuesday. But for more than a week it has been at the centre of a political firestorm fueled by a Guardian {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/books/2024/apr/26/trump-kristi-noem-shot-dog-and-goat-book"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 report}}}\uc2  of its startling story of how Noem {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/books/2024/apr/26/trump-kristi-noem-shot-dog-and-goat-book"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 says}}}\uc2  she shot dead Cricket, a 14-month-old wirehaired pointer she deemed \u8220\'20\'1Cuntrainable\u8221\'20\'1D, and an unnamed goat Noem said menaced her children.\par \par \uc2 Noem has defended the story as an example of how she is willing to do unpleasant things in life and politics.\par \par \uc2 But the resulting revulsion has seemingly ended any hope of Noem being named running mate to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , the former president and presumptive Republican nominee in November.\par \par \uc2 Noem\u8217\'20\'19s claim to have met Kim, the North Korean dictator, unravelled amid reporting {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.thedakotascout.com/p/gov-kristi-noems-account-of-meeting"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 by the Dakota Scout}}}\uc2 . Noem\u8217\'20\'19s publisher, Center Street, said it would remove the passage from future editions.\par \par \uc2 Amid a media tour in which Noem was challenged on \uc2 CBS\uc2  about an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/books/article/2024/may/06/kristi-noem-book-biden-dog"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 apparent threat to kill Joe Biden\u8217\'20\'19s dog}}}\uc2 , the governor sought friendlier turf at \uc2 Newsmax\uc2 . Eric Bolling, a former Fox News host, duly attempted to give her a way to climb off her hurtling train of bad PR.\par \par \uc2 Bolling {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.mediaite.com/tv/newsmax-host-asks-kristi-noem-if-her-book-editor-was-a-liberal-plant-who-inserted-unflattering-stories/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CYou don\u8217\'20\'19t write the whole book at once, you write a chapter or two, you send it to the editors and they edit. They read it, they add, they subtract.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAnd here\u8217\'20\'19s my question: the editor, was she possibly a plant? A liberal plant? Because I\u8217\'20\'19m not sure either one of these stories, this dog story, the North Korea story, seems like the \uc2 Kristi Noem\uc2  I know.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Read the full story:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/books/article/2024/may/07/kristi-noem-dog-killing-liberal-plant"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kristi Noem rejects \u8216\'20\'18liberal plant\u8217\'20\'19 claim on dog-killing tale: \u8216\'20\'18Buck stops with me\u8217\'20\'19}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.57pm BST\par \par \uc2 Interim summary\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s been a relatively quiet day so far in US politics. Here\u8217\'20\'19s where things stand:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  spoke at the \uc2 US Holocaust Memorial Museum\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Day of Remembrance ceremony, honoring Second War War victims of the Nazis, condemning the \uc2 Hamas\uc2  attacks of 7 October, and denouncing violence during pro-Palestinian demonstrations on US college campuses. \u8220\'20\'1CWe have an obligation to learn the lessons of history \u8230\'20\'26 to not surrender our future to the horrors of the past. We must give hate no safe harbor against anyone,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 New York supreme court justice Daniel Doyle blocked an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights amendment from appearing on the November ballot, a significant setback for Democrats hoping to use the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2023/nov/10/state-abortion-laws-us"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  access debate}}}\uc2  to galvanize voters.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Speaker Mike Johnson dismissed a threat to his position from rebel Republican congress members \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene\uc2  and \uc2 Thomas Massie\uc2 , insisting at a press conference: \u8220\'20\'1CI intend to lead this conference in the future.\u8221\'20\'1D Johnson is meeting the duo again this lunchtime as they decide whether to advance a vote for his removal after he colluded with Democrats to pass a Ukraine funding bill.\par \par \uc2 There\u8217\'20\'19s more to come, including the daily media briefing from White House press secretary \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.03pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.31pm BST\par \par \uc2 Reuters says \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will next Tuesday meet with chief executives of \uc2 Citigroup\uc2 , \uc2 United Airlines\uc2 , \uc2 Marriott International\uc2  and other corporations across a range of industries at the White House.\par \par \uc2 Citing an administration official, the agency says the purpose of the meeting is \u8220\'20\'1Cthe national and global economy\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Polling for November\u8217\'20\'19s election indicates Biden is weaker on the economy in voters\u8217\'20\'19 minds, and the meeting is an opportunity to try to gather some momentum with less than six months remaining.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.40pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.09pm BST\par \par \uc2 Judge strips \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights amendment from New York ballot\par \par \uc2 A New York judge on Tuesday blocked an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights amendment from appearing on the November ballot, the Associated Press reports, a significant setback for Democrats hoping to use the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2023/nov/10/state-abortion-laws-us"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  access debate}}}\uc2  to galvanize voters.\par \par \uc2 State supreme court justice Daniel Doyle ruled state lawmakers failed to follow procedural rules regarding constitutional amendments, and incorrectly approved the amendment before getting a written opinion on its language from the attorney general.\par \par \uc2 The lawsuit was filed by Republican state assemblywoman Marjorie Byrnes.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights amendments have passed in every state they have appeared, including Republican-controlled states, since the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  ended almost 50 years of federal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  protections in 2022.\par \par \uc2 Similar amendments are on the ballot elsewhere this November, including Florida, where a six-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban took effect last week. An effort by Florida\u8217\'20\'19s Republican attorney general \uc2 Ashley Moody\uc2 , similar to the New York lawsuit, to strip the amendment was rejected by the state\u8217\'20\'19s supreme court last month.\par \par \uc2 The New York state attorney general\u8217\'20\'19s office did not immediately comment.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.46pm BST\par \par \uc2 We bring news of a presidential election event unlikely to ever happen: a head-to-head debate between \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , the presumptive Republican nominee, and independent candidate \uc2 Robert F Kennedy Jr.\par \par \uc2 Kennedy\u8217\'20\'19s campaign put out a statement Tuesday morning challenging Trump to a debate at the Libertarian convention in Washington DC from 24 to 26 May.\par \par \uc2 In an accompanying open letter {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RobertKennedyJr/status/1787876409177735639"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 posted to X}}}\uc2 , Kennedy claims that polls have both himself and Trump \u8220\'20\'1Ccrushing\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  in November (spoiler: they don\u8217\'20\'19t), so it makes sense for the two to debate at an event they\u8217\'20\'19re both scheduled to speak at anyway:\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s perfect neutral territory for you and me to have a debate where you can defend your record for your wavering supporters. You yourself have said you\u8217\'20\'19re not afraid to debate me as long as my poll numbers are decent. Well, they are.\par \par \uc2 So let\u8217\'20\'19s meet at the Libertarian convention and show the American public that at least two of the major candidates aren\u8217\'20\'19t afraid to debate each other. I asked the convention organizers and they are game for us to use our time there to bring the American people the debate they deserve!\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Commission on Presidential Debates\uc2  has announced {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://debates.org/2023/11/20/2024-sites/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 three debates for this year}}}\uc2 , the first scheduled to take place on 16 September in San Marcos, Texas. Participants have yet to be announced.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.51pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.22pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  also addressed recent {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-campus-protests"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pro-Palestinian protests}}}\uc2  on numerous US colleges and campuses, which turned violent in several cities and led to more than 2,000 arrests:\par \par \uc2 I understand people have strong beliefs and deep convictions about the world. In America we respect and protect the fundamental right to free speech, to debate, and disagree, to protest peacefully and make our voices heard.\par \par \uc2 I understand. That\u8217\'20\'19s America. But there is no place on any campus in America, or any place in America, for antisemitism, or hate speech, or threats of violence of any kind.\par \par \uc2 Whether against Jews or anyone else, violent attacks, destroying property, is not peaceful protest. It\u8217\'20\'19s against the law. And we\u8217\'20\'19re not a lawless country. We\u8217\'20\'19re a civil society. We uphold the rule of law. And no one should have to hide or be brave just to be themselves.\par \par \uc2 Biden acknowledged {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/mar/26/benjamin-netanyahu-handling-us-relations-un-israel-gaza-ceasefire-vote"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 recent friction}}}\uc2  between his administration and Israel\u8217\'20\'19s prime minister \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2  over the course of the war in Gaza, and Israel\u8217\'20\'19s military push into Rafah. But he said his support for Jewish people in the US was unshakable:\par \par \uc2 To the Jewish community, I want you to know I see your fear, your hurt and your pain. Let me reassure you as your president, you\u8217\'20\'19re not alone. You belong. You always have and you always will.\par \par \uc2 And my commitment to the safety of the Jewish people, the security of Israel, and its right to exist as an independent Jewish state is ironclad, even when we disagree.\par \par \uc2 He said his administration was \u8220\'20\'1Cworking around the clock\u8221\'20\'1D to free hostages still held by \uc2 Hamas\uc2  in Gaza:\par \par \uc2 We will not rest until we bring them all home.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.07pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden: 'We must give hate no safe harbor'\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is condemning the \u8220\'20\'1Cferocious surge of antisemitism\u8221\'20\'1D during the \uc2 US Holocaust Memorial Museum\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Days of Remembrance ceremony.\par \par \uc2 He\u8217\'20\'19s commemorating the 6 million Jewish people murdered by the Nazis during the Second World War at the event in Washington DC, also attended by congressional leaders, including Republican speaker Mike Johnson and Democratic House minority leader \uc2 Hakeem Jeffries\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Biden said the Holocaust was \u8220\'20\'1Cone of the darkest chapters in human history\u8221\'20\'1D:\par \par \uc2 Never again, simply translated for me, means never forget.\par \par \uc2 The president also condemned the \uc2 Hamas\uc2  attacks in Israel on 7 October last year, and antisemitism on display during recent pro-Palestinian demonstrations at some US colleges and universities:\par \par \uc2 This ancient hatred of Jews didn\u8217\'20\'19t begin with the Holocaust. It didn\u8217\'20\'19t end with the Holocaust either. Or even after our victory in world war two, this hatred continues. That hatred was brought to life on October 7 2023.\par \par \uc2 Over 1,200 innocent people, babies, parents, grandparents, slaughtered in their kibbutz, massacred, brutally raped, mutilated and sexually assaulted. Thousands more carrying wounds, bullets and shrapnel from the memory of that terrible day they endured.\par \par \uc2 We have an obligation to learn the lessons of history \u8230\'20\'26 to not surrender our future to the horrors of the past. We must give hate no safe harbor against anyone.\par \par \uc2 This post was amended to correct \u8220\'20\'1Cscourge\u8221\'20\'1D to \u8220\'20\'1Csurge\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.05pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.49pm BST\par \par \uc2 There\u8217\'20\'19s more pressure on beleaguered Texas Democratic congressman \uc2 Henry Cuellar\uc2  to resign, this time from the Citizens for Responsibility and Ethics in Washington (Crew) group.\par \par \uc2 Cuellar and his wife Imelda were {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/may/03/henry-cuellar-doj-indict"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 indicted last week for bribery}}}\uc2  over their connections with Azerbaijan, prompting {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/may/04/dean-phillips-henry-cuellar-indictment"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 calls from some fellow Democrats}}}\uc2  for him to step down.\par \par \uc2 On Monday, according to Punchbowl, Cuellar\u8217\'20\'19s chief of staff Jake Hochberg resigned.\par \par \uc2 Crew released a statement on Tuesday echoing calls for the congressman to step aside. Its president Noah Bookbinder said:\par \par \uc2 Representative Cuellar\u8217\'20\'19s alleged wrongdoing is blatantly and astonishingly corrupt. The actions outlined in the government\u8217\'20\'19s indictment demonstrate that he abused his position to enrich himself and benefit foreign interests, betraying his constituents.\par \par \uc2 While Representative Cuellar deserves a fair trial and the presumption of innocence, the serious charges leveled against him make it inappropriate for him to remain in office. Serving in Congress is a privilege, not a right, and Americans should be able to trust that their representatives, regardless of party or ideology, are working for them.\par \par \uc2 Out of respect for his constituents and for the office he holds, Representative Cuellar must resign.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.23pm BST\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19ll be hearing from \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  within the next short while. The president is scheduled to deliver remarks at the \uc2 US Holocaust Memorial Museum\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Days of Remembrance ceremony in Washington DC.\par \par \uc2 In a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.whitehouse.gov/briefing-room/statements-releases/2024/05/07/biden-harris-administration-ramps-up-actions-to-counter-antisemitism-on-college-campuses-and-protect-jewish-communities/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 White House statement}}}\uc2 , Biden says this year\u8217\'20\'19s remembrance is \u8220\'20\'1Cparticularly sobering\u8221\'20\'1D as it\u8217\'20\'19s the first since the \uc2 Hamas\uc2  terrorist attacks on Israel on 7 October last year killed at least 1,160 people, the deadliest day for Jewish people since the Holocaust.\par \par \uc2 It also comes against a backdrop of violence on US university and college campuses, during pro-Palestinian demonstrations by students and activists. At least 1,000 people have been arrested.\par \par \uc2 enltrWatch the national commemoration of the Days of Remembrance live as we remember the six million Jews who were murdered during the Holocaust and the other victims of Nazi persecution. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/vVyrxxUVrW"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/vVyrxxUVrW}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 US Holocaust Museum (@HolocaustMuseum) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/HolocaustMuseum/status/1787858701547680005?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 7, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 The Biden administration on Tuesday announced \u8220\'20\'1Cseveral new actions to counter the abhorrent rise of antisemitism in the US\u8221\'20\'1D, which the president is expected to outline in his speech.\par \par \uc2 They include guidance to all school districts and colleges in the country on how to counter antisemitic discrimination; online campus safety resources; and a partnership with technology companies to address a rise of antisemitic content online.\par \par \uc2 The measures, the statement says, reaffirms \u8220\'20\'1Cour nation\u8217\'20\'19s sacred commitment to the Jewish people following the Holocaust: Never Again\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19ll bring you Biden\u8217\'20\'19s remarks as they happen.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.42pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.53pm BST\par \par \uc2 Johnson: Talks with rebels 'not a negotiation'\par \par \uc2 Speaker Mike Johnson has dismissed a threat to his position from rebel Republicans \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene\uc2  and \uc2 Thomas Massie\uc2 , insisting at a press conference Tuesday morning that \u8220\'20\'1CI intend to lead this conference in the future\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 He said he had \u8220\'20\'1Ca good discussion [that] I thought was productive\u8221\'20\'1D with the pair on Monday over Greene\u8217\'20\'19s threats to call a motion to vacate, essentially a vote to oust him, over his collusion with Democrats to fund a Ukraine funding bill.\par \par \uc2 He insisted the talks, which will resume Tuesday lunchtime, were \u8220\'20\'1Cnot a negotiation\u8221\'20\'1D, despite reports that Greene and Massie had made a series of demands in return for backing down on a vote. They include no more Ukraine funding, and pledge from him to only introduce legislation supported by Republicans.\par \par \uc2 Johnson said:\par \par \uc2 Everybody knows I have lengthy, detailed discussions on a daily basis with members across the conference. There are 217 of us. It takes a lot of time, this is why I don\u8217\'20\'19t get enough sleep these days.\par \par \uc2 When you have the smallest majority in history you have to quite literally get everyone to work together. I\u8217\'20\'19ve heard Marjorie and Thomas\u8217\'20\'19s ideas, just like I have every day for the last six months, heard others. It\u8217\'20\'19s not a negotiation at all.\par \par \uc2 So I take Marjorie\u8217\'20\'19s ideas, and Thomas\u8217\'20\'19s, and everybody else\u8217\'20\'19s equally, and we assess them on their own value. And where we can make improvements and changes and all of that we do, and that\u8217\'20\'19s what this is. There\u8217\'20\'19s nothing more than that going on.\par \par \uc2 Whether Greene and Massie feel the same way is another matter. We hope to find out this afternoon.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.36pm BST\par \par \uc2 Speaker Mike Johnson is now at the podium, and delivering a full-throated defense of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , and attack on \u8220\'20\'1CDemocratic supporters of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D he says are orchestrating \u8220\'20\'1Csham trials\u8221\'20\'1D against the former president.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s a direct echo of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s own falsehoods about his various prosecutions, which were brought by a justice department independent of the White House, or state prosecutors.\par \par \uc2 Johnson says Trump, the presumptive Republican presidential nominee, is the victim of \u8220\'20\'1Clawfare\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Celection interference\u8221\'20\'1D, because his legal troubles are keeping him from the campaign trail. Which is another favorite Trump claim.\par \par \uc2 Now he\u8217\'20\'19s finally addressing his talks with rebel Congress members \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene\uc2  and \uc2 Thomas Massie\uc2  on Monday \u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.45pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.22pm BST\par \par \uc2 Home appliances are the first topic of discussion at the Mike Johnson press conference. The speaker himself has yet to speak.\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  -directed bureaucrats, the Republicans are insisting, are determined to take away Americans\u8217\'20\'19 stoves, dishwashers, showers, air conditioners and other household appliances.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , take your hands off our home appliances,\u8221\'20\'1D Arizona congresswoman \uc2 Debbie Lesko\uc2  says, touting a bill that would prevent federal regulators from imposing energy efficiency standards on them.\par \par \uc2 The Biden administration, Lesko insists, is engaged in a \u8220\'20\'1Cscheme to take away Americans\u8217\'20\'19 appliances in the name of a radical environmental agenda\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.34pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.05pm BST\par \par \uc2 Speaker Mike Johnson is about to address reporters at a news conference with Republican leadership in Washington DC.\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19re watching to see if he has anything to say about his talks with \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene\uc2  and her ongoing pledge to oust him.\par \par \uc2 You can {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=q8f4P5PdxT4"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 watch the press conference here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.59pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s hush-money trial in New York, and today\u8217\'20\'19s development that adult movie star Stormy Daniels is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/may/07/trump-trial-judge-day-13"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 set to testify}}}\uc2 , is soaking up much of the oxygen surrounding the former president. But as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/may/07/trump-trial-justice-system-violence"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Peter Stone reports}}}\uc2 , his constant attacks on the US justice system is fueling threats of violence and undermining the rule of law:\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s verbal assaults on judges, prosecutors, witnesses, jurors and the broader US justice system, are undermining the rule of law and American democracy while fueling threats and potential violence against individuals involved with the legal cases against him and egging on his extremist allies, former federal prosecutors and judges say.\par \par \uc2 In his campaign to win the presidency again, and in the midst of various criminal and civil trials, Trump has launched multiple attacks on the American legal system on his Truth Social platform to counter the 88 federal and state criminal charges he faces.\par \par \uc2 Trump, the all but certain Republican presidential nominee for 2024, has accelerated glorifying the insurgents who attacked the Capitol on 6 January 2021. He has called them \u8220\'20\'1Cpatriots\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Chostages\u8221\'20\'1D, while promising that if he wins, he will free those convicted of crimes as one of his \u8220\'20\'1Cfirst acts\u8221\'20\'1D in office.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, Trump has repeatedly cast doubt on the electoral system. He has refused to say he will accept the results of the 2024 elections, a ploy similar to what he did in 2020 before falsely claiming the election was rigged \u8211\'20\'13 a claim he still maintains.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf everything\u8217\'20\'19s honest, I\u8217\'20\'19ll gladly accept the results,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump told the Milwaukee Journal Sentinel last week. \u8220\'20\'1CIf it\u8217\'20\'19s not, you have to fight for the right of the country.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Darkly, Trump has also warned that if he loses the election there will be \u8220\'20\'1Cbedlam\u8221\'20\'1D and a \u8220\'20\'1Cbloodbath for the country\u8221\'20\'1D. These words referred, in part, to the fallout Trump predicted for the auto industry, but have distinct echoes of his false charges that he lost to \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  in 2020 due to fraud.\par \par \uc2 Read the full story:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/may/07/trump-trial-justice-system-violence"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s scattershot attacks on justice system are causing real damage}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.01pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 Talks could end impasse over vote for Johnson's removal\par \par \uc2 A lunchtime summit Tuesday could finally offer clarity on whether \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene\uc2  still intends to press ahead with her drive to oust the House speaker, Mike Johnson, or accept a face-saving alternative that would give the impression of a win.\par \par \uc2 The extremist Georgia congresswoman is scheduled to meet Johnson for a second successive day to discuss her promise to call a motion to vacate, the procedure that could lead to a vote for his removal, over his collusion with Democrats to pass US funding for Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 Politico {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/newsletters/playbook/2024/05/07/inside-the-johnson-mtg-talks-00156448?nname=playbook&nid=0000014f-1646-d88f-a1cf-5f46b7bd0000&nrid=ef9757b7-1c82-4c99-8e9a-082111707afd&nlid=630318"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported this morning}}}\uc2  that Monday\u8217\'20\'19s talks, also attended by Greene\u8217\'20\'19s new ally, the Kentucky congressman \uc2 Thomas Massie\uc2 , were cordial, if not entirely fruitful. The outlet said Johnson told reporters afterwards that they had made a promise to \u8220\'20\'1Ckeep this team together\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 But it\u8217\'20\'19s not platitudes Greene is seeking, it\u8217\'20\'19s concessions. Politico listed four demands of the Greene-Massie alliance, most prominently a pledge from Johnson there will be no more US aid for Ukraine as it battles a Russian invasion.\par \par \uc2 They also want implementation of the so-called {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.congressionalinstitute.org/2013/07/17/the-hastert-rule/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Hastert rule}}}\uc2  (named for former speaker Dennis Hastert ), in which legislation is only brought for a floor vote if a majority of Republicans support it; defunding of special counsel investigations into former president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  ; and adoption of the \u8220\'20\'1CMassie rule\u8221\'20\'1D that automatically cuts government funding when no agreement is reached by a certain deadline.\par \par \uc2 With substantial Ukraine funding {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/20/us-house-approves-61bn-aid-ukraine#:~:text=US%20House%20approves%20%2461bn,House%20of%20Representatives%20%7C%20The%20Guardian"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 already passed}}}\uc2 , and likely to last until beyond November\u8217\'20\'19s election, that demand might not be the hurdle it seems. And Johnson will be keen to avoid the embarrassment of having to rely on Democratic support in any vote to remove him.\par \par \uc2 He certainly has nothing to lose by extending the talks today, and several political analysts see the frozen Greene-Johnson relationship beginning to thaw.\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19ll be watching for developments.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.57pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.10pm BST\par \par \uc2 Standoff between \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene\uc2  and Mike Johnson continues with ouster vote looming\par \par \uc2 Good morning, US politics blog readers.\par \par \uc2 The never ending story, also known as the Republican speaker saga, continues today with a scheduled next round of talks between firebrand extremist \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene\uc2  and Mike Johnson, the leader she has promised to unseat.\par \par \uc2 The pair met for several hours on Monday, with some observers suggesting the Georgia congresswoman is looking for an off-ramp, knowing that Democrats have already promised to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/30/marjorie-taylor-greene-mike-johnson-democrats"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 keep Johnson in place}}}\uc2  in any House vote to oust him.\par \par \uc2 But it\u8217\'20\'19s not an olive branch that Greene, and her new close ally \uc2 Thomas Massie\uc2  of Kentucky, are seeking. They want a block on further US funding for Ukraine, which caused her outrage in the first place, and a host of other political concessions we\u8217\'20\'19ll look at in the blog shortly.\par \par \uc2 As things stand, Greene, Johnson and probably Massie are set to converse again at lunchtime. Whether Greene can be talked out of pressing ahead with a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/may/06/house-speaker-mike-johnson-marjorie-taylor-greene"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 potentially embarrassing \u8220\'20\'1Cmotion to vacate\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2 , the vote that could see Johnson booted, remains to be seen.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else we\u8217\'20\'19re watching today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Texas Democratic congressman {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/may/04/dean-phillips-henry-cuellar-indictment"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Henry Cuellar}}}\uc2  is fighting for his political life days after he and his wife were indicted for bribery, fraud and money laundering over their links to Azerbaijan. Democratic leadership issued a lukewarm message of support, and Cuellar\u8217\'20\'19s chief of staff Jake Hochberg quit Monday, with other staff said to be planning to join him.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Johnson has a busy day, aside from his meeting with Greene and Massie. He\u8217\'20\'19ll be hosting a press conference with Republican leadership this morning, and meeting King Abdullah of Jordan in Washington DC this afternoon.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will deliver remarks at the \uc2 US Holocaust Memorial Museum\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Days of Remembrance ceremony this morning and meet the Romanian president, \uc2 Klaus Iohannis\uc2 , at the White House this afternoon.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 White House press secretary \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s daily media briefing is scheduled for 2pm ET.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.40pm BST\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240507ek57001ry\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
