\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18This is life and death\u8217\'20\'19: inside a Florida clinic after the six-week  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  ban\b0\par\par\uc2 Carter Sherman \par \uc2 2,079 \uc2 words\par \uc2 3 May 2024\par 14:01 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 State\u8217\'20\'19s fall as the last bastion of access to the procedure in the deep south means women will have to travel farther for care\par \par \uc2 Rose hadn\u8217\'20\'19t even missed her period when the thought hit her: \u8220\'20\'1CI need to take a test.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The Florida resident, who has two kids, had given birth just three months ago. She thought that she and her husband were being careful. But the pregnancy test confirmed her suspicion: she was pregnant and, she realized, didn\u8217\'20\'19t want to be.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt would just be a very big financial, physical, emotional strain,\u8221\'20\'1D said Rose, who asked to be identified by a nickname. Her last two pregnancies were enormously difficult and she feared for her health. She wants to be a tattoo artist, but she\u8217\'20\'19s not working at the moment. Her husband has only recently started a new job. Rose continued: \u8220\'20\'1CI want to start a career and go to school and learn new things and it\u8217\'20\'19s a lot harder with more kids. It\u8217\'20\'19s already more difficult with the kids that I have.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 By the time she took a pregnancy test, Rose estimates that she was maybe four weeks into her pregnancy. She was lucky: many people don\u8217\'20\'19t realize they\u8217\'20\'19re pregnant that early. Rose also moved swiftly to secure an appointment at a Florida \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinic. Still, by Tuesday, when Rose sat in a dimly lit room decorated with butterfly collages and a doctor pressed a white pill into her hand to start a medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Rose was six weeks and four days into her pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 Had Rose arrived at the clinic a single day later, she would not have been able to get an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Florida. On Wednesday, Florida banned \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  past six weeks of pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere\u8217\'20\'19s still a lot I can do at my age, and that I want to do at my age and that I\u8217\'20\'19m not really gonna get a chance to do if I\u8217\'20\'19m continuing to be pregnant and have more kids,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 Rose is 19 years old.\par \par \uc2 For nearly two years after the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  overturned Roe v Wade, Florida stood as the last bastion of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access in the US deep south. Even though the state had a 15-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, providers there performed more than 84,000 abortions in 2023, including almost 9,000 on out-of-state patients. But on 1 April, the Florida supreme court ruled to uphold the 15-week ban \u8211\'20\'13 and, due to legislative maneuvering by Florida\u8217\'20\'19s Republican-controlled state legislature, that decision paved the way for the six-week ban to take effect on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 The impact of the ban will ripple across the US. Women who are past six weeks \u8211\'20\'13 about 60% of Florida abortions take place after that point in pregnancy \u8211\'20\'13 will have to travel at least several states away for abortions, further burdening the relatively few \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinics that have survived Roe\u8217\'20\'19s fall. Women who can\u8217\'20\'19t afford to travel may self-manage their abortions, a process that, if undertaken early enough in pregnancy, is medically safe but legally fraught.\par \par \uc2 Women may also be forced to remain pregnant against their will.\par \par \uc2 The phone rang off the hook on Tuesday, the last day before the ban took effect, at the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinic that performed Rose\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Bread and Roses Women\u8217\'20\'19s Health Center in swampy Gainesville, Florida. A squat building nearly hidden behind a lush wall of ivy, Bread and Roses\u8217\'20\'19s walls are decorated in butterfly motifs and motivational posters. One small, framed poster featured a uterus-shaped American flag under the stark word: \u8220\'20\'1Cvote\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Bread and Roses normally sees somewhere between 20 and 30 patients a day, but throughout April, as the ban neared, the clinic added extra hours and started to see closer to 40 patients a day. Desperate to squeeze in as many patients as possible on Tuesday, staffers barely had time to even eat. The doctor who was performing abortions kept attempting to heat up her pasta lunch, only to be repeatedly interrupted. Kristin, the clinic director, made toast but was pulled away to do ultrasounds; by the time she remembered to return to it, hours later, the bread had hardened into a hockey puck. (Kristin asked to be identified by her first name due to safety concerns.)\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s not okay to force somebody to do that with their body\par \par \uc2 Rose\par \par \uc2 Almost every phone call seemed to include some version of the same conversation, as clinic staffers asked would-be patients: do you know about the six-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban? When was your last menstrual period? Do you think you\u8217\'20\'19re less than six weeks along?\par \par \uc2 If a caller seemed like they were past that limit, staffers steered them towards resources to help them find an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinic in another state. One woman, pregnant from her husband\u8217\'20\'19s repeated sexual assaults, cried on the phone on Wednesday as a staffer told her that she likely couldn\u8217\'20\'19t get an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Florida. The woman, who lived in a state with a near-total \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, was confused by Florida\u8217\'20\'19s ban and overwhelmed by the difficulty of having to travel even farther than she had imagined.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis law is changing everything,\u8221\'20\'1D a Bread and Roses staffer told another, baffled caller. \u8220\'20\'1CIf you are over six weeks, we just would not be able to move forward with an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s horrible,\u8221\'20\'1D the staffer added. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s not fair at all.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Yet another woman who called Bread and Roses on Wednesday had accidentally gone to a crisis pregnancy center, an anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  facility that aims to convince people to continue their pregnancies. They\u8217\'20\'19re often located close enough to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinics to confuse people. (A similar facility was located just two doors down from Bread and Roses.) People at the crisis pregnancy center told the woman that taking \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills could lead her to give birth on the toilet, according to a Bread and Roses staffer, who was enraged by the sheer misinformation. How could this be legal, but an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  past six weeks was not?\par \par \uc2 Complicating everything is the fact that Florida also requires patients to go to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinic for a consultation at least 24 hours before they actually get the procedure or pills. That restriction further cuts down on the amount of time that women have to recognize they are pregnant, realize they want an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and get to a clinic.\par \par \uc2 Floridians past six weeks of pregnancy may have to venture to clinics in states like New Mexico, Kansas and Illinois. North Carolina is a closer option for many Floridians \u8211\'20\'13 but that state only permits abortions until 12 weeks of pregnancy and its waiting period is also even more onerous than Florida\u8217\'20\'19s. It requires people to show up at a clinic for an initial consultation at least 72 hours before their \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 One patient at Bread and Roses on Tuesday, who asked to be identified by her initial A, was little more than five weeks into her pregnancy. A new mom with a months-old baby at home, A had always opposed \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but she had developed heart failure during her last pregnancy. Then she had a seizure about a week after giving birth.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAfter my condition after my last pregnancy, I realized it\u8217\'20\'19s something people should have a right to if need be,\u8221\'20\'1D A said of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CI feel like women should have rights to their bodies. I think it\u8217\'20\'19s cruel, honestly, for people with health conditions, like myself.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 A, who isn\u8217\'20\'19t working right now, didn\u8217\'20\'19t know what she would do if she had been unable to get an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Florida. With a sigh, she suggested: \u8220\'20\'1CI would have been stressed out and delivered the baby.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Rose already knows what it\u8217\'20\'19s like to be denied an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . When she got pregnant with her son at 16, she considered having an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but her deeply conservative mom refused to let her get one, she said. Then, due to an injury sustained at birth, Rose\u8217\'20\'19s son was born with severe disabilities.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI was a 17-year-old kid taking care of a heavily disabled child,\u8221\'20\'1D Rose said. \u8220\'20\'1CI love my son very much. I don\u8217\'20\'19t regret him.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 But, she added: \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s not okay to force somebody to do that with their body.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 I don\u8217\'20\'19t understand how somebody can\u8217\'20\'19t see how harmful this law is. This is life and death for some people\par \par \uc2 Kristin\par \par \uc2 Most minors involve parents in their decision to get an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but minors in Florida who cannot or will not do so must, instead, go to court to convince a judge that they are mature enough to get an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . (The default assumption is that they are mature enough to give birth.) Their victory is far from guaranteed: in the two years before Roe\u8217\'20\'19s demise, Florida {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.hrw.org/report/2023/02/09/access-denied/how-florida-judges-obstruct-young-peoples-ability-obtain-abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 judges denied more than 12% of 200-plus minors\u8217\'20\'19 requests}}}\uc2 . Even if a minor succeeds, the court process can also take days, if not weeks.\par \par \uc2 Under a six-week ban, minors will likely be unable to surmount these legal hurdles in time. But even if they can secure a parent\u8217\'20\'19s permission for an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , minors are especially likely to be denied them under Florida\u8217\'20\'19s six-week ban. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ansirh.org/research/research/one-three-people-learn-theyre-pregnant-past-six-weeks-gestation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Two in three 15- to 19-year-olds}}}\uc2  realize they are pregnant after six weeks.\par \par \uc2 Because Bread and Roses staffers prioritized patients who seemed like they were less than six weeks into their pregnancy, all of the patients who showed up for consultations on Tuesday could legally get an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  by Wednesday. But on Wednesday, the clinic had to tell three or four people that they were past Florida\u8217\'20\'19s legal limit, according to the doctor performing abortions on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 The clinic did not track how many people called but seemed beyond the six-week limit already. Kristin, the clinic director, estimated that about half of callers were not able to be scheduled.\par \par \uc2 Kristin suspects that, in the coming days, Bread and Roses will be forced to turn away even more. As the ban made headlines so much in April, she thinks people might be paying more attention than normal to their periods and pregnancies; if the ban falls out of headlines, people may forget about it until it\u8217\'20\'19s too late. On Wednesday afternoon, Kristin sat in the clinic\u8217\'20\'19s parking lot, clad in black scrubs, and scrunched her knees to her chest.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI feel exhausted today. I feel incredibly sad and angry. I\u8217\'20\'19m so angry,\u8221\'20\'1D Kristin said. \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m so naive. I want to think that people have the best intentions and this law is just so harmful. I don\u8217\'20\'19t understand how somebody can\u8217\'20\'19t see how harmful this law is. This is life and death for some people.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn the deep places of my heart, I don\u8217\'20\'19t understand it,\u8221\'20\'1D she repeated.\par \par \uc2 There is a sliver of hope for Bread and Roses staffers: in November, Florida is set to vote on a ballot measure that would enshrine \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in the state constitution, making the six-week ban unconstitutional. Similar measures have already triumphed in states across the country, including Republican strongholds like Kansas and Ohio.\par \par \uc2 Notably, ballot measures in increasingly red Florida must garner 60% of the vote to pass. Even if \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights supporters do win in November, Florida\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws would not officially change until January. Floridians will have to live under the six-week ban for months.\par \par \uc2 Clinics may also not survive the ban. Unable to perform most abortions, they\u8217\'20\'19re facing a devastating financial hit \u8211\'20\'13 but it\u8217\'20\'19s impossible to map its exact blast radius.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHow do you plan for it, when you don\u8217\'20\'19t know what to expect?\u8221\'20\'1D Kristin said. \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19ll be fine. We\u8217\'20\'19re not closing. We\u8217\'20\'19ll figure it out.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Like many other patients at Bread and Roses, Rose had never heard of the ballot measure before her \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  appointment. She is not registered to vote, but she does want to vote for the ballot measure.\par \par \uc2 The six-week ban, she said, is \u8220\'20\'1Cevil\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFlorida, along with the United States, is going downhill,\u8221\'20\'1D Rose said. \u8220\'20\'1CI used to like living here, but I\u8217\'20\'19m planning on moving out as soon as I can.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240503ek53001ur\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
