\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Arizona governor signs into law measure to repeal 1864  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  ban\b0\par\par\uc2 Carter Sherman \par \uc2 320 \uc2 words\par \uc2 2 May 2024\par 20:53 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 State supreme court had ruled that the near-total \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban could be enforced, unleashing unprecedented outrage\par \par \uc2 After weeks of national outcry and intense political warfare, \uc2 Katie Hobbs\uc2  on Thursday signed into law a measure to repeal an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/09/arizona-supreme-court-abortion-decision"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 1864 near-total \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  ban }}}\uc2  that was passed before Arizona even became a state.\par \par \uc2 The signature of the Democratic Arizona governor is the result of a stunning turn in Arizona politics and the white-hot debate over \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights post-Roe v Wade. The 1864 ban, which only permits abortions to save a woman\u8217\'20\'19s life, had long threatened to return to force, but in April the Arizona supreme court ruled the ban could be enforced.\par \par \uc2 The decision unleashed unprecedented outrage in a state that promises to be a major battleground in the November elections \u8211\'20\'13 and a handful of Republicans, who hold a one-seat majority in the Arizona state house and senate, ultimately broke with the Arizona GOP and joined Democrats to vote for the repeal.\par \par \uc2 Hobbs\u8217\'20\'19 signature does not alone guarantee that the ban will not take effect. Arizona legislation typically takes effect 90 days after the conclusion of the state legislative session, which may last into the summer. Arizona Democratic lawmakers lacked the numbers to add an emergency clause into the repeal to let it go into effect earlier; although legal maneuvers have delayed the ban\u8217\'20\'19s implementation, the it may temporarily come into force.\par \par \uc2 On Wednesday, Planned Parenthood of Arizona announced that, in light of Hobbs\u8217\'20\'19 anticipated signing of the bill, it was filing a legal motion to ask the courts to hold off on enforcing the 1864 ban.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is currently banned after 15 weeks of pregnancy in Arizona. Come November, the state looks likely to hold a ballot measure that would ask voters to enshrine \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights into the state constitution.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240502ek520035x\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
