\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Biden campaign condemns Trump\u8217\'20\'19s refusal to commit to honoring November election results \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Chris Stein \par \uc2 4,644 \uc2 words\par \uc2 2 May 2024\par 20:01 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 This live blog is now closed. For more on US politics, read our stories here.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 Closing summary\par \par \uc2 In a surprise address from the White House, \uc2 Joe Biden{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/may/02/trump-biden-election-campaign-politics-latest-updates?page=with:block-6633acbf8f081efe1175c1e0#block-6633acbf8f081efe1175c1e0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 condemned violence}}}\uc2  on university campuses where pro-Palestine demonstrations are taking place, while saying the unrest {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/may/02/trump-biden-election-campaign-politics-latest-updates?page=with:block-6633ad998f081efe1175c1fb#block-6633ad998f081efe1175c1fb"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 would not spur him}}}\uc2  to change his policies in the Middle East. Meanwhile, his campaign {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/may/02/trump-biden-election-campaign-politics-latest-updates?page=with:block-6633bdcd8f08715725f7b465#block-6633bdcd8f08715725f7b465"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 hit out}}}\uc2  at \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , who yesterday held a rally in swing state Wisconsin and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/may/02/trump-biden-election-campaign-politics-latest-updates?page=with:block-6633866e8f0863b97d7f7250#block-6633866e8f0863b97d7f7250"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 refused to commit}}}\uc2  to accepting the results of the November presidential election. Trump also repeated his debunked claim that the 2020 election was marred by fraud.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else happened today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Biden{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/may/02/trump-biden-election-campaign-politics-latest-updates?page=with:block-6633d9bc8f082dacd422070e#block-6633d9bc8f082dacd422070e"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 met}}}\uc2  with the families of four law enforcement officers killed while serving a warrant in North Carolina last week, as well as those wounded in the shooting.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/may/02/trump-biden-election-campaign-politics-latest-updates?page=with:block-663399d38f08ce8daad5793f#block-663399d38f08ce8daad5793f"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 stayed away}}}\uc2  from the issue of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in his Wisconsin appearance, which Democrats have used to direct voter anger against Republicans in recent elections there and in other states.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 In addition to Wisconsin, Trump also visited fellow Great Lakes swing state Michigan, where his fans {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/may/02/trump-biden-election-campaign-politics-latest-updates?page=with:block-6633a0578f08566ae4badb0e#block-6633a0578f08566ae4badb0e"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 offered a reprieve}}}\uc2  from the dreary New York courthouse in which he has lately been spending a lot of time.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The campus protests are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/may/02/trump-biden-election-campaign-politics-latest-updates?page=with:block-6633b8268f082dacd4220514#block-6633b8268f082dacd4220514"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the latest complication}}}\uc2  to Biden\u8217\'20\'19s re-election chances, after he sparked the ire of key Democratic voting groups by backing Israel\u8217\'20\'19s invasion of Gaza.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Napping in court? {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/may/02/trump-biden-election-campaign-politics-latest-updates?page=with:block-6633e9888f081efe1175c590#block-6633e9888f081efe1175c590"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Not me}}}\uc2 , Trump said, despite reports to the contrary.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.01pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.47pm BST\par \par \uc2 Perhaps you have heard that South Dakota\u8217\'20\'19s Republican governor \uc2 Kristi Noem\uc2  killed a dog (the Guardian {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/books/2024/apr/26/trump-kristi-noem-shot-dog-and-goat-book"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 broke the story}}}\uc2 , after all!). Noem now says she had no choice, but blamed \u8220\'20\'1Cfake news\u8221\'20\'1D (must be referring to us) for pushing the story that may have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/30/kristi-noem-puppy-trump-vp-candidate"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sunk her chances}}}\uc2  of becoming \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s running mate, the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/martin-pengelly"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Martin Pengelly}}}\uc2  reports:\par \par \uc2 Kristi Noem\uc2 , the governor of South Dakota whose chance of being \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s presidential running mate was widely deemed over after she published a description of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/books/2024/apr/26/trump-kristi-noem-shot-dog-and-goat-book"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 shooting dead a dog and a goat}}}\uc2 , claimed reports of the story were \u8220\'20\'1Cfake news\u8221\'20\'1D but also that the dog in question, Cricket, a 14-month-old wirehaired pointer, was \u8220\'20\'1Cextremely dangerous\u8221\'20\'1D and deserved her fate.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou know how the fake news works,\u8221\'20\'1D Noem told Fox News. \u8220\'20\'1CThey leave out some or most of the facts of a story, they put the worst spin on it. And that\u8217\'20\'19s what\u8217\'20\'19s happened in this case.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI hope people really do buy this book and they find out the truth of the story because the truth of the story is that this was a working dog and it was not a puppy. It was a dog that was extremely dangerous.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2  first {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/books/2024/apr/26/trump-kristi-noem-shot-dog-and-goat-book"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2  Noem\u8217\'20\'19s story of killing Cricket the dog and an unnamed, un-castrated male goat. The story is contained in Noem\u8217\'20\'19s book, No Going Back: The Truth on What\u8217\'20\'19s Wrong With Politics and How We Move America Forward, which will be published next week. \uc2 The Guardian\uc2  obtained a copy.\par \par \uc2 In the book, Noem says her description of killing a dog and a goat illustrates her willingness to do anything \u8220\'20\'1Cdifficult, messy and ugly\u8221\'20\'1D in politics as well as on her {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/south-dakota"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 South Dakota}}}\uc2  farm \u8211\'20\'13 a defence she repeated before her Fox News interview.\par \par \uc2 Noem says Cricket ruined a pheasant hunt and then killed a neighbour\u8217\'20\'19s chickens, all the while presenting \u8220\'20\'1Cthe picture of pure joy\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/may/02/kristi-noem-response-dog-killing"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kristi Noem calls dog shooting report \u8216\'20\'18fake news\u8217\'20\'19 but insists on need to kill animal}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.56pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.31pm BST\par \par \uc2 Legal proceedings can be dull, sometimes so dull they put you to sleep \u8211\'20\'13 even if you happen to be a former president.\par \par \uc2 On the first day of his trial in New York, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  appeared to shut his eyes for an extended period of time. That was a couple of weeks ago now, but he just got around to denying doing so, in a post {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://truthsocial.com/@realDonaldTrump/posts/112372819456433498"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 on Truth Social}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 Contrary to the FAKE NEWS MEDIA, I don\u8217\'20\'19t fall asleep during the Crooked D.A.\u8217\'20\'19s Witch Hunt, especially not today. I simply close my beautiful blue eyes, sometimes, listen intensely, and take it ALL in!!!\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more on the alleged nap:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/15/trump-asleep-first-day-hush-money-trial"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Fake snooze? Trump appears to doze off during first day of hush-money trial}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.16pm BST\par \par \uc2 Yesterday, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  was appearing before crowds in Michigan and Wisconsin \u8211\'20\'13 two swing states that will put him well on his way to the White House, if he wins them in November.\par \par \uc2 Today, he\u8217\'20\'19s back at the defense table in a Manhattan courtroom, where his lawyers are cross-examining \uc2 Keith Davidson\uc2 , a former attorney for Stormy Daniels, the adult film actor at the center of the case against him for allegedly falsifying business records.\par \par \uc2 Follow our live blog for the latest from the trial:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/may/02/trump-trial-hush-money-stormy-daniels-keith-davidson-latest-updates"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Tensions high between Trump lawyer and Stormy Daniels\u8217\'20\'19 ex-attorney at hush-money trial \u8211\'20\'13 live}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.53pm BST\par \par \uc2 Fun fact about \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 : the 2020 election was the first one in which he faced a sustained campaign of negative television advertising, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2024/05/02/us/politics/biden-election-campaign-opponents.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the New York Times reports}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 And it goes without saying that 2024 will be his second. In a look back at his lengthy political career, the Times recounts what it was like for the Republicans who attempted to oust Biden from his Senate seat in Delaware, over the 36 years he represented the state.\par \par \uc2 Biden was something of juggernaut, his ex-opponents recount, both personally, and in the campaign infrastructure he wielded:\par \par \uc2 In Delaware, Mr. Biden was so well known and, in his early years in office, had such a wellspring of sympathy from voters after the tragic crash that killed his first wife and daughter, that no rival ever mounted a sustained case that he should not be re-elected. For years, bumper stickers promoting his re-election just said \u8216\'20\'18Joe,\u8217\'20\'19 while opponents lost with an array of long-forgotten slogans.\par \par \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18I don\u8217\'20\'19t think he ever broke a sweat once he was an incumbent,\u8217\'20\'19 said Jane Brady, a Republican {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/1990/11/08/us/the-1990-elections-state-by-state-northeast.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 who lost to Mr. Biden by 27 points in 1990}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The only negative ad run against Mr. Biden between 1978 and 2008, according to the \uc2 University of Oklahoma\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s archive, is one that his campaign would most likely embrace today. That 30-second spot reminded viewers that President \uc2 Ronald Reagan\uc2  endorsed John Burris, Mr. Biden\u8217\'20\'19s Republican challenger in 1984, while Mr. Biden backed the unpopular Democratic presidential nominee, \uc2 Walter Mondale\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The Biden of today often makes gaffes, to the chagrin of his supporters, and the delight of his enemies. Here\u8217\'20\'19s an example of a recent one, which was seized on by the conservative media:\par \par \uc2 Just last week, Mr. Biden prompted the crowd at an endorsement event to chant, \u8216\'20\'18Four more years!\u8217\'20\'19 and then added \u8216\'20\'18pause\u8217\'20\'19 as it appeared to have been written into his teleprompter, an episode that drew much {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://nypost.com/2024/04/24/us-news/biden-reads-pause-instruction-off-teleprompter-in-speech-to-union-members/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 mocking in conservative news media}}}\uc2  and quiet forehead-slapping among Democrats.\par \par \uc2 Back in the day, the Times reports such things did not happen:\par \par \uc2 Mr. Biden\u8217\'20\'19s opponent in 1996 and 2002 was Ray Clatworthy, an entrepreneur who owned restaurants and local Christian radio stations. During {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.c-span.org/video/?75509-1/delaware-senatorial-debate"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a 1996 televised debate}}}\uc2 , Mr. Clatworthy accused Mr. Biden of raising taxes while voting to increase his own salary and accused him of \u8216\'20\'18attempting to portray himself as a conservative\u8217\'20\'19 in an election year.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Biden spoke quickly and precisely, without entering the verbal cul-de-sacs endemic to many of his presidential speeches 28 years later.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Biden sought to pin down Mr. Clatworthy on his anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  stance and then delivered a clear statement of his own views on the issue after Mr. Clatworthy accused him of flip-flopping to endorse \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in his 1988 presidential campaign.\par \par \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18My position has been consistent from the very beginning,\u8217\'20\'19 Mr. Biden said of his \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  stance. \u8216\'20\'18I believe government should stay out \u8211\'20\'13 no constitutional amendment, no public funding.\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.09pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.23pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is now in Charlotte, North Carolina, where he is meeting with the families of four law enforcement officers killed and four others who were wounded while serving a warrant last week.\par \par \uc2 The shooting was the deadliest attack against police in the United States since 2016. Here\u8217\'20\'19s more about what happened:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/30/north-carolina-officers-killed-shootout"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Officers killed in shootout identified as rifle found in suspect\u8217\'20\'19s North Carolina home}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.04pm BST\par \par \uc2 As \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  rallied elsewhere in Wisconsin, demonstrators convened outside the venue that will host the Republican National Convention this summer to decry his vow to bring back hardline immigration policies if elected, the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/alice-herman"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Alice Herman}}}\uc2  reports:\par \par \uc2 Led by a mariachi band, hundreds of demonstrators on Wednesday morning marched across Milwaukee to the Fiserv Forum \u8211\'20\'13 the home of the \uc2 Milwaukee Bucks\uc2  and, in July, the venue of the Republican National Convention.\par \par \uc2 The rally, organized by the immigrant and workers\u8217\'20\'19 rights group Voces de la Frontera, is an annual event, but in 2024 it holds particular weight. The focus of the rally extended beyond immigration, to fear of authoritarianism under Republican candidate {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  and critique of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s handling of the US role in Israel and Gaza.\par \par \uc2 This year, May Day also fell on the same day as a Trump campaign event in Waukesha, which organizers seized on to denounce Trump\u8217\'20\'19s immigration policy and call on Biden to use his executive authority to adopt protections for undocumented workers.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe reject [Trump\u8217\'20\'19s] political platform, which promises dictatorship, deportations and separation of families,\u8221\'20\'1D Voces de la Frontera executive director Christine Neumann-Ortiz told the crowd on Wednesday, to applause.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/may/01/wisconsin-immigration-march-trump-rally"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Activists march for immigrant rights in Wisconsin: \u8216\'20\'18We\u8217\'20\'19re making this country strong\u8217\'20\'19}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.34pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.24pm BST\par \par \uc2 While \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  kept mum about \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in a visit to to the swing state of Wisconsin, he was far more open in a pair of interviews with Time in which he described in depth what he would like to do if returned to the White House. \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/edpilkington"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ed Pilkington}}}\uc2  has more:\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has warned that \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and his family could face multiple criminal prosecutions once he leaves office unless the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  awards Trump immunity in his own legal battles with the criminal justice system.\par \par \uc2 In a sweeping interview with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://time.com/6972021/donald-trump-2024-election-interview/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Time magazine}}}\uc2 , Trump painted a startling picture of his second term, from how he would wield the justice department to hinting he may let states monitor pregnant women to enforce \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws.\par \par \uc2 Trump made the threat against the Biden family in an interview with Eric Cortellessa of Time, in which he shared the outlines of what the magazine called \u8220\'20\'1Can imperial presidency that would reshape America and its role in the world\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Trump made a direct connection between his threat to appoint a special prosecutor to investigate the Bidens should he win re-election in November with the case currently before the supreme court over his own presidential immunity.\par \par \uc2 Asked whether he intends to \u8220\'20\'1Cgo after\u8221\'20\'1D the Bidens should he gain a second term in the White House, Trump replied: \u8220\'20\'1CIt depends what happens with the supreme court.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/30/trump-second-term-abortion-immigration"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump threatens to prosecute Bidens if he\u8217\'20\'19s re-elected unless he gets immunity }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.29pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.57pm BST\par \par \uc2 A potentially landmark lawsuit by youth activists against the federal government over its role in fueling the climate crisis was struck down by an appeals court, on the request of the Biden administration, the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/dharna-noor"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Dharna Noor}}}\uc2  reports:\par \par \uc2 A federal appeals court on Wednesday evening granted the Biden administration\u8217\'20\'19s request to strike down a landmark federal youth climate case, outraging climate advocates.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is a tragic and unjust ruling,\u8221\'20\'1D said Julia Olson, attorney and founder of Our Children\u8217\'20\'19s Trust, the non-profit law firm that brought the suit.\par \par \uc2 The lawsuit, Juliana v United States, was filed by 21 young people from Oregon who alleged the federal government\u8217\'20\'19s role in fueling the climate crisis violates their constitutional rights.\par \par \uc2 The Wednesday order from a panel of three Trump-appointed judges on the ninth circuit court of appeals will require a US district court judge to dismiss the case for lack of standing, with no opening to amend the complaint.\par \par \uc2 The decision affirmed an emergency petition filed by the justice department in February arguing that \u8220\'20\'1Cthe government will be irreparably harmed\u8221\'20\'1D if it is forced to spend time and resources litigating the Juliana case. It\u8217\'20\'19s a measure the justice department should never have taken, said Olson.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe Biden administration was wrong to use an emergency measure to stop youth plaintiffs from having their day in court,\u8221\'20\'1D she said in a statement. \u8220\'20\'1CThe real emergency is the climate emergency.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/may/02/youth-climate-lawsuit-juliana-appeals-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Court strikes down youth climate lawsuit on Biden administration request}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.45pm BST\par \par \uc2 The day so far\par \par \uc2 In a surprise address from the White House, \uc2 Joe Biden{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/may/02/trump-biden-election-campaign-politics-latest-updates?page=with:block-6633acbf8f081efe1175c1e0#block-6633acbf8f081efe1175c1e0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 condemned violence}}}\uc2  on university campuses where pro-Palestine demonstrations are taking place, while saying the unrest {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/may/02/trump-biden-election-campaign-politics-latest-updates?page=with:block-6633ad998f081efe1175c1fb#block-6633ad998f081efe1175c1fb"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 would not spur him}}}\uc2  to change his policies in the Middle East. Meanwhile, his campaign {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/may/02/trump-biden-election-campaign-politics-latest-updates?page=with:block-6633bdcd8f08715725f7b465#block-6633bdcd8f08715725f7b465"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 hit out}}}\uc2  at \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , who yesterday held a rally in swing state Wisconsin and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/may/02/trump-biden-election-campaign-politics-latest-updates?page=with:block-6633866e8f0863b97d7f7250#block-6633866e8f0863b97d7f7250"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 refused to commit}}}\uc2  to accepting the results of the November presidential election. He also repeated his debunked claim that the 2020 election was marred by fraud.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else has happened today so far:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/may/02/trump-biden-election-campaign-politics-latest-updates?page=with:block-663399d38f08ce8daad5793f#block-663399d38f08ce8daad5793f"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 stayed away}}}\uc2  from the issue of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in his Wisconsin appearance, which Democrats have used to direct voter anger against Republicans in recent elections there and in other states.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 In addition to Wisconsin, Trump also visited fellow Great Lakes swing state Michigan, where his fans {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/may/02/trump-biden-election-campaign-politics-latest-updates?page=with:block-6633a0578f08566ae4badb0e#block-6633a0578f08566ae4badb0e"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 offered a reprieve}}}\uc2  from the dreary New York courthouse in which he has lately been spending a lot of time.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The campus protests are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/may/02/trump-biden-election-campaign-politics-latest-updates?page=with:block-6633b8268f082dacd4220514#block-6633b8268f082dacd4220514"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the latest complication}}}\uc2  to Biden\u8217\'20\'19s re-election chances, after he sparked the ire of key Democratic voting groups by backing Israel\u8217\'20\'19s invasion of Gaza.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.24pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden campaign condemns Trump's refusal to commit to honoring November election results\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s re-election campaign has come out swinging against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s refusal in an interview yesterday to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/may/02/trump-biden-election-campaign-politics-latest-updates?page=with:block-6633866e8f0863b97d7f7250#block-6633866e8f0863b97d7f7250"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 commit to accepting}}}\uc2  the results of the presidential election in November.\par \par \uc2 From spokesman James Singer :\par \par \uc2 President Biden has said, \u8216\'20\'18You can\u8217\'20\'19t love your country only when you win.\u8217\'20\'19 But for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , his campaign for revenge and retribution reigns supreme.\par \par \uc2 In his own words, he is promising to rule as a dictator on \u8216\'20\'18day one\u8217\'20\'19, use the military against the American people, punish those who stand against him, condone violence done on his behalf and put his own quest for power ahead of what is best for America.\par \par \uc2 Bottom line: Trump is a danger to the constitution and a threat to our democracy. The American people are going to give him another electoral defeat this November because they continue to reject his extremism, his affection for violence and his thirst for revenge.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.27pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.59pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is already facing heat from some Democratic voters for his support of Israel as it invades Gaza following the 7 October attack. As the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/adam-gabbatt"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Adam Gabbatt}}}\uc2  reported earlier this week, the unrest on college campuses targeted at America\u8217\'20\'19s closest Middle East ally could present the latest complication to his campaign for another four years in the White House:\par \par \uc2 The policies of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/democrats"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Democrats}}}\uc2  towards Israel, which have prompted thousands of students across the country to protest, could affect the youth vote for Biden and hurt his re-election chances, experts have warned, in what is already expected to be a tight election.\par \par \uc2 Thousands of students at universities across the US have joined with pro-Palestine rallies and, most recently, encampments, as Israel\u8217\'20\'19s war in Gaza has killed more than 34,000 people.\par \par \uc2 Some of the protests began as a call to encourage universities to ditch investments in companies that provide weapons and equipment to the Israeli military. But as the Biden administration has continued to largely support Israel, the president has increasingly become a focus of criticism from young people. Polling shows that young Americans\u8217\'20\'19 support for Biden has been chipped away since 2020.\par \par \uc2 With Biden narrowly trailing Trump in several key swing states, it\u8217\'20\'19s a voting bloc the president can ill afford to lose.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe real threat to Biden is that younger voters, especially college-educated voters, won\u8217\'20\'19t turn out for him in the election,\u8221\'20\'1D said Jonathan Zimmerman, a professor of history of education at the \uc2 University of Pennsylvania\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t expect that the protesters on campuses today are going to vote for Trump, almost none of them will. That\u8217\'20\'19s not the danger here. The danger is much simpler: that they simply won\u8217\'20\'19t vote.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/may/01/university-protests-presidential-election-biden-youth-vote"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 What do the US campus protests mean for Joe Biden in November?}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.37pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  spoke about the nationwide protests against Israel at college campuses after police arrested more than 100 people at the \uc2 University of California, Los Angeles\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Follow our live blog for more on the ongoing demonstration wave:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/may/01/university-protests-pro-palestinian-demonstrators-arrested-latest-news"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Joe Biden expected to address US campus protests after more than 100 people arrested at UCLA \u8211\'20\'13 live}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 In his brief speech on the pro-Palestin e protests on college campuses, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  cast himself as a defender of free speech rights, but said the demonstrations should not disrupt students\u8217\'20\'19 learning.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CDissent is essential to democracy, but dissent must never lead to disorder or to denying the rights of others, so students can finish the semester and their college education. Look, it\u8217\'20\'19s basically a matter of fairness. It\u8217\'20\'19s a matter of what\u8217\'20\'19s right. There\u8217\'20\'19s the right to protest, but not the right to cause chaos. People have the right to get an education, right to get a degree, right to walk across campus safely without fear of being attacked,\u8221\'20\'1D the president said.\par \par \uc2 He later added:\par \par \uc2 There should be no place on any campus, no place in America for antisemitism, or threats of violence against Jewish students. There is no place for hate speech, or violence of any kind, whether it\u8217\'20\'19s antisemitism, Islamophobia, or discrimination against Arab Americans or Palestinian Americans. It\u8217\'20\'19s simply wrong. There\u8217\'20\'19s no place for racism in America. It\u8217\'20\'19s all wrong. It\u8217\'20\'19s not American.\par \par \uc2 Biden concluded with:\par \par \uc2 As president, I will always defend free speech. And I will always be just as strong in standing up for the rule of law. That\u8217\'20\'19s my responsibility to you, the American people, my obligation to the constitution.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.37pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.16pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden says no plans to change Middle East policies, call in national guard in response to protests\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  spoke for just three minutes before wrapping up.\par \par \uc2 Just after he finished, a reporter asked if the protests would make him reconsider any of his Middle East policies.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNo,\u8221\'20\'1D the president replied.\par \par \uc2 Another asked if he planned to send the national guard to universities hit by the demonstrations, as some {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/25/first-thing-dozens-more-protesters-arrested-as-mike-johnson-suggests-calling-in-national-guard"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republican}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.hawley.senate.gov/hawley-demands-biden-use-national-guard-protect-jewish-students-amid-pro-hamas-campus-protests"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 lawmakers}}}\uc2  have called for.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNo\u8221\'20\'1D was Biden\u8217\'20\'19s answer.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.55pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.13pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden says 'violent protest is not protected, peaceful protest is' in response to college demonstrations\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  attempted to draw a fine line between peaceful protests, which he says are protected by the law, and violent demonstrations, in his White House remarks amid widespread pro-Palestine protests at college campuses.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn America, violent protest is not protected. Peaceful protest is,\u8221\'20\'1D the president said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s against the law when violence occurs. Destroying property is not a peaceful protest. It\u8217\'20\'19s against the law. Vandalism, trespassing, breaking windows, shutting down campuses, forcing the cancellation of classes and graduations. None of this is a peaceful protest. Threatening people, intimidating people, instilling fear in people is not peaceful protest. It\u8217\'20\'19s against the law.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.15pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.08pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has begun his speech, which he says will address the recent anti-Israel protests on college campuses.\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19ll let you know what he says.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.04pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is often late to begin his speeches.\par \par \uc2 This one, scheduled to start at 10.30am, appears to be no different.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.45pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden to address campus protests in unscheduled speech - report\par \par \uc2 NBC News reports that the topic of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s surprise address from the White House will be the protests against Israel that have occurred on college campuses nationwide:\par \par \uc2 enltrNew: President Biden is expected to address growing protests on college campuses nationwide when he speaks from the Roosevelt Room shortly in previously unscheduled remarks, multiple sources tell {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/mikememoli?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @mikememoli}}}\uc2  & me\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Monica Alba (@albamonica) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/albamonica/status/1786043025069604905?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 2, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.41pm BST\par \par \uc2 The White House announced at 10.29am that \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  would make an unscheduled speech at 10.30am \u8211\'20\'13 a one -minute warning.\par \par \uc2 But the president is now 10 minutes late.\par \par \uc2 The speech is already unusual for its short notice, and the White House\u8217\'20\'19s lack of detail about what the president is addressing.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.42pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.34pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden to make unscheduled speech from White House\par \par \uc2 The White House just announced that \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will imminently deliver remarks, but the topic was not specified.\par \par \uc2 The speech was not previously scheduled. We will let you know what the president has to say.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.19pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s rally in Wisconsin yesterday was part of a brief campaign trip through two swing states that will be crucial to deciding the November elections. \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 David Smith\uc2  documented the former president\u8217\'20\'19s appearance in Michigan farm country:\par \par \uc2 At a remote rural airport in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/michigan"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Michigan}}}\uc2 , an outsized plane touched down as music from \uc2 Tom Cruise\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s film Top Gun boomed from loudspeakers. Late afternoon sunshine gleamed off five giant golden letters on the plane\u8217\'20\'19s side \u8211\'20\'13 \u8220\'20\'1CTRUMP\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 and its Rolls-Royce engines. A crowd bedecked in red roared as the plane rolled to a standstill behind a blue \u8220\'20\'1CTRUMP\u8221\'20\'1D lectern.\par \par \uc2 A door opened and men in dark glasses and dark suits from what {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  would call \u8220\'20\'1Ccentral casting\u8221\'20\'1D made their way down the stairs. \u8220\'20\'1CTrump! Trump!\u8221\'20\'1D the audience chanted, raising hundreds of camera phones in eager anticipation. Great Balls of Fire, Macho Man and YMCA blared. Finally, the former and would-be future president emerged, clapping and fist-pumping to the sound of whoops and cheers and Lee Greenwood\u8217\'20\'19s God Bless the USA.\par \par \uc2 How different the warm embrace from Trump\u8217\'20\'19s recent experience as a defendant on criminal trial in a chilly, dingy courtroom in New York. On those days, threatened with prison, he looks old, vulnerable and small. Back on the election campaign trail, it is all about hypermasculine energy and bigness \u8211\'20\'13 big plane, big crowds, big promises and big lies.\par \par \uc2 Trump had spent Tuesday in the now grimly familiar routine of the courtroom, where he is charged with 34 counts of falsifying business records to cover up a hush-money payment to the adult film performer Stormy Daniels. But the the court does not sit on Wednesday, freeing him to get a fresh shot of adulation from his fan base.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/may/01/trump-michigan-rally-new-york"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump trades New York worries for hit of adulation from his Maga faithful}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.25pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.59pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump declines to address Wisconsin \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban in swing state appearance\par \par \uc2 The Milwaukee Journal Sentinel asked \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  for his thoughts on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/sep/14/wisconsin-abortion-planned-parenthood"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Wisconsin\u8217\'20\'19s \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  ban}}}\uc2 , which is being challenged before the state supreme court, where liberal justices recently gained a majority.\par \par \uc2 The former president declined to comment, and generally avoided the issue in his rally in Waukesha, instead {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/08/trump-abortion-states"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 repeating}}}\uc2  that he thought it should be up to states to regulate the procedure, the \uc2 Journal Sentinel\uc2  reports.\par \par \uc2 Trump had a major role in the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s overturning of Roe v Wade in 2022, which paved the way for states to outlaw the procedure entirely, but has since fueled a string of Democratic victories in state and federal elections. He appointed three of the conservative judges who signed on to that ruling, but has since tried to avoid campaigning forcefully on the issue of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Yesterday, \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  traveled to Florida to decry a strict \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban that went into effect there, and warned voters not to believe Trump\u8217\'20\'19s insistence that he was not interested in passing a federal law cutting off access to the procedure. Here\u8217\'20\'19s a recap of her speech:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/may/01/speaker-mike-johnson-marjorie-taylor-greene-updates"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Arizona senate passes bill to repeal 1864 \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  ban; Harris says Trump\u8217\'20\'19s insistence he doesn\u8217\'20\'19t back national ban is \u8216\'20\'18gaslighting\u8217\'20\'19 \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.37pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump refuses to commit to accepting election loss and repeats 2020 lies in swing state Wisconsin rally\par \par \uc2 Yesterday, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  had the day off from his trial in New York City on charges related to falsifying business records, and held a rally in Wisconsin, a swing state crucial to his presidential election chances. After a speech spent attacking \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  over his handling of border security and inflation, Trump gave {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.jsonline.com/story/news/politics/elections/2024/05/01/economy-and-immigration-takeaways-from-donald-trumps-wisconsin-rally/73501778007/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 an interview}}}\uc2  to the Milwaukee Journal Sentinel, in which he falsely insisted that he won Wisconsin in 2020 (he did not) and \u8220\'20\'1Cother locations\u8221\'20\'1D, and refused to commit to accepting the results of this year\u8217\'20\'19s vote.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf everything\u8217\'20\'19s honest, I\u8217\'20\'19ll gladly accept the results. I don\u8217\'20\'19t change on that. If it\u8217\'20\'19s not, you have to fight for the right of the country,\u8221\'20\'1D the former president said.\par \par \uc2 The comments were yet another indication that Americans should be prepared for a rocky election aftermath, should Trump lose in November to Biden. After the Democrat defeated him in 2020, Trump spent weeks {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/01/trump-indictment-full-text-2020-election-jan-6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 attempting various plots}}}\uc2  to prevent Biden from taking power, culminating in the attack on the Capitol on January 6. Of course, there\u8217\'20\'19s the chance that Trump could indeed win election again, as he did in 2016 \u8211\'20\'13 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://projects.fivethirtyeight.com/polls/president-general/2024/national/?ex_cid=abcpromo"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 polls currently show}}}\uc2  a tight race with Biden, including in Wisconsin.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else is happening today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump is back in Manhattan as his trial resumes with testimony from \uc2 Keith Davidson\uc2 , a lawyer for adult film actor Stormy Daniels, who is at the heart of the allegations against the former president. We have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/liveblog/2024/may/02/trump-trial-hush-money-stormy-daniels-keith-davidson-latest-updates"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a live blog covering}}}\uc2  everything that goes on in the courtroom.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Police moved in against protesters at the \uc2 University of California, Los Angeles\uc2  as colleges nationwide grapple with anti-Israel demonstrations. Follow {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/may/01/university-protests-pro-palestinian-demonstrators-arrested-latest-news"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 our live blog}}}\uc2  for more on this developing story.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Biden is heading to North Carolina to pay his respects to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/30/north-carolina-officers-killed-shootout"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the four law enforcement officers killed}}}\uc2  while serving a warrant earlier this week, then will speak about his economic policies in the city of Wilmington at 4.30pm ET.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.05pm BST\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240502ek52001xs\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
