\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Arizona senate passes repeal of 1864 near-total  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  ban\b0\par\par\uc2 Maanvi Singh \par \uc2 862 \uc2 words\par \uc2 2 May 2024\par 15:12 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Democrats pick up support of two Republicans to repeal law reinstated three weeks ago, with governor expected to ratify repeal\par \par \uc2 Arizona lawmakers have repealed the state\u8217\'20\'19s 160-year-old statute banning nearly all abortions.\par \par \uc2 The 1864 law, which {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/09/arizona-supreme-court-abortion-decision"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 was reinstated}}}\uc2  by the state supreme court three weeks ago, has made \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  a central focus in the battleground state and galvanized Democrats seeking to enshrine \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 In the state senate, Democrats picked up the support of two Republicans in favor of repealing the ban. The Democratic governor, \uc2 Katie Hobbs\uc2 , is expected to ratify the repeal, which narrowly cleared the Arizona house last week after three Republicans joined with all the Democrats in the chamber.\par \par \uc2 Dozens of demonstrators for and against the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  gathered at the capitol before the vote, and others packed into the chamber\u8217\'20\'19s gallery to watch. As senators began to vote, Republicans in the chamber voiced bombastic protests and criticisms in floor speeches.\par \par \uc2 Antony Kern, a Republican who has been indicted as a fake elector in a plot to undermine the 2020 election results, said his fellow Republicans backing the ban were the \u8220\'20\'1Cepitome of delusion\u8221\'20\'1D. He claimed the vote would take the state down a slippery slope towards acceptance of pedophilia, as supporters cheered from the gallery with silent claps. Kern also compared the chamber repealing the bill to Nazi Germany.\par \par \uc2 Another Republican senator, JD Mesnard, played a sonogram recording of his child\u8217\'20\'19s heartbeat on the floor. He said: \u8220\'20\'1CThese will be fewer, these heart beatings.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Republican Shawnna Bolick gave a 20-minute speech in defense of her vote to support the repeal, covering stories about her own pregnancies, other pregnancies, and her critiques of the state\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic governor. Ultimately, she said, repealing the ban would allow Republicans to maintain a less extreme version of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions. She said: \u8220\'20\'1CWe should be pushing for the maximum protection for unborn children that can be sustained. I side with saving more babies\u8217\'20\'19 lives.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The civil-war era statute, which predates Arizona\u8217\'20\'19s statehood, bans nearly all abortions, including those sought by survivors of rape or incest. It also imposes prison terms for doctors and others who aid in abortions. The law had been blocked by the 1973 supreme court Roe v Wade decisions that granted the constitutional right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe are relieved that lawmakers have finally repealed this inhumane \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban \u8211\'20\'13 something extremist politicians refused to do for far too long,\u8221\'20\'1D said Victoria L\u243\'00\'F3pez, director of program and strategy for the ACLU of Arizona. \u8220\'20\'1CUnfortunately, cruel \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans like the law from 1864 have been at the center of political stunts for years, causing lasting harm to people who need abortions and their providers.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Last month, the state\u8217\'20\'19s Republican-appointed supreme court justices suggested it could be reinstated since Roe was overturned in 2022.\par \par \uc2 The repeal would not take effect until June or July, 90 days after the legislative session. Arizona\u8217\'20\'19s attorney general, Kris Mayes, a Democrat, has vowed not to enforce the ban in the meantime. Providers, including \uc2 Planned Parenthood\uc2 , have been preparing resources to help patients seeking abortions to travel out of state during the time that the ban is in effect.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CToday\u8217\'20\'19s vote by the Arizona senate to repeal the draconian 1864 \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban is a win for freedom in our state,\u8221\'20\'1D Mayes said.\par \par \uc2 Once the 1864 measure is stricken, a 2022 statue banning procedures after 15 weeks of pregnancy would supplant it as the state\u8217\'20\'19s ruling \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights advocates have emphasized that repealing the ban is not enough. \u8220\'20\'1CThis is an important step, but our work isn\u8217\'20\'19t done,\u8221\'20\'1D said \uc2 Ruben Gallego\uc2 , a US congressman from Arizona who is running for the \uc2 US Senate\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CArizona women deserve better. That\u8217\'20\'19s why we\u8217\'20\'19re going to pass a constitutional right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and defeat anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  extremists.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Democrats have been pushing for a ballot measure in November that would enshrine the right to abortions in the state\u8217\'20\'19s constitution. In the weeks since the ban was reinstated , the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://arizonaforabortionaccess.org/what-is-the-aaa/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Arizona for \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22  Access}}}\uc2  effort saw its volunteers grow from about 3,000 to more than 5,000.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNothing has changed about the need for the Arizona \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access act,\u8221\'20\'1D the group organizing the ballot measure said following the passage of the repeal.\par \par \uc2 The issue has placed enormous pressure on the Arizona GOP, from conservatives who support the ban and from swing voters who oppose the extreme measure. On the senate floor on Wednesday, Bolick, as she cast her vote in favor of the repeal, said: \u8220\'20\'1CI want to protect our state constitution from unlimited abortions up until the moment of birth.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In the key swing state \u8211\'20\'13 one that historically leaned Republican but backed Joe Biden in 2020 \u8211\'20\'13 the issue could help turn out more voters who could help flip the statehouse blue.\par \par \uc2 Republican lawmakers are considering putting one or more competing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  proposals on the November ballot, including a 14-week ban and a \u8220\'20\'1Cheartbeat protection act\u8221\'20\'1D that would make \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  illegal after six weeks. No such measures have been introduced yet.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240501ek51002jp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
