\par\par \uc2 World news\par \b \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Resist the state\u8217\'20\'19: activists teach Floridians to \u8216\'20\'18self-manage\u8217\'20\'19 abortions in wake of ban\b0\par\par\uc2 Carter Sherman \par \uc2 857 \uc2 words\par \uc2 2 May 2024\par 14:35 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 As the state bans \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  past six weeks of pregnancy, a community care network springs to action in Gainesville\par \par \uc2 On Wednesday, the same day Florida banned \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  past six weeks of pregnancy, a small group of young people gathered in a reading room in Gainesville, Florida, to listen to a talk about how to induce your own \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  through pills \u8211\'20\'13 and how to support your friends going through abortions.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou don\u8217\'20\'19t have to take them alone,\u8221\'20\'1D one organizer, who gave her name as J, told the group of more than a dozen attendees. \u8220\'20\'1CWe are ultimately here to be establishing a community care network around \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  support.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 There was also another reason for the event: it was, in the words of another organizer, \u8220\'20\'1Ca big fuck you to Florida\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Although more than a dozen states, including Florida and all of the deep south, have implemented strict \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans in the wake of the fall of Roe v Wade, those bans target people who provide abortions, not women who undergo them. \u8220\'20\'1CSelf-managing\u8221\'20\'1D your own \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  using pills remains legally fraught, but experts widely believe that it is medically safe if the pills are used early enough in pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 Sitting on comfy chairs on a dais beneath a Powerpoint-style presentation, whose slides were frequently rendered in sepia tones and wreathed in floral imagery, J and another organizer, who gave their name as E, walked the rapt group through the steps of using \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills: how to find them online, what to expect, how to know if something\u8217\'20\'19s gone wrong. At least two attendees scribbled notes.\par \par \uc2 If you want to go to a hospital, E and J emphasized, you do not need to tell your medical provider that you had an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Instead, they said, just say you had a miscarriage.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COther people snitching on you is really a security risk,\u8221\'20\'1D said E, whose pronouns are they/them. \u8220\'20\'1CNurses and doctors are fucking snitches sometimes.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 For E and J, the fight for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and reproductive rights was nestled within a broader fight for bodily autonomy \u8211\'20\'13 one that, in their view, was inextricably intertwined with causes like prison abolition and the pro-Palestine movement. The pair peppered their talk with mentions of \u8220\'20\'1Ccomrades\u8221\'20\'1D and urged attendees to \u8220\'20\'1Cresist the state\u8221\'20\'1D. One slide celebrated the labor holiday of May Day, which coincidentally also fell on Wednesday, complete with an illustration of a molotov cocktail.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s May Day, we deserve access to care, we should fight for our and our comrades\u8217\'20\'19 bodily autonomy. And so we did it,\u8221\'20\'1D J said in an interview after the talk, with a giggle. \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m really glad that we had a space that reminded me of the ways that we can care for each other and build a better world, and how that is possible, because in a lot of ways it already exists.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The attendees grew increasingly interactive throughout the talk. When E and J asked the crowd for suggestions on how to best support people through abortions, people offered up the methods they had used for their friends or had been supported with through their own abortions. One attendee said they had helped a friend by being a \u8220\'20\'1Csilly little guy\u8221\'20\'1D during their \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . (Several people laughed.) Another person said that, after their \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , they tried to talk about it as much as possible.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMaking it normal and not as fucking weird is the only way I know how to help right now,\u8221\'20\'1D they said.\par \par \uc2 They had set up a table with a veritable buffet of reproductive health resources: multiple black-and-white zines with information about self-managed \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ; a zine titled Free Bleed: A Non-Gendered, Analog Period Tracker, which featured a calendar for people looking to track their periods without the use of apps; stacks of emergency contraceptive pills, pads and condoms.\par \par \uc2 On another table lay a framed poster that read: \u8220\'20\'1CBlessed are the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers.\u8221\'20\'1D Covered with flowers, bones and a candle, the table had the look of a shrine.\par \par \uc2 During the talk, nobody mentioned that, come November, Florida voters will have a chance to vote on a ballot measure to enshrine \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights into the state constitution. In an interview, though, E said that they had gathered signatures to get the measure on the ballot.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m pretty confident in our collective ability to get that passed,\u8221\'20\'1D E said. \u8220\'20\'1COnce the people have the opportunity to decide, it\u8217\'20\'19s pretty clear people don\u8217\'20\'19t like these bans.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 E had an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Florida before Roe fell. At the time, they were beyond six weeks of pregnancy; today, they wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t have been able to get that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in a Florida clinic.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI have deep empathy for everyone that is now affected, that finds out they\u8217\'20\'19re pregnant today and has to deal with the repercussions of the state criminalizing that for no reason, for arbitrary reasons,\u8221\'20\'1D they said. \u8220\'20\'1CWe don\u8217\'20\'19t need to have these bans or anything that are barriers to access to healthcare like this.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240502ek52001jp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
