\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 First Thing: Police move in on pro-Palestinian encampment at UCLA\b0\par\par\uc2 Jem Bartholomew \par \uc2 1,303 \uc2 words\par \uc2 2 May 2024\par 12:52 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 LAPD\uc2  action at \uc2 University of California, Los Angeles\uc2  marks latest flashpoint in mounting tensions on US college campuses. Plus, Arizona senate passes repeal of 1864 \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  banDon\u8217\'20\'19t already get First Thing in your inbox? Sign up here\par \par \uc2 Good morning.\par \par \uc2 Hundreds of law enforcement officers {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/may/01/university-protests-pro-palestinian-demonstrators-arrested-latest-news?page=with:block-66336c2a8f082a27705c925e#block-66336c2a8f082a27705c925e"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 breached a Gaza solidarity encampment}}}\uc2  at the \uc2 University of California, Los Angeles\uc2  campus on Thursday morning, removing barricades and threatening students with arrest.\par \par \uc2 LAPD\uc2  officers in tactical gear filed on to the UCLA campus around sunset on Wednesday and began to force their way into the encampment at about 3.1am PDT. They were met with about 300 to 500 protesters in the encampment \u8211\'20\'13 and another 2,000 people gathered outside the barricades in support \u8211\'20\'13 who shouted \u8220\'20\'1Cshame on you\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 It is the latest crackdown on pro-Palestinian protesters demanding universities divest from companies linked to Israel\u8217\'20\'19s war effort in Gaza, and comes amid ongoing fallout from events on Tuesday, when counter-demonstrators attacked the UCLA encampment.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile in Gaza, a senior \uc2 Hamas\uc2  official told AFP overnight that its response to a proposed truce deal brokered by Egypt and Qatar was \u8220\'20\'1Cnegative\u8221\'20\'1D, but that discussions were still taking place.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Where have the campus protests spread? As well as sweeping the US and resulting in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/may/02/where-are-the-us-college-campus-protests-and-what-is-happening"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 more than 1,300 arrests}}}\uc2  nationwide, encampments are now spreading internationally, with similar demonstrations in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/education/2024/may/01/uk-students-begin-new-wave-of-protests-against-gaza-war-after-us-arrests"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the UK}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/apr/30/paris-regional-leader-suspends-sciences-po-funding-over-gaza-protests"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 France}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/may/01/australian-university-students-gaza-encampment-pro-palestinian-camping-protests"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Australia}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 This is a developing story. Follow our {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/may/01/university-protests-pro-palestinian-demonstrators-arrested-latest-news"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 live coverage here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Arizona senate passes repeal of \u8216\'20\'18inhumane\u8217\'20\'19 near-total \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban from 1864\par \par \uc2 Arizona lawmakers have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/may/01/democrat-close-repeal-arizona-abortion-ban"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 repealed}}}\uc2  the state\u8217\'20\'19s 160-year-old statute banning nearly all abortions.\par \par \uc2 The 1864 law, which {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/09/arizona-supreme-court-abortion-decision"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 was reinstated}}}\uc2  by the state supreme court three weeks ago, has made \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  a central focus in the battleground state and galvanized Democrats seeking to enshrine \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 In the state senate, Democrats picked up the support of two Republicans in favor of repealing the ban. The Democratic governor, \uc2 Katie Hobbs\uc2 , is expected to ratify the repeal, which narrowly cleared the Arizona house last week after three Republicans joined with all the Democrats in the chamber.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 What were the details of the law? The civil-war era statute, which predates Arizona\u8217\'20\'19s statehood, bans nearly all abortions, including those sought by survivors of rape or incest. It also imposes prison terms for doctors and others who aid in abortions. The law had been blocked by the 1973 supreme court Roe v Wade decisions that granted the constitutional right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 What did pro-choice advocates say? \u8220\'20\'1CWe are relieved that lawmakers have finally repealed this inhumane \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban \u8211\'20\'13 something extremist politicians refused to do for far too long,\u8221\'20\'1D said Victoria L\u243\'00\'F3pez, the director of program and strategy for the ACLU of Arizona.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 What happens now? The repeal will not take effect until June or July, 90 days after the legislative session. Once the 1864 measure is stricken, a 2022 statute banning procedures after 15 weeks of pregnancy will supplant it as the state\u8217\'20\'19s ruling \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law.\par \par \uc2 Harvey Weinstein\uc2  faces New York retrial after 2020 rape conviction overturned\par \par \uc2 Harvey Weinstein\uc2  will be {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/may/01/harvey-weinstein-overturned-trial"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 retried in New York}}}\uc2 , the Manhattan district attorney\u8217\'20\'19s office said on Wednesday, a week after the state\u8217\'20\'19s highest court {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/apr/25/harvey-weinstein-rape-conviction-overturned"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 threw out}}}\uc2  his 2020 rape conviction.\par \par \uc2 The district attorney, \uc2 Alvin Bragg\uc2 , said via his office staff that his team was determined to retry the case against the disgraced movie mogul.\par \par \uc2 Legal experts say that may be a long road and may come down to whether the women he is accused of assaulting are willing to testify again. One of the women, Mimi Haley, said on Friday she was still considering whether she would testify at any retrial.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Why was the New York conviction overturned? Last week\u8217\'20\'19s ruling said the court \u8220\'20\'1Cerroneously admitted testimony of uncharged, alleged prior sexual acts against persons other than the complainants of the underlying crimes\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 What was Weinstein\u8217\'20\'19s prison term for this case? He got 23 years in 2020 for two sex crimes: forcing oral sex on a production assistant in 2006 as well as rape in the third degree of an actor in 2013. He was also convicted in LA in 2022 of another rape, and sentenced to 16 years in prison.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 What happens next? One of Weinstein\u8217\'20\'19s accusers was in court on Wednesday and asked the judge for an early fall retrial.\par \par \uc2 In other news \u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Police in Dublin, Ireland were sent in to dismantle about 200 tents of asylum seekers on Wednesday, which was labeled by critics as social {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/may/01/dublin-ireland-police-buses-dismantle-tent-city-asylum-seekers"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Ccleansing\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 At least 48 people died in south-eastern China after a highway section collapsed in a mountainous area on Thursday, sending more than 20 cars down a steep slope.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Colombia\u8217\'20\'19s president announced his government will sever diplomatic relations with Israel, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/may/01/colombia-sever-ties-israel-gaza-genocide"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 saying}}}\uc2  the country has \u8220\'20\'1Ca genocidal president\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Heavy rains and floods in Kenya\u8217\'20\'19s Maasai Mara national reserve saw scores of people evacuated, after over a dozen hotels, lodges and camps were {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/may/01/kenya-floods-tourists-evacuated-maasai-mara-river-bursts-banks"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 flooded}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Five civilians were killed in Ukraine on Wednesday as Russia struck the eastern Kharkiv and Donetsk regions. It came as the US imposed {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/may/02/ukraine-war-briefing-us-hits-china-with-sanctions-over-war-supplies-to-russia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 new sanctions}}}\uc2  on nearly 300 entities in Russia, China and other countries for supplying \u8220\'20\'1Ccritical inputs to Russia\u8217\'20\'19s military-industrial base\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Stat of the day: China accounts for nearly one-third of the world\u8217\'20\'19s 339 jailed writers with 107 in prison\par \par \uc2 The 2023 Freedom to Write Index shows at least {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/may/01/writers-jailed-china-pen-america"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 339 people are imprisoned globally}}}\uc2  for exercising freedom of expression. China put 107 people behind bars because of their published statements, more than any other country. Many have been arrested for \u8220\'20\'1Cpicking quarrels and provoking trouble\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Don\u8217\'20\'19t miss this: How the fiction of Brooklyn\u8217\'20\'19s bard Paul Auster captivated a generation\par \par \uc2 Like Saul Bellow\u8217\'20\'19s Chicago or Philip Roth\u8217\'20\'19s New Jersey, the American writer Paul Auster \u8211\'20\'13 who died this week aged 77 \u8211\'20\'13 will always be synonymous with Brooklyn, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/books/2024/may/01/brooklyns-bard-paul-austers-tricksy-fiction-captivated-a-generation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 writes Lisa Allardice}}}\uc2 . His writing had a postmodern playfulness, and his subjects were loss, grief and identity, with versions of himself (in various degrees of disguise) popping up in his fiction, along with references to 19th-century American writers, notebooks and baseball.\par \par \uc2 \u8230\'20\'26 or this: Daniel Radcliffe says rupture with JK Rowling over her trans views is \u8216\'20\'18really sad\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 The Harry Potter actor Daniel Radcliffe has described his falling out with JK Rowling as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/film/2024/may/01/daniel-radcliffe-says-rupture-with-jk-rowling-over-trans-rights-is-really-sad"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Creally sad\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2  because the wizarding world she created was \u8220\'20\'1Cso deeply empathic\u8221\'20\'1D. Radcliffe and co-stars \uc2 Emma Watson\uc2  and Rupert Grint have feuded with the author for years over her gender-critical statements on trans women. \u8220\'20\'1CI will continue to support the rights of all LGBTQ people,\u8221\'20\'1D Radcliffe said.\par \par \uc2 Climate check: Why are chimps dying of the virus that causes the common cold in humans?\par \par \uc2 Viruses that cause the common cold in humans are devastating populations of chimpanzees and gorillas. In some ape communities, it\u8217\'20\'19s a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2024/may/02/great-ape-tourism-chimpanzee-common-cold-reverse-zoonoses-uganda-aoe"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 bigger killer than habitat loss or poaching}}}\uc2 . A community of 205 animals in Uganda\u8217\'20\'19s Kibale national park were coughing and sneezing for weeks \u8211\'20\'13 with the outbreak causing more than 12% to die. Experts say ecotourism is a risk factor.\par \par \uc2 Last Thing: \u8216\'20\'18The whole town could come\u8217\'20\'19 \u8211\'20\'13 Reynolds and McElhenney plan for 55,000 Wrexham\u8217\'20\'19s stadium\par \par \uc2 Wrexham\u8217\'20\'19s Hollywood owners, \uc2 Rob McElhenney\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/film/ryan-reynolds"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ryan Reynolds}}}\uc2 , plan to develop the club\u8217\'20\'19s Racecourse Ground into a stadium with up to 55,000 seats. The town had a population of about {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/660448e991a320001a82b108/Wrexham.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 45,000}}}\uc2  in 2021. \u8220\'20\'1CThe whole town could come to a game,\u8221\'20\'1D Reynolds said.\par \par \uc2 Sign up\par \par \uc2 First Thing is delivered to thousands of inboxes every weekday. If you\u8217\'20\'19re not already signed up, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/info/2018/sep/17/guardian-us-morning-briefing-sign-up-to-stay-informed"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 subscribe now}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Get in touch\par \par \uc2 If you have any questions or comments about any of our newsletters please email {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:newsletters@theguardian.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 newsletters@theguardian.com}}}\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240502ek52001p5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
