\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Arizona senate passes bill to repeal 1864  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  ban; Harris says Trump\u8217\'20\'19s insistence he doesn\u8217\'20\'19t back national ban is \u8216\'20\'18gaslighting\u8217\'20\'19 \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Chris Stein (now) and Maya Yang (earlier) \par \uc2 7,674 \uc2 words\par \uc2 1 May 2024\par 20:46 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 This live blog is now closed. You can read our full story on Arizona\u8217\'20\'19s strict \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban here:Arizona senate passes repeal of 1864 near-total \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 Closing summary\par \par \uc2 A showdown is set to take place {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/may/01/speaker-mike-johnson-marjorie-taylor-greene-updates?page=with:block-663240e08f084fb5cf82ab4b#block-663240e08f084fb5cf82ab4b"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 next week}}}\uc2  between Republican House speaker Mike Johnson and far-right congresswoman \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene\uc2 , who is leading a charge to remove Johnson as the chamber\u8217\'20\'19s leader over his collaboration with Democrats. But, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/may/01/speaker-mike-johnson-marjorie-taylor-greene-updates?page=with:block-66322fe18f08df7ec2bda062#block-66322fe18f08df7ec2bda062"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 unlike the last time}}}\uc2  something like this happened, Democratic leaders say they will oppose Greene\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/may/01/speaker-mike-johnson-marjorie-taylor-greene-updates?page=with:block-66314e8d8f087e1780c9cdd7#block-66314e8d8f087e1780c9cdd7"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 motion to vacate}}}\uc2 , and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/may/01/speaker-mike-johnson-marjorie-taylor-greene-updates?page=with:block-66326ae58f084fb5cf82ae00#block-66326ae58f084fb5cf82ae00"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 there are already signs}}}\uc2  that rank-and-file lawmakers will follow along. As for Greene, she only has two other Republicans on board with her ouster attempt \u8211\'20\'13 not exactly resounding numbers. We\u8217\'20\'19ll see if anything changes in the days to come. Meanwhile, \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  traveled to Florida to tell voters in a state \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is hoping to win in November that \uc2 Donald Trump{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/may/01/speaker-mike-johnson-marjorie-taylor-greene-updates?page=with:block-66328adf8f08be140582cdec#block-66328adf8f08be140582cdec"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 is to blame}}}\uc2  for the strict \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban that went into effect today. And in swing state Arizona, the state senate {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/may/01/speaker-mike-johnson-marjorie-taylor-greene-updates?page=with:block-66329b8f8f08cb0a1ccaa723#block-66329b8f8f08cb0a1ccaa723"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 finally approved}}}\uc2  a repeal of its stringent law against \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  that dates back to the 19th century. The Democratic governor, \uc2 Katie Hobbs\uc2 , is expected to sign the bill.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else went on today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Florida Democrats have had a tough go of it in recent years, but they {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/may/01/speaker-mike-johnson-marjorie-taylor-greene-updates?page=with:block-663298688f084fb5cf82b03d#block-663298688f084fb5cf82b03d"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 hope}}}\uc2  a measure to expand \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access that will be on the ballot in November will turn their fortunes around.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Johnson issued a brief response to Greene\u8217\'20\'19s push to remove him as speaker, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/may/01/speaker-mike-johnson-marjorie-taylor-greene-updates?page=with:block-663249818f08be140582ca2a#block-663249818f08be140582ca2a"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 warning}}}\uc2  that it was \u8220\'20\'1Cwrong for the country\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The aftershocks from a violent night on college campuses continue to reverberate, with the \uc2 University of California, Los Angeles\uc2 , canceling classes following an attack by counter-protesters on a pro-Palestinian encampment. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/may/01/speaker-mike-johnson-marjorie-taylor-greene-updates?page=with:block-663259848f084fb5cf82aced#block-663259848f084fb5cf82aced"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Follow}}}\uc2  our live blog for more.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Louisiana{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/may/01/speaker-mike-johnson-marjorie-taylor-greene-updates?page=with:block-663261a88f084fb5cf82ad96#block-663261a88f084fb5cf82ad96"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 might not get}}}\uc2  another majority-Black congressional district after all, further complicating Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 hopes of retaking the House majority in November.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Biden{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/may/01/speaker-mike-johnson-marjorie-taylor-greene-updates?page=with:block-66327fea8f08cb0a1ccaa5c9#block-66327fea8f08cb0a1ccaa5c9"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ordered}}}\uc2  the cancellation of billions of dollars in debt accrued by students who attended a private college system accused of fraud.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.03pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.49pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Associated Press notes that voting in the senate on the bill to repeal Arizona\u8217\'20\'19s strict \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions is ongoing, but the legislation has the votes to pass, with the requisite two Republicans supporting it alongside 14 Democrats.\par \par \uc2 However, Arizona for \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  Access, a coalition of reproductive rights groups, warns that the fight to keep the procedure available is far from over:\par \par \uc2 enltrMUST READ! Our statement on today\u8217\'20\'19s Arizona Senate vote to repeal one extreme ban and revert to another. It\u8217\'20\'19s a repeal with no set date to take effect & nothing has changed about the need for the Arizona \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  Access Act. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/AZforaccess?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #AZforaccess}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/cNEmy4B5zI"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/cNEmy4B5zI}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Arizona for \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  Access (@azforaccess) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/azforaccess/status/1785749457029697695?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 1, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more on the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  battle in the south-west swing state that could prove crucial to \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s or \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s chances of winning the White House:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/may/01/democrat-close-repeal-arizona-abortion-ban"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Arizona Democrats to make final push to repeal near-total \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  ban}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.53pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.41pm BST\par \par \uc2 Arizona senate passes bill to repeal 19th century-era \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban\par \par \uc2 Arizona\u8217\'20\'19s state senate has passed legislation to repeal a ban on almost all abortions in the state that dates back to 1864, the Associated Press reports.\par \par \uc2 The measure, which the house approved last week, now goes to Democratic governor \uc2 Katie Hobbs\uc2 , who said she will sign it.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.32pm BST\par \par \uc2 Despite their struggles in Florida in recent years, Democrats hope the presence on the November ballot of a measure to broaden access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  could sway voters they will need to win the state for \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 . Last month, the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/richardluscombe"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Richard Luscombe}}}\uc2  took a close look at their plans:\par \par \uc2 Democrats in Florida are teaming up with operatives from \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s re-election campaign in an all-out assault on Republicans\u8217\'20\'19 extremist positions on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , believing it will bring victory in presidential and \uc2 US Senate\uc2  races in November.\par \par \uc2 They fired an opening salvo on Tuesday, tearing into \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cboasting\u8221\'20\'1D about overturning federal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  protections {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/08/trump-abortion-states"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a day earlier}}}\uc2 , and assailing the incumbent Republican senator \uc2 Rick Scott{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thehill.com/policy/healthcare/3949607-rick-scott-on-6-week-abortion-ban-if-i-was-still-governor-i-would-sign-this-bill/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 for supporting}}}\uc2  Florida\u8217\'20\'19s six-week ban that takes effect next month.\par \par \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , the Republican Florida governor and former candidate for the party\u8217\'20\'19s presidential nomination who {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/apr/13/florida-six-week-abortion-ban-republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 signed the ban into law}}}\uc2 , also found himself under fire.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe word is accountability,\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 Nikki Fried\uc2 , chair of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/florida"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Florida}}}\uc2  Democratic party, told an online launch meeting attended by Jasmine Burney-Clark, state director of the Biden-Harris campaign, and Democratic state representative \uc2 Anna Eskamani\uc2 , a former regional senior director of \uc2 Planned Parenthood\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe are here because \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  bragged about overturning Roe v Wade. Then we got here in Florida because we had an individual who wanted to run for president and wanted to take our state into extremism, the Republican legislature who voted for it, and \uc2 Rick Scott\uc2  \u8230\'20\'26 who said on the national stage he will push for a national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s incumbent on all of us, the party, the candidates, the campaigns, to make sure that we are making that very distinct link.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/10/florida-democrats-abortion-ban-elections"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Florida Democrats bet \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  will motivate swell of voters who feel bans go \u8216\'20\'18too far\u8217\'20\'19 }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.17pm BST\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s the moment when \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  warned Florida voters against believing \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s insistence that he would not support federal limits on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 :\par \par \uc2 enltr"Trump wants us to believe he will not sign a national [\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ] ban. Well, I say enough with the gaslighting."\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 VP \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  argues \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  recently calling \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  a states' issue can't be believed because he previously endorsed a federal 20-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/BSaU0QfDou"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/BSaU0QfDou}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1785747637930545244?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 1, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.01pm BST\par \par \uc2 As she closed out her speech, Harris compared and contrasted a second \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  term with four more years of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , and repeated the president\u8217\'20\'19s promise to sign legislation restoring the protections in Roe v Wade, should Congress approve it.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe great Maya Angelou once said, \u8216\'20\'18When someone tells you who they are, believe them the first time.\u8217\'20\'19 And \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has told us who he is. So here\u8217\'20\'19s what a second Trump term looks like: more bans, more suffering, less freedom,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBut we are not going to let that happen because you see, we trust women. We trust women to know what is in their own best interest. And women trust all of us to fight to protect their most fundamental freedom.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 No Democratic president has won Florida\u8217\'20\'19s electoral votes since \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  in 2012, and at the state level, the GOP controls the governor\u8217\'20\'19s mansion and the legislature. The state\u8217\'20\'19s Democrats have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jul/07/democrats-florida-comeback-ron-desantis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 generally struggled}}}\uc2  in recent years, though there have been {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/may/17/florida-jacksonville-mayor-donna-deegan-ron-desantis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 some signs}}}\uc2  of a comeback.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis November, up and down the ballot, reproductive freedom is on the ballot. And you, the leaders, you the people, have the power to protect it with your vote. \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  may think he can take Florida for granted. It is your power that will send \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and me back to the White House,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAnd when Congress passes the law that restores the reproductive freedoms of Roe, our president, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , will sign it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.04pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.51pm BST\par \par \uc2 'Enough with the gaslighting': Harris responds to Trump's insistence that he does not back national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  may say that he does not plan to push for a national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, but \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  told voters in Florida that they should not believe him.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAs much harm as he has already caused, a second Trump term would be even worse,\u8221\'20\'1D the vice-president said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s friends in the \uc2 United States Congress\uc2  are trying to pass a national ban and, understand, a national ban would outlaw \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in every single state, even in states like New York and California. And now Trump wants us to believe he will not sign a national ban. Well, I say enough with the gaslighting.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more on just what Trump has said about a national ban:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/08/trump-abortion-states"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump says each US state should determine different \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  laws}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.02pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.47pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/08/trump-abortion-states"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 recently said}}}\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy should be left to the states, and declined to endorse a national ban on the procedure that some Republicans have called for.\par \par \uc2 Harris took him to task: \u8220\'20\'1CTrump says he wants to leave \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  up to the states, he says, up to the states. All right. So here\u8217\'20\'19s how that works out. Today, one in three women of reproductive age live in a state with a Trump \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban \u8211\'20\'13 many with no exception for rape or incest.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 She then explained why she cared so much about this issue, relating a story from when she was growing up:\par \par \uc2 As many of you know, I started my career as a prosecutor specializing in crimes against women and children. What many of you may not know is why? So, when I was in high school I learned that my best friend was being molested by her stepfather. And I said to her, well, you\u8217\'20\'19ve got to come and live with us. I call my mother. And my mother said of course she does. And so she did.\par \par \uc2 So, the idea that someone who survives a crime of violence to their body of violation of their body would not have the authority to make a decision about what happens to their body next. That\u8217\'20\'19s immoral. That\u8217\'20\'19s immoral.\par \par \uc2 And one does not have to abandon their faith or deeply held beliefs to agree the government should not be telling her what to do.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.49pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.39pm BST\par \par \uc2 Harris assails 'Trump \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban' in Florida\par \par \uc2 Harris then pivoted to the meat of her argument to Florida voters: that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  was to blame for the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban that just went into effect in the state, as well as others like it nationwide.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAcross our nation, we witnessed a full on assault, state by state, on reproductive freedom, and understand who is to blame: former president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  did this,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  hand-picked three members of the United States supreme court because he intended for them to overturn Roe, and as he intended, they did.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Harris harkened back to her {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2020/oct/14/amy-coney-barrett-supreme-court-open-mind"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 grilling}}}\uc2 , as a senator on the judiciary committee, of two of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s supreme court nominees, saying it was clear after their confirmation that the days of nationwide \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access were numbered:\par \par \uc2 And it happened just as \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  intended. Now, present day because of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , more than 20 states have \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans, more than 20 Trump \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans. And today, this very day at the stroke of midnight, another Trump \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban went into effect here in Florida. As of this morning, four million women in this state woke up with fewer reproductive freedoms than they had last night. This is the new reality under a Trump \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.43pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.32pm BST\par \par \uc2 Harris calls push for reproductive rights 'a fight for freedom' in Florida speech\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  has taken the stage in Jacksonville, Florida, where she likened \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access to a \u8220\'20\'1Cfundamental freedom\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is a fight for freedom, the fundamental freedom to make decisions about one\u8217\'20\'19s own body and not have their government tell them what they\u8217\'20\'19re supposed to do,\u8221\'20\'1D the vice-president said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAs we know, almost two years ago, the highest court in our land, the court of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/2017/oct/08/thurgood-marshall-film-biopic-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Thurgood}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/18/abortion-rights-campaigner-anniversary-rbg-death"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 RBG}}}\uc2 , took a constitutional right that had been recognized from the people of America, from the women of America. And now, in states across our nation, extremists have proposed and passed laws that criminalize doctors, punish women \u8211\'20\'13 laws that threatened doctors and nurses with prison time, even for life, simply for providing reproductive care.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.28pm BST\par \par \uc2 Florida\u8217\'20\'19s six-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban doesn\u8217\'20\'19t just mark the end of most patients\u8217\'20\'19 access to the procedure in the state, but also in the rest of the south-eastern United States. \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/carter-sherman"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Carter Sherman}}}\uc2  reported from a clinic trying to squeeze in appointments before it went into effect about how reproductive health access in Florida was about to change:\par \par \uc2 A six-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban went into effect on Wednesday in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/florida"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Florida}}}\uc2 , cutting off access to the procedure before many people know they are pregnant and leveling the south-eastern United States\u8217\'20\'19 last stronghold for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 The ban went into force weeks after Florida\u8217\'20\'19s state supreme court issued a decision clearing the way for it to take effect. Strict bans now {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2023/nov/10/state-abortion-laws-us#:~:text=Since%20Roe%20was%20overturned%20in,referendums%20to%20protect%20abortion%20rights."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 blanket all of the American deep south}}}\uc2 , increasing the strain on the country\u8217\'20\'19s remaining clinics. The closest clinic for most Floridians past six weeks of pregnancy is now several states away in North Carolina, which outlaws \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after 12 weeks of pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 Last year, Florida \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers performed more than 84,000 abortions, state data found \u8211\'20\'13 including more than 9,000 for out-of-state patients, according to the \uc2 Guttmacher Institute\uc2 , which tracks \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions. Roughly 60 % of Florida abortions {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tampabay.com/news/florida-politics/2024/04/04/florida-abortion-six-week-ban-pregnancy-planned-parenthood/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 occur after six weeks of pregnancy}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 On Tuesday, the last day before the ban took effect, an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinic in Gainesville, Florida, was trying to squeeze in as many patients as possible. The clinic had added hours throughout April, but the rush was compounded by the fact that, in addition to the impending ban, Florida requires people to have an in-person consultation at an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinic at least 24 hours before they get the procedure or take \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills. A patient could have arrived on Tuesday exactly six weeks into her pregnancy, but have been too late to get an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  given that the ban came into effect on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/may/01/florida-six-week-abortion-ban-takes-effect"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Florida\u8217\'20\'19s six-week \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  ban takes effect, ending access in south-east US}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.34pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.14pm BST\par \par \uc2 Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s Republican representative \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene\uc2  is doubling down on her attempts to oust House speaker Mike Johnson.\par \par \uc2 In an address today, Greene said:\par \par \uc2 We have to have a Republican majority in January and under Mike Johnson\u8217\'20\'19s leadership, we\u8217\'20\'19re not going to have one \u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 Hakeem Jeffries\uc2  has endorsed Mike Johnson because he knows Mike Johnson\u8217\'20\'19s leadership is going to hand the House majority to Democrats in January. It will make our voters not vote for him \u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 enltrHakeem Jeffries has endorsed Mike Johnson because he knows Mike Johnson\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cleadership\u8221\'20\'1D is going to hand the House majority to Democrats in January. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/YGO5U6FrkM"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/YGO5U6FrkM}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Rep. \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene\uc2 ???? (@RepMTG) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RepMTG/status/1785712922729001436?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 1, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.21pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.51pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has announced the approval of $6.1b n in student debt cancellation for 317,000 borrowers who attended the Art Institutes, a private college system that was closed last year amid fraud claims.\par \par \uc2 In a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.whitehouse.gov/briefing-room/statements-releases/2024/05/01/statement-from-president-joe-biden-on-6-1-billion-in-student-debt-cancellation-for-317000-borrowers-who-attended-the-art-institutes/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 statement}}}\uc2  released on Wednesday, Biden said:\par \par \uc2 This institution falsified data, knowingly misled students, and cheated borrowers into taking on mountains of debt without leading to promising career prospects at the end of their studies \u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 While my predecessor looked the other way when colleges defrauded students and borrowers, I promised to take this on directly to provide borrowers with the relief they need and deserve \u8230\'20\'26 And in total, we have approved debt cancellation for nearly 4.6 million Americans through various actions.\par \par \uc2 Today\u8217\'20\'19s announcement builds on all we\u8217\'20\'19ve done to fix broken student loan programs and bring higher education more in reach.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.56pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.29pm BST\par \par \uc2 Arizona Democrats are expected to make a final push to repeal the state\u8217\'20\'19s near-total \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, which dates back to 1864.\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2  and agencies report:\par \par \uc2 Fourteen Democrats in the state senate are hoping to pick up at least two Republican votes to win final approval for a bill repealing the ban, which narrowly {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/24/arizona-repeal-abortion-ban-democrats"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 cleared the Arizona house}}}\uc2  last week and is expected to be signed by the Democratic governor.\par \par \uc2 The near-total ban, which predates Arizona\u8217\'20\'19s statehood, permits abortions only to save the patient\u8217\'20\'19s life \u8211\'20\'13 and provides no exceptions for survivors of rape or incest. The law had been on the books since 1864, but had been blocked since the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s 1973 Roe v Wade decision guaranteed the constitutional right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  nationwide.\par \par \uc2 In a ruling last month, however, the Arizona supreme court suggested that following the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s decision last year to overturn Roe v Wade, doctors could be prosecuted under the civil war-era law. Under the law, anyone who assists in an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  can be sentenced to two to five years in prison.\par \par \uc2 Read the full story here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/may/01/democrat-close-repeal-arizona-abortion-ban"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Arizona Democrats to make final push to repeal near-total \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  ban}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.56pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.12pm BST\par \par \uc2 The day so far\par \par \uc2 A showdown is set to take place {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/may/01/speaker-mike-johnson-marjorie-taylor-greene-updates?page=with:block-663240e08f084fb5cf82ab4b#block-663240e08f084fb5cf82ab4b"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 next week}}}\uc2  between Republican House speaker Mike Johnson and far-right congresswoman \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene\uc2 , who is leading a charge to remove him as the chamber\u8217\'20\'19s leader over his collaboration with Democrats. But, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/may/01/speaker-mike-johnson-marjorie-taylor-greene-updates?page=with:block-66322fe18f08df7ec2bda062#block-66322fe18f08df7ec2bda062"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 unlike the last time}}}\uc2  something like this happened, Democratic leaders say they will oppose Greene\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/may/01/speaker-mike-johnson-marjorie-taylor-greene-updates?page=with:block-66314e8d8f087e1780c9cdd7#block-66314e8d8f087e1780c9cdd7"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 motion to vacate}}}\uc2 , and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/may/01/speaker-mike-johnson-marjorie-taylor-greene-updates?page=with:block-66326ae58f084fb5cf82ae00#block-66326ae58f084fb5cf82ae00"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 there are already signs}}}\uc2  that rank-and-file lawmakers will follow along. As for Greene, she only has two others on board with her ouster attempt \u8211\'20\'13 not exactly resounding numbers. We\u8217\'20\'19ll see if anything changes in the days to come. Meanwhile, \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/may/01/speaker-mike-johnson-marjorie-taylor-greene-updates?page=with:block-66326df68f08cb0a1ccaa4de#block-66326df68f08cb0a1ccaa4de"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 set to speak}}}\uc2  at 2.45pm in Jacksonville, Florida, and blame \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  for the state\u8217\'20\'19s strict \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, which went into effect today. We plan to cover that live.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else has happened today so far:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Johnson issued a brief response to Greene\u8217\'20\'19s push to remove him as speaker, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/may/01/speaker-mike-johnson-marjorie-taylor-greene-updates?page=with:block-663249818f08be140582ca2a#block-663249818f08be140582ca2a"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 warning}}}\uc2  that it was \u8220\'20\'1Cwrong for the country\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The aftershocks from a violent night on college campuses continue to reverberate, with the \uc2 University of California, Los Angeles\uc2 , canceling classes following an attack by counter-protesters on a pro-Palestinian encampment. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/may/01/speaker-mike-johnson-marjorie-taylor-greene-updates?page=with:block-663259848f084fb5cf82aced#block-663259848f084fb5cf82aced"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Follow}}}\uc2  our live blog for more.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Louisiana{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/may/01/speaker-mike-johnson-marjorie-taylor-greene-updates?page=with:block-663261a88f084fb5cf82ad96#block-663261a88f084fb5cf82ad96"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 might not get}}}\uc2  another majority-Black congressional district after all, further complicating Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 hopes of retaking the House majority in November.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.18pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.54pm BST\par \par \uc2 'There is one person responsible for this nightmare: \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 ,' Biden says as Florida \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban takes effect\par \par \uc2 Earlier this morning, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  hammered \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  as Florida\u8217\'20\'19s strict \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban went into effect, saying the former president \u8220\'20\'1Cripped away the rights and freedom of women in America\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere is one person responsible for this nightmare: \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . Trump brags about overturning Roe v Wade, making extreme bans like Florida\u8217\'20\'19s possible, saying his plan is working \u8216\'20\'18brilliantly\u8217\'20\'19. He thinks it\u8217\'20\'19s brilliant that more than 4 million women in Florida, and more than one in three women in America, can\u8217\'20\'19t get access to the care they need,\u8221\'20\'1D the president said in a statement released through his re-election campaign.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTrump is worried the voters will hold him accountable for the cruelty and chaos he created. He\u8217\'20\'19s right. Trump ripped away the rights and freedom of women in America. This November, voters are going to teach him a valuable lesson: don\u8217\'20\'19t mess with the women of America.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.07pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.40pm BST\par \par \uc2 Harris in Florida to castigate Trump as state's strict \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban goes into effect\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is traveling to Florida this afternoon to train voters\u8217\'20\'19 ire on \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  as the state\u8217\'20\'19s ban on abortions after six weeks of pregnancy goes into effect.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CToday at the stroke of midnight, another Trump \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban went into effect here in Florida,\u8221\'20\'1D the vice-president will say in a speech in Jacksonville.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis ban applies to many women before they even know they are pregnant \u8211\'20\'13 which tells us the extremists who wrote this ban don\u8217\'20\'19t even know how a woman\u8217\'20\'19s body works. Or they just don\u8217\'20\'19t care.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s re-election campaign hopes to benefit from voters\u8217\'20\'19 concerns over \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans, which the supreme court made possible with its 2022 ruling overturning Roe v Wade. Trump appointed three of the five conservative justices who signed onto that decision.\par \par \uc2 Florida was once considered a swing state, but Democrats have struggled there in recent years, and the state voted for Trump in past two presidential elections. The Biden campaign says it hopes to win Florida again, aided by a measure set to be on the November ballot that would protect access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  up to around 24 weeks of pregnancy, and when necessary to protect a woman\u8217\'20\'19s health. Here\u8217\'20\'19s more on that:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/01/florida-abortion-right-constitution-vote-november-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Florida supreme court clears way for both \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  ballot measure and six-week ban}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.22pm BST\par \par \uc2 Signs emerge rank-and-file Democrats will not support Greene\u8217\'20\'19s ouster attempt at Johnson\par \par \uc2 The top three Democratic lawmakers in the House, including minority leader \uc2 Hakeem Jeffries\uc2 , say they will not support far-right congresswoman \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s effort to boot her fellow Republican, Mike Johnson, from the speaker\u8217\'20\'19s post.\par \par \uc2 The next question is whether other Democrats will go along with them. Leadership\u8217\'20\'19s position can be influential on lawmakers, but it\u8217\'20\'19s ultimately up to each member of Congress to decide. In the days to come, we can expect to hear from various House representatives about where they fall on this issue.\par \par \uc2 Fox News reports that \uc2 Jamaal Bowman\uc2 , a progressive Democrat from New York, says he is no fan of Johnson, but nonetheless plans to reject Greene\u8217\'20\'19s motion to vacate when it comes up for a vote:\par \par \uc2 enltrA) From colleague Ryan Schmelz. Dem NY Rep Bowman on Greene's effort to throw out Johnson: I think, Leader Jeffries decision to table as it relates to stabilizing the chamber and the institution is very important because at some point, we need to get back to governing.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Chad Pergram (@ChadPergram) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ChadPergram/status/1785692305984225566?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 1, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrB) Bowman: Speaker Johnson, he's dangerous. He's an election denier, he\u8217\'20\'19s a fundamentalists, and he's not the leadership this country needs...but I\u8217\'20\'19m going to be in alignment with Leader Jeffries\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Chad Pergram (@ChadPergram) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ChadPergram/status/1785692307523527162?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 1, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.40pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more from the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/joan-greve"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Joan E Greve}}}\uc2  on far-right congresswoman \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s vow earlier this morning to force a vote next week on removing Mike Johnson as House speaker. As things stand right now, it does not seem to have the support to succeed:\par \par \uc2 Congresswoman {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/marjorie-taylor-greene"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene}}}\uc2  announced on Wednesday that she would move to force a vote next week on removing her fellow Republican Mike Johnson as House speaker, even though the measure appears certain to fail.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI think the American people need to see a recorded vote,\u8221\'20\'1D Greene said at a press conference. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd so next week, I am going to be calling this motion to vacate \u8211\'20\'13 absolutely calling it. I can\u8217\'20\'19t wait to see Democrats go out and support a Republican speaker and have to go home to their primaries and have to run for Congress again.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The news came one day after House Democratic leaders {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/30/marjorie-taylor-greene-mike-johnson-democrats"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 issued}}}\uc2  a statement indicating they would vote to table, or kill, Greene\u8217\'20\'19s motion to vacate if it came up for a vote. In the statement, Democratic leaders cited Johnson\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/20/us-house-approves-61bn-aid-ukraine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 successful effort}}}\uc2  to shepherd a foreign aid package through the House last month to justify blocking Greene\u8217\'20\'19s motion.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAt this moment, upon completion of our national security work, the time has come to turn the page on this chapter of pro-Putin Republican obstruction,\u8221\'20\'1D the leaders said. \u8220\'20\'1CWe will vote to table \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s motion to vacate the chair. If she invokes the motion, it will not succeed.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/may/01/marjorie-taylor-greene-oust-mike-johnson-speaker-vote"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene to force vote on ousting Mike Johnson as speaker}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.41pm BST\par \par \uc2 Control of the House will also be up for grabs in the November election, and a crucial aspect in determining which party has the advantage is how congressional district lines are drawn at the state level. Under a judge\u8217\'20\'19s ruling, Louisiana was set to get a second Black-majority district, likely giving Democrats the advantage, but the Associated Press reports an appeals court has just forbidden that map from going into effect:\par \par \uc2 A new congressional map giving {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/louisiana"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Louisiana}}}\uc2  a second majority-Black House district was rejected on Tuesday by a panel of three federal judges, fueling new uncertainty about district boundaries as the state prepares for fall congressional elections.\par \par \uc2 The 2-1 ruling forbids the use of a map drawn up in January by the legislature after a different federal judge blocked a map from 2022. The earlier map maintained a single Black-majority district and five mostly white districts, in a state with a population that is about one-third Black.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe will of course be seeking supreme court review,\u8221\'20\'1D the state attorney general, Liz Murrill, said on social media. \u8220\'20\'1CThe jurisprudence and litigation involving redistricting has made it impossible to not have federal judges drawing maps. It\u8217\'20\'19s not right and they need to fix it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The governor, \uc2 Jeff Landry\uc2 , and Murrill had backed the new map in a January legislative session after a different federal judge threw out a map with only one mostly Black district.\par \par \uc2 The National Democratic Redistricting Committee, chaired by former attorney general \uc2 Eric Holder\uc2 , said backers of the new map will probably seek an emergency order from the supreme court to keep the new map in place while appeals are pursued.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/may/01/louisiana-congressional-map-rejected"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  US judges reject new Louisiana voting map with second majority-Black district}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.23pm BST\par \par \uc2 The nationwide protests at college campuses were sparked by Israel\u8217\'20\'19s invasion of Gaza in response to \uc2 Hamas\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s 7 October attack. But as the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/adam-gabbatt"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Adam Gabbatt}}}\uc2  reports, all signs point to them emerging as significant issue for \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  as he pursues re-election in November:\par \par \uc2 The policies of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/democrats"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Democrats}}}\uc2  towards Israel, which have prompted thousands of students across the country to protest, could affect the youth vote for Biden and hurt his re-election chances, experts have warned, in what is already expected to be a tight election.\par \par \uc2 Thousands of students at universities across the US have joined with pro-Palestine rallies and, most recently, encampments, as Israel\u8217\'20\'19s war in Gaza has killed more than 34,000 people.\par \par \uc2 Some of the protests began as a call to encourage universities to ditch investments in companies that provide weapons and equipment to the Israeli military. But as the Biden administration has continued to largely support Israel, the president has increasingly become a focus of criticism from young people. Polling shows that young Americans\u8217\'20\'19 support for Biden has been chipped away since 2020.\par \par \uc2 With Biden narrowly trailing Trump in several key swing states, it\u8217\'20\'19s a voting bloc the president can ill afford to lose.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe real threat to Biden is that younger voters, especially college-educated voters, won\u8217\'20\'19t turn out for him in the election,\u8221\'20\'1D said Jonathan Zimmerman, a professor of history of education at the \uc2 University of Pennsylvania\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t expect that the protesters on campuses today are going to vote for Trump, almost none of them will. That\u8217\'20\'19s not the danger here. The danger is much simpler: that they simply won\u8217\'20\'19t vote.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/may/01/university-protests-presidential-election-biden-youth-vote"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 What do the US campus protests mean for Joe Biden in November?}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.04pm BST\par \par \uc2 In addition to the police\u8217\'20\'19s dispersal of protesters at \uc2 Columbia University\uc2 , yesterday saw violent clashes break out at the \uc2 University of California, Los Angeles\uc2 , involving pro-Israel counter protesters.\par \par \uc2 We have a separate live blog following the latest in the demonstrations, which you can read here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/may/01/columbia-university-protest-live-updates-nypd-new-york-police-enter-campus-pro-palestinian-demonstrators-latest-news"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Rival protest groups violently clash at UCLA; police arrest dozens at Columbia University - live}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.07pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 Police moved in yesterday evening to clear a \uc2 Columbia University\uc2  building that had been taken over by protesters, making dozens of arrests. Here\u8217\'20\'19s what happened at the college that has become a flashpoint for the nationwide wave of protests against Israel, from the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/diana-ramirez-simon"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Diana Ramirez-Simon}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/jonathan-yerushalmy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Jonathan Yerushalmy}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/edwardhelmore"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Edward Helmore}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/erum-salam"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Erum Salam}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 Dozens of students have been arrested after hundreds of New York City police officers entered \uc2 Columbia University\uc2  on Tuesday night to clear out an academic building that had been taken over as part of a pro-Palestinian protest.\par \par \uc2 Live video images showed police in riot gear marching on the campus in upper Manhattan, the focal point of nationwide student protests opposing Israel\u8217\'20\'19s war in Gaza. Police used an armoured vehicle with a bridging mechanism to gain entry to the second floor of the building.\par \par \uc2 Officers said they used flash-bangs to disperse the crowd, but denied using teargas as part of the operation.\par \par \uc2 Before long, officers were seen leading protesters handcuffed with zip ties to a line of police buses waiting outside campus gates. An \uc2 NYPD\uc2  spokesman, Carlos Nieves, said he had no immediate reports of any injuries following the arrests.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/30/new-york-police-columbia-university-student-protests"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Dozens arrested at Columbia University as New York police disperse Gaza protest }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.30pm BST\par \par \uc2 Punchbowl News reports that the House oversight committee will be paying a visit to \uc2 George Washington University in Washington\uc2  DC to see the encampment set up by pro-Palestinian protesters:\par \par \uc2 enltrNEW from me and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/maxpcohen?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @maxpcohen}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 Members of the House Oversight Committee will be heading to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/GWtweets?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @GWtweets}}}\uc2  this afternoon to view the encampment there.\par \par \uc2 COMER\uc2  signaled he'll probe why MPD has not cleared the encampment, as GW has requested.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Jake Sherman (@JakeSherman) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JakeSherman/status/1785674478413811950?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 1, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 The visit by the GOP-led committee, which has spent much of the past nearly year and a half investigating the Biden administration, comes as Republicans turn up the heat on administrators of universities where protests against Israel\u8217\'20\'19s invasion of Gaza are taking place.\par \par \uc2 Just a few minutes ago, \uc2 Elise Stefanik\uc2 , a New York Republican who is a high-ranking member of House leadership, called on the trustees of \uc2 Columbia University\uc2 , one of the campuses at the center of the protest wave, to remove Minouche Shafik as president, citing the recent storming of a university property by demonstrators:\par \par \uc2 This violence is a direct result of the appeasement policies president Minouche Shafik has used to address antisemitism on campus. President Shafik has allowed campus to be taken by mob rule, and she must immediately be removed so this occupation can be met with swift and overwhelming response to retake campus, restore order and protect Jewish students.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.42pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.10pm BST\par \par \uc2 How does the speaker of the House lose his job?\par \par \uc2 The mechanism in the House of Representatives to remove the speaker from his leadership post is called the motion to vacate.\par \par \uc2 The chamber\u8217\'20\'19s current rules allow any one member, Democrat or Republican, to introduce the motion. If it is introduced as a \u8220\'20\'1Cprivileged\u8221\'20\'1D resolution, the House must consider it at some point, although it could be delayed with procedural votes.\par \par \uc2 It only needs a simple majority to pass.\par \par \uc2 The procedure was last used to remove Johnson\u8217\'20\'19s predecessor Kevin McCarthy just six months ago \u8211\'20\'13 the only time in US history a House speaker has been ousted.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.13pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.55pm BST\par \par \uc2 Johnson says ouster attempt 'wrong for the country'\par \par \uc2 In a brief statement released shortly after Republican representatives \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene\uc2  and \uc2 Thomas Massie\uc2  finished their press conference in which they announced they would attempt to remove Mike Johnson from his leadership post next week, the speaker issued a brief statement about their plans:\par \par \uc2 This motion is wrong for the Republican Conference, wrong for the institution, and wrong for the country.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.38pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.54pm BST\par \par \uc2 Greene wrapped up the press conference by demanding, essentially, that Mike Johnson resign or be fired:\par \par \uc2 What I\u8217\'20\'19m calling on is, like my colleague here said, Mike Johnson \u8230\'20\'26 can pray about it, think about it all weekend, do the right thing and resign, giving our conference time to elect a new leader, a new speaker of the house. He should reject the endorsement of \uc2 Hakeem Jeffries\uc2  and the entire Democrat leadership team. That is not an endorsement that any Republican speaker should ever want or embrace. And this vote will be called next week, and I would just want to urge all our colleagues to prepare for it. It\u8217\'20\'19s the right thing to do for America. It\u8217\'20\'19s time to clean house and get our conference in order and get ready to support President Trump\u8217\'20\'19s agenda. God willing, he wins in November and we take back full power here in Washington in January.\par \par \uc2 The problem Greene faces is she does not have appear to have the votes to boot Johnson from the speaker\u8217\'20\'19s chair. Besides herself and \uc2 Thomas Massie\uc2 , the only other lawmaker publicly supporting the ouster attempt is Arizona\u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 Paul Gosar\uc2 , who was not at the press conference. Asked by a reporter about his absence, Greene said Gosar supports the effort but \u8220\'20\'1Che had another thing he had to attend to\u8221\'20\'1D, without elaborating.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.31pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.47pm BST\par \par \uc2 Greene has cast herself as a devoted acolyte of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 But Trump has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/23/trump-mike-johnson-ukraine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 spoken highly}}}\uc2  of Mike Johnson, even after Greene announced her push to remove him from office. A reporter asked Greene why she is continuing with her campaign against Johnson, given that the former president appears to support him. \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m the biggest supporter of President Trump and that\u8217\'20\'19s why I proudly wear this Maga hat,\u8221\'20\'1D the congresswoman replied as she donned the distinctive red cap.\par \par \uc2 Greene continued:\par \par \uc2 I fight for his agenda every single day, and that\u8217\'20\'19s why I\u8217\'20\'19m fighting here against my own Republican conference, to fight harder against the Democrats.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 A reporter asked Greene why she wanted to wait until next week to vote on the motion to vacate.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C Everybody needs the weekend to prepare,\u8221\'20\'1D Greene replied. \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m not irresponsible. I care about my conference. I have been measured, I have given this time. I have given warning after warning after warning. And that\u8217\'20\'19s why we don\u8217\'20\'19t have to rush. We can do it next week.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Massie chimed in, \u8220\'20\'1CI think this is a somber decision for Mike Johnson. He deserves a weekend to think about it. He should resign because he knows what\u8217\'20\'19s coming next week.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He added:\par \par \uc2 I\u8217\'20\'19m actually not going to concede that the vote will fail.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.32pm BST\par \par \uc2 Greene then yielded to \uc2 Thomas Massie\uc2 , one of two fellow Republicans publicly supporting her effort.\par \par \uc2 The Kentucky lawmaker elaborated on why they will press on with their effort to remove Mike Johnson, despite Democratic leaders\u8217\'20\'19 intervention to protect his job, and an apparent lack of enthusiasm among the GOP:\par \par \uc2 Now, you may say \u8230\'20\'26 congressman Massie, \uc2 Hakeem Jeffries\uc2  just told you, he\u8217\'20\'19s gonna save Mike Johnson\u8217\'20\'19s bacon. So why go through with it? It\u8217\'20\'19s a futile exercise \u8230\'20\'26 Why would you go through with this? Look, we didn\u8217\'20\'19t get elected to make excuses. We didn\u8217\'20\'19t get elected to say we shouldn\u8217\'20\'19t even try. We got elected to come here and give it our best and also to impose transparency. What we\u8217\'20\'19ve seen here is the coming out of the uniparty, and it will be consolidated and it will be transparent and apparent next week to all Americans when this vote happens. Too many of our colleagues have thrown up their hands in frustration and apathy. \u8216\'20\'18Oh, we shouldn\u8217\'20\'19t even try. Let\u8217\'20\'19s just coast this one out\u8217\'20\'19. I tell you what, it\u8217\'20\'19s too dangerous to coast this one out. We cannot coast this one out. \uc2 Hakeem Jeffries\uc2  knows if we coast this one out, we lose the majority.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.26pm BST\par \par \uc2 Greene said she thought voting on the motion to remove Johnson, which at this point does not appear to have enough support to succeed, would help Republicans maintain their slim majority in the House after the November elections:\par \par \uc2 I\u8217\'20\'19m gonna tell you, at over $34tn in debt, with millions and millions of people invading our country and an economy that I don\u8217\'20\'19t even know how is staying afloat because every business owner I know has been suffering, and people fed up with the drama on television and fed up with the fighting and fed up with the bullshit from Washington DC, are ready for a Republican majority that\u8217\'20\'19s ready to support President Trump and his agenda in January of 2025. And I\u8217\'20\'19m happy to deliver that vote for everyone next week.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.34pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.21pm BST\par \par \uc2 Greene says she'll demand vote on removing Johnson next week\par \par \uc2 After a lengthy denunciation of Mike Johnson, Majorie Taylor Greene said she will call for a vote on her motion to remove him as speaker of the House next week.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNext week, I am going to be calling this motion to vacate, absolutely calling it,\u8221\'20\'1D Greene said.\par \par \uc2 She indicated she thought the vote would hurt vulnerable Democrats:\par \par \uc2 I can\u8217\'20\'19t wait to see Democrats go out and support a Republican speaker, and have to go home to their primaries and have to run for Congress again, having supported our Republican speaker, a Christian conservative, I think that\u8217\'20\'19ll play well. I\u8217\'20\'19m excited about it.\par \par \uc2 And also be a pain for Republicans she disagrees with:\par \par \uc2 [I] also can\u8217\'20\'19t wait to see my Republican conference show their cards and show who we are. Because voters deserve it. Is the Republican party \u8230\'20\'26 have they finally learned their lesson? Have they finally heard the message from voters back at home? Are they willing to actually fight? Are they going to just keep going along to get along? Because it\u8217\'20\'19s really easy to do that in Washington DC.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.27pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.17pm BST\par \par \uc2 Greene recounted how she went from supporting Mike Johnson as speaker to threatening to remove him from office.\par \par \uc2 She blamed Johnson for the passage of a March government funding bill that \u8220\'20\'1Cfully funded \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s agenda\u8221\'20\'1D:\par \par \uc2 So, I entered a motion to vacate but I didn\u8217\'20\'19t call it for a vote. I was controlled. I was responsible. I was being conscious and caring about my conference in our majority. It was a warning to stop serving the Democrats. And support our Republican conference and support our agenda. And he didn\u8217\'20\'19t do it.\par \par \uc2 She then railed against Johnson for allowing a vote on the foreign aid package for Israel, Ukraine and Taiwan:\par \par \uc2 What\u8217\'20\'19s when Mike Johnson fully joined the disgusting business model of Washington DC, to fund forever wars. Yeah, that\u8217\'20\'19s what this is. The uniparty is make \u8216\'20\'18Ukraine great again\u8217\'20\'19. The uniparty is all about funding every single foreign war. They think this is the business model that needs to be done \u8230\'20\'26 Americans do not want to spend their hard-earned tax dollars to fund the murder and killing in foreign countries. They\u8217\'20\'19re fed up with it, and they\u8217\'20\'19re screaming it as loud as they possibly can.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.09pm BST\par \par \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene\uc2  has begun her press conference outside the US Capitol, where she is expected to announce whether she will press on with her campaign to remove fellow Republican Mike Johnson as speaker of the House.\par \par \uc2 She started off by reminding everyone of her affinity for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 I was one of the Americans in 2016 that looked at a presidential stage of 17 Republican candidates, and the only one that stood out to me was \uc2 Donald John Trump\uc2 . The very man that stood out and represented Republican voters and Americans all over the country, that we\u8217\'20\'19re sick and tired of a Republican establishment failing us over and over again. That\u8217\'20\'19s why I supported him in 2016, that\u8217\'20\'19s why I supported him in 2020, and that\u8217\'20\'19s why I support him now.\par \par \uc2 To make her point that the speaker is insufficiently loyal, the Georgia lawmaker spoke before photos of Johnson with \uc2 Hakeem Jeffries\uc2 , the Democratic House minority leader.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.13pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.55pm BST\par \par \uc2 Far-right lawmakers accuse Johnson of belonging to 'uniparty'\par \par \uc2 In the below tweet, \uc2 Thomas Massie\uc2 , one of two other House representatives known to be backing \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s motion to vacate, accuses speaker Mike Johnson of belonging to the \u8220\'20\'1Cuniparty\u8221\'20\'1D:\par \par \uc2 enltr. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RepMTG?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @RepMTG}}}\uc2  and I will hold a press conference tomorrow at the Capitol triangle. \uc2 Hakeem Jeffries\uc2  endorsed Mike Johnson to remain as Speaker today. We will discuss how this affects the Motion to Vacate the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/uniparty?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #uniparty}}}\uc2  Speaker. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/2e1Fxapi3K"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/2e1Fxapi3K}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Thomas Massie\uc2  (@RepThomasMassie) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RepThomasMassie/status/1785397177914662964?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 30, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 Uniparty is a term that has become popular on the far right to describe Republicans working with Democrats \u8211\'20\'13 the allegation being that the two parties are essentially the same. Lawmakers like Massie would prefer that Johnson hold fast and reject compromises with Democrats, like the foreign aid bill that funded Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s defense, or the government funding legislation enacted in March that Greene seized on to begin her push to remove Johnson as speaker.\par \par \uc2 Of course, there would have been consequences to holding up those two bills that could have harmed the GOP overall. If the government funding bills did not pass, Washington would have shut down, while if Ukraine did not receive more support, Russia could have made further battlefield gains. That could blow back on Republicans, particularly lawmakers in vulnerable seats \u8211\'20\'13 a group that does not include Greene or Massie.\par \par \uc2 Massie goes on to accuse Johnson of receiving the endorsement of \uc2 Hakeem Jeffries\uc2 , the Democratic minority leader. Here\u8217\'20\'19s more from him:\par \par \uc2 enltrWhy does \uc2 Hakeem Jeffries\uc2  want Mike Johnson as Speaker?\par \par \uc2 DEMS WANT:\par \par \uc2 *nothing done on the border\par \par \uc2 *no conservative policy victories\par \par \uc2 *more money for Ukraine\par \par \uc2 *a Dem majority in November\par \par \uc2 *expanded DOJ, \uc2 FBI\par \par \uc2 *no budget cuts\par \par \uc2 Hakeem knows Mike can deliver all of these things as Speaker. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/NGpd1YfghR"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/NGpd1YfghR}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Thomas Massie\uc2  (@RepThomasMassie) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RepThomasMassie/status/1785408873718800657?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 30, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.05pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.40pm BST\par \par \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene\uc2  to announce next move after Democrats intervene to protect speaker Mike Johnson\par \par \uc2 Good morning, US politics blog readers. We\u8217\'20\'19re kicking the day off with a press conference from far-right Republican congresswoman \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene\uc2 , who yesterday suffered a serious setback in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/mar/22/marjorie-taylor-greene-motion-mike-johnson"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 her campaign}}}\uc2  to remove Mike Johnson as speaker of the House. The chamber\u8217\'20\'19s top Democrats announced that they would oppose Greene\u8217\'20\'19s effort, a reversal from just a few months ago, when the party was more than happy to lend its votes to the GOP insurgency that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/oct/03/kevin-mccarthy-oust-republican-house-speaker-vote-result-matt-gaetz"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 booted}}}\uc2  Kevin McCarthy from the speaker\u8217\'20\'19s chair. But even before Democrats moved to protect Johnson \u8211\'20\'13 a staunch conservative who has lately worked with the minority party to pass bills dealing with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/apr/21/house-approves-61bn-aid-for-ukraine-what-we-know-so-far-and-what-happens-next"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 foreign aid}}}\uc2 , government spending and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/12/fisa-surveillance-act-reauthorized"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a controversial surveillance law}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 Greene only had two known co-signers of her motion to vacate the speaker\u8217\'20\'19s chair, which isn\u8217\'20\'19t much. She yesterday accused Johnson of making a \u8220\'20\'1Cslimy back room deal\u8221\'20\'1D for Democratic support, and hinted she might put her motion up for a vote anyway. The speaker, meanwhile, has said little about the drama.\par \par \uc2 Greene\u8217\'20\'19s press conference is scheduled for 9am ET outside the Capitol, and the Georgia lawmaker will be joined by \uc2 Thomas Massie\uc2 , one of her two colleagues supporting the effort. We\u8217\'20\'19ll tell you what they have to say.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else is going on:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Florida \u8217\'20\'19s ban on abortions after six weeks of pregnancy \u8211\'20\'13 when many women do not yet realize they are yet pregnant \u8211\'20\'13 goes into effect today, and \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is traveling to Jacksonville for a 2.45pm speech on the administration\u8217\'20\'19s fight to protect reproductive rights.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Protests against Israel continue at college campuses nationwide, with police clearing demonstrators from \uc2 Columbia University\uc2  last night, and clashes breaking out at the \uc2 University of California, Los Angeles\uc2 . Follow our live blog {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/may/01/columbia-university-protest-live-updates-nypd-new-york-police-enter-campus-pro-palestinian-demonstrators-latest-news"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 for more}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  announced his administration had canceled $6.1b in debt for students who attended the Arts Institutes, a for-profit college accused of fraud.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.21pm BST\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240501ek51001ux\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
