\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  refuses to say whether he supports a US national  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  ban\b0\par\par\uc2 Maya Yang \par \uc2 591 \uc2 words\par \uc2 29 April 2024\par 15:22 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Senate minority leader says he is \u8216\'20\'18not advocating anything at this level\u8217\'20\'19 and that issue is too divisive among lawmakers for consensus\par \par \uc2 Asked whether he supports a federal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, the \uc2 US Senate\uc2  minority leader, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/mitch-mcconnell"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Mitch McConnell}}}\uc2 , said on Sunday that he is \u8220\'20\'1Cnot advocating anything at this level\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The Republican, during remarks in a new interview published by NBC\u8217\'20\'19s Meet the Press, stopped short of saying whether or not he supported a 15-week federal ban on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  with exceptions, but he instead portrayed the issue as \u8220\'20\'1Ca practical matter\u8221\'20\'1D that was too divisive among federal lawmakers to result in a consensus among them.\par \par \uc2 Alluding to comments from 2022 in which he {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thehill.com/homenews/senate/3480725-mcconnell-says-national-abortion-ban-possible/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  a national ban was \u8220\'20\'1Cpossible\u8221\'20\'1D, McConnell said, \u8220\'20\'1CI said it was possible. I didn\u8217\'20\'19t say that was my view. I just said it was possible.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The Meet the Press host, Kristen Welker, pressed McConnell to explain if he supported a federal ban, prompting the Kentucky senator to reply: \u8220\'20\'1CThe reason I said it was possible is because the supreme court has put this back into the legislative arena. And we\u8217\'20\'19re seeing it play out all across the country. And I think in the end, it\u8217\'20\'19ll reflect the views of these individual states. But I said: \u8216\'20\'18Possible\u8217\'20\'19. I didn\u8217\'20\'19t say that was my view.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t think we\u8217\'20\'19ll get 60 votes in the Senate for any kind of national legislation,\u8221\'20\'1D he continued, referring to the number of votes needed to end the debate on bills in the Senate and get a vote on them. \u8220\'20\'1CI think it\u8217\'20\'19s a practical matter. It\u8217\'20\'19s gonna be sorted out at the state level.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 McConnell went on to reaffirm that he believes the issue of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access is one that should be decided by individual states after the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s decision in 2022 to eliminate the federal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights once established by the Roe v Wade case.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m not advocating anything at this level,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CIt seems to me views about this issue at the state level vary depending where you are. And we get elected by states. And my members are smart enough to figure out how they want to deal with this very divisive issue based upon the people who actually send them here.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 McConnell said he also does not think legislation seeking to federalize \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights would get the 60 votes it would need to be voted on in the Senate either.\par \par \uc2 In 2022, the South Carolina Republican senator \uc2 Lindsey Graham{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/sep/13/republican-national-abortion-ban-lindsey-graham"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 proposed}}}\uc2  a federal ban that would prohibit abortions after 15 weeks. Following Graham\u8217\'20\'19s proposal at the time, McConnell {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thehill.com/homenews/senate/3641225-mcconnell-throws-shade-on-grahams-proposed-national-abortion-ban/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told}}}\uc2  reporters: \u8220\'20\'1CWith regard to his bill, you\u8217\'20\'19ll have to ask him about it. In terms of scheduling, I think most of the members of my conference prefer that this be dealt with at the state level.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 McConnell\u8217\'20\'19s latest interview comes after the supreme court recently {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/24/emergency-abortion-care-us-supreme-court-what-to-know"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 heard}}}\uc2  an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights case centering on how states can decide when to permit emergency abortions. The case involves Idaho, which has one of the country\u8217\'20\'19s strictest \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans and only permits doctors to perform an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  to save the patient\u8217\'20\'19s life. However, under federal law, doctors are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/2024/apr/24/us-supreme-court-abortion-rights-emtala"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 required to}}}\uc2  stabilize patients\u8217\'20\'19 health if either their life or limb is threatened.\par \par \uc2 The conservative-majority \uc2 US supreme court\uc2 , which {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/24/emergency-abortion-care-us-supreme-court-what-to-know"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 appeared}}}\uc2  divided as of Wednesday, is expected to rule on the case in June.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240428ek4s001gt\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
