\par\par \uc2 Opinion\par \b \uc2 Discussing \uc2 Sonia Sotomayor\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s retirement is not sexist \u8211\'20\'13 it\u8217\'20\'19s strategic\b0\par\par\uc2 Arwa Mahdawi \par \uc2 1,280 \uc2 words\par \uc2 27 April 2024\par 13:04 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 The liberal justice has been called the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s conscience but we can\u8217\'20\'19t afford a repeat of \uc2 Ruth Bader Ginsburg\par \par \uc2 Sexism and Sonia Sotomay\par \par \uc2 or\par \par \uc2 A month ago Josh Barro (a man) at the Atlantic wrote a piece headlined {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theatlantic.com/politics/archive/2024/03/sonia-sotomayor-should-retire/677764/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Sonia Sotomayor Should Retire Now}}}\uc2 . Around the same time the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s Mehdi Hasan (a man) similarly {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2024/apr/01/for-the-sake-of-all-of-us-sonia-sotomayor-needs-to-retire-from-the-us-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 opined}}}\uc2  that \u8220\'20\'1Cfor the sake of all of us, \uc2 Sonia Sotomayor\uc2  needs to retire from the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2 .\u8221\'20\'1D The \uc2 University of Colorado Boulder\uc2  law professor Paul Campos (a man) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.newsweek.com/sonia-sotomayor-staying-supreme-court-poses-risk-1885312"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 also went on CNN}}}\uc2  to argue that 69-year-old Sotomayor should consider stepping down as a justice in order to give Joe Biden time to fill the seat with another liberal judge should the worst happen. And pundit Nate Silver (you guessed it \u8230\'20\'26 another man) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.natesilver.net/p/sonia-sotomayors-retirement-is-a"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said much the same thing}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 It is a truth universally acknowledged that once you can count at least three instances of something, then, congratulations, you\u8217\'20\'19ve got {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.npr.org/templates/story/story.php?storyId=1140359#:~:text=Three%20Times%20%3D%20A%20Trend%20Bob,what%20might%20otherwise%20be%20dismissed."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a trend}}}\uc2 . In this case, various commentators proclaimed, an extremely gendered trend. The fact that a bunch of men were clamouring for a high-profile woman to retire immediately sparked cries of sexism.\par \par \uc2 In Slate, for example, Dahlia Lithwick {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://slate.com/news-and-politics/2024/04/justice-sotomayor-retirement-calls-sexism.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pointed out}}}\uc2  that \u8220\'20\'1Cvirtually every prominent person pushing [the argument that Sotomayor should retire] is male. And the people defending her are female.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Please, I\u8217\'20\'19m begging everyone, let\u8217\'20\'19s not have this ridiculous debate again. We had {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2023/apr/15/clinging-to-power-does-not-make-dianne-feinstein-a-feminist-hero"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 this exact same conversation}}}\uc2  last year, you may recall, in relation to the late \uc2 Dianne Feinstein\uc2 . The Democratic senator, then 89 years old, was urged to step down after health issues caused her to miss a number of important judiciary committee sessions. These calls, in turn, were labelled sexist. \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t know what political agendas are at work that are going after Senator Feinstein in that way,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.yahoo.com/lifestyle/pelosi-calls-feinstein-resign-ve-120350021.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Nancy Pelosi said at the time}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19ve never seen them go after a man who was sick in the Senate in that way.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Do women in positions of high power frequently get judged by higher standards than their male peers? Yes, of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.npr.org/2016/06/02/480487259/women-held-to-higher-ethical-standard-than-men-study-shows"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 course they do}}}\uc2 . But criticizing a woman is not, it goes without saying, automatically sexist. It certainly wasn\u8217\'20\'19t sexist to suggest than an 89-year-old senator with obvious health problems might think about retiring. Nor is it sexist to suggest that we might learn a little something from the fact that \uc2 Ruth Bader Ginsburg\uc2  refused to quit the supreme court only to die in 2020 and have the highly conservative \uc2 Amy Coney Barrett\uc2  nominated as her replacement by \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  just eight days after her death. In no world is it sexist to suggest that we might want to do everything possible to avoid a repeat of this.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s also wrong, it should be noted, to suggest that it is only female justices who have been urged to retire. Justice \uc2 Stephen Breyer\uc2 , the oldest jurist in the court\u8217\'20\'19s liberal faction, stepped down in 2022 following {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/2022/01/29/inside-campaign-pressure-justice-stephen-breyer-retire/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 what the Washington Post}}}\uc2  described as \u8220\'20\'1Can extraordinary campaign designed to pressure him to retire and make way for a new nominee to be named by a Democratic president\u8221\'20\'1D. A truck even drove around the supreme court building with a billboard that said: \u8220\'20\'1CBreyer, retire.\u8221\'20\'1D And the pressure worked. Breyer stepped down and was replaced by 51-year-old {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ketanji-brown-jackson"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ketanji Brown Jackson}}}\uc2 , the first Black woman on the supreme court.\par \par \uc2 Breyer, of course, was 83 \u8211\'20\'13 far older than Sotomayor is. Amid the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/feb/19/us-congress-presidency-gerontocracy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 gerontocracy}}}\uc2  that is the \uc2 US government\uc2 , Sotomayor is basically a spring chicken. Nevertheless, she is still the oldest of the three liberal justices (\uc2 Elena Kagan\uc2  is 63). It would be remiss not to at least have a conversation about how best to avoid an RBG repeat. We have no idea what will happen in the future, but we can make sure we learn from the past.\par \par \uc2 It can\u8217\'20\'19t be particularly nice for Sotomayor, I will acknowledge, to have her health and mortality be a widespread talking point. It can\u8217\'20\'19t be very pleasant for people to seize on her diabetes, the early death {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.npr.org/transcripts/167699633"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 of her father}}}\uc2 , and the fact that she has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.huffpost.com/entry/sonia-sotomayor-medic-retirement_n_65d8ec05e4b0cc1f2f7bab77"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 travelled with a medic}}}\uc2 , as evidence that her health might be compromised. But now is not the time to be pussyfooting around the issue in case Sotomayor\u8217\'20\'19s feelings get hurt. Now is the time to be terrified that, should the worst happen and another rightwing justice takes Sotomayor\u8217\'20\'19s place resulting in a 7-2 conservative majority, the civil rights of millions will be irrevocably hurt. Now is the time to be strategic.\par \par \uc2 Let me clear: none of this is meant as a slight to Sotomayor, who has consistently shown herself to be, as the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.thenation.com/article/politics/sonia-sotomayor-liberal-justice/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Nation put it}}}\uc2 , \u8220\'20\'1Cthe conscience of the supreme court\u8221\'20\'1D. She\u8217\'20\'19s an incredibly impressive truth-teller whose {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.npr.org/2023/06/30/1185339349/colorado-supreme-court-same-sex-marriage-decision"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 impassioned dissents frequently go viral}}}\uc2 . At a time when many public servants seem more interested in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/2023/nov/13/us-supreme-court-ethics-code"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 private enrichment}}}\uc2  than protecting civil liberties, Sotomayor is out there fighting the good fight. Her retirement would be a huge loss. But if the worst-case scenario does transpire, it\u8217\'20\'19s nothing compared to what the rest of us are set to lose.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  heard one of the most sadistic, extreme anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  cases yet\par \par \uc2 The latest example of Sotomayor being an inspirational badass came at a supreme court hearing this week when she pushed back on Idaho\u8217\'20\'19s assertion that its strict \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban supersedes a federal emergency care law. Sotomayor told the story of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jun/22/post-roe-abortion-women-of-color"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Anya Cook}}}\uc2 , a Florida woman who was turned away by an emergency room after her water broke at 16 weeks because her treatment required an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . She was only able to get treated the next day, when she was near death. \u8220\'20\'1CWhat is at stake now \u8211\'20\'13 what was being debated in court on Wednesday \u8211\'20\'13 is how much women can be forced to suffer, how much danger they can be placed in,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2024/apr/25/supreme-court-idaho-anti-abortion-case"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Moira Donegan wrote in relation to the case}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CThe anti-choice movement, and its allies on the bench, have shown once again that there is no amount that will satisfy them.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Fifty women talk about life as a domestic worker under the Gulf\u8217\'20\'19s kafala system\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CUnder kafala (\u8216\'20\'18sponsorship\u8217\'20\'19) laws, domestic workers are vulnerable to abuse within their employers\u8217\'20\'19 home \u8211\'20\'13 and leaving their workplace is a criminal offence,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/global-development/2024/apr/25/kafala-labour-system-gulf-women-talk-about-life-as-a-domestic-worker-in-the-gulf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Guardian reports}}}\uc2 . A decade after Qatar was advised by the \uc2 UN\uc2  to abolish kafala and replace it with a regulated labour network, the system is thriving across Lebanon, Jordan and the Gulf states and vulnerable women are suffering.\par \par \uc2 Honduras referred to \uc2 UN\uc2  human rights committee over total \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/global-development/2024/apr/24/honduras-referred-to-un-human-rights-committee-over-total-abortion-ban"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Campaigners filed a petition}}}\uc2  on behalf of a woman known as Fausia, who was raped and then forced to give birth under Honduras\u8217\'20\'19s extreme \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws.\par \par \uc2 The Viking women with intentionally reshaped skulls\par \par \uc2 While examining Viking remains from the island of Gotland in the Baltic Sea, researchers found oblong-shaped adult female skulls. They think the skulls were deliberately reshaped {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.atlasobscura.com/articles/viking-elongated-skulls"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in order to signal status}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Anne Hathaway says she had to kiss 10 men during \u8216\'20\'18gross\u8217\'20\'19 chemistry audition\par \par \uc2 This sounds {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/film/2024/apr/23/anne-hathaway-kiss-10-men-during-gross-chemistry-audition"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 extremely unhygienic}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The week in pawtriarchy\par \par \uc2 A Utah couple thought {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.businessinsider.com/couple-accidentally-sent-cat-amazon-package-arrived-6-days-later-2024-4"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 they\u8217\'20\'19d lost their beloved}}}\uc2  cat, named Galena. Turns out they\u8217\'20\'19d accidentally shipped her in an Amazon return package, alongside five pairs of steel-toed work boots but without any food or water. Galena was rescued six days later by an Amazon worker in California who took her to a vet. She\u8217\'20\'19d lost a bit of weight but was otherwise completely unharmed. Cat-astrophe averted!\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240427ek4r0012x\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
