\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Arizona house votes to repeal state\u8217\'20\'19s near-total ban on  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 Dani Anguiano \par \uc2 907 \uc2 words\par \uc2 24 April 2024\par 21:59 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Three Republicans join Democrats to support repeal of law first approved in 1864, with measure now heading to state senate\par \par \uc2 Lawmakers in the Arizona house have voted to repeal a controversial 1864 law banning nearly all abortions, amid mounting pressure on the state\u8217\'20\'19s Republicans.\par \par \uc2 Three Republicans joined with all 29 Democrats on Wednesday to support the repeal of the law, which predates Arizona\u8217\'20\'19s statehood and provides no exceptions for rape or incest.\par \par \uc2 The move follows weeks of effort by Democrats in the state legislature to undo the law, while the issue increasingly put Republicans on the defensive in a key battleground state.\par \par \uc2 The measure will now head to the state senate, where it is expected to pass, and then to the governor\u8217\'20\'19s desk.\par \par \uc2 The Arizona supreme court {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/09/arizona-supreme-court-abortion-decision"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 earlier this month}}}\uc2  concluded the state could enforce a long-dormant law that permits abortions only to save the pregnant patient\u8217\'20\'19s life. The ruling suggested doctors could be prosecuted under the law, first approved in 1864, and that anyone who assists in an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  could face two to five years in prison.\par \par \uc2 The ruling put enormous pressure on Republicans in the state, who are under fire from some conservatives in their base who firmly support the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, and from swing voters who strongly oppose the measure and will decide crucial races including the presidency, the \uc2 US Senate\uc2  and the GOP\u8217\'20\'19s control of the legislature.\par \par \uc2 Some prominent Republicans, including the GOP candidate for Senate, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/apr/11/kari-lake-arizona-abortion-reversal"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kari Lake}}}\uc2 , have come out against the ban. But Republicans in the statehouse repeatedly blocked efforts by Democratic lawmakers to repeal the law.\par \par \uc2 A week ago, one Republican in the Arizona house joined 29 Democrats to bring the repeal measure to a vote, but the effort failed twice on 30-30 votes.\par \par \uc2 The office of the Arizona attorney general, Kris Mayes, on Tuesday had asked the state supreme court to reconsider its decision, the Arizona Republic {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.azcentral.com/story/news/politics/arizona/2024/04/24/arizona-abortion-ban-attorney-general-asks-state-supreme-court-to-reconsider/73432217007/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 On Wednesday, dozens of people gathered outside the state capitol before the House and Senate were scheduled to meet, many of them carrying signs or wearing shirts showing their opposition to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 Anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  protesters sang Amazing Grace and chanted \u8220\'20\'1Cshame on you\u8221\'20\'1D, Jeremy Duda of Axios reported.\par \par \uc2 The AZ House doesn\u8217\'20\'19t convene until 10am, but the gallery is already full. Pro-life folks are making the most of their ability to make noise before lawmakers come to the floor, singing \u8220\'20\'1CAmazing Grace\u8221\'20\'1D and chanting \u8220\'20\'1CShame on you!\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/sFDf2rxsCl"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/sFDf2rxsCl}}}\uc2  \u8212\'20\'14 Jeremy Duda (@jeremyduda) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/jeremyduda/status/1783171343552516121?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 24, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 Some Republicans were critical of their colleagues\u8217\'20\'19 move to side with Democrats in repealing the ban.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI am disgusted today,\u8221\'20\'1D said \uc2 Rachel Jones\uc2 , a Republican representative who voted against repeal. \u8220\'20\'1CLife is one of the tenets of our Republican platform. To see people go back on that value is egregious to me.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The civil-war era law had been blocked since the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s 1973 Roe v Wade decision guaranteed the constitutional right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  nationwide.\par \par \uc2 After Roe v Wade was overturned in June 2022, the then Arizona attorney general, \uc2 Mark Brnovich\uc2 , a Republican, persuaded a state judge that the 1864 ban could be enforced. The law had not actually been enforced while the case made its way through the courts.\par \par \uc2 If the proposed repeal is signed into law by the Democratic governor \uc2 Katie Hobbs\uc2 , a 2022 statute banning the procedure after 15 weeks of pregnancy would become the prevailing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law.\par \par \uc2 Many \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers in the state {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/17/arizona-abortion-ban-doctors-future"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 had vowed}}}\uc2  to continue providing the procedure until the ban went into effect. In neighboring California, providers were gearing up to treat Arizona patients seeking \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care.\par \par \uc2 The battle over \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access in Arizona will ultimately be decided in November. \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights advocates are pushing to ask Arizona voters to create a constitutional right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . They have collected about 500,000 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/24/arizona-abortion-1864-ban"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 signatures}}}\uc2 , more than the almost 384,000 needed to put it on the ballot.\par \par \uc2 The proposed constitutional amendment would guarantee \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights until a fetus could survive outside the womb, typically around 24 weeks. It also would allow later abortions to save the parent\u8217\'20\'19s life, or to protect her physical or mental health.\par \par \uc2 Republican lawmakers, in turn, are considering putting one or more competing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  proposals on the November ballot.\par \par \uc2 A leaked planning document outlined the approaches being considered by house Republicans, such as codifying existing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  regulations, proposing a 14-week ban that would be \u8220\'20\'1Cdisguised as a 15-week law\u8221\'20\'1D because it would allow abortions until the beginning of the 15th week, and a measure that would prohibit abortions after six weeks of pregnancy, before many people know they are pregnant.\par \par \uc2 House Republicans have not yet publicly released any such proposed ballot measures.\par \par \uc2 Reproductive rights advocates say the issue has mobilized voters and report that people are seeking out signature-gatherers and asking about locations where their friends and family can sign to put \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access on the ballot.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19ve had women come up with three kids, and they\u8217\'20\'19re signing. And I tell them, moms are the most important signature here, because they understand what this issue is, and what pregnancy does to the body, what pregnancy does to your life,\u8221\'20\'1D Susan Anthony, who has been gathering signatures in Arizona, told the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/24/arizona-abortion-1864-ban"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Guardian}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The Associated Press contribute\par \par \uc2 d\par \par \uc2 reporting\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240424ek4o002gz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
